// GENERATED data -- do not hand-edit.
// Source: runescape.wiki Quick guide pages (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0).
window.QUEST_GUIDES = {"'Phite Club":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak with Grand Vizier Hassan in the Merchant district of Menaphos. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Phite Club. > Accept > Any > 2 I'll help if I get to end him.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"1 free inventory space","r":"","s":["Speak to the faction heads, preferably ending with worker (closest to tomb)\n  - Speak to Grand Vizier Ehsan (Merchant) also in the same building. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Phite Club. > Any}\n  - Speak to 'Admiral' Wadud (Ports) in the Golden Scarab Inn in the Port district. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Phite Club. > Any}\n  - Speak to Commander Akhomet (Imperial) in the Imperial district. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Phite Club.}\n  - Speak to Batal (Worker) in the Worker district. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Phite Club.}","Enter the Shifting Tombs and speak to Ozan inside.","Exit the Shifting Tombs and use the mask you received from Ozan with the bucket of blood next to the fish stall in the Merchant district.","Speak to Akhomet in the Imperial district. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Phite Club.}","Give the signets to Batal in the Worker district. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Phite Club.}","Give the certificate to Wadud in the Port district. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Phite Club.}","Speak to Ehsan in the Merchant district. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Phite Club.}"],"t":"One small favour"},{"n":"Combat equipment and food; recommended = Feathers of Ma'at, Beast of Burden familiar or Combat Summoning familiar, emergency teleport","r":"","s":["Gear up for a battle.","Speak to Hassan in the Merchant district. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Phite Club. > 1 Yes, let's go confront the Pharaoh.}","Kill four level 105 Menaphos palace guards. This will be a checkpoint for the final fight.\n  - Use Protect from Magic prayer and finish off the ones using melee combat style first.","Fight the Pharaoh. {Chat: Any}\n  - Use Protect from Magic.\n  - \"Kneel\" or \"Usurpers!\" - Use the freedom ability to break free and prevent further damage.\n  - Move off the green fire as soon as it spawns."],"t":"Confronting the Pharaoh"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Watch the cutscene. {Chat: Any}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finale"}]},"2017 Easter event":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Easter Bunny south of the Burthorpe lodestone for a magical bunny notepaper."],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"Bucket of compost, Bucket of water, cooked Shrimp","r":"Explorer's ring","s":["Talk to the dark green Cabbage in the southern part of the Falador cabbage patch.","Give 'Cabbage' the items by talking again.","Speak to 'Cabbage' again then view the divine egg (cabbage)."],"t":"'Cabbage'"},{"n":"Normal logs, 10 potato seeds","r":"","s":["Talk to Dave the giant ent at the Draynor Manor entrance (front doors).","Give Dave the items by talking again.","Speak to Dave again then view the divine egg (ent)."],"t":"Dave the giant ent"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the dwarf in the blue shirt in the western part of the Dwarven Mine (he is standing in the hallway east of Hammerspike Stoutbeard).","Right-click catch with him.","Catch 10 chickens.","Speak to him again then view the divine egg (dwarf)."],"t":"Dwarf"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Druid woman east of Kaqemeex in the Taverley druid circle.","Play \"Stone, Net, Sickle\" with her three times (winning or losing is irrelevant).","After playing view the divine egg (druid)."],"t":"Druid"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to the Easter Bunny.","Read your magical bunny notepaper then view the divine egg (bunny).","Talk to the Easter Bunny again.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Bunny"}]},"A Christmas Reunion":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Cait or Diango in Christmas Village. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Talking to Cait or Diango"},{"n":"3 split fir logs, 15 steel nails","r":"","s":["Fully build the three piles of planks."],"t":"Building the workbenches"},{"n":"A free backpack space","r":"","s":["Talk to Cait or Diango in Christmas Village.","Talk to three of the pixies found in the following areas. You can optionally scan with the magical thingymabob for status indicators for how close you are to the correct spot."],"t":"Recruiting the pixies"},{"n":"A free backpack space, thread (or the effect from a Crafting cape), 6 bolts of cloth, red dye, green dye","r":"","s":["Talk to Cait or Diango in Christmas Village. {Chat: Any}","Talk to Iffie in Varrock. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'A Christmas Reunion'. > Any}","Use red dye on green dye. {Chat: 1 Make Christmas dye.}","Craft the pixie uniform pattern."],"t":"Creating the pixie uniforms"},{"n":"Chocolate dust, bucket of milk, biscuits","r":"","s":["Talk to Cait or Diango in Christmas Village. {Chat: Any}","Add hot chocolate powder to the hot chocolate storage and enter \"0\", \"2\", and \"3\" when prompted.","Add biscuits to the biscuit storage and enter \"1\", \"2\", and \"2\" when prompted.","Talk to Cait or Diango in Christmas Village.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Stocking the kitchen"}]},"A Clockwork Syringe":{"sections":[{"n":"Combat gear, 1 free backpack space","r":"Food, super restores, and prayer potions","s":["Go to your player-owned house portal, and attempt to enter your house.","Attempt to enter again and choose the \"A Clockwork Syringe\" option from your portal. {Chat: 4 A Clockwork Syringe. > 1 Yes.}","Read the delivery note.(If Pete doesn't appear check your bank for the note) {Chat: Accept}","Attempt to enter your house again and select the \"A Clockwork Syringe\" option once more. {Chat: 4 A Clockwork Syringe. > 1 Yes.}","Investigate the large crate. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Kill the level 98 Barrelchest Mk II."],"t":"Delivery note in the house"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the estate agent.","Interrogate the zombie head.","Torture the head using all five options.","Interrogate the head once more when it reaches maximum stress."],"t":"Dealing with the delivery"},{"n":"Zombie head","r":"Ectophial for reaching Port Phasmatys, or 325 coins to charter a ship","s":["With the zombie head, talk to Bill Teach on Mos Le'Harmless, either in the Other Inn or on The Adventurous ship. {Chat: 1 Speak about A Clockwork Syringe.}\n  - Head to the docks of Port Phasmatys, cross the gangplank on the easternmost ship, right-click travel via Bill Teach to travel to Mos Le'Harmless.\n  - Alternatively, charter a ship directly to Mos Le'Harmless from Port Sarim.\n  - You can also use fairy ring DIP if you have repaired the bridge there and partial completion of A Fairy Tale III - Battle at Ork's Rift.","Walk north to Harpoon Joe's House of 'Rum'.","Sit in the chair in the north-east corner and ask Joe for a \"Long Drop\". {Chat: 1 A Long Drop.}","Talk to Bill.","Place-evidence on table nearby to set the zombie head on top.","Talk to Bill again.","Climb-up the ladder."],"t":"Warning Bill Teach"},{"n":"Fishbowl helmet, diving apparatus, and pirate spell sheet","r":"Dungeoneering cape, Combat gear, food, prayer potions, antipoison, and emergency teleport","s":["Select-spell with the pirate spell sheet in your backpack to travel to Braindeath Island. {Chat: 1 Braindeath Island.}\n  - The spell can only be used on the floor 1 of Mos Le'Harmless.","Go directly west and talk to Captain Braindeath. {Chat: # Speak about A Clockwork Syringe. > 3 Nothing}\n  - Optional: get a diving apparatus and a fishbowl helmet from him, if you don't already have them.","Go to the Braindeath Island 'Rum'-geon entrance:\n  - Optional: If you have it, activate the Dungeoneering cape to travel directly there, skipping these steps. {Chat: 8 Braindeath Island.}\n  - Climb-down the wooden stair to the west.\n  - Head north past 50% Luke and open the gate.\n  - Head north across the two bridges to the mysterious entrance.","Equip your diving apparatus and fishbowl helmet.","Enter the mysterious entrance.\n  - Optional: kill a crab in order to complete the hard Daemonheim achievement Alcrabholic.","Go down all three paths and search the dead brewers to discover their names.","Return to Captain Braindeath and receive the Twiblick night special. {Chat: # Talk about A Clockwork Syringe. > 1 I found the three missing brewers... > 1 Yes, I'm ready.}","Teleport back to Mos Le'Harmless with the pirate spell sheet. {Chat: 2 Mos Le'Harmless.}","Return to the basement in Joe's pub. {Chat: 1 A Long Drop.}","Talk to Bill and receive the unlocked Twiblick night special.","Open the box. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 Yes! > 1 Just open it already!}","Talk to Bill again. {Chat: 2 How are we going to use this to get information? > Any > Any > Any > Any}\n  - Select any of the remaining chat options to give the zombie head a makeover.","Talk to Bill again."],"t":"Finding the workers"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return south to Bill's ship, cross the gangplank, talk to him, and use the \"A Clockwork Syringe\" option to begin your travel. {Chat: # Speak about A Clockwork Syringe. > 1 Yes, let's get underway.}","Talk to Bill. {Chat: 3 Awesome! I'll get right on it!}","Climb-down two ladders to the hold of the ship (lowest level).\n  - Open and search the gun locker.\n  - Open and search the repair locker.\n  - Take 3 gunpowder from the powder barrel.\n  - Take a barrel from the barrel stack.\n  - Use the gunpowder on the chain.\n  - Use the anvil to smith the heated chain and cannonball together.\n  - Use your cannonball and chain on the barrel to receive a cannonball barrel-boat.","Go back up the ladder to the main deck. On the eastern cannon, choose 'Take-The-Ride' option to go to Bloodsplatter Isle. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Getting into Bloodsplatter Isle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Investigate the Perch Rock. {Chat: Any > 2 I'm ready to begin.} You must steer him around while dropping cannonballs on the Barrelchests.","Leave the Isle by diving at the pier and swim. {Chat: 1 Swim.}","Climb the ladder and talk to Bill on his ship, request to go to Bloodsplatter Isle. {Chat: 2 Can you take me to Bloodsplatter Isle?}","Walk in to the middle of the factory building in order to get caught.","Escape your cell and collect the following items directly north of the cell:\n  - Surgical mask.\n  - Roll of bandage.\n  - Barrelchest parts (abscond with shelf).\n  - Barrel from the stack.","Return to Bill by using the signalling point at the end of the dock where you arrived. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Get the Barrelchest disguise from Bill. {Chat: 1 Cap'n...I've a problem. > 1 I've gathered the things you asked for.}","Talk to Bill again and have him send you back to the island. {Chat: 2 Can you take me to Bloodsplatter Isle?}","Enter the the factory and take 3 barrels from the stack and 3 gunpowder from the barrel - where you picked up the supplies for the Barrelchest disguise."],"t":"Investigating Bloodsplatter Isle"},{"n":"Barrelchest disguise","r":"","s":["Change into the Barrelchest disguise. Must be 3x3 clear around your character.","Letter One: Go to the south-west room, sabotage the southern gas canister. 'Tell-joke' to each of the Dis-orderly and then brutalise each of them. Investigate the noticeboard.","Letter Two: Kill each of Grimterns in the western-most room. Investigate the noticeboard after killing them.","Letter Three: Talk to one of the drunk zombies lying on the beds in the north-west room, then investigate the noticeboard.","Letter Four: Loosen each of the three undead arms in the north-east room, then inspect one of the arms, finally investigate the noticeboard.","Letter Five: This step requires at least 300 life points. Use the three gunpowder on the barrels in your backpack. Then in the south-eastern room, finish-building on each of the three incomplete barrelchest stations, then detonate one of them to destroy all three. Finally, investigate the noticeboard.","Change out of the barrelchest disguise from your backpack. Changing in the middle of the factory gets you caught.","Return back to Bill by signalling him from the dock to the south. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Collecting evidence"},{"n":"Evidence files","r":"","s":["Talk to Bill onboard his ship and show him the evidence files.","Return to Bloodsplatter Isle. {Chat: 2 Can you take me to Bloodsplatter Isle?}\n  - The barrelchest disguise is no longer required.","Head back into the factory and enter the easternmost room.","Pull the lever to activate the three conveyor belts. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Left-click the conveyor belts to load Bundle o' kegs onto them.\n  - Continue loading the conveyor belts until each of the conveyor belts explode.\n  - You can safely ignore the zombies that make it to you; killing them does nothing and they automatically die when all three belts explode."],"t":"Destroying the factory construction line"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Jump over the destroyed wall between the conveyor lines, and head east through the door opening to the docks.","Climb-down the ladder at the end of the dock.","Board the unoccupied zomboat and sink all the boats.\n  - Fire cannonballs at the boats either by left-clicking on them, or using the minigame menu.\n  - Don't forget to repair your boat when it gets to about 25% health - it is not instant and you can only repair while your boat is at a stand still.","After you sink all of the other boats, climb up the east ladder and talk to Bill on his ship.","Head back to the basement in Joe's pub. {Chat: 1 A Long Drop}","Talk to Bill to finish the quest.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Battle at sea"}]},"A Fairy Tale I - Growing Pains":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Martin the Master Gardener in Draynor Village. {Chat: 2 General Chat > 1 Anything I can help with? > Accept > 1 Now that I think about it, you're right!}","Talk to 5 different gardeners near farming patches around RuneScape. Easy options include:\n  - Frizzy, on the other side of the wall, just west of Martin. {Chat: 2 Are you a member of the Group of Advanced Gardeners?}\n  - Elstan, to the north of Frizzy. {Chat: 2 Are you a member of the Group of Advanced Gardeners?}\n  - Alain, north of Taverley lodestone. {Chat: 2 Are you a member of the Group of Advanced Gardeners?}\n  - Dantaera, north-west of Catherby lodestone. {Chat: 2 Are you a member of the Group of Advanced Gardeners?}\n    - If you do not have secateurs yet, buy them from Vanessa's Farming Shop just to the south.\n  - Ellena, east of the Catherby lodestone, beside the fruit tree patch on the beach. {Chat: 2 Are you a member of the Group of Advanced Gardeners?}","Note that:\n  - Spirit Tree Patch gardeners all count as the same gardener.\n  - The gardeners in Prifddinas won't work.\n  - The zombie farmer does not work.\n  - Head Farmer Jones in Taverley won't work.\n  - Wyson the gardener in Falador won't work.\n  - Demetrius in Wendlewick won't work.","The fifth gardener you talk to will mention fairies.","Talk to Martin again. {Chat: 2 Talk about farming problems.}"],"t":"G.A.G"},{"n":"Dramen staff, secateurs","r":"","s":["Equip your dramen staff or lunar staff and head to the Lumbridge Swamp to enter the Lost City shed.","Run south and talk to the Fairy Godfather (near Chaeldar, the Slayer master) about the Queen. {Chat: 2 Where's the Fairy Queen?} Make sure to finish the whole dialogue.","Run west to the bank, then go north a few steps and talk to Fairy Nuff.","Travel to the Dark Wizards' Tower, west of Falador (use the skills necklace teleport to Crafting Guild or teleport to Port Sarim lodestone, and then run north-west).","Climb to the top, talk to Zandar Horfyre.\n  - Player with low combat level should be aware of the aggressive dark wizards inside the tower.","Teleport to Port Sarim and talk to Malignius Mortifer (just north-west of Port Sarim, pictured right) about a Tanglefoot. {Chat: 2 I need help with fighting a Tanglefoot.} or {Chat: 1 I need help with fighting a Tanglefoot.} if Swan Song has been completed.\n  - Talking to Malignius at the Um ritual site will not work.","Head back to Draynor Village and enter the gates of Draynor Manor.","Dig the gravestone directly inside the north fence of the manor, west of the gallows. It resembles a celtic cross.","Return to Malignius. {Chat: 2 I was asking you about fighting a Tanglefoot...} or {Chat: 1 I was asking you about fighting a Tanglefoot...} if Swan Song has been started.","Fetch the items that Malignius requested (they will be listed in your quest journal), then make your way to the Nature Spirit. Bring multiple of any edible item, or bring a filled druid pouch to ward off ghasts.\n  - Make sure to clean any requested herbs.\n  - Make sure to bring extra of any requested food items."],"t":"Finding a cure"},{"n":"Secateurs, and requested items.","r":"Teleport to Barrows or Burgh de Rott for quick access to Nature Grotto}}{{Checklis","s":["Talk to the Nature Spirit in Mort Myre Swamp to receive magic secateurs."],"t":"Magic secateurs"},{"n":"Dramen staff, Magic secateurs","r":"Combat gear}}{{Checklis","s":["Return to Zanaris, then enter the shady grove (dungeon icon) west of the cosmic altar.\n  - You can use a cosmic altar teleport to teleport to the cosmic altar.","Run south around the bend then north to the opening with the Tanglefoot.","Equip your magic secateurs and kill Tanglefoot. Off-hand weaponry will work here, but will only deal as much as the secateurs would.","Take the Queen's secateurs (area loot will not work).","Talk to the Fairy Godfather, Next to the Slayer Master icon.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The final fight"}]},"A Fairy Tale II - Cure a Queen":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Martin the Master Gardener in the Draynor Market. {Chat: 2 Talk about farming problems and fairies. > Accept}","After 5 minutes have elapsed, talk to him again. {Chat: 2 I suppose I'd better go and see what the problem is, then.}","Go to Fairy Nuff's cottage, north of the Zanaris bank.","Enter the house and take Nuff's healing certificate from the floor in the south-east corner. Keep this in your inventory throughout the quest.","Right-click Study Nuff's certificate (using Read will not allow you to reach the Fairy Resistance HQ).","Head south and read the rune temple sign, on the ground south of the cosmic altar.","Talk to the Fairy Godfather (located in the Throne Room) about the Queen's disappearance. {Chat: 1 Where is the Fairy Queen? > 1 Do you have any idea who could have done this? > 1 Yes, okay.}","Talk to the Co-ordinator just north of the throne room at the crossroads. {Chat: 2 The fairy rings.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"Dramen staff or lunar staff, Nuff's certificate","r":"","s":["Talk to Fairy Fixit near the fairy ring, south-west of the wheat field.","Make sure you have Nuff's certificate in your inventory. It can be retrieved from her grotto if lost.","Equip your dramen or lunar staff, click on the fairy ring, and teleport to the following codes (in this order):\n  - air\n  - dlr\n  - djq (Dialling this will appear to fail and take you back to Zanaris; continue regardless.)\n  - ajs","In the Fairy Resistance Hideout, talk to Fairy Nuff and Fairy Very Wise in the northeastern clearing.","Return to Zanaris and pickpocket the Fairy Godfather for the queen's secateurs (may take several attempts). The Fairy Godfather, Fat Rocco and Slim Louie need to be looking away from you when you pickpocket.","Return to the Resistance Hideout by selecting the \"Fairy Resistance HQ\" option in the Fairy Ring. Nuff's certificate must be in your inventory.","Talk to Fairy Nuff."],"t":"Resistance hideout"},{"n":"Vial of water, Nuff's certificate","r":"Equipment and food for combat","s":["Travel to the Cosmic Entity plane using ckp.","Wait for a starflower to spawn (may take 1-2 minutes).","Pick the star flower and use it on a vial of water.","Ensure you have equipment required to fight at least one gorak, then travel to the Gorak Plane using dir.","Kill Goraks until you receive gorak claws.","Grind the Gorak claws, then use the resulting gorak claw powder on the magic essence (unfinished).","Return to the Resistance Hideout by first teleporting back to Zanaris by choosing \"Use Fairy ring\" and then clicking the Fairy Resistance HQ as a teleport destination.","Talk to Fairy Nuff.","Right-click use the magic essence (3) on the Fairy Queen. She is laying on the stretcher near Fairy Nuff, not as an interactable NPC.","Finish dialogue with the Fairy Queen.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Magic essence"}]},"A Fairy Tale III - Battle at Ork's Rift":{"sections":[{"n":"Nuff's certificate, Dramen staff or the Lunar staff","r":"","s":["Use any fairy ring to travel to Zanaris. If you can start the quest, you will be redirected to the Sparse Plane.\n  - If you cannot start the quest, enter and leave Zanaris via fairy rings repeatedly until Fairy Very Wise appears and talks to you. It may require up to 30 minutes after completing A Fairy Tale II - Cure a Queen. If you've declined her before, you have to travel by fairy ring BIR to reach her.","Talk to Fairy Very Wise and accept her offer {Chat: 4 Of course I'll help. What do I need to do?}. After accepting her offer, Nuff's certificate is no longer needed to reach the Fairy Resistance headquarters.","Accept the teleport from her {Chat: 1 Please teleport me there right away!}, or use the fairy ring to get to the Fairy Resistance headquarters (AIR, DLR, DJQ, AJS).","Talk to the Fairy Queen south-east in the headquarters and then finish talking to the Tooth Fairy (she automatically speaks to you after you speak with the queen). {Chat: 2 Yes, I'll help. > Accept}","Be wary of cutscenes that may trigger epilepsy. Talk to the Tooth Fairy, then turn on the projector to watch the first briefing. {Chat: 2 Show a non-flickering briefing.}","Talk to the Tooth Fairy again after the briefing. {Chat: 5 Right, I understand about fairy tooth magic now. > 1 Yes, I'm ready.}","Turn on the projector to watch the second briefing.","End of cutscenes.","After both briefings, agree to collect her wand. {Chat: 3 Yes, I'll go and collect your wand.}","Run north-west and take a hammer and secateurs from on top of the crates. You may use area loot. Use them on each other to create a tooth extractor.","Leave through the fairy ring."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"Bucket of milk and tooth extractor","r":"","s":["Go to the house north-west of Zanaris bank. Use your tooth extractor on the door to pick the lock on it.","Talk to Gnarly. {Chat: 4 Can I do something for you...in return for the wand?}","In no particular order, compliment him with the following responses (Only 3 compliments may be needed to continue to the next part):\n  - \"Your enamel shimmers like a river of silver in the moonlight.\"\n  - \"I've never seen such amazing, inspired and dream-like toothiness.\"\n  - \"I can see your bicuspid ancestry is an example to all molar-kind.\"\n  - \"You're a wonderful guard tooth with lovely cusps.\"","Use the bucket of milk on him {Chat: 2 Okay, I'll close my eyes. > 2 Okay, okay! Keep your enamel on, I'll pick you up.}. Gnarly should jump into your inventory.","Use the fairy rings to go back to the Fairy Resistance HQ.","Talk to the Tooth Fairy in the south-east room, then turn on the projector.","After the briefing, agree to the tooth extraction. {Chat: 2 Yes, I understand all of that. > 2 Yes, I accept. > 3 Pain? Bring it on! Replace my tooth. > 4 Okay, thanks.}","Step onto the yellow flowers and use the wave emote. There will be a cutscene.","Leave through the fairy ring."],"t":"Gnarly"},{"n":"Dramen staff or Lunar staff","r":"4 regular planks (has to be regular planks), 8 nails of any kind, and if you have level 85 Firemaking, 8 willow logs","s":["Talk to General Bre'egth outside of the Zanaris mill, northwest of the fairy ring. {Chat: 3 What's wrong with your mouth?}","Talk to any other Ork about K'Chunk. {Chat: 4 Do you know anything about K'Chunk?}","Run to the fairy ring, talk to Fairy Fixit about K'Chunk. {Chat: 2 What do you know about K'Chunk?}","Teleport to dip and talk to K'Chunk. {Chat: 4 You knocked out Bre'egth's tooth, didn't you?}\n  - Recommended: Bring 4 regular planks and 8 nails of any kind to fix the bridge by using a plank on the broken bridge.\n  - Recommended: Bring 8 willow logs if you have level 85 Firemaking, light the bonfire for K'Chunk and receive 10,000 Firemaking experience.","Pickpocket him for the tooth."],"t":"Bre'egth's Tooth"},{"n":"Dramen staff or Lunar staff and tooth extractor","r":"","s":["Teleport to bkq.","Head down the waterfall to talk to the Wood Dryad to the west. {Chat: 2 Have you seen Gromblod?}","Talk to General Gromblod.","Talk to the Wood Dryad again.","Teleport to clr.","Pick a mango from the mango tree.\n  - Optional: unblock this end of the hollow log if you haven't yet.","Return to bkq.","Talk to Gromblod, giving him the mango, he will spit it out about 15 tiles south of where he is standing. It does not appear as a red dot on the minimap.","Pick up the mango with tooth and use the tooth extractor on it."],"t":"Gromblod's Tooth"},{"n":"Dramen staff or Lunar staff, and tooth extractor","r":"","s":["Teleport to alp and talk to General Shredflesh. {Chat: 4 Can I help with something? > 1 So your tooth is really hurting, is it? > 2 Which tooth is it that's so terribly painful and hurting? > 3 And the pain is very high is it? > 4 I'm a dentist; I can extract it for you!}","In no particular order, calm him with the following responses:\n  - \"What's a bit of pain for a huge ork hero like you?\"\n  - \"If the tooth isn't pulled out, all your teeth will hurt much worse!\"\n  - \"Let me pull it out! What are you, an ork or a goblin?\"\n  - \"I'll make sure it doesn't hurt a bit; I'm a professional.\"","Use the extractor on him.","Clear the pile of rock behind him if you haven't yet already.","Go back and talk to the Tooth Fairy in the hideout.","Turn-on the projector to watch another briefing. {Chat: 5 Okay, thanks.}","She gives you the fairy wand."],"t":"Shredflesh's Tooth"},{"n":"The fairy wand, the 3 teeth and combat equipment. You will not use the fairy wand to fight, but you will need it during the fight to heal the farming patches and the friendly generals. You can also use the fairy wand to access the fairy ring system, so you can bank your Dramen or Lunar staff at this point.","r":"","s":["Prepare for the final battle, with the above listed items.","Teleport to bir, dip, clr, alp. (If the fairy ring at bir does not appear, lobby and start over.)","Look-through the fairy tree where you'll encounter a cutscene.","After the cutscene talk to the Tooth Fairy.","How to kill the Fairy Godfather:\n  - Use all 3 teeth on the farming patches.\n  - Stand by the patches and kill the generals and ork warriors; Prioritise any general using the drum near the rift, to stop new orks from spawning.\n  - Once the teeth have grown, instruct them to fight.\n  - Focus on ork warriors while the teeth focus on killing the generals.\n  - After you and the teeth kill the generals, kill the godfather.\n  - You must let the teeth attack the godfather to reduce the shields. Ensure all 3 teeth are attacking the godfather at once, as each one removes a layer of his 3-layer shield.\n  - If all 3 teeth are not attacking the godfather, you will not land hits as his shield will still be active. The melee tooth will not path around the player if you are in the way.","Talk to the Fairy Godfather for a cutscene.","Continue dialogue with the Fairy Queen and accept her teleport. {Chat: 1 Yes, please teleport me there now.}","Talk to Martin the Master Gardener. {Chat: 2 Talk about farming problems and fairies.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"The final battle"}]},"A Guild of Our Own (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"Lockpick, blackjack, vial of stench (a)","r":"","s":["In a building south-east of Ardougne market, pickpocket the Registrar for a cuckoo clock key.","Get ready, the next steps are time sensitive. You can try again if you fail with no consequence. Make sure to equip a blackjack first.\n  - In the north room, wind the clock on the wall.\n  - Go in the south room, wait for the Registrar to get to the clock room.\n  - Lure, knock out, then steal-from the guard.\n  - Pull the vault lever behind the desk.\n  - Go down the trapdoor that opens, the following steps are no longer time sensitive.","Right-click pick-lock on the vault door.","Right-click check the chest for traps, then open it. You should receive some bonds.","Inspect the boxes under the square hole in the wall to exit. {Chat: 1 Leave the vault.}"],"t":"Guild registry"},{"n":"Bonds (A Guild of Our Own)}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["Bank (recommended) or destroy your vial of stench (a).","Re-enter the building and talk to the Registrar.","Return to Darren Lightfinger. {Chat: 3 I'd like to talk about the caper I'm doing for you.}","Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"A Shadow over Ashdale":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"Decent armour, some food, a gem bag, weapons to deal damage from a distance.","s":["To start, talk to Gudrik, east of Gerrant's Fishy Business in Port Sarim. {Chat: 1 Ask about A Shadow over Ashdale. > Accept}","Talk to him again. {Chat: 1 Can you take me to the island of Ashdale? > 1 Ashdale by night (A Shadow over Ashdale).}","Once you arrive at Ashdale, head north into Lucy's house to speak with her. {Chat: 1 I'm here to help. > 3 Why haven't you tried to leave?}","Enter the storm drain just west of the house."],"t":"Return to Ashdale"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go through in the sewer, killing or running past crassians.","Climb up the ladder at the end of the sewer.","Run west, then south up the stairs. Continue south through Ashdale, through the gate and into the house.","Inspect the bust by the fireplace.","Climb down the staircase. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Sewer raider"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Ignore the crassians and enter the eastern room.","Pick up the valve outer wheel, valve inner wheel and pitch.","Repair the pipe on the ground.","Combine the valve parts to create a valve wheel.","Repair the socket on the central barrel.","Turn the valve wheel on the filled barrel, repeating this process on each of the barrels to move the water through the pipes to open the door.","Continue through and kill the crassian scouts in the next room to open the barrier.","Pull the lever to the south when the crassian warrior isn't looking.\n  - If seen, simply try again.","Do the same with each crassian warrior guarding a lever to kill them.","Optionally loot the chests along the path for some coins and uncut gems.","Run past the scouts."],"t":"Smuggler's cavern"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb on the ship.","Kill the 4 tentacles, moving to avoid their attacks.","Kill Agoroth, ideally from a distance.","Continue dialogue with Lucy and agree to return to Port Sarim. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Continue dialogue with Gudrik and ask for a reward. {Chat: 1 Ask about A Shadow over Ashdale. > 1 Is there a reward?}\n  - The reward requires seven free backpack spaces.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Release the Kraken"}]},"A Soul's Bane":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Launa who is east of Varrock and south of the path leading to Silvarea. {Chat: Accept}","Enter the rift."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Near the entrance is a set of weapons.","Only these weapons will defeat the monsters in this room. Different weapons kill different monsters. Kill monsters until the rage meter at the top of the screen is full. Certain equipment will not allow progress. To be safe, un-equip all gear except the anger weapons.\n  - Anger sword - kills Angry unicorn\n  - Anger spear - kills Angry bear\n  - Anger maul - kills Angry giant rat\n  - Anger battleaxe - kills Angry goblin","Watch the short cutscene.","Enter the exit to the east to proceed."],"t":"Room of Rage"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["'Look-inside' a dark hole, if the fear reaper does not show up right away move onto the next hole that has the 'look-inside' option. Move around the room in a clock-wise rotation until the fear reaper has been killed 5 times.","Continue the process until you receive a cutscene.","After the cutscene, Enter the black hole on the west wall to proceed."],"t":"Room of Fear"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Start attacking a confusion beast, if you do not deal any damage immediately move onto another beast until you find the one that takes damage.\n  - Any confusion beast that you hit will continue to attack you, if you are low combat it is advised to continue hitting a beast until it goes away.","Find and kill the confusion beast 5 times in total in order to proceed.","After all beasts have been killed enter the remaining confusing door for a cutscene."],"t":"Room of Confusion"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill each of the hopeless creatures 3 times.\n  - Eating food will cause the hopeless creature to restore 75% of their life points.","Cross the bridge and 'Use' the exit to proceed."],"t":"Room of Hopelessness"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill all three of Tolna's heads.","Talk to Tolna.\n  - If he doesn't spawn, exit the room and re-enter.","On the surface, talk to Tolna again.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Tolna"}]},"A Tail of Two Cats":{"sections":[{"n":"catspeak amulet","r":"","s":["Equip your catspeak amulet, have your pet cat with you, and talk to Unferth. His house is in eastern Burthorpe, south of Dunstan and east of Tam McGrubor. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Starting the quest"},{"n":"5 death runes","r":"","s":["Speak to Hild in the building north of the Heroes' Guild. She will enchant the catspeak amulet for 5 death runes.","Locate Bob the Cat using the catspeak amulet.\n  - Right-click and \"open\" the amulet.\n  - Click on the whiskers until the arrow and the eyes glow white.\n  - Run in the direction of the arrow, occasionally re-checking the amulet, until you find Bob.\n  - The easiest way to find Bob is to keep hopping worlds in the Carwen Essencebinder Magical Runes Shop in Burthorpe.","Talk to Bob."],"t":"Cathunt"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Ask Gertrude about Bob's parents in her house west of Varrock. {Chat: 4 Ask about Bob's parents.}\n  - If Rat Catchers hasn't been started. {Chat: 5 Ask about Bob's parents.}","Speak to Reldo in the Varrock library. {Chat: 3 Ask about Robert the Strong.}","Go back and talk to Bob the cat again, in the same spot you found him."],"t":"Strong lineage"},{"n":"4 potato seeds, logs, chocolate cake, bucket of milk","r":"","s":["Go to Sophanem and talk to the Sphinx. {Chat: 1 Ask the Sphinx for help. > 2 Skip the cutscene and view summary.}\n  - Talk to Raetul and buy a full desert robe set, if you don't have them already.","Return to Unferth's house in Burthorpe and do the following:\n  - Rake the patch behind his house and plant potato seeds in it. Your cat will notify you when they are done (typically 25–35 minutes to grow). A supreme growth potion from player-owned farm cannot be used to accelerate growth. It will not get disease, and it does not need composting or watering.\n    - If you don't have your cat out, chatbox will tell \"Perhaps I should have a look and see if Unferth's potatoes have grown...\".\n  - Use the logs on fireplace, then light the fireplace.\n  - Use the chocolate cake and bucket of milk on the table.\n  - Make his bed upstairs.\n  - Give Unferth a haircut. {Chat: 2 Cut Unferth's hair}","Talk to Unferth once all the chores are done."],"t":"Memories and Bob's list"},{"n":"vial of water, desert robe outfit, druid's robe outfit or other white robes","r":"","s":["Talk to the Apothecary in south-west Varrock. {Chat: 1 Tell the Apothecary that Unferth is ill. > Any}","Unequip your weapons and equip the doctors hat/nurse hat and your white robes.","Return to Unferth with a vial of water.","Talk to Bob the cat. If he's not at his previous location, locate him again using the catspeak amulet (e).","After the cutscene, talk to Unferth again.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Down with the \"sickness\""}]},"A Void Dance":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak with Commodore Tyr at the Void Knights' Outpost. {Chat: Accept > 1 Why do you need me? > 1 Wait, you're sending Jessika? > 2 Where should I start? > 3 I'm on my way.}","Speak with Captain Korasi."],"t":"Starting"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the Port Sarim docks and speak to Korasi. {Chat: 2 On my way.}","Right-click talk to Captain Tobias, just north of Korasi. {Chat: 2 No, thank you.}","Speak with Gerrant in the fishing shop. {Chat: 1 I'm tracking an escaped animal.}\n  - Or, if Heroes' Quest is complete {Chat: 2 I'm tracking an escaped animal.}","Follow the path pictured right, searching the bushes, plants, and stones.","Finally check the mound.","Return to Captain Korasi at the docks. {Chat: 2 See you there.}","Talk to the Bartender in Port Sarim's pub. {Chat: 2 Bye then.}","Search the piles of junk on the floor at the north-east corner for a key.","Go down the trapdoor in the north-west corner of the pub.","Inspect the suspicious-looking wall on the north side wall.","Open the door to the room south.","Complete the puzzle (follow the steps below, or alternatively, use the image on the right to position the barrels in order to push out the barrow along the red-line path):"],"t":"Pest-y business"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After completing the puzzle, leave the room.","Speak with the Bartender again. {Chat: Any}"],"t":"The Barrel Puzzle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Korasi on the dock. {Chat: 3 To Musa Point, then.}","Travel to Musa Point by paying Captain Tobias, just north of Korasi.","Speak with Zembo in the pub. {Chat: 3 Seen anything odd lately?}","Speak with Shopkeeper Kofi in the general store directly west of the pub.","Take-from the table in the south-west corner of the shop.","Use the chisel on the plank to make a jointed plank and a jointed log.","Use the jointed plank on the jointed log to make a joist.","Use the joist on the Shop wall on the north end of the shop.","Talk to Kofi for a cutscene.","Follow the trail just like the one at Port Sarim.","After Korasi and Jessika appear, search the mound again to get wood shards.","Finish dialogue with them. {Chat: 3 Onwards, then.}","With at least 16 free inventory spaces, head to Rimmington.","Ask Rommik in the crafting shop about the waxwood. {Chat: 1 I need to ask you about waxwood.}"],"t":"Getting hotter..."},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to westernmost building in Rimmington (Chemists's House, long with a green Taskmaster asterisk in it).","Inside, on the Eastern wall, talk to Korasi {Chat: 3 I'll see about this experiment, then.}.","Talk to the Chemist. {Chat: 3 Ask about A Void Dance. > 1 Analyse the sample.}","Analyse the sample by keeping the power and heat at an OK level and keeping the current ingredient as the desired one. {Chat: 2 Analyse the sample.}","When you start to analyse the sample, the in-game table in the top-right shows the combination for how to make each sample. Put the correct secondary sample in the hopper to get the desired sample (top left table).","If you are struggling refer to the full guide for more details."],"t":"Gooey analysis"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Accept Jessika's offer to teleport you to Falador Park. {Chat: 1 Go with Jessika.}","Talk to Korasi or Jessika.","South of the east Falador bank, talk to Ali Tist. {Chat: 2 Yes, I would.}","Attempt-puzzle with the puzzle box.","Return to Korasi or Jessika.","Propose a solution to open the box. {Chat: Any > Any > Any}","Talk to Ali Tist and then to Korasi or Jessika.","On the floor 3 of the western tower of White Knights' Castle, talk to Sir Amik Varze. {Chat: 2 Speak about the A Void Dance quest.}","With the search warrant he gives, go back and talk to Ali Tist. {Chat: 1 I want to examine your stock.}"],"t":"Predicament"},{"n":"Onion}}An onion can be picked from the field nearby the wandering man with a walking stick at the location of Clue #","r":"","s":["Speak with Korasi or Jessika to get a commorb.","You can right click the clue scroll to dig."],"t":"Whodunnit?"},{"n":"","r":"Bring combat equipment to avoid banking before the next section","s":["Try to enter the hatchway and then again to enter the hideout.","Talk to Korasi or Jessika for a second cutscene.","Talk to Korasi or Jessika again for a void drone 'bug'.","Investigate the low box near the door without being caught by the workers to place the drone.","Wait until some workers go by, a cutscene will play.","Investigate the low box to retrieve the drone.","Talk to Jessika.","Pick-pocket a worker walking south from the guarded door.","Knock on the guarded door. {Chat: Any}","Talk to Korasi.","Enter the next room then right-click murder any indentured worker."],"t":"Quick thinking"},{"n":"Combat equipment","r":"","s":["The enemies in next room can drain your prayer points to heal themselves.","Enter the next door. Kill the Black Knight Guardian on your side.","Talk to the pest cage (void leech). {Chat: 4 Enough of this. > Any}","Accept the teleport to the Void Knights' Outpost. {Chat: 1 Go with Korasi.}","Talk to Commodore Tyr for a cutscene.\n  - If you cancel the cutscene, you may need to lobby.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Aftermath":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Adrasteia in the library on the floor 2 of White Knights' Castle in Falador. {Chat: Accept}","Enter Senntisten through the ancient door at the Varrock Dig Site.","Once inside, enter the Zamorakian Undercity by using the nearby pulley lift (a few steps east of the larger-looking pulley used to enter and exit Senntisten). {Chat: 2 Story mode}","Talk to Sir Cadian close to the entry.","Clear the Zamorakian Undercity on any difficulty.\n  - Players who have already cleared it may skip this step."],"t":"To fight a god"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Adrasteia in the library on the floor 2. She is not in the throne room.","Go to the throne room on the floor 3 and talk to Saradomin. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to anyone again to continue the dialogue. {Chat: Any}"],"t":"The edicts re-established"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to the Kharid-et Dig Site and talk to Dr Nabanik. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Nex, Trindine, Wahisietel, or Azzanadra."],"t":"The Zarosians"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Armadyl in his tower south of Falador."],"t":"Armadyl's regret"},{"n":"2 free backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Talk to Adrasteia in the library on the floor 2, not the one in the throne room. {Chat: Any}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"All Fired Up":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to King Roald in Varrock Palace. {Chat: 3 Greet the king. > 1 Oh? Tell me more! > Accept}","Talk to Blaze Sharpeye in Silvarea which is north-east of the Varrock Dig Site and south-west of the Paterdomus Temple on the River Salve. {Chat: 1 Does it matter what type of log I use?}"],"t":"Getting Started"},{"n":"two sets of 20 unnoted logs (each set must be all the same type of log)","r":"","s":["Add-logs to the unlit beacon next to Blaze (requires 20 logs). {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Light the beacon.","Talk to Blaze Sharpeye again. {Chat: 2 Okay.}","Acquire 20 more logs by chopping or banking.","Go north-west to the beacon near the Odd Old Man, add 20 logs and then light it."],"t":"Tending the Beacons"},{"n":"5 unnoted logs of the same type","r":"","s":["Go back and talk to Blaze again. {Chat: 1 Oh, alright, then.}","Add-logs to the beacon (requires 5 logs). {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Blaze. {Chat: Any}","Talk to King Roald. {Chat: 2 Talk about All Fired Up.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing Up"}]},"Alpha vs Omega":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Rasial, the First Necromancer on the bridge in the City of Um. {Chat: Accept}\n  - If Rasial, the First Necromancer isn't there, home teleport to the City of Um or relog.","Talk to Kharen in City of Um to travel to Rasial's Citadel. {Chat: 1 Yes.}\n  - You must talk to Kharen; using the right-click travel option will not start the fight."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Defeat Hermod, the Spirit of War. Cannot be killed with deathtouched dart.","Defeat Rasial, the First Necromancer. Cannot be killed with deathtouched dart.","A cutscene ensues. Continue speaking with Rasial, the First Necromancer."],"t":"The fight"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Death in the City of Um to complete the quest."],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Anachronia base camp tutorial":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Board the Stormbreaker on the west side of River Salve at the Varrock Dig Site.\n  - You may teleport to Varrock or to the Archaeology Campus."],"t":"Set sail"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Complete the intro animations until you wind up at the landing zone.","Follow the directions on the map and investigate the bones blocking your path.","After investigating the second bones, you will be teleported to the base camp."],"t":"Arriving at Anachronia"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Giles in the base camp to begin the tutorial.","Assign at least one worker to gather wood, vines and stone respectively on the base camp management interface.","Continue talking to Giles to skip the wait.","When the base camp management interface appears again, build the Town Hall.","Congratulations, tutorial complete!"],"t":"Safe haven away from monsters"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Manage base camp with Giles in the Town Hall on the eastern side of the base camp. Alternatively, you may attempt to build Anachronia lodestone to open the interface.","Unassign workers and assign 10 workers to gather clay.","Wait for about 20 minutes. You may do anything during this period but you need to board the Stormbreaker to Anachronia if you leave the island.","Manage base camp with Giles again.","Once your workers have collected adequate materials, build the lodestone."],"t":"Building the lodestone"}]},"Ancient Awakening":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Overseer Siv in the Command Centre in the Fort Forinthry. {Chat: 2 Talk about 'Ancient Awakening'. > Accept > Any}","Go north of Fort Forinthry and enter the Wilderness crypt entrance. Pray Protect from Magic against the risen ghosts inside."],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go across the bridge and enter the ancient door.\n  - If the bridge is missing, log out and back in to have it reappear.","Talk to any character near the map table. {Chat: Any > Any > Any}","Collect 20 dragonkin artefacts in the tomb. Kill any tomb zombies that appear, and then collect the artefacts they drop. The zombies are based on your combat level, e.g. 3,200 life points at combat level 152. One can be collected from each Dragonkin artefact hotspot throughout the crypt as well.","Talk to anyone near the map table again. {Chat: Any}"],"t":"Finding artefacts"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the Jolly Boar Inn, south-west of Fort Forinthry. Use the marker to continue the quest at the entrance, then stay on the floor 1.","Talk to Bill at the bar. {Chat: 2 I don't need to know your family history, Bill.}","Go up the staircase, talk to Ellamaria. {Chat: 4 Let's skip the small talk.}","Continue the quest with the marker near the bridge west of the Champions' Guild.","Talk to Aster slightly south. {Chat: 3 I need you to return to the fort.}","Go back to Fort Forinthry, continue Ancient Awakening at the Town Hall.","Talk to anyone in the Town Hall.","Leave through the marker at the entrance to the Town Hall. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Jolly Boar Inn"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Gear up for combat.\n  - Most of the enemies are weak to magic (earth or fire spells)","Go to the Grove east of the fort and interact with the rowboat to travel to Ungael. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Kill all of the attacking monsters.","Talk to the team and make your way north-east up the path.","Interact with the Ruins Entrance.","Go up the stairs to the east, then head west. Interact with the tower entrance. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Watch the cutscene."],"t":"Ungael"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Defeat 12 waves of Zemouregal's minions. After each wave of enemies, you have to activate necrotic energy and sometimes choose a power-up for one of your allies. See the full guide for details on all waves and power-ups.","Watch the cutscene."],"t":"Undead waves"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Aster. {Chat: Any}","Interact with the doorway to the south.","Walk west, then south, then interact with runic projector.","Collect three motes of energy from:\n  - Go north to catch the mote just outside the tower.\n  - Searching bookcase in the north.\n  - Searching ruined pillar in the south-west.","Interact with the runic projector."],"t":"Getting off the island"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Listen to the archivist. {Chat: Any > 2 What is this place? > 3 Tell me about Vorkath. > 4 Tell me about this tomb. > 1 Can you activate this conduit?}","Inspect the mysterious device to the south-east.","Finish the conversation.","Return to Fort Forinthry and continue via the marker in front of the Town Hall.","Talk to anyone in the Town Hall."],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Animal Magnetism":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ava inside the western room of Draynor Manor. {Chat: 1 I would be happy to make your home a better place. > Accept}\n  - To get to her room, a candle sconce (North of the entrance) must be pulled."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"ghostspeak amulet, 20 ecto-tokens","r":"","s":["Talk to Alice at the farm west of the Ectofuntus. {Chat: 4 I'm here about a quest.}","Equip your ghostspeak amulet.","Talk to Alice's husband.","Talk to Alice again. {Chat: 4 I'm here about a quest.}","Talk to Alice's husband.","Talk to Alice again. {Chat: 4 I'm here about a quest.}","Talk to Alice's husband.","Talk to Alice again. {Chat: 4 I'm here about a quest.}","Head to Netty's house east of the Slayer Tower.\n  - If Vessel of the Harbinger is completed, Netty will be at the Last Call in the City of Um.","Unequip the ghostspeak amulet and talk to Netty. {Chat: 2 I'm here about the farmers east of here.}\n  - {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Animal Magnetism.'} if at the Last Call.","Talk to Netty again to receive the altered ghostspeak amulet. {Chat: 1 'Animal Magnetism'.}","Talk to Alice's husband to give him the altered ghostspeak amulet. {Chat: 1 Okay, you need it more than I do, I suppose.}","Talk to him again.","After the cutscene, buy two undead chickens from Alice's husband for 20 ecto-tokens. {Chat: 1 Could I buy those chickens now, then? > 2 Could I buy 2 chickens?}"],"t":"Undead poultry"},{"n":"5 iron bars","r":"","s":["Talk to Ava in Draynor Manor.","Talk to Helda who is also on the western side of the manor and give her five iron bars.","Talk to Helda again to receive the selected iron.","Take the selected iron to the mine north-east of Rimmington (using the Port Sarim lodestone is recommended).","Face north and left click the selected iron to hammer it and make bar magnet.","Talk to Ava."],"t":"Making a magnet"},{"n":"mithril hatchet, holy symbol","r":"","s":["Attempt to cut an undead tree with a mithril hatchet. Undead trees can be found beside the path that leads you to the entrance.","Talk to Ava.","Go to Burthorpe and talk to Turael (or Spria). {Chat: 3 I'm here about a quest.}","Give them a mithril hatchet and holy symbol. {Chat: 3 Hello, I'm here about those trees again. > 1 I'd love one, thanks.}","Attempt to cut another undead tree with the blessed hatchet until you receive some undead twigs.","Talk to Ava."],"t":"Blessed hatchet"},{"n":"hard leather, polished buttons","r":"","s":["Talk to Ava to help her translate the note.","Translate Ava's research notes. The solution is in the image to the right.","Talk to Ava.","Use the pattern with a piece of hard leather and polished buttons to create a container.","Talk to Ava.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Another Slice of H.A.M.":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to either NPC in the north eastern most building on the floor 2 of Dorgesh-Kaan.\n  - Ambassador Alvijar {Chat: Accept}\n    - If Ambassador Alvijar says you might be a human spy, you haven't completed The Giant Dwarf yet.\n    - If you have just completed Death to the Dorgeshuun, you may need to exit to the lobby and re-enter the game for him to appear.\n  - Ur-Tag {Chat: 1 What are you arguing about? > Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["While on the same floor, head west then south until you find a Transportation map ().","Enter the doorway, head south down the tracks and talk to Tegdak (you need 2 free spaces for the specimen brush and trowel).","Use the trowel on the 6 artefacts on the ground to dig them up. They have the same sparkles as time sprite.\n  - If you need more backpack space, you can talk to Tegdak per restored artefact, you don't need to give all in at once.","Use each of them on the specimen table.","Talk to Tegdak and Zanik will be following you after the dialogue.","If Zanik isn't following you, dismiss any pets/familiars and talk to Zanik. {Chat: 1 Yes}\n  - Zanik will now be following you.\n  - If you lose Zanik you will need to return here to retrieve her. (Teleporting will leave Zanik behind)","With Zanik following, exit the train tunnel using the doorway to the north.","Talk to the Goblin scribe, in the building directly west of the quest start point.","In the house just west of the Goblin scribe, climb down the stairs.","Talk to Oldak.\n  - If you have Invention unlocked. {Chat: 2 No - talk about quest or other things.}","You will be teleported to Goblin Village with Zanik, receiving a Dorgesh-kaan sphere in your inventory."],"t":"Artefacts"},{"n":"A ranged, magic or necromancy weapon and its ammunition to defeat 2 H.A.M. members behind object.","r":"You can find a crossbow and 50 bronze bolts on the ground at their location","s":["In Goblin Village, in the northernmost building, talk to either General Bentnoze or Wartface.","After the cutscene, go behind the buildings to the west, go south, then climb up the ladder to the east.\n  - If you attempt to walk around the front of the buildings, you will be stopped by falling arrows.","Kill the H.A.M. Mage and H.A.M. Archer.\n  - A crossbow and 50 bronze bolts can be found on the ground here.","Talk to either General about how to rescue Zanik. {Chat: 2 How can I rescue Zanik?}.\n  - If Recipe for Disaster: Freeing the Goblin Generals was started. {Chat: 3 How can I rescue Zanik?}"],"t":"The Goblin Village"},{"n":"A light source (and a rope if you have never entered the caves from the surface before)","r":"water altar teleport or enlightened amulet","s":["With a light source, head to the Lumbridge Swamp Caves entrance north-west of the Water altar.\n  - If you brought a water altar teleport or Enlightened amulet to teleport to Lumbridge Swamp, use them now for quicker travel.","Talk to Sergeant Slimetoes or Mossfists outside the entrance to the Lumbridge Swamp Caves.","Climb down the dark hole under the tree entering the Lumbridge Swamp Caves.\n  - If you haven't already placed rope in the entrance you will need rope.","Go down the ladder, directly south east of the Climbing Rope.","For the next part, you need to distract the guards by luring them to Slimetoes and Mossfists.\n  - If a guard catches you by getting too close, you will be thrown out to the Lumbridge Swamp Caves.\n  - Finishing the dialogue and waiting allows the first guard to return with the second guard and they should begin fighting the goblins.\n  - Once the 2 guards are fighting the goblins, carefully go towards the south end of the tunnel. (A guard will begin patrolling the tunnel once you get close)\n  - Let the patrolling guard spot you from a distance, then lure the guard to the goblins.\n  - For the final guard blocking the exit, step next to the pillar in his view and he will spot you. Lure him to the goblins.","With the guards engaging the goblins, it is safe to run south to the ladder."],"t":"Infiltrating H.A.M."},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enabling legacy combat for this section can make your fight with Sigmund significantly quicker.","Equip the ancient mace and climb down the ladder.","Initiate combat with Sigmund.\n  - If you have legacy combat enabled, simply use the Ancient Mace's special attack at the start of the fight and finish him however you choose.\n  - If you have do not have legacy combat enabled, use the Ancient Mace's special attack to disable Sigmund's prayers once you reach 100% adrenaline.\n    - The special attack ability can be found in the Constitution ability book or you can click on your adrenaline bar on your main ability bar to use the special attack once at 100% adrenaline.\n    - You can use any combat style you choose once Sigmund's prayer is down.","After defeating Sigmund, untie Zanik.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Sigmund Reloaded"}]},"As a First Resort":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to Oo'glog and talk to Chief Tess. {Chat: 1 What exactly is going on around here? > Accept > 1 So about this 'business venture'.. > 1 Can I help at all?}","Talk to Balnea in the Oo'glog bank. {Chat: 1 Um, yes. So, what's going on around here? > 2 What's the problem? > 1 Okay, I'll bite. Tell me more. > 1 But of course! > 1 Well, why not? I've nothing better to do. > 1 Sure thing.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"10 eucalyptus logs, 8 achey tree logs, 4 spears and 2 raw chompies","r":"","s":["Talk to Chargurr north of the bank. {Chat: 1 I think I could get that stuff for you.}","Talk to Chargurr with 8 achey tree logs and 10 eucalyptus logs in the backpack to add them to the fire pit.","Talk to Chargurr. {Chat: 2 Fine, I'll get some spears for you}","Give her four spears. {Chat: 2 Yes, I'd like to give 4 spears to Chargurr.}","Talk to Chargurr. {Chat: 2 But of course! I'll bring you some chompy birds.}","Use two raw chompies on Chargurr.","Talk to Chargurr.","Light the fire pit.","Talk to Chargurr."],"t":"The food"},{"n":"8 stripy feathers (or a bird snare)","r":"","s":["Talk to Balnea located in the bank. {Chat: 1 Right-ho. I'll go and see Snurgh at the hotel and 'transition' away.}","Talk to Snurgh who is in the easternmost building of Oo'glog. {Chat: 1 Sure, I'll bring you some feathers.}","Give her 8 stripy feathers.\n  - You can obtain the feathers using a bird snare to catch tropical wagtail in the Feldip Hunter area, north of the Oo'glog lodestone.}}"],"t":"The beds"},{"n":"8 larupia furs (tatty or regular) and 4 wolf bones (if you need to trap the larupias, bring a teasing stick)","r":"","s":["Talk to Balnea. {Chat: 1 You're going to ask me to go to the salon, right? > 1 Yeah, sure, I'll go to the salon.}","Talk to Kringk in the building east of the bank. {Chat: 2 Why, sure, I'd be happy to help.}","Give her 4 wolf bones and 8 larupia furs. {Chat: 1 You sure can!}"],"t":"The salon"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Balnea.","Talk to Seegud in the building north-east of the bank.","Head north-east of Seegud to the thermal spring.","Use a pile of eucalyptus logs and a tansymum, on the fire pit nearby.","Light the fire pit. The insects won't disperse.","Talk to Seegud. {Chat: 2 I think I'm a little stuck. > 1 Can you explain what I should be doing again?}","Head back to the spring and talk to Snarrk."],"t":"First trial"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["The \"long brown stone\" always represents eucalyptus logs.","Correct plant and stone combinations are different for every player; you'll need to check and record combinations to solve the puzzle.","You can use the calculator below to mark which stone type represents which plant. Your browser will remember the selections as long as you don't clean browser cache for the wiki.","If you get the message, \"The pungent smell makes the insects disperse\", the combination is correct.","If you get the message, \"The fire has a pungent aroma, but it doesn't seem to have any effect on the insects\", add more logs and a different plant to the fire pit and light them.","Fresh logs are required for each attempt, otherwise you will not disperse the insects even if you find the correct combination.","In the worst case, you need 5 piles of logs and 1 of each plant for the next step.","Move to the thermal bath, north-east of Seegud. There is 'a pile of long brown and yellow egg-shaped stones'. This fire pit requires a pile of eucalyptus logs and one of the five plants in order to disperse the insects. By trial and error, determine which plant is needed for this pool and represents the 'yellow egg-shaped' stones. If done correctly, the swarm of insects above the pool will vanish completely.","In the worst case, you need 4 piles of logs, 4 plants for yellow egg-shaped stone, and 1 of each other plant for the next step.","Move to the mud bath to the east. There is 'a pile of long brown, red sphere and yellow egg-shaped stones'. This fire pit requires eucalyptus logs and two plants. The primary plant of this pool is the same as the plant used at the thermal bath. Figure out the secondary plant by using any of the other four unused plants, until the correct combination is discovered.","In the worst case, you need 3 piles of logs and 3 plants for red sphere stone, 1 of each other plant (except for yellow egg-shaped stone) for the next step.","Move to the salt-water spring west of the thermal bath. There is 'a pile of long brown, red sphere and green gumdrop stones'. This fire pit requires eucalyptus logs and two plants. Be sure to use the secondary plant from the mud bath as the primary plant for this pool. Find the secondary plant by using the three remaining herbs until the correct one is found.","In the worst case, you need 2 piles of logs and 2 plants for green gumdrop stone, 1 of each other plant (except for yellow egg-shaped and red sphere stones) for the next step.","Head west to the yellow sulphur spring. There is 'a pile of long brown, purple tall and green gumdrop stones'. This fire pit requires eucalyptus logs and two plants. Use the secondary plant for the salt-water spring as the primary plant for this spring. One of the two remaining herbs will be the secondary plant, so try them both.","You need 1 pile of logs, 1 plant for red sphere stone, 1 plant for purple tall stone, and 1 unused plant for the next step.","Head to the Bandos pool. There is 'a pile of long brown, red sphere, purple tall and orange squarish stones'. This fire pit requires eucalyptus logs and three plants. Use the secondary plant from the mud bath, the secondary plant from the sulphur pool and the unused herb.","Drop all primweeds and stinkblooms to free up your backpack spaces.","Keep all other unused plants as you will need them in the next task.","After all of the bugs are taken care of, talk to Seegud."],"t":"Finding the correct combinations"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Balnea. {Chat: 1 Sure, anything to avoid talking to you for a while.}","Talk to Chief Tess. {Chat: 1 Talk about As a First Resort quest. > 1 I know how to smoke a trap to remove my scent.}"],"t":"The animals"},{"n":"4 logs and at least 5 fever grass (8 recommended)","r":"","s":["Head to the salt-water spring.","Use the deadfall traps to catch diseased kebbits. To bait the trap, use fever grass on it, then light a fever grass from the inventory and move around.\n  - Catch two from the western and eastern side.","Do this until all four kebbits are caught."],"t":"Kebbits"},{"n":"Bird snare and a few tansymum","r":"","s":["Set up a bird snare west of the bank.","Light a tansymum from the inventory and move around.","Do this until all birds are caught."],"t":"Wimpy birds"},{"n":"Box trap and a few lavender","r":"","s":["Head west of Chief Tess and the sulphur spring.","Set up a box trap.","Burn lavender from the inventory and move around the area.","Once the box shakes, check the trap.","When all four platypodes are caught, head to the north-east corner of the village and release them next to the plants in the water."],"t":"Platypodes"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Dismiss any followers before continuing.","Talk to Balnea and do not skip the cutscene.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Azzanadra's Quest":{"sections":[{"n":"5 free backpack space","r":"Face mask, masked earmuffs, or Slayer helmet, and food","s":["Go up the stairs in Burthorpe Castle. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Azzanadra at the north-west corner. {Chat: Accept}\n  - Before continuing, make sure Azzanadra asks you to meet at Kharid-et Dig Site. Use the quest log if needed.","Travel to Kharid-et Dig Site (use dig sites map or other means) and enter the main fortress. Talk to Azzanadra at the Praetorium war table (not in the Praetorium)."],"t":"Prepare to enter Elder Halls"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to the World Gate and talk to Azzanadra. Teleporting, logging out or going to lobby will require starting this part over from this step.\n  - Use the Sixth-Age circuit to teleport, or run south from the Eagles' Peak lodestone, or teleport to the Outpost with a traveller's necklace and run west.","Equip a face mask or masked earmuffs to protect against volcanic ash. Having a slayer helmet on the slayer helmet stand counts for this.","Enter the World Gate, travelling to the 'Approach' destination (first option). Make sure to finish the dialogue with Azzanadra upon entry.","Head east over the ledges, then up the cliffside.","Continue east, climbing down the drop, then talk to Azzanadra to the south-east. {Chat: 4 Let's just keep going}","Continue north, crossing the stepping stones and up the cliffside.","Continue north, wall run the overhang and talk to Azzanadra again. {Chat: 4 Let's just keep going}","Climb the cliffside, continue west and slide down the slope and head west.\n  - You can heal up by standing under the archway with the glowing crystals.","Continue south, wrapping around east and north, then climb the nearby cliffside which is south of the archway.","Walk across the rock formation and talk to Azzanadra again. {Chat: 4 Let's just keep going}","Continue east and climb down the drop, then traverse the rock bridge to the east.","Talk to Azzanadra again.","Enter the opening."],"t":"Travel through Freneskae"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Azzanadra.","Inspect the fragmented sphere at each end of the halls.","Talk to Ariane back at the centre, she gives you a blank observation. Azzanadra will replace this if you lost yours.","Collect memories from the elder god memory wisps (50 each).\n  - Bik memory wisp (western hallway).\n  - Wen memory wisp (northern hallway).\n  - Ful memory wisp (north-eastern hallway).\n  - Jas memory wisp (south-western hallway).","Inspect the blank observation in your backpack.","Talk to Azzanadra.","Light voice and Shadow voice will speak to you. {Chat: 5 I've heard enough. I have a world to save.}"],"t":"Inside the Halls"},{"n":"Slayer bell","r":"","s":["Travel to White Knights' Castle in Falador and enter the courtyard. Talk to Sir Upticious near the entrance.","Go up the eastern ladder then up the staircase by Sir Renitee to the altar in the castle. Talk to Father Frith. {Chat: Any}","Go to the floor 1, walk one room west from the ladder and talk to Sir Owen. {Chat: Any}","Return upstairs and talk to Father Frith.","Talk to Sir Amik Varze on the floor 3 in the west wing of the castle. {Chat: 1 Ask about 'Azzanadra's Quest'. > Any}","Talk to Padomenes in the courtyard. {Chat: 1 Ask about Azzanadra's Quest. > Any}","Talk to Sir Vyvin, found next to Father Frith on floor 3. {Chat: 1 [Ask about Azzanadra's Quest.]}","Talk to Sir Owen on the floor 1, in the room west of the ladder.","Search the nearby drawers. {Chat: 1 Look for ritual documents.}","Go up the ladder into Sir Renitee's room and crack open the safe.","Right-click the slayer bell and use the 'Cut clapper' option to create a silent bell.","Travel to the Paterdomus and enter the Mausoleum to the north.\n  - Use the Skeletal horror Teleport or invitation box to get there quickly.","Use the bell on the well to create a silent bell (blessed).","Return to Saradomin's throne in the White Knights' Castle by the altar and next to Father Frith on floor 3.","Ring the bell three times, calling Saradomin's name each time. {Chat: 1 Saradomin!}","Speak to Saradomin. {Chat: 3 The world is in danger. > Any > 2 We need to find the eggs. > 1 We need your crown.}","Travel to Kharid-et and talk to Azzanadra at the Praetorium war table. {Chat: ~}"],"t":"Retrieving the crown"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to the Hall of Memories (use the Sixth-Age circuit or memory strands to teleport to Memorial to Guthix)","Enter the pool. {Chat: 1 Yes. > Any > Any}","Capture the 6 Archivist's memories, then talk to the Archivist {Chat: Any > Any}.","Capture the 6 restricted memories.","Interact with each of the plinths in the north-west and north-east.","Search the memory bud in the centre to receive a restricted engram.","Leave the Hall of Memories and use the restricted engram on the fountain of energy."],"t":"Hall of Memories"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to the entrance of the TzHaar City (use the TokKul-Zo to teleport to the main plaza then run south and exit the volcano). You can use the boss portal or the combat portal attuned to TzHaar Fight Cave to get there.\n  - Alternatively, fairy ring BLP is located near the fight cave. From here, leave the city through the exit to the south.","Talk to Trindine on the surface of Karamja Volcano.","Enter the city, talk to Ga'al just north of the entrance. {Chat: Any}","Go north to the main plaza (you can teleport back here using the TokKul-Zo), talk to Trindine.","Talk to TokHaar-Hok.","Travel to the TzHaar City library (north-west of the main plaza), go inside.","Talk to Trindine."],"t":"TzHaar City"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to the Wizards' Tower (use the wicked hood, stardust, or traveller's necklace to teleport)","Talk to Wizard Trindy on floor 1 at entrance of the Wizards' Tower. {Chat: Any}","Search four bookcases to the west.","Talk to Wizard Trindy at the eastern bookcases."],"t":"Wizards' Tower"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Kharid-et Dig Site's praetorium war table.","Talk to Azzanadra."],"t":"Return to Kharid-et Dig Site"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to the entrance of the Heart of Gielinor.\n  - Use The Heart teleport and leave by the wooden lift.\n  - See other fast travel options if not using The Heart teleport.","Talk to Azzanadra.","Enter the Heart {Chat: 1 Yes.} and continue the dialogue.","Observe each of the eggs at the end of the corridors.\n  - Bik's egg.\n  - Wen's egg.\n  - Ful's egg.","Talk to Ariane."],"t":"Gielinor's Elder Halls"},{"n":"blank observation","r":"","s":["Return to Kharid-et and enter to the main fortress. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Walk to the praetorium war table (you need to walk into the room where the table is to start the dialogue).","Stand next to any four shadow anchors around Kharid-et (see the map).","Harvest Trindine wisps until you get 50 memories.","Inspect the blank observation and finish the dialogue or Ga'al will not spawn for the next step.","Return to the TzHaar City main plaza.","Talk to Ga'al in the main plaza.","Return to the Wizards' Tower.","Walk to the entrance to trigger the dialogue.","Return to the Hall of Memories and enter the pool. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to the Archivist.","Return to the Heart of Gielinor (enter from the entrance). {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Ariane. A cutscene will follow. {Chat: Any}","Talk to Ariane again.","Return to the White Knights' Castle, talk to Ariane on the bridge.","A cutscene will follow. {Chat: Any}","Return to Kharid-et, talk to Azzanadra at the praetorium war table to complete the quest.\n  - You need 3 free backpack spaces upon quest completion for the experience lamps rewarded."],"t":"Trindine and Azzanadra's plan"}]},"Back to my Roots":{"sections":[{"n":"soft clay","r":"","s":["Talk to Horacio outside Handelmort Mansion in East Ardougne and accept the quest. {Chat: 2 So... who are you? > 2 Do you need any help? > Accept}","Talk to Wizard Cromperty in his house to the north-east of the market. {Chat: 1 Talk about Back to my Roots}","Talk to an RPDT employee south of the southern bank in Ardougne.","Open the smelly package on the table outside.","Return to Wizard Cromperty. {Chat: 1 Talk about Back to my Roots}","Make a pot lid (any pot lid acquired before this point will not work). The potter's wheel and pottery oven in the north-west area of East Ardougne, Draynor Village or a portable crafter will work.","Return to Wizard Cromperty. {Chat: 1 Talk about Back to my Roots}","Talk to Garth, the farmer located at the fruit tree patch in Brimhaven, north of the Karamja lodestone. {Chat: 2 Talk about the Back to my Roots quest.}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"pot lid, filled plant pot, empty pot","r":"antipoison, anti-poison totem, or other protection/cure from poison","s":["South-east of the nature altar, enter the maze by climbing the vine (north side). Do not leave the maze until you have followed all steps in this section.\n  - Monsters in the maze drop body parts used in One Foot in the Grave. It is highly recommended to collect these during your time in the maze if you also plan to complete this quest.","Navigate the maze to reach the roots using the solution provided.","Once you reach the root, dig the loose soil, cut the root, then use it on your plant pot.","If it does not grow, dig up and cut a different root. Out of the five roots in the area, only one of them can successfully grow. Try a different root until it works.\n  - Fast travelling before covering the plant will destroy the clipping.","Once the correct root takes, use the potted root on your empty pot to make a sealed pot.","If you have not obtained all 6 body parts from One Foot in the Grave, it is highly recommended to do so now.}}"],"t":"Karamja vine maze"},{"n":"a hatchet, or melee weapon with hatchet on tool belt.","r":"antipoison, anti-poison totem, or other protection/cure from poison","s":["Return to Horacio and speak to him.","Use the sealed pot on the east patch to plant the vine.","Attempt to attack the wild jade vine. {Chat: 1 Okay, I'm ready for combat.}","Once killed, cut the remaining vine.","Talk to Horacio.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The battle"}]},"Back to the Freezer":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Chuck in the Ardougne Zoo {Chat: 1 Back to the Freezer Quest > Accept}","Note down the blue text.\n  - Alternatively, the Passphrase may also be found in your quest journal.","In the Rellekka marketplace, talk to Skot or Mundsen.","When prompted, tell them the passphrase from Chuck."],"t":"Start"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After telling the passphrase, finish the dialogue and cutscene.","South-west of Pollnivneach, talk to Dundee, who will give you a crocspeak amulet. {Chat: 1 Ask about the penguins.}","Equip the crocspeak amulet.","Just west, talk to Croc. {Chat: 4 Bye}","South-west, investigate the T.A.R.D.I.S.."],"t":"Desert"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Chuck in Ardougne. {Chat: 1 Back to the Freezer Quest}","Note down the agent's favourite food Chuck tells you. Favourite food may be found in your quest journal.","Return to the T.A.R.D.I.S.","Unequip any item in your cape and weapon slot.","With your clockwork suit in your backpack talk to any named penguin and you will automatically equip your clockwork suit.\n  - If you don't have a clockwork suit with you return to the zoo and speak with Chuck. Chuck will give you a clockwork suit.","In order, talk to the following penguins:\n  - Emperor Wing {Chat: 1 Remind me what happened. > 2 What happened to you at the party?}\n  - Elon {Chat: 2 What happened to you at the party?}\n  - Hugh {Chat: 2 What happened to you at the party?}\n  - Gordon {Chat: 2 What happened to you at the party? > 3 Are you a spy?}","Gordon will give you a G.P.S.. If he does not, simply talk to him again.","Walk to the edge of the icy patch to get out of the clockwork suit.}}"],"t":"The secret-secret agent"},{"n":"Ice cooler","r":"","s":["Head to the pier north of Fremennik Province lodestone and north-east of Rellekka, travel to the Iceberg via the smaller boat.","Locate with the G.P.S., follow the directions until you find the Mysterious Hatch.","To the north-east, right click Jim the polar bear and choose \"Tuxedo-Time\".","Interact with the hatch and type in \"1234\" to enter.","Enter the north-east room and search the interactable cupboard on the north wall for a hat.","Exit the room and then follow the corridor south.","Head west and take the first turn north. Enter the large door leading to the large room in the centre of the bunker.","Enter the locker room to your west and search Gordon's locker on the west side for the de-lore-ing device parts list and de-lore-ing device (incomplete).","Exit the large door to go back to the main corridor","Enter the southwest room full of crates and search or look in them until you find both a hammer and flax.","In the north-western most room, Peruse the ice shelf (looks like a normal shelf) for The Penguin Book of Gielinor.","Behind you, Get Ice from the Ice Maker by the door to take ice cubes.","Use the hammer on the ice cubes to create the flax cap-ice-i-tor.","Use the flax cap-ice-i-tor on the de-lore-ing device (incomplete) for the de-lore-ing device.","Operate the de-lore-ing device."],"t":"The secret bunker"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take the monkey wrench (north & slightly east), use it on the de-lore-ing device then operate the device again.","Take the penguin bongos and cowbells in the north-west corner, use either on the device, operate the device again.","Pick cabbage, use it on the device, operate the device again.","Speak to the man with a dragon pickaxe, use worthless old boots on the device, operate the device one last time."],"t":"Time travelling!"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Gordon in the south-western room.","Talk to Elon in the centre of the bunker.","Get the fishing rod from the corner of the War room south of the big door.","Go to the 'cold storage' crate room in the southwest and search until you have both the cog and coolant holder.","Use the cog on the fishing rod to create the 'fishvention' rod.","Go to the western room and gather Pure S-now - wait until you have gathered all 2,000. (Process takes about a minute)","Search the crate north of the Mysterious Ice Block in the same room for a lemon.","Use the Mysterious ice block in the room to craft 2000 lemon sole runes.","Go to the north-western room and click on the Ice Maker twice to create cool-ant and an ice box.","Talk to Buzz who is in the prison in the eastern room for 21 killerwatt energy.","Leave the bunker via the door to the north.","Walk east, talk to Jim the polar bear to exit your disguise. {Chat: 1 Yes}}}"],"t":"Back in the bunker"},{"n":"Insulated boots","r":"","s":["Make your way to the top floor of Draynor Manor (staircase then ladder).","Enter the eastern room, then the Interdimensional Rift.","Kill 10 Killerwatts until you have 121 killerwatt energy.}}"],"t":"Getting Energy"},{"n":"50 of each: bright, flickering, gleaming, and sparkling energy","r":"","s":["Return to the iceberg.\n  - Head to a pier north of Fremennik Province lodestone and north-east of Rellekka, travel to the Iceberg via the smaller boat.","Head to north-east of the iceberg, talk with Jim the polar bear, right click \"Tuxedo-Time\".","Re-enter the bunker via the Mysterious Hatch.","In the centre of the bunker, talk to Elon to give him all the items.","Fill the energy container to the north-west with your divination energy.","Configure the battery control station, north-west.","Solve the puzzle. See the full guide for advice on solving the puzzle.","Once complete, speak to the following penguins, in order:\n  - Elon, in the same (central) room, roaming around T.A.R.D.I.S.\n  - Gordon, in the south-west room (northern part).\n  - Hugh roaming around the north-west room.\n  - Emperor Wing, in the central room again, easy to recognise due to his size.","Click the T.A.R.D.I.S. in the centre for a cutscene.","Return to Chuck. {Chat: 1 Back to the Freezer Quest}","Quest complete!}}"],"t":"Returning to the iceberg"}]},"Bar Crawl (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"Games necklace for quick travel to the Barbarian Outpost}}{{Checklis","s":["Talk to barbarian guard located east of Barbarian assault. {Chat: 1 I want to come through this gate. > 2 Looks can be deceiving, I am in fact a barbarian. > Accept}","Bars are marked with on the world map. It may be helpful to turn off other map icons so that it is easier to locate the bars during the miniquest.}}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"208 gold coins, barcrawl card","r":"Unlocked multiple lodestones on the lodestone network, grand seed pod, games necklace, restore potions & food","s":["If you lose/drop your barcrawl card, you will have to start the entire miniquest all over again.","You can visit the bars in any order. None of the beers are physical items, they're consumed automatically.","Go to the floor 2 of the Grand Tree and talk to Blurberry. {Chat: Any} You can use Home Teleport to Al Kharid and then take the Gnome Glider to the Tree Gnome Stronghold, Ardougne lodestone and run north-west, or Eagles' Peak lodestone with 61 Agility and head east.","Home Teleport to Seers' Village, and then visit the Forester's Arms. Talk to the Bartender. {Chat: 3 I'm doing Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl.}","Home Teleport to Ardougne, then proceed to the Flying Horse Inn, located directly north of Ardougne castle. Talk to the Bartender. {Chat: 3 I'm doing Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl.}","Home Teleport to Yanille, and then visit the Dragon Inn. Talk to the Bartender. {Chat: 4 I'm doing Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl.}","Home Teleport to Karamja. Run north and then east until you reach the Dead Man's Chest. Talk to the Bartender. {Chat: 4 I'm doing Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl.}","Home Teleport to Port Sarim. Run north-east to the Rusty Anchor. Talk to the Bartender. {Chat: 1 I'm doing Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl.}","Run south and 'Pay Fare' to Captain Tobias just east of the lodestone. Run west to the pub and talk to Zembo. {Chat: 3 I'm doing Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl.}","Home Teleport to Varrock and run north to the Blue Moon Inn. Talk to the Bartender. {Chat: 4 I'm doing Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl.}","Home Teleport to Fort Forinthry and head south-west to the Jolly Boar Inn. Talk to the Bartender. {Chat: 4 I'm doing Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl.}","Home Teleport to Falador and go to the Rising Sun Inn. Talk to Emily or Kaylee. {Chat: 2 I'm doing Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl.}","Return to the Barbarian Outpost, ideally by using a games necklace, and talk to the Barbarian guard.","Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Visiting the bars"}]},"Battle of Forinthry":{"sections":[{"n":"Combat weapon, equipment, and supplies, food (a Beast of Burden is allowed if more food is needed)","r":"","s":["Talk to the Raptor in Fort Forinthry. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Battle of Forinthry'. > Accept > 1 Yes, I am ready.}","Watch the cutscene.","Begin Encounter with Fort Forinthry Gate."],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Run north to the camp with an undead giant.","Kill the undead giant. The other enemies are optional.","Disrupt the place of power.","Head west.","Kill the undead giant. The other enemies are optional.","Disrupt the place of power.","Head south.","Kill the undead giant. The other enemies are optional.","Disrupt the place of power.","Defeat the Zemouregal & Vorkath encounter.\n  - Pray Protect from/Deflect Necromancy.\n  - Drink 1 dose of super antifire.\n  - First use of extra action Ballista after Vorkath lands.\n  - Dive, Surge, or Escape during Vorkath's AoE (10x10 area).\n  - Second use of extra action Ballista when the Raptor mentions \"Ready the Balista\"\n    - Use Balista as often as possible after this.\n  - Target Zemouregal only after killing Vorkath."],"t":"The battle"},{"n":"4 empty backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Talk to the Raptor, near the Guardhouse.","Talk to guard captain Sofía or Overseer Siv in the Guardhouse.","Talk to Aster or Bill in the Command Centre.","Talk to Oak or Zoe east of the Command Centre.","Talk to Copperpot, Father Flint or Granny Rowan in the Chapel.","Talk to Princess or Rodney in the Kitchen.","Talk to the Raptor, near the Guardhouse.","Talk to Bill in the Town Hall.","Head east of the Kitchen and collect 4 stone wall segments from the pile of stone.","Fully repair the fortifications with the 4 repair hotspots to the west, north of the broken Workshop.","Talk to Aster, Overseer Siv, or Rodney in the Town Hall. {Chat: 1 Yes, begin the feast.}"],"t":"Wrapping up"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Raptor, near the Guardhouse.","Enter floor hatch to the east of the Command Centre.","Talk to Zemouregal in his prison cell. {Chat: Any}"],"t":"The aftermath"}]},"Battle of the Monolith":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Each of the battles can last around 10 minutes.","Position your allies in the positions indicated for each battle, then start the battles.","It is recommended to train skills at the bank chest during the battles to make good use of time."],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ali the Wise or Wizard Trindy found north west of the mysterious monolith (Archaeology Guild). {Chat: accept}","Move Thaerisk Cemphier, Commander Zilyana, and Helwyr south-west of the barricade.","Press the start button to begin the battle."],"t":"First battle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ali the Wise.","Move Helwyr and Nex just inside the southern barricade.","Move Zilyana and Thaerisk just inside the northern barricade.","Start the battle."],"t":"Second battle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Wizard Trindy or Ali the Wise. {Chat: 3 The TokHaar?}","Head to the Fight Kiln and enter it. {Chat: 1 The Battle of the Monolith.}","Return to the Archaeology Guild and talk to Ali the Wise again. {Chat: 1 Begin the third battle.}","Move Helwyr and Commander Zilyana just outside the northern barricade of the Gower farm.","Move Thaerisk and Nex just outside the southern barricade of the Gower Farm.","Move the 3 TokHaar just outside the Varrock east gate.","Start the battle."],"t":"Third battle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ali the Wise.","Move Helwyr to the southern barricade.\n  - Helwyr is located west of the south barriers.","Move Thaerisk and Nex to the crossroads outside Varrock's east gate. (Sometimes an enemy can slip the crossroads defence and start attacking the north-western barricade.)\n  - Nex is located south-east of Varrock.","Move Commander Zilyana to the northern barricade.","Start the final battle."],"t":"Fourth Battle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ali the Wise for a cutscene. {Chat: 3 Leave. > 1 Yes!}}} Quest Complete!"],"t":"Aftermath"}]},"Beneath Cursed Tides":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Wizard Myrtle at the fountain near the entrance to the Wizards' Tower. (Fairy ring DIS) {Chat: 2 [Continue] > Accept > 1 I know Vannaka!}","Go to the Edgeville Mausoleum just south of the bank and talk to Vannaka. {Chat: 1 Talk about Beneath Cursed Tides. > 4 [Continue...] > 1 Yes, I do.}","Return to the Wizards' Tower, and talk to Wizard Myrtle. {Chat: 2 What's the plan then? > 1 How do I get to Mudskipper Point?}","Make your way to Mudskipper Point. The fastest route is via fairy ring AIQ. Alternatively, you can run south from the Port Sarim lodestone.","Unequip your weapons and dismiss followers and then talk to Wizard Myrtle. {Chat: 1 Sounds perfect, let's do this! > 2 I'd like to dive to the sunken island. > 1 Yes, I'm ready.}\n  - If you have completed the Recipe for Disaster: Freeing Pirate Pete subquest, or have built any kind of diving suit in the Aquarium. {Chat: 1 Sounds perfect, let's do this. > 1 Underwater breathing spell. > 2 I'd like to dive to the sunken island. > 1 Yes, I'm ready.}","East of the room, read the message in the bottle for the key and open the door."],"t":"The sunken island"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Brynna, the survival expert (directly to the south).","Catch two raw shrimps.","Gather the seaweed nearby.","Cut a tree to get a soggy branch.","Interact with the boulder.","Cook both shrimp on the steam vent (two squares west of the boulder) to receive two boiled shrimps.","Push the boulder (next to the steam vent) to get it hot enough to burn the shrimp next.","Boil 1 shrimp again to burn it. Keep one boiled shrimp.","Talk to Brynna twice.","Continue through the west gate.","Go to the building to the west and talk to the master chef.","Go to the large jellyfish south-east of the chef's house and play the music box. {Chat: 2 Turn second handle. > 3 Turn third handle. > 1 Turn first handle.}","Gather tasty seaweed.","Talk to the master chef again.","Prepare the large table 3 times by matching the 3 tastes with 3 ingredients (large table is in the same house).}} :{| class=\"wikitable lighttable align-center-1 align-center-2 align-center-3\" ! Recipe Number ! Recipe ! Solution |- | First | Sweet, Sour, Spicy | 1 up, 2 up, 3 up |- | Second | Mellow, Sour, Bitter | 2 down, 2 up, 3 down |- | Third | Spicy, Salty, Bitter | 3 up, 1 down, 3 down |}"],"t":"Krillinary expert"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Continue through the west door to the small house in the north.","Climb down the ladder.","Talk to mining instructor. {Chat: 1 Absolutely! > 3 Good bye.}","Mine soggy copper ore and soggy tin ore.","Add the ores to furnace.","Right click and close the doors.","Operate the pump and light the furnace.","Retrieve the bronzish bar from the furnace.","Smith a bronze dagger.","Talk to the mining instructor again.","Continue through the east gate.","Talk to Vannaka, the combat instructor. {Chat: 1 Sure, I'm up for a challenge. > 2 Let's get on with the task.}","Open the gate and click on the sword in the middle of the room to begin combat training.","Click on the rats and other elements bouncing on the screen.","Exit the cage and climb the ladder to the north-east."],"t":"Mining and combat"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the financial advisor in the house directly to the east. {Chat: 1 Can we skip to the task?}","Enter the vault (the code is 139).","Talk to the financial advisor again."],"t":"Fishy business"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Leave through the 2 doors to the east.","Head south to the church through double doors.","Talk to Brother Brace.","Read the friend list.","There will be 2 fish just east of the bank and 3 fish back through the 2 doors leading through the bank.","One of the five fish will tell you where the book is. Search for it.","Give the book to Brother Brace.","Go through the south door to the south-east building and talk to Wizard Terrova. {Chat: 1 I certainly am. > 1 Can you give me some runes to cast this 'strike of air'?}","Attack a chicken.","Talk to the wizard."],"t":"Fishy friends and magic"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pick any option during the cutscene.","Channel the spell while repelling Crassians.","Finish Hector Vivian.","Talk to Wizard Myrtle. {Chat: 1 We did it!}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Commotion in the ocean"}]},"Beneath Scabaras' Sands":{"sections":[{"n":"Four free backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Enter the Golden Palace in Menaphos. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Pharaoh Osman, Chosen of Tumeken. {Chat: Accept}","Go across the bridge east of the Menaphos lodestone into Sophanem and talk to the High Priest. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Beneath Scabaras' Sands'.}","Go to Pollnivneach and talk to Hakeem the Mayor. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Beneath Scabaras' Sands'.}","Go to Nardah and talk to Awusah the Mayor. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Beneath Scabaras' Sands'.}","Go to Al Kharid and talk to Emir Ali Mirza in the Al Kharid palace. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Beneath Scabaras' Sands'. > Any}"],"t":"Collecting reports"},{"n":"Report: Al Kharid, report: Nardah, report: Pollnivneach, and report: Sophanem","r":"Food, combat gear, and means to avoid poison such as antipoisons","s":["Enter the Golden Palace in Menaphos. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Kill the 4 Profane Scabarites and burst the 4 corrupted scarabs nearby.","Head down the steps near the Menaphos lodestone and kill the 4 Profane Scabarites and burst the 4 corrupted scarabs.\n  - The Profane Scabarites and corrupted scarabs from the previous step must be dealt with for the ones on the lower level to spawn.","Head back up to the palace and talk to Commander Akhomet.","Enter the Golden Palace and talk to Pharaoh Osman, Chosen of Tumeken."],"t":"Under attack!"},{"n":"any restored Zarosian artefact and 4 free backpack spaces","r":"15 free backpack spaces","s":["Enter the Grand Library. {Chat: 1 Beneath Scabaras' Sands}","Talk to Kohnen's assistant. You do not need to follow the assistant, and can just run ahead to Leela and Maisa who are in the south-western corner (down two levels, yellow dot on the minimap).","Talk to Leela or Maisa.","Search the nearby bookcases until you obtain The Shiny Scarab.\n  - The location can be different for each player.","Talk to Leela or Maisa again.","Enter the Uzer Mastaba. {Chat: 1 Head directly to the Pharaoh Queen.}\n  - You may use fairy ring DLQ.","Talk to Senliten.","Talk to Lead Archaeologist Kerner in the ruins of Uzer.","Talk to Lead Archaeologist Kerner again. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Gather scorched sand from any of the nearby locations. Continue screening the sand with the screening tray until you have 30 Kharidian gold and 2 ancient rubies.","Restore the damaged golden scarab with the nearby archaeologist's workbench.","Return and enter the Golden Palace {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"The hunt for the golden scarab"},{"n":"Golden scarab and 2 free backpack spaces","r":"15 free backpack spaces, food, combat gear, and means to avoid poison such as antipoisons","s":["Talk to Pharaoh Osman, Chosen of Tumeken.","Talk to Leela just outside the northern gates of Menaphos.","Release the golden scarab.","Follow the golden scarab at the locations indicated on the map on the right until you reach the Scabarite Cavern.\n  - Teleporting directly to the cavern will not work.\n  - Don't miss the final golden scarab spot directly in front of the cavern. Doing so will cause you to have to repeat the entire path from Menaphos.","Enter the cave entrance. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Head south and follow the golden scarab once more.","Scavenge the piles of debris in the cavern until you have five sets of boat materials. If a Profane Scabarite appears, it must be killed to obtain the materials. Teleporting out will result in loss of materials.","Repair the old boat.","Travel with the old boat.","Head east and up the steps and talk to Scabaras.","Go back down the steps and interact with Fear. You need to keep interacting with Fear to scare it up the steps to Scabaras. Guide it up the northern side of the steps as it is more likely to get stuck on the southern side.\n  - Only use the guide going up the first two stairs, after that, it is not accurate!","Go through all options during the flashback. Scabaras will expect a specific response to each of his three statements, and the order is random for each player.\n  - \"Mention of his children would have given him pause.\" {Chat: 3 Amascut and Icthlarin are not ready.}\n  - \"What if we had proposed an alternative?\" {Chat: 1 There has to be another way.}\n  - \"What would Lady Elidinis have thought?\" {Chat: 2 What insight has Lady Elidinis provided?}","Following the cutscene, continue through the dialogue. {Chat: Any}","Interact with Ego at the bottom of the steps.","Pick from a cavern dwellberry bush near the old boat. Filling your backpack with several is helpful, but only one cavern dwellberry is needed if you're picking it back up just after dropping them in the next step.","Drop the cavern dwellberries to lure Ego up the steps.\n  - Ego can only be lured within five game squares.","Go through all options during the second flashback.\n  - \"Taking a firmer stance against her transgression may have dissuaded her.\" {Chat: 1 That is unacceptable!}\n  - \"What if we had challenged her perspective?\" {Chat: 2 Your father sought to protect you.}\n  - \"What if we had placated her?\" {Chat: 3 You are right.}","Following the cutscene, continue through the dialogue.","Interact with Melancholy at the bottom of the steps and use the chat options to motivate the scarab to make it move up the steps repeatedly. Go through all chat options until it moves from each stop."],"t":"Discovering the temple"},{"n":"Three free backpack spaces","r":"Food, combat gear, and means to avoid poison such as antipoisons","s":["After the third flashback, head down the steps to find Grief.\n  - Grief appears as a red dot on the minimap.","Keep stamping out Grief until it transforms into a level 146 monster.","Defeat the monster.","Talk to Scabaras. {Chat: 1 Ask about Amascut's plan. > 5 Continue Quest.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Stomping out the grief"}]},"Benedict's World Tour (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Benedict in a house north-west of the Varrock lodestone. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to Varrock Palace. Go to the north-west staircase and then to the top floor to collect the fox pelt.","Head to the roof of Al Kharid Palace and collect the toffee apple.","Head to Het's Oasis and go to the statue in the centre to collect the package.\n  - Teleport there with a ring of duelling. {Chat: 1 Het's Oasis}\n  - If you are below 65 Agility, run north around the whirligig pool to cross the fallen palm tree, which has no Agility requirement.","Enter the low-level Runespan portal to collect the crystal to the south-west (on the same island you start on).\n  - Teleport there with the wicked hood or stardust.","Head to Mudskipper Point and head south-west to collect the toy ship.\n  - Use a fairy Ring aiq or the Port Sarim lodestone to teleport there","Head to the floor 3 of Lumbridge Castle and collect a pipe by the north stairs.","Head to the west side of the White Knights' Castle in Falador, and climb the stairs and ladders to the roof to collect a monocle.","Head to the beacon south of Paterdomus to collect a scarf.\n  - Teleport there with either the Skeletal horror Teleport, an invitation box, a Fort Forinthry Teleport, an Archaeology journal.\n  - Alternatively, teleport there with a Dig Site pendant to the Varrock Dig Site. {Chat: 1 Digsite}","Teleport to Ashdale lodestone and head directly south to collect the surgical mask."],"t":"All players"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to White Wolf Mountain and collect the raw fish-like thing, which is right next to the glider.\n  - Ride on the gnome glider of Captain Dalbur from Al Kharid. {Chat: 2 Sindarpos}","Head to the Grand Tree and head south of the floor 3 to collect a flask of tea.\n  - Ride on the gnome glider. {Chat: 1 Ta Quir Priw}\n  - Alternatively, teleport via spirit trees.","Head to Castle Wars, then head north-west of the portals, and walk on to the spectating wall to collect the sweets.\n  - Teleport with a ring of duelling. {Chat: 2 Castle Wars Arena}","Enter the Polypore Dungeon and go slightly east to collect cinnamon, which is next to the neem drupe branch.\n  - Use a fairy Ring bip to teleport there.\n  - Alternatively, the Dungeoneering cape teleport (0, 7) or\n  - Delver's anklet (3) can be used.","Head to the top floor of the Sorcerer's Tower north-east of Ardougne to collect a money pouch.","Teleport to Anachronia lodestone to collect the foot slightly south-east of the lodestone.","Head west of the Menaphos gates to pass through the world window and continue slightly north to collect the frogburger.\n  - If you did not finish the dialog with Benedict, talk to him again to complete the miniquest.","Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Members-only"}]},"Between a Rock...":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Dondakan the Dwarf about cannonballs in the Keldagrim south-west mine. {Chat: 2 Why are you firing a cannon at a wall? > 1 So why were you trying to get through the rock again? > 1 Sounds interesting! > Accept > 3 I'll be back later.}","In the western half of the Keldagrim Palace (the big building in the centre of Keldagrim) floor 1, talk to the Dwarven Engineer."],"t":"The dwarven scholar"},{"n":"A few empty backpack spaces","r":"A weapon of any kind to kill low-level scorpions and mining gear","s":["Teleport to the Falador lodestone and run north-east to the Dwarven mines (stay outside)\n  - Teleport using the skull sceptre and run west.\n  - Or teleport to the Invention Guild and run directly east.","Talk to Rolad, who is located in the most north-eastern building near the ladder to the mines. There is a pause in the dialogue; be sure to finish the whole conversation.","Go down the ladder to enter the Dwarven mines.","Kill scorpions in the southeast to get the first page. It will appear in your backpack.","Search the mine carts just to the north for the second page. They may also be in the mine carts just south of the ladder you entered the dungeon from.","Mine any ore rocks in the mine to find the last page (the rocks in the resource dungeon connected to the mine do not work).","Return to Rolad {Chat: 1 Of course.} and read the book. Don't destroy the book yet.\n  - If you don't have an ammo mould for the next step, it can be bought from Nulodion for 5 coins. The ammo mould can be stored on your tool belt.}}"],"t":"Arzinian Avatar"},{"n":"gold bar and ammo mould (tool belt works)","r":"","s":["Return to Dondakan in the Keldagrim south-west mine. Talk to him, and then use a gold bar on him.","Head to any furnace with an ammo mould and make a golden cannonball.\n  - There is a furnace in the west side of the Keldagrim Palace.","Return to Dondakan and use the golden cannonball on him. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm sure this will crack open the rock. > 1 So you want to... fire me into the rock? > 2 I can't argue with that, shoot me in!}"],"t":"Yellow stones"},{"n":"3 gold bars (must be in the backpack, metal bank does not work)","r":"","s":["Read the dwarven lore book to find a piece of base schematics. {Chat: 1 Yes.}\n  - If you lost the book, you may speak to Rolad.","Teleport to the Taverley lodestone, run north and enter the cave by the tree patch.","Go to the bar inside the Dwarven Tunnel and talk to Khorvak, a dwarven engineer. {Chat: 1 No, I've had enough of buying drinks for people!}","Talk to the Dwarven Engineer on the west side of the floor 1 of the Keldagrim Palace (the same one you went to earlier) for another part of the schematics.","Assemble on any of the schematics.","Move around (and rotate if needed) the pieces, referring to finished schematics pictured right.","Smith a gold helmet on the anvil in the same room which requires three gold bars by using a gold bar on the anvil. {Chat: 1 Gold helmet}\n  - If you are proceeding or completed Legends' Quest. {Chat: 2 Gold helmet}"],"t":"Cannon ergonomics"},{"n":"gold helmet, 6-15 backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Prepare to fight a level 50-56 enemy, along with your gold helmet.","Return to Dondakan, equip your gold helmet and ask him to shoot you into the rock. {Chat: 1 You may fire when ready!}\n  - During the cutscene, click directly on the text \"Click to continue\", clicking anywhere else will exit and restart the cutscene.","Once inside the cave, do not remove the gold helmet or you will have to restart.","Mine at least 6 gold ores, which is required to damage the enemy, and keep them in the backpack. The more ores mined (up to a maximum of 15), the lower its combat level.","Jump-through the first wall of flames and right-click talk on the next ring of fire.","Kill the Arzinian Avatar.","Speak to Dondakan.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Striking gold"}]},"Big Chompy Bird Hunting":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Rantz east of Feldip Hills. {Chat: 3 How do I make the 'stabbers'?. > Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Chop down two Achey Trees.","Craft ogre arrow shafts from the logs.","Use feathers on the ogre arrow shafts.","Obtain some wolf bones. There are some wolves just south-west of Rantz, by the swamp.","Craft wolf bone arrowheads from the wolf bones.\n  - Be careful not to bury the bones.","Use the wolf bone arrowheads on the shafts.","Use 6 ogre arrows on Rantz."],"t":"Fletching some arrows"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Ask Rantz all possible questions. {Chat: 1 How do we make the chompys come? > 2 What are 'fatsy toadies'? > 3 Where do we put the fatsy toadies? > 4 What do you mean 'sneaky..sneaky, stick da chompy?' > 5 Ok, thanks.}","Enter the cave north of Rantz.","Unlock the Locked Ogre chest in the north-west corner, then search it to receive ogre bellows.","Exit the cave and run a short distance south-west to the swamp.","At the swamp, fill bellows via the swamp bubbles, then bloat 3 nearby swamp toads for 3 bloated toads."],"t":"Bloated toads"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Remove any Armour/Augmented Armour this will stop you from killing Chompy","Talk to Rantz.","Drop a bloated toad where the arrow points and wait for a chompy to appear.\n  - You may need to drop more toads if the bird doesn't spawn.","Talk to Rantz after the chompy appears.","Wait until Rantz has fired his bow and missed the bird, then talk to him.","Convince him to let you try shooting the bird instead. He'll give you an ogre bow. {Chat: 2 Come on, let me have a go... > 1 I'm actually quite strong...please let me try.}","Place another toad in the clearing.\n  - Alternatively, you can kill the same chompy bird, if it has not left.","Kill the chompy bird that appears with the ogre bow.","Pluck the carcass and take the raw chompy.","Talk to Rantz. Take note of the specific ingredient he wants on the chompy"],"t":"Hunting"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go back into the cave and talk to Fycie and Bugs. Take note of the specific ingredients they want on the chompy, all are possible but not necessarily needed.","Obtain the ingredients that they ask for and use the raw chompy on the spit-roast north of Rantz.\n  - In case you forgot the ingredients, using the raw chompy on the spit-roast will list them out.","Talk to Rantz.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Cooking the bird"}]},"Biohazard":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Elena in a house just west of the East Ardougne north bank, across the river. {Chat: Accept}","Talk to Jerico, who is in the building south of the Ardougne north bank.","Search the cupboard in Jerico's house for some bird feed.","Go to the outside eastern wall of Jerico's house and pick up a pigeon cage.","Go back across the river, west of the castle to the West Ardougne gate.","Use bird feed on the watchtower fence (the spears, highlighted in red on your minimap) where several Mourners are perched above.","Open the pigeon cage.","Go south along the wall and talk to Omart. Make sure to finish the dialogue {Chat: 1 Okay, Let's do this}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the east side of Martha Rehnison's house, highlighted in the picture (do not enter the house), north-west of where you breached the wall.","Take the rotten apple on the east outside of the house.","Squeeze through the gap in the metal fence directly east of the rotten apple.","Use the rotten apple on the cauldron in front of you. Make sure you right click it, as the left click option is to eat it."],"t":"Mourner Headquarters"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to Nurse Sarah's house in the corner, south-west of the church.","Search the box on the north side of the house to obtain a doctors' gown.","Equip the gown.","Go to the north-east corner of the city and enter the Mourner Headquarters.","Open the door to the west and go upstairs.","Open the door to the east and kill a Mourner to obtain a key that automatically goes into your inventory.","Use the key on the gate in front of you to get into the caged room.\n  - You can dispose of the key now","Search the crates in the caged room to find the distillator.","Teleport back to the Ardougne lodestone.","Talk to Elena in a house just west of the East Ardougne north bank, across the river."],"t":"Infiltration"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Without teleporting, go to a bank and deposit your plague sample. Teleporting with the plague sample in your inventory will destroy it, forcing you to retrieve another sample from Elena.","Teleport to Falador and go to the west bank to retrieve the three vials and the plague sample.","Go south to Rimmington.\n  - (Optional) requires level 5 Agility. Head southwest and climb over the crumbling wall.\n  - (Optional) requires level 26 Agility. Head south and climb into the underwall tunnel.","Enter the westernmost house in Rimmington and talk to the Chemist. (Do not mention that you have the sample or he will take it away from you, and you will be forced to go back to Elena to get a new one. Also, do not give the wrong vial as it will force you to go back and get new ones). {Chat: 3 Ask about Biohazard. > 2 It's ok, I'm Elena's friend. > 2 I just need some touch paper for a guy called Guidor.}","At the fire outside the house talk to Chancy. {Chat: 2 You give him the vial of liquid honey...}","Talk to Da Vinci. {Chat: 1 You give him the vial of ethenea...}","Talk to Hops. {Chat: 3 You give him the vial of sulphuric broline...}","Make sure to bank sample before teleporting. You can quickly bank the sample by running east and attempting to charter a ship to Entrana by right-clicking one of the monks.","Teleport to Varrock."],"t":"Samples"},{"n":"Touch paper, Plague sample, Priest gown top, Priest gown bottoms","r":"","s":["Go to the bank and get the plague sample.","Go through the gate in the south-east corner of Varrock.","Talk to the 3 chemist's assistants at the Dancing Donkey Inn to get the vials back.","Equip the priest gown top and bottoms now.","Go to the building south-east of the pub and go inside.","Talk to Guidor, tell him you are sent by Elena, and give him the samples. {Chat: 1 I've come to ask your assistance in stopping a plague. > 2 I've been sent by your old pupil Elena. > 1 That's why Elena wanted you to do it.}"],"t":"Delivering the samples"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go back to Ardougne and talk to Elena.","Go to Ardougne Castle, south of Elena's house, and climb either the stairs to the north or south.","Talk to King Lathas, who is in the middle chamber of the floor 2 of the castle. {Chat: 1 I don't understand...}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Birthright of the Dwarves":{"sections":[{"n":"1 backpack space","r":"","s":["Talk to King Veldaban on the top floor of Keldagrim Palace. {Chat: 1 Hello, Veldaban. > 1 So you're king - what now? > 3 So what are you going to do? > Accept > 2 Okay, bye.}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"2 backpack spaces, Royal dwarven seal","r":"","s":["Enter the records chamber cave to the west of the bank (along the west wall).","Talk to Lieutenant Brae. {Chat: 1 He's not coming. He sent me instead. > ? Thanks.}","Talk to Vigr.","Talk to Brendt. {Chat: 2 Why did King Sorvott say you were from the Red Axe? > 2 I'll come back.}","Talk to Grundt. {Chat: 3 What was the nickname of your ship's captain?}","Talk to Brendt. {Chat: 3 Grundt says the ship's captain was Sigridsdottir. > Any > Any}","Talk to Klaas. {Chat: 1 Calling for the overthrow of the king is treason. > 1 How do you know Veldaban isn't the rightful king? > 2 I think the Red Axe told you to say this. > 3 I'll come back.}","Go to the western floor 1 of the Consortium in the north-eastern room.","Talk to Sieglinde. {Chat: 2 I want to search the workshop. > 3 Bye.}","Right click search the furnace.","Read the bundle of letters.","Go to the King's Axe Inn, south of the bank, and talk to Meike. {Chat: 1 Klaas is calling for a revolution. > 1 Why does Klaas think Veldaban isn't the rightful king? > 1 Could he have got the idea from the Red Axe? > 2 Goodbye.}","Return to the cave the suspects are in.","Talk to Vigr. {Chat: 1 Here are some letters I found in your workshop. > Any}","Talk to Klaas. {Chat: 1 I spoke to Meike. She vouched for you. > Any}","Don't forget to judge all the dwarves and make sure they are gone. Otherwise you won't find Veldaban in the cave later on.","Return to King Veldaban. {Chat: 1 I've dealt with the suspected spies. > 1 Vigr said the Red Axe broke off contact with him. > 2 Goodbye.}"],"t":"Investigating the spies"},{"n":"","r":"Combat equipment","s":["Go to the Taverley Dungeon and kill chaos dwarves (south of the Lesser demons) until Ikadia the Exile appears.","After she talks to you and teleports away, go to the chaos druid circle in the north-eastern corner of the dungeon and talk to her. {Chat: 2 I am ready.}","Defeat her and talk to her again. {Chat: Any > Any}"],"t":"Taverley chaos dwarves"},{"n":"No Summoning familiar, 5 backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Go to the Yanille's Watchtower\n  - Use Watchtower Teleport or Watchtower teleport tablet\n  - Alternatively, teleport to Yanille lodestone to Yanille and use the northern shortcuts to go under the north wall (requires 16 Agility) then west outside the northern wall\n  - If you do not have the Watchtower quest completed, Climb-up the Trellis on the northern side of the Watchtower.","Dismiss any Summoning familiar you have, and talk to the Watchtower Wizard on the top floor. {Chat: 1 King Veldaban sent me... > Any > 1 I'm ready.}\n  - You'll be given a memory wand. Keep the wand for the rest of the quest, do not destroy it.","Use the wand on the 4 floating objects.","Catch all the loose memory fragments. There will be 16 fragments total, 4 of each type.","Investigate each memory void. Based on the text that appears, use the corresponding memory fragment on the memory void following the table below:","After the cutscene, return to King Veldaban. {Chat: 1 I investigated Taverley dungeon. > Any > 1 I got a wand from the Watchtower Wizard. > 2 I'll keep hold of it. > 2 I'll meet you in the Barendir caves.}"],"t":"Yanille's Watchtower Wizard"},{"n":"","r":"Food, sign of life, run enhancing items, 1 backpack space","s":["Proceed to the north end of the tunnel and enter the cave at the end.","Talk to Veldaban. If Veldaban isn't there, make sure the cave with suspects is empty.","Talk to Nulodion. He'll give you explosive gears.","Fire the cannon. This part is not a safe death. Should you die, your gravestone will be a short walk inside the Barendir caves.","After the cutscene, stand behind the pillars to get the cannons to shoot them down, and sabotage the cannons as you progress. The first one is to the west. Do not stand near a cannon if it is about to explode, as it will hit for 5,000+ damage. Praying against range is strongly recommended.","After destroying all 5 cannons, walk up onto the platform with Colonel Grimsson.","Pull the lever that's on top of the platform above the minecart, then get into the mine cart."],"t":"The assault on the Red Axe"},{"n":"3 backpack spaces, memory wand","r":"","s":["After getting in the cart, there will be a cutscene and you will end up in another memory.","Use the Memory wand on the royal Red Axe standard (flag, west of Veldaban), the Zamorakian Chaplain, and the chaos dwarf standing next to him.","Catch all the loose memory fragments. There will be 9 fragments total, 3 of each type.","Investigate each memory void. Based on the text that appears, use the corresponding memory fragment on the memory void following the table below:","Talk to Veldaban. You will then be put into the next memory.","In the next memory, use the wand on the two trolls directly next to Grimsson (each provide 6 memory fragments) and repeat the memory fragment process following the table below:","Talk to Grimsson (his dialogue won't appear while he's busy fending the trolls).","In the next memory, use the wand on Zamorak and repeat the memory fragment process.","In the next memory, use the wand on the 3 dwarves, catch the memory fragments only when they're not labelled \"dangerous\", and repeat the process following the table below:"],"t":"Repairing the memories"},{"n":"","r":"Combat equipment","s":["Kill Grunsh or let him go.","Enter the eastern doorway behind King Veldaban, then enter the palace and go up to the floor 2.","Try to open the door with the chaos dwarf behind it.","Right click and talk to one of the directors. {Chat: 4 My friend here would like to join the Red Axe.}","Kill 7 of the 8 directors.","Talk to the remaining director.","Go upstairs to the top floor of the palace."],"t":"Veldaban of the Red Axe"},{"n":"No follower","r":"Magic combat equipment and food","s":["Talk to Grimsson and begin the fight. {Chat: 3 All right, Grimsson - bring it on.}","Kill Grimsson. If Veldaban dies, you will respawn outside the cave and need to re-enter and try again from the start.","Kill Chaos Grimsson. Try to lure and isolate him on the side with the stairs, just outside the main room. When his adrenaline bar fills up and he's about to charge you, go down the stairs and wait for 10 seconds before coming back up.","Kill Chaos Hreidmar.","Either kill or save Veldaban. {Chat: Any}","Speak with any director.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The final confrontation"}]},"Blood Runs Deep":{"sections":[{"n":"One free inventory space, combat gear","r":"Magic or Ranged or Necromancy combat equipment and food for all parts of the quest","s":["Talk to Baba Yaga on Lunar Isle about the man in the bed. {Chat: 1 Talk about the man in the bed. > Accept > 1 Is there anything we can do? > 1 Yes? > 1 An excellent idea!}","Talk to Baba Yaga again to go to the Dream World. {Chat: 1 Talk about the man in the bed. > 1 I am ready. > 1 I've no idea. > 1 I think I've got it.}","Listen Silas. {Chat: 1 He's crazy.}","Search the bookcase to obtain a prophecy tablet.","Climb the stairs.","Eavesdrop-on Silas and continue through the tunnel. {Chat: 1 She didn't count on us finding out.}","Talk to Silas. {Chat: 1 I'm a friend of your nephew.}","Read Our Lives. {Chat: 1 What do you mean, 'not working'?}\n  - Prepare to face multiple (4-7) Dagannoth and Wallasalki at a time. This will go on for a few minutes.\n  - Do not use your dwarf multicannon in this area or you will lose it."],"t":"The sick man's dream world"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Baba Yaga to be teleported to Rellekka. {Chat: 1 Talk about the man in the bed. > 1 What is? > 2 I'm ready. What's your trick?}\n  - Prepare to face many Dagannoth.","After killing sufficient Dagannoth, Brundt the Chieftain will command you to get onto his boat.","Talk to Queen Sigrid. {Chat: 1 What is the matter, Your Majesty? > 1 I'll set out right away.}","Talk to Brundt to get another seal of passage. {Chat: 2 I'll go with you.}"],"t":"The Dagannoth attack"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Bank before teleporting to Waterbirth. Bring prayer potions and a full load of food. Leave 1 space empty.","Talk to Jarvald (on the western pier) and select the option Travel-Waterbirth to head to Waterbirth Island. If he says he's not taking you, you will have to talk to him first and get to the option where you ask \"Can I come?\"","Talk to Bardur near the cave entrance for a rope. {Chat: 1 What kind of voices? > 1 Could it be an old man echoing from underground?}","Make your way to the southwestern tip of the island and tie the rope on the hole.","Climb-down the hole.","Talk to King Vargas. {Chat: 1 We aren't out yet. > 1 Come on, this isn't the King Vargas I'm used to. > 1 No, I can imagine. > 1 Certainly, I've got some here.}","Lead King Vargas down the path to the north-east and go down the ladder.\n  - Don't get too far ahead of King Vargas in the tunnels, or the dagannoth will get him and return him to the first chamber meaning you will have to start over. Staying close to King Vargas also ensures he will not be attacked so you won't have to feed him any food. It's recommended to turn off run while escorting King Vargas.","Continue to the far-east side of the next tunnel, past the small obelisk, and climb up the ladder.","The next ladder to climb up is to the west, in this short tunnel dagannoth will spawn that prioritise attacking King Vargas, make sure you attack them so they will focus their attacks on you instead.","Make your way through the last two short tunnels with rock lobsters and climb up the ladder. {Chat: 1 Well, as quickly as you can, please. > 1 Don't touch anything!}"],"t":"Saving King Vargas"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Eir. {Chat: 1 Pardon? > 1 I'm not supposed to be here? > 1 Can you at least explain where I am? > 1 How do I get back then?}","Talk to Nial Swiftfling. {Chat: 1 [Say nothing] > 1 The dagannoths are mounting a massive attack on nearby settlements. > 1 It's nothing I can't handle.}","Talk to Asleif Hamalsdotter. {Chat: 1 Just passing through. > 1 You realise they're waiting for a huge battle? > 1 I don't recall that working out so well last time.}","Talk to Eir. {Chat: 1 Yes, please.}\n  - If the spiritual realm sequence is interrupted, speak with Brundt in the long hall in Rellekka to obtain a letter. Read the letter to return.","Speak to Brundt the Chieftain. {Chat: Any}","Talk to King Vargas. {Chat: Any > Any > Any > Any > Any > Any > Any > Any > 2 [Cut to the chase]}","Talk to Princess Astrid or Prince Brand. {Chat: Any}","Talk to Brundt to continue and bank. {Chat: 2 Actually, could you drop me off at the bank on Etceteria?}\n  - Prepare for a fight with Dagannoth sentinels and the Dagannoth Mother."],"t":"Fremennik spiritual realm"},{"n":"Balmung","r":"Combat equipment for Melee, Ancient Magic (smoke, shadow, ice, & blood spells) and Ranged styles, and a way to teleport out - as you cannot leave the room while in combat","s":["Talk to Brundt in the long hall in Rellekka when you are ready. {Chat: 2 Ask about the war against the daggermouths. > 1 Yes, let's go now.}","Talk to Baba Yaga on the boat. {Chat: 1 [Say nothing] > 2 What do you think? > 1 Yes, I have. > 1 No, of course not! > 1 I'm ready.}","Climb down the hole on the southwestern tip of the island.","Enter the southern tunnel. {Chat: 1 That sounds reasonable.}","Enter the next tunnel to fight the Dagannoth sentinels. {Chat: 1 Good luck.}\n  - After defeating the sentinels, you can go to bank to get more food. You don't need to fight the sentinels again. Also you don't need the tablets or the seal of passage for the fights (saves you a few slots for food).","Alternate attacks between the dagannoth, keeping their health within approximately 500 life points to prevent them from healing each other.\n  - High level players with good equipment can just kill one then the other, it is easy to deal more damage than the amount that they are healed.\n  - There is a common glitch that prevents you from attacking the second sentinel. In this case stand on top of the sentinel you cannot attack. This will prevent it from attacking or healing the first sentinel.","Continue to the next tunnel.","Go to the south-east intersection and enter the tunnel entrance.\n  - Use the picture on the right for reference.","Proceed south and enter the tunnel.","Go through the next tunnel and select either chat option. {Chat: Any}","Start the battle with Balmung (the special weapon you received from Brundt) and kill the Dagannoth Mother, switching styles according to her colour.\n  - If you have trouble telling between the colours (specially red/orange/yellow), you can use the chatbox. It will say \"The dagannoth changes to red...\" etc.","After the Dagannoth Mother has been defeated, go back to the previous room, collect the pickaxe, plank, and tinderbox and use them to collapse one of the pillars.","Talk to Eir. {Chat: 1 I seem to have died again. > 1 Yes, I am.}","Check the bodies and finish chat. {Chat: Any}","Talk with Baba Yaga and Koschei.","Attempt to climb up the rope. {Chat: Any > Any}","Quest complete!","Speak to Brundt to receive your reward. {Chat: 2 Ask about the war against the daggermouths.}"],"t":"Waterbirth"}]},"Boric's Task I (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head down the stairs behind Doric's hut to speak to Boric. {Chat: 1 Do you have any Mining tasks for me? > Accept}","Head to Seers' Village coal truck mining site, west of McGrubor's Wood.","Deposit 30 coal into the coal truck.\n  - It does not need to be mined, it can be purchased off the Grand exchange. Make sure it isn't noted.","Talk to the Dwarven Miner to the south. {Chat: 1 Yes.}}} Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Mining some coal"}]},"Boric's Task II (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head down the stairs at Doric's workshop to speak to Boric. {Chat: 1 Do you have any Mining tasks for me? > Accept}","Head to the following mining locations and mine any ore. Multiple ores may need to be mined. A living rock brawler will spawn, kill it. The locations are:\n  - Legends' Guild south-west mine\n  - Al Kharid mine\n  - Karamja north-west mine\n  - Lumbridge south-west mine\n  - Agility Pyramid north-west mine","Head back and talk to Boric.}} Miniquest Complete!"],"t":"Having a brawl"}]},"Boric's Task III (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head down the stairs at Doric's workshop to speak to Boric. {Chat: 1 Do you have any Mining tasks for me? > Accept}","Head to the Mining guild. You must speak with one of the dwarves at the guild before mining. {Chat: 1 Boric sent me here to mine some ores.}","Mine 10 runite ore and 15 orichalcite ore.\n  - Boosts and perks such as Varrock armour, Shooting Star, and extra ore gained from leveling do count towards the 25 total ores.","Return to Boric with the ore in your inventory (cannot be noted or in an ore box).}} Miniquest Complete!"],"t":"Mining for the Guild"}]},"Bringing Home the Bacon":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Eli in Falador Farm north of Port Sarim. {Chat: Accept}","Eat the piece of bacon he gives you. {Chat: ~}","Make sure you have at least 3 (better 6) free inventory spaces or Eli won't be able to give you planks","Speak to Eli again.","During the cutscene, avoid clicking too fast through the dialogue or you will have to restart the cutscene.","Build the hotspots and keep adding bacon until Eli has escorted the pigs away (focus on the middle one and they will all swarm to it).","Talk to Eli. Choose any 1 of the 3 show pig suggestions. {Chat: 1 Maybe they can fight?} or {Chat: 2 Maybe they can carry an altar?} or {Chat: 3 Maybe they can carry items?}"],"t":"Protecting the pork"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["If necessary, gather 5 wheat from the field south-east of the Draynor lodestone.","Talk to Martin the Master Gardener in Draynor Village. {Chat: 3 Bringing Home the Bacon.} ({Chat: 4 Bringing Home the Bacon.} if Vampyre Slayer is completed)","Go north-west of Martin and talk to each character (accuse each to quickly find the suspect). {Chat: 1 You're the one that picked Martin's pockets!}\n  - Continue until you have found the suspect (usually Pickpocket Dan)","View cutscene after accusing."],"t":"Piglet payment"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go back to Eli in the storm cellar and talk to him for construction materials. {Chat: 1 You broke your hammer on a hiker? > 4 I think I should go.}","Build the pig machine in the north of the cellar.\n  - Click a second time on the pig machine again to improve it.","Speak to Eli. {Chat: 4 I think I should go.}","Speak to Eli again to give him the 5 wheat you gathered. {Chat: ~}","Go outside and put bacon on the decoys then poison them with the sleeping potion."],"t":"Adulterate the addicts"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Eli.","Pick 5 onions just south of Draynor bank. These must be picked after having talked to him; you cannot use onions you already have, even if you picked them yourself.","Deliver the 5 onions to Eli. {Chat: ~}","Interact with pig machine.","Watch the cutscene about the pig.","Talk to Eli to receive a pig. {Chat: ~}","Take the pig to each location (a cutscene will play once you reach the correct area).\n  - Lumbridge Castle courtyard.\n  - Varrock Marketplace (in the centre of the fountain).\n  - Ardougne Marketplace.\n  - Falador centre (just south of the north gate).","Return to Eli.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Prized pig"}]},"Broken Home":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Maria, who can be found just south of the Silvarea limestone quarry, north-east of Varrock. You can use the invitation box to reach her quickly. Finish the dialogue.\n  - Deposit all of your items (backpack and equipment) in the bank deposit box and enter the mansion. {Chat: 1 Enter.}\n  - The Persistent Rage relic power cannot be active while entering."],"t":"Starting the quest"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Purple shading is for the rooms with purple energy that will hurt you.","Cyan shading is for when Senecianus chases you in monster form.","Before entering any door, check if there is smoke emitting from the bottom. If there is no smoke, enter the door normally. If there is smoke, right-click Peek through the door, then click the Enter Room button (the animation is irrelevant). Peeking through doors will negate ALL damage taken from the ghost.\n  - Alternatively, you can click on the smoke doors to go through and quickly go back through them, taking 0 damage and getting rid of Ormod quicker.","You do not heal life points over time; only mystery meat heals you. Mystery meat restores all of your life points once eaten. The Eat Food ability does not consider mystery meat to be food, so you must click to eat it. Deaths are safe (safe for hardcore ironmen as well). The Persistent Rage relic power cannot be used to replenish adrenaline for Regenerate during the quest.","Safe rooms save your progress. Dying, exiting the house, or lobbying reverts you to your last saved state with the items and life points that you saved with but not the time.","Temporal chests cannot be opened on the first playthrough when completing the quest itself, so ignore them.","Timers (e.g. 30 minutes remaining) are general guides for the replay challenge. Challenges cannot be completed on the first playthrough, so these should also be ignored. The timer does not pause during dialogue, so players who are trying to do the time challenge should spacebar through the dialogue as quickly as possible. However, players can reset their progress by speaking to Maria outside the mansion. The correct dialogue options are given by the speech bubble icons in the steps below.","You need to have very low latency between your computer and your RuneScape server. Otherwise, the monster will kill you even before the screen shows up, making it impossible to pass this part of the quest."],"t":"Helpful information"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open WEST wall's SOUTH door to a safe room.","Open NORTH door.","Open WEST door.","Take the raven key and clock hands on the floor.","Open EAST door.","Open SOUTH door to a safe room."],"t":"Getting raven key"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use the clock hands on the grandfather clock to receive an eye gem.","Optional food: Search the chest to get mystery meat.","Open EAST door.","Open EAST door (raven key).","Open SOUTH door after the cutscene.","Open EAST door.","Sort the pile of books for two eye gem (the second and the third).\n  - First pick any random order of books.\n  - The order is from bottom to top.\n  - Then use the hints given to swap out any books that are not in the correct place for books higher up on the stack.\n  - Repeat the process for any incorrect books until the whole stack is correct.","Optional temporal chest: Open and search the temporal chest, requires level 10 in all skills."],"t":"Repairing grandfather clock and organising books"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open WEST door.","Open NORTH door.","Open EAST door.","Open NORTH door.","Open SOUTH wall's MIDDLE door."],"t":"Heading to statue puzzle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Push the WEST statue.","Walk two steps SOUTH. Push the EAST statue.","Walk one step SOUTH. Push the WEST statue.","Push the most SOUTH-WEST statue.","Walk one step NORTH-EAST. Push the EAST statue.","Push the SOUTH statue.","Push the WEST statue.","Take the fourth eye gem from the table."],"t":"Solving statue puzzle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open NORTH door.","Optional temporal chest: Open and search the temporal chest by the staircase, requires level 20 in all skills.","Ascend the stairs to the WEST.","Open EAST door.","Open EAST door after the cutscene.","Open WEST wall's SOUTH door.","Search Ingram's research notes for the spider key and a scroll fragment."],"t":"Getting spider key"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open EAST door.","Open WEST wall's NORTH door.","Open WEST door.","Open SOUTH door to the upstairs lobby (unbolt).","Open WEST door (spider key).","Open SOUTH door.","Search the dead servant for the fifth eye gem. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Open WEST door.","Draw back the curtain. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to the faceless servant for the statue key {Chat: 1 Yes.}."],"t":"Getting statue key"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open EAST door.","Open NORTH door.","Open NORTH door.","Open EAST door.","Open SOUTH wall's WEST door (statue key)."],"t":"Heading to four statues"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take the eye gem on the floor.","Investigate the first statue twice.","Open WEST door.","Investigate the second statue twice.","Open SOUTH door.","Investigate the third statue twice.","Open EAST door.","Take the scythe key on the floor.","Open WEST door.","Open NORTH door.","Open EAST door."],"t":"Getting scythe key"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open NORTH door.","Open WEST door.","Open SOUTH door.","Open EAST door.","Open EAST door (scythe key).","Open SOUTH wall's EAST door to a safe room."],"t":"Heading to Saradomin shrine"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Investigate the shrine for the grand piano key and skull key.\n  - Optional food: Search the chest for mystery meat.","Open NORTH door.","Peek through the WEST door after the scream and then click \"Go Back\".","Open NORTH wall's EAST door (unbolt).","Open WEST wall's NORTH door.","Open WEST door.","Descend the stairs."],"t":"Getting skull key"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open SOUTH wall's EAST door to purple area.","Open WEST door and enter it, go quickly through after the glass shatters.","Open WEST door to purple area.","Open WEST wall's SOUTH door to a safe area."],"t":"Shattered windows"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open NORTH door.","Open NORTH door (skull key).","Open EAST wall's SOUTH door.","Search Ormod's scribblings for a scroll fragment.","Open WEST door.","Open NORTH door.","Open WEST door.","Play the grand piano."],"t":"Searching Ormod's scribblings"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open SOUTH hidden door to purple area.","Search the scorched skeleton in SOUTH-EAST corner for an eye gem.","Open NORTH hidden door.","Open EAST door.","Open SOUTH wall's EAST door.","Descend the stairs."],"t":"Searching scorched skeleton"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open WEST wall's NORTH door.","Search the butler for the cleaver key.","Open EAST door.","Optional safe room and food:\n  - Open NORTH wall's WEST door to a safe room.\n  - Search the chest for mystery meat.\n  - Open SOUTH door.","Open NORTH wall's EAST door (cleaver key).","Turn off running.","Walk over broken glass to avoid taking damage equal to 10% of your maximum life points. Walk to dodge the knives that are thrown from the haunted knife blocks at regular intervals.","Turn on running.","Open SOUTH wall's EAST door."],"t":"Walking through knives maze"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open NORTH wall's MIDDLE door.","Search the chest of drawers for a large pipette.","Open SOUTH door.","Open NORTH wall's EAST door.","Use the large pipette on the pig to get large pipette of pig bile.","Open SOUTH door.","Open EAST door.","Search the furnace for human ashes.","Open WEST door.","Use the large pipette of pig bile and human ashes on the cauldron in the SOUTH-WEST corner of the room.","Use the large pipette on the cauldron to get alkaline concoction.","Use the alkaline concoction on the SOUTH door.","Open SOUTH door."],"t":"Making alkaline concoction"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open WEST door. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Investigate the frozen servant for the doll key. {Chat: 1 Take the key? > 1 Pull the key free?}","Open EAST door.","Optional temporal chest:\n  - Open EAST wall's SOUTH door.\n  - Open and search the temporal chest, requires level 40 in all skills.\n  - Open WEST door.","Open EAST wall's NORTH door.","Take the snake key from the key hooks next to the ladder."],"t":"Getting doll key"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb the ladder to purple area (snake key). {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Use the stairs in the CENTRE of the grand hall to purple area.","Open WEST door.","Open WEST door (doll key).","Ascend the stairs.","Take the tusks key on the floor.","Descend the stairs."],"t":"Getting tusks key"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open EAST door.","Open NORTH door.","Open EAST door.","Open SOUTH wall's EAST door (tusks key).","Investigate the bust.","Enter the trap door to the SOUTH-WEST.","Search the thief for an eye gem.","Climb the ladder."],"t":"Searching the thief"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open NORTH door.","Open SOUTH wall's WEST door.","Open WEST door.","Open SOUTH door.","Open EAST door.","Investigate the statue twice.","Open EAST secret door to a safe room."],"t":"Heading to shrine of the son"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take the mother's hairbrush from the shrine of the son.","Open WEST secret door.","Open WEST door.","Open NORTH door.","Open EAST door.","Open NORTH door to leave the statue room.","Open WEST door.","Open SOUTH door.","Open WEST door.","Ascend the stairs.","Talk to the emaciated spirit and finish the dialogue for the noose key."],"t":"Taking back mother's hairbrush"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open EAST door.","Open EAST door to purple area.","Open NORTH door (unbolt).","Open EAST door.","Open SOUTH door (noose key).","Open and climb into the cupboard."],"t":"Heading to hidden basement"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Follow the corridor.","Peek through peephole along north wall and then click \"Go Back\".","Open WEST door (unbolt).","Optional temporal chest:\n  - Open EAST wall's SOUTH door.\n  - Open and search the temporal chest, requires level 30 in all skills.\n  - Open WEST door.","Open EAST wall's NORTH door.","Optional safe room:\n  - Open NORTH wall's WEST door.\n  - Search the chest for mystery meat if you have not yet done so.\n  - Open SOUTH door."],"t":"Going through long corridor"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Descend the stairs.","Open EAST door.","Descend the stairs.","Move all statues except the north statue.","Stand on the MIDDLE yellow pressure plate.","Descend the stairs behind the ancient door.","Optional temporal chest: Open and search the temporal chest, requires level 50 in all skills.","Descend the stairs.","Descend the stairs.","Climb down the mountaineering gear to a safe room. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Solving ancient door puzzle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Optional temporal chest: Open and search the temporal chest in the south, requires level 60 in all skills.","Optional food: Search NORTH chest for mystery meat.","Open EAST door.","Search the reception desk for Nabor's notes on insanity and the chains key.","Open NORTH door.","Open EAST door.","Optional temporal chest: Open and search the temporal chest in the north-west, requires level 70 in all skills.","Open EAST door (chains key).","Open EAST door.","Open EAST door.","Head to the SOUTH-WEST cell to take the dagger key on the floor.","Optional temporal chest: Open and search the temporal chest in the north-east, requires level 80 in all skills.","Open WEST door.","Open WEST door.","Open WEST door.","Open WEST door.","Open SOUTH door.","Open WEST door to a safe room."],"t":"Getting dagger key"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb the rope.","Ascend the stairs.","Ascend the stairs.","Ascend the stairs to ancient door.","Ascend the stairs.","Open WEST door.","Ascend the stairs.","Optional safe room:\n  - Open NORTH wall's WEST door.\n  - Search the chest for mystery meat if you have not yet done so.\n  - Open SOUTH door."],"t":"Leaving hidden basement"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Ascend the stairs.","Warning: The monster chases you after this room.","Open NORTH door.","Open SOUTH wall's WEST door.","Open SOUTH door.","Open SOUTH door to a safe room."],"t":"Back to grandfather clock"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open EAST door to purple area.","Use the stairs in the CENTRE of the grand hall to purple area.","Move the servant next to the EAST door in purple area.","Warning: The monster chases you after this room.","Open EAST door.","Open SOUTH wall's WEST door (dagger key).","Search Ingram's rantings for the last scroll fragment.","Combine the fragments and Nabor's notes on insanity to make a Break Curse scroll.","Optional temporal chest:\n  - Open EAST door.\n  - Open and search the temporal chest, requires level 90 in all skills.\n  - Open WEST door."],"t":"Breaking curse"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open NORTH door and run east away from the monster.","Use the scroll on the monster. You can use the scroll while the monster is spawning.","Talk to the monster and choose an ending for Ormod. {Chat: Any}","Open WEST door. You won't get hurt in this purple area.","Use the stairs in the CENTRE of the grand hall.","Talk to \"Lenian\" and finish the dialogue. At this point you get a notification saying what challenges you have completed.","Exit the house through the south door. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Maria to claim your reward.","Congratulations, quest complete!"],"t":"Dialogue with Ormod"}]},"Buyers and Cellars":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Guildmaster Darren Lightfinger in the Thieves' Guild north of the house with a furnace in Lumbridge (enter the trapdoor). {Chat: 2 What are you doing down here? (Skip speech.) > 2 And what is it you need done? (Skip speech) > Accept > 2 No, I think I've got the hang of this. > 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"Logs (or chop down a swamp tree)}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["Talk to Chief Thief Robin, south of Lumbridge Castle inside the castle wall. {Chat: 1 Go ahead.}","Talk to Father Urhney in his house to the south in the Lumbridge Swamp. {Chat: 3 Nice chalice. > 3 Can I have a look at it?}\n  - If The Restless Ghost has been completed, {Chat: 4 Nice chalice. > 3 Can I have a look at it?}","Light a fire outside one of Urhney's windows.","Talk to Urhney and mention the chalice then the fire. {Chat: 3 Nice chalice. > 4 Fire! Fire!}\n  - If The Restless Ghost has been completed, {Chat: 4 Nice chalice. > 4 Fire! Fire!}","Pickpocket Urhney quickly to get a complex key.","Open the display case."],"t":"The chalice"},{"n":"Golden chalice}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["Return to Darren's cellar.","Use the chalice on Darren.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Cabin Fever":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to Port Phasmatys.","Talk to Bill Teach in the inn. {Chat: 1 Yes, I've always wanted to be a pirate! > Accept}","Run to the dock and cross the gangplank to board the eastern-most ship.","Talk to Bill Teach. {Chat: 1 Let's go Cap'n!}"],"t":"Setting sail"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Search the repair locker, take 4 ropes.","Search the Gun Locker, take 1 fuse.","Climb-up the ship's ladder.","Climb the climbing net next to the central mast.","Use rope from the backpack on the hoisted sail on the ship you are on.\n  - The same actions of climbing and using the rope are used to change ships every time.","Add fuse on the powder barrel on the eastern ship.","Light the fuse (you may fail and have to retry).","Climb the climbing net and use the rope on the hoisted sail as before.","Talk to Bill."],"t":"Sabotage"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb-down the ship's ladder.","Search the repair locker and take:\n  - 30 tacks\n  - 6 planks\n  - 3 swamp paste","For each of the three leaks in the hull:\n  - Fill the ship hull.\n  - Waterproof the ship hull.","Climb-up the ship's ladder and talk to Bill.\n  - Be sure to finish all the dialogue, or else you won't be able to proceed."],"t":"Fixing the leaks"},{"n":"2 ropes","r":"","s":["Board the other ship (climb and use rope as before).","Climb-down their Ship's ladder.","Plunder the closed chest for 5 plunder.","Return to your ship (climb and use rope as before).","Climb-down your ship's ladder.","Store-plunder on the plunder storage.","Return to and talk to Bill."],"t":"Pirate plunder"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb-down the ship's ladder.","Search the gun locker for a cannon barrel.","Repair the broken cannon on the top deck.","Talk to Bill.","Search the gun locker and take:\n  - Ramrod.\n  - Some fuses (take 3 in case of failure).\n  - Some cannon canisters (take 3 in case of failure).","Climb-up the ship's ladder.","Prepare and fire the cannon. If you miss you will need to repeat these steps.\n  - If you make a mistake, you can empty-out the cannon. You will still need to clean it with the ramrod (final instruction).\n  - Take-powder from the powder barrel next to the cannon on the deck.\n  - Use gunpowder on the cannon.\n  - Then the ramrod.\n  - Then a canister.\n  - Then a fuse.\n  - Fire! the cannon. Check your chat log to see if you hit or not.\n  - Use the ramrod on the cannon again to clean it.","Talk to Bill.","Return to the gun locker and take:\n  - At least 5 cannon balls.\n  - At least 5 fuses.\n  - 2 cannon barrel (the cannon may blow up).","Fire the cannon as before, substituting the canister for a cannon ball, until you put three holes in the enemy's ship.","Quest complete!","Talk to Bill to claim another reward."],"t":"Cannon"}]},"Call of the Ancestors":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["The Liberation of Mazcab grouping teleport may be helpful for a few parts of this quest. Especially if you lack reputation.","Talk to Tunks at the desert goebie camp, north-west of the Menaphos gates. {Chat: Accept}","Go through the world window","Go slightly to the north then east to Kanatah.","Talk to Acca Kanatah. {Chat: 2 I've simply come to help. > 1 Talk about Call of the Ancestors. > 2 The airut are gathering to completely wipe out Kanatah. > 2 Ok, I'm done talking. What do I need to do?}","If you have a pet, dismiss it and go east to the beach and talk to Tunks for a cutscene. {Chat: 1 No problem.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Jump over the chasm and collect the bundle of logs.","Headbutt the cracked wall. Control Peck by clicking on him and squeeze through the hole. Gather the bundle of logs.","Talk to Acca Kanatah. {Chat: 1 Talk about Call of the Ancestors. > 2 Great, where do I get more?}"],"t":"Gathering the bundles of logs"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter Nemi Forest, to the west of Mazcab. Select the correct option on the chatbox when entering the Forest. {Chat: 1 Enter Nemi Forest for Call of the Ancestors.}\n  - Talk to Mazcab guide by the city entrance to get to Nemi Forest faster, if you have the reputation. {Chat: 2 Forest Entrance}","Talk to the Ancient goebie {Chat: 1 Acca Kanatah needs to create more poison. > 1 Friend? > 1 Looks like we're visiting a temple then.}","Enter the temple to the north, then talk to Xinachto {Chat: 1 I'm an adventurer! > 5 Goodbye.}"],"t":"Nemi poison"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the first door on the western wall.","Control Lunch. Step on the second tile from the west, then the one east of it, then the easternmost one, then the westernmost one. Do not step on a pressure plate twice.","Control Tunks. Jump over the chasm, then press the easternmost pressure plate, the one west of it, then the westernmost pressure plate, then the remaining one to the east of it.","Control Lunch. Headbutt the cracked wall on the western wall. Then step on the westernmost plate.","Control Peck. Squeeze through the small gap you just opened, and the one to the north, then investigate the magic.","To exit, control Lunch and exit the southern door."],"t":"First trial"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the door on the eastern wall.","Control Tunks and jump over the chasm to the north once.","Control Lunch at the entrance and headbutt the cracked wall on the west.","Control Peck, squeeze through, and pull the lever.","Control Lunch and push the heavy block onto the north-eastern pressure plate.","Control Tunks and stand on the pressure plate on the centre platform.","Control Lunch and pull the heavy block onto the south-eastern pressure plate. Walk around to stand on the north-eastern pressure plate.","Control Tunks, jump the chasm north and stand on one of the north-western pressure plates.","Control Peck and squeeze through the north-western gap.","Control Lunch, and walk past the three pillars and stand on one of the north-western pressure plates.","Control Peck and pull the lever, squeeze back through the gap and investigate the magic.","To exit, go through the southern door as any of the goebies."],"t":"Second trial"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the door on the northern wall.","Control Lunch and headbutt the western wall.","Control Peck and squeeze through. Pull the lever to reveal a pressure plate."],"t":"Third trial"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Control Tunks. Jump over chasm then place Tunks on the north-eastern small tile and then place Lunch on the south-eastern large tile."],"t":"=Lever 1="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Place Tunks on the north-western small tile and then place Lunch on the south-eastern large tile.","Place Tunks on the south-eastern small tile and then place Lunch on the north-western large tile."],"t":"=Lever 2="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Place Tunks on the southern small tile and then place Lunch on the north-western large tile.","Place Tunks on the south-western small tile and then place Lunch on the south-eastern large tile.","Place Tunks on the northern small tile and then place Lunch on the south-western large tile."],"t":"=Lever 3="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Place Tunks on the north-western small tile and then place Lunch on the south-western large tile.","Place Tunks on the north-eastern small tile and then place Lunch on the south-eastern large tile.","Place Tunks on the eastern small tile and then place Lunch on the north-eastern large tile.","Place Tunks on the south-eastern small tile and then place Lunch on the north-western large tile."],"t":"=Lever 4="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Investigate the magic as Peck, then exit the southern door.","Talk to Xinachto, break the shackle. {Chat: 4 Why is Xinchto allowing this to happen? > 2 You're right, break the shackles!}","Go outside through the southern door.","Talk to the Ancient goebie."],"t":"=Release Xinachto="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill the waves of Airut and chargers by clicking on the ground or the minimap to attack.\n  - If you fail, speak to the Ancient goebie to start the waves again."],"t":"Fighting"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Ancient goebie to obtain poisonous nemi stalks.","Run south-east to exit the Nemi forest.","Run east to Kanatah and talk to Acca Kanatah. {Chat: 1 Talk about Call of the Ancestors. > 1 I found the poison. > 3 We explored a lost temple, freed a spirit and used forgotten magic to defeat airut.}\n  - Talk to Mazcab guide outside Nemi Forest to return quickly to Acca Kanatah if you have the reputation. {Chat: 4 Kanatah}"],"t":"Wrapping Up"}]},"Carnillean Rising":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Outside the Carnillean Mansion south-west of East Ardougne, talk to Xenia. {Chat: 2 Yes, I remember you. > 1 Thanks for fixing it! > Accept}","Talk to Ceril Carnillean. {Chat: 1 So, you want me to turn Philipe into an adventurer. > 1 How do you expect me to create a quest? > 1 Where can I find all that stuff? > 4 I'll come back later.}","Search the bookcase in the room with Henryeta Carnillean for a book about the Carnillean family.","Talk to Butler Crichton. {Chat: 1 Sir Ceril says you'll help me create a quest. > 1 Yes, let's go.}","Head into the basement and enter the hole on the east wall (cutscene will begin), then head back to the house."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the floor 2 and take the red and black dragon head from the wall (2 heads in total).","Open and search the southern wardrobe for the armour and sword.","Tear the net curtain from the north-east wall.","Take the money pouch from the bed or Henryeta's necklace from the dresser."],"t":"Master bedroom"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Search his painting set for red paint."],"t":"Philipe's room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Sarsaparilla. {Chat: 3 I'm creating a quest for Philipe. Will you help?}, then talk again. {Chat: 3 Are you just going to stay in here? > 2 You were talking about your ambitions. > 2 I'm directing a drama. Would you like a part? > 4 Damsel in distress > 1 Yes, follow me.}","Open and search the wardrobe for her dress. {Chat: 1 I need to borrow a costume.}"],"t":"Sarsaparilla's room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the cellar and talk to Claus the chef. {Chat: 2 Drunken jailer}","Search the cupboard, take everything (wooden boards, twine, shears, and Sir Ceril's wine).","Search the barrel of junk to collect rusty spikes.","Pick up the spider from the floor.","(optional) Pick up 7 buckets of water from the floor.\n  - It is faster to skip this step and build a spike pit instead."],"t":"The cellar"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Right-click build on the hole hotspot. (The cave going into the next area) {Chat: 1 Cobweb}","Enter the cave and talk to Sarsaparilla {Chat: 1 Yes, follow me.} and Claus. {Chat: 1 Follow me.}","Continue through the cave and talk to the goblins. {Chat: 3 Can you help me? > 3 Here, you can have this armour. > 1 Patrolling guards}","Head to the south-easternmost part of the tunnels and enter the passage.","Search the spoils near the heap for bone scraps south-west of the room.","Take the cave mouse to have the wolves follow you out."],"t":"The cave"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head north to the centre bridge.","\"Build\" the \"jailer\" hotspot by leading Claus to it.\n  - If the money pouch was taken, use it on Claus.","Cross the bridge and build the dragon hotspots. The wolves will move into position.","Use the dragon heads on the wolves.","Build the Damsel hotspot.\n  - If the necklace was taken, use it on Sarsaparilla.","Head back south across the bridge.","Build hotspots in these locations as you backtrack up towards the cellar:\n  - Decoration - on the wall east of the fire {Chat: 1 Bloodstains}\n  - Traps - east and west of the fire {Chat: 1 Tripwire}\n  - Decoration - west of the fire at the end of the hall {Chat: 2 Scary eyes}\n  - Decoration - on the north wall before turning around towards the cave entrance {Chat: 3 Impaled skulls}\n  - Obstacle - on the floor in the southernmost corridor, heading towards the cave entrance {Chat: 2 Spike pit}"],"t":"Building the quest"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head back into the house and talk to Philipe. {Chat: Accept}","Pickpocket him. Talk to him again. {Chat: 4 A bag of sweets. > Accept > 1 Okay, follow me.}","Proceed through the cave while Philipe follows. {Chat: Any}","Watch the cutscene where Philipe attempts to pass the guards.","Talk to Slimepits (one of the goblins) until a dialogue window with the Butler appears - do not continue dialogue until Philipe passes.","Talk to Philipe again to have him follow.","Continue towards Claus. {Chat: Any}","Talk to Philipe again to have him follow.","Continue towards the dragons and talk to Philipe. {Chat: Any}","After the dragons are slain, a cave wolf matriarch will arrive.","Attempt to attack the matriarch to focus its attacks on you. Dodge or withstand the attacks until Philipe kills it. If you run in circles around the matriarch, most of her attacks will miss and you will take very little damage.\n  - Do not use Protect from Magic or the matriarch will revert her attention back to Philipe."],"t":"Philipe"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Philipe for a cutscene. {Chat: 1 Yes, let's go now!}","Talk to Ceril.","Talk to Xenia. {Chat: 4 So what happens now?}","Talk to Ceril.","Quest complete!","Loot the chest near Ceril."],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Catapult Construction":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["North of the Tyras camp, talk to the guard next to the catapult. {Chat: Accept > 1 I guess you're going to get fired, then. > 1 What do you suggest? > 1 Alright, I'll go and speak to General Hining.}","Talk to General Hining in Tyras Camp. {Chat: 1 So, the Tyras Camp catapult is broken? > 1 Perhaps I can help to repair it? > 2 General, I believe I can be of service to you.}","Teleport to the Tirannwn lodestone, then take the north-western path, cross the leaves trap, and then the sticks trap (south west of the log crossing shortcut) to find the Catapult engineer.","Talk to the Catapult engineer for schematics. {Chat: 3 General Hining asked me to find you. > 2 I'm quite an experienced carpenter.}","Read the schematics. {Chat: 3 Make the repair parts.}","Talk to the engineer again. {Chat: 1 Can I read the letter?}","Talk to Rolad at the Dwarven Mine camp, south of Ice Mountain. (North-east of Falador lodestone) {Chat: 2 Can I have the metal parts for the Tyras Camp catapult please?}","Talk to Thaki inside Port Sarim's pub. {Chat: 2 You're right, I'm not a sailor.}","Search the drunken sailor outside.","Wear the sailor's hat and talk to Thaki again."],"t":"Fetching the materials"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to the catapult north of the Tyras Camp and talk to the guard.","Copy the solution below. Use the big buttons to swap sides."],"t":"Building the catapult"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the guard. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll have a go.}","Move the catapult left or right so the arrow at the bottom middle aligns with the target rock.\n  - Shoot the middle rock - 0/6 green bars on Counterweight.\n  - Left rock (four points left of middle rock) - 5/6 green bars on Counterweight.\n  - Right rock (two points right of middle rock, one turn left from far right) - 6/6 green bars on Counterweight.","Talk to the guard again.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Catapult testing"}]},"Chef's Assistant":{"sections":[{"n":"Chef's hat or some other item to enter Cook's Guild","r":"","s":["Head to the Cooks' Guild, the building just south-west of the Grand Exchange main entrance.","To start, talk to the Head chef in the Cooks' Guild. {Chat: 1 Do you have any quests for me? > 1 Of course, discrete is my middle name! > Accept > 2 Cool story, can we get on with this? > 1 Sounds tasty! > 2 Consider myself braced. > 2 Pull yourself together! > 1 Would you like me to get some more for you?}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"Logs, steel bar, bucket of milk, pot of flour, pat of butter, pot of cream, cake tin","r":"","s":["Speak to Phil or Delphie in Falador, south of the party room. {Chat: 1 Sure, what do I need?}","Repair the broken dairy churn in the northern part of the room using logs and a steel bar.","Speak with Phil or Delphie again.","Use bucket of milk on the dairy churn and churn it into some cream cheese.\n  - If not done already, make a pot of cream and a pat of butter once you're there.","Return to the head chef in the Cook's Guild. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Chef's Assistant'.}","Make biscuits by combining a pot of flour and pat of butter, then cooking the dough at the range upstairs. Be aware you can burn the biscuits in which case you need to make new ones.\n  - Pick up cake tin from upstairs if you do not already have one.","Speak to the head chef. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Chef's Assistant'. > 1 Sorry Chef.}","Click the cake tin to create cheesecake.","Speak to the head chef again. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Chef's Assistant'.}"],"t":"Obtaining the ingredients"},{"n":"Cheesecake","r":"Lumbridge teleport, Fort Forinthry Teleport","s":["Deliver the cheesecake to Mess Sergeant Ramsey, can be found east of the Taverley lodestone, inside The Pick and Lute pub. {Chat: 1 The Head Chef asked me to bring you this to try.}","Deliver the cheesecake to the Cook in Lumbridge, who can be found inside the Lumbridge Castle. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Deliver the cheesecake to the Cook of the Jolly Boar Inn, who can be found in the Jolly Boar Inn, south of Fort Forinthry. {Chat: 1 The Head Chef asked me to bring you this to try.}","Return to the head chef. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Chef's Assistant'.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Cheesy delivery!"}]},"Children of Mah":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Kharshai beneath the helmet shop in Rellekka (requires completion of the Koschei's Troubles miniquest) or all the way north of Rellekka in the Rellekka Hunter area, next to the Arctic (azure) habitat mine. {Chat: 1 I want to talk about Children of Mah. > Accept > 5 I'm ready to go to the ritual site. > 1 I want to talk about Children of Mah. > 1 Yes. > 1 Yes, I want to leave.}"],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"1 free inventory slot","r":"TokKul-Zo, Dig Site pendant","s":["Go to the Mahjarrat Ritual Site via:\n  - Kharshai at the quest start location can teleport you there.\n  - If you have completed Ritual of the Mahjarrat you can use:\n    - DKQ, exit the Glacor Cave, and then go north-west.\n    - Use the canoe in the snowy hunter area north of Rellekka (requires partial completion of the Tale of the Muspah).","Investigate the ritual marker to summon Kharshai","Talk to Kharshai with a free inventory slot to receive the charged engrammeter.","Investigate the ritual marker to leave, or teleport to Varrock Dig Site using a Dig Site pendant or Archaeology journal.","Go to the entrance of the throne room of Senntisten on the east side of the Varrock Dig Site.","Harvest the memory spring near the entrance of the Zarosian throne room.","Enter the throne room and harvest the 4 other memory springs inside. There are two on each side of the mine cart track (near the stairs) and two down the stairs near the material caches.","Return to the ritual site and investigate the ritual marker. (If you have not completed Ritual of the Mahjarrat, then return to Kharsai at the quest starting point to teleport back.)","Continue Azzanadra's dialogue. {Chat: 1 Yes, let's go!}"],"t":"Ritual site"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Perjour just to your south. {Chat: 3 Could I see that book of yours? > 4 Goodbye.}","Talk to Zebub a little further south. {Chat: 2 Say goodbye.}","Inspect the broken mouthpiece on the pillar next to Zebub.","Talk to Duke Sucellus to the north. {Chat: 3 What has happened so far? > 4 Goodbye.}","Talk to Jhallan just to the east. {Chat: 2 Say goodbye.}","Inspect the wall marking on the pillar next to Jhallan."],"t":"Inside Kharsai's memories"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Inspect the broken enchantment down the first flight of stairs.","Talk to Pernix. {Chat: 2 An inquisitor was sent for. > 3 A red pair of horns. > 2 There is a plot to overthrow Zaros. > 2 Say goodbye.}","Head down a flight of stairs and talk to Akthanakos. {Chat: 3 Mah. > 3 Icthlarin. > 1 A camel. > 2 Say goodbye.}"],"t":"Northern platform"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head back up and then down the staircase to the south. Talk to the warpriest. {Chat: 1 Use 'Inquisitorial Truth Serem'.}","Inspect the stashed weapons south of the stairway. They are partially hidden under the stairway.","Inspect the wall marking on the north-eastern pillar. Rotate your camera to face south-east if having trouble seeing the marking.","Talk to Sliske. {Chat: 3 Do you have any suspects? > 4 Goodbye.}"],"t":"Southern platform"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Azzanadra. {Chat: Any}","Talk to the 3 suspects. {Chat: Any}","Talk to either Azzanadra or Zamorak to choose a side. {Chat: 1}","Watch or skip the cutscene. {Chat: 1}"],"t":"Centre"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go through the dialogue at the Ritual marker. {Chat: 1 Yes, let's go!}\n  - If the dialogue is interrupted, talk to Zamorak.","Talk to the Mahjarrat once more. }}"],"t":"After the memory"},{"n":"","r":"Sixth-Age circuit, combat equipment, food, Shard of Zaros, sign of life or portent of life, 1-2 free inventory spaces to remove weapon and shield","s":["Go to the World Gate, dial Freneskae, and enter it (left click, select \"Children of Mah\"). {Chat: 1 Children of Mah.}","Optionally inspect the four Mahjarrat deathstones along the route for a master quest cape requirement.","Talk to Kharshai.","Unequip weapon(s) and jump on the rock. The first deathstone is before the first lava ride. {Chat: 1 Yes.}\n  - Avoid taking damage using the keyboard or on-screen arrows.\n  - The mini-map can help you predict upcoming obstacles.\n  - The off-hand Enhanced Excalibur can be activated prior to departure, and will heal you during the ride.","Equip weapon(s) and attack muspahs until a grand force muspah appears.","Stand next to the interactable wall and attack it until its adrenaline bar fills and it destroys the wall with its special attack.","Repeat in next area. (Note: There is a checkpoint right before the second river of lava)","Heal up, un-equip weapon(s), and jump on the rock. The second deathstone is before the second lava ride. {Chat: 1 Yes.}\n  - Avoid taking damage using the keyboard or on-screen arrows as before.","Talk to Seren. The third deathstone is to the east of Seren. {Chat: Any > 2 [Continue...]}","Enter the cave. The final deathstone is right before meeting with the mahjarrat.","Go west and talk to Zemouregal. {Chat: Any > 2 [Continue...] > 2 [Continue...] > 2 Stay silent.}","Watch or skip the cutscene.","Speak with Zaros.}}"],"t":"Pilgrimage to the ritual site"},{"n":"","r":"3 empty inventory spaces. Bank all your equipment and bring food. If you want to speed up this part, whenever you need to go up or down the northern path, teleport to the world gate and re-enter the quest instance.","s":["Go up the northern path and talk to Seren at the end. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Investigate the core of Mah.","Intercept the shadows heading towards the core from the muspahs.\n  - Insert the glowing orb into the light shard between the core and the shadow heading towards it. The orb must be retrieved from the light shard it's in before it can be inserted into another.","Navigate the area by going from one circle of light to another.\n  - Touch the light shard at the end of the path.\n  - Go back half way and exit on Zemouregal.","Investigate the core and intercept the shadows as before. Two orbs will be given this time. Failing three times will result in the option to toggle an easier mode.","Navigate the area using the circles of light as before.\n  - Touch the western light shard.\n  - Touch the eastern light shard.\n  - Touch the central light shard.\n  - Go south and exit on Seren.","Investigate the core and intercept the shadows as before. Three orbs will be given this time. If you're having issues completing this round, after three failed attempts, there will be an option for easy mode."],"t":"Mah's nightmares"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Seren. {Chat: 2 [Continue...]}","Go down the path and talk to Seren at the ritual site. {Chat: 2 [Continue...]}","Go back up the path and talk to Zaros. {Chat: 2 [Continue...]}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"City of Senntisten":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ariane at the entrance to the Heart of Gielinor and enter the Elder Halls. {Chat: Accept > 1 Yes}","Talk to Charos. Go through all chat options about what to do with the eggs. {Chat: 1 Could we destroy them? > 2 Could we drain them? > 3 Could we hide them? > 4 Could we fight the elder gods? > 5 Could we move them? > 4 I'm stumped.}","Talk to Azzanadra, after which a cutscene will play. {Chat: ~}","Talk to Charos and Ariane. {Chat: ~}","Go to the Archaeology Guild, upstairs onto the balcony. Talk to Dr Nabanik. {Chat: ~}","Teleport to Port Sarim lodestone and go north-west to the Armadyl's tower teleporter to teleport up to Armadyl's Tower. Climb to the top and talk to Armadyl.","Go to Burthorpe Castle and climb up the stone staircase. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Talk to Icthlarin south-east of the table.","Talk to Seren west of the table.","Talk to Moia south of the table. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Zamorak. {Chat: 2 Er, help?}","Go to the throne room on the floor 3 (east side) of the White Knights' Castle and talk to Saradomin. {Chat: 1 City of Senntisten}","Return to Dr Nabanik on the balcony of the main building at the Archaeology Guild."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the City of Senntisten through the ancient door to the north of the Archaeology Guild. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Excavate the forum entrance. (Use your grace of the elves charges to move the materials to the material storage container if you have it. Porters also work.)","Interact with the pedestal to obtain Pontifex Maximus figurine (damaged).","Exit via the pulley. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Intern Jimmy at the entrance to get materials.","Restore the Pontifex Maximus figurine at an archaeologist's workbench. (The one south by the guild is closest.)","Return to Azzanadra, and interact with the pedestal to place the artefact upon it.","Follow Azzanadra to the cathedral, and speak with him. (You may go directly to the cathedral and wait for him.) {Chat: 5 No, let's bring in the eggs.}\n  - Alternatively, you can turn off run energy and click on him once, following him all the way to the cathedral.","Search the bookcases, chests, crates, and pews in the cathedral, including the upstairs balconies, for a light globe (see map below).","Talk to Azzanadra.","Pass through the western cathedral door.}}"],"t":"Senntisten"},{"n":"Combat gear and food}}{{checklis","r":"","s":["Within the city, put light globes on the light pedestals to illuminate the immediate area. When outside of an illuminated area, you will receive stacks of Shadows of the Empire debuff. The more stacks you have, the more damage you are dealt. Standing in an illuminated area will remove stacks of the debuff. This includes stepping into houses with lights. The ward only dims the light from the globes.","Light globes will persist when teleporting out and additional light globes are spread through the west district of the city. You don't need to obtain all light globes to complete the quest, so it may be more beneficial to juggle them as you explore new areas.","See the map for ward and objective locations.","Blood ward\n  - Head to the blood bank (north-western building in southern section).\n  - Inspect the blood bottle by the interior door leading to the blood ward.\n  - Search the old desk.\n  - Search the pile of books on the table near the entrance.\n  - Head north to the marketplace and enter the southern house south of the colosseum gateway.\n    - The correct house is marked with Bloodied Note on the map.\n  - Search the ransacked desk near the chimney for the Blood Bank Ledger.\n  - Return to the blood bank.\n  - Search the shelves for bottles of blood:\n    - Bottle of blood (human)\n    - Bottle of blood (unicorn)\n    - Bottle of blood (dragon)\n    - Bottle of blood (aviansie)\n  - Be prepared for a dangerous boss fight immediately after finishing the puzzle. The Blood Warden will heal from any damage-over-time abilities. Additionally, its special attack will cause it to heal over time.\n  - Inspect the blood bottle to start the puzzle, and add blood:\n    - 2/8 human blood\n    - 3/8 unicorn blood\n    - 1/8 dragon blood\n    - 2/8 aviansie blood\n  - Kill the Blood Warden\n  - Take the ward from the pedestal.\n  - Activate the blood bottle near the door to exit.\n  - Talk to Azzanadra with the ward. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Ice ward\n  - Go down two flights of stairs from the cathedral to the west, then enter to the house immediately to the south.\n  - Take the ice ward from the pedestal.\n  - Go back to the cathedral and talk to Azzanadra with the ward. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Shadow ward\n  - Ensure you have enough healing ability with you as you will take a lot of damage while returning the shadow ward. Each open house is to lower said stacks of damage.\n  - Go to the northern-most building, where the ward is located, and head upstairs.\n  - Take the journal on the desk to get the Inquisition Profiles.\n  - Read the Inquisition Profiles and complete the dialogue. {Chat: 1 Yes}\n  - Open the marked drawers as below. Start from the bottom and work your way up or zoom in for ease.\n  - Head downstairs and take the ward from the pedestal.\n  - Return to Azzanadra as fast as possible. Be prepared to take a lot of damage. Using a powerburst of acceleration will make this easier.\n  - Talk to Azzanadra with the ward. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Smoke ward\n  - The smoke ward can be found in the large building directly south of the ice ward on the map. As you approach an animation with gargoyle sentinels should play.\n  - Find and smash the stones to reveal the gargoyles sentinels. Smash them manually to complete the final blow, or automatically if relevant perk is available.\n    - Directly outside the arsenal, the building with the ward.\n    - Further west and south of the first, in a clearing in front of a house door.\n    - To the north in the market, the square containing the market stalls.\n    - West of the market, slightly south of the colosseum gateway.\n  - Return to the arsenal and take the ward from the pedestal.\n  - Talk to Azzanadra with the ward. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Wards"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Azzanadra and complete the dialogue."],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Civil War I (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Adrasteia (floor of the White Knights' Castle's eastern side). {Chat: Accept > Any}"],"t":"Letter from Anne Dimitri"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to Edgeville.","Talk to Anne Dimitri (just north of Quercus in the Wilderness).","Kill 144 demons in the Wilderness for the Gross Misconduct achievement if not already completed."],"t":"Meeting Anne Dimitri"},{"n":"A free space in backpack","r":"","s":["Talk to Anne Dimitri. (This is done automatically if you already had Gross Misconduct completed.)","Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Jerrod's offer"}]},"Civil War II (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Anne Dimitri (just north of Quercus in the Wilderness). {Chat: Accept}","Talk to Nikkel (west of the PvP hatch, west of Quercus). {Chat: 1 Discuss Civil War II. > Any}"],"t":"Contacting Anne Dimitri"},{"n":"A free space in backpack","r":"","s":["Talk to Anne Dimitri. Watch the cutscene.","Miniquest complete!"],"t":"The recording"}]},"Civil War III (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"Free slot in backpack","r":"","s":["Talk to Anne Dimitri, who is just north of Quercus in the Wilderness. {Chat: Accept}","Head to the Garden of Kharid and talk to Polletix. {Chat: 1 How's it going? (Civil War III)}\n  - If you haven't done so already, complete the Power Planter I achievement, which involves earning 250 Crux Eqal favour and purchasing the first unlock in Sydekix's Shop of Balance. You can earn favour by planting and harvesting herbs from any herb patch in the game, including the one in the Garden of Kharid. You can ask the daily herb from Polletix, and planting and harvesting the daily herb always grants the maximum of 50 favour per seed.\n  - If you hadn't completed the achievement before, talk to Polletix again. {Chat: 1 How's it going? (Civil War III)}","Return to Anne Dimitri and talk to her.","Head to the White Knights' Castle throne room (floor) and talk to Adrasteia.","Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Walkthrough"}]},"Clock Tower":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Brother Kojo at the Clock Tower located south-west on the path going south from Ardougne Zoo. {Chat: Accept}","Go into the central room and down the ladder.","Go through the northeast passage and look for a tile with four colours."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the northeast door closest to the dark grey tile and go as far east as possible.","There will be a cog surrounded by fire. With a bucket of water in your inventory or Ice gloves equipped, pick it up.","Place the black cog on the black spindle, next to the ladder you came down when you entered the dungeon."],"t":"Black cog"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go back to the tile room and head through the door by the red tile.","Go to the end of the passage and grab the cog in the room with the ogres.","Return to the entrance and go up the ladder, to the floor 1 and place the red cog on the red spindle."],"t":"Red cog"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Exit the clock tower.","Go just south of the Ardougne Zoo, near the camel enclosure, in a corner against the fence, and down the ladder.","Follow the path. Push the wall at the end and pick up the cog.","Climb the nearby ladder.","Re-enter the Clocktower north of you and climb the stairs to the floor, and place the blue cog on the blue spindle."],"t":"Blue cog"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to the basement","Enter the north-west door closest to the white tile.","Follow the western passage and pick up the rat poison.","Go up the middle path, and pull the western red lever on the southern wall to so that both prison doors are open.","Go through the gates and use the rat poison on the food trough, which is on the southern wall.","Wait for the game message 'They seem to be dying.' then head through the west gate and pick the cog up.","Climb up the ladder, enter the clock tower, and climb the stairs to the floor 3.","Place the white cog on the white spindle at the top of the clock tower."],"t":"White cog"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Report back to Brother Kojo, on the floor 1 of the Clock Tower.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Cold Front":{"sections":[{"n":"Free backpack slot","r":"","s":["Talk to the Queen of Snow at the snowball arena in Christmas Village. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to her again. {Chat: Any > Any > Accept}","Continue through the dialogue. {Chat: Any}","Inspect each of the three snowmen and go through all the options for all three. {Chat: 1 Inspect their head. > 2 Inspect their face. > 3 Inspect their equipment. > 4 Inspect their body.}","Talk to the Queen of Snow again.","Inspect each of the three snowmen again.","Talk to the Queen of Snow again and go through all the options. {Chat: 1 Delegate. > 2 Keep it simple. > 3 Delay. > 4 Prioritise. > 5 Be honest.}","Leave Cold Front using the quest marker. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Talking to the Queen of Snow"},{"n":"Chisel of conditional worth and 25 coal","r":"","s":["Use the chisel of conditional worth on the coal and make five pieces of 'perfect' coal.","Take 20 carrots from the bucket o' carrots near the hungry reindeer on the south-western wall outside of Diango's Workshop.","Use the chisel of conditional worth on the carrots to make a 'perfect' carrot.","Gather 10 branches by chopping fir trees.","Use the chisel of conditional worth on the branches to make two 'perfect' branches.","Return and talk to the Queen of Snow {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to the Queen of Snow again in the centre of the snowball arena."],"t":"Finding the perfect materials"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Make a snowball with one of the piles of snow and push it to the marked spot at the top of the hill. The snowball needs to be pushed so that it becomes a large snowball precisely when reaching the reticule on the top of the hill, requiring a total of eight pushes. {Chat: Any}\n  - You can't push diagonally, nor south from under the Queen of Snow.\n  - At any point, you can break the snowball down, and the pile of snow will reappear in the spot where you broke it down.","Repeat with another pile of snow to make an enormous snowball positioned next to the large snowball, requiring a total of 10 pushes.","Repeat with the remaining pile of snow to make an average snowball positioned next to the previous snowballs, requiring a total of five pushes.","Continue through the dialogue. {Chat: 3 She deserves support. Not Judgement. > 1 You taught her to feel ashamed for having needs. > 3 You made her this way. > Any > Any}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Constructing the perfect snowman"}]},"Cold War":{"sections":[{"n":"10 oak planks and 10 steel nails","r":"","s":["Talk to Larry near the penguin enclosure in the Ardougne Zoo. {Chat: 1 Cold War > Accept}","Talk to Larry again when carrying 10 oak planks and 10 steel nails. {Chat: 1 Cold War > 1 Yes, I have all the materials. > 1 Yes}","Use an oak plank on the firm snow patch.","Attempt to enter the bird hide structure to cover it in snow with spade. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Enter snowy bird hide.","Take note of the emotes the left penguin is doing. The snowy bird hide can be re-entered to watch again if needed. You can check the quest journal later in the quest if you aren't sure.","Talk to Larry. {Chat: Any}","Travel using the nearby boat. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Talk to Larry once on the dock."],"t":"Penguin spotting"},{"n":"Clockwork (or a steel bar to make one), silk and plank (+1 of each material if you wish to make a suit for the subsequent quests now)","r":"","s":["Make a clockwork suit on crafting table 3 or 4 in a player-owned house, which requires a clockwork, regular plank, and some silk.\n  - Making an extra suit at this point is optional for the subsequent quests.","Return to Larry (in Ardougne Zoo or north of Fremennik Province lodestone). {Chat: 1 Cold War > 1 Yes, I have it. > 1 Yes}","Talk to Larry on the iceberg. {Chat: 2 It looks like a warning message to keep us away. > 1 Yes}\n  - Accept teleport to the Ardougne Zoo."],"t":"Clockwork penguin"},{"n":"Clockwork suit","r":"","s":["Unequip cape and weapons and use the tuxedo-time option on Larry.","Enter the penguin pen and talk to the penguin.","Use the greeting emotes from earlier. If you haven't noted down the emotes, look in your quest log after you've talked to the penguin.","Read the mission report and exit the penguin pen.","Talk to Larry twice. {Chat: 1 Cold War}"],"t":"Suit up!"},{"n":"Clockwork suit, raw cod (or a ring of charos)}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["Go to the west section of the Lumbridge cow field by the gate and steal a cowbell from a dairy cow by using the steal-cowbell option for later on in the quest.\n  - Players without 15 Thieving can get a cowbell by talking to the dairy cow in Zanaris.","Talk to Larry inside the sheep pen west of Fred the Farmer's house in Lumbridge.","Enter penguin suit by right clicking Larry and selecting 'tuxedo time' or using the clockwork suit on Larry and talk to the penguins disguised as a sheep (the sheep with flippers).","Do the greeting emotes.","Talk to sheep penguin again.","Talk to Larry twice. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Equip the ring of charos or have a raw cod in the inventory and use the tuxedo-time option on Larry and enter the penguin suit again once at Ardougne Zoo.","Enter penguin pen and talk to penguin. {Chat: 1 The penguins in Lumbridge refuse to talk to me. > 2 I must have left the outpost before they gave out the phrase. > 1 Sure!}","Talk to Larry twice. {Chat: 1 Cold War}"],"t":"Incognito!"},{"n":"Clockwork suit","r":"","s":["Go back to the Lumbridge sheep pen.","Enter penguin suit by right clicking Larry and selecting 'tuxedo time' or using the clockwork suit on Larry.","Talk to sheep penguin.","Talk to Larry twice.","Talk to Fred the Farmer nearby. {Chat: 2 I need to talk to you about penguins. > Any}\n  - Note: Chat options may vary for some players. Choose the option for penguins.","Enter penguin suit and talk to sheep penguin again. {Chat: Any}","Talk to Larry twice. {Chat: 1 Yes}"],"t":"Intelligence"},{"n":"Clockwork suit, swamp tar, 5 feathers","r":"","s":["Dismiss any pets or followers.","Talk to Larry on the iceberg and get in the penguin suit again and talk to KGP Agent north-west of Larry.","Do the greeting emotes.","Talk to Noodle twice. {Chat: 1 Yeah, I got it.}","Talk to KGP Agent.\n  - Make sure you finish the dialogue or you won't be able to enter the penguin lair.","Investigate avalanche just north of KGP Agent.","Enter the first west room.","Talk to KGP Agent.","Exit room through the west door and then through the north door.","Walk north to the agility course."],"t":"Surprise, surprise"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb down the steps and into the water.\n  - Stepping across the checkered flag should automatically drop you in water.","Avoid the moving ice in the water.","Climb the stepping stone at the end.","Jump across the next stones until you reach the other side.","After crossing, continue on the path until you come to an arch covered in icicles. Use the tread softly option to pass. This must be repeated several times at each arch. Players who fail will be hit with a small amount of damage.","Next, climb up the ice. This can be very annoying, as players lose 20 life points each time they fail, and the failure rate is surprisingly high. For players with low Agility levels, a small amount of food may help.","After that, a short cutscene will play of the player sliding down a hill.","Talk to the Agility Instructor to leave the gate.","Leave the outpost and talk to Larry on the iceberg (twice)."],"t":"Agility course"},{"n":"Clockwork suit, mahogany plank, leather, cowbell","r":"","s":["Enter the penguin suit and return to the outpost.","Enter the second east room and talk to Ping and Pong.","Return to Larry and exit penguin suit.","Use a mahogany plank on the leather.","Enter penguin suit and return to Ping and Pong.","Talk to them again. {Chat: 2 Yes.}","Operate the control panel in the north-west corner of the main hall.","Enter the War Room to the east."],"t":"Berg bards"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill an Icelord and exit the pen.","Climb the chasm to the east in the room.","Talk to Larry.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Conclusive evidence"}]},"Contact!":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the High Priest in Sophanem {Chat: Accept}, then after the cutscene, {Chat: 5 Is there any way into Menaphos from below?}.","Talk to Jex in front of the building in the north-east corner of the city.","Climb down the ladder in the church east of Jex, and down again in the second trapdoor.\n  - You can speak to one of the Sophanem Guards here if you still need a torch, they will sell you one for 200 coins.\n  - Protect from magic prayers and auto-retaliate off is recommended.","Follow the red line through the maze (pictured right). You can avoid traps by clicking on them, or walking around them where appropriate.\n  - You can use the high contrast mode to make the traps easier to spot, except for the pitfalls.\n  - For high level players you can take the ladder in the north, marked (2) on the map.\n  - Then run south west to ladder marked (6) to skip most of the maze.\n  - Run east while avoiding the traps, north, and then west again and climb down the ladder.","Run towards the larger room.","Search Kaleef's body and read the parchment.","Talk to Maisa to the west. {Chat: 2 Draynor Village > 4 Ozan and Leela.}"],"t":"Tunnels under Sophanem"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Osman inside the Al Kharid palace. {Chat: 2 I want to talk to you about Sophanem. > ~ > 3 It would drive a wedge between the Menaphite cities.}","Prepare to fight a level 86 foe - a giant scarab.","Talk to Osman outside the northern Sophanem gate. {Chat: 3 I know of a secret entrance to the north.}","Run all the way back to Kaleef's body."],"t":"Osman"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill the giant scarab and take the Keris.\n  - Optional: Players with level 50 Attack may head back up the ladder and kill a scarab mage or locust rider with the Keris dagger. This completes the Ludikeris achievement.","Return to Sophanem and talk to the High Priest (there is no shortcut back, teleporting is possible).","Quest complete!"],"t":"The final fight"}]},"Cook's Assistant":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Obtain the following items: a bucket of milk, a pot of flour, and an egg:\n  - Buy from the Grand Exchange for Pot of flour GE price + Bucket of milk GE price + Egg GE price coins.\n  - Create them yourself:\n    - Bucket of milk: use a bucket on a dairy cow or prized dairy cow in the Lumbridge cow field.\n    - Egg: spawns at the chicken farm north-west of the cow field.\n    - Pot of flour: with an empty pot (found by the Cook in Lumbridge Castle), head to the Mill Lane Mill next to the cow pens and pick some grain from outside. Climb up to the top floor of the mill and use the grain with the hopper, then pull the lever. Climb down and take the flour from the flour bin with an empty pot.","Talk to the Cook in Lumbridge Castle's kitchen with all the items in the backpack. {Chat: 1 What's Wrong? > Accept > 1 Can I help?}","Congratulations, quest complete!"],"t":"Walkthrough"}]},"Corporate Egg-spionage":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Easter Bunny outside their house in the Blooming Burrow. {Chat: 1 Do you have a quest for me? > Accept}"],"t":"Learning about a business opportunity"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the Egg Plant on the western side of the burrow and talk to either the Easter Bunny, Angus Almond, Carmilla Caramel, or Chad Berry.","Talk to the Easter Bunny just north."],"t":"Inside the factory"},{"n":"Free backpack space","r":"","s":["Just outside of the Egg Plant, north-east of Nougat Bunny's stall, confront the Suspicious Rabbit.","Go east by passing the two bridges and then midway south (north of the Thieving icons on the map) and confront the Loitering Hare.","Go all the way south-east and confront the Odd Jackrabbit from behind.","Talk to the Easter Bunny."],"t":"Confrontation"},{"n":"Three free backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Talk to Count Rivance outside of Gerrant's Fishy Business at the eastern wall."],"t":"Translation"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Easter Bunny. {Chat: 1 Yes!}","Talk to either Angus Almond, Carmilla Caramel, or Chad Berry. {Chat: 1 Carmilla has been replacing your gold with chocolate coins! > 2 You pay your employees overtime! > 2 You've been cooking the books! > 3 You have an almond allergy!}","Talk to the Easter Bunny.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Corporate synergy"}]},"Creature of Fenkenstrain":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Dr Fenkenstrain at his castle to the north-east of Canifis. {Chat: Accept > 4 Braindead. > 4 Grave-digging.}","Go upstairs by the eastern or western staircase and read from the bookcases in the western and eastern rooms:\n  - \"The Joy Of Grave Digging\" in the west bookcase. {Chat: 4 The Joy of Gravedigging}\n  - \"Handy Maggot Avoidance Techniques\" in the east bookcase. {Chat: 3 Handy Maggot Avoidance Techniques}\n  - Use the marble amulet on the obsidian amulet in your backpack to form the star amulet."],"t":"Gravedigger"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Equip your ghostspeak amulet.","Talk to the Gardener Ghost on the floor 1 in the northern side. {Chat: 2 What happened to your head?}","Lead him south-east into the Haunted Woods. (Don't worry about him getting stuck he will teleport back to you)","Periodically talk to him for directions and dig at graves by choosing the \"Dig\" option until the decapitated head is found.\n  - The grave is about 10 squares east and 5 squares south of the fairy ring. Choose the \"Dig\" option on the nearby grave."],"t":"Decapitated head"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the tavern in Canifis.","Take a pickled brain off the table for 50 coins or by using Telekinetic Grab on it.\n  - Telekinetic grabbing the brain completes a medium Morytania achievement, Brain Bending.","Use the decapitated head on the pickled brain."],"t":"Pickled brain"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head east of Fenkenstrain's Castle to the tombstones just west of the Musician.","Use the star amulet on the easternmost memorial.","Push the memorial to enter Fenkenstrain's Dungeon.","Kill an experiment creature with a wolf's body and woman's head and pick up the cavern key.","Continue north-west and open the entrance.","Go up the ladder.","Go north and right-click dig on all 3 of the graves to obtain torso, arms and legs"],"t":"Arms, legs and torso"},{"n":"A needle, 5 spools of thread, 3 spools of bronze wire, and a silver bar","r":"","s":["Teleport back to Canifis and talk to Dr Fenkenstrain in his castle. {Chat: 1 I have some body parts for you.}","Talk to Dr Fenkenstrain again to turn in needle and thread.","Talk to the Gardener Ghost to receive the shed key. {Chat: 2 Do you know where the key to the shed is?}","Enter the shed next to Gardener Ghost, and search the cupboard for a garden brush.","Take 3 garden canes from the pile just outside.","Use the 3 garden canes on the brush for an extended brush, consuming 3 spools of bronze wire.","Go up the west stairs, and use the extended brush on the fireplace in the nearby room for a conductor mould.","At any furnace, make the conductor with a silver bar. In the smelting interface, look under the 'casting metals & glass' section. Under the 'silver casting' subsection of that section, there will be an option to make a conductor.\n  - Be sure to make only one, as the furnace will try to use multiple bars.","Go back to the castle and go up either staircase.","Go up the ladder in the southern room.","Repair the lightning conductor."],"t":"Lightning"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Dr Fenkenstrain.","Go upstairs and use the ladder in the central northern room.","Talk to Fenkenstrain's Monster.","Pickpocket Dr Fenkenstrain.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Lord Rologarth"}]},"Crocodile Tears":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"enchanted water tiara, waterskins, or other desert heat protection","s":["Bring Leela to Senliten by talking to her along the fence north of the prison in Draynor Village. Agree to travel with her and you will end up in front of Senliten.\n  - If you sent her to Senliten without following her, travel to the Uzer Mastaba (the pyramid south of Uzer) via some other means. {Chat: 1 Head directly to the Pharaoh Queen.}","Speak with Senliten. {Chat: 3 Talk about Crocodile Tears. > 3/4 Where are you going with this? > Accept}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"A cat, kitten, or hellcat","r":"","s":["Talk to the Sphinx in Sophanem with your cat (do not wear a catspeak amulet or cramulet). {Chat: 2 Can you tell me about the gods of the Menaphites? > 3 Tell me about the minor gods. > 3 Tell me about Crondis. > 2 Thanks, I think I now have a better understanding of this place.}","Talk to Jex, who is north-east of the Sphinx. {Chat: 2 Could you tell me more about the minor gods? > 3 Could you tell me more about Crondis? > 1 Could you tell me more about Crondis's connection with crocodiles? > 2 Could you tell me more about Crondis's followers? > 3 Could you tell me more about the Crondis's influence over the desert?}","Return to Senliten. {Chat: 3 Talk about Crocodile Tears.}","Right click Leela to return to the surface."],"t":"Learning about Crondis"},{"n":"rope","r":"enchanted water tiara, waterskins, or other desert heat protection","s":["Enter the temple again but use the explore option. {Chat: 2 Explore the temple.}","Head north and click the ship to get the dowsing rod (Pick up relic Massive stone boat).","Click the dowsing rod and follow the arrow to the following locations in the desert, until your character starts talking, before moving to the next location.",":If you encounter a bug where the dowsing rod suddenly no longer functions, you must destroy it and acquire a new one from the boat inside the temple before repeating each location.\n  - The oasis just north-west of the temple.\n  - The oasis by the Camel Warriors, east of Sophanem.\n  - The oasis near the Bedabin Camp.","Return to Senliten. {Chat: 3 Talk about Crocodile Tears.}","Head to the waterfall north of the Dominion Tower and climb it.","Walk north through both sets of double doors","Talk to the spirits (Tirrie, Nirrie, or Hallak) in the north part of the cave. {Chat: 1 I need your help to charge the dowsing rod.}"],"t":"Dowsing for Crondis"},{"n":"charged dowsing rod","r":"","s":["Talk to Portmaster Kags in the Menaphos Port district on the southwest pier by the house portal. {Chat: 3 Transport to Crondis's pyramid.}","Enter Crondis's pyramid.","Talk to the High Priest of Crondis."],"t":"Dealing with Crondis"},{"n":"fishing bait","r":"enchanted water tiara or other desert heat protection, weight-reducing clothes, food if you fail Agility obstacles or take desert heat damage","s":["You must wait until after Crondis asks for each item before gathering it or the requirement will not be satisfied.","Catch a raw beltfish either on the northwest or southeast pier of the Menaphos Port district or in the VIP skilling area.\n  - If using Bait and Switch first catch a beltfish, then obtain it via trading or bank raw.","Return to Crondis {Chat: 1 Yes, of course.}","Cut two acadia logs at the acadia trees in the Menaphos Imperial district.","Return to Crondis. {Chat: 1 Yes, of course.}","Collect four pyramid tops from the Agility Pyramid.","Return to Crondis. {Chat: 1 Yes, of course.}","Catch eight plover birds in southern Sophanem. Any sort of double drop will not count for this. It must be 8 catches, not just 8 plover birds.\n  - Sophanem Slayer Dungeon teleport and run south is the fastest way to get there.","Return to Crondis. {Chat: 1 Yes, of course.}","Without teleporting after buying, purchase at least 20 (preferably 24) croc ices from Rokuh in Nardah near the fountain to ensure you still have 16 left to turn in (because one croc ice is eaten automatically every 15 seconds, and teleporting with them turns them into chocolatey goo).\n  - Run west and Nardah magic carpet to Menaphos.\n  - Use the Merchant District Shifting Tombs to get to the Port District and return to Crondis' pyramid.\n  - They do not need to all be collected in one trip."],"t":"Crondis fetch quests"},{"n":"Combat gear and food for fighting Ukunduka","r":"Full backpack of food or healing potions, as this challenger utilises a special move enabling it to steal your food items, one by one.","s":["Talk to Crondis. Use any chat option except 1 for all dialogue boxes.\n  - If not already equipped for combat, leave the conversation just before the player yells \"THAT'S ENOUGH!\" to prepare for the fight.\n  - Talk to Crondis again to continue forward to the fight when you return. {Chat: 2 THAT'S ENOUGH!}","Kill Ukunduka (stay out of melee distance or use Saradomin brews). There is a safe spot on the stairs leading up to Crondis.","Talk to the High Priest of Crondis.","Return to Senliten.","After the cutscene, speak with Senliten. {Chat: 3 Talk about Crocodile Tears.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Boss fight"}]},"Curse of the Black Stone":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use the ring of kinship to quickly teleport to Daemonheim. You can get one for free as you'll need to visit Daemonheim many times during the quest.","Talk to Bryll Thoksdottir beside Marmaros the rewards trader in Daemonheim. {Chat: 2 [Curse of the Black Stone] > Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"Combat gear and a backpack space","r":"","s":["Travel to Waiko via Quartermaster Gully in the northern part of Port Sarim.","Talk to Zhuka (bamboo merchant) at the southern part of the marketplace. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Jade Spider?}","Travel to Whale's Maw by talking to Quartermaster Gully (via travel option and select Whale's Maw).","Talk to Sea Witch Kaula at the northwestern part of the island. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Jade Spider}","Dig the lump of sand near the western-most ship. {Chat: 2 Get on with tortle hunting.}","Check the tortle to the south to obtain a note from the Jade Spider.","Travel to Tuai Leit via Quartermaster Gully.","Speak to Sensei Seaworth {Chat: 1 Ask about the Jade Spider.}, who is south-west at the market.","Travel to Goshima via Quartermaster Gully. {Chat: 1 Search for the Jade spider.}","Kill all 12 crassians on the island.","Open and go through the Gate of Goshima and talk to Madame Shih (the Jade Spider) in the easternmost building. {Chat: 1 She mentioned something}\n  - If you've already completed Temple of Aminishi at least once, you may skip the battle. {Chat: 1 Skip the dungeon.}\n  - Otherwise complete the Temple of Aminishi and defeat and Seiryu the Azure Serpent before returning back to Madame Shih."],"t":"The Jade Spider"},{"n":"Uncut dragonstone, rope","r":"'Chipped' Varrock teleport or Dave's spellbook, ring of kinship, dragon trinkets, or Dungeoneering cape","s":["Talk to Mr Mordaut in his office in the basement of Varrock Museum that is accessed behind the stairs. {Chat: 2 [Curse of the Black Stone]}\n  - Use a 'chipped' Varrock teleport, Dave's spellbook, the Varrock lodestone or Fort Forinthry lodestone to get to the museum quickly.","Go to Daemonheim and investigate the fireplace to the east of the fountain to find a carved dragonstone (left).","Cut your uncut dragonstone to create the carved dragonstone (right). {Chat: 1 Create right eye.}","Use either the left or right carved dragonstone on the fountain. {Chat: 1 Place the stone in the eye socket.}","Enter the crumbling watchtower to the west.","Talk to Hannibus in the west room.","Head to the room with the entrance to the adamant dragon dungeon in the Brimhaven Dungeon between the fire giants and black demons, and north of the iron and steel dragons.\n  - Either via the dungeon entrance just west of the Karamja lodestone and navigating to the room\n  - via a metallic dragon trinkets' teleport option {Chat: 5 Adamant Dragons - Brimhaven Adamant Dungeon}\n  - via the Dungeoneering cape teleport {Chat: 0 More... > 6 Brimhaven metal dragon dungeon} and heading north-west\n  - with the Kethsi ring.","If you used a Kethsi ring or metallic trinket to teleport directly into the dungeon, first go out by ascending the stairs.","Enter the adamant dragon dungeon {Chat: 1 [Curse of the Black Stone]} and investigate the mithril smelter on the easternmost wall of the easternmost room to obtain a metallic object.\n  - If you have Eek with you, you may investigate the adamant smelter for some extra dialogue.","Talk to the adamant dragon in the south-western room to heat the metallic object. {Chat: 1 Can you heat this metal? > 3 Your baby is cold, warm her up.}","With a rope in the backpack, investigate one of the pits north of the entrance. {Chat: 2 Attach a rope and drop the heated metal into the pit.}","Investigate the dragon head near the stairs. {Chat: 1 Smash the tablet on the teeth.}"],"t":"The dungeon"},{"n":"Combat gear","r":"Ring of kinship, Goshima teleport","s":["Head back to Kerapac's Lab by entering the crumbling watchtower in Daemonheim.","Investigate the effigy shelves in the room with Hannibus. {Chat: 2 I'm looking for clues.}","Referencing the image to the right, activate the following dragonkin statues in any order: 1, 3, 5","Enter the portal in the northern room. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Kerapac.","Talk to Bryll Thoksdottir back in Daemonheim. {Chat: 3 [Curse of the Black Stone]}\n  - If you have already completed Dragonkin Laboratory at least once, you may skip the battle. {Chat: 2 Skip the dungeon.}\n  - Otherwise complete the Dragonkin Laboratory and defeat the Black Stone Dragon before returning back to Bryll Thosdottir.","Travel back to Goshima. {Chat: 1 [Curse of the Black Stone]} (A cutscene will start)","Head back to Daemonheim and talk to Bryll Thoksdottir. {Chat: 2 [Curse of the Black Stone]}"],"t":"Kerapac's lab"},{"n":"Law rune, raw fish, and two backpack spaces","r":"Traveller's necklace or wicked hood, Mask of the Yellow Wyrm, ring of kinship","s":["Speak to Wizard Myrtle near the Wizards' Tower. {Chat: 1 Curse of the Black Stone. > 4 Can you help me get the fish now? > 1 Yes.}\n  - Use the traveller's necklace or wicked hood to navigate to the Wizards' Tower, or use the fairy ring DIS to teleport, or run to it from the Draynor lodestone.","Give Wizard Myrtle any raw fish and a law rune to obtain small raw sillago.","Fill the empty enchanted \"vacuum\" vial on the Ice Mountain near Edgeville.","Dry the wet seaweed while standing near the huge fountain at Abbey of St. Elspeth Citharede.","Combine the potion of waterbreathing and drink it.","Return to Daemonheim and speak with Hannibus next to the heroes of the Shadow Reef and the Fremennik ship (Shadow reef) on the east coast.\n  - If he is not there, instead talk to Bryll Thoksdottir. {Chat: 3 [Curse of the Black Stone]}"],"t":"Enchanted \"vacuum\" vial"},{"n":"","r":"'Chipped' Varrock teleport; Desert amulet 2,3,or 4 or the Heart teleport; ring of kinship","s":["Travel to the Edgeville lodestone to activate the artefact northwest. {Chat: 1 Yes - Meet with Hannibus.}","Talk to Mr Mordaut at the Varrock Museum. {Chat: 2 [Curse of the Black Stone]}","Travel to the Heart of Gielinor to meet with Vindicta. {Chat: 1 Yes - Meet with Vindicta.}\n  - You may need to leave the dungeon via the lift, and re-enter for the chat option to appear.","Talk to Bryll Thoksdottir near the ring of kinship's teleport location {Chat: 2 [Curse of the Black Stone]} and then Quartermaster Gully near the Heroes of the Shadow Reef (you may talk to him at Port Sarim)."],"t":"Preparing for war"},{"n":"","r":"Arc journal or Waiko teleport","s":["Travel to Waiko and speak to Steven's wife the seagull in the north-east (top of northernmost rock pillar)","Speak to the 6 seagulls (locations on the map) to find evidence.\n  - On a water barrel near the Khan's house, on the eastern part of the island\n  - In the village, on a water barrel east of the southern pier\n  - On the southern pier, on a water barrel\n  - On a crate in the shipwreck, near the western pier\n  - On a crate on the western pier\n  - Inside of a cage on the northern pier","Go back to Steven's wife and speak to her."],"t":"Marriage counselling"},{"n":"Disguise to enter the Black Knights' Fortress; combat gear","r":"Dragon trinkets or Dungeoneering cape; ring of charos (a); ring of kinship; master archaeologist's outfit","s":["Talk to Quartermaster Gully at the war table, east of Daemonheim.","Talk to Bryll Thoksdottir.","Talk to Bosun Higgs.","Talk to Lieutenant Crane next to the map table in the Black Knights' Base in the very south of Taverley Dungeon {Chat: 1 Evie sent me.}\n  - Teleport via an Archaeology teleport or the master outfit {Chat: 0 Collectors > 4 Isaura} and heading south.\n  - Via the Dungeoneering cape {Chat: 0 More... > 1 Taverley blue dragon dungeon} and heading east through the gate, then south.","Run north-west of the Edgeville lodestone to reach the Black Knights' Fortress.","Talk to the fortress guard at the entrance of the fortress while wearing the disguise.","Interact with Tessa's suit of armour in the western barracks room.","Head to the north west corner and head up the stairs.","Talk to the slave standing along the north wall on the floor 2 of the Black Knights' Fortress.","Talk to Lieutenant Crane about Tessa:\n  - If wearing a ring of charos (a) lie to skip the steps to free Tessa. {Chat: 2 [Lie - Ring of Charos] She's fine. > 1 Yes, I just want to kill the ambassador.}\n  - Otherwise {Chat: 1 She's a slave.} and proceed with these steps:\n    - Return to the fortress and interact with Tessa's suit of armour.\n    - Head upstairs to smuggle out Tessa. {Chat: 3 Pick lock.}\n    - Give her the suit of armour. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 Yes. > Any}\n    - Return to Lieutenant Crane.\n    - Head back to Daemonheim and speak to Bosun Higgs at the war table.\n    - Talk to Commandant Bletchley in the Black Knights' Fortress on the floor 2. He is standing along the north wall.\n    - Talk to Lieutenant Crane."],"t":"Elite forces"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Bryll Thoksdottir near the war table in east Daemonheim.\n  - If you have already completed the dungeon, skip the battle. {Chat: 2 Skip the dungeon.}\n  - Otherwise, choose any option for your speech. {Chat: Any}\n  - Complete the Shadow Reef.\n  - If this is your first time completing the dungeon, travel back to Bryll Thoksdottir after defeating the Ambassador."],"t":"The Shadow Reef"}]},"Damage Control (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to Waiko.","Talk to Bosun Higgs who is next to your ship (if you have just completed the Harbinger miniquest you may need to relog for the chat option to show up). {Chat: 1 Damage Control miniquest. > Accept}","Talk to Rosie in the Waiko marketplace for a ship repair kit in exchange for 2,500 chimes.","Talk to Bosun Higgs to set sail. {Chat: 1 Damage Control miniquest.}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Collect the 6 cannon parts at the locations shown, while avoiding the malignant entity.","Take the Goshima note hanging on the left wooden pillar next to the gate entrance.","Talk to Bosun Higgs. {Chat: 1 Damage Control miniquest.}"],"t":"Cannon parts"}]},"Daughter of Chaos":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Adrasteia in the White Knights' Castle's throne room (floor, east side). {Chat: Accept > 2 I'll see it done.}","Talk to Anne Dimitri downstairs 1 floor in the interrogation room (floor, centre). {Chat: Any}","Teleport to Edgeville.","Cross the Wilderness wall north of the Grand Exchange underwall tunnel.\n  - Make sure PVP is turned off. Most of the quest takes place in instances."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Anne Dimitri. {Chat: 1 I'm ready.}","Talk to Anne Dimitri again after arriving at the abandoned camp.","Investigate 3 points of interest. (yellow dots on minimap)","Talk to Anne Dimitri.","Capture 6 memory fragments.","Interact with the Restored Memory twice.","As Moia:\n  - Talk to Bilrach in the west.\n  - Kill the 9 enemies.\n    - You have Vault, Drain, and Blast abilities that you can trigger with the buttons on your screen (not the ability bar).\n    - Use Vault to escape the area of effect of chaos rifts.\n    - Use Drain as often as possible for healing. This ability is channelled. Moia will be uncommanded for a brief time by running to the target as this ability needs to be use semi-close to the enemy.\n    - Use Blast as often as possible near enemies to deal extra damage.\n    - If you die, you can lower the combat difficulty at any point of the quest when restarting the battle at Anne Dimitri in Wilderness.\n    - Optionally, use the health orbs after killing any of the 9 required enemies.\n  - Talk to Bilrach again."],"t":"Abandoned camp"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Anne Dimitri. {Chat: 4 We should move on.}","Talk to Anne Dimitri again.","Inspect 3 points of interest.","Talk to Anne Dimitri.","Capture 6 memory fragments.","Interact with the Restored Memory twice.","As Moia:\n  - Kill the 6 enemies as in the previous section.\n  - Talk to the wounded cultist in the south-western corner of the isle."],"t":"Red Dragon Isle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Anne Dimitri.","Interact with the Restored Memory.","As Moia:\n  - Kill Avaryss, the Unceasing using the abilities as in previous sections. She periodically summons two greater demons that can be killed for health orbs."],"t":"Wilderness Crater"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Moia. {Chat: Any > Any}","Talk to Trindine. {Chat: 2 I'll report back to Adrasteia.}"],"t":"Confronting Moia"},{"n":"Three free spaces in backpack","r":"","s":["Talk to Adrasteia in the White Knights' Castle's throne room (floor, east side).","Quest complete!"],"t":"Reporting back"}]},"Dead and Buried":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Raptor in Fort Forinthry. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Dead and Buried'. > Accept}","Continue with the portal in front of the Town Hall to enter. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to the Herald of Varrock. {Chat: ~ > ~ > ~ > 4 (Conclude interview.) > 1 Yes, I've asked enough questions.}"],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"14 acadia frames, 6 stone wall segments.","r":"","s":["Talk to Bill. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Dead and Buried'.}","Check plans on the Fort Forinthry blueprints and select Ranger's Workroom (Tier 1).","Build the Ranger's Workroom in the south-west near the Guardhouse.","Talk to guard captain Sofía in the newly-built Ranger's Workroom.","Talk to the Raptor. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Dead and Buried'.}"],"t":"Building the workroom"},{"n":"Combat gear, food, and two free backpack spaces.","r":"Varrock Teleport","s":["Continue with the portal by the Wilderness crypt entrance outside the northern gate","Talk to the Raptor.","Collect six out of nine materials from the six spooky holes in the western room.\n  - Kill the three material ghouls that spawn to collect the last three materials.","Construct the bridge near the Raptor.","Cross the bridge and investigate the ancient door.","Push either of the two pillars. Switch to the Raptor and push the other pillar to unlock the door.","Search the ancient door to receive the dragonkin device.","Speak to the Raptor to show him the device.","Go to the Varrock Library and continue with the portal by the entrance. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Retrieving the dragonkin device"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Reldo for a potion of dreamless sleep.","Drink the potion, then inspect the dragonkin device to enter the dream. {Chat: 1 Enter dream.}","The aim is to step on the pressure plates, unlock all the boulders, and enter the final barrier. As the player, you can push and pull boulders one tile at a time. As the Raptor, you can push boulders five tiles, and pull by one tile.\n  - It might glitch and not show the boulder, although it is there and interactable.\n  - For rooms that don't have enough boulders, you need to step on a pressure plate to spawn one."],"t":"In the dream"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Player steps on a pressure plate.","Switch to the Raptor and step on the other pressure plate.","Pull and push the boulder to the middle plate outside boulder gate 2."],"t":"Boulder puzzle 1 (going clockwise)"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["The player steps on a pressure plate.","Switch to the Raptor and step on the other pressure plate.","Pull and push both boulders to the outer pressure plates at boulder gate 3."],"t":"Boulder puzzle 2"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["The player steps on a pressure plate.","Switch to the Raptor and step on the other pressure plate.","Walk through to boulder gate 4."],"t":"Boulder puzzle 3"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["The player steps on either of the two furthest pressure plates from the gate.","Switch to the Raptor and push the boulder to any pressure plate next to the gate.","Repeat for the other pressure plate.","The player steps on the pressure plate by the gate.","Switch to the Raptor and step on the pressure plate by the gate.","Walk through."],"t":"Boulder puzzle 4"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["The Raptor steps on the western-most pressure plate.","The player pulls the boulder and pushes it to the second pressure plate (going clockwise).","The player steps on the third pressure plate, and the second boulder appears.\n  - If the second boulder does not spawn, exit to the lobby and continue again with the portal at the library.","The player pushes and pulls the boulder to the fourth pressure plate.","The player steps on the third pressure plate to open the gate.","Run to the strange girl to start a cutscene."],"t":"Boulder puzzle 5"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go through all the chat options, then delve deeper into the dream.","Interact with the dim light.","Lower the health of the Nightmares as the player, then swap to the Raptor to deal the finishing blow.\n  - Currently this part is glitched if you are in a group, which will prevent the player from progressing as expected. Simply leaving the group and re-entering the instance will allow progress.","Interact with the pillar of light and talk with the character that appears.","Continue on the path, and repeat the same process with the dim lights along the way.","Finally, speak to the Raptor that appears.","Read the ancient writings on the wall at the end of the path."],"t":"The nightmare"},{"n":"10 free inventory spaces}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["Finish talking to the Raptor, then go back to the crypt in the Wilderness.","Continue with the portal in front of the crypt.","Enter the ancient door, then investigate the map table in the central room.","Kill fetid zombies around the crypt and collect 10 map pieces. Do not leave the crypt.","Deposit onto the map table to start the puzzle.","Complete the map (shown below) using the same strategy as for solving a puzzle box or sliding puzzle.\n  - Speaking to the Raptor to turn on accessibility mode is advised; this will highlight tiles while they are in the correct position.","Finish the following dialogue with the Raptor before continuing."],"t":"Back to the crypt"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Overseer Siv in the Command Centre back at Fort Forinthry. {Chat: 2 Talk about quests.}","Talk to the Raptor to finish the quest."],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Deadliest Catch":{"sections":[{"n":"1 space in your backpack","r":"","s":["Talk to Jones the fisherman outside the Fishing Guild bank. {Chat: Accept > 1 You need an extra rower? > 2 You need a giant harpoon? > 3 You need a particular sea chart? > 4 Can you tell me more about the Thalassus? > 2 That's horrible! > 5 Actually, I'll be right back.}","Pickpocket the Master fisher (near the guild entrance) for the sea chart. This may take several attempts.","Talk to the Master fisher. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Deadliest Catch.}"],"t":"Getting Started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Linza who is east of the Fishing Guild in Hemenster.","Go to the Tower of Life south of Ardougne. (Fairy ring DJP or Kandarin monastery Teleport)","Talk to 'The Guns'.","Talk to Bonafido for builder's tea.","East of the tower, pick the southern most of the 3 lowland heather bunch directly east of the Tower of Life. Only one is needed.","Use the heather on the tea.","Talk to 'The Guns'. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Preparing a Hunt"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head back to the Fishing Guild and talk to Jones. {Chat: 1 Lead the way!}","Track the Thalassus via the wreckage. Dismiss your follower if you have one.\n  - The track is always the same during the same session, even after a reset.\n    - Optional: Each shipwreck has some loot, but you can only take 3 \"items\" in total. PC: Right click and loot; Mobile: Long press and loot.\n      - Note: The remaining loot will sink when the loot window has been closed for that specific shipwreck."],"t":"Fish Finding"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the group of mermaids. {Chat: 2 The Thalassus has eaten Jones the mighty fisherman. > 1 It should, he's been hunting for decades. > 3 Very horrid! After he's killed the Thalassus, he'll probably come after you. > 2 Trust me, I'm a great adventurer, I should know. > 3 Did I mention Jones has a harpoon with him? > 1 It's no ordinary harpoon.}"],"t":"The Mermaids"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Track the Thalassus again. Note that it takes a different path this time.\n  - Optional: It is possible to loot 3 items again.","Talk to Jones.","Talk to Linza. She is at her smithing corner like previously.","Talk to Jones again.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Rescuing Jones"}]},"Dealing with Scabaras":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"Rope","s":["Talk to the High Priest in Sophanem. {Chat: 1 What news? > Accept}","Climb the ladder behind the altar.","After the cutscene, talk to Maisa. {Chat: 1 Why are you here?}","Talk to the High Priest.","Go to the south-east of the Agility Pyramid, take the rope shortcut just to the east.\n  - If you haven't unlocked this shortcut, enter to the swamp south-east of Sophanem and go north, then climb the fallen pillar and the low wall. Last, use the rope on the rock.","Climb over the low wall and talk to Lead archaeologist Abigail and Assistant archaeologist Kerner by the tents. Read their questions carefully and always round down the answer. {Chat: 1 I've had dealings with his sort before; feel free to test me.}","Talk to them again for an empty crate."],"t":"Running errands"},{"n":"Ugthanki dung, bronze gear, bucket (if you do not have Ugthanki dung)","r":"","s":["Fetch the bronze gear that are written in your quest journal.","At this point, if you have 60 Crafting, continue with the section Distressing by players."],"t":"Distressing bronze gear"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use the bronze gear on the crate.","Return to the archaeologists. This will take 3 hours so if 60 Crafting is achievable by any boosts within that time frame it is highly recommended to do that instead. {Chat: 1 Indeed, I am. > 1 Indeed, I would.}","Continue with the section Collecting scabarite notes."],"t":"Distressing by archaeologists"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["While standing in the desert, use Ugthanki dung on the bronze items.","Use the oxidized bronze items on the crate.","Travel to Pollnivneach (Pollnivneach Teleport or Magic carpet network are easiest).","Enter the kebab shop North-West of the well in the center of the town.","Talk to Isma'il the Kebab seller and purchase Red hot sauce {Chat: 3 Would you sell me that bottle of special kebab sauce?}","Head to the building South-West.","Go inside the fenced area with two Jasim the Camels.","Use the Red hot sauce on the trough to the South.","Use a bucket on the dung produced by Jasim the Camel to get Ugthanki dung.","While standing in the desert, use Ugthanki dung on the bronze items.","Use the oxidized bronze items on the crate."],"t":"Distressing by players"},{"n":"pyramid top, 10 Gold artefact, smelly crate","r":"Weapon}}{{Checklis","s":["Talk to Simon Templeton at the Agility Pyramid. {Chat: 1 Some archaeologists asked me to deliver some artefacts to you. > 1 I'd like to supply some gold objects from Pyramid Plunder. > 1 I'd like to supply a golden Agility Pyramid artefact. > 1 I'd like to supply a crate of bronze antiquities.}","Talk to the archaeologists (back at the campfire along the shortcut to the east) for a book scabaras research.","Kill undead creatures nearby until you get 4 different scabarite notes. They should have different examine texts.\n  - Dried zombies and skeletons to the north.\n  - Mummies to the west.\n  - Locust lancers, rangers, scabaras lancers, and rangers in the swamp to the south-east.","Copy the notes to the scabaras research.","Talk to the archaeologists for a key scabarite key.","Run north and enter the northernmost dungeon."],"t":"Collecting scabarite notes"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["This section is a race against time. Read it fully before continuing. You need to pass all challenges successfully in one go, otherwise you need to tell the clay golem to reset the levers so you can try again.","It is possible to empty the storage box of logs so you might need to bring your own in case you fail at first attempt. If you have a lower Firemaking level, you might not be able to stoke the furnace. For example, the storage box may give you magic logs, but if your Firemaking level is below 95, you won't be able to continue, unless you bring your own logs."],"t":"Preparation"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use the logs on the furnace to stoke the furnace.","Talk to the golem. {Chat: 3 I am ready for you to operate the levers. > 4 Set the mysterious box room to the highest power. > 1 Set the empty room to the second highest power. > 2 Set the narrow walkway room to the second lowest power.}","Relight the furnace.","Enter the narrow walkway room.\n  - Cross the pipe and pull the lever.","Enter the empty room.\n  - Pull the lever.","Enter the scarab room.\n  - Kill the level 92 giant scarab.\n  - Pull the lever.","Enter the mysterious box room.\n  - Investigate the mysterious mechanism to start the puzzle. Clicking outside of the interface will fail the attempt and you'll have to start the whole process over.\n  - Starting from the upper left corner, note the runes shown, flipping three runes in a row. Do this for all rows until all runes are noted. You should finish with 8 attempts left.\n  - On the right side of the interface to increase your attempts from 20 to 35. Click on the cog, mechanical screw parts and dial (three areas) and you will receive an extra 15 attempts giving 35 in total. If you don't, you will fail partway through the puzzle in the next section!\n  - Flip the rune in the upper left corner. Use your notes to identify the locations of other matching runes and flip them over (You are matching groups of 3 runes). Continue until all runes have been flipped.","Once you have completed all 4 challenges in a row, it is possible to teleport out and restock without having to do them again."],"t":"Challenges"},{"n":"","r":"antipoison, food","s":["Run to the High Priest of Scabaras in the north-west room in the dungeon. Disarm the traps along the way.","Talk to the High Priest. {Chat: 2 Conversion, eh? > 2 I do not fear your pathetic beetle-brained magics.}","Defeat him.","Talk to him again. {Chat: 4 By all the deities, what is going on here? > 1 I sense the hand of the Devourer in this. Am I correct?}","Defeat him.","Talk to him once more. {Chat: 4 By all the deities, what is going on here? > 2 Sounds like the Devourer dragged you into heresy for her own ends.}","Defeat him.","Talk to him once more. {Chat: 2 Conversion, eh? > 1 I sense the hand of the Devourer in this. Am I correct?}","Return to the High Priest in Sophanem.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Vault area"}]},"Death Plateau":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Commander Denulth who is located north east of the Burthorpe Lodestone, south of the agility course. {Chat: 1 Do you have any quests for me? > Accept} (The quest icon can be hidden by the block of soldiers he's south of.)"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"1 Free inventory space","r":"","s":["Head west past the castle and through a defensive wall.","Go north (past troll invasion) and into a cave.","Talk to Sabbot. {Chat: 1 I've been sent to look for a route to Death Plateau. Can you help?}","Exit the cave and follow the path to the west.","At the intersection, head west and then go south and into a house.","Talk to Freda."],"t":"The dwarves"},{"n":"","r":"A weapon","s":["Home Teleport to Burthorpe.","Speak to Dunstan outside the house to the south-east of Denulth to add spikes to the climbing boots. {Chat: 1 Can you put some fresh spikes on these climbing boots for me?}","Bring the spiked boots back to Freda.","Read the Survey that is received.","Go back to Sabbot's cave and mine the wall west of him.","Proceed through the cavern's obstacles and climb the cliffside at the end.","Exit the cave through the cave exit.","The Map will approach the player. {Chat: 3 Prepare to die, troll!}","Kill The Map.\n  - The Map will not be counted as killed if you are in a group.","Home Teleport to Burthorpe."],"t":"Boots and routes"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Commander Denulth.","Watch or skip the cutscene.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Death to the Dorgeshuun":{"sections":[{"n":"A light source, 2 full sets of H.A.M. robes}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["Take a light source and go to the Lumbridge Castle cellar.","Squeeze through the hole in the wall.","Right click on Kazgar, and use the option \"Follow\".","Talk to Mistag and ask about the favour. {Chat: 1 What is this favour? > Accept > 4 Can you show me the way out of the mines?}\n  - Alternatively to leave mines, right click on Mistag and use \"Follow\".","Return to the Lumbridge Castle cellar, talk to Zanik. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm [Player name]! > 1 Yes, I have two sets of robes!}"],"t":"What's with the cabal?"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Cook inside Lumbridge Castle.","Talk to Duke Horacio upstairs in the castle. {Chat: 3 Have you heard of any HAM activity lately?}","Go east outside the castle on the floor 1 for a cutscene.","Talk to an unnamed man or a woman (there are many in the marketplace).","Talk to either the Lumbridge General Store shopkeeper or his assistant. {Chat: 2 No, thanks.}","Talk to Doomsayer near the castle gate. {Chat: 1 Don't worry, Zanik.}","Talk to the Lumbridge Sage right in front of the castle gate.","Take Zanik to a level 2 goblin across the east bridge.\n  - Make sure to not click while Zanik walks off the bridge of the east side. She starts a dialogue that is easy to click away from accidentally.","Talk to Father Aereck in the church. {Chat: 4 Bye.}","Talk to Bob at Bob's Brilliant Axes. {Chat: 1 Let's go, Zanik.}","Talk to Zanik. {Chat: 3 Will you tell me about the mark on your forehead?}\n  - If she doesn't have the talk option, teleport away and talk to her in the Lumbridge Castle cellar.","After the cutscene, put on your set of H.A.M. robes and prepare to head to the H.A.M. hideout."],"t":"Lumbridge safari"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open and then climb down the trapdoor in the Lumbridge forest northwest of the Lumbridge Castle to enter the hideout.","Talk with Johanhus Ulsbrecht (in the southern room) about the cave goblins. {Chat: 4 Are you planning to do anything about the cave goblins? > 3 That's good.}","Go next to the southern hanging brazier in the main room - Zanik will spot a trapdoor (Make sure Zanik is beside you and not trapped in the previous room).","Pick-lock on the hidden trap door by right clicking it, then climb down."],"t":"Requiescat in pace"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Walk past the first guard (Zanik shoots him).","Squeeze through the crack in the wall behind where the first guard stood.","Squeeze through the crack in the opposite wall while the guard in the corridor has his back turned.","Go behind the west guard. Talk to him for a cutscene.","Continuing the dialogue then wait for the corridor's guard to turn his back, tell Zanik \"Now!\". {Chat: 1 Now!}","Go east to the end of the central corridor, but not around the corner.\n  - Talk to Zanik, telling her to wait. {Chat: 2 Wait here.}","Run out of the corridor and south down to the south-east corner, making the north-east guard follow you. Zanik will shoot him.","Go to the end of either the west or east passages, but not around the corner.\n  - Talk to Zanik, telling her to wait again. {Chat: 2 Wait here.}","Go to the other passage, via the central corridor, and approach the guard (Zanik shoots him).","Listen at the door (you will be caught)."],"t":"Slipping past the guards"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pick the jail's door lock and leave the H.A.M. hideout.","Pick up Zanik, lying near a tree south of the hideout entrance.","If you have finished the Tears of Guthix quest, you can teleport there with her using a games necklace.","Climb down the trapdoor in the Lumbridge castle, and squeeze through the hole in the cellar wall.","Squeeze through the hole to the south, run south then jump across the stepping stones.","Enter the tunnel to reach the Tears of Guthix cavern.","With Zanik in your inventory and both hands free, talk to Juna. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Collect 20 blue tears from the walls to trigger a cutscene.\n  - Green tears empty your bowl.","Talk to Zanik. {Chat: 1 Let's Go!}"],"t":"Divine resurrection"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Prepare for the fight against Sigmund and his guards (but keep the H.A.M robes with you). Zanik is considered a follower. Pets and familiars cannot be used during the battle.","Teleport to Lumbridge then enter the castle cellar.","Talk to Zanik and have her follow you. {Chat: 1 Let's go!}","Go to Seth Groats's farm on the east side of the river near the cow paddock, enter the fenced area through the gap on the south side.","Unequip any weapons or shields.","Equip full H.A.M. set.","Search one of the empty crates by the tree. {Chat: 1 I don't know, what are you thinking? > 1 Good idea.}","After Zanik climbs in the crate, carry it down into the trapdoor just north of the empty crates.","Go west and walk up to Sigmund, instead of immediately clicking to attack him. You must trigger the dialogue with Sigmund in order to have Zanik attack him, which is needed to complete the quest.\n  - Kill the guards first. This allows Zanik to attack Sigmund who will then switch to Protect from Missiles.\n  - Kill Sigmund, who uses the Protect from Missiles prayer. If he's protecting against your attack style, avoid him so he switches back to Protect from Missile.","Smash the drilling machine at the centre of the room.","Go east then south and unblock the tunnel for a cutscene.","Quest complete!"],"t":"To be continued..."}]},"Defender of Varrock":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Dismiss any followers now.","Talk to Captain Rovin in Varrock Palace, on the floor of north-west tower. {Chat: 1 Ooh, good, sounds like a quest. > Accept > 1 Okay, let's get going.}\n  - If he will not give you the quest, make sure you have claimed kudos from Historian Minas at Varrock Museum.","Enter the Graveyard of Shadows, then talk to Hartwin. {Chat: 1 I want to talk about the mission.}\n  - Make sure Hartwin is following you in this section.\n  - If you lose Hartwin for any reason, he can be found back at the Varrock Palace.","Inspect the tree stump just south of the west graveyard entrance (just south of the arch) to uncover more footprints.","Follow the footprints and continue searching bushes, trees, stumps, mushrooms, and bones to uncover more footprints.\n  - Search the small forest of dead trees south of the Graveyard of Shadows, northwest of the Chaos Temple for a grubby key.","The trail eventually leads to Simon near the Chaos Temple.","Run south to the trapdoor, unlock it using the grubby key and climb down."],"t":"Tracking"},{"n":"combat equipment to kill six or more armoured zombies","r":"","s":["Run north and look over the balcony.","Run west and take 3 bottles.","Kill 3 armoured zombies, using the bottles on red mist to fill them.","Proceed deeper into the cave through the door.","Run north and kill 3 armoured zombies again, using the bottles on red mist to fill them.","Go through the next door and look over another balcony.","Hartwin will give you a Varrock teleport tablet to return to Varrock quickly.","Return to Captain Rovin in Varrock."],"t":"Undead army"},{"n":"blurite ore, light source, and a spade (tool belt does not work)","r":"a redberry pie (optional for 1,000 Smithing experience if you give the pie to Ramarno)","s":["Talk to Thurgo in Thurgo's Peninsula, south of Port Sarim lodestone, north of fairy ring aiq. {Chat: 3 I'd like to ask about the Shield of Arrav.} or {Chat: 4 I'd like to ask about the Shield of Arrav.} if you have 99 Smithing.\n  - If you don't have a blurite ore, now is the opportune time to mine one in the snowy area of the dungeon nearby.","Climb Ice Mountain, west of Edgeville.","Dig with your spade 2 steps on the location east of the white tree, next to the material caches, near the dungeon icon ().","Dig the churned-up snow then enter the hole.","Talk to Ramarno. {Chat: 4 I wish to use the Sacred Forge.} If you have a redberry pie, you can give it to Ramarno for 1,000 Smithing experience.","Use blurite ore on the forge.","Talk to Ramarno for a cutscene (note that pressing escape during the cutscene will reset it)."],"t":"The Sacred Forge"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Captain Rovin, ignoring the zombies. He gives you a restored shield.","Talk to Reldo in the library on the floor 1: \"I'd like to talk about the invading zombies.\"","Read the Varrock Census on the lectern.","Search the scrolls on the floor a few steps south after talking to Reldo about the situation.","Read the list of elders."],"t":"Zombie invasion"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the following NPCs until one mentions they are not a blood descendant:\n  - King Roald, southeast corner of the floor 1 {Chat: 1 Talk about Zombies.} or {Chat: 2 Talk about Zombies.} if the quest Lord of Vampyrium has been completed.\n  - Aeonisig Raispher, next to King Roald. {Chat: 1 Defender of Varrock. > 1 Talk about the zombie invasion.}\n  - Sir Prysin, west of the king.\n  - Curator Haig Halen, in the Varrock Museum. {Chat: 1 Talk about the zombie invasion.}\n  - Horvik the smith north-east of Varrock Square. {Chat: 2 Talk about the zombie invasion.}","Talk to Dimintheis in south-east Varrock where you started the quest Family Crest. {Chat: 2 Ask about something else.}","Talk to Captain Rovin.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Shield of Arrav"}]},"Demon Slayer":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Gideon Bede inside the church in north-east Varrock. {Chat: Accept}","Climb down the trapdoor in the room.","Walk north and speak to any of the spirits. {Chat: 1 I come seeking Silverlight.}"],"t":"The trials"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to the Spirit of the Mind inside the eastern room. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 I seek the Silverlight. > 3 A sword that slays demons. > 2 A powerful demon threatens Varrock. > 1 Delrith. > 3 Gideon Bede.}"],"t":"Mind"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to the Spirit of Faith in the northern room, who'll guide you to the other side. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","The correct pathway is:\n  - 3 north\n  - 2 east\n  - 3 north\n  - 2 west\n  - 1 south\n  - 2 west\n  - 4 north"],"t":"Faith"},{"n":"Combat gear, food}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["Speak to the Spirit of the Body in the western room. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Defeat all 10 skeletons."],"t":"Body"},{"n":"Melee gear, food","r":"","s":["Talk to the spirits in the central room.","Take Silverlight from the altar. Make sure you actually take the Silverlight in the rock in the centre of the room or you will not be able to do the next steps.","Go back up the ladder.","Read the scroll to the north of the trapdoor.","Head south to Aubury's Rune Shop. South of the shop is a trapdoor just outside the Zamorak temple. Climb down the trapdoor.","Make your way west to the large room, killing all the cultists along the way.","Fight Delrith. Run into Gideon's dome shield to negate most of the damage. Only Silverlight or Darklight will work.","Speak to Gideon again.","Quest complete!"],"t":"For Varrock!"}]},"Desert Slayer Dungeon (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the well in Pollnivneach.","In the room with mighty banshees, pass the mystic barrier to the southwest and climb down the stairs. The quest is just about killing 4 bosses in their specific locations. Below is a recommended order.","Mightiest turoth (SW - bottom left barrier)\n  - Use Slayer Dart and Protect from Melee prayer. If you stand far away from the Mightiest turoth, it will use Ranged-based attacks on you. Ignore the minions.\n  - If you choose to use melee, do not forget to bring a leaf-bladed spear or sword.","Kurask overlord (NW - top left barrier)\n  - Use same strategies as above.","Basilisk boss (SE - bottom right barrier)\n  - Use melee and wield the mirror shield.\n  - Use Protect from Magic prayer. Also watch your stats as they will be drained with each attack. Bring a restore potion.\n  - Take a dose of Super strength potion and Super attack potion, a Combat potion, or Super warmaster's potion to help.","Monstrous cave crawler (NE - top right barrier)\n  - Use melee and Protect from Ranged prayer. The poison from its ranged attack severely reduces the duration of any antipoison potions, including super antipoison. Every second or third hit poisons the player even with potions. An anti-poison totem will not work.}} Miniquest Complete!"],"t":"Getting started"}]},"Desert Treasure":{"sections":[{"n":"One backpack space","r":"Desert heat protection, Archaeology journal","s":["Talk to Asgarnia Smith for some etchings. He is in the Bedabin Camp south-west of the Shantay Pass. {Chat: 2 Do you have any quests? > Accept}","Talk to Terry Balando in the Exam Centre. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Desert Treasure quest.}\n  - If he offers you a Codex Ultimatus, refuse it or talk to him again.","Talk to him again for the Translation. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Desert Treasure quest.}}}"],"t":"Asgarnia Smith"},{"n":"650 coins, 1 charcoal, 1 ashes, 1 bones, 1 blood rune, 6 steel bars (can be noted), 12 magic logs (can be noted), 6 molten glass (can be noted), translation, and one backpack space.","r":"","s":["Talk to Asgarnia again and offer to help him. {Chat: 1 Help him}","Run south to the Bandit Camp.\n  - If you're wearing any Zamorak or Saradomin equipment, bandits become aggressive.","Talk to the bartender at the pub for a Bandit's brew. {Chat: 2 Buy a drink > 1 Buy a beer}","Talk to the bartender again. {Chat: 2 I heard about four diamonds...}","Talk to Eblis, by or in the eastern-most building of the Bandit Camp. {Chat: 2 Ask about Desert Treasure > 4 Tell me of The four diamonds of Azzanadra > 1 Yes > 1 Yes, I will go get those for you.} (if the first chat option is not 'Ask about Archaeology' {Chat: 4 Tell me of The four diamonds of Azzanadra > 1 Yes > 1 Yes, I will go get those for you.})\n  - He will not speak to you if you're wearing any Zamorak or Saradomin equipment.","Use all the items on Eblis, then talk to him again. {Chat: 2 Ask about Desert Treasure}","Run south-east, and talk to Eblis by the Bandit Camp lodestone. {Chat: 2 Ask about Desert Treasure}","Retrieving the four diamonds can be done in any order.",":Jump to §Blood diamond",":Jump to §Ice diamond",":Jump to §Smoke diamond",":Jump to §Shadow diamond"],"t":"Bandit Camp"},{"n":"Garlic, silver bar, spice, food, air spells if using magic","r":"","s":["Enter the pub in Canifis. After a short cutscene, talk to Malak. {Chat: 5 I am looking for a special Diamond... > 1 Yes > 3 How can I kill Dessous? > 3 Actually, I don't need to know anything.}","Take a silver bar and talk to Ruantun in the Draynor Sewers for a Silver pot.","Take the pot to the High Priest on Entrana for a Blessed pot.","Talk to Malak in Canifis for a blood-filled Blessed pot (this deals 50 damage).","Crush the garlic, use the garlic powder on the blessed pot, then add spice to get a completed Blessed pot.","Prepare for a level 84 boss fight. If you die, you will have to re-do the previous step.\n  - Note: It is recommended to bank your cake or chocolate bar, as a ghast may turn it into rotten food on the journey.","Run south-east to the Graveyard (map pictured right).","Use the pot on the tomb, then kill Dessous.","Return to Canifis.","Speak to Malak to receive the Blood diamond.","Bank the blood diamond immediately. While holding the blood diamond, a stranger capable of dealing over 5,000 damage per attack can spawn at any time."],"t":"Blood diamond"},{"n":"A sweet (cake, chocolate cake (partial cakes work), chocolate bar, cooking apple, or pineapple pizza), spiked boots, and climbing boots (or Trollheim Teleport or Trollheim tablet).","r":"Combat equipment (if using Magic, which is recommended, bring runes for casting your best fire spell), 4 or more regular or super restore potions, a few prayer potions (depending on your combat level), lots of good food or Saradomin brews if using super restore potions, an emergency teleportation method, a God banner (only if all combat tasks have been completed) or overloads, and run energy restoring, Endurance relic power, salt-water spring or a flask of salt water.","s":["Prepare for combat by getting plenty of food, a few super restore and super energy potions (even at max combat). Also grab a cake or a chocolate bar if not already in your inventory.\n  - Get runes and a magic weapon for fire spells if using Magic. Only fire spells will work if using Magic on Kamil.","If you don't have spiked boots, get them first from Dunstan in Burthorpe (requires an iron bar).","If you used your climbing boots to get the spiked boots, then get a new pair of climbing boots from Freda.","Consider using the Endurance relic power in place of energy potions to keep your run energy up.","Travel to Trollheim using Trollheim Teleport.\n  - Otherwise, take the path from the Fremennik Slayer Dungeon or the Death Plateau to Troll Stronghold with climbing boots.","Take the path that leads to the snow area north-west of Troll Stronghold.","Talk to the troll child a few squares west of the ice gate.","Use a cake or a chocolate bar on him. Talk again to help him. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Enable Protect from Melee, and head east through the ice gate.","Kill 5 trolls, then travel through the cave entrance to your east and keep running.","Kill Kamil when he appears.","After you kill Kamil once, continue the path to the north and walk to the ice ledge. You can use Surge.","Equip your spiked boots and climb the path to the top.","Pass through the ice gate and across the bridge.","Break the two ice blocks at the top (by casting a fire spell or choosing the \"smash-ice\" option).","Talk to the trolls, the child will give you the Ice diamond.","Bank the ice diamond immediately. While holding the ice diamond, a stranger capable of dealing over 5,000 damage per attack can spawn at any time."],"t":"Ice diamond"},{"n":"Face mask, masked earmuffs or slayer helmet, ice gloves","r":"","s":["Prepare for combat by bringing plenty of food, few super energy potions, melee gear, or water spells if using magic, or ice arrows if using ranged.","Travel to Pollnivneach.","With your face mask and ice gloves equipped enter the Smoke Dungeon.\n  - If Smoking Kills is complete the dungeon can be entered from the Pollnivneach well and through the dark stairs to the west.\n  - Otherwise the player can enter the smokey well which is located west of Pollnivneach.\n    - Killing a dust devil completes the achievement Drafty in Here.","Light the four standing torches, 1 in each corner of the dungeon. This part is timed and torches will go out if you are not fast enough.","Consider using the Endurance relic power in place of energy potions to keep your run energy up.","Open the burnt chest in the middle of the dungeon to receive a Warm key.\n  - Each torch will remain lit for exactly 5 minutes, and you will receive a game message when each one dies out. You will be unable to open the chest if any of the torches have gone out, even if you have lit all 4 torches before attempting.","With the warm key, open the gate on the eastern side of the dungeon.","Defeat Fareed for the Smoke diamond.\n  - You must use melee, ice arrows, necromancy, or water spells.\n  - You must wear ice gloves to wield a main-hand weapon while fighting him, including staves and bows. Off-hand weapons are not restricted.","Bank the smoke diamond immediately. While holding the smoke diamond, a stranger capable of dealing over 5,000 damage per attack can spawn at any time."],"t":"Smoke diamond"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to Rasolo (north-west from Ardougne lodestone; see the map to the right). {Chat: 3 Ask about the Diamonds of Azzanadra > 1 Yes}}}"],"t":"Ring of visibility"},{"n":"Lots of lockpicks, hair clips, or a master thief's lockpick","r":"A few doses of antipoison","s":["Unlock the secure chest in the southern-most tent. You might consume between 10 to 100 lockpicks.\n  - Hair clips are very useful here, as you can reclaim them from Merlin for free.\n  - You can steal from the level 54 Bandits around the camp to get lock picks and antipoison.\n  - Master thief's lockpick also works and will never break.\n  - Five finger discount upgrades help."],"t":"Stealing the cross"},{"n":"Gilded cross, combat equipment, earth spells if using magic}}{{Checklist; * Prepare for combat before returning the cross to Rasolo who will give you a [[ring of visibility]","r":"","s":["Equip the ring, run into the nearby triangular fenced area and climb down the ladder. You may equip any other ring now as this was only required to see the invisible ladder.","Run east to Damis and kill him in both phases for the Shadow diamond. See the map below for the path to take.\n  - If Damis despawns, run a small distance back from where you came, then run back.","Bank the shadow diamond immediately. While holding the shadow diamond, a stranger capable of dealing over 5,000 damage per attack can spawn at any time."],"t":"Getting the diamond"},{"n":"All 4 diamonds; recommended = Energy potions, weapon, weight-reducing equipment, antipoison","r":"","s":["Make sure your weight is less than 5 or you'll keep failing traps.\n  - Boots of lightness and any other weight reducing equipment helps.","Return to the Bandit Camp, and head directly south of Eblis to the pyramid.","Use the diamonds on the obelisks surrounding the pyramid.\n  - Blood diamond in the north-west obelisk.\n  - Shadow diamond in the south-west obelisk.\n  - Ice diamond in the south-east obelisk.\n  - Smoke diamond in the north-east obelisk.","Climb down the ladder at the top of the pyramid.","Run through the pyramid using the map. Don't stand still, or you may be transported back to the start.\n  - There's a possibility that scarabs spawn in Azzanadra's room so bring a weapon, antipoison, and some more food just in case.","Talk to Azzanadra.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Jaldraocht Pyramid"}]},"Desperate Creatures":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to the Curator just north of Burthorpe lodestone. {Chat: ? Talk about 'Desperate Creatures'. > Accept > 3 What do I need to do first?}\n  - Slayer cape teleport to Turael/Spria is a good option as you'll need to teleport a few times."],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to Anachronia and run west.","Use the Tome of tracking to find all four flowers.","After the dialogue between Hannibus and Vindicta teleport back to Burthorpe and speak to the Curator. {Chat: ? Talk about 'Desperate Creatures'. > 1 Talk about your progress.}","Talk to the Curator again for the next task. {Chat: ? Talk about 'Desperate Creatures'. > 1 Talk about your progress.}"],"t":"Task 1"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to Anachronia.","Find the 4 shrubberies around the camp using the tome.","Finish the dialogue with Mr Mordaut and teleport back to Burthorpe and speak to the Curator. {Chat: ? Talk about Desperate Creatures. > 1 Talk about your progress.}","Talk to the Curator again for the next task. {Chat: ? Talk about Desperate Creatures. > 1 Talk about your progress.}"],"t":"Task 2"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to Anachronia and navigate to the Anachronia Swamp Fortress.\n  - Teleport to the Xolo dig site using the Orthen teleportation device or teleport to Laniakea via Slayer cape.","Alternatively exit Anachronia base camp to the north down the stairs, not via the Agility shortcut.\n  - Run east to the liverworts.\n  - Run south past the lampenfloras while staying as far west as possible.","Find all four mushrooms.","Finish the dialogue with Zaros and teleport back to Burthorpe and speak to the Curator. {Chat: ? Talk about Desperate Creatures. > 1 Talk about your progress.}","Talk to the Curator again for the next task. {Chat: ? Talk about Desperate Creatures. > 1 Talk about your progress.}"],"t":"Task 3"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to Anachronia and navigate to an area south of the liverworts and north of the lampenfloras.\n  - The fastest way to get there is by teleporting to Anachronia and running slightly east to use the Orthen teleportation device. Then teleporting to the Moksha ritual site [M] and then exiting and running north-east.\n  - Alternatively, leave Anachronia base camp to the north down the stairs, not via the Agility shortcut. Run east to the liverworts. Run south towards the lampenfloras.","Find all four insects.","Finish the dialogue with Charos and Thok and teleport back to Burthorpe and speak to the Curator. {Chat: ? Talk about Desperate Creatures. > 1 Talk about your progress.}","Talk to the Curator again for the next task. {Chat: ? Talk about Desperate Creatures. > 1 Talk about your progress.}"],"t":"Task 4"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to Anachronia and run north.\n  - Fastest way to get there is by using the War's Retreat boss portal / the Max Guild boss portal or the Grouping System teleporting to Rex Matriarchs and heading west to the Teleportation Device and activating it, taking you where you need to be.\n  - Alternatively, leave Anachronia base camp through the southern exit and head north-east to central Anachronia","Find all four frogs.","Finish the dialogue with Prehistoric Potterington.","Teleport back to Burthorpe and speak to the Curator. {Chat: ? Talk about Desperate Creatures. > 1 Talk about your progress.}"],"t":"Task 5"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Seren on the floor 2 of the Burthorpe Castle. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Desperate Creatures'.}","Go downstairs, head south and speak to the Curator. {Chat: ? Talk about 'Desperate Creatures'.}"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Desperate Measures":{"sections":[{"n":"2 backpack spaces, 100 orthenglass in material storage (can be obtained from Anachronia north excavation site during quest, recommended to bring multiple sign of the porters if collecting there)","r":"Around 10 backpack spaces, Archaeology journal, activated Anachronia lodestone.}}{{Checklis","s":["Speak to Seren on the floor 2 of Burthorpe Castle (north of the lodestone). {Chat: Any > Accept > Any}","Head to Anachronia to speak with Mr Mordaut in the base camp. {Chat: 1 Anachronia. > 1 Ask about Desperate Measures.}","Go north of the base camp, and down the two flights of stairs to the dragonkin gate. Do not begin the Agility course.","Dismiss any pets or followers and then speak with Thok or Charos. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Inside the flashback, go to Charos. Finish all dialogue before continuing else you will exit the flashback and have to start over.","Smash the feral dinosaurs.","Continue east along the path, attacking more dinosaurs as you go.","Talk to Laniakea and then follow her across the bridge. After Kerapac leaves, finish the conversation with Charos. {Chat: 1 Not much. > 3 [Leave]}","Uncover and excavate the dragonkin remains excavation hotspot that appears 4 tiles south and 3 tiles east of Thok and Charos to obtain a dragonkin device (damaged).","Restore the dragonkin device at an archaeologist's workbench.","Talk to Charos {Chat: 4 [Leave]}.","Excavate the orthen rubble spot, which appears about three paces north of him, to obtain a dragonkin tablet (damaged).\n  - If you do not have enough orthenglass, you can destroy the tablet and excavate again.","Restore the dragonkin tablet at an archaeologist's workbench.","Talk to Charos. {Chat: 5 [Leave]}"],"t":"Finding the dragonkin artefacts"},{"n":"Dragonkin device, Dragonkin tablet","r":"Quick access to Anachronia Dinosaur Farm","s":["Head to the Anachronia Dinosaur Farm (from the Manor Farm, go to the top floor of the manor and teleport using the mystical tree).","Speak to Hannibus next to Prehistoric Potterington. {Chat: 5 [Leave]}","Travel to the Nodon Hibernatorium on the north-eastern coast of Anachronia, east of the Herby Werby entrance and south-east of the Observation outpost (see map).","Enter the southern door next to Hannibus using the dragonkin device you restored earlier.","Talk with Hannibus inside. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Speak with Hannibus again {Chat: 1 Yes.} to start a memory.","Eventually, one of the Nodon caretakers will walk to the south-eastern corner of the room. Wait for the Nodon caretaker to finish putting in the passcode on the pylon, and you will be able to cycle the symbols.\n  - You must first click on the pylon in the shared memory.\n  - Talk with Hannibus to exit the dream. {Chat: 2 No. > 1 Yes.}","Cycle each of the three symbols outside of the dream until they match what you saw in the dream. Your character will interrupt when a symbol is input correctly. Continue that dialogue instead of exiting the chat box, otherwise, Hannibus won't recognise the correct sequence.","Re-enter the dream and start the shared dream again. This time, follow the other dragonkin outside.","Follow him until he walks to the door at the front of the ruins and speak a passphrase.","Speak to Hannibus again and exit the dream (you can lobby and log back to go faster). Return to the front of the ruins and enter the door with the passphrase you heard earlier (should be in the chat box)."],"t":"Nodon hibernatorium shared memory"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Inside the front door, speak with Hannibus {Chat: 1 Yes.} again to enter another shared dream. If the room is empty it means you actually do not have the right code, even if you cannot change it.\n  - Ensure you rotated three characters on the pylon; one on the left, one on the right, and one in the centre. May need to zoom in to see. Hannibus should also be now standing in front of the door, he wasn't before.","Speak with Hannibus, next to a water pool, inside the dream to start a shared memory. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Skip the cutscene on Kerapac's device.","Attack Kerapac until he flies off or watch your party of NPCs try to fight him. It may take about 1 minute. No damage will be done to or by you in the fight.","Return and talk to Seren in Burthorpe.","Speak to Primrose located in the house by the Needle (far west of the Piscatoris Fishing Colony).\n  - The nearest fairy ring is AKQ.\n  - Memory strand can also be used to teleport to Memorial to Guthix, which is south of the house.","Talk to Primrose and exhaust all chat options (focus on finding the needles weakness). {Chat: 1 Ask about Desperate Measures. > 1 Ask how she's doing. > 1 Ask about the Needle > 1 Can the Needle be destroyed? > 1 Can the Needle be counteracted? > 2 Does the Needle have any weaknesses? > 4 Ask about Gail. > 1 Was she vulnerable to anything? > 1 What was it like being her? > 4 [Leave]} Your quest log should update to speak to Seren.","Return to Seren."],"t":"The Kindra council memory"},{"n":"1 backpack space","r":"","s":["Make your way to Heart of Gielinor in the Kharidian Desert. (The Heart teleports can be used, or travel to Nardah using the magic carpet network and run south-west). Alternatively, the nearest fairy ring is DLQ, then run south.","Speak with Seren outside the Heart. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Speak to Jas about Kerapac. {Chat: 1 [Ask about Kerapac.] > 2 Can you intervene? > 1 Why not? > 1 Point out her power.}","Speak to Jas about the Needle. {Chat: 5 [Ask about something else.] > 2 [Ask about the Needle.] > 2 Can it be stopped?}","Ask for Jas' help {Chat: 4 [Ask about something else.] > 1 Can you help?} then exit the dialogue. The Eye of Jas should be in your inventory.","Talk to Seren."],"t":"Meeting Jas"},{"n":"Eye of Jas, nothing equipped in your main-hand and off-hand, or enough backpack space to unequip.","r":"","s":["Return to the Anachronia base camp and speak with Charos near the lodestone.","After Kerapac turns up, speak with Thok to start the fight. You can't be wielding anything in your hands. {Chat: 1 I'm ready.}","Follow the instructions set out when starting the fight with your team members (Hannibus, Thok, Charos, and Laniakea).\n  - If you get the message \"you need to finish speaking with Charos before you can start the encounter\", you also have to change Charos attack type (just choose closest), then you need to move Hannibus one square away and move him back to his original place.\n  - Keep them in their default positions, and stand two squares west of Charos. You should win without moving, but if you struggle then move your character around to get early hits on the bigger dinosaurs.\n  - If you exit dialogue with Charos too early you may need to reset the instance by right clicking Thok and clicking Leave."],"t":"Dinosaur invasion"},{"n":"The Measure (received in first step by speaking to Charos, if Fate of the Gods is not completed), Eye of Jas, 1 backpack space (2 if you didn't already have the Measure)","r":"food, weapon, armour, and prayer potions for the next step","s":["After the fight is complete, speak with Charos next to the lodestone. Go north past the Anachronia Agility Course and speak with Charos once more. {Chat: Any} The Measure should be in your inventory after speaking to him—if not, it may be in your bank; you will need to speak with Charos again before proceeding.","You have to use The Measure near Charos a total of four times in the ruined areas surrounding the volcano. He will speak to you automatically if done correctly. If anytime during this Charos disappears or you are unable to interact properly with him, log out and back in or try hopping worlds. Charos will be standing right at the spot you need to use The Measure at. When you arrive at one of the spots where Charos is at, place The Measure. After placing The Measure, it's unnecessary to fully finish speaking to Charos. Players may proceed to the next location.\n  - The first location is a bit north of the entrance where you talk to him.\n  - The second location is north of the lodestone. Start the Agility course, enter through the cave, cross the roots, and walk north till you reach the camouflaged jadinkos.\n  - The third location can be reached by teleporting to the Anachronia lodestone, then head west past the bridge and north-west past the arcane apoterrasaur until you reach the dragonkin ruins. Alternatively, players that have unlocked the Orthen teleportation device can teleport to the third location.\n  - The last location is directly east of the previous location, up a flight of stairs.","Prepare for combat.","Speak with Charos again (north of the base camp). (If he is not there, step into the room north of Thok and step out again. He might appear in the northern room, if so, place a measure in front of him.)","Enter Kerapac's laboratory. (An entrance will have spawned where you met Thok and Charos north of the base camp.)","Enter the correct codes into the pylons on the four corners of the area, as given in the image on the right. The codes are the same for all players.\n  - The south-western room's solution is 2-1-4.\n  - The north-western room's solution is 7-1-5.\n  - The north-eastern room's solution is 4-1-6.\n  - The south-eastern room's solution is 3-1-4."],"t":"Kerapac's laboratory"},{"n":"A weapon to kill a level 91 version of the black stone dragon","r":"food, armour, prayer potions","s":["Enter the room to the north that has now opened up and prepare for a battle with the black stone dragon. (If you die while fighting the dragon, it is a safe death.)","After defeating the dragon, talk to Kerapac when he appears.","Choose any chat option, and after the cutscene, the lab will start to collapse and you will get a timer on your screen and have to escape. When you hit a dead end, turn around or interact with a nearby character to continue. Failing restarts the escape.\n  - If you get sent back out before talking to Kerapac or the escape sequence by logging out or being interrupted (such as conjures), you may re-enter Kerapac's lab to trigger the sequence again.","After escaping the lab and the following cutscenes, return to Seren in Burthorpe (requires 4 backpack spaces to collect reward).","Quest complete!"],"t":"Black stone dragon"}]},"Desperate Times":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Seren on the floor 2 of Burthorpe Castle. {Chat: Accept}","Talk to Osman for a location. (north-east of the table next to Garlandia) {Chat: 1 Do you have anywhere we could plant the garden?}","Talk to Sir Amik Varze for a workforce. (Directly north of the table) {Chat: 2 Do you have a workforce to plant it?}","Talk to Azzanadra for seeds. (North-west of the table, next to Commander Zilyana) {Chat: 1 Desperate Times > 3 Do you have any seeds we could use? > 1 Yes}","Talk to Vanescula Drakan for a location. (By the staircase) {Chat: 1 Do you have anywhere we could plant the garden? > 1 Change to Morytania. > 1 Yes.}","Talk to Zarador for a location. (South-western corner of the room) {Chat: 1 Do you have anywhere we could plant the garden? > 1 Change to Feldip. > 1 Yes}","Kerapac will appear. Complete the dialogue and proceed to The Needle.\n  - If the dialogue containing Kerapac does not start, talk to Seren. {Chat: ~}"],"t":"Attending the council"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to the Needle and talk to Kerapac. {Chat: 3 Let's get on with it. > 3 Say nothing. > 1 Yes, I'm ready.}\n  - It is located west of Piscatoris Fishing Colony (Phoenix Lair Teleport, fairy ring AKQ, Sixth-Age circuit teleports to Guthix memorial, or via memory strands within the currency pouch).","Close the 5 temporal instabilities\n  - 2 on the path from the needle to the house.\n  - 1 inside the courtyard of the house.\n  - 2 upstairs in the house.","Talk to Kerapac again.","Go inside McGrubor's Wood. Descend into the mysterious hole just south of the house. {Chat: 1 Yes}\n  - Navigate to using fairy ring ALS or the Seers' Village lodestone and go west around the fence to enter McGrubor's Wood.","Run through and investigate the coffin.","Read the letter from Charos."],"t":"The Needle"},{"n":"old necklace or necklace of Charos","r":"","s":["Go to the Varrock Dig Site and step on the strange portal near the entrance to the Empty Throne Room. It is found north of the screening station."],"t":"First key"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Step on the portals until a room with a chest unlocks.\n  - If the room has a note on a recipe: If the amount of each & every ingredient can be represented with a single Roman numeral (e.g. 1000g of Bacon = \"M\"), those are the code. If not, the code is the first letter of each ingredient.\n    - Note: Roman numerals for some of the steps below: 1=I, 5=V, 10=X, 50=L, 100=C, 500=D, 1,000=M.\n  - If the room has 4 random items, the code for the chest is the first letter of each item (e.g. Plank, Jute Fibres, Catfish and Diamond Bolt). Order is starting from farthest item from the chest to the closest item to the chest. If this doesn't work, try the letters in the opposite order.\n  - If the room has coins on the ground examine each pile, the code is the number of coins in each pile. Go clockwise, as represented in Roman numerals (e.g. 500 coins = \"D\").\n  - If there is a plaque next to the room's door, the code is the first letter of each lodestone name depicted (e.g. Lumbridge, Falador, Draynor Village and Varrock).\n  - If the room has only one item on the ground with a four-letter word in its name, the combination is those four letters. (e.g. Beer = BEER or Swordfish = FISH).\n  - If the room has a clean herb on the ground, the combination is HERB.","When the chest is unlocked, note the order of the icons.","Repeat for as many chests as needed until you have the full solution.","Rearrange the slide puzzle in the middle to match the icons seen from the chests. (North side is up. If you accidentally did the puzzle upside down, just rotate the outer pieces until they are in place.)","Step on the exit portal to the west."],"t":"Key rules"},{"n":"An outfit to gain access to the Black Knights' Fortress or a skull of remembrance","r":"","s":["Enter the Black Knights' Fortress, and step on the portal on the floor 1 of the Black Knights' Fortress in the south-east room near the entrance to the fortress.","Follow the key rules above again.","Step on the exit portal to the west."],"t":"Second key"},{"n":"old necklace or necklace of Charos","r":"","s":["Step on the portal in the south-east room on the floor 2 of Varrock Palace. The portal is hidden behind the eastern bath screen. King Roald and Sir Amik Varze will be at the table near the stairs.","Follow the key rules above for this part.","Step on the exit portal to the west."],"t":"Third key"},{"n":"3 rune bars, 2 runite stone spirits, 10 gleaming energy, 10 mind runes, old necklace or necklace of Charos}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["Talk to Reldo in the Varrock Palace library (the northern-most room of the floor 1 of the palace) {Chat: 1 [Use Charos's Necklace.] > Any > Any > Any}","Give Charos 3 rune bars, 2 runite stone spirits, 10 gleaming energy, and 10 mind runes.\n  - Runite stone spirits in an ore box will not work. They must be in the backpack."],"t":"The big reveal"},{"n":"Combat gear to defeat 5 level 50 opponents and 5 empty inventory spaces","r":"","s":["Return to The Needle. (Phoenix Lair Teleport, fairy ring AKQ, Sixth-Age circuit teleports to Guthix memorial, or via memory strands within the currency pouch)","Talk to Kerapac.","Manoeuver through the paths and kill the 5 Sliske clones, pick up the fragments. Make sure lootshare is turned off.\n  - The Sliske clones appear to spawn from stepping on specific spots, so if the clones don't spawn step through each path comprehensively until they spawn","Combine the fragments into Sliske's mask.","Walk to the bottom of the platform, wear the mask, and kill Guthix. {Chat: 1 Yes - Kill him}","Harvest the five memories on Naragun, each memory shows up as a yellow dot on the minimap, and go through the dialogue until the NPCs teleport away.","Talk to Guthix near the empty fairy ring. {Chat: Any}","Click each mutable anima once so both the green particles will end up on Kerapac. There are 4 in total.","Go into the room to the west, jump the gap outside the window on the south-east side, run across the planks, drop down the rock face, climb the rock face, and climb through the obstacle.","Run around through each room and open the door at the last room.","Switch all the green mutable anima.\n  - Use temporal rifts to teleport between levels. There are 3 levels in total with the bottom and top floors containing 1 mutable anima each and the middle floor containing 2.","Redirect the green mutable anima to Kerapac (refer to the image).\n  - Harvest all three unrefined anima (red dots on the image) to unlock the three frozen anima. Make sure to finish the dialogue with each NPC.\n  - Switch the green mutable anima according to the direction on the image. All of these can be clicked while standing on the main floor.\n  - Disable bloom in graphics settings if it is difficult to see the direction the green mutable anima is facing.","After a cutscene, return to the Council of Burthorpe and talk to Seren. (If cutscene doesn't start, talk to Kerapac.)"],"t":"The device"}]},"Devious Minds":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the monk just outside of Paterdomus which is east of Silvarea. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"Bowstring and mithril 2h sword","r":"","s":["Head to Doric's hut north of the Falador lodestone and use a mithril 2h sword on the whetstone outside of the hut.","Use a bowstring on the slender blade.","Return to the monk. {Chat: 1 Yep, got it right here for you.}"],"t":"The weapon"},{"n":"Large pouch","r":"","s":["Use the orb on a large pouch.","Bank everything that you are not allowed to take to Entrana, and ensure you keep the large pouch in your inventory.","Reach Entrana either through the Abyss or by using a law altar teleport.\n  - If entering through the Abyss, enter the Abyss via the Mage of Zamorak north of Edgeville, then make your way to the law rift. Dismiss any summoning familiar. Leave the Law Rune Temple by using the portal.","Head into the church of Entrana to the south.","Use the pouch on the prayer altar. Doing this will cause you to lose your large pouch.","Watch the cutscene.\n  - Talk to the High Priest if you didn't during the cutscene."],"t":"Entrana"},{"n":"","r":"Entrana access (or law altar teleport)","s":["Return to the monk, back outside Paterdomus.","Search the Dead Monk.","Talk to the High Priest back on Entrana.","Talk to Sir Tiffy Cashien in Falador Park.\n  - {Chat: 2 Devious Minds} if The Slug Menace has not yet been started.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Diamond in the Rough":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Osman in Al Kharid palace without a follower or pet. {Chat: Accept}","Talk to Ozan just outside the palace, north of your current location.","After the cutscene, inspect the Het scales to receive the heavy weight.","Climb the rope to end up on the roof (the vault has a teleblock active).","Home Teleport to Al Kharid lodestone.","Head south-east to the Shantay Pass."],"t":"Stealing the diamond yet again"},{"n":"","r":"Four backpack spaces, combat equipment","s":["Go through the Shantay Pass. {Chat: 4 Let's keep going.}\n  - Do not interrupt the cutscene, or you will have to go back to the palace to retrieve Ozan.","Inspect the sundial (Het).","Click the \"D\"\" symbol on the outer ring to align the sundial to the symbol of Het (human face). Continue dialogue with Ozan.","Head south-west to the sundial (Apmeken). Inspect it. {Chat: 1 Yes.}\n  - It is possible for the scene to be interrupted and nothing happens afterwards. In this case, just inspect it again.","After the cutscene, kill the bandits and their king.","Pick up the sundial gnomon dropped by the last bandit killed. Ozan will take it if the backpack is full.","Inspect the sundial to fix it.","Click the \"W\" symbol on the left bottom corner of the outer ring to align the sundial to the symbol of Apmeken (monkey head). Continue dialogue with Ozan.","Head north-west for a cutscene, north of the fairy ring. {Chat: Any > Any > Any > Any}"],"t":"Following the sundials"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After the cutscene, keep entering any of the tunnels. Ozan will eventually mention he is sitting on something uncomfortable.","Inspect the sundial (Crondis).","Click the \"L\" symbol on the right bottom corner of the outer ring to align it to Crondis (crocodile head).","Enter the tunnel the sunbeam points to and walk through the tunnel at the end of the path.","Slice open the dung kalphites until the Kharid-ib is found.\n  - A bronze scimitar can be found on the ground near the torch for players without a slashing weapon.\n  - The sparkling kalphites contain gems and must be slashed open. They appear to have an extra glowing circle near their heads.\n  - You must slice open any three kalphites before they will begin to sparkle.\n  - Changing various game settings can help identify the sparkling ones.\n    - Switch your graphics settings' \"Lighting Detail\" option to \"Low\".\n    - Switch your skybox setting \"Midday\".\n    - Switch your audio settings' \"Ambient Sounds\" option on. A twinkle sound indicates the sparkling one is nearby.","For the last kalphite, pick up the kharid-ib and a cutscene ensues.","Climb-out the exit (the rope that appears in the centre).","Talk to Ozan or Leela.","Inspect the sundial (Scabaras).","Click the \"P\" symbol on the outer ring to align it to Scabaras (beetle)."],"t":"The Kalphite Nursery"},{"n":"","r":"Combat equipments","s":["Head south-west and talk to Lady Keli. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 Yes.}","Kill Apep and Heru.\n  - Epilepsy warning: There is a full screen flash effect during the fight.","Talk to Prince Ali Mirza.","Continue dialogue with Osman and Leela.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Encountering Lady Keli"}]},"Dimension of Disaster":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["2 Zemomarks (optional)","Cabbage","Rotten tomato","Beer glass","Black hood This item is not needed if the appropriate override set has been bought using silver pennies.","Black robe (top)","Black robe (bottom)","Black mushroom","Vial","Dog hair","Zombie mask","Zombie shirt","Zombie trousers","Zombie gloves","Zombie boots","Vial This item is not needed when replaying the quest.","3 tin ore","4 fire runes","1 nature rune","Must be on the standard spellbook and prayer book.","Zombie mask","Zombie shirt","Zombie trousers","Zombie gloves","Zombie boots","Lockpick","Mith crossbow","Mith grapple","Darklight","Vial of purple mist (or Vial, Vial of water, Delphinium flower)","Vial of orange mist (or Vial, Vial of water, Raw onion)","Ring of life (or gold ore, diamond, 10 earth runes and 1 cosmic rune)","11 Raw undead beef"],"t":"Subquests"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Aris. {Chat: 1 Dimension of Disaster.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Dimension of Disaster: Coin of the Realm":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Aris. {Chat: 1 Dimension of Disaster. > Accept > 1 Here's the coin. Tell my fortune. > 1 What do you see? > Any > Any > Any > Any}","# Replay: {Chat: 1 Dimension of Disaster. > Accept > 1 Here's the coin. Tell my fortune. > 1 Ugh, we've been through this already.}","Investigate coin, choose \"Flip\".","Talk to Aris. {Chat: 1 Dimension of Disaster. > Any}","# Replay: {Chat: 1 Dimension of Disaster. > 2 Skip it.}","Use Double-headed coin on fountain (at Varrock Square).","Enter dimensional portal.","Talk to the Image of Zemouregal. {Chat: 3 Get to the point.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Dimension of Disaster: Shield of Arrav (Quick guide)"],"t":"Next sub-quest"}]},"Dimension of Disaster: Curse of Arrav":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Arrav in the centre of the castle to start the quest. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ernie upstairs in a pottery building south of the east bank in New Varrock and east of Aubury's Rune Shop to get a decorated cooking urn.\n  - If you have an active urn in your bank in the real dimension, it might get teleported to you and will count towards the quest progression. {Chat: 1 Arrav said you might have a canopic jar.}","Go to the zombie cow pen south-east of the eastern bank, kill roughly 11 cows (the exact number of meat needed varies), and collect the raw undead beef. It needs one backpack space or the urn may not start filling.","Chop and light some logs (there is a tree west next to Ernie's house) and cook the meat to fill your cooking urn.\n  - Also, a range can be used to cook the raw undead beef.\n  - If you have a started decorated cooking urn in your real bank, you might need a free inventory space for it to teleport into your inventory when you start cooking.\n    - Note: There is still a bug with this quest where sometimes you will receive a stackable urn whilst having a partially filled one in your inventory. You may need to go to the real Varrock to check your bank.*","Use the full cooking urn on Ernie if your setting to teleport full urns automatically is disabled. Otherwise, when full, it will teleport directly to him.","Talk to Ernie to get an empty canopic jar. {Chat: 1 Now will you give me the canopic jar? > 4 Farewell.}","Stop at Aubury's Magic Shop for 1 cosmic and 10 earth runes (a staff of earth also works).\n  - Optional: sell the cooked meat to the general store.","Buy a diamond from Urist Loric in New Varrock square and cut it.\n  - Optional: buy the 3 other gems, cut them, and sell them in the General Store for more Zemomarks than purchase price.","Buy gold ore from Sani at the furnace west of New Varrock square.","Make a diamond ring\n  - Smelt the ore by clicking on the furnace and then the gold ore under \"Core Ores\" on the left side of the smelting menu\n  - Make a diamond ring by clicking on the furnace and then the gold bar under the \"Casting Metals\" menu on the left side of the smelting menu.","Enchant the diamond ring to get a ring of life (1 cosmic, 10 earth runes and have standard magic book active).","If you don't already have one, buy a watering can at the general store in New Varrock Square and fill it up. Alternatively, you can pick up an already filled watering can in the atrium (centre room) of the castle.\n  - Replay: Not needed if you saved vial of purple mist.","Go to the church in north-east of New Varrock and speak with Father Lawrence. If you are using Ancient Curse prayers, switch to normal prayers by praying at the altar.","Activate a prayer depending on what Father Lawrence says:","After activating the correct prayer five times, Father Lawrence will give you the sacred oil.","Make sure you have a vial of red mist\n  - If you need one:\n    - Get a vial from the kitchen on the floor 1 of the castle.\n    - Head to the floor 2 using the stairs in the south-eastern corner of the fort.\n    - Kill an armoured zombie and collect the red mist that they drop.","Go to the south-eastern corner of the floor 1 in New Varrock Castle and pass through the north red barrier.","Search the corpse of Ambassador Ferrnook to obtain dwellberries.","Add the sacred oil, ring of life, and dwellberries to the canopic jar and make a prepared canopic jar.\n  - If you accidentally eat the dwellberries, simply search the corpse again.","Show the canopic jar to Arrav. {Chat: 1 Where is your heart? > 2 How do I get into the vault? > 3 How do I get through orange and purple barriers? > 4 Farewell.}}}"],"t":"Preparing the jar"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Arrav.\n  - Replay: If you kept the orange and the purple mists, skip ahead to taking the heart after this.","Get two vials from the easternmost room and fill them with water.","Talk to Ellamaria in the south-easternmost room near the steel cages to get Delphinium seeds.","Rake the Delphinium patch that's east of Arrav in the courtyard and plant the seeds, then water the patch and pick them.","If you don't have three total vials of red mist, head upstairs with empty vials and kill armoured zombies to collect the mist.","Buy an onion from Xuan north-west of the fountain, or pickpocket zombie citizens until you get one.","Talk to Thessalia and have her make a yellow dye and a blue dye. {Chat: 1 Arrav said you can make some dye. > 1 I have the ingredients to make yellow dye. > 2 I have the ingredients to make blue dye.}","Use the yellow and blue dyes on separate vials of red mist to get a vial of orange mist and a vial of purple mist.","Go back to the New Varrock castle and enter the north-west room (orange barrier) on the floor 1 and search the desk to get a code key. Optional: search the chest in this room (90 thieving and lockpick required) to complete an elite task/achievement.","Go up one floor, to the floor 2 to the south-east corner by the armoured zombies.\n  - Replay: If you kept the dyes/mists, skip to this step.\n  - In the south-eastern room, search the Crate of decoder strips to get decoder strips if you don't have them and can't remember the combination.\n    - Replay: Skip this step if you kept the decoder strips or you remember the combination."],"t":"Obtaining the heart"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the north-easternmost room on the floor 2 (purple barrier). Search the footlocker near the bed to get a vault key.","Head to the south-westernmost room, unlock the large vault door to the west, and enter the room.\n  - Before proceeding across the light beams, it is highly recommended that you deface the 3 paintings on the north wall of this room to complete the Bank-Z achievement. If you don't do it now, you need to replay all 4 New Varrock quests in order to complete this New Varrock achievement.","Equip the mithril crossbow and mithril grapple, and grapple the chandelier on the ceiling to cross the beams of light. If you've lost your crossbow and grapple, you can reclaim them from your respective gang, Black arm or Phoenix.","Fill in the code using the decoding strips and the code you got from Zemouregal's desk in the downstairs study to unlock the door (the code is random for everyone).\n  - Replay: The old code is displayed in chatbox, but the final combination is the same every time. If needed, decoder strips can be found in the armoured zombie room to the east of the vault outer door.","Enter the vault and take the heart from the pedestal.","Return to Arrav and talk to him.","Go to the Museum in east New Varrock.","Press the big red button (near the rock remains) to distract Orlando Smith (choose any option).\n  - Pickpocket the key from Curator Haig Halen\n  - Then take the shield of Arrav from the display case.\n  - If you have not completed the elite achievement Dark Imperator-ment, pressing the button again and using the remaining three options will do so (requires 91 Constitution and 75 in each of Attack, Magic and Ranged).","Head back to Arrav and talk to him to give him the shield and Darklight."],"t":"Taking the heart"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open the throne room door (behind Arrav) and enter the room by pressing OK","Talk to Sharathteerk.","Defeat Sharathteerk. You can spare or kill him, it doesn't matter.\n  - Pick-up the healing orb to heal yourself back to full health.","Go up the north-east stairs.","Defeat Zemouregal\n  - Replay: You can choose to skip the fight if you've purchased this option from Aris' Reward Shop.\n  - For the Moo-er of All Bombs achievement: it is highly recommended that you lure the five cows to him in order to complete the achievement on your first time through so you can skip the fight in the future (assuming you purchased this option from Aris' Reward Shop).\n    - This can be easily completed in the final phase of the fight, during which he spawns many cows continuously, thus be wary of attacking him in this final phase before getting the achievement.\n    - You must destroy all the Protection Portals before the cows will damage Zemouregal (and count towards your achievement).\n    - If you are having troubles remember the following:\n      - You can use the cows to help you destroy the portals.\n      - Each portal you have tagged before being exploded will still drop healing orbs, so if HP is a problem you should try to hit as many portals as you can 1-2 times and moving on to the next.\n      - It is better to die and try the fight again than to accidentally kill Zemouregal because completing this fight will force you to replay through the entirety of Dimension of Disaster again including all four of the quests again.","Final cutscene. {Chat: 4 I guess this is goodbye.}"],"t":"The Fight"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Be sure to talk to Aris and complete the main quest to earn your silver pennies.\n  - Do not use \"Complete\" in her right-click menu. You will not be rewarded your 5 silver pennies."],"t":"Complete main quest"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Dimension of Disaster: Coin of the Realm/Quick guide"],"t":"Back to beginning"}]},"Dimension of Disaster: Defender of Varrock":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Reldo in the Castle library of New Varrock. {Chat: Accept > 5 Arrav?}","In the courtyard just east of you, talk to Arrav. {Chat: 1 Would you be willing to bring down Zemouregal?}","Tell Reldo what you learned from Arrav.","Search the northern-most bookshelf along the western wall for Heart magic notes.","Talk to Reldo again.","If not wearing the zombie override version, equip the full Zombie outfit (mask, shirt, trousers, gloves, and boots). This can be purchased from Thessalia's Fine Clothes. See Zemomark for ways to earn more currency.\n  - Replay: Full New Varrock Zombie outfit cosmetic override can be purchased from Aris' Reward shop with silver pennies (you must talk to Aris in the real Varrock. You must exit New Varrock to access her reward shop in Varrock Square in the southwest corner).","Return to the New Varrock Castle. Enter the kitchen which is located on the floor 1 on the east side of the castle. You must enter the kitchen via the west door as a barrier prevents you from entering via the south door. Take 2 vials from the table.\n  - Replay: If you have saved red mist from a previous run, just head upstairs.","Head upstairs via the south-east staircase of the castle and kill 2 armoured zombies - collecting the red mist that they emit upon dying by clicking on it with a vial in your inventory.\n  - Replay: If you have saved red mist, skip.}}"],"t":"Zombie disguise"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go north and listen to Zemouregal over balcony.","On this same floor, enter the red barrier in the hallway to the centre balcony.","Head west, passing through 2 additional red barriers. You will be in a room with several coffins, a large wood table, and a tin soldier strapped to the table.","Inspect the tin soldier on the operating table in the south-western room.","Exit the castle by returning the way in which you entered.","Talk to the Trial Announcer at the east Varrock bank to get tin soldier head. {Chat: 3 Can I have a tin soldier head? > 1 I'd like to get ahead of competition. > 3 I have to go.}","Get three tin ores, four fire runes, and a nature rune. These can be purchased from Sani's ore shop south of the west bank and Aubury's rune shop south of the east bank.","Return to the tin soldier. Inspect him three times to activate him fully. {Chat: 1 Yes.}, {Chat: 1 Go-go, roboto!}, {Chat: 1 Yes.}\n  - Inspect the tin soldier one last time or just use a vial of red mist on the tin soldier if it has not automatically been applied."],"t":"Tin soldier"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Replay: Skip this step if you have the decoder strips.\n  - If you don't have the decoder strips, go to the armoured zombie room on the east side of the floor 2 of the castle, take the strips from the crate, then go to the next section.","Return to the far eastern room.","Search the crate in the armoured zombie room for some decoder strips.","Kill another armoured zombie if you need to refill empty vial with red mist.","Enter the red barrier to the far north-western room.","Scry the scrying pool in the north-eastern corner. Select {Chat: 1 New Varrock square > 2 Demon camp > 3 Graveyard > 4 Saradominist church > 5 Throne room balcony > 6 Garden of Hostility} (need to re-click on the scrying pool after each one) to unlock the medium New Varrock achievement Scrying Game and then {Chat: 7 Control the tin soldier} to continue the quest.","As the tin soldier, enter the room north and search Zemouregal's lab desk for the code."],"t":"Getting the code"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Unlock the treasure room safe (north-west corner of the north-west room) using the code you were given in the chatbox. Drag the red sliders over the numbers.","Enter the treasure room safe.","Smash the black prism."],"t":"Black prism"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Arrav twice.","Quest complete!","Pick up the watering can for the next sub-quest.\n  - Replay: Not needed if you saved purple mist."],"t":"Finishing up"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Dimension of Disaster: Curse of Arrav/Quick guide"],"t":"Final sub-quest"}]},"Dimension of Disaster: Demon Slayer":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Aris in New Varrock Square. {Chat: Accept}","Talk to Sir Prysin in a house north-west of the church.","Search everything inside the house and the drain outside until you find the key.\n  - Replay: The key will always be found in the same place you first found it.","Climb down the trapdoor inside the church along the western wall (be sure to complete the dialogue).\n  - Replay: Click the trapdoor, complete the dialogue, then head straight to Aris.","Attempt to pull Silverlight. You will fail.\n  - Replay: Skip this step.","Talk to Aris in her tent, she will give you a spirit measure."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the cemetery north of the New Varrock west bank and inspect the tombstone stack next to the statue of Zemouregal on the north wall.","Talk to Spirit of Faith. Move 1 step east. Talk again. Then watch the short cutscene."],"t":"Spirit of Faith"},{"n":"Cabbage, rotten tomato, dog hair, and beer glass or beer","r":"","s":["Pick up a rotten tomato in the crate north of the Blue Moon Inn and pick a cabbage to the south of the pub.","Talk to Dr Harlow in the Blue Moon Inn (exit dialogue after the first box comes up). Your Spirit measure may say \"WooOOooOOooOOooOOooOOoo!\" when you do.","At the cost of 2 Zemomarks, buy beer from the Bartender in the Blue Moon Inn. {Chat: 1 A glass of your finest ale. > 4 Nothing, thanks.}","To get dog hair, go west to Gertrude's house, just north of the tanner. Search the kennel next to her house. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 Yes. > 1 Reach left. > 1 Yes. > 2 Reach right. > 1 Rub in some jelly. > 3 Reach further in. > 1 Leave it where it is.}","Talk to the Apothecary to the south-east of the Kennel. {Chat: 2 Do you know a potion to sober someone up? > 4 Nothing, thanks.} He will use the cabbage, dog hair, and rotten tomato.","Add sobriety potion to beer for a sobriety potion in a beer glass.\n  - Keep the vial for later.","Talk to Dr Harlow.","Talk to the Spirit of the Body, and let them kill you {Chat: 2 Would you killing me count? > 1 Yes, do it - I'll be fine! > 1 Yes! Kill me already!}"],"t":"Spirit of the Body"},{"n":"Vial","r":"","s":["Fill vial with blood at blood fountain at the front of the Varrock castle or north-west of eastern bank.\n  - Optional: Take a free bronze sword from the weapon store two buildings south of Aris (only necessary if you don't have any other weapons yet).","Head to the house south of Sir Prysin's house (near the church).","Search the southern bookcase.","Kill the animated book.","Talk to Spirit of the Mind. {Chat: Any > Any > Any > Any > Any > Any > Any > Any > Any > Any > Any}\n  - Replay: {Chat: 4 I'm looking for you! > 3 A sword that slays demons. > 4 I need it to help Delrith get home. > 4 Agrith Naar. > 4 Aris!} (Always choose the last option whenever that last option says, \"I'm looking for you!\")"],"t":"Spirit of the Mind"},{"n":"Black mushroom","r":"","s":["Climb down the trapdoor in the church.","Take Silverlight from the altar.","Buy a black robe set from Thessalia's Fine Clothes (90 Zemomarks)\n  - Replay: Can use cosmetic override (Cultist outfit) if bought, or saved outfit.","Pick a black mushroom by Evil Dave in south-east New Varrock.","Use the mushroom on your Silverlight for a dyed version.","Equip the robes and dyed Silverlight, then talk to Evil Dave (located South-East of New Varrock)\n  - The Darklight and the dyed Silverlight override do not work with Silverlight equipped."],"t":"Evil Dave"},{"n":"","r":"Armour and food","s":["Pass barrier.\n  - Optional: It is recommended to loot the chest in the northeast corner of the area to work towards completing the Pick All achievement.","Talk to Delrith.","Talk to Delrith again for the fight (First time only: Don't forget to loot the chest).","Fight with Agrith Naar - choose \"Yes\".\n  - Replay: Choose \"Yes\" to skip the fight if unlocked from Aris' Reward Shop.\n  - Kill minions when they spawn.\n  - Run away when Agrith says \"Prepare to be incinerated!\"","Pass barrier.","Return to Aris.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up - Boss Fight"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Dimension of Disaster: Defender of Varrock/Quick guide"],"t":"Next sub-quest"}]},"Dimension of Disaster: Shield of Arrav":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Orlando Smith in the New Varrock Museum. {Chat: Accept > 3 Farewell.}","Speak to Charlie the Tramp {Chat: 1 Can you help me find the Black Arm Gang hideout? > 1 Give him a couple Zemomarks}","Speak to Katrine in the Black Arm Gang Hideout. {Chat: 1 I've heard you're the Black Arm Gang. > 1 I'd rather not reveal my sources. > 2 I want to join your gang. > 4 Farewell.}","Talk to Jonny the Beard in the Blue Moon Inn.","Talk again and defeat Jonny the Beard.\n  - If he disappears when you start fighting him, be sure to have auto retaliate on. You can reset the fight by walking upstairs and talking to him again.","Take the black arm to Katrine {Chat: 1 I've got your arm. > 1 I want to join the Black Arm Gang. > 4 Farewell.}\n  - Join the Black Arm Gang.","Talk to Moira in the back room until you get the documents.","Talk to Baraek in New Varrock square. {Chat: 1 Can you tell me where I can find the Phoenix Gang? > 1 Sure have 2 zemomarks. > 4 Farewell.}","Talk to Straven near the south-eastern wall of New Varrock. {Chat: 1 I know who you are! > 2 I want to join your gang. > 1 What do I have to do to join the Phoenix gang?}","Talk to Lowe in his archery emporium.","Go upstairs and take the moving egg by walking around the normal eggs.","Talk to Straven. {Chat: 1 I've got your phoenix eggling. > 3 Clap at the egg. > 1 I want to join the Phoenix Gang.}","Join Phoenix Gang. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Open the door to Molly's room using the pass phrase.","Talk to Molly in the next room until you get the documents."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the West New Varrock Bank.","Talk to Skeleton Clerk. {Chat: 1 I'm here for the Shield of Arrav. > 3 Goodbye.}","Head to the East New Varrock Bank and go upstairs.","Talk to the Skeleton Clerk. {Chat: 1 I'm here for the Shield of Arrav. > 3 Goodbye.}","Use the 2 shield pieces together to make the Shield of Arrav.","Talk to Orlando Smith at the New Varrock Museum.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Dimension of Disaster: Demon Slayer (Quick guide)"],"t":"Next sub-quest"}]},"Dishonour among Thieves":{"sections":[{"n":"Invitation box, 1 free inventory space.","r":"","s":["Open the invitation box to teleport to the Empyrean Citadel. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Moia. {Chat: Any > Accept > Any}","Talk to Sliske. {Chat: 3 [Continue] > Any}","Activate the communication device in your backpack. {Chat: 2 Teleport to Zamorak's Hideout.}","Continue dialogue with Zamorak. {Chat: Any > 1 Yes, to steal the Stone of Jas. > 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Moia. {Chat: 4 [More...] > 2 Zemouregal and Enakhra. > 1 Teleport me. > 1 Yes.}","Kill the armoured zombies.","Go upstairs and talk to Zemouregal or Enakhra. {Chat: 1 I've come to speak with you. > 3 [Continue]}","Search the orange and brown chest for 3 cut gems, 5k coins, and 250 Dungeoneering tokens before leaving the room. }}"],"t":"Enakhra/Zemouregal"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the cave entrance north-west of the Kandarin Monastery.","Board the raft.","Talk to Hazeel. {Chat: 3 [Continue]}","Go down the trapdoor behind Handelmort Mansion.","Talk to Jerrod. {Chat: 2 A friend of Hazeel's. > 3 The red eyes.}","Search the dead butler for a cell key.","Unlock the cell door.","Talk to Jerrod.","Search the orange and brown chest for 3 cut gems, 5k coins, and 250 Dungeoneering tokens before leaving the room."],"t":"Hazeel/Jerrod"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the Ruins of Uzer (fairy ring dlq, then north-east).","Enter and talk to General Khazard. {Chat: 3 [Continue] > 1 Yes.}","In the shadow realm, search Palkeera's corpse.","Speak to Khazard.","Search the orange and brown chest for 3 cut gems, 5k coins, and 250 Dungeoneering tokens before leaving the room."],"t":"Khazard"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the Black Knights' Base in the Taverley Dungeon.\n  - Via the Master archaeologist's outfit to Isaura, an artefact collector in the base. {Chat: 0 Collectors > 4 Isaura}\n  - Via an Archaeology teleport purchased from Ezreal in the Archaeology Guild for 250 chronotes.\n  - Via a hoardstalker ring or dungeoneering cape {Chat: 0 More... > 1 Taverley blue dragon dungeon} and running south.","Talk to Lord Daquarius in the south-west corner. {Chat: 1 Dishonour Among Thieves.}","Talk to the Preaching Black Knight in the middle. {Chat: Any}","Speak to the group of black knights in the north-east corner. {Chat: Any}","Get the poison from the chest in the north-west corner.","Talk to Lord Daquarius.","Search the orange and brown chest for 3 cut gems, 5k coins, and 250 Dungeoneering tokens before leaving the room."],"t":"Lord Daquarius"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter Death's office.\n  - Home Teleport to the Draynor lodestone and head north.\n  - War's Retreat Teleport and then exit to Death's office via the portal. {Chat: 2 Death's office}","Continue dialogue with Death and Nomad. {Chat: 2 [Continue] > Any}","If ready for combat, accept the teleport to the hideout. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Nomad"},{"n":"Combat equipment and food if lower-levelled","r":"","s":["Activate the Communication device to return to Zamorak's Hideout. {Chat: 2 Teleport to Zamorak's hideout}","Continue the dialogue. {Chat: 1 Move on. > Any}","Search the orange and brown chest for 3 cut gems, 5k coins, and 250 Dungeoneering tokens on the western end of the hideout before leaving the room.","Go to the Barrows and enter the dungeon to the south-east (outside the stone wall).\n  - Via Drakan's medallion {Chat: 1 Barrows}","Search the orange and brown chest for 3 cut ruby gems, 5k coins, and 250 Dungeoneering tokens just North of the lair entrance.","Enter Sliske's lair (you cannot enter with a familiar summoned)."],"t":"The plan"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["From the first room, enter the cave entrances as follows:\n  - Blue (blue paint above the entrance) (western door)\n  - 5 (V) (on the floor) (south door)- players that use \"low detail\" may have some trouble seeing the V-shape. You can examine the slabs to be told which number is engraved on it, if it is unclear.\n  - A sinister green face (northern most door).\n  - Triangle (north-eastern most door).\n  - Red (red paint above the door) (south-eastern door).\n  - Complete face (On the floor) (north-eastern door).\n  - Grey (may also appear as a white colour; western door in the north-eastern corner).","Watch a cutscene. {Chat: any}"],"t":"Sliske's maze"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Wait for the Wight to face away from you and forward dive behind them to close the gap. Left-click to assassinate them.","Wait for the masks to scan 3 times.","Move quickly to the middle of the room and pull the lever.","Get caught, walk west to room 2 (pull the lever)."],"t":"Room 1"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Stand on the right side of the hallway with the shadow and forward dive to the doorway on the east, avoiding the shadow along the way (use the crevices on the sides of the hallway to hide).\n  - It may be very hard to see the shadow. It is a pulsating black light on the floor, moving up and down the corridor.","Assassinate the Wight and pull the lever.","Go through the passageway now open at the beginning of the room, forward dive past the Wight, and assassinate them.","Proceed up the hallway and dive past the last two masks to the lever.","Enter room 3."],"t":"Room 2"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Forward dive past the guard (1) to the east and assassinate him.","Continue north and dispatch the next guard (2).","Stand in the doorway to the main hallway and wait for the guard (3) to come to you and dispatch him (watch for the shadow on the floor).","Continue across the hallway and dispatch the guard walking around the pillar (4).","Go north to the lever (2) and pull it. Rocks will fall, distracting the guard (5). Dispatch him and pull the lever (3).","Return to Jerrod. You can get caught to get back quickly.","Go back east and then down the narrow hallway and stop before entering the main hallway, wait for the shadow to go to the far end and cross the main hallway, enter the room across from you and assassinate the guard (6).","Return to the south-east corner and pull the lever (1).","Head to the north-east lever, avoiding the shadow. Stand in the south-east corner of the hallway where the shadow is patrolling; when the shadow moves away, move one space north, click the option to turn 45 degrees left, then forward dive. Assassinate the guard (7).","Go behind the shadow and pull the lever (4).","Jerrod will kill the last guard (near lever 5) by the doors. Pull the final lever by the door, watching for the main hallway shadow.","Once inside, finish the dialogue. {Chat: 1 Okay, will do.}"],"t":"Room 3"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Right click track with Jerrod. Use chat options 1 or 2 to direct the camera to face the footprints. Then select option 3 to track. If done correctly, Jerrod will start following the footprints.","Right-click read mind with Moia in the centre. If she doesn't let you, wait for Jerrod to be in position.\n  - Mouse around the interface until you find the position such that the probe blinks fast (approximately twice per second), then left-click to probe the memory. Turning on sound effects can help.","After reading the first wraith's mind, light and shadow levels will show up on the top of the screen, trending in opposite directions. To maintain their balance, right-click switch on either Nomad or Enakhra to make it go the opposite direction.","After reading the second wraith's mind, the passageways on the western and eastern walls will show glowing yellow eyes. Talk to Zemouregal to move the purple portals to the two spots with eyes. Note the compass to make sure you are selecting the correct location.","Keeping an eye on the light and shadow levels, repeat this process for 5 total memories: track with Jerrod, read mind with Moia, then select the corresponding locations for the glowing eyes with Zemouregal.","Open the large vault door.","Watch the cutscene. {Chat: Any > Any}"],"t":"Memories"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Fight and kill your shadow apparition.\n  - Run off the platform when teleported to the centre and move out of the path of the smoke. It travels straight down the stairs.\n  - Stand near the boss when he summons darkness or you will take massive damage.\n  - Click rapidly to escape cocoons."],"t":"Your apparition"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill 30 wights around the room.","Use Nomad's special attacks to kill multiple wights with a single hit."],"t":"Wights"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Touch the Stone of Jas. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Kill everyone's apparition.","All damage is increased to 10,000 and above, capping at 25,000.\n  - As such, bleed attacks are helpful here as well as AoE."],"t":"Apparitions"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Stop Nomad. {Chat: 1 You don't have to do this. > 1 Stop Nomad - throw the spear back.}\n  - You must choose to stop him, otherwise he becomes powerful in future quests.","Make sure to watch the final cutscene without skipping; Otherwise, you will need to re-enter the hideout {Chat: 3 [Continue] > 2 [Continue] > 3 Remain neutral. > 2 No}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Do No Evil":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["If you did not bring Leela to Senliten's tomb, speak to Leela in Draynor Village, who is just north of the northern fence line of the jail; she will teleport the player to Senliten. Leela can only be found there afterwards.\n  - If you need to return later, you can pick the option to return to the Pharaoh Queen directly (without having to go through the pyramid)."],"t":"Before starting the quest"},{"n":"Any kind of cat, kitten, or hellcat, 1,000 coins and desert survival equipment","r":"","s":["Talk to Senliten in Uzer Mastaba. {Chat: 2 Talk about Do No Evil. > 3 Where are you going with this? > Accept}\n  - Inside the pyramid east of fairy ring code dlq or north-east of Nardah which is easily reached by using Desert amulet 2 or above.","Head to Sophanem and talk to Jex north of the Sphinx. {Chat: 2 Could you tell me more about the minor gods? > 4 Could you tell me more about Apmeken? > 1 Could you tell me more about Apmeken's connection with monkeys? > 2 Could you tell me more about Apmeken's followers? > 3 Could you tell me more about Apmeken's influence over the desert?}\n  - Players can right click on Coenus by the bridge (near the Menaphos lodestone) to pass through to Sophanem.\n  - To quickly enter the magic carpet network, use a charged amulet of glory and teleport to Al Kharid, or use a Desert amulet 2 to teleport to Nardah.","Drop your cat and talk to the Sphinx {Chat: 2 Can you tell me about the gods of the Menaphites? > 3 Tell me about the minor gods. > 4 Tell me about Apmeken.}","Go back and talk to Senliten. {Chat: 2 Talk about Do No Evil.}."],"t":"Senliten's concern"},{"n":"Any monkey greegree, a monkeyspeak amulet, at least 10 coins, and a lot of backpack space (20+ to make it easy in one try).","r":"","s":["Fill your entire backpack with Green bananas by using take banana from the pile of bananas crate to the east and lay a trail to lure the guard to the crate (you can place bananas every few squares to ensure the guard does not give up. Key-binding the Green banana will make this step easier). You will have to go counter-clockwise around the building due to the large gorilla posted on the north side. See the full guide for advice on luring the guard efficiently.","Return to the three wise monkeys and talk to them.","Remove your greegree and speak to them in human form.","Equip your greegree and speak to them again. {Chat: 2 The baboon head. > 4 On the monkey's shoulder.}","Talk to Awowogei, who is in the building south of the temple. {Chat: 1 To build the greatest monkey colony ever! > 5 Next. > 3 Choc ices from Nardah.}","If you don't have a monkeyspeak amulet mould, Hamab's crafting stall sells one, which is needed for the next step."],"t":"Three Wise Monkeys"},{"n":"1,000 coins, Monkey greegree, rope, Monkeyspeak amulet, Monkeyspeak amulet mould, Ancient Magicks spellbook, runes for either Ice Burst, Ice Blitz, or Ice Barrage.","r":"Anti-poison potions, good armour, energy potions, and food.","s":["Talk to Rokuh in Nardah next to the fountain. {Chat: 1 Commission Awowogei's choc ice. > 1 Deal! > 2 So, if I don't teleport it won't melt?}","You should receive one chimp ice. If it melts, right click on Rokuh to buy another. Click to stop it from melting. Higher level spells, like Ice Barrage, will last longer.\n  - Unlike standard ancient spell casting, you do not need a staff/wand and orb/book for this. Only the runes are enough.","Helpful things to keep in mind:\n  - Looking at the world map prevents the chimp ice from melting.\n    - If you are out of run energy, rest and pull up the world map.\n  - Talking to NPC's prevents the chimp ice from melting.\n  - Using transportation such as magic carpets and eagles prevents the chimp ice from melting.","Take the chimp ice to King Awowogei without teleporting (this route requires completion of Eagles' Peak. For a full list of routes, see the in-depth quest guide):\n  - From Nardah, use the magic carpet to Uzer.\n  - Run north-west to the desert eagle lair located north of the Uzer Hunter area and north-east of the Dominion Tower. Enter the tunnel shown in the picture, and use the rope that spawns nearby on an eagle to be transported.\n  - Exit the cave via the north-west entrance and climb down the mountain.\n  - Run east into Tree Gnome Stronghold, up floor 2 of the Grand Tree and find Daero to the east to travel to the Secret Hangar.\n  - Talk to Waydar to travel to Crash Island.\n  - Talk to Lumdo to travel to Ape Atoll. You get a checkpoint here where you can restart if the chimp ice melts.\n  - Run to King Awowogei. The chimp ice can't be frozen while transformed as a monkey, so choose your moments carefully. An easy method is to freeze it at the mahogany tree before the main gate, turn into a monkey, and enter the gate. Run east to the small obelisk across from the agility course and hide in the grass to freeze it again. Then turn back into a monkey, and run to King Awowogei.","Go to the wise monkeys and add them to the barrel."],"t":"Chimp ice"},{"n":"ring of charos (a), Ava's accumulator, monkeyspeak amulet, monkey greegree, a spade, barrel of monkeys, a weapon to kill low-level enemies -- if you have a gem bag and wear the desert clothing set below you can bring the items from the next section to avoid bank travel.","r":"","s":["Teleport to Bandit Camp in the Kharidian Desert","Head north-east around the cliff to the area shown here on the map (you need to be below the cliff) and release the monkeys (open the barrel).","Equip Monkey Speak Amulet and talk to one of the Wise Monkeys.","With your ring of charos (a) equipped, speak to Ali Morrisane (north of the Al Kharid lodestone). {Chat: 2 Talk about Do No Evil.}\n  - There is currently an issue where this option might only show up after completing The Feud, despite this quest not being listed as a requirement any more.","Unequip your Ava's accumulator if you're wearing it.","Take the crate to and talk to Ava in Draynor Manor until you get Ava's alerter. {Chat: 5 Talk about making a metal detector.}","Pick up the spade in the easternmost room if you do not already have one.","Go to the fountain in the south-western corner of the manor's grounds.","Wear your Ava's alerter and walk two steps east from the dead tree that can be converted to a hidey-hole, just north-east of the fountain. Dig when it says Bwuk! Bwuk! Bwuk! Bwuk!","Return to Ava. {Chat: 5 Talk about Ava's alerter.}","Teleport to Bandit Camp and in the area north-east of the monkey camp search for crates using the map pictured right. You should dig up 5 crates, repeat this until you receive bundle of carpets.\n  - If you obtain any uncut gems or noted waterskins, save them for the next step.\n  - If you discover a scarab, kill it and then dig again.","Talk to the three wise monkeys twice for a book.","Read the book or at least open it."],"t":"The colony"},{"n":"1 hammer & 1 saw (toolbelt works for both), 6 teak planks (protean planks and planks stored in the plank box will not work), 10 bolts of cloth, 1 rope, 1 uncut sapphire, 1 uncut emerald, 1 uncut ruby, 1 uncut diamond (gems are obtained during quest), 1 pair of desert boots, 1 desert robe, 1 desert shirt and 1 Monkeyspeak amulet, 10 noted bananas, 3 noted knives, 3 noted waterskins (4), and a spade. The desert equipment, knives and waterskins can be bought at the Bandit Camp general store nearby.","r":"","s":["Clear Rubble from the four building spots in the colony.","Build-on the 3 stall plots using your supplies.","Stock the stalls.\n  - Careful not to stock a stall twice - each one needs to be stocked with one set of items.","Build-on Tent plot","Talk to the wise monkeys.","Talk to them again. {Chat: 2 Right, I'll get on with it.}"],"t":"Building the colony"},{"n":"gorilla greegree (also a ninja monkey greegree (small) if using the fairy ring), 1 Monkeyspeak amulet","r":"","s":["Head back to Ape Atoll and find the building with the monkey knife fighters; it is located just east of the building with the Monkey Child.","Punch and then quickly pickpocket the monkey fighters for 6 Monkey knives. The success rate is fairly low, so be prepared to punch at least 30 monkeys.\n  - If you are fast enough, you can get three pickpockets until the monkey wakes up again","Return to the three wise monkeys and hand the knives over.","Talk to the monkeys again."],"t":"Arming the colony"},{"n":"Ghostspeak amulet and Monkeyspeak amulet","r":"","s":["Return to the pyramid south of the Ruins of Uzer, east of dlq, and click the door for a cutscene.","Enter the pyramid and speak to Senliten. {Chat: 2 Talk about Do No Evil. > Any}","Teleport to Bandit Camp and head back to the colony.","Investigate any Corpse to make a ghost monkey appear.","Try to talk to the ghost monkey.","Use one of the amulets on the other to create a cramulet.","Talk to the ghost monkey. {Chat: 3 I must try to rescue them.}"],"t":"Boss fights"},{"n":"masked earmuffs or a slayer helmet, a cramulet and combat gear.","r":"","s":["Climb down the well in the middle of Pollnivneach, pass through the Wavering mystic barrier to the north {Chat: 2 You're going to die here.}.","Kill Leeuni (50,000 life points).","After defeating Leeuni, talk to Iwazaru.","Return to the monkey colony and speak to the ghost monkey again to unlock the next boss.}}"],"t":"Leeuni"},{"n":"2 ropes if you have never entered the Kalphite Queen's lair, a cramulet and combat gear","r":"","s":["After the battle, talk to Mizaru. Leave through the east exit to unlock a shortcut or get transported {Chat: 5 Return to the colony.}.","Return to the monkey colony and speak to the ghost monkey again to unlock the next boss."],"t":"Ayuni"},{"n":"a cramulet and combat gear","r":"","s":["Warning! Eruni hits much harder than the other two. Although she has lower defence. Be prepared for an intense fight. Protection prayers and high-healing food strongly recommended.","Head to the ruins of Uzer, down the steps and through the door to the north into the demonic realm.","Eruni will be invincible whenever she summons lesser demons; they must be killed immediately.","After defeating Eruni, speak to Kikazaru, who will take you to the colony."],"t":"Eruni"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to the three wise monkeys at the colony - Apmeken will appear and speak to you. {Chat: 2 And what of Apmeken?}","Return to Senliten. {Chat: 2 Talk about Do No Evil.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Doric's Task I (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Doric in his hut north of Falador. {Chat: 1 Do you have any more Smithing tasks for me? > Accept}","Smith an iron full helm +1\n  - It can not be purchased off the Grand Exchange or smithed on any other anvil but Doric's, however players can buy an unimproved iron full helm from the Grand Exchange and upgrade themselves to +1.","Deliver it to Aksel at Artisans' Workshop. {Chat: 1 Doric sent me here with another delivery.}}} Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Delivery for Aksel"}]},"Doric's Task II (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Doric in his hut north of Falador. {Chat: 1 Do you have any more Smithing tasks for me? > Accept}","Smith two steel chainbodies.\n  - Make sure you are smithing chainbodies, not platebodies.\n  - Purchasing chainbodies from the Grand Exchange will not complete the task.","Deliver the chainbodies to Commander Denulth, north-east of Burthorpe lodestone. {Chat: 1 Ask about Doric's Tasks}\n  - There are breaks in the dialogue. Make sure the conversation is completed.","Return to Doric and speak to him. {Chat: 1 Do you have any more Smithing tasks for me? > Accept}","Have 2 unnoted bronze bars in your inventory.","Use the anvil in the same room as Doric to make the cannon repair part.","Return to Burthorpe and head north to the castle. Outside the castle, climb the ladder west of the entrance to reach the roof.","Repair the middle broken cannon to the north.","Return to Commander Denulth. {Chat: 1 I've fixed the cannon.}}} Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Attack of the Trolls"}]},"Doric's Task III (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Doric in his hut north of Falador. {Chat: 1 Do you have any more Smithing tasks for me? > Accept}","Make a mithril longsword +1 and a mithril warhammer +1.","Head north to Goblin village and talk to either General Bentnoze or General Wartface TWICE in the building in the back.}} Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Warhammers and longswords"}]},"Doric's Task IV (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Doric in his hut north of Falador. {Chat: 1 Do you have any more Smithing tasks for me? > Accept}","Make an adamant burial set in the Artisans' Workshop located in southeast Falador.\n  - You must make the \"burial set\" and not make the burial items individually.\n  - If the player has never made burial armour before they must first talk to Suak. {Chat: 2 How can I make burial armour?}. To make a burial set the player first needs to acquire:\n    - Adamant full helm +2.\n    - Adamant platelegs +2.\n    - Adamant platebody +2.\n    - Adamant armoured boots +2.\n    - Adamant gauntlets +2.\n  - It is possible to buy all five pieces off the Grand exchange to complete this task.","Talk to Suak."],"t":"Burial armour"}]},"Doric's Task V (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Doric in his hut north of Falador. {Chat: 1 Do you have any more Smithing tasks for me? > Accept}","Smith 4 Gnome platebodies on Doric's anvil.\n  - Have 4 steel platebodies in the backpack to make them.","Smith 3 rune swords +1 on any anvil.","Talk to Commander Montai on the Battlefield south of Ardougne.}} Miniquest complete!"],"t":"A gnomish request"}]},"Doric's Task VI (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Doric in his hut north of Falador. {Chat: 1 Do you have any more Smithing tasks for me? > Accept}","Smith an orikalkum warhammer +3. This cannot be one that was bought or traded, or smithed before accepting the quest.","Deliver the warhammer to Skulgrimen, in the armour hut just north of the long hall in Rellekka. {Chat: 3 I have your order from Doric & Son.}}} Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Fremennik of War"}]},"Doric's Task VII (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Doric in his hut north of Falador. {Chat: 1 Do you have any more Smithing tasks for me? > Accept}","Head to the northwesternmost building in western Keldagrim.","Talk to Santiri. {Chat: 1 Doric sent me here to make your dreams come true. > 1 I'll ask him for it now.} (If this is your first time in Keldagrim, you may need to talk to Santiri to accept an unrelated task, talk to him again to cancel it, and then talk to him a final time to start dialogue about the miniquest.)","Talk to the Supreme Commander in the building south of him up the stairs. {Chat: ? (3 or 4 depending on completed quests) I must go now.}","Use the black guard warhammer on an anvil (one is located south of the building the Supreme Commander is in).","Talk to Santiri. {Chat: 1 I have your warhammer.}","Talk to the Librarian, in the northeasternmost building in western Keldagrim. {Chat: ? (2, 3, or 4 depending on the situation) Can you tell me about first-generation black warhammers?}","Head to the Stonemason in the southernmost building in western Keldagrim. {Chat: 4 Do you know anything about crushing warhammers?}","Use the cracked warhammer on the stone crusher in the northwest corner of the building.","Talk to Santiri. {Chat: 1 I have your warhammer.}","Head to eastern Keldagrim and use the crushed warhammer on the well.","Talk to Santiri. {Chat: 1 I have your warhammer.}"],"t":"Nostalgic Warhammers"}]},"Doric's Task VIII (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Doric in his hut north of Falador. {Chat: 1 Do you have any more Smithing tasks for me? > Accept > 1 I'm sure it will be fine.}\n  - Ensure you received a weapons crate.","Smith 5 necronium 2h greataxes on any anvil.","Left-click add items to the weapons crate. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Head to the Gem Store in Falador and investigate the tree stump, just south. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Watch the cutscene.","Investigate the tree stump again.}} Miniquest Complete!"],"t":"The mysterious client"}]},"Dragon Slayer":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Guildmaster in the Champions' Guild. {Chat: 2 Can I have a quest? > Accept}","Talk to Oziach in the house directly north of the Edgeville lodestone. {Chat: 1 Can you sell me a rune platebody? > 1 The Guildmaster of the Champions' Guild told me. > 1 I thought you were going to give me a quest. > 1 A dragon, that sounds like fun.}","Go back to the Guildmaster and talk about the map pieces to get the key, about protection against dragon breath, and about buying a boat. {Chat: 2 I talked to Oziach... > 1 How can I find the route to Crandor? > 1 Where is Melzar's Map piece? > 1 Where is Thalzar's Map piece? > 2 Where is Lozar's Map piece? > 3 Where can I find the right ship? > 2 How can I protect myself from the dragon's breath? > 3 Okay, I'll get going!}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"Maze key","r":"Food and combat equipment, 2 backpack spaces","s":["Go to Melzar's Maze, north-west of Rimmington.","Enter the door with the maze key.","Kill the small zombie rat with the long tail, pick up the red key and use it on the north-west door, then go up the ladder.","Kill the thin hooded ghost with the patterned robe to receive the orange key, go through the door second from the north on the eastern wall and climb the ladder.","Kill the skeleton with the small round shield and pick up the yellow key. Use the key on the south-western most door and climb down until you get to the zombies.","Kill the zombies. One of them will drop a blue key. Pass through the blue door.","Kill Melzar the Mad, pick up the magenta key and pass through the magenta coloured door.","Kill the lesser demon, pick up the green key, and go through the green door.","Open the chest and search it for the map part.\n  - Note: Make sure you finish the dialogue, or you will not receive the map part."],"t":"First map part"},{"n":"Unfired bowl, wizard's mind bomb, lobster pot or a crayfish cage, and silk","r":"","s":["Talk to the Oracle on Ice Mountain. {Chat: 1 I seek a piece of the map to the island of Crandor.}","Travel south into the dwarven mines. Find the room with a sealed door in the north-eastern area of the mine and use all the items on the \"Magic door\". (Unfired bowl, wizard's mind bomb, lobster pot or a crayfish cage, and silk)","Open the chest in the room and search for the second map part after opening. You need to click again to search after the dialogue, it does not automatically loot or search."],"t":"Second map part"},{"n":"Either 10,000 coins, or a halberd, Ranged, Magic or Necromancy weapon","r":"","s":["Head to Port Sarim Jail and talk to Wormbrain in the cell.\n  - You may need to speak with the Guild Master at this point before you can attack Wormbrain.","There are two ways to obtain the third map part:\n  - Talk to Wormbrain and pay him 10,000 coins for the map part. {Chat: 1 I believe you've got a piece of map that I need. > 3 I suppose I could pay you for the map piece... > 2 Alright then, 10,000 it is.}\n  - Attack Wormbrain and use the loot interface or Telekinetic Grab to get the map part that he drops. You may need to drop an item in order for the loot interface to open.","Use a map part on any one of the other parts to form the complete Crandor map."],"t":"Third map part"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Duke Horacio on the floor 2 of Lumbridge Castle. {Chat: 1 I seek a shield that will protect me from dragonbreath. > 1 Elvarg, the dragon of Crandor island! > 1 Yes. > 2 So, are you going to give me the shield or not?}\n  - You can also buy an anti-dragon shield from the Grand Exchange to skip this step entirely.\n  - If the dialogue option for the anti-dragon shield doesn't appear, you need to talk to the Guildmaster about protection from dragon fire"],"t":"Obtaining an anti-dragon shield"},{"n":"Crandor map, 2,000 coins, 90 steel nails, 3 planks, and a hammer (tool belt works)}} {{Checklis","r":"","s":["If you haven't already, ask the Guildmaster in the Champions' Guild about the boat and the captain of the ship.","In Port Sarim, buy the ship Lady Lumbridge from Klarense, by the Void knight Squire. {Chat: 4 I'd like to buy her. > 1 Yep, sounds good.}","Repair the damaged deck of the ship.","Go to Draynor Village. In the house north-east of the bank talk to Ned. {Chat: 2 Talk about something else. > 1 You're a sailor? Could you take me to Crandor?}"],"t":"Obtaining a ship"},{"n":"Food, potions, combat equipment, anti-dragon shield","r":"Antifire potion, amulet of glory with at least 1 charge to teleport to Edgeville","s":["Prepare the battle against Elvarg.\n  - Melee is recommended due to how hit chances are calculated.\n  - Players with level 37 Prayer can use Protect from Magic.","Board your ship and talk to Ned. Tell him you're ready to sail to Crandor Isle. {Chat: 1 Yes, let's go!}","After crashing on the island, follow the light grey path around and up to the top of the mountain. Climb down the hole.","Move past the skeletons until you see Elvarg behind a short wall of spikes protruding from the ground on the east.","Before you climb over to Elvarg its advisable to open the shortcut in the wall south of the short wall.","Climb over it and kill Elvarg.\n  - Wear your dragonfire protection before hopping over, or your stats will get drained resulting most likely in a failed kill.\n  - If you leave Crandor before killing Elvarg or opening the shortcut, you will need 3 planks and 90 steel nails to repair the ship to get back."],"t":"The fight"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take Elvarg's head to Oziach in Edgeville.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Conclusion"}]},"Dream Mentor":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the mine in the north-east area of Lunar Isle.","Crawl-through the cave entrance (quest minimap icon).","Talk to the fallen man (close the interface when it appears). {Chat: Accept}","Starting with one of your 7 item foods, feed him 4 food while cycling through your different foods.\n  - Starting with a food item of which you brought 7 items will ensure you do not run out of variety.","Talk to him again. {Chat: 1 Just don't worry. > 1 Of course.}","Feed him 4 more food as before."],"t":"A helping hand"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to repeatedly to raise his spirits:\n  - Of the four chat options, choose the one that appears on the table below.\n  - Select the response according to the table.\n  - Repeat until a short cutscene plays and he sits up.","Feed him 6 more food.","Talk to him and raise his spirit as before until he stands up.","Exit the cave and climb up the ladder.\n  - Or just use the Lunar Isle lodestone","Talk to 'Bird's-Eye' Jack in the bank. {Chat: 2 Cyrisus in the mine} You will need 1 free inventory space for Cyrisus's chest.","Select the equipment he needs. The equipment is usually, but not always, dependent on your highest combat stats (Magic, Ranged, Melee):\n  - Melee: Dragon helm, Abyssal whip, Ahrim's robe top, Ahrim's robe skirt, Ranger boots\n  - Ranged: Splitbark Helm, Karil's top, Torag's platelegs, Adamant boots, Magic shortbow\n  - Magic: Robin Hood hat, Dragon Chainbody, Black dragonhide chaps, Infinity boots, Ancient staff","You can use the NPC Contact spell to ensure you have the right equipment.","Return and talk to Cyrisus for a cutscene. {Chat: 1 Talk about the Armament}","Right-click \"inspect\" and fill the remaining stats until he tells you that he is ok (if not already)."],"t":"Raising his spirit"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Oneiromancer at the astral altar (most south-eastern part of the Lunar Isle) for a dream vial (herb). {Chat: 2 Cyrisus}","Change your spellbook as necessary if you wish to use magic in the final fight.","Use an astral rune on an anvil (there's one on Lunar Isle in a small building to the south), then grind the shards. Add it to the potion.","Prepare for 4 fights (below level 100). Prayers and emergency teleports won't work. Neither will familiars."],"t":"Dream potion"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Light the Ceremonial Brazier in the long hall building, near the lodestone.","Talk to Cyrisus (dismiss any followers before). {Chat: 1 Yes, let's go!}\n  - Do not click away of the chat or you will be teleported out","During the fight, you can leave at any time by using the pedestal.\n  - Kill The Inadequacy\n  - Kill The Everlasting (can safespot by the pedestal)\n  - Kill The Untouchable (can safespot by the pedestal)\n  - Kill The Illusive","Return to the Oneiromancer. {Chat: 2 Cyrisus}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Dreamland"}]},"Druidic Ritual":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Kaqemeex south of the Heroes' Guild. {Chat: 1 Talk about Druidic Ritual. > 1 What do you need help with? > 1 I'm pretty sure I've heard that before. > Accept}","Run directly south and enter the last house on the west near the Herblore icon.","Talk to Sanfew. {Chat: 1 I've been sent to help make an ointment of imbalance for Kaqemeex. > 4 Ok, I'll do that then.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"Vial","r":"","s":["Go north and enter the Burthorpe Slayer Cave directly east of the crayfish pond.","Head south and fill your vial at the subterranean spring for a vial of living water.","Exit the cave."],"t":"Untainted living water"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head south until you find wandering wyrmwood, then take-from one of them for wandering wyrmwood."],"t":"Wandering wyrmwood"},{"n":"One coin","r":"","s":["At the west part of the lake, bait the Sparkling Fishing Spot.","Gather-scales from the stone fish, choosing the chisel option."],"t":"Stone scales"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Sanfew for a cutscene.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Duck Quest":{"sections":[{"n":"vial of water, duck food","r":"","s":["Head south of the bank in Draynor Village and fish the fishing spot?. {Chat: Accept > Any}","Pick up the nest debris just north of the bridge leading to the Wizards' Tower.","Continue picking it up south east along the coast, east through the swamp, when you reach the graveyard head north past the Lumbridge castle towards Fred the Farmer's house (through Lumbridge market), north over the bridge, then just west near the Waddle Willow tree.","Talk to Breadstix. {Chat: 2 What are you up to at the moment? > 2 What's the language? (Continue Quest)}","Use duck food on a vial of water to make a duckspeak potion.","Talk to Breadstix again.","Drink the potion. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Jemima. {Chat: 3 Okay - I'll start the Inducktion.}","Talk to Invigilatoad. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Eat each of the six peas. They are indicated as red dots on the minimap.","Talk to Invigilatoad again. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Sit down at the relaxing spot at the end of the path to the west.","Talk to Paddlington Badger on the west edge of the sanctuary.","Interact with the floor button on the east side of the sanctuary.","Press the floor button south from Paddlington badger. {Chat: 4 Something might happen?}","Press the floor button on the east side of the sanctuary.","Interact with the tree bud directly north of the east button.","Interact with the toad statue twice.","Talk to duckling's dad or mum.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Walkthrough"}]},"Dwarf Cannon":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Captain Lawgof by the coal truck mining site west of Seers' Village. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["From the inside, inspect and repair the six broken sections of wall along the west and south side of the area (look for the sections with crumbling stones).","Talk to Captain Lawgof.","Exit the gate to the south and go to the tower just outside the gate, directly east of Glarial's tombstone.","Climb up two ladders and take the dwarf remains.","Talk to Captain Lawgof.","Head south-east to the cave entrance at the eastern wall of the Fishing Guild.\n  - Quickest way to get there is to teleport to Ardougne lodestone and then run north.","Enter the Goblin Cave.","Go as far north-west as possible and search the crates in the north-east corner of that room.","Once you find Lollk, return and talk to Captain Lawgof. {Chat: 1 Okay, I'll see what I can do.}","Use the toolkit you got from Captain Lawgof on the broken multicannon next to him.","In this order:\n  - Use the hooked tool on the spring.\n  - Use the pliers on the safety switch at the bottom.\n  - Use the tooth tool on the gear located at the bottom of the hammer.","Talk to Captain Lawgof. Make sure to finish conversation. {Chat: 2 Okay then, just for you!}\n  - This conversation must be completely finished.","Go to the Dwarven Mines north-east of Falador."],"t":"Repair and retrieval"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["In the outpost, talk to Nulodion. He is standing right next to the Dwarf multicannon, outside of the entrance to the Dwarven Mine north of Falador.","# If you drop the ammo mould he gives you and speak to him again he will give you another. The second ammo mould can be added to your tool belt after the quest to save having to revisit him.","Return to Captain Lawgof.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Eadgar's Ruse":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Start the quest by speaking to Sanfew, who lives on the east side of Taverley, south-west of the summoning shop. {Chat: 2 Ask general questions. > 1 Have you any more work for me, to help reclaim the circle? > Accept}\n  - If Zogre Flesh Eaters is not complete, use the following option: {Chat: 1 Have you any more work for me? > Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"Climbing boots","r":"","s":["Equip your climbing boots and make your way to the Troll Stronghold via either the main entrance or the secret entrance.\n  - From the main entrance, go south and then climb down the stairs into the Troll kitchen.\n  - If using the secret entrance, go to the ambush commander and climb the nearby wall, then head west.\n    - Once inside, go all the way north and climb up the stairs.\n    - Go south into the Troll kitchen.","Speak to Burntmeat."],"t":"The troll cook"},{"n":"Climbing boots, vodka, pineapple chunks, 10 wheat, 5 raw chickens, 2 logs, ranarr potion (unfinished)","r":"","s":["Walk out of the stronghold's main entrance and head east to the top of the mountain (Eadgar's cave). Located on top of the mountain with the thrower trolls, the world map marks this as Trollheim.","Enter the cave.","Talk to Eadgar. {Chat: 2 What do you have to offer? > 1 I'd like some mountain goat stew, please.}","Talk to Parroty Pete at the Ardougne Zoo. He is located at the northern end by the wolves. {Chat: 3 What do you feed them?}","Talk to him again. {Chat: 2 When did you add it?}","Use the pineapple chunks on the vodka to obtain alco-chunks.","Use the alco-chunks on the Aviary Hatch on the west side of the parrot cage for a drunk parrot.","Return to Eadgar. {Chat: 3 No thanks, Eadgar.}","Go back to the stronghold and climb down the northern Stone Staircase.","Unlock the Prison Door to the east and climb down the staircase.","Use the drunk parrot on the rack north of the prison cells.","Talk to Tegid in Taverley for a dirty robe. He is located south of Sanfew, washing laundry in the lake. {Chat: 2 Sanfew won't be happy...}","Talk to Eadgar with the wheat, raw chickens, logs and the dirty robe. {Chat: 3 No thanks, Eadgar.}"],"t":"Tricking the trolls"},{"n":"ranarr potion (unfinished)","r":"","s":["Exit the cave and find a grassy area and pick the thistle.","Use the troll thistle on a fire.\n  - If you didn't bring logs, there are two fires just west in the encampment.","Grind the dried thistle.","Use the ground thistle on ranarr potion (unfinished) to obtain a troll potion.","Talk to Eadgar to give him the potion.","Go back to the prison in Troll Stronghold.","Search the rack to retrieve the drunk parrot.","Talk to Eadgar {Chat: 3 No thanks, Eadgar.} to obtain a fake man.\n  - Speak to him again if you don't receive the fake man the first time."],"t":"Truth serum"},{"n":"Fake man","r":"","s":["Talk to Burntmeat back in the kitchen of the stronghold. {Chat: 2 I'll be going now.}","Open and right-click search the Kitchen Drawers along the south wall for the storeroom key.","Climb-down the stone staircase directly north of the kitchen drawers to enter the storeroom.","Open the Storeroom Door with the key.","Obtain goutweed:\n  - At the next door, wait until the guard patrolling the northernmost lane goes south.\n  - Open the door and run west, then surge directly south to search the Goutweed Crate.\n  - If done correctly, you will surge through the western most guards and be able to immediately obtain a goutweed.\n  - Alternatively, use safe spots (U-shaped areas with boxes on three sides) to pass the guards.\n  - Run to the first safe spot, the middle safe spot in the third row of boxes from the entrance, after the trolls patrolling the first row and the eastern second row just pass you.\n  - Wait for the troll which travels north on the western side to make the turn to the east, then run to the safe spot on the southern side of the third row.\n  - Wait until the troll guard approaching you from the south has turned the west, then run to the crate with the goutweed. Make sure that you are standing to the side of the crate or you will get caught.","Return to Taverley and talk to Sanfew with the goutweed.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Obtaining goutweed"}]},"Eagles' Peak":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Charlie in Ardougne Zoo. {Chat: 1 Ah, you sound like someone who needs a quest doing! > Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to Eagles' Peak west of the Tree Gnome Stronghold.\n  - If Eagles' Peak lodestone is activated, teleport to it and run northwest.\n  - Alternatively, teleport to the Memorial of Guthix using memory stands in the currency pouch and run southeast.","Go to the northern side of the mountain's base to a campsite.","Inspect the books for a Bird book.","Read the book to obtain a Metal feather.","Climb the rocks attached to the mountain next to the campsite (25 Agility needed).","Use the metal feather on the rocky outcrop.","Enter the cave, then head south until a cutscene with Nickolaus plays.","Shout-to Nickolaus. {Chat: 1 The Ardougne zookeeper sent me to find you. > 2 So it's not that you're trapped then? > 1 Could I help at all?}","Pick up 10 eagle feathers in the dungeon (called \"giant feathers\" on the floor)."],"t":"Eagles' Peak"},{"n":"10 eagle feathers, 1 Swamp tar, 1 Yellow dye","r":"","s":["Head to the south-east corner of Varrock to the Fancy Clothes Store.","Talk to the Fancy-Dress shop owner. {Chat: 2 Well, specifically I'm after a couple of bird costumes.}","Have the owner make you two eagle capes and two fake beaks. {Chat: 2 I've got the feathers and the materials you requested. > 1 Okay, here are the materials. Eagle me up.}","Equip your disguise (eagle cape and fake beak) and go back to the Eagle's Peak cave and shout to Nickolaus."],"t":"The disguise"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the intersection by the entrance of the dungeon and follow the east path.","Go through the tunnel entrance."],"t":"Golden feather"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Exit the tunnel (next to the birdseed holder)","Enter the middle tunnel to the west. (South of the entrance you originally used to enter the cave)","Inspect the stone pedestal and complete the trail by inspecting the first pile of rocks to the east, then north-east.","Inspect the opening in the wall to the north and kill the kebbit.","Take the silver feather dropped by the kebbit.","Exit this tunnel back into the main cave."],"t":"Silver feather"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the south-west corner of the main cave and enter through the entrance.","Try to grab the feather from the pedestal.","Operate each winch in the 4 corners of the room in any order.","Grab the bronze feather from the pedestal.","Leave the tunnel into the main cave."],"t":"Bronze feather"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Back in the main cave, head directly east to a stone door with an eagle carved in it.","Use each feather on the door.\n  - Use the golden feather on the door\n  - Use the silver feather on the door\n  - Use the bronze feather on the door","Open the stone door","While wearing the disguise, click the eagle to Walk-past the giant eagle directly north","Talk to Nickolaus."],"t":"The eagle door"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head back to the campsite by teleporting to Eagles' Peak lodestone and running northwest, or alternatively:\n  - Walk-past the eagle again\n  - Exit the main cave back to eagles peak\n  - Climb down the rocks","Talk to Nickolaus. {Chat: 1 Well I was originally sent to find you because of a ferret. > 1 That sounds good to me.}","Watch the cutscene.","Take the ferret back to Charlie in the Ardougne Zoo.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Eclipse of the Heart":{"sections":[{"n":"pet cat or kitten, monkeyspeak amulet or cramulet.","r":"Ring of duelling to teleport to Het's Oasis; desert amulet 2 or higher to teleport to Nardah, combat equipment, at least 4 free inventory spaces.","s":["Enter the Golden Palace in Menaphos. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Speak with Leela inside the pyramid. {Chat: Accept}","Speak with Leela outside the pyramid.","Cross the bridge to Sophanem and speak with Ozan. {Chat: 1 Yes. > ~}","Speak with the following citizens (if you need to leave the area to visit a bank, you will need to talk to Ozan again to proceed):\n  - The Sphinx (west of larger pyramid, cat is required but catspeak amulet is not required to proceed the quest)\n  - Jex (inside the north-east temple)\n  - Raetul (north-east of larger pyramid; by silk stall)\n  - Urbi (south of the larger pyramid)\n  - Nathifa, south of the Sophanem Slayer Dungeon (must speak to the other 4 before Nathifa dialogue progresses) {Chat: 3 What proposition? (Continue quest) > ~}","Speak to Ozan and prepare well for an intense battle which includes four waves of multiple heavy hitting enemies and stuns. Death is unsafe here.","Go to the Sophanem Slayer Dungeon and inspect the dungeon entrance.\n  - If this option does not appear, speak to Ozan again.","Kill the waves of soul devourers. You may need to speak to Het or Apmeken to continue receiving waves. If you die, you will have to restart all waves.","Talk to Het or Apmeken and finish the dialogue.","Return to Ozan and finish the dialogue.","Speak to Scabaras in the Temple of Isolation with at least 1 backpack space. {Chat: 3 (Continue quest)}\n  - The entrance to the temple is north of Pollnivneach in the Scabarite Cavern, where you can use the old boat.","Head to Het's Oasis and speak to Het (outside west entrance) to continue the quest and be transported to the agility course.\n  - There is a possible graphical bug. After talking to Het to continue the quest, your screen will remain black. Re-log and talk to Het again to fix.","Talk to Het to be tasked with doing the agility course.","Complete 1 lap of the agility course (from your current location) by climbing the rope ladder.","Start a new lap on the course until you get back to Crondis and Het.","Speak to Het by the rope ladder.","Gather 1 of each flower from the perfect flower bushes in each corner of Het's Oasis, do not teleport as you will need to speak with Het again. Each one will be marked with a light beam.\n  - Perfect iris bush (north-east)\n  - Perfect rose bush (north)\n  - Perfect hollyhock bush (south)\n  - Perfect hydrangea bush (south-east)","Speak to Crondis by the rope ladder.","Go to the monkey colony north-east of the Bandit Camp and talk to Apmeken with a monkeyspeak amulet or cramulet equipped.","Run slightly north (somewhere quieter) and talk to Apmeken again. {Chat: 3 We could go get a chimp ice? (Continue quest)}","Head to choc ice stall in Nardah and speak to Rokuh.\n  - You may teleport to Nardah using a desert amulet 2 or higher.\n  - Buying choc Ice without speaking to him will not progress the quest.\n  - If Apmeken is not following you, he will not give you the Ice. Return to the monkey colony and speak to Apmeken.","Head back to the monkey colony and continue quest (unlike other instances, players may teleport without the item melting, and ice spells are not required).","Kill Mizaru, Kikazaru and Iwazaru.\n  - Remember to kill the demons for Kikazaru; beware Iwazaru can unequip your helmet to the backpack.","Speak to Apmeken in the Monkey Colony to receive Apmeken's Favor.","Speak to Scabaras in the Temple of Isolation."],"t":"Gathering desert demigods"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Puzzle solution:\n  - Het northeast, then north\n  - Scabaras north, then northeast\n  - Elidinis west once\n  - Apmeken west once\n  - Scabaras southeast\n  - Elidinis northeast\n  - Apmeken west, then south\n  - Scabaras west twice\n  - Crondis north, then west\n  - Elidinis southeast, then south\n  - Het south, then southeast\n  - Scabaras northeast, then north\n  - Crondis west once\n  - Het northwest once\n  - Elidinis north, then west\n  - Het southeast, then south\n  - Scabaras south, then southeast","Talk to Memory of Tumeken.","Go through gate."],"t":"=Puzzle 1="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Move:\n  - Icthlarin north west\n  - Scabaras west\n  - Het north east, then north west\n  - Amascut north west, then north east\n  - Apmeken east\n  - Crondis south east\n  - Scabaras south west","Move:\n  - Het west\n  - Amascut north west\n  - Apmeken north east\n  - Crondis east then south east\n  - Apmeken south west\n  - Amascut south east\n  - Het east","Move:\n  - Icthlarin south east\n  - Apmeken west\n  - Amascut south west\n  - Het south east\n  - Icthlarin east\n  - Scabaras north east","Move:\n  - Apmeken north west\n  - Amascut west\n  - Het south west\n  - Icthlarin south east\n  - Scabaras east\n  - Apmeken north east, then north west","Move:\n  - Scabaras west, then south west\n  - Icthlarin north west, then west\n  - Het north east, then north west\n  - Amascut east, then north east\n  - Scabaras south east, then east\n  - Icthlarin south west, then south east\n  - Apmeken south east, then south west","Move:\n  - Het west\n  - Amascut north west\n  - Scabaras north east\n  - Icthlarin east\n  - Apmeken south east\n  - Het south west\n  - Amascut west then north west","Move:\n  - Het north east, then east\n  - Apmeken north west, then north east\n  - Icthlarin west, then north west\n  - Scabaras south west, then west\n  - Het south east\n  - Apmeken east","Talk to memory of Tumeken","Go through gate"],"t":"=Puzzle 2="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Move:\n  - Elidinis northwest\n  - Icthlarin west\n  - Crondis northeast\n  - Apmeken east\n  - Scabaras east\n  - Het southeast\n  - Amascut west","Move:\n  - Elidinis southwest\n  - Icthlarin northwest\n  - Crondis west\n  - Apmeken northeast\n  - Scabaras east\n  - Elidinis southeast\n  - Amascut east","Move:\n  - Het northwest\n  - Elidinis west\n  - Amascut southeast\n  - Icthlarin southwest\n  - Crondis northwest\n  - Apmeken west\n  - Scabaras northeast","Move:\n  - Amascut east\n  - Icthlarin southeast\n  - Het east\n  - Elidinis northwest\n  - Icthlarin west\n  - Het southeast\n  - Crondis southwest","Move:\n  - Apmeken northwest\n  - Het northeast\n  - Crondis southeast\n  - Apmeken southwest\n  - Het northwest\n  - Crondis northeast\n  - Icthlarin east","Move:\n  - Elidinis southeast\n  - Apmeken west\n  - Icthlarin northwest\n  - Crondis southwest\n  - Het southeast\n  - Icthlarin northeast\n  - Crondis northwest (this opens the other pillar space)","Move:\n  - Het southwest\n  - Icthlarin southeast\n  - Crondis northeast, then north\n  - Icthlarin northwest then southwest\n  - Het northeast, then northwest","Move:\n  - Elidinis east then northeast\n  - Icthlarin southeast then west\n  - Elidinis southwest\n  - Het southeast\n  - Crondis south, then southwest","Go through gate.","Open sarcophagus.","Talk to memory of Tumeken.","Talk to Scabaras (down the first set of stairs to the south) - Make sure to finish the dialogue, there's a brief animation.","Head to Menaphos and speak to Pharaoh Leela at the top of the stairs north-west of the Menaphos lodestone, not inside the throne room."],"t":"=Puzzle 3="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Pharaoh Leela twice.","Speak to Urluk and the council south west of Leela.","Speak to the four aspects (Het, Apmeken, Scabaras, and Crondis), then Commander Akhomet.\n  - If Crondis does not respond to your clicks, move to the south side of the pool edge, and try again.","Speak to Leela. {Chat: 1 I am. > 5 Akhomet's forces. > 1 Apmeken's forces. > 2 Het's forces > 2 Scarabas' forces}"],"t":"Preparing defences"},{"n":"18 regular ghostly ink, 31 greater ghostly ink, 20 powerful ghostly ink, 16 basic ritual candle","r":"Underworld Grimoire 2 or higher, extra 8 powerful and greater ghostly ink, and ectoplasm can be used during ensoul beacon for 4 Speed III glyphs","s":["Speak to Icthlarin. {Chat: 5 Continue Quest.}","Go to the Ungael ritual site.","Take beacon from the soul beacon north of the Archivist. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Place the soul beacon (corrupted) on the pedestal of the ritual site and draw the corresponding glyphs for the ensoul beacon ritual.","Perform ritual, closing shadow rifts as they appear.\n  - If you're unable to start the ritual, attempt to take the soul beacon again.","Interact with the soul beacon west of the ritual site.","Go to the Um Ritual Site and continue the quest via the portal. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk with Vorkath, then to Icthlarin.","Place the soul beacon on the pedestal and perform the powerful ritual of severance. Simply ignore the creatures that appear - Vorkath and Icthlarin will deal with them."],"t":"Performing rituals"},{"n":"","r":"Food and combat equipment","s":["Prepare for the encounter of Amascut, the Devourer.","When you're ready, return to the Um Ritual Site and speak to Icthlarin to continue.","Run through the city to the Great Pyramid and speak to any of the lesser gods for a cutscene.","Speak to Tumeken, click through all the chat options to continue. {Chat: 1 What are you? > 2 Why is everyone frozen? > 3 Why are you speaking to me? > 4 Continue.}","The fight then begins with Amascut. Attack the soul obelisks, she switches between magic, ranged, and melee attacks. During the last phase, you will be teleported onto a platform.","After the fight, go through the dialogue. {Chat: ~}","Speak to Icthlarin to leave the instance. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Finish the remaining dialogue. {Chat: ~}"],"t":"Confronting Amascut"}]},"Elemental Workshop I":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["In Seers' Village, go to the house immediately south of the anvil.","Search the bookcase on the eastern wall to find a battered book.","Read the book,{Chat: Accept} then right-click on the book and click \"Cut-open\" to get a battered key. Do not drop the book.","Go to the building with the anvil and click on the northern wall to open the odd-looking wall.","Go down the stairs."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go into the room to the north.","(Red Indicator) Turn the water controls east of the water wheel to turn it green","(Red Indicator) Turn the water controls west of the water wheel to turn it green.","Pull the lever by the water wheel.","(Optional) To obtain leather, search the crate north of the staircase in the middle room.","Go to the eastern room.","With thread and leather, fix the bellows.","Pull the lever by the bellows.","Go to the western room and mine an elemental rock.","Kill the earth elemental and pick up the elemental ore it drops.","Go back to the middle room and search the small boxes in the north-east part of the room to obtain a stone bowl."],"t":"Repairing a workshop"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the south room.","Use the stone bowl on the lava trough to the south.","Use the bowl of lava on the furnace in the room.","Use the elemental ore and four coal on the furnace.","With the slashed book, go to the middle room and smith an elemental shield on an anvil workbench.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Elemental Workshop II":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the Exam Centre in the south of the Archaeology Campus and search the bookshelf on the eastern wall in the Exam Centre. {Chat: Accept}\n  - Use Archaeology journal to teleport to the Archaeology Campus just north of the Exam Centre.\n  - If you end up with Varmen's notes, you searched the wrong bookshelf.","Read the scroll inside the beaten book and keep the book."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the building with an anvil west of the Seers' Village bank.","Click on the odd-looking wall to enter it.\n  - If it says \"You see a small hole in the wall but no way to open it\", go to the building directly south and search the bookcase on the east wall for a battered key.","Go down the stairs.","Go north to the water elemental room and search the machinery in the southwest of the room to get a key."],"t":"The second key"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Obtain 2 elemental ores from the west room by attempting to mine the elemental rocks, and defeating the earth elementals that spawn.","Go back to the north room (where you got the key) and pull the lever to start the water wheel (if the wheel is already turning, this step can be skipped).","Go to the east room and pull the lever to start the bellows (if the bellows are already working, this step can be skipped).","Smelt two elemental bars in the south room. ('Use' the ore on the furnace.)","Open the hatch in the middle room, and climb down it."],"t":"Elemental bars"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take from the schematic crate south of the stairs and take both options.","Go back up the spiral stairs and smith a crane claw on the workbench using an elemental bar.","Go back down and lower the Old crane using the lever directly next to the schematic crate.","Use the claw on the crane to repair it.","Place an elemental bar on the jig cart.","Pull the west lever by the schematic crate.","Pull the east lever.","Pull the west lever twice.","Pull the east lever.","Pull the west lever twice.","Pull the lever behind you, by the mine cart sign.\n  - If the lever is pulled and it says the system is not pressurised, go upstairs and activate the water wheel and bellows."],"t":"The claw"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb the staircase in the south-west corner.","Move to the west side by the steam press.","Open the junction box and connect the pipes by clicking on a pair of pipe holes. Refer to the solution on the right.\n  - Top left and bottom right.\n  - Top middle and top right.\n  - Bottom left and bottom middle.","Go downstairs and pull the lever next to the three small pipes.\n  - If successful, you will get a message that the bar has been flattened.","Pull the lever by the mine cart sign."],"t":"The press"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Search all of the crates in both the area with the track and the upper level with the junction box to find 3 cogs and a pipe.","Go back up the northeast platform stairs.","Go north of the water tank and 'use' the pipe item on the piping with a hole in it.","Go back down to the water tank and pull the 'old lever' in front of the tank's door to open it.","Turn the corkscrew lever (to the east) twice to load the elemental sheet into the water tank.","Pull the old lever to close the door.","Turn the water valve west of the old lever to open the valve.","Turn the water valve east of the old lever to raise the water level.","Wait for the water to fill the tank, then turn the east valve again, to lower the water level back down.","Turn the water valve west of the old lever to close off the water valve.","Pull the old lever to open the door.","Turn the corkscrew twice.","Pull the old lever to close the door.","Pull the lever by the mine cart sign."],"t":"The water tank"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go over to the machine on the east side.","On the side of the machine are three pins, place the cogs on the correct pins.\n  - The small cog goes on the upper left pin, the medium cog on the lower left pin, and the large cog on the right pin.","Pull the lever just to the south to start the fan.\n  - If the message says the fan is sucking, the cogs are not on the correct pins. Turn the fan off and position the cogs correctly.\n  - If the machine says \"It must be powered somewhere else\", head upstairs and make sure the water wheel to the north is rotating. If not, pull the lever near the wheel.","Pull the lever again.","Pull the lever by the mine cart sign.","Go by the claw and pick up the primed bar."],"t":"The fan"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go down another level in the workshop (north west stairwell).","Enter the east door (mind door).","Place the bar on the extractor gun. If you miss this step, you will take 10% damage by doing the next step.","Operate the extractor hat.","Take the bar from the extractor gun.","Go back up to the top floor of the workshop.","On the workbench, smith a mind helmet, with the beaten book in the backpack. (If you have another Elemental bar in your inventory you may have to drop it)","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Elemental Workshop III":{"sections":[{"n":"12 coal, 1 soft clay}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["Search the north-east bookcase in the Seers' Village church. {Chat: Accept}","Read the ragged book.","Use soft clay on the book to get the key mould. If you do not have soft clay, you can mine some from the clay rocks in the western mine of the workshop then use it on the sink in the northern room.","Enter the Elemental Workshop and go into the mine to the west. Mine 3 elemental rocks, killing the earth elementals that appear, then pick up the 3 elemental ores that they drop. Simply killing the earth elementals wandering around the mine will not yield the ore.","In the fire elemental room (south), use the elemental ore on the furnace to create 3 elemental bars. 4 coal is required per bar.","Use 1 elemental bar on the furnace again to make a ragged elemental key.","Climb down the hatch in the centre of the middle room.","Prime the remaining two elemental bars (see primed bar on how to do this) using the jig cart, but don't infuse them with the Mind machine.","Go down the northwest stairwell.","In the middle of the hallway, open the 'Body door' on the western wall with the ragged elemental key."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head down the stairs.","Label the levers as follows and use the interface to move them. The levers on the north and south are the same, and the levers east and west are the same so feel free to use the closest lever to your current orientation. You can use the Minigame window to hit the levers, you don't need to run to each one.","The \"Reset\" and \"Undo\" levers can be found on the west wall (when the camera is not locked into the fixed overhead view; otherwise, they're to the north)"],"t":"The puzzle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pull the levers in the following order:\n  - C, 2, F, 6\n  - C, 2, F, 6\n  - C, 2, E, 5\n  - B, 3, F, 2\n  - B, 3, F, 2\n  - E, 4, F, 3","A cutscene will play. Pull the reset lever."],"t":"First section"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pull the levers in the following order:\n  - A, 5, C, 6\n  - B, 5, D, 6\n  - C, 5, E, 6\n  - C, 5, F, 6\n  - D, 5, E, 3\n  - F, 4, E","No cutscene will play. Pull the reset lever."],"t":"Second section"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pull the levers in the following order:\n  - 2, B, 6, A\n  - 5, B, 6, C\n  - 5, B, 2, C\n  - 5, B, 3, E\n  - 6, F, 5, B\n  - 3, C, 6, F\n  - 2, C, 6, E\n  - 3, B, 5, E\n  - 6, F, 4, E\n  - 6, F, 4, E\n  - 5","A cutscene will play. Pull the reset lever."],"t":"Third section"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pull the levers in the following order:\n  - 2, C, 3, B\n  - 2, A, 3, E\n  - 2, B, 3, F\n  - 2, C, 3, F\n  - 2, C, 5, F\n  - 2, E","A message appears: \"you hear a crunching of gears\". Pull the reset lever."],"t":"Fourth section"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pull the levers in the following order:\n  - B, 2, A, 3\n  - B, 2, F, 6\n  - B, 2, D, 3\n  - F, 6, C, 5\n  - D, 6, F, 5\n  - C, 6, F, 2\n  - E, 5, F, 2\n  - E, 5, D, 6\n  - F, 4, E, 6","Many of the gears start moving and the machine makes a noise.","Pull the reset lever."],"t":"Lowering the tower"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pull the levers in the following order:\n  - 4, E, 6, F\n  - 4, E, 6, A\n  - 5, B, 6, E\n  - 5, A, 6, F\n  - 5, B, 2, A\n  - 3, B, 4, C\n  - 2, B, 6, E\n  - 5, C, 2, D\n  - 3, E, 5, C\n  - 3, F, 6","Many of the gears start rotating and the central column stats rotating.","Do not pull the reset lever."],"t":"Spinning the tower"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["If your puzzle looks exactly like Figure 1, pull the levers in the following order:\n  - B, 4, C, 3","If your puzzle looks like that image, but with the left and right sides reversed (\"inverse position\"), pull the levers in the following order:\n  - B, 4, C, 5","A message appears: \"As the machine raises, you hear a whirring noise from the level above\". Do not pull the reset lever."],"t":"Raising the tower"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go upstairs (click the metallic stairs on the bottom-left or bottom-right of the screen), and make a body bar.","The metallic stairs may be blocked by your interface due to the camera angle, so closing out or resizing your interface may be needed.\n  - Put a primed bar in the slot next to the door.\n  - Enter the room and flip the lever.\n  - Push the button.\n  - Flip the lever.\n  - Retrieve the body bar from the slot.","Go downstairs.","If your puzzle was in the \"guide position\" mentioned above, pull the levers in the following order:\n  - 2 (The tower drops)\n  - 4, B (The tower spins)\n  - C, 3 (The tower rises)","Or if your puzzle was in the \"inverse position\", pull the levers in the following order:\n  - 4, 3 (The tower drops)\n  - 4, B (The tower spins)\n  - C, 3 (The tower rises)","Go upstairs and make a second body bar.\n  - Put a primed bar in the slot next to the door.\n  - Enter the room and flip the lever.\n  - Push the button.\n  - Flip the lever.\n  - Retrieve the body bar from the slot.","Use a workbench on the first-level basement (the level with water, air, and fire elementals where you can obtain elemental ore) to create a body body. The ragged book must be in your inventory.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Body body"}]},"Elemental Workshop IV":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Read the book completely. (8 pages).","Pick up the knife on the ground next to you in the Sorcerer's Tower then head to the anvil near the bank in Seers' Village.","Use a knife on the whetstone in the building of the Elemental Workshop, west of the bank, to receive a keyblade.","Head down into the workshop.","Make 2 primed bars in the same way you did in the previous Elemental Workshop quests.\n  - Optional: Make 5 more if you want a full set."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the basement.","Use the keyblade on the southern door.","Head through the door and east to the pillar room via the Cosmic door. (dismiss any followers)","Solve the first puzzle (solution pictured right).\n  - Place the runes into the correct emitter locations\n  - Operate the control panel south-east\n  - Rotate the pillars using the controls interface (bottom right)\n    - Pressing the circle on the control interface grid rotates the pillar. They have to match with the picture shown here\n  - Press \"Power Up\"","Solve the second and third puzzles.\n  - Adjust the height of the emitters using the same Control Panel","Operate the draining machine in the south-east corner of the room.","After the cutscene, use a primed bar on the Machine directly south of the control panel.","Correct the pillar that has changed position.","Power up the control panel again.","Operate the draining machine.\n  - Note: you might need to drink a dose of restoration potion (operating this machine drains your Runecrafting level)","Take the cosmic bar.","Head upstairs to the workbench to make cosmic gloves. You can log out and log back in to quickly be placed back in the first room of the Elemental Workshop."],"t":"The cosmic room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head back downstairs into the newly-opened chaos room.","Take the Shabby book from the table in the north-west corner. Read it and keep it in your inventory during the quest.","Operate the CPU (using the 6 levers) and input the following commands in order:\n  - Make the automaton move cubes from shelves/belt by moving the cubes on the conveyor belt into the CPU (instruction cubes on belt are labelled get/put/break)\n  - The first command will need to be aligned with the left side of the belt. Once in place, push the cube down the belt using the lever to \"input\" the first command\n  - The second command will need to be aligned with the right side of the belt. Once in place, push the cube down the belt using the lever to \"input\" the second command\n    - Get + Nature (grabs cube from shelf)\n    - Put + Mind (this puts whatever he is holding onto the machine)\n  - Put the cube with the fire rune on it onto the conveyor belt.\n    - Get + Cosmic\n    - Put + Mind\n  - Put a blank token on the workbench.\n    - Break + Law\n    - Get + Fire\n    - Put + Water\n  - Carve the token.\n  - Take the new astral token and use it on the broken astral token to replace it.\n  - Put the cube with the astral rune on it onto the conveyor belt.\n    - Get + Body\n    - Put + Mind\n  - Put the cube with the earth rune on it onto the conveyor belt.\n    - Get + Astral\n    - Put + Mind\n  - This instructs Da-Vi to break the second wall, then turn the chaos machine on.\n    - Break + Earth\n    - Operate + Chaos","Equip your cosmic gloves.","Use a primed bar on the machine, in the room with the Automaton.","Operate the draining machine (drains Thieving level).\n  - Requires level 39 Thieving. Use Super restore if needed.\n  - If it says \"machine unpowered\" input \"Operate+Chaos\" again then try again.","Take the chaos bar.\n  - Optional: repeat the last 3 steps for each primed bar if you want to make more chaos pieces.","Head upstairs to a workbench to make chaos boots. Lobbying will automatically put you right next to the anvil.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The chaos room"}]},"Enakhra's Lament":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the granite and sandstone quarry southwest of the Bandit Camp lodestone.","Talk to Lazim. {Chat: Accept > 2 Okay, I'll get on with it.}","If you don't already have your sandstones, mine 5 of sandstone in the nearby quarry.","Give Lazim 32 of sandstone. {Chat: 1 Yes, I have more stone. > 1 Here's a medium 5 kg block. > 1 Yes, I have more stone. > 1 Here's a medium 5 kg block. > 1 Yes, I have more stone. > 1 Here's a medium 5 kg block. > 1 Yes, I have more stone. > 1 Here's a medium 5 kg block. > 1 Yes, I have more stone. > 1 Here's a medium 5 kg block. > 1 Yes, I have more stone. > 1 Here's a medium 5 kg block. > 1 Yes, I have more stone. > 1 Here's a small 2 kg block.}","Craft the sandstone (32kg) he gives you, use it on the flat ground.","Talk to Lazim. {Chat: 2 I'll do it right away!}","Give Lazim another 20 kg of sandstone. {Chat: 1 Yes, I have more stone. > 1 Here's a medium 5 kg block. > 1 Yes, I have more stone. > 1 Here's a medium 5 kg block. > 1 Yes, I have more stone. > 1 Here's a medium 5 kg block. > 1 Yes, I have more stone. > 1 Here's a medium 5 kg block.}","Craft the sandstone (20kg) he gives you, use it on the statue base.","Chisel the headless statue, speak to Lazim. {Chat: 4 I think it should have a camel's head.}","Mine or obtain two 5 granite chunks.","Craft a 5 chunk of granite. {Chat: 1 Carve a head for the statue. > 4 The head of a camel}","Use the stone camel head on the headless statue."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Lazim.","Talk to him again. {Chat: 2 Do you know where the statue's head is?}","Interact with the fallen statue four times, use the \"Chisel\" option. {Chat: 1 Chisel > 1 Remove the statue's left arm} {Chat: 1 Chisel > 1 Remove the statue's right arm} {Chat: 1 Chisel > 1 Remove the statue's left leg} {Chat: 1 Chisel}","Take-sigil from the nearby pedestal for the letter \"M\".","Go north and through the door. Click to skip the cutscene.","Go all the way west and through the door to the south. Click to skip the cutscene.","Go south and take the path to east which is leading to the middle room. Unlock the door using the M sigil.","Optionally, leave the middle room and go through the remaining two outer doors, gather the remaining three sigils, and unlock the remaining three doors that lead to the middle room. The outer doors will become permanently locked post-quest if the stone limbs are destroyed as they cannot be reclaimed.","Climb up the middle room's ladder."],"t":"Underground"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use your soft clay on the pedestal for a camel mould (p).","Craft your second chunk of granite 5. {Chat: 1 Carve a shape to fit the pedestal.}","Use the new head on the pedestal, a cutscene starts (which can be skipped).","Talk to Lazim.","Use either bread, cake, pie, potato, or a pizza on Pentyn in the north-western room. {Chat: 4 It's okay, I don't need any help.}","Go to the west room, equip your staff or wand, melt the fountain.\n  - If you have a waterskin, you can refill it at the fountain for a Hard Desert Achievement, Enaqua.","Go to the northeast room, clear the furnace with a staff or wand equipped.\n  - Retrieve coal from the metal bank if it is not already in the backpack.","Go to the east room, investigate each brazier, using the respective resource on each of them.\n  - Retrieve coal from the metal bank at the furnace in the northeast room if you did not bring it.","Pass-through the magical barrier in the centre, climb-up the ladder."],"t":"Enakhra's temple"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Lazim.","Climb-over pile of bones south.","Climb-down the stone ladder.","Talk to the Boneguard. {Chat: 2 Of course, I'll help you out. > 4 Okay, I'll start building.}","Take-rock from the nearby rubble for a chunk of sandstone. Do this three times.","Inspect the wall to add the sandstone then inspect it again to chisel it. Repeat this twice more.","Talk to the Boneguard for the final cutscene (this can also be skipped).","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing off"}]},"Enlightened Journey":{"sections":[{"n":"3 papyrus, 1 ball of wool, 1 sack of potatoes, and 1 white candle","r":"","s":["If you don't have a sack of potatoes yet, fill an empty sack with potatoes in the farm north-east of Auguste. Pick the 6 that are there, wait for more to respawn, then pick 4 more. Click fill on the sack.","Talk to Auguste on Entrana, north of the Herblore shop. {Chat: Accept}","Talk to him again. {Chat: 1 Umm, yes. What's your point?}","Talk to him for a third time. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Use a papyrus with a ball of wool.","Use an unlit candle on the balloon structure.","Talk to Auguste to launch the origami balloon. (Do not use the balloon's Launch option or you will need to make another.)","Talk to Auguste again with two papyrus and a sack of potatoes. {Chat: 1 Yes, I have them here.}","Speak with Auguste once more and he will give you Auguste's sapling and basket of Apples."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"12 willow branches","r":"","s":["Fill 8 sacks with sand at the sandpit just south-east of Auguste","Give Auguste the items listed above. {Chat: 1 Yes, I want to give you some items. > 1 Dye. > 1 Sandbags. > 1 Silk. > 1 Bowl. > 2 Fine thanks.}","Bank for the willow branches. Go back and use the branches on the balloon frame on the platform.","Obtain at least 10 normal logs from nearby trees."],"t":"The Big Balloon"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Auguste to begin the flight. {Chat: 2 Okay.}\n  - You must take all items from your BoB and dismiss it at this point to begin the flight.","In the event the client doesn't load the interface properly, you will need to restart, requiring another 10 logs."],"t":"In Flight"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Auguste.\n  - Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing Up"}]},"Enter the Abyss (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["If you have PVP enabled bank all your equipment, gear and items so that you don't lose anything to player killers.","North of Edgeville jump the Wilderness wall and run north to the tip of the river Lum and speak to the Mage of Zamorak without wearing Saradomin or Guthix equipment. {Chat: Accept}","Go to the Temple of Zamorak in southeast of Varrock.","Without wearing Saradomin or Guthix equipment, speak to the Mage of Zamorak.{Chat: 2 Where do you get your runes from? > 1 Yes}","Continue the dialogue where the mage explains how to use the scrying orb."],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"2 backpack space","r":"","s":["With the scrying orb in the backpack go to Aubury's Rune Shop in southeast of Varrock.","Choose the \"teleport\" option on Aubury.","Head to the Wizard's Tower south of Draynor and go to the floor 3.","Choose the \"teleport\" option on Archmage Sedridor in the south.","Head to Wizard Cromperty who is located in the blue-tiled house in northeast of Ardougne.","Choose the \"teleport\" option on Wizard Cromperty.","Go to the Temple of Zamorak in southeast of Varrock.","Without wearing Saradomin or Guthix equipment, talk to the Mage of Zamorak twice. The step requires 2 backpack space.","Miniquest complete!","After the completion of the miniquest, speak to the Mage of Zamorak a third time to unlock the Abyss."],"t":"Getting the readings"}]},"Ernest the Chicken":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Veronica located just inside the gate to Draynor Manor. {Chat: Accept}","Enter the manor. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["On the floor 2, grab the fish food in the room south of the staircase.","On the floor 1, take the poison from the room south of the kitchen, in the northwest of the manor.","Use the poison on the fish food.","Exit the manor through the eastern-most room (or teleport to the Draynor lodestone) and walk to the fountain in the southwest corner of the yard.","Use the poisoned fish food on the fountain.","Search the fountain for the pressure gauge."],"t":"Pressure gauge"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Walk along the west side of the manor until a compost heap is found.","Search it for a grimy key.","Go inside the manor and enter the small room behind the staircase.","Take the rubber tube."],"t":"Rubber tube"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to the entrance hall of the manor and go into the room to the west.","Search the candle sconce on the western wall to open the wall.","Climb down the trap door ladder to the north in the new room.","There will be a puzzle with the solution as follows."],"t":"Oil can"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pull levers A, B up","Enter Door 1","Pull lever D up","Enter Door 1","Pull levers A, B down","Enter Doors 3, 4 & 5","Pull levers E, F up","Enter Doors 6 & 7","Pull lever C up","Enter Doors 7 & 6","Pull lever E down","Enter Doors 6, 8 & 3","Go through Door 9 and obtain the oil can."],"t":"Puzzle solution"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Leave the basement.","Pull the lever on the eastern wall.","Go up the stairs, then up the ladder, and talk to to Professor Oddenstein. {Chat: 1. I'm looking for a guy called Ernest. > 2. Change him back this instant!}","Talk to him again.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Evil Dave's Big Day Out":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the Basement of Doom, located under a house west of Edgeville bank.","Talk to Evil Dave. {Chat: 1 Evil Dave's big day out. > 1 I was looking for a quest. > Accept}","After the cutscene, admire the mirror to the west.","Go upstairs and talk to Doris."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Do your chores.\n  - Search the wardrobe for a broom and bed bug cleaner.\n  - Sweep the rug.\n  - Search the shelf for a bar of soap.\n  - Wash the dishes in the sink.\n  - Choose the take knife option on the sink.\n  - Chop the vegetables.\n  - Go downstairs and clean your bed.","After the cutscene go back upstairs and talk to Doris.","Go back downstairs and search the bookcase by the stairs. {Chat: 2 No, I need to find the spellbook.}","Search behind the boiler in the southeast corner.","Search the drapes by the bed.","Investigate Dave's spellbook.","Investigate it again to teleport to the Makeover Mage. (If you interact with Dave's spellbook again and get the message \"I don't need to use the spellbook right now\", interact with the drapes once more and the option to teleport to Makeover Mage will appear.) {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Chores of doom"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to one of the bankers and withdraw the law rune, stew, and old rug from Dave's bank.","Talk to one of the Grand Exchange clerks. {Chat: 3 Air runes.}","Drink the stew and refill the flask from any of the water fountains around the Grand Exchange.","Go to one of the Exchange clerks (Clark or Kent) to exchange the water flask for an air rune."],"t":"Making a withdrawal"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to the makeover mage and ask to turn into a girl. {Chat: Any}.","After you teleport back, talk to Doris. {Chat: Any > Any > Any}","Attempt to redo the following chores.\n  - Sweep the rug.\n  - Wash the dishes.\n  - Chop the vegetables.","Open the door and go north to the general store and speak to the shopkeeper. {Chat: 1 Go to the shops}","Return to the house and redo all the chores again.\n  - Sweep the rug.\n  - Wash the dishes.\n  - Chop the vegetables.\n  - Go downstairs and clean your bed.","After the cutscene, go upstairs and talk to Doris","Open the door. {Chat: 2 Carry on with the Quest. > 1 I'm ready to sneak in.}"],"t":"Double trouble"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Search the suit of armour to the west for a knight's helmet.","Search the crates in the west for some gunpowder.","Use the gunpowder on the helmet.","Use the hand-written note on the helmet.","Use the helmet with fuse on the torch on the wall.","Get close to the guard and throw the lit decoy bomb.","Sneak past the guards and enter the door to the tower where you will meet a drunken Sir Amik (the easiest way is to go past them once the third guard turns east).","Talk to Sir Amik to determine you need to give him more to drink.","Click the barrel to open the drinks menu and wait for the on screen prompt to show which drink you need. Take the drink and talk to Amik, as soon as the drink is removed from your inventory go back to the barrel and wait for the next on screen prompt. Repeat 5 times until Amik starts a new dialogue. (If you have trouble completing this part, take a drink, drop it, take one again and before the time runs out use loot area to grab them; you will be able to stack the drinks hence having more chance to complete this part.)","Talk to Doris. {Chat: Any > Any}"],"t":"Sneaking in"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Redo your chores again.\n  - Sweep the rug.\n  - Wash the dishes in the sink.\n  - Chop the vegetables.\n  - Go downstairs and clean your bed."],"t":"Busted again"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Felicity or Margaret the hell-rats.\n  - If they appear as normal hell-rats: go up the stairs for a dialogue and go back down.","Recruit any 3 of the other hell-rats.","Climb up the stairs to get to Shantay Pass.","Talk to Shantay.","Shake the coconut tree and pick up the coconut that falls out.","Use the coconut on Shantay.","Click the empty shell to add a hell-rat to it.","Climb up the rope on the northeastern wall and throw the Shell-rat.","Climb back down and try to open the Jail door. You will then hand the Coconut drink to the Shady man inside.","Once inside, talk to him to receive a jewel.","Search the barrel inside of the jail cell to take one.","Talk to the border guards to exchange the jewel for a rope.","Use the rope on the coconut tree.","Click the barrel in your inventory to load the last hell-rat into it.","Use the old rug (you got from the bank earlier) on the barrel.","Roll the barrel past the Shantay pass.","Talk to Shantay.","Search the hole that has a slight twinkle to it.","As a hell-rat, enter the sparkling holes. You can also hover your mouse over the holes until you spot the hole with a little rat icon next to it. You will have to repeat this 4 times.","Attempt to enter the mysterious entrance as a hell-rat.","Enter the mysterious entrance.","Grab Dave from the empty cooking range south-east.","Select the Clean Bed option.","Gather 5 hell-rats. If cutscene does not begin, gather the sixth hell-rat."],"t":"Infiltrating"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Doris.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Extinction":{"sections":[{"n":"Combat equipment","r":"Super restores or runes for Crystal Mask, food","s":["Talk to Moia or Hebe outside of Senntisten, north of the Archaeology Guild. {Chat: Accept}","Enter Senntisten via the ancient door. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Kill 12 TzekHaar monsters.","Enter the cathedral door to the south.","Talk to Moia. {Chat: ~ > 3 Continue...}"],"t":"Defending Senntisten"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head out of the cathedral to the east and continue east to the Croesus Front.","Remove each fungus from the skilling node; Croesus will use mechanics from the boss fight in the following order: Yellow Smoke, Stun, Green Smoke, Blue Smoke, Slime, Red Smoke.\n  - You may want to bring either super restore potions or the runes for Crystal Mask.\n    - If your stats get too low, Gorvek will save you by teleporting you back to the cathedral. Your fungus removal progress will be saved.\n  - Fishing\n  - Woodcutting\n  - Mining\n  - Hunter","Return to the cathedral and talk to Saradomin. You can't teleport back, but you can lobby and re-enter Senntisten."],"t":"Croesus Front"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head out of the cathedral to the south. Pass through the barrier and talk to Azzanadra. This is an unsafe death.","Light the braziers following the combinations below, after lighting, enter the portal and kill the generating glacors. You can ignore the glacytes.\n  - Food is advised as whilst lighting the braziers the Arch-Glacor will use similar mechanics from the boss fight.\n  - Light only the east brazier, then enter portal to kill the glacor.\n  - Extinguish the east brazier and light only the middle brazier, then enter portal to kill the glacor.\n  - Extinguish the middle brazier and light only the west brazier, then enter portal to kill the glacor.\n  - Lastly, light both the west and middle braziers, then enter portal and kill the glacor.","Return to the Cathedral and talk to Saradomin. You can lobby to get there faster."],"t":"Glacor Front"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head out of the Cathedral to the west and command the abandoned siege engine.\n  - Click attack on each of the siege engines to destroy them, and for the two at the back, click on the floor nearby.\n  - Repeat this a few times until you enter another dialogue with Kerapac.\n  - After the dialogue, kill the remaining siege engines.","Return to the Cathedral and talk to Seren."],"t":"Nodon Front"},{"n":"The Measure and Communication device (Extinction)","r":"Sixth-Age circuit","s":["Talk to Moia. {Chat: 4 Continue...}","Retrieve the Measure.\n  - If the quest Fate of the Gods is not done or if The Measure is lost, upon finishing dialogue with Vicendithas (see below), visit Mr Mordaut east of the Anachronia lodestone to reclaim it, the quest does not need to be completed. If option does not exist, talk to Vicendithas and try again. {Chat: 3 Extinction (Quest)}\n  - Alternatively, teleport to the World Gate and travel to the Elder Halls where it can be picked up from the north of where you teleport in.","Teleport to the Anachronia lodestone, and head north to the Effigy Incubator laboratory.","Enter the door under the Dragonkin statue. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Do the following once inside the Effigy Incubator area:\n  - Talk to Vicendithas.\n  - Talk to Vicendithas again to give him the Measure.\n  - Talk to Hannibus.\n  - Talk to Vicendithas.\n  - Talk to Hannibus again.\n  - Talk to Vicendithas again.\n  - Wait a moment and talk to Vicendithas again.\n  - Activate the communication device and talk to Moia. {Chat: 2 Continue.}\n  - Talk to Vicendithas. {Chat: 2 Continue.}"],"t":"Searching for Seren"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the World Gate and talk to Moia (or one of the other NPCs). {Chat: 4 Tarddiad}\n  - Closest teleport is Sixth-Age circuit or Eagles' Peak lodestone.","Enter the World Gate to Tarddiad and do the following once inside:\n  - Talk to Hannibus (or one of the other NPCs).","Investigate the three resonating crystals:\n  - First crystal: to the south-east, next to Vicendithas.\n  - Second crystal: just north-east of the first, next to Adrasteia and Moia.\n  - Third crystal: in the Stone Gazebo, west of the previous crystal.","Talk to Vicendithas (or one of the other NPCs) to the north over the bridge.","Talk to Moia (or one of the other NPCs) and then enter the World Gate to Naragun and do the following:\n  - Talk to Hannibus (or one of the other NPCs) just inside the World Gate.\n  - Continue up the path and talk to Adrasteia or Hannibus.\n  - Continue along the path and talk to Vicendithas or Moia.\n  - Continue to the end of the path and talk to Adrasteia (or one of the other NPCs).","Exit Naragun using the World Gate.\n  - Talk to Moia (or one of the other NPCs).","Enter the World Gate to Kethsi and do the following:\n  - Continue the dialogue with Kerapac. {Chat: Any > Any > Any}","Enter the World Gate again to Freneskae and do the following:\n  - Talk to Adrasteia (or one of the other NPCs). {Chat: 1 Yes}\n  - Descend ledge to the north. {Chat: 1 Extinction}\n  - Talk to Hannibus (or one of the other NPCs).\n  - Exit rock face to the west. {Chat: 1 Continue Extinction.}"],"t":"Hopping worlds"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Approach the dark portal.","Descend the ledge to the north again. {Chat: 1 Extinction}","Talk to Hannibus (or one of the other NPCs).","Exit rock face again. {Chat: 1 Continue Extinction.}","Talk to Moia (or one of the other NPCs) {Chat: 4 Continue...} and a cutscene will play."],"t":"Final stop"},{"n":"At least 6 free inventory spaces","r":"","s":["While inside Erebus your time and movement speed will be limited.","You must obtain 100% Erebus Rift Attunement by mining shadow animica rocks and capturing regular and skittish motes of shadow anima. There are 25 of these objects to find.","Obtaining 100% attunement takes multiple trips into Erebus.","You can initially explore Erebus for 1 minute before you are pulled out of the area.","When you are pulled out of the area you will keep the level of Erebus Rift Attunement and any item that you gained, but some aspects of the environment reset to their initial state.","As your attunement grows, you will gain the following benefits:\n  - At 20% attunement your movement speed is increased slightly.\n  - At 40% attunement you can stay in Erebus for an additional 15 seconds at a time (a minute and 15 seconds without the handicap).\n  - At 60% attunement you can run in a normal way.\n  - At 80% attunement you can stay in Erebus for an additional 30 seconds at a time (a minute and 30 seconds without the handicap).","After twenty attempts (entering and leaving) your available time can increase by one second for each time that you enter Erebus. Talk to Kerapac to toggle this."],"t":"Erebus"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["When you are ready to start, approach dark portal. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Mine the two shadow animica rocks and crush the resulting shadow animica for a total of 8% attunement. (8% total attunement.)","Capture the two motes of shadow anima for 8% attunement. (16% total attunement.)","Enter the rift in the east.","Capture the skittish mote of shadow anima for 4% attunement. (20% total attunement; you now move slightly faster.)","Capture the telekinetic soul remnant.","Return back to the initial area.","Levitate the boulder using the enduring soul remnant.","Move the boulder out of the way to open the way north.","Mine the shadow animica rock and crush the resulting shadow animica for 4% attunement. (24% total attunement.)","Capture the abyssal soul remnant.","Use the abyssal soul remnant to enter the rift in the south.","Capture the regular and skittish motes of shadow anima for 8% attunement. (32% total attunement.)","Leave via the extra action button or wait for the time to expire"],"t":"First visit"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Re-enter Erebus and re-obtain the abyssal soul remnant. The following must be done without exiting, so you may wish to re-enter again after obtaining the remnant to guarantee you have enough time.","Capture the telekinetic soul remnant.","Use the abyssal soul remnant to enter the rift in the west.","Capture the regular and skittish motes of shadow anima for 8% attunement. (40% total attunement; you may now stay for a minute and 15 seconds at a time without the handicap.)","Levitate the boulder using the enduring soul remnant.","Move the boulder out of the way to open the way east.","Mine the shadow animica rock and crush the resulting shadow animica for 4% attunement. (44% total attunement.)","Capture the two regular and one skittish mote of shadow anima for 12% attunement. (56% total attunement.)","Leave via the extra action button or wait for the time to expire"],"t":"Second visit"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Re-enter Erebus and re-obtain the abyssal and enduring soul remnants. The following must be done without exiting, so you may wish to re-enter again after obtaining the remnants to guarantee you have enough time.","Use the abyssal soul remnant to enter the rift in the west.","Levitate the boulder using the enduring soul remnant.","Move the boulder on one of the three circles on the timeworn lodestone in the east.","Return to the initial area and capture another telekinetic soul remnant.","Return to the area with the three circles and levitate the boulder (which has an abyssal soul remnant underneath) using the enduring soul remnant.","Move the boulder to another of the circles of the timeworn lodestone.","Capture the revealed abyssal soul remnant.","Use the abyssal soul remnant to enter the rift in the east.","Capture the mote of shadow anima for 4% attunement. (60% total attunement; you may now run.)","Capture the telekinetic soul remnant.","Return to the previous area.","Levitate the remaining boulder using the enduring soul remnant.","Move the boulder to the last circle on the timeworn lodestone.","Go on top of the timeworn lodestone. You will be teleported to an island and find the relic of the titans. Carrying this causes the western rift in the initial area to be active when entering Erebus, and automatically moves the three boulders on timeworn lodestone when entering any rifts.","Mine the shadow animica rock and crush the resulting shadow animica for 4% attunement. (64% total attunement.)","Capture the mote of shadow anima for 4% attunement. (68% total attunement.)","Leave via the extra action button or wait for the time to expire"],"t":"Third visit"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Re-enter Erebus and re-obtain the abyssal and enduring soul remnants. The following must be done without exiting, so you may wish to re-enter again after obtaining the remnants to guarantee you have enough time.","Navigate back to the island through the timeworn lodestone, ensuring you still have the soul remnants.","Use the dark shadow anima bridge to traverse to the next island. (The anima bridges are one-way only.)","Capture the two motes of shadow anima for 8% attunement. (76% total attunement.)","Levitate the boulder next to the Boiling Rift using the enduring soul remnant.","Move the boulder to open the way to the inactive rift.","Enter the rift using the abyssal soul remnant.","Mine the shadow animica rock and crush the resulting shadow animica for 4% attunement. (80% total attunement; you may now stay for a minute and 30 seconds at a time without the handicap.)","Capture the two motes of shadow anima for 8% attunement. (88% total attunement.)","Use the dark shadow anima bridge to traverse to the next island.","Capture the three motes of shadow anima for 12% attunement. (100% total attunement.)","Harvest the font of unimaginable memories to receive an unimaginable memory.","Re-enter Erebus and re-obtain an abyssal soul remnant.","Navigate back to the Boiling Rift.","Give the unimaginable memory to the Boiling Rift to transform it into a soul geyser.","Activate the soul geyser to travel to the next island.","Use the abyssal soul remnant to activate the inactive rift and travel through it.","Activate the Idol of the Leviathan.","A cutscene will play."],"t":"Fourth visit"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Moia (or one of the other NPCs).","Take the 5 needle shards on the floor.","Talk to Hannibus.","Descend ledge to the north. {Chat: 1 Extinction}","Talk to Hannibus (or one of the other NPCs). {Chat: ~ > ~}","Teleport through the portal.","Talk to Moia (or one of the other NPCs).","Talk to Elder Chahoua to the south.","Talk to the Pastkeeper (north of Elder Chahoua, next to Hannibus).","Talk to the Plantkeeper (north of Seren).\n  - Take 4 different seeds from around Iaia.\n    - Just north-east of the Plantkeeper - flowering marsh plant.\n    - West of the Plantkeeper - roundleaf marsh plant (slightly south and before the path continues west).\n    - South-west of the Plantkeeper - marsh-fire plant.\n    - Just east of Elder Chahoua - longleaf marsh plant.\n  - Talk to the Plantkeeper.","Talk to the Pondkeeper (north-east of the Plantkeeper).\n  - Catch 4 fish in the fishing spot just north.\n  - Talk to the Pondkeeper.","Talk to the Craftmaster (south-east of the Pondkeeper).\n  - Collect the 3 Ilujankan tools nearby to the east.\n  - Talk to the Craftmaster."],"t":"Iaia"},{"n":"1 free inventory spot, combat gear, Needle Shards","r":"powerburst of vitality, tons of food & potions","s":["This is the final boss fight. Deaths are unsafe, so focus on surviving.\n  - Each phase serves as a checkpoint, so if you teleport or die during the fight, you will resume from the start of the phase you left off at.\n  - Re-gear if necessary and teleport back to the World Gate to resume, {Chat: 1 Continue Extinction}. Enter the World Gate twice.","Talk to Moia.","Talk to Seren.","Talk to Vicendithas.","Place 2 Needle shards on any of the marked spots.\n  - Kill the small shadows that spawn to gain a light core.\n  - Attack the Dark Lord while having a light core in your inventory and repeat.\n  - After the Dark Lord is dead, move the unstable energy to the Light Lord until it also dies.","Place another Needle shard on any marked spot.\n  - Kill the Small, Large, and Enraged muspahs; after each wave, damage Mah's Core (Mah wisp).\n    - Avoid the fire walls (magic damage), lightning and fire balls (typeless damage).\n    - Low level players may try to trap the melee muspah behind the core or Seren for semi safe-spotting.","Place another Needle shard on any marked spot.\n  - Avoid the fire, and then avoid the eggs (Surge and Bladed Dive can help).\n  - Focus on surviving for around 2 minutes; you do not need to kill everything.\n  - Defensive abilities such as Barricade and Reflect can help.\n  - A powerburst of vitality may be very helpful.\n  - Try staying in the south-west corner as the eggs won't go there.\n  - If you survive long enough, you can continue.","Head south towards the World Gate. Don't Surge or Bladed Dive as you may encounter a bug and have to talk to Seren again.","Activate the World Gate for a cutscene."],"t":"Finale"},{"n":"","r":"Pontifex shadow ring","s":["Talk to Seren. {Chat: ~}","Return to Senntisten via the ancient door. {Chat: 1 Yes}\n  - You are able to use the Pontifex shadow ring teleport option to teleport to the surface entrance.","Head south, enter Cathedral door, and talk to Azzanadra.","Talk to Azzanadra again after Saradomin and Armadyl leave.","Exit Senntisten (can leave quickly by lobbying or teleporting with your pontifex shadow ring) and talk to Azzanadra outside with 4 backpack space. {Chat: 4 Continue...}","Quest complete!","Unlock the Dream of Iaia and claim warped gem:\n  - Talk to Vicendithas in the Effigy Incubator laboratory.\n  - Talk to Hannibus. {Chat: 3 [Continue.] > 1 Yes.}\n  - Enter the hibernation pod to the west near the exit. {Chat: 2 Yes, and don't ask me again.}\n  - Exit via the hibernation pod. {Chat: 2 Yes, and don't ask me again.}\n  - Talk to Vicendithas for the warped gem. {Chat: 1 Do you have any Extinction rewards for me?}\n    - Combine the gem with a ring of vigour in your backpack. {Chat: 1 Yes.} This causes the effects of the ring of vigour to become passive effects for the player."],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Eye for an Eye (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"combat gear & food (prepare to kill enemies weak to fire spells)}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["Talk to Ichi on the east side of Cyclosis island (if you have just completed the Jed Hunter miniquest you may need to relog for the chat option to show up). {Chat: Accept}","Talk to Lookout Ekahi. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"30 alaea or regular sea salt}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["Talk to Lookout Ekahi again, in the centre of the island.","Kill all 27 Zyclopes.","Talk to Lookout Ekahi. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Lookout Ekahi again.","Talk to Ichi.","Talk to See in the south-west corner of the island. {Chat: 1 Do you know anything about zyclopes?}","Mine 30 sea salt crystals from the salty crabletines on the north-west beach if you don't have them already.","Talk to Sinuman in the north-east corner for a bag of crushed salt. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Daya on the west side of the island to receive a bag of blessed salt. {Chat: 1 Do you know anything about zyclopes?}","Return to Ichi east on the island. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Night watch"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go along the northern coast and speak to Undead Jed. Do not click anywhere until Undead Jed becomes attackable.","Kill Undead Jed.","Talk to Lookout Ekahi.","Talk to Lookout Ekahi again. {Chat: 1 Eye for an Eye miniquest.}"],"t":"Searching for Lookout Ekahi"}]},"Eye of Het I":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Icthlarin at the entrance to Het's Oasis. {Chat: Accept > 4 Continue...}"],"t":"Earthquake aftermath"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Clear the fallen masonry at points along the agility course. If you have already cleared it, this will be mentioned in the chat and you can start closing the rifts.\n  - At the start of the course.\n  - At the bottom of the rope ladder next to the Statue of Het.\n  - On a walkway on the eastern side of the course.\n  - At the end of a walkway further along the southern-most part of the course to the west.","Finish the course or teleport back to the Het's Oasis. A ring of duelling is the fastest teleport method back.","Talk to Icthlarin."],"t":"Clearing the rubble"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Close the rifts around Het's Oasis. They must be cleared in this particular order. (When closing a rift, it will direct you to the next one. Alternatively, refer to the map here.)\n  - Next to Icthlarin.\n  - North-eastern corner of the Het's Oasis.\n  - South-eastern corner of the Het's Oasis.\n  - Behind the statue of Het in the middle of Het's Oasis. (Can do the agility course to get there.)","Finish the agility course or teleport back to the Het's Oasis with a ring of duelling."],"t":"Closing the rifts"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Icthlarin again {Chat: 1 Yes!}","Stabilise the three unstable rifts that spawn.","Talk to Icthlarin after stabilising the rifts.","Pry the hidden door at the back of the statue of Het.\n  - Right-clicking the door brings up two options. Ensure you click just below the statue.\n  - Choose \"Pry open hidden door\".","If you have completed Our Man in the North and have level 80 Strength, the Eye of Het can be found in the statue's left hand inside the tomb. Take the eye.\n  - If you don't meet these requirements, the relic will simply be placed into your inventory upon attempting to enter.","Talk to Icthlarin at the entrance of Het's Oasis. Talking to Icthlarin at Het's statue does not work.\n  - Note: If you encounter a bug where Icthlarin says you still need to find the relic after you have obtained it, either teleport out or log out and back in and talk to Icthlarin near the bonfire.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Stabilise the rifts"}]},"Eye of Het II":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Icthlarin at the entrance to Het's Oasis. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the stranger near the tents north-east of the oasis.","Search the chest just outside of the tent with the bank chest to find some badly-hidden notes.","Read the badly-hidden notes.\n  - Make sure to proceed through all the dialogue, or you won't be able to progress.","Talk to Azzanadra at the Glacor Front (south of the cathedral in Senntisten). {Chat: 1 Talk about the Duel Arena. > Any}\n  - Wearing the shard of Erebus will keep glacors from attacking along the way.\n  - You can teleport to Arch-Glacor (and Azzanadra) using an attuned boss portal at War's Retreat, or by using the grouping system.","Head to the cathedral and talk to the gods. (You can use the pontifex shadow ring to teleport directly to the cathedral.)\n  - Talk to Seren. {Chat: 3 Talk about the Duel Arena.}\n  - Talk to Zamorak. {Chat: 3 Talk about the Duel Arena.}\n  - Talk to Armadyl. {Chat: 3 Talk about the Duel Arena.}\n  - Talk to Saradomin. {Chat: 3 Talk about the Duel Arena.}"],"t":"Gather more information"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Attempt to talk to Trindine in the following locations.\n  - At the northern entrance to the cathedral.\n  - West near Nex at the stairs near the Nodon Front.\n  - South beside Helwyr at the Glacor Front.\n  - East over the bridge at the Croesus Front.\n  - North of the Senntisten Dig Site's archaeologist's workbench. {Chat: 1 Gather Everyone.}","Talk to any god in the cathedral. (Select who you want to accuse)","Talk to Azzanadra. {Chat: Any} (If the player logs out or teleports out during this sequence, they can speak to Azzanadra at the Glacor Front to resume it.)"],"t":"Following Trindine"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Icthlarin at the entrance to Het's Oasis again."],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Family Crest":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Dimintheis in the house next to the Fancy Clothes Store in south-eastern Varrock. {Chat: 3 Hi, I am a bold adventurer. > 2 So where is this crest? > Accept}"],"t":"Patriarch"},{"n":"Swordfish, bass, tuna, salmon, and shrimp","r":"","s":["Go to Gertrude's house west of Varrock and talk to Caleb, who is inside the house (although he can sometimes wander outside). {Chat: 1 Are you Caleb Fitzharmon? > 2 So can I have your bit? > 1 Ok, I will get those.}","Talk to him again with swordfish, bass, tuna, salmon, and shrimp in the backpack to get a crest part.","Then ask Caleb where the rest of the crest is. {Chat: 1 Uh... what happened to the rest of it?}."],"t":"Caleb's piece"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Avan just south of the Al Kharid mine. {Chat: 2 I'm looking for a man named Avan Fitzharmon.}","Travel to the Dwarven mines north-east of Falador.","Head south-west of the general store and talk to Boot. {Chat: 1 Hello. I'm in search of very high quality gold.}"],"t":"Avan's request"},{"n":"Two rubies and two backpack spaces, combat equipment and food to survive under hellhound attacks","r":"","s":["Travel to Witchaven, south-east of the Ardougne lodestone. Climb down the ruins just to the west of the town. Run past the hobgoblins towards the elongated room with the Ogres.","Solve the puzzle:\n  - Logging out will reset this puzzle.\n  - Head to the northern lever located outside the room and pull it up.\n  - Head to the southern lever, located inside the room, and pull it up.\n  - Return to the northern room and pull the lever outside the room down.\n  - Enter the northern room and push the lever in there up.\n  - Leave the room and pull the one outside the northern room up.\n  - Go back to the southern room and pull the inside lever down.\n  - Now enter the room with the hellhounds.","Mine two 'Perfect' gold ore in the hellhound room. You will continue to mine gold while being attacked by hellhounds if you turn auto-retaliate off.","Smelt the ores into bars and then craft a 'Perfect' ring and a 'Perfect' necklace with two rubies at any furnace. There is a furnace just northwest of the Al Kharid lodestone. {Chat: 1 Yes smelt 'perfect' golden ring. > 2 Yes smelt 'perfect' golden necklace.}","Go back to south of the Al Kharid mine and give them to Avan."],"t":"Creating the necklace"},{"n":"Antipoison","r":"","s":["Talk to Johnathon on the floor 2 of the Jolly Boar Inn south-west of the Fort Forinthry lodestone.","Use an antipoison on him. {Chat: 2 Where can I find Chronozon?}"],"t":"Helping Johnathon"},{"n":"Runes, magic weapon and standard spellbook to cast Air, Water, Earth, and Fire Blast, alternatively a deathtouched dart","r":"","s":["Teleport to Edgeville and prepare for the final fight which will use multiple casts of the four blast spells. The other elemental spells do not work.","Enter Edgeville Dungeon and run north and then west.","Kill Chronozon when it appears.\n  - Chronozon must be hit with all four elemental blast spells or deathtouched dart in order to be killed, or otherwise it will return to full health when it is nearly dead. Once it has been hit with all four elemental blast spells, other types of damage can be used to kill it.\n  - Only the following elemental spells will work: Air Blast, Water Blast, Earth Blast, Fire Blast.\n  - If you use a high tier magic weapon (tier 70+), it will be very hard as you will kill him before being able to deal all 4 types of damage, therefore use a low-tier weapon (tier 30 or 40).","Kill him and take the crest piece."],"t":"Defeating Chronozon"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Dimintheis.","Quest complete!","Talk to Dimintheis again for cooking and smelting gauntlets. {Chat: 1 Ask about gauntlets. > 1 Reclaim lost gauntlets > 1 Yes please.}"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Fate of the Gods":{"sections":[{"n":"combat gear and a face mask (alternatively, a masked earmuffs, or a slayer helmet not on slayer helmet stand)","r":"","s":["Optional: Equip a ring of visibility to skip some dialogue.","Find the World Gate, south of the Eagles' Peak lodestone.","Talk to Azzanadra. {Chat: Accept > 2 I'll help if I can. > Any > 4 Okay, let's hear your proposal. > Any > Any}"],"t":"Powering the World Gate"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Rotate the right controls near the gate until you reach .","Rotate left until you reach .","Rotate right until you reach .","Step away from the controls, and speak to Sliske."],"t":"Combination lock"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Put on a face mask or equivalent protection to avoid taking 50 damage every 15 seconds while in Freneskae.","Enter the World Gate to enter Freneskae."],"t":"Preparing for Freneskae"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Run through Freneskae using the map below to reach the Sanctum. Move fast and avoid the hazards. There are healing points along the way if needed.","Optional: collect the memoriam crystals along the way. They are numbered on the map below; for efficiency, start with collecting number 9, then 2, 1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8.}}"],"t":"Freneskae"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Optional: Deposit collected Memoriam crystals in the middle to see memories.","Go to the north side of the room to the door puzzle.","Match the symbols up together to light up the lines in between them three times to open the door, then enter.","Kill the four nihils then enter the next area to the north. All nihils use a special attack after hissing. Each nihil always runs in the same direction. Therefore, a pair of nihil (ice and shadow or smoke and blood) can be killed first, leaving areas between the tracks unused and safe. Don't stand in the middle, as you might be dashed by multiple nihils at once.\n  - Killing the nihils while all 4 are attacking you will unlock the title the Annihilator and the achievement Annihilator.\n  - The smoke nihil attacks with Magic. Its special attack will decrease Attack, Strength, Magic, Ranged, and Defence by 15. Its charge will decrease these stats by 5.\n  - The shadow nihil attacks with Ranged, and its special attack creates Nex-like shadow bomb at the position of player that deals rapid damage. Players should move away as soon as the floor below them is darkened by a circular spot. Shadow nihil darkens the whole screen whenever it approaches the player, both when charging or fighting the player, but this causes no gameplay difference.\n  - The blood nihil attacks with melee. Its special attack causes all incoming damage to heal it, indicated when the creature lowers its head and begin to glow. It also will passively heal other nihil if it is damaged. Its charge inflicts a bleed similar to Slaughter that begins at 100 damage.\n  - The ice nihil attacks with Magic, and its special attack applies a six second stun and drains player's Prayer points by 50% of its maximum. Its charge drains the player's Prayer points by 25% of its maximum."],"t":"The Sanctum"},{"n":"good equipment and a lot of food","r":"a beast of burden and a quick teleport","s":["Attempt to descend the ledge to the north then speak to Zaros. {Chat: Any > 5 I've heard all I need to. > 2 No, just tell me the crucial info. > 2 Yes, allow him in for now.}\n  - If you accept Zaros' help against Mah, he will provide you with full prayer for use with Ancient Curses along the fight and less damage from Mah.","Defend against monsters while Mah has her nightmare (progress displayed at the top of the screen).\n  - Use Freedom or Anticipate after Mah clenches her hands to avoid being stunned when she screams in agony (though you will still take damage).","When the progress is 0%, climb down the ledge next to Mah's hand.","Collect The Measure and place it on the ground near faint wisps to activate them for harvesting (wisps can be found on the centre and edges of the cave. After revealing one, it will be a yellow dot on minimap).","Convert Mah memories into Mah Energy using the Energy rift. When you gather 250 energy, weave it into a simulacrum (dark to help Zaros, light to hinder Zaros). Hop worlds if you are having trouble finding wisps. You will be outside of the World Gate, enter again using the checkpoint option.","Return and speak to Zaros by exiting the rock face on the wall between two hallways (west of the energy rift). Speak to Zaros again after the cutscene. {Chat: Any}","Talk to Azzanadra through the world gate. {Chat: 1 I'm ready. > Any}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Meeting Zaros"}]},"Father and Son (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Irwinsson. {Chat: 1 Tell me more about yourself. > Accept}","Talk to Sigli the Huntsman located at the main gate of Rellekka.","Head back to Anachronia and give Irwinsson his greatbow. {Chat: 1 Talk about Sigli.}"],"t":"Getting started"}]},"Field of Screams":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Death, Famine, Frank, Pestilence, or War in the Harvest Hollow. {Chat: Accept}","Wear or enable as a cosmetic override four components from the above table. If wearing an item, you must not override its slot with a cosmetic override.","Talk again to one of Death, Famine, Frank, Pestilence, or War. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 Can you check my outfit?} (This choice will affect the quest's rewards.)"],"t":"Learning about Halloween plans"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the clan representative just outside of Gertrude's house.","Talk to Gertrude.","Talk to the clan representative again."],"t":"Gertrude"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the clan representative in the floor of the east side of the White Knights' Castle outside the room where Sir Renitee and Ambassador Spanfipple are.","Talk to Ambassador Spanfipple.","Head back downstairs, go to the west stairs of the castle, go upstairs, and investigate the suit of armour. (The correct suits of armour in this step and following steps periodically say {Chat: Teehee!} and are marked with a quest icon in their tooltip.)","Head back downstairs, climb the ladder on the north-east side of the castle to get to the floor. Investigate the suit of armour.","Go downstairs back to floor, then head to the east side to investigate the suit of armour. {Chat: 1. Trick}","Go up the ladder to the east and talk to Ambassador Spanfipple.","Talk to the clan representative."],"t":"Ambassador Spanfipple"},{"n":"Free slot in backpack","r":"","s":["Talk to the clan representative on the floor 2 of Lumbridge Castle outside Duke Horacio's room.","Read duke's dream diary on a table in the south-eastern corner of the room.","Talk to the cook downstairs.","Talk to any examiner in Exam Centre for a quiz. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Answer three questions correctly. (The questions are randomly selected and may not be in the following order.)\n  - \"How many legs do dragons have?\" {Chat: 2 4.}\n  - \"True or false: bronze, silver and mithril are all types of ferrous dragon.\" {Chat: 2 False.}\n  - \"What are the three main classifications of dragon?\" {Chat: 3 Chromatic, ferrous, and gemstone.}\n  - \"Which of these is the weakest type of dragon?\" {Chat: 1 Black.}\n  - \"Which of these would not protect you against dragonfire?\" {Chat: 3 Dragonstones.}","Talk to the cook.","Talk to Duke Horacio.","Talk to the clan representative."],"t":"Duke Horacio"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the captain you chose earlier in Harvest Hollow (either Death, Famine, Frank, Pestilence, or War).","If you haven't completed Maize Maze before:\n  - Complete the Maize Maze.\n  - Talk to the captain you chose earlier.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Maize Maze"}]},"Fight Arena":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Lady Servil west of the Monastery which is south of Ardougne. {Chat: Accept}","Head east and into the northeasternmost building (south of the monastery).","Borrow the Khazard armour from the northeasternmost suit of armour.","Equip the armour and enter the prison south of the building where you got the equipment (east of the big circle of the arena in the map)."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Lazy Khazard Guard sitting in the south-eastern corner of the jail.","Talk to Angor in the bar to the west, and buy a bottle of Khali brew for five coins. {Chat: 2 I'd like a Khali brew, please.}","Run back and talk to the Lazy Khazard Guard. Wait for him to pass out and then Steal keys from the table.","Use the keys on Sammy's cell door north of Lazy Khazard Guard."],"t":"Keys"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill the Khazard ogre.","Talk to Hengrad.","Open the prison door.","Kill the Khazard scorpion.","Kill Bouncer.","Kill General Khazard or walk out the door.","Talk to Lady Servil at the quest start point northwest of the arena.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The arena"}]},"Final Destination (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Lookout Ekahi (if you have just completed the previous miniquests you may need to relog for the chat option to show up). {Chat: 1 Final Destination miniquest. > Accept > 1 Yes.}","Fire the cannon.","Climb the ladder.","Kill the Zyclopses.","Climb another ladder.","Kill the zombies.","Kill the 2 skeletons.","Climb the ladder.","Kill 2 more Zyclopses.","Defeat Captain Cora then talk to her."],"t":"Commandeering the ship"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Captain Cora again.","Run east to the gates. Cora will talk to you.","Run southwest to the destroyed colony. Cora will talk to you again.","Jiangshi will appear between the colony and the gates, talk to Jiangshi.","Talk to Captain Cora."],"t":"Goshima"}]},"Fishing Contest":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to either Austri (north of the Taverley lodestone) or Vestri (north of the Catherby lodestone) who can both be found guarding caves on either side of White Wolf Mountain. {Chat: 1 I was wondering what was down that tunnel? > 2 Why not? > 3 If you were my friend I wouldn't mind it. > 1 Well, let's be friends! > 1 And how am I meant to do that? > Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["If you don't have the worms:\n  - Go to McGrubor's Wood just west of the Seers' Village lodestone and enter through the loose railing along the north fence, or use fairy ring als .\n  - Run to the west side of the woods and 'check' the red-coloured vines to receive red vine worms; take at least three.","Head to Hemenster (south-west of Seers' Village and directly west of the Ranging Guild)."],"t":"Getting Some Help"},{"n":"garlic, 3 red vine worms, fishing pass","r":"","s":["Enter the gate.","Use the garlic on the eastern wall pipes by the north side.","Either talk to Bonzo and pay him 5 coins or fish at a fishing spot to start the contest. {Chat: 1}"],"t":"The Vampyre"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Give the carp to Bonzo. {Chat: 1}","Report back to Austri or Vestri.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing Up"}]},"Flag Fall (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Boni at the Waiko market. {Chat: 1 How do I claim an uncharted isle? > Accept}\n  - If you have just completed Impressing the Locals you may need to relog for the chat option to show up.","Buy at least 5 supplies from Rosie in the marketplace, or take them from the crate next to her.","Talk to Quartermaster Gully to charter your ship on a voyage.\n  - A trip to a Short Junket costs 5 supplies per voyage.","Collect all the driftwood (if any) from the island.","Repeat this process until 5 driftwood has been gathered.","Return to Boni. {Chat: 1 How do I claim an uncharted isle?}","Miniquest complete!"],"t":"A quest for driftwood"}]},"Forgettable Tale of a Drunken Dwarf":{"sections":[{"n":"Beer, 2 barley malt, 2 buckets of water, beer glass, empty pot","r":"","s":["Talk to Commander Veldaban west of the Keldagrim bank. {Chat: Accept > Any > 1 Sounds like just the job for me!}\n  - If you did not bring beer, go to the bar south of the bank prior to speaking to Commander Veldaban. Purchase 3 beer by speaking to the Barman (one to empty out).","After the cutscene, speak to the Drunken Dwarf. {Chat: 2 I need to know about the Red Axe...}","Speak to him again with a beer in your inventory. {Chat: 2 I need to know about the Red Axe...}","Collect the four Kelda seeds:\n  - The drunken dwarf gives the first seed.\n  - Fulfil the rowdy dwarf's request for the second seed. He walks a circle around the brewery in east Keldagrim. Give him the random item he asked for.\n    - If you can't find the item he asks for or it is difficult to obtain (e.g. flier for Bob's Axes), talk to him again multiple times until there is a dialogue option that will change the item he asks for. You may need to lobby.\n    - If you have accepted a task to fetch an item for the dwarf before this point in the quest, fulfilling that task now may not count towards the quest and you will have to perform another one.\n  - Talk to Khorvak in a cave north of the Taverley lodestone (under White Wolf Mountain, not on the top). There is a convenient cart to the south of the rowdy dwarf that will take you straight to the cave. The cave is also accessible northeast of the Catherby lodestone. {Chat: 2 No wait, I want to borrow it after all.}\n  - Talk to Gauss to have a beer with him, located in the bar south of the Keldagrim bank for the fourth seed.","Talk to Rind the gardener, east of the pub where you have just talked to Gauss.","Plant the four seeds in the nearby Kelda Hops Patch.","Wait 20 minutes and harvest the Kelda hops.\n  - A supreme growth potion (sundry) will not work here. If you choose to spend the waiting time logged out or in lobby, upon login the hop patch may appear weedy as if nothing was planted in it. Simply click the patch and you will receive your hops all the same.\n  - Optionally, talk to Rind and he will ask you to deliver a letter to Elstan at the allotment patches south of Falador. Upon returning to Rind, he will reward you 2 marrentill seeds.","Go to the brewery, upstairs in the pub, on the eastern side of Keldagrim.","Pick up the empty pot in the corner of the room and ask Blandebir to fill it up with ale yeast for 25 coins. {Chat: 4 Can you sell me any ale yeast? > 1 Fill your pot}","Select \"Brew\" option on fermenting vat and select \"Kelda stout\".","Wait up to 5-20 minutes, until you get a notification in your chatbox.\n  - \"Perhaps I should have a look and see if my Kelda Stout has brewed...\"","Turn the valve on the connected pipe behind the vat and then use the empty beer glass in your inventory on the barrel to drain it.\n  - If you are drinking your beer to empty it, ensure you have \"Destroy empty beer glasses when drinking\" disabled in the Settings/Interfaces/Inventory menu, or you will have to buy another.","Return to the Drunken Dwarf in the eastern-most of the two houses between the two wells in east Keldagrim and talk to him about the Red Axe. {Chat: 2 I need to know about the Red Axe...}"],"t":"Quid pro quo"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the southern most cart conductor that is near the closed tunnel in south-east Keldagrim, the other cart conductor in the area will not work. {Chat: 1 Ask about closed off tunnel.}","Talk to the director of the Consortium mining company you joined during The Giant Dwarf. If you don't remember, you can talk to Commander Veldaban and he will tell you. {Chat: 3 Can you help me with a boarded up tunnel?} (There are eight mining companies in the Consortium, each stationed in the upstairs of the marketplace.)","Un-equip any weapons you are holding, and if you have a familiar out, pick it up. Then ride the southern cart into the tunnel."],"t":"The drunken dwarf"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Collect the square stones from the box.","Operate the controls: To place/rotate stones, click once for green, twice for yellow, three times to remove the stone.\n  - There will be no confirmation prompt after you've set the route. Just click on the minecart or walk away once you've added the stones.\n  - Alternatively, place all of the Green stones then the Yellow stones, or vice versa.","After each part, ride on the cart, search the newly found box, and take the cart back to the initial platform."],"t":"Room 1: a chasm"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After the dialogue, crawl along the southern path, and through the cave entrance to the east."],"t":"Room 2: eavesdropping"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take the stones from the box and follow the patterns below."],"t":"Room 3: another chasm"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Search all three crates with papers on top of them.","Search the bookcases until you find the \"Red Axe Employee Records\" book. Read it.","Enter the cave entrance to the east. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Room 4: reports"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take the stones from the box and follow the patterns below.}} Forgettable Tale of a Drunken Dwarf - Chasm Puzzle 7.png|Part 1 Forgettable Tale of a Drunken Dwarf - Chasm Puzzle 8.png|Part 2 Forgettable Tale of a Drunken Dwarf - Chasm Puzzle 9.png|Part 3 {{Checklist|","Watch the entire cutscene as you enter the last room."],"t":"Room 5: yet another chasm"},{"n":"Beer, kebab","r":"","s":["Go back and speak to Commander Veldaban west of Keldagrim bank.","Head to the Laughing Miner Pub in eastern Keldagrim. While inside, consume either your beer or kebab, though you'll need both in your inventory. If you don't have a kebab yet, talk to Kjut in his shop south-east of the northern bridge.\n  - You must watch the entire cutscene!","Quest complete!"],"t":"Kebabs and beer"}]},"Forgiveness of a Chaos Dwarf":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Commander Veldaban in the building west of the bank in west Keldagrim. {Chat: 3 Do you have a quest for me? > Accept > 2 Do you think the Red Axe is behind it?}","After the cutscene you will be transported next to the Keldagrim Watchtower, continue dialogue with Commander Veldaban. {Chat: 4 I'll deal with the chaos dwarf. > 1 I'm ready.}","Head into the Keldagrim Watchtower next to you, travel upstairs to the roof, and kill the chaos dwarf and pick up the mysterious slip.","Talk to Commander Veldaban about the slip. {Chat: 3 The chaos dwarf dropped a slip of paper. > 1 I'll take the slip to the Grand Exchange now.}","Talk to any Grand Exchange clerk at the Grand Exchange in Varrock. {Chat: 5 I have this dwarven order slip...}\n  - Grand Exchange clerks in Prifddinas, the Max Guild, and Menaphos do not work.\n  - If you have never used the Grand Exchange (common for ironmen), the Grand Exchange clerk will refuse to talk to you. Speak to the Grand Exchange Tutor just south and state that \"I want the basics from you.\" before talking to the Grand Exchange clerk."],"t":"Initial Battle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Ask the barmaid for his stout. {Chat: 4 Commander Veldaban wants a Guardsman's Stout. > Any}","Talk to Veldaban about the battle then take him to the headquarters. {Chat: 4 I didn't know you had a lady-friend. > 2 What was the Battle of Barendir? > 1 The barmaid said she'd seen you with someone. > 2 Let's talk about something else. > 1 Are you drunk? > 1 What are you doing here? > 4 Do you think the Red Axe is involved? > 3 Do you think the missing persons are connected to the chaos dwarves? > 2 Who's on the case now? > 1 Why did he take you off the case? > 4 Let's talk about something else. > 3 I have the Grand Exchange Package > 5 Let's Talk about something else > 1 Let's go.}","After the cutscene, head back to watchtower in the south area of west Keldagrim, where you fought the chaos dwarf."],"t":"Drunk Commander"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use the boot on the footprints south of the watchtower building (where you defeated the chaos dwarf).","Follow the footsteps south and then west to reach a small fire pit (the one across the bridge - it looks different from the other fire pits in the area).","Use the bowl on the fire pit, remove it, then use the rod on the fire pit.","Turn the rod.","Enter the tunnel west, then enter the doorway at the west end.","Free your hands.","Attempt to ride the train cart (you don't go far).","Leave through the tunnel back to Keldagrim. {Chat: 2 Return to Keldagrim.}","Dismiss any followers you may have.","Talk to Commander Veldaban back where the quest started {Chat: 3 I found a secret door in the mines. > 1 Let's go.} and take him back to the caves."],"t":"Investigation"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Try to control the Dwarven Machinery and have Veldaban do it while you ride the cart. {Chat: 3 You take the stones and man the board. I'll ride the cart.}","Click on the cart to begin.","Follow these choices:\n  - Yellow {Chat: 2 Yellow Stone}\n  - Green {Chat: 1 Green Stone}\n  - Yellow {Chat: 2 Yellow Stone}\n  - Green {Chat: 1 Green Stone}\n  - Green {Chat: 1 Green Stone}\n  - Yellow {Chat: 2 Yellow Stone}\n  - Yellow {Chat: 2 Yellow Stone}\n  - Yellow {Chat: 2 Yellow Stone}\n  - Yellow {Chat: 2 Yellow Stone}","Pull the bridge lever."],"t":"Cart Labyrinth"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head south to the prison and open the door.","Talk to Fjoila. {Chat: 4 You should get back to Keldagrim now. > 1 You told the prisoner we'd look for Hilda.}","Head south, turn either of the switches and go through the doorway. Commander Veldaban may be stuck up north.","Watch the cutscene. {Chat: Any}","After the cutscene, talk to Veldaban in the room. {Chat: Any > 3 That wasn't Hilda. Hilda was gone by then. > 4 There are still some things in the package.}","Use the metal rectangle then the turnscrew on the sorting machine.","Squeeze through the hole and ride the train cart for a cutscene.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Rescue and Escape"}]},"From Tiny Acorns (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Darren Lightfinger in the Thieves' Guild. {Chat: Accept}","Talk to the market guard in Varrock Square. {Chat: 2 Who's the dwarf over there? > 1 Do you know what he's working on?}","Pickpocket Urist Loric until successful. He is the dwarf just north east of the Varrock General Store.","Left click to put-down Urist's talisman.","To steal from the crafting stall, follow these steps quickly:\n  - Talk to Urist Loric again.\n  - Run to the guard and right-click to distract him.\n  - Steal from the crafting stall.","Talk to Urist Loric for the banker's note.","Go back to the Thieves' Guild","Use the banker's note on Darren with the toy dragon in the backpack.","Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Walkthrough"}]},"Fur 'n Seek":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Odd Old Man in Silvarea. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Make your way to Fremennik Province.","Obtain the animal fur. Use the table below as a reference."],"t":"Obtaining the furs"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use a bag of salt on each of the hides.","Return to the Odd Old Man's house with 8 of any type of logs and the scrubbed hides in inventory.","Head to the north-east, add logs to the fire pit and stretch skins on the ribcage. Do not walk away after clicking - it will process all furs automatically.","Talk to the Odd Old Man.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Garden of Tranquillity":{"sections":[{"n":"Ring of charos","r":"","s":["Talk to Queen Ellamaria in the garden of Varrock Palace. {Chat: Accept}","Talk to her again to receive a trolley that is needed later. {Chat: 1 How am I supposed to move statues all the way here?}","Equip the ring of charos and talk to the Wise Old Man in Draynor Village. {Chat: 1 Queen Ellamaria has sent me to seek your guidance.}\n  - Show them a range of colours so that they can come to a compromise.\n  - Take his generous gift even though you have no need for it.\n  - It's absolutely, unquestionably the most interesting thing I've ever done!\n  - Put on the silly helmet and jump into the cannon.\n  - You of course Pkmaster0036, no one could ever challenge your greatness!\n  - Ask me nicely and I might consider it.\n  - No, especially not that wise old man, who doesn't look at all suspicious.","Thanks for your help, Wise Old Man. {Chat: 1 Thanks for your help, Wise Old Man.}","If you don't have onion seeds, cabbage seeds or marigold seed, purchase them from Draynor Seed Market."],"t":"The ring of charos (a)"},{"n":"Ring of charos (a), and 3 (6 recommended) onion seed; if travelling by ship: ghostspeak amulet, and 2 ecto-tokens (if Ghosts Ahoy has not been completed)","r":"compost or supercompost, and supreme growth potion (universal), sundry variant or sunburst bracelet to skip growth cycles","s":["Charm Lyra at the allotments near Port Phasmatys (east of the Canifis lodestone). Accept to grow the patch of onions. {Chat: 1 Do you have any orchid seeds to spare? > 2 [Charm] If you tell me your problems, I may be able to help you. > 2 [Charm] Yes, I was wondering about that. > 2 [Charm] Times must be very hard for you. > 2 [Charm] Whatever you've done, I'm sure you had just cause. > 2 [Charm] And what is the nature of this fee that you pay? > 2 [Charm] If not yours, then whose blood are you offering? > 2 [Charm] How can you deal with so much guilt? > 1 That's a deal - I'll grow a patch of onions for you.}","Plant onion seeds in allotment patch. Planting in one patch is enough, planting two increases the success rate of healthy growth. This will take about 40 minutes, so continue the quest and come back later.\n  - Apply compost or supercompost to allotment patch to protect the crops."],"t":"Orchids from Port Phasmatys"},{"n":"Ring of charos (a), and 3 (6 recommended) cabbage seed","r":"compost or supercompost, and supreme growth potion (universal), sundry variant or sunburst bracelet to skip growth cycles","s":["Charm Kragen at the allotments at Manor Farm. Accept to grow the cabbages. {Chat: 1 Do you have any snowdrop seeds to spare? > 2 [Charm] You seem to be a little irritable, my friend. > 2 [Charm] I don't like to see a fellow human being so upset. > 2 [Charm] So what ails you, my friend? > 2 [Charm] Well, is there anything I can do for you? > 2 [Charm] So what can I do for you? > 1 That's a deal - I'll let you know when your cabbages are ready.}","Plant cabbage seeds in allotment patch. Planting in one patch is enough, planting two increases the success rate of healthy growth. This too will take about 40 minutes, so continue the quest and come back later. Rosemary must be fully grown to protect cabbage.\n  - Apply compost or supercompost to allotment patch to protect the crops."],"t":"Snowdrops from Ardougne"},{"n":"Ring of charos (a), and 1 marigold seed","r":"compost or supercompost, and supreme growth potion (universal), leafy variant or sunburst bracelet to skip growth cycles","s":["Use cabbage-port on your explorer's ring 3 or teleport to Draynor Village lodestone and run north-west past the wall to the farming patch in Falador farm.","Charm Elstan at the allotments north of Port Sarim and agree to grow some marigolds. {Chat: 1 Do you have any delphinium seeds to spare? > 2 [Charm] That is why I have come to an expert for advice. > 3 [Charm] Not just AN expert, Elstan - they say you are THE expert. > 2 [Charm] Oh no, I love listening to gardening stories... > 2 [Charm] Millions? Ah, just what I wanted to hear... > 1 Okay, I'll grow you some marigolds.}","Plant a marigold seed in the flower patch. This will take about 20 minutes.","Apply compost or supercompost to flower patch.","Add water till fully grown this will take 10 to 20 minutes.","Pick up the grown marigold.","Talk with Elstan and finish the dialogue. Aborting the dialogue between handing him the unnoted marigolds and receiving the seeds, you will have to grow the marigolds again."],"t":"Delphiniums from Falador"},{"n":"Ring of charos (a), fishing rod or fly fishing rod, and 3 free backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Go to the Edgeville Monastery. Try to take a seed from one of Brother Althric's rose bushes.","Charm Brother Althric near the monastery rose bushes. {Chat: 2 [Charm] These are the most beautiful rosebushes I've ever seen.}","Unequip the ring of charos and use it on Edgeville's well east of the lodestone.","Try to take a seed from one of Brother Althric's rose bushes again.","Talk to Brother Althric.","Pick 4 pink, white and red rose seeds (just click each type of bush once; you will pick 4 of them automatically).","Use your fishing rod on the well and equip the ring of charos."],"t":"Rosebushes from the Edgeville Monastery"},{"n":"Ring of charos (a), secateurs or magic secateurs, a filled plant pot, and watering can or magic watering can","r":"","s":["Talk to Dantaera at the Catherby allotment farming patch with the ring equipped. Select all the options beginning with [Charm]. {Chat: 1 Do you know how I could grow a White Tree? > 2 [Charm] I think that there is something that you are not telling me. > 2 [Charm] A secret is a dreadful burden to have to keep to yourself. > 2 [Charm] Unless you allow me to do this she will die anyway.}","Interact with the white tree on Ice Mountain west of Edgeville, select secateurs.","Use the white tree shoot on a plant pot and water it.","It will take 3 minutes for the shoot to turn into a White tree sapling. It is recommended to plant the tree in the Queen's Garden as soon as possible, as this will take about 6 minutes longer to grow than the other plants."],"t":"The white tree"},{"n":"Ring of charos (a), 2 plant cure, and rune essence or pure essence","r":"","s":["Charm Bernald who is south of the Taverley pub. {Chat: 2 [Charm] But it is the only way that these vines will be cured. > 1 I accept the deal.}","Use a plant cure on his grapevines.","Talk to Bernald again.","Run north and talk to Alain at the tree patch. Do not charm him. {Chat: 1 I need to ask you about strong plant cures. > 1 Are you sure there's nothing you can suggest?}","Use an essence on any anvil (you will find anvils walking north), grind the shards, use the rune dust on a plant cure.","Return to Bernald.","Use the new plant cure on his grapevines.","Talk to Bernald."],"t":"Vines from Taverley"},{"n":"Trolley","r":"","s":["If you have no trolley, talk to Ellamaria in the Varrock Palace garden to receive one.","Teleport to Lumbridge, and at the entrance of the Lumbridge Castle courtyard, use the trolley on the southern statue.","Push the trolley east across the nearby bridge.\n  - You may select the \"Big-push\" option to move the statue more quickly.","Push it into the Queen's garden and use the \"place\" option when statue is close to the plinth, the one against the east wall. If you are not fast enough to push it and place it, it will disappear and respawn in Lumbridge.","Teleport to Falador, and use the trolley on the statue of Saradomin south of the Falador lodestone.","After the cutscene, push it north out the gates and onto the garden plinth using the place option again.","If you take too long to move the statues to the plinth, they will vanish and return back to their original position."],"t":"Rock and roll"},{"n":"4 white rose seed, 4 pink rose seed, 4 red rose seed, 4 snowdrop seed, 1 white tree sapling, 4 vine seed, 3 orchid seed (pink), 3 orchid seed (yellow), 4 delphinium seed, 2 compost or supercompost, and ring of charos (a)","r":"","s":["You can now return to the patches and collect your seeds from the farmers (if you haven't done it already)\n  - Orchid seed (pink) and orchid seed (yellow) from Lyra east of Canifis.\n  - Snowdrop seeds from Kragen north-east of Ardougne.\n  - Delphinium seeds from Elstan north-east of Port Sarim.","Plant the seeds back at the garden.\n  - Use your buckets of compost on the nearby plantpots. If having issues with \"this patch needs weeding first\", use regular compost, not supercompost.\n  - Plant the rose seed, flower seeds, and white tree sapling in their spots.\n  - Plant the vine seeds in the vine patch.\n  - Plant the orchids in the plant pots. You may use Inspect option on a plant pot to find out what goes there.","Wait for everything to grow which takes around 15 minutes; 20 for the White Tree if you haven't planted it yet.","Talk to the Queen.","Charm King Roald while equipped with the ring of charos (a). {Chat: 1 Ask King Roald to follow you. > 2 [Charm] Of course, your majesty - please forgive me. > 2 [Charm] The Queen asked me to bring you.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing the garden"}]},"Gertrude's Cat":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to Gertrude's house north-west of the Varrock lodestone.","Talk to Gertrude. {Chat: Accept}","Go behind the house and pick up a doogle leaf."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the northeastern corner of Varrock Square.","Talk to Shilop or Wilough, giving them 100 coins. {Chat: 2 What will make you tell me? > 2 Okay then, I'll pay.}","Go south-west to an abandoned house between the Smithing workshop and the tanner, near the west wall of Varrock.","Climb a ladder found inside the building."],"t":"The secret hideout"},{"n":"1 bucket of milk, 1 raw sardine, 1 doogle leaf}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["Don't skip any dialogue for this section.","Use a bucket of milk on Fluffs.","Use a doogle sardine on Fluffs (use raw sardine on doogle leaf).\n  - If this fails, talk to Gertrude and find out about doogle sardines.","Climb down the ladder and search the jiggling crate in the ruined building directly east to find three little kittens. (Note: The location of the jiggling crate is different for every player.)","Return to Fluffs, and use the three little kittens on her (you might need to use them on her twice).","Watch the cutscene."],"t":"Convincing Fluffs"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Gertrude.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Ghosts Ahoy":{"sections":[{"n":"Ghostspeak amulet","r":"","s":["To enter Port Phasmatys, either pay two ecto-tokens as an entrance fee to pass the energy barrier or charter a ship to reach the town. Each entry through the barrier, until the end of the quest, will cost two ecto-tokens.","Equip the ghostspeak amulet. You need to equip the amulet when you talk to the ghost residents in the town.","Talk to Velorina at Port Phasmatys, in the northernmost building just east of the entrance. {Chat: 1 Why, what is the matter? > 1 Yes, I do. It is a very sad story. > Accept}","Talk to Necrovarus at the Ectofuntus just outside the town, to the north.","If you do not already have a bucket of slime, obtain it now for later use in the quest.\n  - Open and climb down the trapdoor on the west side of the Ectofuntus to enter the basement. You do not need a bucket to obtain one.\n  - If you intend to proceed with the quest Vessel of the Harbinger after this quest, obtain the second one.","Talk to Velorina. {Chat: 1 Do you know where this woman can be found?}"],"t":"Ghostly trouble"},{"n":"nettle tea, silk, thread, bucket of milk","r":"","s":["Teleport to Canifis lodestone.","If you haven't already made nettle tea, pick some nettles just east. Use the nettles on the bowl of water to get nettle-water.","Head north-west to Netty's house which is on the east side of the Slayer Tower, talk to Netty in her house. {Chat: 1 You are doing so much for me - is there anything I can do for you?}","If you haven't already made nettle tea, run south of Netty's house and cut down a swamp tree for logs. Light a fire and use the nettle-water on it to get nettle tea. It is possible to accidentally boil your tea over.","Talk to Netty to get her porcelain cup. {Chat: 1 I'm here about Necrovarus.}","Use your nettle tea on her cup, and use your bucket of milk on it.","Talk to Netty again. {Chat: 1 I'm here about Necrovarus. > 1 You are doing so much for me - is there anything I can do for you?}","Repair the model ship with the silk. Bring thread just in case."],"t":"Getting help"},{"n":"3 red dye, 3 blue dye, 3 yellow dye, combat equipment","r":"","s":["Go inside the shipwreck just north of Alice's farm, east of the Canifis lodestone.","Climb the ladders to reach the top deck (there is a ladder on the outer cabin wall)."],"t":"The map"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Wait for the \"wind speed\" to become \"low\", which is shown on the top of the screen. Search the mast to determine the colours and their positions. You need to search for 3 different results, take note if needed.","Dye the model ship with the same colours and position as the mast. Orange dye is made from red and yellow; green dye is made from blue and yellow; purple dye is made from red and blue dye. If you make a mistake when painting, simply paint over the piece again."],"t":"Dyeing the ship"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb down a ladder and enter the captain's cabin.","Talk to the old man. {Chat: 3 Is this your toy boat?}","Use the key on the chest by the Captain and open it for a map scrap.","On the floor 1 of the ship, open and search all unlocked chest in the eastern end of the ship until a giant lobster spawns.","Kill the giant lobster.","Search the chest again for a map scrap.","On the floor 2 of the ship, go to the northwest part of the ship's deck.","Cross the gangplank to the rocks.","Jump to the rocks on your side until you find a chest. Open it for another map scrap.","Put the pieces together to get the map."],"t":"Collecting the map scraps"},{"n":"spade in the backpack, treasure map","r":"","s":["Right-click and choose \"Travel\" on the ghost captain on the south-east docks (the one with the smaller boat, not the one directly east of Velorina) to get a ride to Dragontooth Island.{Chat: 1 Please take me to Dragontooth Island.}","Dig with a spade at the location () shown to the right to obtain the book of haricanto.","Right-click and choose \"Travel\" on the ghost captain to go back Port Phasmatys."],"t":"Dragontooth Island"},{"n":"oak shieldbow","r":"","s":["Talk to Ak-Haranu (who is not a ghost) around the docks. {Chat: 1 Okay, wait here - I'll get you your bow.}","Go to the inn and talk to Robin. {Chat: 2 Talk about something else. > 1 Yes, I'll give you a game.}","Win 4 games of Rune-Draw against him to get a signed oak shieldbow. The easiest method is to choose \"draw\" until one player loses by drawing a death rune and repeating this until you have four wins total.\n  - Talk to Robin every time you finish a game. {Chat: 2 Talk about something else. > 1 Yes, I'll give you a game.}","Talk to Ak-Haranu to get the translation manual."],"t":"Translation"},{"n":"","r":"bucket of slime","s":["Ask the ghost innkeeper, who is located in the pub, for a job to get a bedsheet. {Chat: 4 Do you have any jobs I can do? > 1 Yes, I'd be delighted.}\n  - Don't give it to Robin like he asks.","Use your bucket of slime on the bedsheet or dip it into the Pool of Slime. You cannot re-enter Port Phasmatys via charter ship if you have dipped bedsheet in the backpack.","Talk to Gravingas west of the inn to get a petition form. {Chat: 1 After hearing Velorina's story I will be happy to help out.}","Wear your bedsheet.","Ask the ghost villager for signatures until you have 10.\n  - You can get multiple signatures from the same ghost if you ask another ghost first.\n  - Some will resist. Just ask others.\n  - If a ghost ask for ecto-tokens, simply leave the conversation and ask the same ghost again.","After you collected 10 signatures, remove your bedsheet.","Talk to Necrovarus at the Ectofuntus. Take the bone key he drops on the floor.","Head upstairs, and use the key on the door on the south-west side. Then open the door.","Open and search the coffin for Necrovarus' mystical robes."],"t":"Revolution"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head north-west of the Canifis lodestone and talk to Netty in her shack (east of the Slayer Tower).","Equip the enchanted ghostspeak amulet.","Talk to Necrovarus near the Ectofuntus. {Chat: 1 Let any ghost who so wishes pass on into the next world.} Once you have talked to Necrovarus, you will be able to enter Port Phasmatys freely. You can pass the energy barrier without needing to pay ecto-tokens.","Talk to Velorina in northern Port Phasmatys.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Persuasion techniques"}]},"Ghosts from the Past (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to The Islands That Once Were Turtles.","Talk to Quartermaster Gully (if you have just completed Harbringer you may need to relog for the chat option to show up). {Chat: 1 Ghosts from the Past miniquest. > Accept > 5 Enough questions. Let's move on.}","Climb both watchtowers on the island and talk to both skeletons of the Skulls pirate and the Skulls mercenary.","Continue north and climb up the observatory.\n  - Talk to the skeleton of the Skulls thief at the top.","Return to Quartermaster Gully. {Chat: 1 Ghosts from the Past miniquest.}"],"t":"Ghosts from the past"}]},"Glorious Memories":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Manni the Reveller in Rellekka longhall. {Chat: Accept}","Talk to King Vargas in Miscellania.","Talk to Manni the Reveller in Rellekka longhall.","Talk to Brundt the Chieftain back in Rellekka Longhall. {Chat: # Ask about the birthday feast.}","After the cutscene you'll be given cave directions.","Then return to Miscellania and talk to King Vargas.","After the cutscene, talk to Mawnis Burowgar in Neitiznot, south of the bank. {Chat: 2 Chieftain Brundt's birthday feast.} Watch the cutscene.}}"],"t":"Birthday feast"},{"n":"Equipment for a battle with a level 81 monster, 4 free backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Travel to the 'i' icon ('question mark' on legacy interfaces) in the snowy Rellekka Hunter area.","Inspect the tracks in the north-west corner of the platform and follow them to a mound of ice in the north-east corner. Inspect the tracks directly in front of the ice mound, then dig through the ice mound and go inside. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Run to the southern wall and enter the tunnel.","Kill Nial Swiftfling and take all of his items.","Talk to Freygerd in Jatizso near the west gate. {Chat: 1 Talk about Nial.}","Talk to King Gjuki Sorvott IV in the central building. {Chat: 2 Talk about Freygerd and the new tax.}","Talk to Freygerd near the west gate. {Chat: 1 Talk about Nial.}","Talk to Mawnis Burowgar in Neitiznot, south of the bank. {Chat: 2 Chieftain Brundt's birthday feast.}"],"t":"The yeti's lair"},{"n":"An empty vial, 10 earth runes and 1 cosmic rune to cast Lvl-4 Enchant, a plank, a staff or pole, a clean irit, herb pouch, and yeti hair.","r":"","s":["Talk to King Vargas in the throne room in Miscellania.","Ensure you have the standard spellbook enabled.","Travel to the Mountain Camp. (Fairy code AJR or east of the Fremennik Province lodestone.)\n  - A pole and plank can be found near the goats if you didn't bring a staff and plank.","Climb the tree next to the lake, use the staff/pole on the clump of rocks, then use the plank on the flat stone.","Stand south of the rocks and listen-to a shining pool in the water.\n  - If the diamond root was not placed in your backpack, open the herb pouch with at least one available backpack space.","Use your vial on the spring that appeared on the rock near you.","Use a clean irit on the vial of mountain water for a mountain irit potion (unfinished).","Grind the diamond root, cast Lvl-4 Enchant on the diamond root dust, then use the enchanted diamond root dust and yeti hair to the unfinished vial to make yeti curse cure.","Return and talk to King Vargas. After the cutscene, he transforms into his human form.","Talk to Brundt the Chieftain in the Rellekka longhall about the birthday feast. {Chat: # Ask about the birthday feast.}","After the cutscene, talk to Manni the Reveller in the longhall and watch another cutscene.","Quest complete!","Optionally after the quest:\n  - Take the unfinished astral rune to Baba Yaga on Lunar Isle. {Chat: 2 Talk about astral runes.}\n  - Take the prophecy tablet to Historian Minas on the floor 2 of the Varrock Museum. {Chat: 2 I have some information that might be of use in your displays.}"],"t":"The king's cure"}]},"Goblin Diplomacy":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to Falador and run north along the road to the Goblin Village.","Talk to General Bentnoze or General Wartface, both of whom are located in the hut. {Chat: 1 So how is life for the goblins? > 2 Wouldn't you prefer peace? > 2 Do you want me to pick an armour colour for you? > 3 What about a different colour? > Accept}","If you need goblin mail, you can grab three suits of goblin mail from the following crates:\n  - Behind the generals' hut.\n  - Behind the western hut.\n  - Up a ladder in the middle of the gate entrance of the camp."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"Orange dye (Combine Red dye and Yellow dye), Blue dye, 3 suits of goblin mail","r":"","s":["Dye one goblin mail blue and another orange.","Use the orange goblin mail on one of the generals.","After the cutscene, use the blue goblin mail on one of them.","Use a normal goblin mail on one of them.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Gower Quest":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to the Gowers at their farm next to rats and a cabbage patch south-east of the Varrock lodestone. {Chat: 1 So about that quest, then? > Accept}","Search the crate in the room to the west to obtain pure essence.","Search the largest water barrel to the west of the southern entrance to obtain a brussels sprout.","Search the scarecrow in the south-western part of the farm with the cabbages to obtain a cruciferous mounting.","Search the food trough on the east side of the farm in the area with the giant rats to obtain a broccoli root.","Spin the broccoli root into broccoli string on the spinning wheel in the main room.","Use the brussels sprout on the cruciferous mounting to make it into an unstrung brassican amulet.","Use the \"Flip\" option on the pure essence to turn it into a life rune.","Use the broccoli string on the unstrung brassican amulet to create a brassican amulet.","Use the life rune on the brassican amulet to enchant it into a cabbagespeak amulet.","Equip the amulet and talk to Crispy the Cabbage south-west on the cabbage field.","Talk to the Gower brothers inside of the house. {Chat: Any}","Speak to the Cabbages again.","Speak to Andrew to receive the disk of returning."],"t":"Gower's Farm"},{"n":"","r":"Armour, weapon, and food (Note: keep 6-7 free spaces)}}If you destroy \"Crispy The Cabbage\", you can reclaim \"Crispy\" from the Gower Farm. {{Checklis","s":["Go to Dwarven Mines (entrance north-east of Falador lodestone).","Go to the \"room\" just before the south-westernmost one (Boot will be in the area).","Scan with the disk of returning.","The room is intentionally black. Move your cursor around to find the hidden objects:\n  - Search the table for a rock.\n  - Use the rock on the wall to the northwest.\n  - Right click on the table to look under it for an orange.\n  - Eat the orange for a key.\n  - Use the small key on the bumpy wall on the right for a tinderbox.\n  - Use the tinderbox on the scary wispy thing and take the skull.\n  - Use the skull on the unusual shape to the west.\n  - Enter The Gate of Lloigh-enn."],"t":"Black Hole Experience"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Thordur. {Chat: Any > Any > 1 Off I go, then.}"],"t":"The Gate of Lloigh-enn"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Spiral Orb (the purple spider DJ in the middle). {Chat: 1 What's up with the cabbage patches? > 2 I'll take a look around myself.}","Look around in this area for 3 NPCs: Lucien, Steve the Chaos Elemental, and Thok.\n  - You can complete the following in any order."],"t":"Lloigh-enn"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Lucien, north-west of spiral orb and next to central bank portal. {Chat: 2 Can you help me fix the life altar? > 3 Not much, man.}","Enter the Central Bank Portal.","Talk to Claire Hick.","Talk to Ernie.","Check out the Locked Vault Door.","Leave the area.","Talk to Sphenishchev, located south of the portal next to the bar, the penguin next to Beastmaster Durzag. {Chat: 2 Will you help me break into the bank?}","Talk to Tim or Crunchy, just south-west of Spiral Orb (the DJ). {Chat: 3 Will you help me break into the bank?}","Ask the bartender for 5 cups of tea and hand them out to all 5 Environment artists around the bar.","Return to Tim and Crunchy. {Chat: 1 Everyone's been watered!}","Talk to Romeo, southeast of Beastmaster Durzag. {Chat: 2 Will you help me break into the bank? > 2 I'll see who I can find.}","Talk to each God Wars Boss to the east.\n  - Commander Zilyana\n  - K'ril Tsutsaroth\n  - General Graardoor\n  - Kree'arra\n  - Nex","Return to Romeo. {Chat: 1 Yes, some people had ideas.}","Talk to Guthix, south of the bar. {Chat: 2 Will you help me break into the bank?}","Talk to one of the cabbages on the north-side of the bar.","Return to Guthix. {Chat: 1 Yes, they're very interested in working with you!}","Enter the Central Bank Portal.","Talk to Claire Hick.","Talk to Ernie. {Chat: 1 I have someone who wants to speak to you.}","Check out the locked vault door, then enter it.","Open the Bank Safety box, then search it for a fragment.","Leave the bank area."],"t":"Lucien"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Chaos Elemental, north of the Grand Exchange Maintenance, southwest of the bar. {Chat: 2 Can you help me fix the life altar? > 2 NO! No, thank you. > 3 Goodbye Steve!}","Enter the Grand Exchange Maintenance portal.","Repair the Grand Exchange pipes. (there are 3 different thickness pipes, each size must fit each other from the beginning to the end, the interface will close when it's correct)","Leave the Grand Exchange area}}"],"t":"Steve"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Thok, just north-west of Clawdia. {Chat: 2 Can you help me fix the life altar?}","Enter Beta Room Portal and talk to Max. {Chat: Any > 2 I'll get right on with that then.}","Max all 3 skills.\n  - First room: You get options to rock, trot, gallop, turn. Just click on the action displayed on top of the screen.\n  - Second room: Fire at other battleships (searching desert island and bubbles give more xp too).\n  - Third room: Stay inside the bank on the white floor tiles.","Talk to Max for the third fragment.","Leave the area."],"t":"Thok"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the Life Altar Portal south, opposite of the Beta Room Portal.","Investigate Life altar.","Speak with the Black Knight Titan. {Chat: 4 Can we just get on with the boss fight?}","Kill it 6 times. 3 Before cutscene, 3 after.","Talk to any of the brothers.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Repairing the Life Altar"}]},"Great Egg-spectations":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Easter Bunny in the northern area of the Blooming Burrow. {Chat: 1 Talk bout 'Great Egg-spectations'. > Accept}","Talk to Cocoa Bunny on the hill in the south-east."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to Musa Point on Karamja.","Eavesdrop on the banoffee chocolate recipe on the table by Luthas.","Pick a banana from the banana tree and slice it if not done so already."],"t":"Banoffee chocolate"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Eavesdrop on the rocky road chocolate recipe on the table in Drogo's Mining Emporium.}}"],"t":"Rocky road chocolate"},{"n":"Grapes}}{{Checklist; * Travel to the Garden of Kharid, north of [[Het's Oasis]","r":"","s":["Eavesdrop on the fruit and nut chocolate recipe in the north-eastern hut.","Dry grapes on the washing line at Garden of Kharid.\n  - Note: grapes can't be dried on the washing line until you've eavesdropped the other 2 chocolate recipes.","Buy some nuts from a pet shop.}}"],"t":"Fruit and nut chocolate"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to Egg Plant in the Blooming Burrow.","Take from the sugar sacks.","Talk to Gooey Bunny to acquire marshmallows.","Cook the sugar into a bottle of caramel on a range. Any range works, but the range in Easter Bunny's house to the north-east is close to next step."],"t":"Gathering the ingredients"},{"n":"Sliced banana, bottle of caramel, dried grapes, nuts, biscuits, marshmallows","r":"","s":["Talk to the Easter Bunny. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Great Egg-spectations'.}","Go back to the Egg Plant.","Complete the actions in the order listed. Be careful to completely finish the dialogue at each station before moving on to the next station. Interrupting the dialogue will require you to repeat the step.\n  - Mix chocolate at the mixing station.\n  - Mould chocolate at the moulding station.\n  - Foil chocolate at the foiling station. {Chat: any}","Return to the Easter Bunny. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Great Egg-spectations'. > any}"],"t":"Creating the chocolate"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to the Lumbridge Market.","Talk to Cocoa Bunny while standing just north of the bank chest. {Chat: 1 > 1}","A cutscene ensues. Give the right samples to the patrons based on what they ask for. {Chat: 2 Offer fruit and nut chocolate. > 2 Offer a sample with less dried grapes in it. > 1 Offer banoffee chocolate.}","Return to the Blooming Burrow.","Talk to the Easter Bunny. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Great Egg-spectations'.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Handing out the chocolate samples"}]},"Grim Tales":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Sylas south of Taverley (north of the Witch's house). {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head up the east side of White Wolf Mountain near the Burthorpe mine entrance and talk to Grimgnash. {Chat: 1 I heard you were a great and mighty Griffin! > 1 There once was graveyard filled with undead. > 2 There lived a skeleton named Skullrot. > 4 Skullrot was insane! > 4 Skullrot hungrily grabbed the gnome's hair. > 3 Started to strangle the poor gnome. > Any}","Once he is sleeping, take a Feather from next to the nest.","Go back to Sylas and talk to him.}}"],"t":"Grimgnash"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the tower directly south-east of Goblin Village.","Go around the south-east side, climb over the crumbling wall, and talk into the drainpipe.","Talk into the drainpipe again. {Chat: 2 I could try and climb up > 2 Is there anything up there that can help?}","Climb up Rupert's beard.","Talk to Rupert.","Right-click climb down Rupert.","Talk to Miazrqa, located over the crumbling wall and to the north of the tower. {Chat: 4 Your second-cousin, twice removed? > 4 I need a key for the house. > 4 I should be off, I think.}"],"t":"Rupert"},{"n":"2 tarromin potions (unfinished) (2 vials of water and 2 clean tarromin)","r":"","s":["Head to the Witch's house south of Taverley, the building next to Sylas.","Open the main door.\n  - Look under the Potted plant to the left of the main door of the witch's house to obtain a key if not given by the princess.","Climb down stairs (cellar bulkhead) and search the crate near the piano for leather gloves. You may need to search multiple times.","Whilst wearing the leather gloves, open the gate and search the Music stand.","Play the piano in the first room (refer to the music sheet pictured right).\n  - The notes \"EFEDC\" are played on the right hand (upper) side and the notes \"AEGA\" are played on the left hand (lower) side.","Right-click Search the now-opened piano.","Make two shrink-me-quick potions.\n  - Combine vial of water and clean tarromin.\n  - Add shrunk ogleroot.\n  - Repeat.","Go upstairs and head into the small room leading to the garden.","Drink one of the potions next to the mouse hole and glyph.","While in the mouse hole, follow these directions:\n  - Run north past the first mouse, find the set of the nails on the eastern wall and climb up them.\n  - Go south-west, and climb up the nails on the northern wall.\n  - Climb up the nails on the south wall in the room.\n  - Run to the north-east corner, and climb down the nails on the eastern wall.\n  - Run north, and climb up the nails on the eastern wall.\n  - Pickup the pendant at the end of the next hallway.","After taking Miazrqa's pendant, leave the mouse hole either by teleporting to Taverley, or Home teleport to Falador, or going back through the entrance.","Talk to Miazrqa.","Talk to Rupert to get Rupert's helmet.","If you need another shrunken ogleroot, you can kill an Experiment No. 2 down the manhole near the entrance to the witch's house, or pick one up from the pile in the room with the experiments.}}"],"t":"The pendant"},{"n":"Watering can (with water), do not have any pets following or in the backpack.","r":"","s":["Talk to Sylas.","Plant the magic beans in the Farming patch next to Sylas and water it using a watering can.","Climb the beanstalk and kill Glod.","Take the golden goblin, climb down the stalk on southern sides and give it to Sylas.","Right-click Use the other shrinking potion on the beanstalk.\n  - Careful not to drink it!","Chop the beanstalk.","Talk to Sylas.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The beanstalk"}]},"Guilded Eggstravaganza":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Easter Bunny in the Lumbridge Crater to start the quest. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Guilded Eggstravaganza'... (Quest) > Accept}"],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Cooks' Guild Apprentice, just north of the Easter Bunny. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Make the Cake of pies on the Cooks' Guild range. {Chat: 1 Yes.}\n  - Bring an uncooked redberry pie, uncooked meat pie, and an uncooked apple pie.","Talk to the Cooks' Guild Apprentice. {Chat: 1 Here is the cake of pies.}","Make a Lemon pie.\n  - Take a Luxury lemon from the crate.\n  - Create an Uncooked lemon pie by using the Luxury lemon on a pie shell.\n  - Cook the Uncooked lemon pie on the Cooks' Guild range.","Talk to the Cooks' Guild Apprentice. {Chat: 1 Here is the lemon pie.}"],"t":"Cooking"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Crafting Guild Apprentice, west of the Cooks' Guild Apprentice. {Chat: 1 Yes. > Any > 2 Let's do it!}","Fill your empty pot with salt from the Barrel of salt by the Cooks' Guild Apprentice and head back to talk to the Crafting Guild Apprentice.","Heat the gold and pot of salt twice at the Crafting Guild's Furnace.{Chat: 1 Heat the gold. > 1 It needs to be hotter. > 2 That'll do.}","Talk to the Crafting Guild Apprentice.","Fill your bucket with vinegar from the Barrel of Vinegar by the Cooks' Guild Journeywoman.","Talk to the Crafting Guild Apprentice.","Paint the egg at the Crafting Guild's Workbench nearby.","Talk to the Crafting Guild Apprentice.","Use the Bag of flawless gems on the Unadorned imperial egg.","Talk to the Crafting Guild Apprentice."],"t":"Crafting"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Fishing Guild Apprentice, south of the Cooks' Guild Apprentice.","Talk to Ames the Courtier. He can be found northwest by the furnace.","Get a Beautiful bucket of flowers.\n  - Go to the Lumbridge General Store.\n  - Talk to the Shopkeeper. {Chat: 1 Ask about flowers for Easter. > 1 Yes}","Talk to Ames the Courtier.","Talk to the Fishing Guild Apprentice."],"t":"Fishing"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Easter Bunny. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Guilded Eggstravaganza'... (Quest) > ~}"],"t":"Finishing the egg"}]},"Gunnar's Ground":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Dororan near the eastern entrance to Barbarian Village. {Chat: Any > 1 Yes > Any > 2 Get to the point. > 1 There must be something you can do. > Accept}","You will receive a scroll containing a love poem, go to Edgeville and speak to Jeffery near the furnace. {Chat: 1 I'm here about a gold ring. > 1 I was hoping you would trade me a gold ring. > 1 This splendid love poem. > 1 Yes, he did. > 1 Just a plain, gold ring.}","Take the gold ring back to Dororan. {Chat: 1 What do you want me to engrave? > 2 That sounds simple enough.}","Click the 'engrave' option on the ring (tool belt chisel works), and show it to Dororan. {Chat: 1 It's come out perfectly. > 1 Of course. > 1 Very well.}"],"t":"Getting the ring"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Gudrun (west of Dororan), but avoid telling her that Dororan is a dwarf. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 The ring isn't from me! > 1 A great poet. > 1 So, you want me to talk to your father?}","Talk to Gunthor, found in the longhall. {Chat: 1 I need to speak with you, chieftain. > 1 Your daughter seeks permission to court an outlander. > 1 You're barbarians > 1 Please wait a moment. > 1 I'm going!}","Return and talk to Gudrun. {Chat: 2 What should we do now?}"],"t":"Promoting the courtship"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Dororan. {Chat: 1 No, she liked the ring. > 2 What are we going to do?}","Help him with his poem. {Chat: 1 I'm sure that's not true. > Any > 5 More words > 3 Stray. > Any > 5 More words > 2 Threat. > Any > 5 More words > 3 Swept to war.}\n  - The phrases are \"stray\", \"threat\", and \"swept to war\"."],"t":"The poem"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Give the poem to Gudrun to read to her father. {Chat: Any > Any > Any > Any > Any}","Talk to Gudrun again to complete the quest.{Chat: Any}"],"t":"Sending the poem"}]},"Guys and Dolls":{"sections":[{"n":"Red dye, blue dye, green dye, purple dye, and an ancient torso or a muspah spine","r":"","s":["Talk to Guy at the bonfire in Harvest Hollow. {Chat: Accept}","Talk to Dolly on the southern docks of City of Um, just east of Buried Bargains.","Talk to Guy at the bonfire.","Talk to Doyle on the western side of Harvest Hollow.","Deposit at the harvest cart next to Doyle.","Talk to Doyle. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Guy at the bonfire.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Walkthrough"}]},"Harbinger (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"food}}{{Checklis","s":["Speak to Navigator Jemi on Cyclosis (if you have just completed the Eye for an Eye miniquest you may need to relog for the chat option to show up). {Chat: 1 Harbinger miniquest. > Accept}","Travel to Tuai Leit. {Chat: Any > Any > Any}","Survive for 2 minutes. The player can simply stand there and wait.\n  - Repairing the hull is unnecessary as the damage dealt by the cannonballs is not enough to sink the ship in 2 minutes and Bosun Higgs repairs most of the damages for you.\n  - White rings will indicate where the cannonballs will hit the ship. To reduce the need for food, move your character to avoid the incoming cannonballs.","Talk to Navigator Jemi to finish."],"t":"Tuai Leit"}]},"Haunted Mine":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to the Zealot, north of the mine west of Burgh de Rott. {Chat: 1 I follow the path of Saradomin. > 1 I come seeking challenges and quests. > Accept > 1 Is there any other way into the mines? > 3 Can I borrow your key?}","Pickpocket Zealot to get Zealot's key.","Climb over the cart to the south and crawl-down the cart tunnel."],"t":"Saradominist Zealot"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Run directly west through the cave and crawl-through the cart tunnel.","Re-enter the cave via the southern entrance.","Descend the nearby ladder to the east.","Go down the ladder directly east.","Go down the south ladder (beware of the moving cart — follow it as it moves south and step off the track when you can)."],"t":"Navigating the cave"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pick a glowing fungus (J).","Use the glowing fungus on the mine cart (K).","Check points settings (L).","Compare your tracks to the correct version (pictured in bright red). Remember the letters where the track needs to be changed. Pull the levers at (M) and (N) so that the bright red arrows match. (You can also examine the levers to find the corresponding letter).}} File:ABCDE Map.png|East set of levers (M) File:FGHIJK Map.png|North set of levers (N) {{Checklist|","Return to (L) and check points settings. Click start.","If you fail and manage to put the mine cart in water, you will need to pick another glowing fungus to put into the mine cart.","Your character will say \"I wonder if that cart is anywhere useful now?\" when the puzzle is complete.","Make your way back to the very first cave room, by backtracking or teleporting out and coming back.\n  - You can use the Drakan's medallion or games necklace for quicker access if you have it, to teleport to Burgh de Rott. Otherwise continue with the instructions in this section.\n  - Go up the ladder by the glowing fungus spawn.\n  - Go north past the haunted cart, then the first wing east, climb up the ladder.\n  - Go west, climb up the ladder.\n  - Go west and exit the cave.\n  - Enter the northern cave.","Go down the nearby ladder, just to the east.","Go north-east and down the ladder by the doors.","Go west and down the ladder in the north-west corner.","Search the cart just south to get the fungus. {Chat: 1 Take it.}"],"t":"Glowing mushrooms"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["With the fungus, go back up the ladder.","Run east, go past the ladder going up, and go down the ladder (beware of the moving cart).","Run south (on the east path when it splits) and use Zealot's Key on water valve (P).","Go down the lift directly south of the water valve.","You should fall into a chamber full of water. From the flooded chamber, walk south onto the track and follow it to the east. Walk down the stairs.","Go directly west and through the door.","Try to pick up the innocent looking key to the west, sitting on the crate just north of the crane.","Kill Treus Dayth.","Pick up the key.\n  - Optional: Add it to the steel key ring if you have it."],"t":"Treus Dayth fight"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Walk up the stairs you came from (in the east room).","Walk down the stairs to the far west.","Open the large door.","Cut a piece of crystal outcrop.","Quest complete!\n  - [Optional] If you want extra salve amulets you can mine multiple crystals.\n  - [Optional] First mine a mithril ore vein to the near the large doors on cave level 2 for an achievement.\n    - You can get there by backtracking. Up the lift, then up the ladder to the north, then up the ladder to the north again. Through both large doors to the West and the vein is immediately north."],"t":"Getting the crystal"}]},"Hazeel Cult":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ceril Carnillean, located in his house to the immediate south of the East Ardougne castle. {Chat: 1 What's wrong? > Accept}","Exit his house and make your way to the south side of it.","There are five valves that must be turned, complete them on the way to the cave to save time later:\n  - Valve 2 is directly behind the Carnilleans' house. Turn it right.\n  - Valve 1 is west of the clock tower, just across the bridge. Turn it right.\n  - Valve 3 is north of the cave, east of the clock tower. Turn it left.\n  - Valve 4 is just south of Ardougne Zoo's penguin cage. Turn it right.\n  - Valve 5 is south-east of the fourth valve, near Brother Cedric. Turn it right.","Enter the cave entrance that is south of valve 3.","Pick a side and follow the guide for the according side.}}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Board the raft.","Go south and talk to Alomone, and then kill him.","Pick up the Carnillean armour he drops.\n  - To get a second piece of armour, kill Alomone again. (You may have to drop the armour before killing Alomone.)\n  - Before talking to Ceril to turn in the quest, drop one on the floor, he will take any you have in the backpack. If you bank it, it will be gone after.","Return to Carnilleans' house and talk to Ceril.","You will get a kind of \"Quest Complete!\" notification, but there is one more step.","Go upstairs and search the wardrobe in the eastern room, on the southern wall.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Carnillean's Side"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the basement of Ceril's house and use the bottle of poison on the range.","Talk to one of the Carnilleans.","Return to the cave entrance.","Board the raft.","Go south and talk to Alomone.","Return to the Carnilleans' house.","Search the crates in the basement for a chest key.","Exit the basement by heading up the ladder, and go upstairs.","Knock on the odd wall which is the north wall in the north-west room.","Climb the ladder and unlock the chest to get the Hazeel scroll.","Return to Alomone and talk to him to give him the scroll. A cutscene will play.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The Cult's Side"}]},"Head of the Family (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"15 fish oil, 5 bamboo, and 450 chimes}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["Talk to the Waiko moai on the hill north-east of Waiko (if you have just completed Impressing the Locals you may need to relog for the chat options to appear). {Chat: Accept > 1 Hello. Who are you? > 4 Farewell.}","Charter a ship to Aminishi (Use Quartermaster Gully).","Run north along the west coast and talk to Aminishi moai.","Sail back to Waiko and talk to Rosie in the north-west section of the marketplace. Don't buy any supplies.","Run south-east past the bamboo stalks and talk to Yuehanxun the Dealer. Confirm the payment of 15 fish oil.","Sail to Whale's Maw and on the north-west coast, talk to Sea Witch Kaula. {Chat: 3 Tell me of the moai that travelled on water.}","Return to Rosie for a soil bag. Don't buy any supplies.","Sail to Aminishi and fill the bag on the beach.","Return to Rosie (with filled bag, 5 bamboo, and 150 chimes) and confirm the payment. Don't buy any supplies.","Sail to Aminishi, run east and talk to Cap'n Ekahi. Confirm the payment of 300 chimes.","Talk to Aminishi moai, north of your ship."],"t":"Moai transport"},{"n":"combat gear for a fight scaled to your combat level","r":"food & potions}}{{Checklis","s":["Travel by the Rowboat next to Cap'n Ekahi on Aminishi.","Enable deflect Melee and defeat the 3 cyclopes. There is a safespot behind the mast.","Return to Waiko moai where you started the quest.","Miniquest complete!"],"t":"An eye for an eye"}]},"Heart of Stone":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Dismiss any followers now. If you recently completed Carnillean Rising, you might have to re-log to start the quest.","Interact with Xenia at the Wizards' Tower entrance south of Draynor Village. {Chat: Accept}","End their fight. {Chat: Any > Any}","On the east side of the Wizards' Tower (outside, near the water), talk to Ariane. {Chat: 1 Okay, I'll talk to Kipple.}","Talk to Kipple. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 2 No}","Solve the puzzle.","Dismiss any followers now.","Talk to Kipple and note the location he tells you. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Tracking down Xenia"},{"n":"Combat equipment (Ranged, Magic, or Necromancy is advised)","r":"Food, amulet of glory to teleport to Karamja","s":["Head to the Karamja Volcano.\n  - Kipple will appear near the entrance.","Right-click open tracker with Kipple to solve the puzzle.","Enter the portal.","Kill attendants while avoiding the fires until the green bar at the top fills up (takes about 5 minutes).","Talk to FulKra. {Chat: 1 Why was Xenia here? > 1 No, it's not right. > 4 I've got no further questions.}","Talk to Kipple. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Karamja Volcano: Ful"},{"n":"","r":"Law altar teleport, food may be required for low-level players","s":["Travel to the north half of Entrana, east of the dungeon entrance.\n  - A quick way to get there is using the law altar teleport. No weapons or armour are allowed on the island.","Right-click open tracker with Kipple to solve the puzzle.","Enter the portal and open the Bik door.","Equip a weapon (three basic weapons are provided) and kill the attendants while staying close to Kipple.\n  - Kipple needs to grab 3 unstable attendants.","Once Kipple has placed 3 unstable attendants by the door, light them. NOTE - There is a bug where sometimes you light them and nothing happens. If this happens leave out the portal and come back in.","Talk to BikKra. {Chat: 1 What was Xenia doing? > 2 I am sorry mighty one, I'll explain. > 1 They could be useful. > 4 I don't care > 4 I have no more questions.}","Talk to Kipple. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Solve the puzzle."],"t":"Entrana: Bik"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to Taverley and climb up White Wolf Mountain.","Right-click open tracker with Kipple to solve the puzzle.","Enter the portal.","Click the circuit nodes until you match the power.\n  - Each circuit node outputs a certain amount of power, but some nodes will consume more power than they generate, causing your total units to decrease instead.\n  - The white spires will redirect power to its other pair.\n  - You need to match the number of power units by activating or deactivating the correct nodes.","Talk to WenKra. {Chat: 1 I am not TokHaar. > 1 What was Xenia doing? > 1 Yes, it should be available to all. > 4 I have no more questions.}","Talk to Kipple. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"White Wolf Mountain: Wen"},{"n":"20 free inventory slots","r":"Desert heat survival gear such as an enchanted water tiara or waterskins. Completing the Crocodile Tears quest grants immunity against desert heat.","s":["Head east of Sophanem, south of the agility pyramid.","Right-click open tracker with Kipple to solve the puzzle.","Head south and enter the portal.","Search any shelf.","Combine the following (right-click use):\n  - Correction with Transition\n  - Dispersal with Arrival\n  - Evolution with Imprinting\n  - Predator with Focus\n  - Conflict with Condemnation","Combine Ariane and the Golem and Golem and I.","Use the 4 combinations on JasKra.","Talk to JasKra. {Chat: 2 Because power corrupts.}","Talk to Kipple. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Sophanem: Jas"},{"n":"Combat equipment (Magic is recommended) and food","r":"Air spells","s":["Head to the Lumbridge cemetery, south of the church.","Enter the portal for a cutscene. {Chat: Any > Any > Any}","Defeat the boss. The boss can hit up to 2,900 damage. Do not attack the prehistoric abyssal yet, avoid his energy balls. Keep running around the cave until Kipple finds the correct spot.\n  - Destroy 3 abyssal anchors in total.\n  - Watch the cutscene.\n  - Kill the prehistoric abyssal as normal.","Talk to Ariane.","Quest complete!","Optional: Talk to Ariane back at the Old Tower to complete the Nano to Kipple, Come in Kipple achievement."],"t":"Confronting Xenia"}]},"Hearts of Sanguine":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Adam in his house in Wendlewick, north of the well. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hearts of Sanguine'. > Accept}","Go north-east into the Highweald Forest and talk to Raz in her cabin at the bottom of the river. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hearts of Sanguine'.}","Go north along the east side of the river and inspect the dead bear.","Talk to Raz. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hearts of Sanguine'.}"],"t":"Creepy behind"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Bartender Gefen inside the Burnt Lobster Tavern south-east of the Wendlewick lodestone. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hearts of Sanguine'.}","Buy a Wendlewick ale from the bartender.","Talk to Matthew. He is sitting alone at the table in the north-western corner of the tavern. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hearts of Sanguine'} Give him a Wendlewick ale. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Miriam, the musician outside.","Talk to Jacob, sitting alone outside. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hearts of Sanguine'.}","Talk to Bartender Gefen. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hearts of Sanguine'.}","Go back and talk to Adam. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hearts of Sanguine'.}"],"t":"Local gossip"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go south-east to the Eastfold Farm (further south-east than the Marigold Farm) and talk to Farmer Rachel. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hearts of Sanguine'.}","Investigate the bloodsplatter to the north at the broken fence.","Follow the blood trail to the north-east and enter the cave entrance.","Talk to Anya. {Chat: 4 What are we dealing with? (Continue Quest) > 2 What do I need to do? (Continue Quest)}","Teleport to the Wendlewick lodestone, go to the floor 2 of the lighthouse, and talk to Esther. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hearts of Sanguine'. > 2 (Continue Quest)}\n  - Be sure to finish the second set of dialogue with Esther before continuing."],"t":"To the farm"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go south-east, then west up the hill and pick the poppies next to the stone structure at the top to obtain a Wendlewick poppy.","To the south-west of the Shrine of Inanna, near the jackalope burrows, kill a hedgehog and pick up the hedgehog spines.","East of the shrine, pick the wolf's tongue mushrooms near the fairy ring to obtain wolf's tongue.","Return to Esther. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hearts of Sanguine'.}","Take a vial from the vial cabinet.","Fill it with oil from the vat of oil.","Sterilise the vial of oil at the fireplace.","Take hedgehog spines from the bucket of hedgehog spines, grind them, and mix the crushed hedgehog spines with the vial of oil (s).","Take a Wendlewick poppy from the sack of flowers, press it on the table, and mix the pressed Wendlewick poppy with the vial of oil (crushed hedgehog spine).","Take wolf's tongue from the sack of mushrooms, weigh out 30g on the desk, and mix the wolf's tongue (30g) with the vial of oil (crushed hedgehog spine, pressed Wendlewick poppy).","You should now have antisanguine.\n  - If at any point you have a black ruined potion, repeat the process from the beginning.","Talk to Esther. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hearts of Sanguine'.}","Go to the lake south of the Shrine of Inanna and test antisanguine on the hedgehog (only the non-attackable hedgehog in this area will work).\n  - Kill it.","Go to the other side of the spring-fed pond (on the east side of the stepping stones) and test antisanguine on the duck.","Go north-east and test antisanguine on the badger."],"t":"Gathering ingredients"},{"n":"10 copper ore and 10 tin ore (un-noted), or 20 free inventory spots","r":"","s":["Go back to Wendlewick and talk to Liat inside the smithy to the east. If someone left the door open, she may wander outside.","Go to the Highweald Forest mine (head directly north from the smithy) and talk to Gidon.\n  - Mine 10 copper ores and 10 tin ores if you don't have any.","Return to Wendlewick and give Liat 10 copper ores and 10 tin ores, both need to be un-noted.","Return to the mine and enter the cave entrance.","Talk to Gidon.","Mine 4 havensilver ore.","Return and talk to Liat.","Smelt the ores at the furnace into havensilver bars.","Smith them at the forge and anvil into a havensilver greatsword."],"t":"Getting a havensilver weapon"},{"n":"Havensilver greatsword and antisanguine","r":"","s":["Equip the Havensilver greatsword.\n  - Unequip armour that decreases melee accuracy (e.g. necromancy armour) or use melee armour.","Return to the Blighted Cave east of the Marigold Farm and talk to Anya outside of it. {Chat: Any}\n  - Canoe station option 2 is a nearby quick travel spot to the cave.","Enter the cave, drink the antisanguine.\n  - You may reclaim it from Anya.","Attack the Sanguine heart.\n  - It will spawn sanguine tumours 3 times during the fight which will make the heart immune to damage until they are destroyed.\n  - It will periodically launch an exploding pustule to the tile you are standing on, you need to move before it explodes to avoid damage and removal of antisanguine protection effect.\n  - It may be beneficial to take additional doses of antisanguine during the fight if damaged.\n  - Death here is safe, placing you outside the cave.","Once the heart reaches 1 life point, attack it again.","Leave the cave exit and talk to Anya again. {Chat: Any}","Return to Wendlewick and talk to Adam. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hearts of Sanguine'.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Fight"}]},"Heartstealer":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Caelyn upstairs in the house directly north of Edgeville bank. {Chat: 2 I'm listening... > 1 What do you need? > Accept > 1 Let's get the disguises. > 3 I'm on it.}","Go to Thessalia's Fine Clothes in Varrock and talk to Thessalia to receive masquerade masks. {Chat: 1 Talk about Heartstealer.}","Return to Caelyn. {Chat: 2 Let's create some Smoke bombs. > 1 I'm ready.}","Click the interactable objects in the room. After failing, lower the difficulty setting by speaking with her. {Chat: 3 That was tougher than I expected. > 1 Yes. > 1 I'm ready.}","Follow Caelyn's instructions / the arrows to click on the areas of the room to make the smoke bombs.","Finish the dialogue with Caelyn to receive paper and crayons. {Chat: 3 I'll get started on that.}","Head to the Varrock Museum and pickpocket Curator Haig Halen. {Chat: Any}","Return to Caelyn."],"t":"Preparations of the heist"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the Varrock Museum and talk to Caelyn outside. {Chat: 1 Give her a pep talk. > 1 Yes}","Wear the Scarlet Thief's mask and talk to Caelyn again. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","After a cutscene, attempt to walk-down the stairs, then climb-up the staircase to the east. {Chat: Any}","Talk to the Drunken Dwarf to the south.","Talk to the Bartender downstairs to get 1 drink token.","Pickpocket an attendee south-west for 1 drink token.","Talk to the masked woman to the west upstairs and accept the dance off. {Chat: 3 We accept.}","After the cutscene, talk to the masked woman again to get the 1 drink token.","Talk to Mr Mordaut, the dragon.","Go downstairs and search the crate next to the Bartender to get a cheese tray.","Go upstairs and talk to Mr Mordaut again for the last drink token.","Talk to the Drunken Dwarf. {Chat: 1 Start the distraction.}","After another cutscene, go down to the basement.","Avoid the guards, following the wires on the ground to find the levers.\n  - There is one lever in each of the north, east and western rooms. Avoid the guards by blocking their line of sight with objects where possible.\n    - North: Avoid the guards and hide in the crate (halfway along the back wall) to avoid the guard.\n    - East: Hide in the crate (Halfway along the eastern wall) to avoid the guard.\n    - West: Notice the walking pattern of each guard. Then walk directly behind the guards along their route waiting for when they turn away to move.","Pull the three levers.","Open the display case.","After a cutscene, take from the display case. {Chat: Any}","Talk to Caelyn. {Chat: 1 What a twist! > 1 That's so sweet. > 2 Is this all?}","Continue dialogue with Caelyn. {Chat: Any}"],"t":"The heist"}]},"Helping Laniakea (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Laniakea at either base camp on Anachronia or the south-eastern part of the island (using Slayer cape). {Chat: 3 Let's talk about you. > 4 Tell me about your poisons. > 1 I'll help you out. > Accept}","Collect the following items (can be quickly collected in order by following the agility course anticlockwise, see pictures below):\n  - Old spring by searching crates next to The Stormbreaker.\n    - Use archaeology journal to teleport to the Archaeology Campus and run north-east to The Stormbreaker and board it\n  - A shimmering feather from the strange bird that can be found on the southern (middle) peninsula of the island.\n    - This is also a short run from the Moksha ritual site\n  - Collect a block of stone by investigating a rock south of Laniakea's second location, at the south-eastern part of the island.\n    - Use the Grouping System to teleport to Raksha under the \"Boss Fights\" tab and exit the stairway to the west\n    - Teleport to Xolo City archaeology site from base camp\n    - Use the Slayer cape to teleport to Laniakea\n  - A jungle vine, found by investigating the dense jungle vines north-west and across the river from the eastern most overgrown idol in the north-eastern corner of the island. It cannot be obtained from the nearby overgrown idols.\n  - Ancient arbuck, found by investigating the strange foliage east of the entrance to the Herby Werby D&D.\n    - Combine it with raw arcane apoterrasaur meat to obtain herby meat.","Collect an immaculate jungle stick by doing the following:\n  - Bring the block of stone (collected above) talk to either Eliza or Alpheus in order to get a dirty stick.\n  - Wash the dirty stick in the mucky water next to Eliza and Alpheus to get the immaculate jungle stick."],"t":"Embarking on an adventure"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Create a custom jungle fishing rod by combining the immaculate jungle stick with the jungle vine.","Create a custom fishing lure by combining herby meat, the shimmering feather, and the old spring.","Go to the strange fishing spot found on the west side of the island (see the picture below) and fish for fugu. The pathway that leads to the fishing spot is by the cannibal jadinkos. The exact fishing spot is north of the luminous snaggler area. The fishing spot can be reached from the luminous snaggler area.","Return to Laniakea and give her the fugu."],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Hermit Permits":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Read the Village Noticeboard in Wendlewick, just north of the pub. {Chat: 4 HELP NEEDED! Crabs running amok. > Accept}","Talk to Grocer Hannah in the Wendlewick food shop, east of the bank. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hermit Permits'. > Any > 1 I could try herding them out? > 2 What if I threatened them? > 3 I could just kill them all.}","Talk to Shelly, the crab in the store.","Follow the crab, talking to it every time it stops.","Enter the cave to the east and talk to Hermit inside to the north-west.","Kill one of the crabs for a fresh crab claw, craft it into an crab amulet (unstrung), and use it on a ball of wool to make a crab amulet.","Talk to Hermit again. {Chat: Any}","Equip the crabulet and talk to Shelly.","Return to Wendlewick, go back to the food shop, and talk to Shelly.","South of the Shrine of Inanna, go to the beach and talk to any of the crabs (Finn, Sandy, or Kai).\n  - (Optional) Travel via the canoe station {Chat: 3 Wendlewick (Grotto)} on the dock next to the Burnt Lobster Tavern and then go south-west.","Return to Wendlewick and talk to Adam (in the northern building). {Chat: ? Talk about 'Hermit Permits'.}","Talk to Zeke in the building to the east. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hermit Permits'.}","Talk to Esther upstairs in the lighthouse. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hermit Permits'.}","Talk to 5 different villagers around Wendlewick to get them to sign the planning permission form. The shop and stall owners work for this. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Hermit Permits'.}","Talk to either Adam, Esther, or Zeke again. {Chat: # Talk about 'Hermit Permits'.}","Go back to the southern beach and talk to one of the crab leaders.\n  - Seaweed can be collected to the west on the same beach.\n  - You also need to bring 3 ropes. If you have the Lorehound pet quest supplies track unlocked you can obtain from there.","Build the three piles of driftwood on the beach into their huts.","Talk to Finn, Sandy, or Kai.","Quest complete!}}"],"t":"Walkthrough"}]},"Hero's Welcome":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"An enchanted lyre or Fremennik sea boots 4","s":["Talk to Freya Lune or Alfrick the Planner near Rellekka docks. {Chat: Any > Any > Accept}","Talk to the following people about \"V\":\n  - Yrsa in the clothes shop nearby. {Chat: 1 Can I ask you about V?}\n  - Peer the Seer who is south-west of the marketplace. {Chat: 1 Can I ask you about V?}\n  - Swensen the Navigator who is in the house south of the marketplace.\n  - Sigmund The Merchant in the middle of the marketplace. {Chat: 1 Can I ask you about V?}\n  - Brundt the Chieftain in the main hall. {Chat: 1 Can I ask you about V?}\n  - Manni the Reveller, also in the hall. {Chat: 1 Can I ask you about V?}\n  - Olaf the Bard, east of the hall. {Chat: 1 Can I ask you about V?}","Return to Alfrick or Freya, right-click celebrate with them.","Watch the cutscene. {Chat: any}"],"t":"Welcoming V"},{"n":"2 backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Return to Alfrick at the docks. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Enter cave entrance and talk to V. {Chat: any > 1 Why can't you do it yourself? > 4 I need to get moving.}","Exit the cave.","Investigate 5 locations on the island. There are 2 of each location that you must pair up:\n  - 2 old docks. (One to the south of the island and one to the east)\n  - 2 fishing boats. (One to the east of the island and one to the west; the western boat is located on land not in the water)\n  - 2 gnarled trees. (One to the south-west of the island and one to the north-west)\n  - 2 cave entrances. (The trapdoors, not the cave you went in earlier) (One in the middle of the island and one to the south-east)\n  - 2 rock formations. (One to the north of the island and one to the north-west)","Return to V in the cave.","After the cutscene, pass the door into the north room.","Search the belongings to the east of the door (south-east corner of the room) and read the journal.","Solve the map fragments."],"t":"Scavenging for energy"},{"n":"Soft clay and a mithril bar.","r":"An antifire or super antifire potion, combat equipment to fight a dragon, and either a games necklace, ring of slaying, slayer cape, or fairy ring BJQ for quick teleport.","s":["Travel to the Ancient Cavern.\n  - If using a games necklace, travel to the barbarian outpost and run south to dive into the whirl pool. Then climb-down the rough hewn steps to the north-east.","Go to the south-west corner of the cavern and climb-up the rough hewn steps.","South of Kuradal in the Ancient Cavern is an ancient door along the western wall. Try to open the door, then use your soft clay on it.","Go to the mithril dragons. (Head north, go down the rough hewn steps, then up the stairs to the north-east.) Attack a mithril dragon, then use your key mould on the dragon.","Go back south west up the rough hewn steps.","Open the ancient door with the key. {Chat: 1 Yes, I am ready.}","Kill the dragon.","After the cutscene, run west to the stepping stones.","Jump diagonally to the chest and open it, then continue north.","Don't step on any pressure plates. Push the crates out of your way (you are able to push the 2 crates in a line).\n  - Push the first eastern crate north twice.\n  - Walk around to the middle and push the two crates north twice.\n  - Push the eastern crate to the east twice, then push the northern-most crate to the west once.\n  - Push the crate to your south once, and walk to the door.","Open the eastern door and search the chest.","Read the notes and equip the dragonkin protection charm.","Enter the bottom floor of the Grotworm Lair near Port Sarim. (There's an agility shortcut from the entrance requiring level 50 Agility.)","Climb the stairs in the centre of the open area, west of the Queen Black Dragon entrance.","Defeat Tarshak, avoiding his charge attack by moving out of the way.","Talk to Phalaks. {Chat: 5 I'm done here.}"],"t":"Ancient Cavern"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take lots of high-healing food, including a full BoB if possible. Wear the Dragonkin protective charm at all times, and pray against melee during stage 2.","Defeat Abomination in the Brimhaven Dungeon in the tunnel found in the south-west corner where steel dragons are."],"t":"Final fight"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Focus on mining the 4 pillars in the room while avoiding his attacks. Surge, double surge, and bladed dive can be useful in avoiding damage from the Abomination's rotating beam of fire.\n  - His charge attacks are often not aimed at the player, meaning you don't always need to move.","When a pillar cannot be mined any more, lure a fireball attack into the pillar. Click the water pool if you get hit to cool off.","Repeat until all 4 pillars are broken.","A good strategy is to stand near the pillar and take the fireball damage, this guarantees the destruction of the pillar as long as it is no longer minable."],"t":"Stage 1"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Lure Tarshak into the falling rocks, don't stand too close yourself.","You may also attack with a regular weapon at the same time.","Once Tarshak reaches 458 life points, he will no longer take damage from falling rocks, and you must deal the final blow yourself."],"t":"Stage 2"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Watch the cutscene. {Chat: Any}","Return to Freya and Alfrick in Rellekka. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Enter the cave and pass the door.","Talk to Freya or Alfrick.","Quest complete!"],"t":"V's Island"}]},"Heroes' Quest":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Achietties outside the Heroes' Guild in Burthorpe. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"fishing rod, fishing bait, harralander potion (unfinished)","r":"dusty key (may be on the keyring)","s":["Talk to Gerrant, the fishing shop owner in Port Sarim, about lava eels. He will give you a vial of blamish snail slime. {Chat: 1 I want to find out how to catch a lava eel.}\n  - Buy a fishing rod and fishing bait from Gerrant if you don't already have them.","Use the blamish snail slime on your harralander potion (unfinished).","Use the blamish oil on your fishing rod.","Enter Taverley dungeon.","If you already have a dusty key (a steel key ring with the dusty key works), or Agility, skip the next step.","To obtain a dusty key:\n  - Use the map (pictured right) to find Velrak the explorer. He is in the southern part of the dungeon.\n  - Kill the Jailer standing by the prison and use the key he drops to get into Velrak's cell.\n  - Talk to him for the dusty key. {Chat: 1 So..do you know anywhere good to explore? > 1 Yes, please!}","Enter the area with the blue dragons, either by using your key on the locked door or by taking the Agility shortcut.","Run to the southernmost lava pool.","Catch a lava eel.","Cook the eel on a range or fire."],"t":"Lava eel"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the Phoenix Gang Hideout in south-east Varrock, down the ladder into the hideout and talk to Straven, learning the gang password from him (Gherkin).","Go to Brimhaven and talk to Alfonse the waiter in the food shop. {Chat: 2 Do you sell...gherkins?}","Go through the door and talk to Charlie the cook. {Chat: 1 I'm looking for a gherkin... > 2 I want to steal Scarface Pete's candlesticks.}","Go to the mansion entrance to the west and talk to Garv. Bribe him with 1,000 coins, or free with a ring of charos (a). {Chat: 1 OK}","Enter the front door near the guard.","Go to the north-west part of the building and open the Treasure room door with a lockpick to enter. {Chat: 1 OK}","Open the northern chest.","Search the chest to take one candlestick.","Bring the candlestick back to Straven to receive a Master Thief's Armband."],"t":"Method (Phoenix Gang)"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to south-west Varrock and talk to Katrine. {Chat: 1 How can I get a master thief's armband? > Accept}","Go to Brimhaven, to the building east of the bar {Chat: 2 Four-leafed clover} and talk to Trobert. {Chat: 1 So can you help me get Scarface Pete's candlesticks? > 1 I volunteer to undertake that mission!}","Equip your Black armour.","Enter the large mansion in the north-west part of town.","Talk to Grip. {Chat: 2 So what do my duties involve?}","Go to the north-west part of the building and open the Treasure room door with a lockpick to enter. {Chat: 1 OK}","Open the northern chest.","Search the chest to take one candlestick.","Bring the candlestick back to Katrine to receive a Master Thief's Armband. {Chat: 1 I have a candlestick now.}"],"t":"Method (Black Arm)"},{"n":"ice gloves, bank all items that cannot be taken to Entrana","r":"","s":["If you do not have ice gloves:\n  - Equip combat gear and food to kill a level 77 Ice Queen.\n  - Climb to the top of the White Wolf Mountain and enter the cave.\n  - Mine the rock slide to the east.\n  - Climb down the south ladder.\n  - Follow the tunnel south-west, then go up the ladder.\n  - Make sure your compass is pointed north and take the east ladder down.\n  - Head north and follow the long tunnel all the way round, then use the ladder at the end.\n  - Take the north ladder back down.\n  - Run north and kill the queen for her gloves.","Sail to Entrana or teleport to the law altar through the Abyss.","Equip the ice gloves.","Kill the Firebird which is located on the northern part of the island, near the law altar, and take the Entranan firebird feather it drops."],"t":"Entrana firebird feather"},{"n":"Entranan firebird feather, lava eel, master thief's armband, at least 9 open inventory slots","r":"","s":["Take the feather, eel, and armband to Achietties outside the Heroes' Guild.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Holy Grail":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to King Arthur in Camelot Castle. {Chat: 1 Tell me of this quest. > Accept}","Go to the floor 2 using the staircase and talk to Merlin. {Chat: 2 Where can I find Sir Galahad?}"],"t":"Royal hunt"},{"n":"None - any equipment banned from Entrana should be banked.","r":"","s":["Go to Entrana by talking to a Monk of Entrana. You will be asked to bank armour and weapons, which can also be done at the bank deposit box at the docks.","Speak to the high priest, who is in the main chapel of the church. {Chat: 1 What can you tell me about this place?}","Speak to the crone who appears.{Chat: 4 I will go searching.}}}"],"t":"The Fisher King"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to Seers' Village lodestone.","Talk to Galahad, located in a building west of McGrubor's Wood and east of the coal trucks. {Chat: 2 I'm on a quest to find the Holy Grail! > 3 Why did you leave?}\n  - You must speak to the crone on Entrana first, or he will not give you the holy table napkin.","Take the holy table napkin to the southern room of the top-most floor of Draynor Manor. The way to the topmost floor is by climbing the main staircase and using the ladder on the southern wall.","Pick up the two magic whistles on the table."],"t":"Another realm"},{"n":"Magic whistle, Excalibur","r":"","s":["Go to Brimhaven and blow the whistle under the wooden watchtower (refer to the map on the right).","Go north-west and defeat Black Knight Titan with Excalibur. Low levels may find it useful to safespot the Black Knight Titan with Magic, Ranged, or Necromancy and last hit him with Excalibur.","Head south along the river and talk to the fisherman by the river. {Chat: 2 Any idea how to get into the castle?}","Be sure to keep the magic whistle in your inventory from this point forward."],"t":"Black guardian"},{"n":"Magic whistle","r":"","s":["Go south-west, to the castle. Take the grail bell on the ground outside the castle and ring it.","Head upstairs using the south staircase and talk to the Fisher King. {Chat: 3 You don't look too well.}","Talk to King Arthur in Camelot Castle. Make sure you have space to receive the magic gold feather.","Teleport to the Falador lodestone.","Head north to the Goblin Village, go into the eastern house, and right-click to open the sacks to find Sir Percival. {Chat: 3 Your father wishes to speak to you.}","Return to the Fisher King's castle in his realm by blowing your whistle north west of Brimhaven (or by using Fairy ring BJR).","Go up the staircase on the east side of the castle, climb to the top floor and grab the Holy grail.","Go back to King Arthur.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Heirloom"}]},"Hopespear's Will (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Make sure you have 5 free inventory spaces.","Head to the cave entrance located just east of the Fishing Guild's entrance. Manor farm Teleport is a quick teleport nearby. Enter the cave and walk north-west until you find two goblin guards guarding the entrance to the temple.","Drink one dose of the goblin potion and climb down the stairs to the north. Do not equip anything when in goblin form.","Once in the temple, enter the crypt through the door to the north. Equip your ring of visibility and amulet of ghostspeak.\n  - If you have received the ability to see into the Shadow Realm from Sliske, you do not need to equip the ring to see Hopespear.","Speak to the Ghost. {Chat: 1 I'm [Player name] > 4 Tell me about the prophecy. > 4 Tell me more about the Chosen Commander. > 3 Tell me about the Big High War God. > 2 Why are you here? > 2 I visited Yu'Biusk. > ~ > 1 What is it? > Accept > 1 I'll do that.}}}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["For the next part, you have to kill each priest skeleton and collect its bones. Make sure to unequip everything for the whole duration of the fight.\n  - At the south-west grave, say the name {Chat: 1 Snothead} Kill Snothead.\n  - At the south-east grave, say the name {Chat: 2 Snailfeet} Kill Snailfeet.\n  - At the north-west grave, say the name {Chat: 3 Mosschin} Kill Mosschin.\n  - At the north-east grave, say the name {Chat: 4 Redeyes} Kill Redeyes.\n  - At the northern grave, say the name {Chat: 5 Strongbones} Kill Strongbones.}}"],"t":"Priests to kill"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport out and use a fairy ring to blq.","Bury all five newly acquired bones.}} Miniquest complete!"],"t":"To Yu'biusk"}]},"Horror from the Deep":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"Lighthouse Teleport or games necklace","s":["Head to the lighthouse north of the Barbarian Outpost and talk to Larrissa. {Chat: 1 With what? > 1 But how can I help? > Accept > 3 I'll see what I can do}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"60 steel nails, 2 planks, molten glass, swamp tar, 1 free inventory slot","r":"","s":["Go south to the Barbarian Outpost, pick up two planks north of the Agility course.","Enter through the gate, then go through the Obstacle pipe.","Talk to Gunnjorn. {Chat: 1 Talk about Horror from the Deep.} (Make sure to have 1 free inventory slot)","Far east of Larrissa, go to a broken bridge, just past the crystal tree.","Fix the bridge from both sides (you can cross the bridge after the first side is repaired and right-click fix the other side).","Talk to Larrissa.","Go to the floor 3 and Repair the lighting mechanism three times.","Return to Larrissa (now inside the lighthouse, floor 1)."],"t":"Preparations"},{"n":"fire rune, air rune, water rune, earth rune (a staff will not work for any of these), any smithable sword, an arrow, combat equipment","r":"","s":["Climb the iron ladder to go to the lighthouse basement.","To open the strange wall, use a fire rune, air rune, water rune, earth rune, a sword, and an arrow on it. {Chat: 1Yes > 1Yes > 1Yes > 1Yes > 1Yes > 1Yes}","Open the eastern strange wall.","Go down the ladder and talk to Jossik.","Kill the dagannoth that appears.","Talk to Jossik again, and then kill the Dagannoth mother when it appears.\n  - Strategies can be found here; note that Necromancy does not have any effect on the dagannoth mother. The below table shows her weaknesses in different forms:","Quest complete!}}"],"t":"The battle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the floor 2 of the lighthouse.","Show the rusty casket to Jossik.\n  - If you had a full inventory when defeating the Dagannoth mother, you will not receive a rusty casket. Instead, you must talk to Jossik, who will have picked it up for you.","You may now choose a book affiliated with three gods: Saradomin's Book of Wisdom, Guthix's Book of Balance or Zamorak's Book of Chaos.\n  - Be sure to choose the same book twice in a row when he asks if you are sure about your selection.}}"],"t":"The God Books"}]},"Housing of Parliament":{"sections":[{"n":"Bucket of water, 2 free backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Talk to Deryn in the owlery, north of the Haunt on the Hill in the City of Um. {Chat: Accept}","Take from the cleaning supplies (in the western corner of the owlery) a cleaning cloth. {Chat: 1 Cleaning cloth.}","Take from the cleaning supplies a scrubby brush. {Chat: 2 Brush.}","Clean up the three spots.\n  - Clean up the owl droppings (either inside or outside on the ground). Only one is clickable.\n  - Slash the cobweb (near the cleaning supplies).\n  - Brush away the dirt pile (near the southern corner on the ground)."],"t":"A lot of mess"},{"n":"1 free backpack space","r":"","s":["Talk to Deryn.","Take 6 nails from the toolbox located under the ladder, click on it 6 times.","Build both piles of planks; one is inside the owlery and the other side of the same wall, outside."],"t":"Building the troughs"},{"n":"Bucket of water","r":"","s":["Talk to Deryn.","Fill the empty trough outside."],"t":"Water trough for a nice bath"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Deryn.","Talk to either the pet shop owner in Taverley or the pet shop owner in Yanille.\n  - Buy some beetle bits from the Pet Shop if you didn't get some beforehand."],"t":"Consulting professionals"},{"n":"1 king worm, 1 piece of beetle bits, 1 of any snail meat, 1 ghostly sole or raw ghostly sole","r":"","s":["Talk to Deryn."],"t":"Taste testing"},{"n":"1 of any snail meat, 2 free backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Go to the City of Um clock tower, located east of Soul Supplies, and climb up the stairs in the eastern room.","Take from the crate of hourglasses, in the southeast corner.","Smash the hourglass that you picked up.","Use the hourglass 'sprinkles' on a snail meat for a snail with hourglass 'sprinkles'."],"t":"Some appetising sprinkles"},{"n":"Snail with hourglass 'sprinkles', 2 free backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Return to the owlery and fill the empty trough inside.","Talk to Deryn to complete the quest."],"t":"One last thing"}]},"Hunt for Red Raktuber":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Larry in the south-west of the Ardougne Zoo and agree to help. {Chat: 1 Hunt for Red Raktuber > Accept}","Go east to the south coast of Witchaven, and inspect one of the giant footprints on the western side of the southern coast.","Return to Larry for a cutscene. {Chat: 1 Hunt for Red Raktuber}"],"t":"Larry's holiday"},{"n":"Penguin suit, 8 Silk, 4 (regular) Planks and 1 Thread","r":"","s":["North-east of Rellekka (north of Fremennik lodestone), travel via the small boat to the Iceberg.","Talk to Larry. {Chat: 1 Alright, I guess so.}","North-west, investigate the avalanche.","Enter the west room, speak to KGP Interrogator. {Chat: 1 Yes, I am. > 1 My captain trusted me to deliver the message. > 2 Your captain must trust you a great deal. > 1 My captain found a greater leader. > 3 What leader could possibly be greater than the Pescaling. > 2 The sea may control your Captain, but he controls your life. > 1 He will bring unity by destroying the humans. > 3 Why not unite all penguins to The Sea, first. > 2 He's only demonstrating his impatience. > 1 Nothing can stop him > 2 If he comes to rescue you, he'll be captured. > 1 'Our sacrifice'? Only you appear to be making the sacrifice.}","Talk to captured penguin and note down the three dance emotes.","Search the crate behind you to get a conch shell, puffer, octopus, monkfish, and a ray.","Take note of which headwear the captured penguin is wearing.\n  - The fish hat will either be a puffer, octopus, monkfish, or ray fish.","Talk to Ping & Pong (who are in a room north-east from interrogation room).","Talk to the KGP Agent by the control panel to the north.","Return to Ping & Pong. {Chat: 4 Chicklings > 5 Squirrels > 1 Blue > 3 Bears > 4 Kiss > 2 Sharks > 1 Yes, that sounds great!}","Return to the KGP Agent by the control panel. Sing him the lullaby. {Chat: 2 I want to sing you a song.}","Operate the control panel. Head north-east into the war room.","Talk to any dwarf. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Speak to the dwarf again.","Exit war room to get caught.","Talk to Larry (twice). {Chat: 1 Alright, I guess so.}","Re-enter the hideout via the avalanche and return to the dwarves. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to them again and give them the supplies to get a toolbox.","Perform practice run on the engine panel north of the dwarves.\n  - Wrench -> wirebox.\n  - Wire cutter -> wirebox.\n  - Wire -> wirebox.\n  - Tape -> wirebox.\n  - Bellows -> pipe.\n  - Click bellows twice, the pressure gauge will point to the red.\n  - Turn valve wheel three times, the pressure gauge arrow points straight up in the green.\n  - Pull lever.","Talk to a dwarf again. {Chat: 2 No.}","Exit war room to get caught.","Talk to Larry. {Chat: 1 Alright, I guess so.}","North-west, talk to Noodle. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Re-enter the hideout via the avalanche. Enter first room to the east.","Navigate to the sorting table without being spotted using the picture to the right (see the full guide for more details).","Search sorting table to get a telegram. Exit the small room and ensure the door is closed before you move further.","Navigate back out of the office the way you came, without being spotted. Once back in the main hall, exit using the southern door. If you are caught you will lose the item and have to repeat the process.","Return to Larry and talk to him twice."],"t":"Penguin espionage"},{"n":"The toolbox, the fish hats, the conch shell, penguin suit","r":"","s":["Southeast of Yanille, just outside the city walls, talk to Larry. {Chat: 1 Alright, I guess so.}","Enter the penguin suit and wear the fish hat the captured penguin was wearing.","Blow the conch shell, then perform the three emotes.","Climb up the ladder and walk all the way to the east, opening doors along the way.","Talk to Captain Marlin.","Pick either honest or lie. {Chat: Any}","In the brig, walk west and search the hatstand to get an electric eel, shark tooth, crab claw, seaweed, and a swordfish.","Open the east door.","Inspect the engine panel.\n  - Crab claw -> wirebox.\n  - Shark tooth -> wirebox.\n  - Electric eel -> wirebox.\n  - Seaweed -> wirebox.\n  - Pufferfish -> pipe.\n  - Click pufferfish twice, the pressure gauge will point to the red.\n  - Octopus -> Turn valve wheel three times, the pressure gauge arrow points straight up in the green.\n  - Swordfish -> lever.\n  - Pull the lever.","Talk to Chuck towards the east side of the island to leave the island and get a cutscene.\n  - If you teleport off the island, talk to Chuck at the Ardougne Zoo to get teleported back to the Desert Island and talk to him again once there.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Disabling the Red Raktuber"}]},"Icthlarin's Little Helper":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["After returning the canopic jar and talking to the priest, you can enter the city through the front gate, so you can use the magic carpet transport system.","It is possible to get out of the city without purposely dying, finishing the quest, or using a teleport. There is a small crack in the north-eastern corner of the wall near the locust. You can re-enter the city from the secret passage north-east of where the quest started, directly north-east of the tent where the wanderer is.","2-3 filled waterskins are recommended. You will not need water within the city, and there are places to fill your water.","Wearing a lot of weight will make you die faster in the desert. Take this into account. Bring more waterskins if you are bringing a lot of armour and weapons with you.","Jumping the pit is risky. You will not always make it, even if you have 100 run energy. A higher Agility level is recommended.","The level 56 Possessed Priest and one of Apmeken, Het, Crondis or Scabaras apparition are not hard to defeat with the help of prayers.","Bring a bucket of sap to minimise running or teleporting back and forth."],"t":"General tips"},{"n":"Cat and 1,000 coins (if taking carpet)","r":"","s":["Head to the north of Sophanem. You can use the magic carpet network south of Shantay Pass from Al Kharid to get to Nardah, and then run southwest.","Talk to the wanderer while your cat is following you. {Chat: 1 Why? [Icthlarin's Little Helper] > Accept > 4 Tell me about Sophanem. [Icthlarin's Little Helper]}\n  - The wanderer is located a short distance north of Sophanem, east of the river but west of the Agility Pyramid.","Open the northern door on the southern pyramid (picture of a cat)."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["You will arrive inside a maze.","Run past the initial wall crushers and walk on the denser rubble (dotted lines indicate the locations of pitfall traps).\n  - Alternatively follow the path shown in the image to the right.","Avoid traps and aggressive monsters until you reach a pit.\n  - [Optional] Run past the wall crushers to the east and open the chest to complete Icthlarin's Little Chest.","Jump across the pit. This requires at least 20% run energy.","Open the doorway of the western room.","Solve the puzzle."],"t":"Graverobbing"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Sphinx with your cat or kitten out. {Chat: 1 I need help. > 1 Okay, that sounds fair. > 2 9. > 1 Totally positive.}","Pick up your cat and talk to the High Priest, located inside the Temple of Icthlarin in the south part of the city.","Note down the name of the canopic jar in the backpack."],"t":"Cats' help"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go back to the southern pyramid and open the door.","Go through the pyramid again. Jump across the pit and open the west doorway.","Take the jar on the ground that has the same name as the one in the backpack previously.","Kill the apparition that spawns. You can safe-spot it by using the table in the room (unless you have the canopic jar of Apmeken or Crondis).","Take the jar again.","Open the doorway to exit the room.","Open the doorway to enter the west room again.","Return the canopic jar by clicking the empty space with the lighting effect (the original location of your jar).","Exit the pyramid. Opening the doorway should automatically take you to the entrance."],"t":"Encountering the apparition"},{"n":"30 coins, willow logs, bucket of sap, salt (salt shaker, bag of salt, or an empty bucket)","r":"","s":["Talk to the High Priest. {Chat: 1 Sure, no problem.}","Talk to the embalmer at the spice shop, north-west of the temple.","Talk to the carpenter at the potter's wheel, just east of the southern pyramid. {Chat: 2 Alright, I'll get the wood for you.}","Talk to him again with willow logs in your inventory.","Talk to Raetul near the Sphinx to obtain linen.","Skip these steps if you already have salt:\n  - Bring an empty bucket just north of Sophanem to a small open lake (refer to map shown right).\n  - Collect from the salty water for a bucket of salty water.\n  - Head back inside Sophanem.\n  - Search the centre piece, located just south-east of the southern pyramid. {Chat: 1 Pour your bucket of salty water into the font.}\n  - Search the centre piece for a pile of salt. {Chat: 1 Scrape it out.}","Talk to the embalmer.","Talk to the carpenter for a holy symbol.\n  - This may take a few seconds before he finishes the symbol."],"t":"Preparing for the ceremony"},{"n":"Cat and combat equipment","r":"","s":["Enter the pyramid once again and jump over the pit.","Open the doorway of the eastern room.","Search the first sarcophagus to your immediate west, on the northern wall, and hide the unholy symbol in it. {Chat: 1 Hide the unholy symbol in this sarcophagus.}\n  - Searching other sarcophagi is optional and not recommended.","Open the doorway to exit the room.","Open the doorway to enter the eastern room again. Finish the dialogue with the High Priest and the wanderer.","Kill the Possessed Priest.","Talk to the High Priest.","Open the doorway to exit the room to return to the temple. {Chat: 1 Yes, return to the high priest in Sophanem.}\n  - You may be given the canopic jar again, which has no further use and can be dropped (it will turn to dust).","Talk to the High Priest.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Icthlarin's little helper"}]},"Imp Catcher":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Wizard Mizgog on the floor 2 of the Wizards' Tower, just southeast of the beam. {Chat: 1 Can I help you? > Accept}\n  - Make a bowl of hot water if you haven't already, by filling a bowl at a water source, then using it on a Cooking range (all available in the Lumbridge Castle kitchen - If you have not done Cook's Assistant, you can use the range in the southeasternmost house in Lumbridge, south of Bob's Axes). You may also light a fire and use a bowl of water on it.","Go to the Water ruins (west side of Lumbridge Swamp) and talk to the Phlegmatic imp. {Chat: 3 Have you tried a bowl of hot water?}\n  - Talk to the imp again, with a bowl of hot water in your inventory.\n  - Take the Phlegmatic bead it drops.","Go to the Fire ruins (north of Al Kharid; outside Het's Oasis), talk to and fight the Choleric imp.\n  - Take the Choleric bead it drops.","Go to the Earth ruins (north-east of Varrock; south of Fort Forinthry) and cheer up the Melancholic imp. {Chat: 3 Why would he be disappointed? > 2 Some days you'll have setbacks. Tomorrow is new day. > 1 Take your time. No one is rushing you to feel better.}\n  - Take the Melancholic bead it drops.","Go to the Air ruins (west of Varrock; southeast of Barbarian Village) and talk to the Sanguine imp.\n  - Race the imp around the altar 4 times by clicking and running inside the four different checkpoints when they appear.\n  - Take the Sanguine bead it drops.","Return and talk to Wizard Mizgog. {Chat: 1 I've got all four beads.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Looking for imps"}]},"Imp Catcher (historical)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["To start, go to the Wizards' Tower South of Draynor Village and talk to Wizard Mizgog on the floor 2."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill imps anywhere in RuneScape until all four beads are found, or you could buy all four beads at the Grand Exchange","Report back to Mizgog.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Obtaining the beads"}]},"Impressing the Locals":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Right click to talk to Trader Stan located at the south-eastern dock of Port Sarim. {Chat: 2 Talk about the Skulls pirate, Jed. > Accept > 1 About a quartermaster. > 2 About a navigator. > 3 About a bosun.} Finish all dialogue.","Talk to Guard Captain Roarkwin in the Port Sarim jail located to the west.","Enter the port portal near the northern dock.\n  - Ignore the dialogue about Meg which triggers after you enter the portal.","Talk to Seasinger Umi to the southeast of the portal.","Talk to the Barmaid in a building to the northwest of the portal. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Climb up the stairs and talk to Mister Gully.","Head to the pottery house in Draynor Village and climb up the stairs.","Talk to the Black Knight sergeant.","Head to Rimmington and talk to Seasinger Jemi near the well.","Back at the Port Sarim docks, talk to Trader Stan. {Chat: 2 Talk about the Skulls pirate, Jed.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Walkthrough"}]},"In Aid of the Myreque":{"sections":[{"n":"1 food, 1-5 buckets and 9 free spaces, preferably charged druid pouch so your food won't rot","r":"","s":["In the hideout behind the Canifis pub, go through the secret wall and squeeze past the stalagmite on the east side of the cave","Talk to Veliaf Hurtz. {Chat: 1 I want to join your organisation. > 3 Can you tell me about the job? > Accept > 1 Ok, I'll do the job.}","Travel to Mort'ton. The fastest way is by heading south of the cave, exiting through the doors, climbing the same tree from In Search of the Myreque and using the swamp boat south, or using a portal to the Barrows in War's Retreat.\n  - If you need a piece of food, there are snails to the west of Mort'ton that can be cooked with level 12 Cooking.","Speak to Florin, south of the bridge to Burgh de Rott, who won't let you pass yet. (Make sure to finish dialogue options)","Search the chest.","Use food on the chest.","Jump the gate.","Talk to Florin. {Chat: 4 Are there any 'out of the way' places in here? > 5 Ok, thanks!}","Climb over the broken down wall in the building just south-east of the well. It'll be near an unreachable pile of rubble that you can mine.","Mine the rubble to clear the trap door, then open the trapdoor and climb down.","Mine and use spade to remove all the rubble piles (15). Your bucket can be emptied on the pile outside the pub.\n  - 1 bucket will allow you to mine 3 piles before it needs to be emptied in the pile outside. There is a bucket next to the well if you need one.\n  - Any items left on the ground when you climb back up the ladder will be lost.","Go up and talk to any villager. {Chat: 3 I'd like to help fix up the town. > 4 Ok, thanks.}"],"t":"Burgh de Rott"},{"n":"11 planks, 10 bronze hatchets, 3 tinderboxes, 44 nails, 2 steel bars, 1 swamp paste, 1 coal and 10 raw mackerel or snails (all un-noted). A beast of burden familiar may also help out in holding all the needed supplies. A plank box may help with inventory space as well.","r":"","s":["Talk to Aurel in the general store. {Chat: 3 I'd like to help fix up the town. > 4 What should I do now? > 5 Ok, thanks.}","Climb the ladder outside and use a plank on the Broken Roof (3 planks, 12 nails required).","Climb down and use a plank on the damaged wall (3 planks, 12 nails required).","Talk to Aurel. {Chat: 4 What should I do now? > 5 Ok, thanks.}","Fill the box with supplies: 10 bronze hatchet, 3 tinderbox and 10 raw mackerel or raw snails (depending on what Aurel asked for. Check the in game quest journal if you forget).","Return the crate to Aurel.","Talk to Cornelius in the bank. {Chat: 4 What should I do now? > 5 Ok, thanks.}","Use 2 planks on the bank booth covered in broken glass while holding 1 swamp paste and 8 nails (any kind).","Use 3 planks and 12 nails on the wall behind it.","Talk to Cornelius. {Chat: 4 What should I do now? > 3 Do you fancy the job?}","Talk to any villager. {Chat: 4 What should I do now? > 5 Ok, thanks.}","Use two steel bars and a piece of coal on the furnace to the east.","Search the furnace to light it. {Chat: 1 yes}"],"t":"General store and bank"},{"n":"A silver melee weapon (silver sickle), combat equipment, food; recommended = For fight with Gadderanks: magic equipment, runes for magic attacks","r":"","s":["Talk to Gadderanks in the general store.","Talk to everyone else in the general store but Aurel.","Kill Gadderanks and the vampyres. (The vampyres can only be damaged by a silver melee weapon)","Talk to Gadderanks.","Talk to Veliaf.","Talk to Veliaf in the Canifis hideout (Take Melee Gear and Sickle). {Chat: 5 Ok, thanks.}","Dismiss your followers if you have any.","Talk to Polmafi then Radigad then Ivan.","Route 1 is generally easier:\n  - Kill the vampyres.","Enter the Mausoleum west of Canifis and talk to Drezel until he gives you a key. {Chat: 2 I found out some things about Efaritay.} then {Chat: 1 Veliaf told me about Ivandis. > 4 Is there somewhere that I might get more information about Ivandis? > 3 The lives of those pitiful few left in Morytania could rest on this!}","Use the key on the east wall, then climb the secret trapdoor.","Find and read the book titled 'The Sleeping Seven' on the westernmost middle-bookcase."],"t":"Vampyre slayer"},{"n":"Rope, water rune, cosmic rune, soft clay, cut sapphire, silver bar, mithril bar (metal bank is fine)","r":"","s":["Return to Canifis and enter the trapdoor south of the pub.","Leave the pub cellar via the south wall and smash the wooden boards on the eastern wall.","Enter and use soft clay on the tomb, then add the rod clay mould to your tool belt.","Smelt a silvthril rod at any furnace (under the Silver Casting section).","Enchant it using the Lvl-1 Enchant spell.","With a rope and the enchanted rod in your inventory, return to Drezel, located underground in the mausoleum west of Paterdomus.","Use the rod on the well in the room west of Drezel to receive the rod of ivandis.","Go back to Burgh de Rott, and go to the cellar in the pub where you previously cleared the rubble.","Talk to Veliaf. {Chat: 1 I have brought you the Rod of Ivandis! > 1 Yes, I've come to give the Rod of Ivandis to you!}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Silvthril rod"}]},"In Memory of the Myreque (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Veliaf Hurtz north of Canifis. {Chat: Accept}","Build ten statues on the statue plinths with two granite (5kg) for each statue.","Add the following items to each statue along with a blisterwood sickle.}} :{| class=\"wikitable lighttable ! Name !! Item |- | Sani Piliu || Blamish blue shell (pointed) |- | Harold Evans || Nail beast nails |- | Andiess Juip || Snakeskin body |- | Flaygian Screwte || Ivandis flail |- | Kael Forshaw || Rune armoured boots |- | Mekritus A'hara || Mort myre pear |- | Radigad Ponfit || Moonlight mead |- | Vertida Sefalatis || Blisterwood stake-thrower crossbow |- | Polmafi Ferdygris || Histories of the Hallowland |- | Safalaan Hallow || Holy water |}"],"t":"Off to Canifis"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Veliaf Hurtz."],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"In Pyre Need":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Priest of Guthix just southwest of the Piscatoris Fishing Colony (slightly north west if using fairy ring AKQ). {Chat: Accept > 4 No more questions.}","Enter the cave."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Proceed through the caves whilst cutting twigs from the trees along the way (you should collect 5 total)"],"t":"The Caves"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["In the final cave, fletch the twigs into ribbons.","Craft the pyre then light it.","Talk to the Phoenix.","Exit the cave entrance.","Talk to Brian Twitcher (Priest of Guthix).","Quest complete!"],"t":"The Phoenix Lair"}]},"In Search of the Myreque":{"sections":[{"n":"Steel weapons, 75 steel nails, druid pouch, normal planks, combat equipment","r":"","s":["Talk to Vanstrom Klause in the Hair of the Dog tavern in Canifis. {Chat: 2 Why do they need help? Are they in trouble? > 4 Perhaps I could help you out here. > 4 Yes, I'll do it! > Accept}","Make sure you finish the dialogue or the quest won't start."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Obtain a Druid pouch with at least six items in it. It is required for the section below. The Ouroboros pouch will not work.\n  - It is required to have six as Ghasts will rot the items within the pouch.\n  - If you do not have charges in your druid pouch, make sure you have prayer points to cast bless to obtain more in the swamp.\n    - You will need a Silver sickle (b) to cast bloom.","Go to Mort'ton by either running through the swamp or using the fairy ring BKR and taking the boat south-east of the fairy ring. Alternatively, use a portal at War's Retreat tuned to the Barrows Brothers for fast access."],"t":"Swamp trekking"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Cyreg Paddlehorn, before the bridge east of Mort'ton. {Chat: 2 Well, I guess they'll just die without weapons. > 2 Resourceful enough to get their own steel weapons? > 3 If you don't tell me, their deaths are on your head! > 3 What kind of a man are you to say that you don't care? > 1 Give wooden planks to Cyreg.}","Use the boat to get to the Hollows.","Go north and climb up the strange tree. Look for a bridge on the map.","Left click the bridge one step north, the bridge will break. Click it again to repair it. You can also right click and select Repair option. Repeat until the bridge is fully repaired (requires 75 steel nails and three planks).","Climb down, go just north-east to the hollow tree, and talk to Curpile Fyod. The questions are random. The answers to his question are as follows: {Chat: 1 I've come to help the Myreque. I've brought weapons.}","Open the doors on the rock behind the tree and follow the tunnel.","Squeeze-past the stalagmite at the east wall, next to the stone brazier.","Talk to Veliaf Hurtz.","Talk to all the other members, first dialogue will be enough. {Chat: 5 Ok, thanks.}","Talk to Veliaf again. Cutscene follows."],"t":"The hideout"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill the Skeleton Hellhound.","Talk to Veliaf. {Chat: 3 How do I get out of here? > 5 Ok, thanks.}","Go back into the tunnel and search the wall to the north. This unlocks the achievement I Wonder How Far It Ghost?","Climb up the ladder. (Do not Teleport to Canifis)","Talk to the stranger next to the stairs where Vanstrom was located.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"It's Snow Bother":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Santa Claus in the southern part of Christmas Village. {Chat: Accept}","Talk to the snow imp following you. {Chat: 1 It's Snow Bother quest.}","Investigate the Christmas spirit map south-east.","Create decorations at the decoration bench in Diango's Workshop to the east; you will fail."],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to the Falador lodestone.","Search the sleigh just inside Falador's northern entrance.","Search five piles of snow (show on map):\n  - By Sir Tiffy Cashien in Falador Park.\n  - North of the Estate agent's office.\n  - On the White Knights' Castle bridge.\n  - Outside Falador west bank.\n  - Inside Flynn's Mace Market.","Add decorations to the missing Christmas decorations just outside the Rising Sun pub."],"t":"Falador"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to the Lumbridge lodestone.","Search the sleigh just to the south-east.","Search five piles of snow (show on map):\n  - Inside Lumbridge Church.\n  - Inside Bob's Brilliant Axes.\n  - By the bank chest in Lumbridge Market.\n  - Inside the kitchen of the Lumbridge Castle.\n  - Inside the northern room of eastern gatehouse of the Lumbridge Castle.","Add decorations to the missing Christmas decorations just south of the Lumbridge lodestone."],"t":"Lumbridge"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Make your way to Varrock Square.","Search the sleigh near the Varrock Palace entrance.","Find the five piles of snow (show on map):\n  - Just inside Varrock Palace courtyard.\n  - Inside Zaff's Superior Spellcasting.\n  - Inside Aris' Reward Shop.\n  - Near Pelters' Veg Stall, behind Varrock General Store.\n  - Inside Horvik's Armour Shop.","Add decorations to the missing Christmas decorations in the north-eastern part of Varrock Square."],"t":"Varrock"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport back to Christmas Village.","Investigate the Christmas spirit map.","Take Santa's request next to the map.","Make five of the following deliveries:\n  - You need to check Santa's sack in your backpack and choose a character in the interface before talking to them with the sack and some backpack space."],"t":"Delivering the presents"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Santa Claus in the southern part of Christmas Village to complete the quest."],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Jed Hunter (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"Uncharted island map, combat gear & food}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["Talk to Bosun Higgs beside your ship. {Chat: 1 Jed Hunter miniquest.}","Talk to Sojobo in the centre of Waiko marketplace.","Kill 3 Gu ronin on uncharted isles.","Return to Sojobo on Waiko.","Return to Bosun Higgs with the Tetsu set. {Chat: 1 Jed Hunter miniquest.}"],"t":"Bosun Higgs"},{"n":"2 tortle shell bowls.","r":"","s":["Talk to Navigator Jemi beside your ship. {Chat: 1 Jed Hunter miniquest.}","Talk to Sea Witch Kaula on the north-western shore of Whale's Maw. {Chat: 4 Ask about communicating with the Thalassus.}\n  - You may have to speak to her twice to give her the tortle shell bowls.","Talk to Navigator Jemi while standing next to Kaula.","Go back to the ship and talk to Navigator Jemi. {Chat: 1 Jed Hunter miniquest.}"],"t":"Navigator Jemi"},{"n":"10 driftwood, 5 sea shells, 1 taijitu.","r":"","s":["Talk to Quartermaster Gully beside your ship. {Chat: 1 Jed Hunter miniquest.}","Talk to Rosie in the centre of Waiko.","Talk to Rosie again.","Deliver the buoyancy materials back to Quartermaster Gully. {Chat: 1 Jed Hunter miniquest.}"],"t":"Quartermaster Gully"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Lookout Ekahi. {Chat: 1 Jed Hunter miniquest.}","Talk to Yuehanxun the Dealer in the south-east of Waiko. She is at the last hut in the South of Waiko, north of the water barrel.","Talk to Lookout Ekahi at the boat to set sail. {Chat: 1 Jed Hunter miniquest. > 1 Yes.}","Once on the ship, talk to Lookout Ekahi again. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Once on the other ship, unlock the hold in the centre of the ship. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Finale"}]},"Jungle Potion":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Trufitus in his house located northeast of Tai Bwo Wannai. {Chat: 3 It's a nice village, but where is everyone? > 1 Me? How can I help? > Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head south-west to some marshy jungle vines (refer to map).","Search one for a grimy snake weed.\n  - Take three if you intend to do Legends' Quest and Zogre Flesh Eaters.","Clean the herb.","Talk to Trufitus to give him a clean snake weed. {Chat: 1 Of course!}"],"t":"Snake weed"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head north-east to some palm trees (refer to map).","Search one for a grimy ardrigal.\n  - Take two if you intend to do Legends' Quest.","Clean the herb.","Talk to Trufitus to give him a clean ardrigal. {Chat: 1 Of course!}"],"t":"Ardrigal"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head south of Tai Bwo Wannai to the scorched earth near two fires (refer to map labelled \"sito foil\").","Search it for a grimy sito foil.","Clean the herb.","Talk to Trufitus to give him a clean sito foil. {Chat: 1 Of course!}"],"t":"Sito foil"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head south-east to the mine.","Search the green-coloured rocks for a grimy volencia moss.","Clean the herb.","Talk to Trufitus to give him a clean volencia moss. {Chat: 1 Of course!}"],"t":"Volencia moss"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head back north near the palm trees and follow the shoreline west to some rocks (refer to map labelled \"rogue's purse\").","Search the rocks to enter the cave {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll enter the cave.} and ignore the level 57 jogres.\n  - (Optional) Kill one jogre to complete one of the easy Karamja achievements, It's a Jungle Ogre.","Search a fungus covered Cavern wall for a grimy rogue's purse.\n  - Take two if you intend to do Zogre Flesh Eaters.","Clean the herb.","Talk to Trufitus to give him a clean rogue's purse. {Chat: 1 Of course!}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Rogue's purse"}]},"Kennith's Concerns":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Kennith in the house west of the church in Witchaven (Fairy ring BLR or Cape of legends and run south). {Chat: Accept}","Climb down the Old ruin entrance to the west.","Enter the wall opening on the eastern wall immediately as you enter.","Navigate through the tunnel.\n  - Take the agility shortcut near the entrance, requiring 30 Agility.","Climb over the rocks and talk to one of the villagers.","Climb back over the rocks and a cutscene will occur.","Exit the tunnels and talk to Kennith again.","Talk to Kennith's parents, Kent and Caroline, east of the church.","Travel north to the entrance of the Legends' Guild (or teleport with Cape of legends) and talk to Kent.","Travel back to Witchaven and talk to Kimberly in the northernmost house next to Jeb and Holgart. {Chat: 1 Of course I will.}","After the cutscene, run around the house to get all four villagers to follow you. (Note: the following must be done without leaving the area, or exiting to the lobby or it must be done over!)","Trap the villagers inside the church.","Talk to Kimberly again {Chat: 2 Okay, I've locked them all up.} and follow her to Kennith's house.","Talk to Kimberly.","After the cutscene, get the villagers to follow you and trap them in the church, again.","Talk to Kimberly again {Chat: 2 Okay, I've locked them all up.}, then follow her to Ezekial Lovecraft's house.","Talk to Kimberly.","Talk to Kimberly again.","Before continuing, if you are currently under the effect of Sign of the Porter or similar buff, make sure to disable the buff.","Head back to the Old ruin entrance, through the wall opening, over the rocks.","Dismiss any active followers.","Talk to one of the villagers.","Once through the dark entrance, talk to Ezekial.","Go through the northeastern wooden door."],"t":"Return of the slugs?"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["When the three minecart villagers turn their back to you, run south to the southern wall and hide there.","Wait for the southern villager to face the barrel, then run past him to the three nooks in the eastern wall. Hide inside these nooks to remain undetected.","While the northern and southern villagers have their backs turned, prospect the wall until you find a crack (The piece of wall that will have the crack has a slightly different texture on top). Mine the wall, then enter the hole.","Run to the other side of the tunnel and pull the lever. Ezekial Lovecraft will enter the area and follow you.","Run back to the eastern side of the tunnel and open the wooden door.","Speak with Kent or Caroline."],"t":"First room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ezekial. Disable any items that would automatically bank ores, such as signs of the porter.","Open the eastern door.","Each time the villagers face and walk towards the middle is when you move.\n  - Harvest up to 2 Rubium along the Northern wall the first time they face the middle, then take cover behind the NE Wall.\n  - Harvest another 2 Rubium giving you 4 total and take cover behind a wall.\n  - Then each time the villagers face and walk towards the middle, Try to fill one Steam vent.\n    - Repeat this 4 times until the villagers pass out","Go through the wooden door."],"t":"Second room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ezekial.","A quick way to proceed to the next room is as follows:\n  - As soon as the mine-cart villagers turn their back, break through the rock in the middle of the room - hide one tile east of where the rock was.\n  - Wait for the north-eastern villager to face to the east and for the door villager to face the door, run north and mine rubium here, while walking behind the patrolling villager (4).\n  - When the door villager turns to face the door, and the southern villager is not looking, run past him to the south and put the rubium in the south-eastern vent.\n  - Wait for the door villager to face the door again, then run back to the middle and hide.\n  - When the mine-cart villagers turn their back, run to the south vent and drop the rubium in, then quickly hide in the middle.\n  - When the mine-cart villagers turn south again, run north to place the last rubium in both northern vents. They should all pass out now.","Go through the wooden door."],"t":"Third room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Katherine or Clive.","Backtrack through the rooms to the tunnel with the lever. Go through the metal door on the western side.","Talk to Kennith.","After the cutscene, talk to Kimberly to find the location of the toy train.","Return to Witchaven and find the toy train. It will be on the ground, but there will not be a red dot on the minimap. Going into game settings > Additional Options > Accessibility and turning on entity highlight will make the toy train easier to find, appearing as the color you have set for interactable items. It can be at one of the following locations:\n  - The North-East building nearest to the dock, outside the northern door, beside the fishing net.\n  - Outside the building, on the north side beside the fishing net.\n  - Near the pillar outside Mayor Hobb's house (which is on the west side).\n  - By the water (south of the town).\n  - South of the house with the well.","Return to the caves and go to the room with Kennith; use the toy train on him.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The new menace"}]},"Kili Row":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Kili by the anvils in north-eastern corner of the City of Um {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the ritual site in the City of Um","Select the Lesser ensoul material (Kili Row) with the pedestal","Complete the ritual (requires Change I glyph which requires two inkwells of regular ghostly ink and one inkwell of basic ghostly ink to draw)","Withdraw the output of the ritual from the ritual chest on the ritual site"],"t":"Lesser ensoul material ritual"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go back to Kili to get a soul urn","Kill five chickens using Necromancy anywhere or go back to the ritual site and perform a lesser communion ritual"],"t":"Soul urn"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Kili","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Kindred Spirits":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Linza in Burthorpe, near the furnaces south of the Burthorpe lodestone. {Chat: accept}","Talk to Relomia in the middle of Draynor Village. {Chat: 1 Kindred Spirits > any > any}","Talk to Linza in south-eastern Daemonheim. Dismiss any followers.\n  - (Optional) Bring some good healing food, no more than 20 pieces.","Open the trapdoor (you need at least 6 free inventory spaces) {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm ready.}","Watch the cutscene."],"t":"Mysterious disappearances"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Interact with the Dragonkin guard.","Talk to Sliske.","Talk to Sliske again. {Chat: 1 You're a better actor.}","Interact with the Dragonkin guard for some Dragonkin food.","Use the Dragonkin food on the latrine.","Use the plate on the loose brick.","Use the plate half on the brick to make a blade.","Use the blade on the barracks bed for a cloth strip.","Use the brick on the cloth strip to create a ludicrous flail.","Talk to Sliske to give him the ludicrous flail, which he will use to distract the guard.","Interact with the Dragonkin guard to steal the bag of crystals.","Talk to Sliske to get back a cloth strip.","Use the bag of crystals on the latrine to get an empty bottle.","Use the cloth strip on the empty bottle to create a bottle on a string.","Use the bottle on a string on the latrine to get a bottle of acid.","Talk to Sliske.","Use the bottle of acid on your cell door.","Talk to Sliske.","Exit through either door.","Watch the cutscene. {Chat: 1 All right Sliske, I'll do it.}"],"t":"Escaping the prison"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the fighting pit directly south.","Talk to Dharok. {Chat: 2 We need to solve this. > 2 Why not let them kill you? > 2 You are already dead.}","After Dharok dies, talk to him again.","Go north, navigate to the centre of the maze. Use the map here as reference.\n  - First choice. {Chat: 3 I think Ahrim should go left. > 1 You'd let someone else be hurt? > 2 That's no reason to hurt someone else.}\n  - Second choice. {Chat: 3 I think Ahrim should be hurt. > 1 Then suffer now so it won't be as bad later. > 3 Think about the innocents Ahrim.}\n  - Third choice. {Chat: 3 I think Ahrim should be hurt. > 2 It's more practical to hurt you. > 3 Sliske won't kill you, he wants you at the end.}\n  - Fourth choice. {Chat: 3 I think Ahrim should be hurt. > 3 Going west gets it over with faster. > 2 It's the hesitation that makes it worse. > 1 So make there be only one choice - you.}\n  - Fifth choice. {Chat: 3 I think Ahrim should be hurt. > 2 Don't be weak Ahrim. > 3 Then fight, Ahrim! > 1 You'll remember it as a moment of weakness. > 2 You're Saradomin's holy warrior.}\n  - Sixth choice. {Chat: 3 I think Ahrim should be hurt. > 1 You're pathetic Ahrim. > 3 A disappointment. > 3 ...knows he's strong enough to continue. > 2 ...Saradomin's greatest soldier.}","Watch the cutscene. {Chat: any}","Enter the impressive doorway.","Talk to Verac. {Chat: 3 I need the Saradomin key. > 1 Make the cut > 1 Reach inside > 1 Go deeper > 1 Pull harder}","Unlock the Saradomin statue.","Talk to Verac.","Pick up the 4 books in the next rooms (do not use area loot to pick up the books).","Investigate the Orrery in the larger room against the western wall. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Investigate the shadow focus in the centre.\n  - If no cutscene occurs, lobby and pick up the books again, without area loot.","Investigate the lever. {Chat: 3 Investigate the lever. > 1 Heroically}","Watch or skip the cutscene.","Escape in 120 seconds.\n  - Run to the illuminated areas and try to climb the ropes.\n  - Right-click check on the ropes first to check if they're climbable. Using the wrong rope will result in you taking damage and getting stunned.\n  - Use Freedom and Anticipation where possible.\n  - The falling rocks can kill you (which will be an unsafe death), but running out of time will only result in the escape sequence being reset. If either happens, the minimap will be usable in the next escape attempt.","Talk to Dharok.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The games"}]},"King of the Dwarves":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Lava-flow miner Sven standing outside of the Lava Flow Mine in Keldagrim East. {Chat: 1 I'd like the tour. > Accept}"],"t":"Starting the quest"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Free all 6 Lava-flow miners (they are all close to the entrance). If you leave the scene by exiting or teleporting, all progress made of rescuing the miners is lost.\n  - Mine the lighter coloured rubble surrounding them, then rescue them and they'll appear in your backpack. Only one Miner can be carried at a time.\n  - Talk to Foreman Jaak with one in your backpack, then move onto the next one."],"t":"Rescuing the miners"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Veldaban near the protesters outside. {Chat: Any > Any > Any}","Go to the top floor of the Keldagrim Palace in the centre of Keldagrim. A short cutscene will play.","Talk to Veldaban. {Chat: 3 Why are you so angry? > 2 You should try to calm down.}","Talk to the Green Gemstone Director. {Chat: 4 I was there when the explosion happened. > 3 I rescued some of the miners.}","Talk to the Yellow Fortune Director. {Chat: 1 Why did you arrest Veldaban? > 1 Veldaban's popular. Arresting him makes you look worse.}","Talk to the Blue Opal Director. {Chat: 2 Tell me about the Lava Flow Mine. > 2 So the chaos dwarf blew up the secondary boilers?}","Talk to the Brown Engine Director. {Chat: 3 What did you want to do about the miners? > 2 It was a difficult decision. I understand.}","Dismiss any pets and talk to the consortium general secretary. {Chat: 1 I've talked to everyone I need to.}"],"t":"Releasing Veldaban"},{"n":"6 soft clay and 6 mithril bars","r":"","s":["Talk to Hreidmar outside the eastern entrance of the Keldagrim Palace.","Talk to one of the protesters. {Chat: 1 Does anyone know where Meike is?}","Head to the King's Axe Inn (Keldagrim West) and talk to Luitger. {Chat: 3 You're not joining the protests? > 3 Goodbye.}","Go to the Black Guard HQ (west of the bank) and talk to Klaas.","Go to the top of the Keldagrim Watchtower (small building just south of the Palace, west Keldagrim) and talk to Meike. {Chat: 3 We could get into the records of the chamber first. > 1 I'll meet you both at the library.}","Go to the library north of the Palace in West Keldagrim.","Talk to Meike or Veldaban.","Talk to the Librarian. {Chat: 3 Could you open the display case, please?}","Talk to Meike or Veldaban.","Open the cabinet north of Meike.","Use the soft clay on Meike and then talk to the librarian about the keys. {Chat: 3 Can you tell me more about the keys?}","Talk to Meike.","Use the furnace (not forge) such as the one in the Palace south of the library, if the prompt doesn't show up go to another furnace. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 Yes.}","Go to the Records Chamber (Enter Entrance in the wall, west of the Black Guard HQ)","Talk to Meike or Veldaban.","Match up the keys with the correct keyholes. See the picture below for the solution.",":","Open the door and watch the cutscene."],"t":"Records chamber"},{"n":"","r":"Combat boosting potions and food","s":["Talk to Veldaban. {Chat: 1 Can you show me the way to the Barendir caverns?}","Enter the tunnel to the east and go to the opposite end of the cavern.","Defeat Colonel Grimsson while making sure Veldaban does not die. If you leave the fight, you can restart by talking to Veldaban in the Laughing Miner pub in Keldagrim East."],"t":"Defeating Colonel Grimsson"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Veldaban. {Chat: 3 We should get reinforcements. > 3 What about the trolls? > Any > 3 I'm going to go and talk to them, with or without you.}","Head back halfway through the cavern until you come to an entrance on the east side. Enter it and speak to Pretty Flower. {Chat: 2 I need to talk to you. > 2 How can I prove I'm worthy?}","Lift the big rock opposite My Arm.","Lift the troll named Big Rock.","Talk to Pretty Flower {Chat: 1 We want you to help defend Keldagrim from chaos dwarves. > 4 I'll just be going.}.","Talk to My Arm {Chat: 3 How can I get Pretty Flower to listen to me? > Any > 3 Wait, what pretty flower are you talking about? > 3 Could I have a pretty flower? > 2 I need to give it to Pretty Flower. > 2 I need to give the plant to the warlord.}.","Talk to Pretty Flower. {Chat: 1 We want you to help defend Keldagrim from chaos dwarves. > 4 Take a look at this pretty flower... > 3 It's a gift from Colonel Grimsson.}","Go out through the same way you entered with Veldaban.","Get back to the east of the Keldagrim Palace by using the quick travel option on the Dwarven Boatman to the west."],"t":"Recruiting the trolls"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the protest east of Keldagrim Palace.","Talk to Veldaban, who is standing within the group of protesters.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"King's Ransom":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Gossip south of the Sinclair Mansion (Fairy ring CJR). {Chat: Accept}","Talk to the Guard inside the gates."],"t":"Shady disappearances"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["From the outside, break the eastern smashed window of the mansion (right click to choose break).\n  - You might have to try again because of the dog","Once inside, go to the large room and take the scrap paper next to the fireplace.","Go up to the floor 2.","Take the address form from the table in the central northern room and read it.","Search the nearby bookcase for a black knight helm.","Go back down the staircase and \"break\" the smashed window again to climb out.","Talk to the Guard three times. {Chat: 1 I have proof that the Sinclairs have left.}{Chat: 1 I have proof that links the Sinclairs to Camelot.}{Chat: 1 I have proof of foul play.} (you can click away after giving the items to skip the first 2 interactions)"],"t":"Déjà vu"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Gossip. {Chat: 3 Tell me about Anna Sinclair.}","Go to the Seers' Village Courthouse, directly south from the mansion gates.","Talk to Anna. {Chat: 1 Okay, I guess I don't have much of a choice.}"],"t":"The Sinclairs"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Dismiss any followers you might have and go down the stairs to begin the trial. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm ready.}","Call the dog handler as a witness {Chat: 2 Dog handler}, talk to Pierre. {Chat: 2 Ask about the thread > 3 Ask about the poison}\n  - You may need to resize your interface and zoom out before descending the stairs since he appears near the bottom of the screen.","For the following options, talk to the judge to call a witness, then choose who you would like to call:\n  - Call the butler {Chat: 3 Butler}, talk to Hobbes. {Chat: 1 Ask about the dagger}\n  - Call the maid {Chat: 4 Next page > 2 Maid}, talk to Mary. {Chat: 4 Ask about the night of the murder}","After the balloons drop, exit via the gate.","Talk to Anna in her cell."],"t":"Courtroom drama"},{"n":"1 air rune and 1 law rune for Telekinetic Grab","r":"","s":["Go to the northeast of Camelot Castle, outside of the castle hedges","Search the statue.","Talk to Merlin. {Chat: 3 What do we do now? > 1 Reclaim Camelot. > 2 Retrieve the Holy Grail. > 3 Save King Arthur.}","Reach the vent on the northern wall, it should trigger a cutscene in which the imprisoned knights lift Merlin out. Do not reach for the vent again afterwards.\n  - If you don't see a cutscene, then talk to Merlin again and exhaust all options.","Cast Telekinetic Grab on the guard fixing his hair outside your cell door. Ask the knights around if you didn't bring any Telekinetic Grab runes.\n  - Drop trick will work here if you would like an extra hairclip.","Use the hairclip on the metal door.","Complete the puzzle.\n  - To complete this puzzle, you must set each of four tumblers to the correct height. The most foolproof way to do this (although not necessarily the quickest) is to set all tumblers to the lowest height and try the lock.\n  - If a tumbler shows a green circle, do not change that tumbler anymore.\n  - For the remaining tumblers, they will each show a blue or red circle. Increase those tumblers height by one and try again.\n  - Continue until the lock unlocks. This method will take at most six attempts.}}"],"t":"Jailbreaker"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Once you have bypassed the gate, climb up two sets of staircases to reach the top floor.","Search the table and click the purple cylinder second from the right."],"t":"The holy grail"},{"n":"Granite, bronze med helm, iron chainbody, holy grail and animate rock scroll","r":"Skull of Remembrance","s":["Go to East Ardougne, northeast corner, and talk to Wizard Cromperty. {Chat: 1 Talk about King's Ransom}","Equip your bronze med helm and iron chainbody and unequip other equipment, then enter the Black Knights' Fortress from Edgeville.\n  - If you have the Skull of Remembrance, you can teleport to the floor of the fortress and head down to the floor.","Climb-down the ladder in the south-west corner.","Remove your bronze helm and iron chainbody, then free King Arthur.","Talk to King Arthur. Give him the bronze helm and iron chainbody.","Return to Camelot and talk to King Arthur.","Quest complete!"],"t":"For Camelot!"}]},"Koschei's Troubles (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Thorvald the Warrior north of Rellekka inside Skulgrimen's Battle Gear. {Chat: Accept > 3 Does he need my help?}","Climb down the ladder."],"t":"Koschei the Deathless returns"},{"n":"Balmung","r":"","s":["Talk to Koschei the Deathless. {Chat: 1 Let's go fight it - together!}","With the Balmung in your inventory, chop down the Blossoming tree north-west of the bridge south of Rellekka.","Take the chest from tree stump.","Return and talk to Koschei.","Open the chest."],"t":"The Axe and the tree"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Inspect the toy ship.","Talk to Koschei.","Climb up the ladder and return to Rellekka.","Go to the well south-east of the longhall.","Use the toy ship on the well."],"t":"Floating the ship"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return and talk to Koschei.","Interact with the jewel. {Chat: 1 Attempt to cut the jewel}","Talk to Koschei. {Chat: Any}","Miniquest complete!\n  - For additional completion, talk to Kharshai. {Chat: 4 I want to talk about your identity crisis. > 3 About that jewel... > 1 May I have a look at the jewel?}\n  - Interact blue jewel {Chat: 2 Attempt to crush the jewel} (Requires Strength)\n  - Talk to Kharshai. {Chat: 4 I want to talk about your identity crisis. > 3 Kharshai, have a look at the jewel.}\n  - Talk to Kharshai again. {Chat: 4 I want to talk about your identity crisis. > 3 About that jewel... > 2 May I have a look at the jewel?}\n  - Interact red jewel {Chat: 3 Attempt to detect any curses} (Requires Prayer)\n  - Talk to Kharshai. {Chat: 4 I want to talk about your identity crisis. > 3 Kharshai, have a look at the jewel.}\n  - Repeat the steps once again but make a new memory instead (blue) and the miniquest will be completed}}"],"t":"The jewel"}]},"Lair of Tarn Razorlor (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Using a Ring of slaying will teleport the player directly to Tarn's lair, skipping most of the quest.\n  - Alternatively, enter level 1 of the abandoned mine by climbing over the mine cart west of the secret entrance and crawling down the cart tunnel.\n  - Head north and enter the entrance. Watch for skeletons and possessed pickaxes.\n  - Navigate the maze, disarm traps along the way or be hit by damage. Watch for skeletons and zombies throughout the maze.\n    - For help see Tarn's Lair#Route"],"t":"Getting to Tarn Razorlor"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill both Terror dogs, Mutant tarn and Tarn","Head north through the passageway and take Tarn's diary.}} Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Fighting Tarn Razorlor"}]},"Land of the Goblins":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Grubfoot in the Dorgeshuun Mines. {Chat: 2 Mistag, why won't you let Grubfoot into the city? > 3 I'll take responsibility for Grubfoot. > Accept}\n  - Dismiss any familiar or Grubfoot won't follow you."],"t":"Land of the Goblins"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["With Grubfoot following, enter Dorgesh-Kaan using the door to the south and head north-west where Oldak is.","In the north-west room, talk to Zanik. {Chat: 3 So why have you come to talk to Zanik? > 3 What was this new dream? > 2 How do you know your dream was true? > Any > 1 I promise not to tell anyone where the temple is. > 1 I'm ready.}"],"t":"Yu'biusk"},{"n":"Black mushroom ink or a vial, toadflax potion (unfinished)","r":"An extra vial or Black mushroom ink, and an extra toadflax potion (unfinished) to make a second potion. (Or, you can attempt to save a dose from your first potion)","s":["If you forgot to bring the toadflax potion, proceed until Zanik has entered into the temple.\n  - Otherwise, you will need to go back to Oldak in Dorgesh-Kaan to meet with her, and provide him two law runes and one molten glass.","Once you teleport with Zanik, head north-west to the temple entrance blocked by two goblin guards.\n  - Pick and grind a black mushroom into an empty vial if you don't already have black mushroom ink.","Talk to the guards and they will allow Zanik to pass into the temple.","Talk to the Makeover Mage south-west of Falador. {Chat: 4 Can you turn me into a goblin? > 1 I need to slip past some goblin guards. > 3 Can you turn me into a goblin or not?}","Use the pharmakos berries on an unfinished toadflax potion to create the goblin potion.\n  - (Optional) After making the potion, collect another set of pharmakos berries if planning to complete the Contract Claws mystery.","Head to the goblin cave (just north of the Ardougne lodestone)."],"t":"You not a goblin!"},{"n":"goblin mail, Enough free inventory spaces to unequip all items","r":"","s":["Unequip all items and dismiss any followers.","In front of the goblin guards, drink the goblin potion (pick any goblin appearance).","Climb down the entrance. {Chat: 1 Me want get into temple. > 1 Yes, I'm [goblin name].}","North, sitting on his throne, talk to the High Priest. {Chat: 1 Can you tell me about Yu'biusk? > 1 I understand the ways of the Big High War God. > 1 I'm ready for the test.}","Take the quiz. {Chat: 1 True. > 1 The Big High War God commands it. > 2 False. > 2 Goblins were not mighty warriors before he chose us. > 2 False. > 1 That's one of the commandments. > 2 Lead goblins to victory over the whole world.}","After the quiz, ask about Yu'biusk. {Chat: 1 Can you tell me about Yu'biusk? > 2 Where is Yu'biusk? > 5 Never mind.}","Dye your goblin mail black with the mushroom ink.","Wear the black goblin mail and go in the north-east room by talking to the goblin in the passage.","Pickpocket the priest for a key. Keep this key. You will need it later.","Talk to Zanik in the prison cell. {Chat: 4 Sit tight. I'll be back soon.}","Search the crate in the room to find the teleport sphere.","Talk to Zanik again, she will teleport. {Chat: 1 I have a teleport sphere here.}"],"t":"Transmogrification"},{"n":"5 coins, 1 black goblin mail, 1 raw slimy eel","r":"Combat bracelet","s":["Leave the cave.\n  - You can equip a piece of equipment to be thrown out, then you can teleport to Draynor.","Talk to Aggie in Draynor Village. {Chat: 4 More... > 2 Can you make dyes for me please? > 4 Can you make black or white dye?}\n  - Or, if Vampyre Slayer is complete. {Chat: 5 More... > 2 Can you make dyes for me please? > 4 Can you make black or white dye?}","Teleport to Seers' Village lodestone and head south-west to Hemenster near the Ranging Guild. Alternatively, use a combat bracelet.\n  - Be sure to have a raw slimy eel or you will have to repeat the next steps.","Attempt to open the gate near Morris. {Chat: 3 I need to catch a Hemenster whitefish.}","After finishing the dialogue, open the gate.","Catch a whitefish.","Return to Aggie and use the goblin mail on her."],"t":"Whitefish"},{"n":"Blue dye, yellow dye, purple dye, orange dye, enough backpack spaces to unequip all items","r":"","s":["Unequip any items and dismiss any followers.","Go back to the goblin temple entrance, take a sip of your goblin potion, and equip your white goblin mail.","Enter the temple.","Steal the white key from the priest in the room west of the temple.\n  - Remove the goblin mail to leave the room quicker.","Repeat the operation of stealing keys, dying your mail in the following order:\n  - Yellow (north-west)\n  - Purple (south-west)\n  - Orange (south-east)\n  - Blue (east)"],"t":"Macabre crypt"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the crypt (large door north of the temple).","Prepare for battle by equipping weapons and armour.","Use the Say-name option on each of the graves. After killing them, talk to them.\n  - South-west: Snothead {Chat: 1 Where is Yu'biusk? > 1 What was your predecessor's name? > 4 Goodbye.}\n  - South-east: Snailfeet {Chat: 2 Snailfeet}\n  - North-west: Mosschin {Chat: 3 Mosschin}\n  - North-east: Redeyes {Chat: 4 Redeyes}\n  - North: Strongbones (ignore his skeleton minions) {Chat: 5 Strongbones}","Talk to Strongbones after defeating him. {Chat: 1 Where is Yu'biusk? > 4 Goodbye.}"],"t":"Prepare for battle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Dorgesh-Kaan and speak with Zanik in the north-west (Oldak's lab).","With a light source, head to the south end of Dorgesh-Kaan using fairy code AJQ. Alternatively, without using fairy rings:\n  - Go up the stairs to the agility course.\n  - At the start of the agility course, climb down the ladder west of the agility cable.\n  - Follow the cave path east then south to the Fairy ring.","Adjust the machines next to Oldak, use combination 9-4-1, activate the machine.","Open the strange box in the north-western part of Yu'biusk for a cutscene.","Continue dialogue with Oldak.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Home portal"}]},"Legacy of Seergaze":{"sections":[{"n":"Rod of Ivandis, or another silver weapon, and 2 backpack space","r":"2 different combat styles and equipment","s":["Talk to the Mercenary Adventurer at the Temple Trekking ending point (west of Canifis). CKS or the Canifis lodestone are good options to reach the area quickly. {Chat: Accept > 3 Okay, thanks.}","Enter the Mausoleum west of the Adventurer.","Talk to Drezel. {Chat: 2 Who do you think these suspicious people are? > 4 Okay, thanks.}","Go through the gate west of Drezel and climb down the stairs north of the well.","Search the sparkling wall storage unit a few steps east of the stairs, then go back up the stairs.","Exit the Mausoleum via the west entrance ladder, enter the Paterdomus temple and head to the top floor.","After the cutscene, kill Fistandantilus and Zaromark Sliver (or wait until they time out and teleport away).\n  - Both enemies have 2,750 life points, a combat level of 77, and a max hit of 220 in magic and ranged. These enemies will use prayer to become immune to your combat style, but do not protect against necromancy. Necromancy or multiple combat styles are recommended for this fight.","Search the crude table in the north-west corner of the room.","Return to Drezel. {Chat: 2 Do you think this has anything to do with the Guthixian Edicts?}","Talk to the Mercenary Adventurer and escort him the same way as any Burgh de Rott Ramble. {Chat: 2 You still want to go to Burgh de Rott? > 1 I can take you to Burgh de Rott.}\n  - Easy path recommended for least time and effort. Be sure to remove any melee-reducing equipment like ranged and magic armour. If you encounter juvinates, you will require your Rod of Ivandis or another silver weapon.","Once in Burgh de Rott, if the dialogue does not automatically start, talk to the Mercenary Adventurer.\n  - If no one with that name is present in Burgh de Rott, skip to the next step."],"t":"An evil conspiracy"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb over the wall inside the Pub and then climb down the trapdoor to the cellar.","Talk to Veliaf Hurtz until he gives you a crate. {Chat: 2 Do you have a job for me? > 3 Okay, thanks.}","Climb up the ladder.","Go south of Burgh de Rott and take the boat to Meiyerditch.","Go to the Meiyerditch Myreque base. Refer to the Meiyerditch shortcut guide for help. Being caught by the vyrewatch and sent to mines provides a fast and reliable route.","Talk to Flaygian Screwte, in the north room, and offer him your help. {Chat: 3 How's the research going? > 4 Can I help in some way? > 5 Okay, thanks.}"],"t":"The Myreque's task"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Ask Andiess Juip or Kael Forshaw in the same room about weapons. {Chat: 2 Hi there, I was wondering if I could ask some questions?}","Go to the next room south (near Mekritus A'hara) and search the middle bunk bed on the eastern half of the north wall for a book.","Read it and remember which page mentioned flails.","Give the book to Flaygian, giving him the proper page number. He will give you 10 nails.","Head to the northernmost part of Meiyerditch and enter the house south of the house with the furnace (\"mass of debris\").","Use the Make-ladder option on the centre post.","Climb up the post.","Jump across the floorboards to the east, then to the north.","Jump west through the damaged wall.","Climb up the ladder and search the trough.","Take a piece of coal from the coal barrel.","Go to the bottom floor and select \"dig\" on the mass of debris (right click).\n  - If the \"dig\" option doesn't appear, you must go back to the top floor and search the trough","Use the coal on the furnace, then light the furnace.","Return and talk to Flaygian, then in the same room;\n  - Take 2 silver and 2 mithril bars from the barrel on the northern wall.\n  - Take a blessed sickle from the shelf on the south-western wall.","Go to the room to the east of the entrance ladder.","Search the crate for a chain link mould and add it to your tool belt.","Return to the furnace and make the Silvthril chain. It can be found by clicking on the silver bar in the smithing interface (scroll with down arrow next to \"Casting Metals & Glass\").\n  - You do not need to make 2, you will have 1 bar of each type left. These are not used at any point in the quest so you can safely deposit them into your metal bank.","Talk to Flaygian, then use the blessed sickle on him. {Chat: 2 How about using this as the head for the flail?}","Talk to Safalaan."],"t":"In search of the weapon"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Proceed to the laboratory; the building south-east of the furnace, third from the top on the east wall and through the slashed tapestry.","Dismiss any followers and climb down the stairs.","After the cutscene, Look at one of the bodies. {Chat: 2 Is there anything I can do? > 3 Okay, thanks.}","Search the door to the south and use the saw in your tool belt.","Go through the door, then after the cutscene continue down the long and winding tunnel.","Continue north on the path to the large chamber where the strange stones are."],"t":"Back to the lab"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["If you need runes for the Lvl-2 Enchant spell, search the corpse next to the rocks before continuing.\n  - Searching the corpse will complete the Bloodstained Treasure achievement, if not already completed.","Search the strange stones in the northern part of the cavern.","Talk to Safalaan. There will be a cutscene and a fight against vyrewatches in which you cannot deal any damage, but the fight will end in another cutscene with Safalaan being attacked.","Make sure you have 4 free backpack spaces, then talk to Safalaan.","Use the emerald on the sickle (right click, don't accidentally make bolt tips).","Use the Lvl-2 Enchant spell on it.","Use the chain on it.","Talk to Safalaan.","Go to the surface, equip the Ivandis flail, kill a vyrewatch, and pick up its corpse.","Return to Safalaan."],"t":"Vyrewatch and the Ivandis flail"},{"n":"Teak pyre logs or better","r":"","s":["Return to the basement of the pub in Burgh de Rott and talk to Veliaf. Ask him what to do. {Chat: 1 The Flail of Ivandis kills Vyrewatch! > 4 What should I do now? > 5 Okay, thanks.}","Return to and talk to Drezel at the Mausoleum. {Chat: 2 Veliaf asked me to bring this Vyrewatch corpse to you. > 4 Okay, thanks.}","Go through the gate, then down the stairs north of the well.","Use the pyre logs on a funeral pyre, then the vyre corpse. Light it.","Take the ornate tomb key from the pedestal.","Use it on the wall storage unit from the beginning of the quest on the north-eastern side of the room (the same one that is still sparkling) to acquire a blood talisman.","After the cutscene, go upstairs and ask Drezel what to do. If you still have the library key: {Chat: 2 What should I do now? > 3 Okay, thanks.}. Otherwise, to bypass getting a new key. {Chat: 1 Talk about items. > 2 What should I do now? > 3 Okay, thanks.}","Report to Veliaf in the Burgh de Rott pub basement.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Back to the Columbarium"}]},"Legends' Quest":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to a Legends' guard at the Legends' Guild north-east of East Ardougne (fairy ring blr). {Chat: 3 Can I speak to someone in charge? > 1 Can I go on the quest? > 2 Yes, I'd like to talk to Grand Vizier Erkle.}","Talk to Radimus Erkle. {Chat: 1 Yes actually, what's involved? > Accept}","If required, take 3-5 papyrus from Radimus' table. Alternatively, Obli's General Store in the Shilo Village sells 10 papyrus as well."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"Radimus notes, 3-5 papyrus, 1-3 charcoal","r":"5 bittercap mushrooms","s":["Chop-down the Jungle Trees/Bushes south of Shilo Village (fairy ring ckr) to access the Kharazi Jungle.","Walk to the western edge of the jungle.","Choose the Complete option on the Radimus notes in the backpack.","Repeat in the centre of the jungle.\n  - If you have completed A Fairy Tale II - Cure a Queen, repair fairy ring cjs with five bittercap mushrooms to make returning to the jungle easier.","Repeat again on the eastern edge of the jungle.","Return north of the Jungle Trees using fairy ring ckr, or by chopping them down again.","Use the notes on a jungle forester, south of Shilo Village. {Chat: 1 Yes, go ahead make a copy!}"],"t":"Kharazi Jungle"},{"n":"Radimus notes, bull roarer, lockpicks, the runes for your version of RuneScape (see the item requirements table above), opal, jade, red topaz, sapphire, emerald, ruby, diamond, and at least 4 backpack spaces.","r":"Combat equipment to kill a lvl 77 Death wing","s":["Return to Kharazi Jungle (fairy ring cjs).","Swing the bull roarer to summon Gujuo, this may take several attempts.","Talk to him. {Chat: 1 I was hoping to attract the attention of a native. > 1 I want to develop friendly relationships with your people. > 1 Can you get your people together? > 1 What can we do instead then? > 1 How do we make the totem pole? > 1 I will release Ungadulu...}","Search the mossy rocks in the north-west of the jungle to enter the Viyeldi caves {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll crawl through, I'm very athletic.}, this may take several attempts.","Choose the Investigate option on the firewall. {Chat: 1 How can I extinguish the flames? > 1 Where do I get pure water from?}","Exit the cave via the Cave Exit.","Swing the Bull roarer to summon Gujuo.","Talk to him to get the sketch. {Chat: 3 I need some pure water to douse some magic flames. > 5 Where is the pool of sacred water? > 5 What kind of vessel? > 2 Ok thanks for your help.}","Re-enter the cave and choose the Search option on the eastern bookcase. {Chat: 1 Yes please!}","Choose the Search on the Ancient Gate.","Smash-to-bits the three boulders.","Open the Ancient Gate. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm very strong, I'll force them open.}","Move past the death wings.\n  - If you want to complete one of the hard Karamja achievements, you can kill a death wing here.","Choose the Jump-over option on the jagged wall.","Search the marked wall. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll read it.}","Use your runes on it in order according to your version:\n  - English: Soul, Mind, Earth, Law, Law. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll go through!}\n  - German: Air, Earth, Blood, Earth, Nature.\n  - French: Law, Air, Death, Mind, Blood.\n  - Portuguese: Fire, Water, Earth, Air, Law.","If the chat option is not already offered, search the marked wall. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll go through!}","Use the cut gems on the carved rocks. Use the map to see which gem goes where.","Take the Binding book."],"t":"Viyeldi caves"},{"n":"Radimus notes, empty vial, at least 2 gold bars, at least 100 prayer points, binding book, sketch, and bull roarer","r":"Combat equipment (including Silverlight to weaken the demon)","s":["Make sure you received a sketch from Gujuo, and use 2 gold bars on any anvil for a gold bowl. This may fail.","Return to Kharazi Jungle (fairy ring cjs) and swing the bull roarer.","Talk to Gujuo. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'd like you to bless my gold bowl.}","Travel to the Water Pool (look for the tree icon on minimap).","Choose the \"Cut-Reed\" option on the Tall Reeds next to it.","Use the acquired hollow reed on the Water Pool.","Choose the Enchant-Vials option on the binding book and create an enchanted vial .","Use the hollow reed on the Water Pool again.","Return to the Viyeldi caves.","Use the golden bowl on the fire wall.","Choose the Use option on the binding book on Ungadulu.","Kill Nezikchened. He will blast the player sometimes exceeding 2500 typeless damage when he dies.","Choose the Talk-to option on Ungadulu. {Chat: 1 I need to collect some Yommi tree seeds for Gujuo. > 1 How do I grow the Yommi tree? > 1 What will you do now? > 3 Okay, thanks...}","Touch the Fire Wall.","Exit the cave.","Use the Golden bowl on the seeds.","Use the seeds on a patch of fertile soil. There's a patch above the pool. This will fail to plant the seeds.","Return to the pool and Use the Hollow reed on it. The water will be dried up.","Swing the Bull roarer and Talk to Gujuo. {Chat: 1 The water pool has dried up and I need more water. > 2 Where is the source of the spring of pure water? > 2 If I went, could you help me? > 5 Ok thanks for your help.}"],"t":"Sacred pool"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Switch to the standard spellbook if you are not already on it.","Collect the herbs using the maps below.\n  - Search palm trees for grimy ardrigal.\n  - Search marshy jungle vines for grimy snake weed.","Clean the herbs.","Use the clean ardrigal and clean snake weed on a vial of water for a bravery potion."],"t":"Picking the herbs"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to the Viyeldi caves.","Traverse the dungeon as before to where you found the Binding book:\n  - Search the eastern Bookcase.\n  - Choose the Search option on the Ancient Gate.\n  - Smash-to-bits the three Boulders.\n  - Open the Ancient Gate. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm very strong, I'll force them open.}\n  - Move past the Death wings.\n  - Choose the Jump-over option on Jagged wall.\n  - Use the Marked wall.","Cast a Charge Orb spell on the north Ancient Gate.","Use the Rope on the Winch.\n  - If you forgot your rope, you can smash the barrels in the room for one.","Drink the bravery potion. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll bravely drink the bravery potion.}","Search and then climb-down the Winch. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll shimmy down the rope into possible doom.}","Climb-over the rocky ledges and rocks to reach the bottom. {Chat: 1 Yes, I can think of nothing more exciting! > 1 Yes, I can think of nothing more exciting! > 1 Yes, I can think of nothing more exciting! > 1 Yes, I want to climb over the rocks. > 1 Yes, I want to climb over the rocks. > 1 Yes, I want to climb over the rocks.}","Kill the 3 different skeletons until you get 3 crystal pieces (Hunk, Chunk, and Lump):\n  - San Tojalon\n  - Irvig Senay\n  - Ranalph Devere","Use each crystal on the north-east furnace.","Use the heart crystal on the searchable mossy rock in the middle of the room.","Run south and use the heart crystal on the recess next to the shimmering field.","Walk-through the shimmering field.","West past the lesser demons, push any of the boulders. {Chat: any > 1 What can I do about that? > 1 I'll do what I must to get the water. > 1 Ok, I'll do it.}","Return to the start of the cavern, back past the shimmering field and Rocks.","Equip the dark dagger.","Take the blue hat.","Kill Viyeldi.\n  - You will need to Attack him during the dialogue as he will disappear after completing the dialogue.","Re-equip your preferred weapon.","Return to the boulders and push one.","Kill Nezikchened.","Push all three boulders.\n  - All three must be pushed while standing on the east side of them.\n  - If one does not move, push it from a different angle."],"t":"Preparation in the caves"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Kharazi Jungle (fairy ring cjs).","Use the hollow reed on the water pool.","Choose the Use option on the yommi tree seeds on the dark brown soil just north-west of the pool, it will appear as Fertile Soil.","Use the golden bowl on it once it stops growing.","Chop the adult yommi tree.","Trim the felled yommi tree.","Carve the trimmed yommi.","Lift the totem pole."],"t":"Planting yommi"},{"n":"Yommi totem, Radimus notes, bull roarer","r":"Weapons, armour, food","s":["Use your Yommi totem on the Totem Pole east of the pool.","Defeat Nezikchened and the three skeletons.\n  - He will appear four times, with a skeleton spawning between each kill.","Use the Yommi totem on the Totem Pole again.","Talk to Gujuo to receive the gilded totem.","Return to the Legends' Guild (fairy ring BLR).","Talk to Radimus.","Talk to him again inside the guild. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll train now.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"The final fight"}]},"Let Them Eat Pie":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Nails Newton a few steps east of the Taverley lodestone. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["(Optional) Gather wheat and fishing bait.\n  - Go south and then east across the bridge and take some fishing bait from the ground near the bait barrel and hanging fish.\n  - Go south and pick some wheat.","Go to the watermill in the north-east of the bank and south of the pub.","Climb the stairs.","Investigate the hopper with fishing bait and wheat in the backpack.","Operate hopper controls.","Go down the stairs.","Take-flour from flour bin to obtain maggoty flour.","Talk to Nails Newton. He will give you a maggoty pie shell."],"t":"The pie shell"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["(Optional) Go north and trade with Head Farmer Jones outside of the flax field to receive a free raw potato.","(Optional) Go east and cage on a fishing spot to catch a raw crayfish.","Go inside the flax field or animal pen and watch the cutscene.","Talk to Nails Newton.","Go north-west into the snowy Hunter area near the animal pens.","Inspect a hole with a raw potato in the backpack to receive a stinking potato.","Use the stinking potato or manky crayfish on the maggoty pie shell to create a terrible pie (uncooked).","Cook the pie at an oven in The Pick and Lute pub which is right next to Nails Newton.","Talk to Nails Newton."],"t":"The filling"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pickpocket Foppish Pierre for expensive spices. His location is marked on the map, which is west of the watermill and north-east of the bank.","Use the expensive spices on the pie to create a mouth-watering pie.","Climb up spiral stairs in the Pick and Lute tavern.","Talk to Rolo the Stout. {Chat: Any > 2 I think I've had enough, thanks.}","After the cutscene, talk to Nails.","Climb up spiral stairs in the Pick and Lute tavern.","Open the chest and steal the seal.","Talk to Nails Newton to receive a forged letter.","Deliver the letter to Foppish Pierre, just south of Nails Newton.","Talk to Nails Newton.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Attentive serving"}]},"Lost City":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Warrior northwest of the Lumbridge swamp to start the quest. {Chat: 1 Why are you camped out here? > 1 Who's Zanaris? > 1 If it's hidden, how are you planning to find it? > 2 Looks like you don't know either. > Accept}","Attempt to chop the swamp tree south of the campsite - There will be an option to \"chop\" tree instead of \"chop down\" tree, and a quest icon on the tooltip.","Talk to Shamus. {Chat: 2 I've been in that shed and I didn't see a city. > 1 Yes, please, a teleport would be useful.}"],"t":"Seeking the lost city"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Bring items to craft a weapon on Entrana. If you plan on using magic, you must have a magic weapon; you cannot cast spells without one. You can also remove tool belt items once you enter the dungeon, e.g. a mithril hatchet, for use in combat.","Talk to the monks in Port Sarim to be transported to Entrana.","Do not craft your weapons now or you'll be thrown out of Entrana.","Run north-west though the wooded area to the dungeon entrance ladder.","Enter the dungeon. {Chat: 2 Well, that is a risk I will have to take.}","Craft your weapons now.","Run to the southern-most part of the dungeon.","Chop the dramen tree.","Kill the dramen tree spirit.\n  - Make sure to let the dialogue appear before chopping again, or you may spawn a second spirit.","Chop the dramen tree again.","Craft the dramen branch using a knife.\n  - If you have not completed the quest Recipe for Disaster: Freeing Sir Amik Varze yet, you may want to get a second dramen branch and craft it with the pestle and mortar. This gives an item required for the quest, cinnamon, and saves an otherwise necessary second trip to the island.","Enter the door to the east or teleport out."],"t":"Entrana"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Wield your dramen staff.","Enter the shed in the centre of the Lumbridge swamp (south-east of the quest start).","Quest complete!"],"t":"Zanaris"}]},"Lost Her Marbles (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Darren Lightfinger.\n  - Talk to Darren {Chat: 3. I've had some success tracking down flame fragments.}. Talk to Robin to collect your loot.\n  - Repeat 4 times in total.","Talking to Robin the 4th time completes the Miniquest."],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Love Story":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Mabel in the barn east of the Draynor Village lodestone. {Chat: 1 Can you tell me what's wrong? > Accept > 3 Okay, off I go.}","Go up the ladder.","Solve the hay bale puzzle:\n  - As you arrive, go north once and push the one hay bale there all the way to the western wall.\n  - Standing where you are, push a pair of hay bales at your immediate south twice.\n  - Go one square east and push another pair of hay bales to the south.\n  - Push the single hay bale directly west of you.\n  - Finally, push the two hay bales to the south of you to clear the path.","Pick up the ring.","Climb down the ladder.","Talk to Zenevivia. {Chat: 3 What's happened to Mabel? > 2 Are you going to give Mabel her ring? > 1 What do you want me to do? > 3 Okay, off I go.}","Search any hay bale for a twig, give it to her.","Talk to her again. {Chat: 2 Will you return Mabel's ring and leave now? > 2 I'm trying to complete this quest. > 5 Alright, I'll accept. I'll make you regret this!}"],"t":"A damsel in distress"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to Draynor Village and talk to the Wise Old Man. {Chat: 1 A woman called Zenevivia wishes to challenge us.}\n  - This option may not show up unless the quest Garden of Tranquillity is completed if you started it.","After the cutscene, talk to him outside his house. If you have a familiar summoned then you must dismiss it to be able to progress. {Chat: 2 No. > 1 Yes, let's go.}","Head to the Rimmington house portal, talk to him again (Home Teleport works, teleport to Port Sarim and head west). {Chat: Any > 3 How can we get in there?}","When he leaves, walk to the house just east of the portal and talk to him once more. {Chat: 2 Yes, I'm ready.}","Open the \"chipped\" teleport to house tablet, solve the puzzle by dragging and dropping tiles from the left side on to the correct spots according to the photo here."],"t":"Wise Old Man"},{"n":"2 oak plank, 1 mithril bar, & 1 steel bar or Clockwork","r":"","s":["While standing next to the Wise Old Man, break the chipped tablet.","Enter the dungeon. {Chat: 2 Traps? Very dangerous. You go first.}","After the cutscene, continue dialogue with the Wise Old Man. {Chat: 2 What are we going to build?}","Craft via on the Clockmaker's bench in the workshop room. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Use the bench again to create a dummy. {Chat: 1 Okay, I'll get on with it.}","Enter the dungeon. During this part, there will be a pulsating purple light around your screen. Any players sensitive to flashing lights should proceed with caution.","Traverse through the dungeon, deactivating all the traps by walking on them and then return to the surface.\n  - Pit guardian rooms have 2 traps each, except for the scabarite room, having only one.","Climb the staircase. {Chat: 1 Yes, get it out now.}"],"t":"Zenevivia's house"},{"n":"combat gear/supplies","r":"Dragonfire protection","s":["Enter the dungeon. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm sure I found them all. Let's enter.}","Traverse through the dungeon, killing all the enemies (high-level players need not worry about using super antifire for the iron dragon as it is fairly weak and may be killed quickly).","Enter the final door, talk to the Wise Old Man. {Chat: Any > 2 She's insane; let's kill her and leave! > 4 Okay, let's go and face her.}","Climb the stairs."],"t":"The dungeon pit"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Zenevivia to start the battle. If you fail your first attempts, return to the Wise Old Man at the house in Rimmington. Right click on the house teleport tabs to modify them for another teleport to the fight.\n  - Avoid the flames on the floor, they deal low damage.\n  - Zenevivia uses magic spells and flames on the floor that can quickly deal around 600 damage.\n  - She will sometimes use protection prayers so prepare to switch attack styles or just use Necromancy.\n  - She can be knocked off pillars using abilities that knock back enemies, such as Kick.","After she is defeated, talk to her."],"t":"The final battle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["You will return to Draynor Village.","Talk to Zenevivia in the Wise Old Man's house. {Chat: 4 Have you still got Mabel's ring? > 2 When will you give me Mabel's ring? > 1 Stealing is wrong. > 1 When are you going to attack?}","Go upstairs and look through the telescope and watch the Wizards' Tower Robbery.","Head downstairs, talk to Zenevivia again. {Chat: 1 Are you going to try any more robberies? > 1 Can I have Mabel's ring back now?}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Robbing the Wizards' Tower"}]},"Lunar Diplomacy":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Choose the 'talk to' option on Lokar Searunner on Rellekka's westernmost dock. {Chat: 2 You've been away from these parts for a while? > 1 Why did you leave? > Accept}","Speak to Brundt the Chieftain in the Longhall for a seal of passage. {Chat: 1 Ask about a seal of passage.}\n  - You will need to keep the seal on you while on the island. Talking to anyone without it will teleport you back to Rellekka.","Return and talk to Lokar. {Chat: 1 Arrr! Yar! Let's be on our way, yar!}","Climb the ladder and board the pirate ship. Talk to Captain Bentley about sailing to Lunar Isle. {Chat: 4 Can we sail to Lunar Isle now?}","Climb down the central ladder.","Below deck, talk to 'Bird's-Eye' Jack to the south-west.","Talk to Captain Bentley again. {Chat: 2 Perhaps it's the Navigator's fault?}","Return to 'Birds-Eye' Jack again."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Must talk to them in this order.\n  - Talk to 'Eagle-eye' Shultz at the very front of the ship (back upstairs).\n  - Talk to 'Beefy' Burns on the lowest level of the ship.\n  - Talk to 'Lecherous' Lee on the very top level, at the south end of the ship.\n  - Talk to First mate 'Davey-boy' on the southern end of the deck near the stairs.\n  - Climb up to the top level at the south end of the ship and talk to the cabin boy (2 inventory spaces required). He is next to Lecherous Lee."],"t":"Talking to the crew"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use the lens on the lantern. Light it.","Use the lantern on the following objects and rub away the symbols:\n  - Cannon: Climb the ladder in the middle. The cannon is on the middle level at the south end of the ship. {Chat: 1 Rub away!}\n  - Wallchart: Climb back up and enter the southernmost room. The wallchart is on the northwestern wall. {Chat: 1 Rub away!}\n  - Chest: Climb down to the lowest level of the ship. The chest is on the ground at the northern end of the ship, just as you come down. {Chat: 1 Rub away!}\n  - Barrel: On the same level, the most southern stack of three barrels. {Chat: 1 Rub away!}\n  - Support: Same level big support column in the middle of the ship. {Chat: 1 Rub away!}","Talk to Captain Bentley."],"t":"Searching for clues"},{"n":"clean guam, clean marrentill, and ground suqah tooth","r":"","s":["Climb down the ladders and walk into the city (there will be a small cutscene).","Go north-east outside the city and kill suqah until these items are obtained:\n  - One suqah tooth.\n  - 4 suqah hides.\n  - If not already in the backpack, one grimy guam and one grimy marrentill. Clean the herbs.","Mine a lunar ore at the mine north-east of the city. Climb down the ladder and mine a stalagmite to the West of the rune essence rock. It looks like a rock jutting out of the ground.\n  - Optional: Mine Rune Essence to complete Runes on the Moon, which is a Hard Fremennik achievement.","Run to the south-east part of the island. Talk to the Oneiromancer near the astral altar.","Return to the city and enter the walking house in the northern section. Talk to Baba Yaga (1 inventory space required). {Chat: 2 The Oneiromancer told me you may be able to help...}","Use the vial on the sink.\n  - Add a guam and a marrentill to the vial of water.\n  - Grind the suqah tooth and use it on the vial to complete the potion.","Return to the Oneiromancer with the potion."],"t":"Lunar Isle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Skull sceptre or Edgeville lodestone for the air altar","Ring of duelling or Al Kharid lodestone for the fire altar","Enlightened amulet or Lumbridge lodestone for the water altar","Fort Forinthry lodestone, Invitation box, or Archaeology journal for the earth altar"],"t":"Travelling options"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use your dramen staff/staves on the following altars in the listed order (you may need talismans to access if you do not have alternate teleports):\n  - Air (west of Varrock)\n  - Fire (north of Al Kharid)\n  - Water (Lumbridge Swamp)\n  - Earth (south of Fort Forinthry)","Before returning to the isle, smelt the lunar ore at any regular furnace and make a lunar helmet at a regular anvil.","Travel back to Lunar Isle by selecting \"travel\" from Lokar Searunner in Rellekka at the westernmost dock, then travel with Captain Bentley and give a lunar staff to the Oneiromancer."],"t":"Elemental runecrafting altars"},{"n":"1 backpack space","r":"","s":["If you have already made the lunar helm, you can skip the next 4 steps.\n  - Climb down ladder north-eastern part of the isle.\n  - Mine a stalagmite for a lunar ore.\n  - You have to use a furnace to smith the ore (the forge in the southern building will not work).\n  - Use an anvil to make the helm, such as the one in the southern building."],"t":"Smithing lunar helm"},{"n":"400 coins, thread or Crafting cape, four suqah hides, 1 backpack space","r":"","s":["Talk to Pauline Polaris in the north-western-most building in the city. {Chat: 2 Pauline.} Choose the correct answer \"Jane Blud-Hagic-Maid\". The answers are randomly ordered.","Talk to Meteora south in the city.","Kill Suqahs until one drops a special tiara. If you haven't already, pick up their hide as well as you'll need four hides later on.","Give Meteora the tiara.","Talk to Rimae Sirsalis in the clothing store south of the bank about ceremonial clothes. {Chat: 2 You know the ceremonial clothes?}","Talk to Rimae Sirsalis again, she will tan your hides. {Chat: 2 You know the ceremonial clothes? > 1 That seems like a fair deal.}\n  - If you didn't bring thread, Rimae's shop sells some.","Craft a lunar torso, trousers, gloves, and boots from your hides."],"t":"Crafting lunar gear"},{"n":"1 backpack space, and a spade","r":"","s":["Go to the biggest building in the city (west of the lodestone) and talk to Selene (she might be outside). {Chat: 2 I'm looking for a ring.}","Exit the city and run south. Dig up near blue flowers with a spade (tool belt doesn't work), they are the flowers to the furthest south west across the bridge."],"t":"Looking for lunar ring"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Give the Oneiromancer all your lunar gear.","Talk to the Oneiromancer again with 11 free inventory slots."],"t":"Giving lunar gear"},{"n":"","r":"Runes for combat spells (preferably fire spells, elemental staff not equippable).","s":["Use the vial on the kindling Oneiromancer just gave you to create soaked kindling.","Get your combat runes and supplies, dismiss your follower, and wear all your lunar items. Four backpack spaces are required.","Do not carry an augmented crystal hatchet in the backpack to avoid a bug later in the quest.","Run to the biggest building in the city (west of the lodestone).","Make sure you're wearing all 8 pieces of Lunar equipment; if you exit to lobby or logout, or are not wearing them all when you add the soaked kindling, you'll have to return to the Oneiromancer to get a new kindling.","Light the ceremonial brazier then use the Soaked kindling on it to enter Dreamland."],"t":"Dreamland"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ethereal Man or Ethereal Lady.","Step on the yellow/green platform south-west of the island.","Talk to Ethereal Fluke.","He will call out a number. You need to make the dice add up to the number he called. When you \"roll\" one of the dice, it will turn the die upside down, so each die only has two possible numbers (1 and 6, 2 and 5, 3 and 4).","He eventually teleports you back to the middle.","Talk to the Ethereal Man/Lady."],"t":"Dicing"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head south-east and step on the pink/purple platform.","Talk to Ethereal Numerator.","Click on the numbers to complete the patterns for four times.}} Here are sequences the Ethereal Numerator may possibly give you, with the next two numbers in the patterns highlighted: :{| class=\"wikitable\" |0||1||3||4|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |6|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |7 |- |1||1||1||2||1||3||1||4|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |1|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |5 |- |1||1||2||2||3|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |3|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |4 |- |1||1||2||3||1||1||4|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |5|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |1 |- |1||2||3|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |4|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |5 |- |1||3||5|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |7|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |9 |- |1||4||2||5|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |3|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |6 |- |1||6||2||5|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |3|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |4 |- |1||9||2||8|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |3|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |7 |- |2||3||5||6|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |8|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |9 |- |2||6||3||7|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |4|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |8 |- |3||4||2||5|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |1|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |6 |- |7||3||6||2|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |5|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |1 |- |8||6||4|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |2|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |0 |- |9||7||5|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |3|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |1 |- |9||8||7||6|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |5|| class=\"table-bg-pink\" |4 |} {{Checklist|","He eventually teleports you back to the middle.","Talk to the Ethereal Man/Lady."],"t":"Number sequence"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head north-east and step on the blue platform.","Talk to Ethereal Perceptive. He might give you a hatchet. {Chat: 1 Ok, let's go!} (Do not carry an augmented crystal hatchet in the backpack or you will be given the following message: \"You do not have a hatchet which you have the Woodcutting level to use\" even if you have another hatchet in the backpack or a hatchet on your toolbelt)","Run west and chop 20 dream logs, depositing them on your log pile.","He will teleport you once you've won the competition.","Talk to the Ethereal Man/Lady."],"t":"Logging race"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head north-west and step on the grey platform.","Talk to Ethereal Guide.","Cross the chasm by jumping on the correct combination of Dream Puffs. Keep a note of the correct steps! You can use the table below to track your path: click cell to highlight it. Click again to cancel a highlight.","Once complete, talk to the Ethereal Man/Lady."],"t":"Memorisation"},{"n":"","r":"Agility cape to prevent you from being electrocuted.","s":["Head east and step on the yellow platform.","Talk to Ethereal Expert and start the race. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Jump over the hurdles. If you fail three times, you will lose the race. Run and stop before each hurdle, before clicking the orb to jump over.","After you have won talk to the Ethereal Man/Lady."],"t":"The hurdles"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head south-east and step on the green platform.","Talk to Ethereal Mimic. {Chat: 1 Suppose I may as well have a go.}","Click on them and then copy the emote that they perform. They teleport after each correct emote.","After five correct emotes, they'll teleport you back."],"t":"Copy cat"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Ethereal Man/Lady to begin the final fight. {Chat: 1 Of course. I'm ready.}","Kill Me (6,000 life points, weakness to fire spells). You can safe-spot them behind the dream tree.\n  - Should you forget your runes after entering the fight, you will not be able to leave the fight in any way unless you log out and back in. This will take you back to Lunar Isle where you can bank to get the runes.\n  - Be sure to equip your Seal of passage before speaking to a banker.\n  - Go back to the Oneiromancer again to get the kindling and potion to return back to the dream.\n  - Re-equip your Lunar amulet before attempting to enter the dream.}}"],"t":"Defeating me"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Read the lectern to return to Lunar Isle. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to the Oneiromancer.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Mahjarrat Memories (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"Rellekka tablet or enchanted lyre","s":["Speak to Kharshai, located under the helmet shop in Rellekka. Agree to help him. {Chat: 3 I want to talk about the Mahjarrat memories. > 1 Tell me more. > Accept > 1 Sign the contract.}","With the engrammeter, head to any divination colony of vibrant wisps or higher. Fill it with 500 divine memories.\n  - You may utilise World 79 (Community Divination World) for more frequent enriched springs.","Visit the locations below, use the charged engrameter to collect the memory.","Return to Kharshai. Talk to him to give him the memory. {Chat: 3 I want to talk about the Mahjarrat memories.}","Recharge the engrammeter with another 500 divine memories, and repeat for the remaining 14 memories."],"t":"Beginning"},{"n":"Macaw, insulated boots, and the invitation box.","r":"Fremennik sea boots 4/14 Rellekka tablets/Enchanted lyre, desert amulet 2, pharaoh's sceptre/sceptre of the gods, camulet/cramulet, ring of kinship, Ardougne cloak, 2x Varrock Teleport runes, Dig Site pendant, and ring of slaying.","s":["Go down the trapdoor, and follow the corridors full of armoured zombies.","Ignore the human detector corridor; squeeze through the pipe in the next room. Follow the passage around to another pipe.","Try to go through it. Then right-click on the summoned macaw and remote view.","Go into the south room in the corridor, use the engrammeter.","Take the final memory to Kharshai, receive your reward."],"t":"Finding the memories"}]},"Making History":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the Outpost; an old, now-derelict tower to the north of West Ardougne.\n  - Traveller's necklace teleports directly to the Outpost.\n  - Eagles' Peak lodestone and run south, then south east.","Speak with Jorral for a cutscene. {Chat: 1 Tell me more.}","After the cutscene, agree to help. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Starting the quest"},{"n":"A spade (the one in your tool belt will not work)","r":"","s":["Talk to the silver merchant in the East Ardougne marketplace.{Chat: 3 Ask about the outpost.}\n  - Do not steal from the stall otherwise the merchant will not talk with you.","Ring of dueling to Castle Wars, run north and cross the bridge south of the Observatory.\n  - West of fairy ring ciq and north-west of Yanille lodestone.","When you're just north of the bridge, play hot-and-cold by feeling the key and walking around until it feels steaming hot, and use the spade to dig. (Between the two trees)","Use the key on the chest to unlock it."],"t":"Erin"},{"n":"Ghostspeak amulet, sapphire amulet, and two ecto tokens or enough money to buy a charter boat to Port Phasmatys if Ghosts Ahoy has not been completed","r":"","s":["Speak to Droalak south of the General Store in Port Phasmatys.\n  - Ectophial or Port Sarim lodestone and charter ship to Port Phasmatys.\n  - Wear the ghostspeak amulet.","Talk to Melina in the building east of the General Store with a sapphire amulet in your inventory.","Talk to Droalak again for the scroll."],"t":"Droalak"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Blanin, west of the cow pen in Rellekka.","Talk to Dron, west of the helmet shop. {Chat: 3 I'm after important answers. > 2 Why you're the famous warrior Dron!}","Answer his quiz. {Chat: 2 An iron mace. > 1 Breakfast. > 2 Lunch. > 1 Bunnies. > 2 Red. > 2 36. > 1 8. > 3 Fifth and Fourth. > 3 Northeast side of town. > 1 Blanin. > 1 Fluffy. > 1 12, but what does that have to do with anything?}"],"t":"Dron"},{"n":"Journal, scroll","r":"","s":["Return to Jorral at the outpost, talk to him until he gives you a Letter.","Talk to King Lathas on the floor 2 of Ardougne Castle. (Remove Mourner Outfit if equipped)","Return to Jorral.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Jorral"}]},"Meeting History":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the Outpost.","Speak to Jorral. {Chat: 2 Anything else I can help you with? > Accept}\n  - As needed, accept his offer to bank your items."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"Enchanted key; Nothing else equipped or in your inventory (although bringing the enchanted key notes will be fine).","r":"","s":["Run east to the sheep pen across the river, or run north-west from Ardougne lodestone.","Right-click rub the key in the location shown right (stand on the flowers west of the sheep pen west of the lodestone)."],"t":"The right spot"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Laura.","Rub the enchanted key again.","Return to Jorral and talk to him.","After the cutscene, go back to the location shown above and rub the key again, choosing \"Past - A.\" (Don't forget to bank your traveller's necklace if you used it to get back to the outpost.)"],"t":"The past"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["While in Past A, talk to Jack.","Rub the key, go to Past B, talk to Jack. {Chat: 2 Perhaps you'd spare the time if I read your mind with magic?}","Answer with the following: {Chat: 1 Super Jack The Fantasmic. > 2 Cosmic, mind, body, and fire runes. > 3 Misalionar. > 2 Seven. > 3 Trying to create fire. > 1 Create chocolate cakes. > 1 Good. > 3 Strawberry.}","Go to Past A, take a spade and 6 plant pots from the backyard.","Use the spade or a plant pot on each seedling.","Use the seedling pots on the correct tree spots using this image.","Go to Past B, talk to Sarah about the trees.","Talk to Jack for a cutscene."],"t":"Helping Jack"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to Past A, talk to Roger.","Go to Past B, talk to Sarah.","Go to Past A, search the south-east side table inside to find a pestle and mortar, bucket of milk and a clean guam.","Search the middle shelf (south side) for a bowl.","Use the bowl on the beehive just west of the house.","Use the pestle and mortar on the clean guam.","Use the bucket of milk on the bowl of honey.","Add the ground guam.","Use the bowl of milk, honey and guam on Baby Sarah (right click so that you don't use the bowl on the basket).","Talk to Roger again for a cutscene."],"t":"Healing Baby Sarah"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to Past B, talk to Laura.","Go to Past A, search either the south-western or south-eastern shelves in the house for a papyrus and charcoal.","Use the charcoal on the papyrus.","Give this to Laura.","Go to Past B, talk to Laura."],"t":"A map for Laura"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to Past A.","Inside the house, search the 3 stone bedside tables (One of them should contain the brooch)","Use the brooch on the soil mound west of the shed Laura is building.","Go to Past B, take the spade from the shed.","Dig up the brooch.","Talk to Laura for a cutscene."],"t":"Laura's brooch"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to the present.","Talk to Jorral.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Merlin's Crystal":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to King Arthur at Camelot. {Chat: 1 I want to become a knight of the round table! > Accept}","Talk to Sir Gawain nearby. Ask him how Merlin got stuck in the crystal. {Chat: 3 Do you know how Merlin got trapped? > 2 Thank you for the information!}","Go upstairs, and talk to Sir Lancelot. Ask if he has any ideas on getting into Keep Le Faye. {Chat: 3 Any ideas on how to get into Morgan Le Faye's stronghold?}","Hide in the crate just west of the candle-maker in Catherby. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb to the top floor.","Attack Sir Mordred until his health drops to 0. If you use bleeds/poisons/conjures, future dialogue will be interrupted until the bleed/poison effect ends. Aggressive familiars would continue to attack when Sir Mordred goes back to full health after reaching 0 health, thus restarting the fight.","Talk to Morgan Le Faye. Spare Mordred's life to discover how to save Merlin. {Chat: 1 Tell me how to untrap Merlin and I might. > 2 Okay, I will do that.}","If you do not have bat bones, exit the keep to the west and kill a Giant bat."],"t":"Inside Keep Le Faye"},{"n":"Bucket, Insect repellent","r":"","s":["Talk to the candle-maker in Catherby. {Chat: 1 Have you got any black candles?}","Gather a bucket of wax from the beehives to the north-west. A bucket can be found at the beehives.\n  - If you do not have insect repellent then speak to the beekeeper for some. You can also add it to your tool belt.","Left click the hive to use insect repellent on it and then use an empty bucket on a beehive to fill the bucket.","Talk to the candle-maker again to get the black candle from him."],"t":"Getting a black candle"},{"n":"Bread","r":"","s":["Talk to the Lady of the Lake in southern Taverley. Ask about the sword Excalibur. {Chat: 2 I seek the sword Excalibur.}","Go to Port Sarim.\n  - If you don't have bread, buy a loaf from Wydin's Food Store, just south of the Port Sarim lodestone.","Enter Grum's Gold Exchange to the north of Port Sarim lodestone.","Give the beggar your bread. {Chat: 1 Yes certainly.}","The beggar will turn into the Lady of the Lake and give you Excalibur for your good deed."],"t":"Getting Excalibur"},{"n":"Bat bones, Black candle","r":"","s":["Go to the Temple of Zamorak south of the Varrock east bank.","Check the chaos altar's inscription.","Return to Camelot and enter the gates.","Run north-east outside of the castle to the ritual site (the gazebo outside the castle).","Stand on the star and light the black candle.","Drop the bat bones on the star.","The magic words are \"Snarthon Candtrick Termanto\". If you get this wrong, you will have to get the black candle remade; or click away before proceeding with the dialogue and re-drop the bat bones to try again."],"t":"Ritual"},{"n":"Excalibur","r":"","s":["Enter the castle and climb the top of the south-east tower.","Smash the giant crystal to free Merlin.","Talk to King Arthur.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Missing My Mummy":{"sections":[{"n":"3 backpack spaces","r":"armour and weapons","s":["Talk to Leela, north of the Draynor Village jail. {Chat: accept}\n  - If Leela does not show up in Draynor Village, you need to complete the Stolen Hearts and Diamond in the Rough quests first, even if Icthlarin's Little Helper is already completed.","Enter the flat-topped pyramid Uzer Mastaba from the west side, south of Uzer.\n  - Teleport to the fairy ring DLQ and then run east.\n  - Teleport to Al Kharid and go south to Shantay's Pass (Or use amulet of glory's teleport to Al Kharid).\n  - Use the magic carpet network to get to Uzer.\n  - Teleport with the traveller's necklace to desert eagles' eyrie.","In the initial east chamber, rummage and kill the skeleton for a canopic jar.","Head north-west and through the imposing doors to the south.","Kill the four skeletons in the room for a mummy hand and the scroll of the dead. The mummy hand and scroll of the dead don't appear in area loot, you need to right click to take them.","Return to Leela in Draynor Village. {Chat: 5 I think I can deal with this myself.}"],"t":"Pharaoh's pyramid"},{"n":"Al Kharid flyer, Sq'irkjuice, ring of charos (a)","r":"","s":["The scroll of praise:\n  - Get an Al Kharid flyer from Waseem the Leaflet Dropper north of the Al Kharid mine (at the entrance to the desert).\n  - With your Al Kharid flyer, talk to Reldo in the Varrock palace library about the pyramid. {Chat: 3 I'd like to talk about a pyramid.} or {Chat: 4 I'd like to talk about a pyramid.} He will give you a scroll of praise.","The copied name papyrus and mummy's name papyrus:\n  - Play the Sorceress's Garden minigame and obtain a mug of any sq'irkjuice.\n  - You need to use the sq'irkjuice on Ali Morrisane at his stall. Then talk with him. {Chat: 3 I have some questions about a tomb. > 1 I'm after ways to reunite the mummy in the pyramid. > 4 I can't think of anything sensible to ask.}.\n    - Talk to him again with a ring of charos (a) equipped. {Chat: 3 I have some questions about a tomb. > 1 I'm after ways to reunite the mummy in the pyramid. > 4 I can't think of anything sensible to ask.}.\n    - This step will only work after talking to the Wise Old Man during the Garden of Tranquillity, as the ring does not allow you to persuade people before this step.\n    - You should have received both a copied name papyrus and a mummy's name papyrus.\n      - Do not destroy the copied name papyrus or you will have to re-obtain a sq'irkjuice for another copy."],"t":"Reclaiming the papyri"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to the pyramid with prayer points.","Again, open the imposing door in the north-west corner.","Kill the golem and descend the stairs (You may be placed in the mummy's tomb after descending the stairs, past the puzzle. If so, you will need to cross the puzzle to do the next 4 steps).","Find a path of blue and green blocks or of red and yellow blocks all the way through.","Go across the tiled room and collect the first canopic jar to the west of the northern staircase.\n  - If you spawn at the bottom of the northern staircase simply pick up the canopic jar to the west.","Collect the two remaining canopic jars and mummy with no hand in the tunnels. If you did not collect the fourth earlier, it can be found on one of the skeleton bodies upstairs. \"Rummage\" them and defeat them.","Use the mummy hand on the mummy with no hand.","Return to the tiled room and cross back towards the empty sarcophagus.\n  - You may go upstairs and back downstairs to teleport to the tomb room to skip the tile puzzle."],"t":"Collecting canopic jars"},{"n":"20 fire rune, 1 willow log, jug of wine, spice, empty pot, and wheat","r":"","s":["Place jar on the shelves 4 times.","Fill the empty sarcophagus.","Pray at the 5 broken statues.\n  - This requires 150 prayer points.","Repair the chair and table.","Use spice on your jug of wine.","Use wheat on your empty pot.","Replace the pot and jug.","Run east and kill the shadow. Then light the enchanted sconces in the following order: south, north, west, east. Shadows will spawn and must be killed between each sconce lighting.","Return to the Queen's chamber and create the statue on the empty base, then carve it 2 times.","Talk to the Pharaoh Queen who has appeared in front of the table to give her the 2 papyri and the Scroll of Praise. {Chat: 5 I have nothing more to say.} (Not required for quest completion, only for 100% rebuild)","Right-click check-progress on your scroll of the dead or pyramid journal to verify you've rebuilt the mummy 75%. Otherwise, check any parts missed. (Or 100% if you want to finish the mummy)","Talk to Leela in Draynor Village.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Restoring the tomb"}]},"Missing, Presumed Death":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Brother Samwell (west of Paterdomus and east of Varrock). {Chat: ~ > ~ > Accept}","Search for the following clues.\n  - Investigate northernmost slaughtered monk. {Chat: 2 Investigate torso.}\n  - Investigate nearby plant (east of the chest).\n  - Investigate the tree with the arrow stuck in it (south of him).","Talk to Brother Samwell. {Chat: 2 I think I've found all the clues. > Any}"],"t":"First crime scene"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Up the limestone quarry, speak to Odd Old Man. {Chat: 2 Ask about the slaughtered monks. > 1 Persuade him. > 1 Persuade him. > 2 Threaten him.}","Talk to Brother Samwell. {Chat: 1 He saw an elf heading east along the path. > 1 He saw a very tall, dark, hooded figure escaping. > Any}","Search for additional clues by following the crystals to the east.\n  - Investigate the killed elf ranger (southeast of the Temple). {Chat: 1 Investigate arms. > 4 Listen to the trapped soul.}\n  - Investigate the plant west of her, near the middle pile of crystals next to the stairs.\n  - Investigate the clothing on the fence, to the south of the tree.","Talk to Blaze Sharpeye by the beacon. {Chat: 2 Ask about the murdered elf. > 2 Threaten him. > 2 Threaten him. > 1 Persuade him.}","Return to Brother Samwell. {Chat: 2 I think I've found all the clues. > Any}"],"t":"Second crime scene"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the Wizards' Tower and speak to Wizard Valina inside the entry way on the lectern. {Chat: 2 I was told by Brother Samwell that you might be able to help us. > 1 Ask about the elves. > 2 Ask about Saradominist wizards. > Any > 3 Ask about teleportation.}"],"t":"Valina's information"},{"n":"Combat equipment","r":"","s":["Return to Brother Samwell. {Chat: Any > 5 I think somebody else did this.}","Learn from Icthlarin about Death's disappearance. {Chat: Any > 2 Someone killed these people. > 1 Why does this concern you? > 1 Is everyone who dies trapped now? > 4 Continue. > 1 I'm ready to help.}","Defeat attacking wights.","Finish the conversation with Icthlarin. {Chat: Any > Any}","While standing next to Icthlarin, open the invitation box. {Chat: 1 We must, Death needs our help.}"],"t":"Fighting with Icthlarin"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Once in the citadel, talk to Icthlarin. {Chat: 1 I want to continue to the citadel.} A cutscene will play.","Enter the door to the west then north to the window to watch another cutscene.","Walk out the south window; jump the gap; run across the planks; drop down the rocks; climb up the rock face; walk in the western window.","Climb through the obstacle to the north.","Open the north door, then continue north into the next room.","Pull all three levers in the room (on the west, south, and east walls) to create light.","Lead all the wights that spawn (a group of 3, then 4) into the light to be able to damage them.","View the east window for another cutscene.","Open the door to the north, then continue east into the next room.","Use the viewing panel. {Chat: 3 Stop wasting my time. > 2 What do I do? > Any}, then rotate the bottom-left machine once, the top-left one twice, the top-right three times and the bottom-right machine once.","View the south window for another cutscene.","Open the door to the east, then continue south into the next room.","Talk to the statue of Death. {Chat: 2 Get to the point. > Any > 3 How do I answer?}","Open the chest and take the correct item, then place on the answer plinth pedestal.\n  - First chest (east) {Chat: 3 Take sand.}, place on answer plinth. {Chat: 1 Yes, final answer.}\n  - Second chest (middle) {Chat: 2 Take water.}, place on answer plinth. {Chat: 1 Yes, final answer.}\n  - Second chest, again {Chat: 1 Take Shadow.}, place on answer plinth. {Chat: 1 Yes, final answer.}","View the west window for another cutscene.","Open the south door, then jump off the drop.","Speak to one of the Barrows brothers to enter the main room. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","After a cutscene, walk forward to continue talking with the Gods. {Chat: 1 Let Sliske carry on with his show. > Any > Any > Any}","Run around rear of other gods and stamp out the smaller flames on the ground to reach Death's cage while avoiding the fireballs from Strisath. Free him from his cage.\n  - The flames might be difficult to see with low graphics settings, especially with shadows turned off.","Run back behind Icthlarin.\n  - Getting hit by the fireballs will reset your progress.","Speak to Icthlarin.","Speak with Brother Samwell.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The Citadel"}]},"Mogre (lore activity)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Skippy, south-west of the Port Sarim lodestone. {Chat: 2 Who are (Dramatic pause) THEY?}","'Right-click' Skippy, Sober-Up. {Chat: 1 Throw the water!}","Talk to Skippy again to give him nettle tea.","Make a hangover cure by using chocolate dust on a bucket of milk, then snape grass on chocolatey milk.","Give Skippy the hangover cure.","Activity complete!"],"t":"Getting started"}]},"Monk's Friend":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Brother Omad on the floor 1 of the Monastery south of East Ardougne zoo. {Chat: 1 Why can't you sleep? > Accept}}}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Exit the monastery and head west to the location shown on the map, there is a circle of stones (not visible on the minimap).","Stand in the circle of stones and climb down the ladder that appears. The stones are the same colour as the grass in high graphics modes, and are very easy to overlook.","Go south, enter the room with thieves, and grab the Child's blanket on the table to the east.","Return to the monastery and talk to Brother Omad. {Chat: 1 Is there anything else I can help with? > 1 Who's Brother Cedric? > 2 Where should I look?}}}"],"t":"The secret tunnel"},{"n":"Jug of water, logs","r":"","s":["North of the Monastery and near a crashed cart, Brother Cedric will be wandering around. Talk to him.","Talk to him again to give him a jug of water. {Chat: 2 Yes, I'd be happy to!}","Talk to him once more to give him a set of logs.","Talk to Brother Omad.","Quest complete!","Pop a balloon for area task."],"t":"The party"}]},"Monkey Madness":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to King Narnode Shareen in the Grand Tree. He will give you a gnome royal seal. {Chat: Accept}","Right-click the ladder, select Top Floor, and take the glider from Captain Errdo to Karamja - 'Gandius'. {Chat: 5}","Head north along the coast to reach the shipyard and try to enter through the gate.","Speak with G.L.O. Caranock in the hut southeast of the gate.","Return to King Narnode. He gives you Narnode's orders.\n  - You can return to Captain Klemfoodle to take the glider to The Grand Tree - 'Ta Quir Priw'","Talk to Daero, found on the east side of the floor 2 of the Grand Tree. He is at the Blurberry bar platform. {Chat: 1 Talk about the journey > 4 Return to previous menu > 2 Talk about the 10th squad > 4 Return to previous menu > 3 Talk about Caranock > 4 Return to previous menu > 4 Leave... > 1 Who is it?}"],"t":"Missing 10th squad"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Daero.","Begin the puzzle by clicking on the Reinitialisation Panel to the south-east in front of the long pipe.","Unscramble the puzzle. Caution: The A3 and A5 pieces look near identical and can make the solving the puzzle difficult (A3 should have a straight cloud bottom on the tile and A5 should have a small curve at the bottom right corner of the tile).\n  - You can use this sliding puzzle solver.\n  - Or pay Glough 200,000 coins. He's located in the tree house south-east of the Grand Tree. {Chat: 1 > 1 > 1} Speak to Daero at the Blurberry bar platform to return to the hangar; you will only have to complete the last move in the puzzle if you pay.","There is a cutscene when the puzzle is correct. Speak to Daero and then to Waydar {Chat: 1 Yes.} to fly to Crash Island.","Speak to Lumdo.","Speak to Waydar who will convince Lumdo to follow orders. {Chat: 4 I cannot convince Lumdo to take us to the island…}"],"t":"Solving puzzle before crashing"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Recommended: turn off auto-retaliate and leave it off until the final battle (Can be toggled on/off by clicking the button left of the adrenaline gauge on the Action Bar).","On the island, travel west then north to a bamboo gate. Stand there getting pelted by poisoned arrows until you are brought to a prison. You will take some damage and be poisoned.","Picklock the cell and escape the prison. Stay at least 2 squares away from the guards.","Stay in the grass to hide from archer monkeys and travel south against the western wall of the Temple of Marimbo.","Go east along the wall of the temple and around the monkey palace. Speak to Garkor."],"t":"Ape Atoll"},{"n":"gold bar, ball of wool, monkey bones; recommended = food, antipoison, prayer potion, energy potion","r":"","s":["Head to the U-shaped building in the southern side of the monkey village. Enter through the southern door otherwise you will be knocked out.\n  - Stay on the dark brown ground at the perimeter of the room.","Search the stacked crates two tiles east of the trapdoor for monkey dentures (you can grab another for making a tooth creature).","Search the south-easternmost crate (which is a different style and slightly darker brown) to crawl down into the basement - you may fall and take up to 50% of your life points in damage. {Chat: 1 Yes, I’m sure}","In the northwest corner there's a cluster of crates around a stalagmite; search the crate directly south of the stalagmite for a monkeyspeak amulet mould.","If you needed to leave to obtain items, teleport to Al Kharid, go north, talk to Captain Dalbur to glide to the Tree Gnome Stronghold, then talk to Daero at Blurberry's Bar to return to the hangar {Chat: 1}, Waydar to return to Crash Island {Chat: 1}, and then Lumdo to return to Ape Atoll {Chat: Any}.","If you didn't need to leave to obtain items, go to the area where you first landed on Ape Atoll. There is a one-way shortcut south of Garkor.","Travel west until you see a dungeon on your mini-map. Climb down."],"t":"Zooknock"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Run through the long dungeon.\n  - Protect from Melee is highly recommended here, as are antipoison and energy potions. Make sure to have several pieces of food (and/or Enhanced Excalibur) for healing from the traps and mobs.","At the end of the dungeon (the most north-eastern part), speak to Zooknock first.","Use the gold bar on Zooknock.","Use the monkey dentures on Zooknock.","Use the monkeyspeak amulet mould on Zooknock. He will give you an enchanted bar and your mould back.\n  - If you use the monkey bones on him here you don't need to get new ones when turning in the talisman. Monkey bones from the monkey zombies in the cave do not work. Keep your monkeyspeak amulet mould as it used in Do No Evil.\n  - Make sure you finish the dialogue after giving him the three items and the bones; otherwise, you will not receive the enchanted bar and your mould back. If you leave the area, you will have to run all the way back through this cave to finish the dialogue to get the enchanted gold bar.}}"],"t":"Ape Atoll Dungeon"},{"n":"monkeyspeak amulet mould, enchanted bar, ball of wool, monkey corpse or monkey bones, 5 bananas; recommended = antipoison, food, other types of monkey bones","r":"","s":["Return to Marim (Ape Atoll) (protect from missiles and surge to gate).","Escape prison and run east into the temple.","Take the southern ladder up, the eastern ladder down, and then the trapdoor down into the dungeon.\n  - Alternatively, you can kill one of the two gorilla guards blocking the trapdoor and climb down that way.","Use the enchanted bar on a pillar of fire and use the amulet on a ball of wool to create an monkeyspeak amulet.","Go to the banana garden west of the prison.","Wait for the monkey's aunt to leave and quickly go into the garden through the corridor at its north-east corner.","When she returns, run back into the corridor.\n  - You can stay in the area with red monkey knife fighters if the guards are called and climb the ladder to the south up and back down again.","Equip the monkeyspeak amulet, talk to the monkey child, and talk to him again {Chat: 4 Well I’ll be a monkey’s uncle!}.","Talk to Monkey child again. {Chat: 2 How many bananas did Aunty want?}","You will have to wait for The Monkey's Aunt to pass by the child once again before the child gives you the Monkey talisman.\n  - If you're obtaining multiple for Recipe for Disaster: Freeing King Awowogei, Do No Evil or Monkey butler then repeat the same step as before {Chat: 2 Wow - can I borrow it? > 1 Ok, I promise!} then speak to the Monkey child again. {Chat: 2 I've lost that toy you gave me...}","Take your monkey bones and Monkey talisman and use it on Zooknock at the end of the dungeon under Ape Atoll.\n  - Make sure to make the standard Monkey greegree for the next steps as other forms will not work.\n    - Bring other monkey bones and multiple talismans if you want to make more greegrees and {Chat: 2 > 1} then use your Monkey talisman and different types of monkey bones on Zooknock.\n      - You can use multiple greegrees on each other to save bank space.","Watch the cutscene. Talk to Zooknock to receive your greegree."],"t":"Monkey's uncle"},{"n":"Monkey greegree, monkeyspeak amulet, 1 backpack space","r":"antipoison, food","s":["During this section, do not teleport while you're carrying the monkey or you will have to re-obtain the monkey. This includes spirit tree teleportation.","Enter Ardougne Zoo and equip your greegree near the monkey zone. Speak to the monkey minder.\n  - If you have other monkeys types on your monkey greegree, make sure to swap it to the Karamjan monkey (brown with red cap). Otherwise the monkey minder will say to you that you aren't getting anywhere near his monkeys.","Talk to an unattackable monkey. Unequip the greegree and talk to the monkey minder again.","Run to the Grand Tree and talk to Daero, {Chat: 1} then Waydar, {Chat: 1} and finally Lumdo.","Equip the greegree, pass through the gates.","Return to Garkor by the kings palace (as a monkey) and speak to him.","Talk to the elder guard west of Garkor, they will say you need permission from Kruk.","Head west from the main gate, walk round and up the hill and then cross the bridge to end up on the other side of the hill.","Talk to Kruk, who will grant you an audience with Awowogei.\n  - You may need to talk to Garkor, then with the Elder Guard outside of the throne room first.","Inside the throne room, talk to Awowogei.","Talk to him again to give him the rescued monkey.","Talk to the southern Elder Guard to exit the throne room.","Talk to Garkor, this will start a cutscene.","Talk to Garkor again after the cutscene for the 10th squad sigil."],"t":"King Awowogei"},{"n":"a weapon to kill a level 70 demon, 10th squad sigil; recommended = food, armour, prayer potions","r":"","s":["Right-click 10th squad sigil teleport when you are ready to kill Jungle Demon.\n  - If you rub the sigil with your greegree equipped and with a full inventory, your greegree will drop on the ground.","Kill the Jungle demon.\n  - Prayer flicking between Protect from Melee and Magic (or Deflect Melee and Magic) can prevent most damage. Begin on Protect From Melee, and as the demon begins the animation for the magic attack swap to Protect from Magic, then wait for the hit and switch back to Protect from Melee. Otherwise, remain on Protect from or Deflect Magic.","Speak to King Narnode in the Grand Tree.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Mountain Daughter":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Run north of the Golden Apple Tree south-east of Rellekka (fairy ring code ajr).","Climb the cliffside to the north of the musician with a rope in your backpack.","Talk to Hamal the Chieftain in the nearby village. Ask him why everyone is so hostile and continue through all the dialogue; he will then offer the quest. {Chat: 1 Why is everyone so hostile? > 1 So what are you doing up here? > Accept} (If The Fremennik Trials is completed: {Chat: 2 Why is everyone so hostile? > 1 So what are you doing up here? > Accept})"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Walk south and Dig-below the Roots for a lump of Mud.","If you do not have a pole and a plank, go north of Hamal's house and pick up one of each.","Run north to the lake, then west along the edge.","Use the mud on the tall tree, climb it.","Use your staff/pole on the clump of rocks.","Use your plank on the flat stone.","Stand next to the pile of rocks and listen to one of the shining pools. {Chat: 2 Hello! Who are you! > 2 So what exactly do you want from me? > 1 That sounds like something I can do. > 1 I'll get right on it.}","Use your plank on the flat stone again. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Searching for the daughter"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Hamal the Chieftain. {Chat: 2 About the people of Rellekka... > 1 Why do you hate them so much?}","Talk to Jokul in the goat farm to the north.","Talk to Svidi wandering near the Fremennik lodestone. {Chat: 2 Can't I persuade you to go in there somehow?}","Go to the longhall in Rellekka, talk to Brundt the Chieftain about the Mountain Camp. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Mountain Camp. > Any} (If Lunar Diplomacy has been started or completed: {Chat: 2 Ask about the Mountain Camp. > Any})","Mine the ancient rock in the mountain camp's southern tent.","Return to Brundt the Chieftain in the longhall. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Mountain Camp.} (If Lunar Diplomacy has been started or completed: {Chat: 2 Ask about the Mountain Camp.})","Give the safety guarantee to Svidi.","Make your way to White Wolf Mountain.\n  - If you have completed The Grand Tree, teleport to Al Kharid lodestone, run north-west and click on \"Glider Captain Dalbur\" {Chat: 2 Sindarpos.}","Wearing leather gloves (or gauntlets), pick from the bush next to the gnome glider.","Eat the fruit.","Return to Hamal the Chieftain in the Mountain Camp. {Chat: 3 About your food supplies... > 2 About the people of Rellekka...}"],"t":"Peace and food"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Listen-to the shining pool again.","Jump-across the flat stone, falling into the water, and run east along the northern shore.","Chop down some of the small trees.","Enter the cave.","If you've not fully completed both tasks in the section above and gone through the dialogue completely, you'll receive a message referring to a stench that prevents you from entering the cave. Repeat the tasks until you're allowed to enter the cave.","Talk to the Kendal. {Chat: 1 It's just me, no one special. > 2 You mean sacrifice? > 3 You look like a man in a bearsuit! > 2 Can I see that corpse? > 1 Hand the body over to me!}","Kill the Kendal.","Take the corpse of woman next to all the skeletons."],"t":"The Kendal"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Hamal the Chieftain. {Chat: 2 But he killed your daughter! > 1 I will.}","Take 5 muddy rocks from the camp. They can be found around the mud pond and in the goat pen north of the tent.","Talk to Ragnar by the lake for Asleif's necklace. {Chat: 1 Thank you. I will make sure she's given a proper burial now.}","Bury the corpse in the centre of the lake.","Use the rocks on the burial mound.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The burial"}]},"Mourning's End Part I":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Eluned in Isafdar and agree to get teleported. {Chat: 1 Talk about Mourning's End > Accept}\n  - You can chop a magic log here if you do not have one yet.","Talk to Arianwyn in Lletya. If you leave the town, the fastest way back is to use the crystal seed you were given."],"t":"Meeting the rebels"},{"n":"Combat gear, two pieces of silk, crystal teleport seed, some bear fur, a bucket of water, and 8 free backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Make your way to Arandar. Some ways of getting there are;\n  - Teleporting to the World Gate using the Sixth-Age circuit or teleporting to rune dragons with five metallic dragon trinkets.\n  - Heading to the entrance on the Kandarin side.\n  - Exiting Lletya and heading north on the Tirannwn side.\n  - Using a Traveller's necklace to the Outpost and running west.\n  - Using Home Teleport to Eagles' Peak lodestone and running south.","Kill a mourner. Pick up all pieces of the mourner outfit including the gas mask and mourner letter.\n  - Kill another mourner to obtain extra set of mourner outfit for Within the Light.\n  - You may now want to unequip and bank any combat equipment as you will not need it to progress the quest any longer.","Read the letter.","Go to Taverley and talk to Tegid at the southern lake, south of Jatix.","Search the laundry basket near him to steal the soap. {Chat: 1}","Use it on the bloody mourner top with a bucket of water in your backpack.","Return to Lletya with your crystal teleport seed.","Talk to Oronwen in the clothing shop {Chat: 3 Do you mend clothes?}, talk again. {Chat: 3 I have all I need to mend my trousers.}\n  - Be sure to bring your bear fur and silk. Kill a grizzly bear just west of Lletya if you need bear fur.\n  - This is an opportune time to trade with her and buy dyes while she is fixing the trousers. It is highly recommended you purchase at least 3 of each.","After one minute has elapsed, talk to her again for the trousers.\n  - If your backpack is full, they will be dropped on the floor."],"t":"Mourners in the mountains"},{"n":"Mourner gear, the mourner's letter, a feather, some toad crunchies, leather, a magic log, and one backpack space","r":"","s":["This is a good time to pick up a rotten apple, in the north-eastern corner of West Ardougne. It's on the floor, next to the small building just west of the fenced garden.","Unequip everything but the mourner suit including the gas mask, head to the the Mourners' headquarters (north-east corner inside of West Ardougne).\n  - If you cannot enter the headquarters, re-equip your mourner suit.","Descend the trapdoor and talk to the Head Mourner in the south-east room of the basement. {Chat: 2 Yes > 2 Yes > 1 Yes}","Talk to the gnome on a rack in the west room. {Chat: 3 You said about toad crunchies and being tickled.}","Use a feather on him twice with the toad crunchies in your backpack.","Talk to the gnome again with a magic log and leather in your backpack.","Release him.","After one minute has elapsed, talk to the gnome again for a fixed device. If he disappeared, simply lobby."],"t":"Amongst the Death Guard"},{"n":"Ogre bellows, fixed device, mourner gear, and at least one bottle of dye of each colour: red, blue, yellow, and green","r":"at least 3 of each dye (including green dye)","s":["Travel to the Feldip Hills (fairy ring AKS).\n  - Fetch an ogre bellows from Rantz's cave if you need one. If you already have one, you won’t be able to obtain another from the chest.","Go to the small swamp slightly south-west of Rantz and make the coloured toads.\n  - Do not fill up your ogre bellows, make sure it is empty. If you need to empty it, bloat toads until it is empty before following the next steps.\n  - Use the bottle of dye on your ogre bellows.\n  - Use your ogre bellows on a swamp toad.\n  - Repeat the process for each bottle of dye.\n  - (it is highly recommended that you make multiple of each toad).","Teleport to the Ardougne lodestone, and head to where Brumty's sheep roam to the west.","Use a toad matching the colour of the nearby sheep on the fixed device in your backpack, equip it.\n  - If you are unsure of the colour of the sheep, you can examine it for a description of the colour (red tinge, green tinge, blue tinge, yellow tinge).","Open the equipment tab and fire the fixed device. (Get out of firing mode to see which direction your character is looking at. This way you can avoid having to struggle with finding the sheep with the arrows.)","Use the arrows to aim at a sheep and then press the middle \"FIRE!\" button once it is in the middle of the screen.","Do that for the three other sets of sheep, making sure to match the colour of the toad to the colour of the sheep.\n  - If done correctly, you will no longer be able to prod the sheep.","Return to the Head Mourner and talk to him."],"t":"Dyeing the non-dying"},{"n":"Rotten apple and approximately 20 pieces of coal, you do not need coal if you already have a barrel of naphtha if you made one extra during Regicide","r":"","s":["Take a rotten apple from the ground west of the headquarters.","Talk to Elena, who lives slightly north-east of Ardougne Castle.","With a rotten apple in your inventory, talk to her again.","Wait one minute or world-hop, then talk to her again."],"t":"Elena's advice"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the fenced-in apple orchard Northwest of Ardougne, west of the combat training camp.","Take an empty barrel, use it on the Rotten Apple Pile.","Then use the Apple Barrel located in the middle of the orchard to make apple barrel.\n  - If you don't already have a barrel of naphtha, take one more empty barrel."],"t":"Apples in a barrel"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Skip this section if you have an extra barrel of naphtha from Regicide.\n  - Return to Isafdar, head to the Poison Waste a few steps south of the Tirannwn lodestone.\n  - Fill your barrel with coal-tar.\n  - Go to the fractionation still in Rimmington outside of the chemist's house.\n  - Use the barrel of coal-tar on the still.\n  - Rotate the tar regulator clockwise twice (don't do a complete rotation), to make the tar flow at maximum. The 'pressure' indicator on the left should go up.\n  - When the pressure enters the green region, rotate the pressure valve clockwise once to let out some pressure. This should stall the pressure indicator.\n  - Start adding coal. This raises the 'heat' indicator on the right. If it's below the green region, add more coal. If it's above, don't add coal until it gets lower.\n    - If the heat reading reaches the dark orange portion, you've spoiled your compound and must start again.\n    - If you run out of coal, your progress will be saved, but you will have to re-set the pressure to add more coal to it.\n  - Exit the interface once the green bar is full."],"t":"After the naphtha"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use the barrel of naphtha on the Apple barrel in your Inventory.","Use the apple mix on your sieve. This was given to you by Elena when she identified the toxin.","Use the toxic naphtha on a cooking range to get 2 toxic powder. A range can be found in the Mourner Headquarters.\n  - Do not use it on an open fire, as the naphtha will explode."],"t":"Preparing the poison"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the largest building in the centre of West Ardougne.","Use one of the toxic powder on the sacks in the west room.","Head to the Church (to the south) and poison the second set of grain (located upstairs).","Return to the Head Mourner in the headquarters.","Quest complete!"],"t":"West Ardougne's woe"}]},"Mourning's End Part II":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Arianwyn in Lletya to report your earlier findings if you haven't done this before.","While wearing your mourner outfit (and with nothing else equipped), talk to the Head Mourner under the trapdoor in the Mourner Headquarters located in West Ardougne who will give you the new key. {Chat: Accept}\n  - If you have completed One Small Favour, add the new key to your key ring to save an inventory slot.","Run west through the cave, keep going until you find the dead bodies. Watch the cutscene.","Search the bodies until you find a colour wheel and Edern's journal.","Enter the temple and climb the staircase to the west of the entrance.","Run south and climb up ladder on the south wall.","Run north and climb down and back up the northern staircase.","Run east to the wall, and then south to the crystal.","Search the crystal to receive a blackened crystal. {Chat: 1 Try to chisel a shard off the crystal.}","Make your way back to Arianwyn in Lletya and speak to him. (Use a charged crystal teleport seed if you have one.)","Use the blackened crystal on Eluned who will have appeared next to Arianwyn after talking to him.","Talk to Eluned again to get a newly made crystal.","Talk to Arianwyn again."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go back to the Temple of Light.","Take the stairs to the west to the middle floor.","Head to the area indicated by the rope on the guide map and use your rope on the rocks.","Head to the area marked with mirror #1 just east of the stairs.","Pull the crystal collector on the wall to reset the puzzle.","Next, collect from the crystal collector and take the four hand mirrors and yellow crystal. {Chat: 3 Take all the items.} If you do not get all 4 mirrors, click destroy all in your inventory and re-collect them.\n  - If you need to save inventory space, drop your new key.","Place Hand mirror Mirror #1 on the pillar radiating light. Click on it and rotate to shine the light north.","Hand mirror Mirror #2 points west. (You may refer to clear diagram in the long guide to understand the light path better)\n  - If done correctly, the lightbeam should point west.","Hand mirror Mirror #3 points south.","Place the Yellow crystal. The light will turn yellow","Hand mirror Mirror #4 points east.","Cross the gap to the other side. Use any agility boosts you have. You will have to cross this gap a second time later.","Open then search the chest to obtain two more hand mirrors and a cyan crystal."],"t":"Chest #1"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pull the crystal collector to reset the puzzle.","Collect from the collector to take all the items again. {Chat: 3 Take all the items.}","Hand mirror Mirror #1 points north.","Hand mirror Mirror #2 points west.","Place the Cyan crystal. The light will turn cyan.","Hand mirror Mirror #3 points north.","Hand mirror Mirror #4 points east.","Place the Yellow crystal. The light will turn green.","Open and search the chest to obtain two more mirrors.","Do not reset the puzzle."],"t":"Chest #2"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pick up the Yellow crystal and replace it with Mirror #5 pointing up (east) to the top floor.","Climb the north ladder to the top floor.","Hand mirror Mirror #6 points west. The light to the west turns blue.","Go back to the middle floor and take the south ladder up to the top floor.","Hand mirror Mirror #7 (north west corner) points down toward the middle floor. Long side of the mirror should be on east side.","Climb down the south ladder to the middle floor and go to the bottom floor via the stairs on the east side.","Head to Mirror #8 in the north west corner, going through the eastern yellow barrier. Turn Mirror #8 to point south.","Go through the southern barrier and follow the path. Open and search the chest to obtain 2 mirrors and a fractured crystal.","Go back through the southern barrier and rotate the mirror to point east.","Exit through the eastern barrier.","Do not reset the puzzle."],"t":"Chest #3"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take the east stairs to the middle floor.","Take out the Cyan crystal and replace it with the Yellow crystal. The light will now be yellow.","Climb up the south ladder to the top floor.","Rotate Mirror #7 (north west corner) to shine the light south. This light should be red.","Hand mirror Mirror #8 (all the way south) point down toward the middle floor. Long side of the mirror should be north side.","Climb down the south ladder to the middle floor.","Use the rope shortcut to reach the bottom floor.","Head to Mirror #9 and open and search the chest to obtain a blue crystal."],"t":"Chest #4"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb up rope and return to the crystal dispenser","Reset the puzzle and take all items (10 mirrors and the yellow crystal).","Hand mirror Mirror #1 points north.","Hand mirror Mirror #2 points west.","Hand mirror Mirror #3 points south.","Place the Yellow crystal. The light will turn yellow.","Hand mirror Mirror #4 points east.","Cross the gap to the other side.","Place the Blue crystal (dark blue, not cyan)","Remove Mirror #4.","Run a little north and remove Yellow crystal.","Rotate Mirror #3 pointing up.","Use the south ladder to head to the top floor."],"t":"=Part 1="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Place Hand mirror Mirror #4 in the new position pointing south.","Place the Fractured crystal on the pillar to the south.","Hand mirror Mirror #5 makes the western light point down. (Big part of mirror east)","Hand mirror Mirror #6 makes the southern light point east.","Hand mirror Mirror #7 points down. (Big part of mirror west)","Go to the bottom floor (south ladder and eastern stairs).","Hand mirror Mirror #8 (where green light comes from ceiling, in south west area), points south.","Hand mirror Mirror #9 points east.","Hand mirror Mirror #10 points north.","Open the chest to obtain 3 mirrors and a second fractured crystal."],"t":"=Part 2="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Reset the puzzle. You should have 13 mirrors, 2 fractured crystals, and the yellow, cyan and blue crystals.","Hand mirror Mirror #1 points north.","Hand mirror Mirror #2 points down. (Big part of mirror south)","Use the east stairs to go down to the bottom floor.","Hand mirror Mirror #3 points west.","Place the Fractured crystal. If you don't see four beams coming out of the pillar at this point, remove the Fractured crystal from the pillar and place the other one from your inventory instead.","Hand mirror Mirror #4 points the northern light up (longest side to north)","Place the Fractured crystal south of the first one.","Hand mirror Mirror #5 points the western light up.","Hand mirror Mirror #6 points the eastern light up.","Climb the east stairs to the middle floor.","Go north and place the Yellow crystal. The light will turn yellow.","Climb up the north ladder to the top floor.","Hand mirror Mirror #7 points west. You should see the light turn red at the pillar to the west.","Climb down the north ladder to the middle floor.","Climb up the south ladder to the top floor.","Hand mirror Mirror #8 points west.","Hand mirror Mirror #9 points west.","Hand mirror Mirror #10 points north.","Cross to the north part of the top floor via the middle stairs.","Hand mirror Mirror #11 points west.","Place the Blue crystal. The light will turn blue.","Hand mirror Mirror #12 points south.","Hand mirror Mirror #13 points east.","Go down the middle stairs twice to the inner part of the ground floor.","Rotate Mirror #14 so it points west.","Go through to the death altar.","When you're ready to leave, make sure to turn Mirror #14 back facing east, towards the entrance door, otherwise to get back in here you will have to go through the Underground Pass to get back."],"t":"Death altar Puzzle"},{"n":"50 randomly assigned items or Death talisman or Death tiara, newly made crystal","r":"","s":["Head west, pass through the light door. A small cutscene with Thorgel will ensue.","If you do not have a death talisman/tiara, read the full quest guide for what to do next.\n  - Do not teleport out, or you'll be locked out!\n  - If you teleport out, you can enter deaths altar though Underground Pass, there are cave stairs in the wall south of Niloof to go through.\n  - If you forgot your death talisman, or stuff from the list, be sure to toggle the light back to the crystal so you can leave.\n  - When trying to return to Thorgel, using the Underground Pass is slower (about three minutes instead of two and a half) but there is no risk of being stuck if the mirror is facing the wrong direction. Teleport to the Tirannwn lodestone and then make your way to the cave. From there climb down the well, and go through the big doors. Then you can walk south to the stairs down to the dwarf camp where Klank is. Once in the dwarf camp, there are stairs on the south wall leading down to Thorgel and the entrance to the death altar.\n    - If you intend to use this method to return instead of returning through the Mourner Headquarters entrance and running through Temple of Light, ensure the beam cast by mirror #14 is focused on the final pillar instead of the light door. You will need to be able to reenter the temple to complete the steps below once the talisman has been obtained.","Enter the \"Mysterious\" 'death' ruins.","Use the newly made crystal on the altar, then enter the exit-portal.","Make sure mirror #14 is turned back east towards the entrance door first!","Use the powered newly made crystal on the black crystal (top floor, eastern room in the centre).\n  - You may teleport at this time if needed.","Head back to Lletya and talk to Arianwyn.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Murder Mystery":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to a guard on the Sinclair Mansion property which is located north of Camelot Castle. {Chat: Accept}\n  - You can use fairy ring CJR, then walk south-east to the mansion entrance.}}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take the pungent pot and criminal's dagger and investigate the window to find a criminal's thread.","Search the barrels in the bedrooms owned by the following two suspects for two silver items.\n  - If the thread is red, search the barrels belonging to Bob to the west and Carol upstairs for a silver cup and silver bottle.\n  - If the thread is green, search the barrels belonging to Anna downstairs and David upstairs for a silver necklace and silver book.\n  - If the thread is blue, search the barrels belonging to Elizabeth and Frank upstairs for a silver needle and silver pot."],"t":"House of crime"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the gardener's shed in the very north-west of the mansion and take three flypapers from the sack. {Chat: 1 Yes, it might be useful.}\n  - You must click the sack 3 times.","Use the pot of flour on the dagger.","Use the flypaper on the dagger to lift the fingerprint.","Repeat with the two silver objects.","Compare each fingerprint by using each suspect's print with the unknown print. The unknown print will then turn to the killer's print.","Go to the mansion's gate and talk to Gossip. {Chat: 2 Who do you think was responsible?}","Go to the Forester's Arms in Seers' Village and talk to the Poison Salesman (to get there quickly, teleport to the Seers' Village lodestone). {Chat: 2 Who did you sell Poison to at the house?}\n  - Or if \"The Fremennik Trials\" is started or finished. {Chat: 1 Talk about the Murder Mystery Quest. > 2 Who did you sell Poison to at the house?}"],"t":"The evidence"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to the mansion and talk to the suspect with the matching fingerprint. {Chat: 3 Why'd you buy poison the other day?}\n  - Or if the player still has the criminal's thread with them {Chat: 4 Why'd you buy poison the other day?}","Find evidence. If your quest log says you have conclusive evidence and to talk to a guard, you may skip this step.\n  - If the prints match Bob, search the beehive in the cow pen.\n  - If the prints match Carol, search the drain on the wall directly north of the row of potatoes.\n  - If the prints match Anna, search the compost heap.\n  - If the prints match David, search the spider web upstairs between the two south rooms.\n  - If the prints match Elizabeth, search the fountain.\n  - If the prints match Frank, search the family crest on the outside of the manor building to the east of the entrance."],"t":"A criminal revealed"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to a guard. {Chat: 3 I know who did it!}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Murder on the Border":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Aster in the Town Hall at Fort Forinthry. {Chat: 1 Talk about quests... > 1 Talk about 'Murder on the Border'. > Accept > Any > Any}"],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"12 willow frames and 6 stone wall segments","r":"","s":["Talk to Bill about building the Kitchen. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Murder on the Border'.}","Check plans on the Fort Forinthry blueprints table near Bill and choose Kitchen (Tier 1).","Build the Kitchen located east of the Town Hall. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Building the kitchen"},{"n":"","r":"Combat gear, food, and three empty backpack spaces","s":["Talk to Aster. {Chat: 1 Talk about quests... > 1 Talk about 'Murder on the Border'.}","Click the light blue portal south of the well to start the cutscene. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Watch the cutscene and welcome the guests as they arrive. {Chat: ~ > ~ > ~ > ~}","Talk to three groups of guests in the Town Hall:\n  - Any guest in the central room on the ground level.\n  - Any guest in the western room on the ground level.\n  - Any guest on the second floor.","Talk to Aster in the central room on the ground level. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Yes, let's start the feast'.}","Converse with the guests during the feast cutscene. {Chat: ~ > ~ > ~}","Once the cutscene is completed, continue the conversation with Aster to obtain a mystery journal. {Chat: ~}}}"],"t":"The banquet"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["(1/8) Go back to the Kitchen and investigate the nut roast located on a table in the southeast corner of the room.","(2/8) At the north-west part of the Fort, by the northern gates, investigate the strange satchel beside the rock (southeast of the guards). {Chat: ~}","(3/8) Talk to Simon outside of the Town Hall {Chat: 2 Link a clue to Simon.} and Link \"How to Poison Dummies for Dummies\".","(4/8) Investigate the half-buried box in the northeastern corner of the fort.","Detect the poison:\n  - Investigate the strange satchel again and take a poison detection potion (base). {Chat: 1 Take a vial. > 2 Leave.}\n  - Search the supply cupboard in the Kitchen and take a hollyhock. {Chat: 1 Take hollyhock. > 4 Leave.}\n  - Use the hollyhock on the vial to create an unheated poison detection potion (hollyhock).\n  - Heat the vial on the range.\n  - (5/8) Use the poison detection potion (hollyhock) on the duke's meal (meat pâté) on the dining table. {Chat: 2 Use it on the duke's meat pâté.}","(6/8) Talk to King Roald in the Chapel. {Chat: 1 Talk to King Roald. > 1 Did you notice anything suspicious? > 3 That's all for now.}","(7/8) Go to the Command Centre and speak to Duchess Alba {Chat: 2 Link a clue to Duchess Alba}, and Link the \"Nut Roast\".","(8/8) Talk to Bianca outside the chapel {Chat: 2 Link a clue to Bianca.}, and Link the \"Stolen Jewellery\". {Chat: ~}"],"t":"Part 1"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Ascend to the top floor of the Town Hall and talk to Aster.","Fight the assassin.\n  - If you die, Princess will kill the assassin for you.","Talk to Aster after defeating the assassin.","Search the assassin's body for an assassin's letter then talk to Aster.","(1/8) Speak with anyone outside by the well. {Chat: 1 Talk about the assassin. > ~}","(2/8) Investigate the wax seal outside the northwestern corner of the Chapel.","(3/8) Speak to Iris in the Workshop {Chat: 2 Link a clue to Iris.} and Link the \"Strange Seal\" to obtain the amulet of spanielspeak clue. {Chat: ~}","(4/8) In the Town Hall, investigate the burnt parchment on the floor near the fireplace.","Find the unearthed coffer:\n  - Talk to Princess, the dog, just east of the stonecutter outside the Workshop {Chat: 2 Link a clue to Princess.} and Link the \"Amulet of Spanielspeak\".\n  - Go to the northwestern corner of the fort next to the ladder and speak to Princess. (Princess will follow you.)\n  - Investigate the miscellaneous items that appear.\n  - Stand near Queen Ellamaria outside by the well, then speak to Princess again.\n  - Stand at the altar in the chapel, then speak to Princess once again.\n  - (5/8) Investigate the unearthed coffer (which may be underneath Aster, Princess, or your character).","(6/8) Talk to Duchess Alba in the Command Centre. {Chat: 1 Talk to Duchess Alba. > 2 What's your beef with King Roald? > ~ > 3 That's all for now.}","Talk to Rodney outside the Workshop and ask about Ellamaria. {Chat: 1 Talk to Rodney. > 2 Ask about Ellamaria. > 3 That's all for now}","(7/8) Speak to Rodney again {Chat: 2 Link a clue to Rodney.} and Link the \"Scorched Will\"","(8/8) Speak to Queen Ellamaria outside by the well and ask about being friends with Bianca. {Chat: 1 Talk to Queen Ellamaria. > 2 I heard you were once friends with Bianca. > 4 That's all for now.} and finish speaking with Aster. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm ready.}","Talk to anyone in the courtyard. {Chat: ~ > ~ > ~ > ~}","Identify the murderer as Bianca. {Chat: 5 Bianca Dunnet > ~}"],"t":"Part 2"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to King Roald. {Chat: 1 End the banquet.}","Talk to Aster in the Town Hall. {Chat: 1 Talk about quests... > 1 Talk about 'Murder on the Border'. > ~}","Talk to Rodney in the Kitchen. {Chat: ~}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"My Arm's Big Adventure":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"Bring all items required for the next step","s":["Go to the Troll Stronghold, head south then downstairs into the kitchen.","Speak to Burntmeat. {Chat: Accept > 2 Alright, I'll lend him a hand.}","Talk to My Arm, east of Burntmeat."],"t":"The adventurer"},{"n":"Climbing boots, 3 buckets of Ugthanki dung, 7 buckets of supercompost, 1 empty bucket","r":"","s":["Travel to Burthorpe and head north-west past Troll Invasion.","Climb the rocks and head east past the thrower trolls to reach the Death Plateau.","Search the cooking pot to obtain a goutweedy lump.\n  - If you receive the message \"... but you can't reach very far into it.\", use an empty bucket on the cooking pot.","Return to the Troll Stronghold kitchen and speak to My Arm.","Once on the surface, talk to him near the farming patch.","Read the farming manual he gives you, then talk to him again.","Use the 3 buckets of ugthanki dung and 7 buckets of supercompost on the soil patch.","Talk to My Arm for a cutscene. {Chat: 1 This is My Arm. We'd like to go to Karamja.}"],"t":"Getting the goutweed"},{"n":"At least 1 free inventory space to receive the gout tubers","r":"","s":["Talk to Captain Barnaby if you find yourself in Ardougne.","Talk to My Arm south-east of the Karamja lodestone. He is east of Jiminua's Jungle Store.","Talk to Murcaily, guarding the tree grove north-east of Tai Bwo Wannai. {Chat: 1 A troll called My Arm wants a favour...}","A cutscene will play. Go through the dialogue.","Talk to My Arm south-east of the Karamja lodestone. Continue through the dialogue while on the boat."],"t":"Getting the tubers"},{"n":"Spade, rake, hardy gout tubers, seed dibber, plant cure, combat equipment to fight a level 56 and 77","r":"supercompost","s":["Return to the roof of the Troll Stronghold where the soil patch was.","If you don't already have the farming tools, right-click talk to the Tool Leprechaun to buy some. {Chat: 4 Would you like to trade?}","Talk to My Arm.","Use the following items on him in order:\n  - Rake (twice as he breaks it)\n    - Pick up and use the rake head on the rake handle, give him the assembled rake again.\n  - Supercompost (optional but recommended). Without supercompost, the patch may become diseased and require curing. Regular compost and ultracompost have no effect.\n  - Hardy gout tubers\n  - Seed dibber\n  - If the patch becomes diseased, a plant cure","Defeat the Baby Roc after the cutscene.","Make sure to have a spade or buy one from the tool leprechaun now, to avoid any extra steps after the next cutscene.","Talk to My Arm.","Defeat the Giant Roc that appears after the cutscene."],"t":"Teaching a troll to farm"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to My Arm.","Use a spade on him.\n  - If needed, you can get the leprechaun to come back by climbing the ladder down and up again.","Return to Burntmeat in the stronghold's kitchen and talk to him.","Return to My Arm and speak with him.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The end?"}]},"Myths of the White Lands":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Explorer Jack who is located in a house west of the Lumbridge General Store. {Chat: 2 You mentioned a quest? > Accept > 1 How do I get to the Land of Snow? > 3 Actually, never mind.}","Go to the Wizards' Tower which is located south of Draynor Village.","Talk to Wizard Isidor who is in the west room on the floor 2 of the tower. {Chat: 2 I'm a friend of Explorer Jack and need teleporting.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Players can move diagonally on ice.","This guide does not work for everyone, some people have encountered puzzle rooms in a different order.","If the puzzle is too difficult to solve, either teleport out and then come back or log out (this will allow you to begin from the entrance of the room) and start over."],"t":"The Land of Snow"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["South","North-East","East"],"t":"To the cave"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["North-east","East","North","South-east"],"t":"First cavern"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["East","South-west","East","North","East","North-east","North","West","South","East","South","Go east and \"Clear\" the wall","North off the ramp","West","North","South-east","South","North-east","East","North","East"],"t":"Second cavern"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["North","South-east","North","East","South","East"],"t":"Third cavern"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["North-east","North","East","North","South-east","South-west","East}} {{Hidden|If getting the agility experience|{{Checklist|","South","East","South","West","Climb up the root and study the wall facing south","Relog to start the section from the beginning}}}}"],"t":"Fourth cavern (and Agility Experience)"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["East","North-west","East","South-west","East"],"t":"Fifth cavern"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["East\n  - You will move to the next room and immediately get pushed back by the yeti's scream. This is required to be able to move the blocks.","South-east","East","South","Push block west","South","North-west","Push block north","North","West","North-east","Push block east","East","South","East","Push block north (block is now in place)"],"t":"=Part one="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["West","South","South","East","North","Push block east","East","South","East","Push block north","North","East","North","Push block west","South","West","Push block north","North-east","North","Push block west","South-west","West","North-east","Push block north (block is now in place)"],"t":"=Part two="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["West","South","Exit-room archway back to the fifth cavern."],"t":"=Part three="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["North-East","North-West","East","Squeeze-through crevice.","Go to the crevice to the east (optionally, you can clear the wall just south of the crevice for 20,000 Woodcutting experience. This requires level 80 Woodcutting and is part of the Caving into the Gains achievement).","Squeeze-through crevice.","Study the nearby wall.","Shout-in the pipe.","Go back through both crevices.","West","South-east","East","Go east back into the Yeti room.","Pick up the stones.","Exit west.","Right-click exit-cave on the cavern archway."],"t":"Fifth cavern, again"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Let the imps enchant the stones.","Return to Explorer Jack in Lumbridge. {Chat: 2 About Myths of the White Lands... > Any}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Nadir (saga)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Start by finding a damaged device on Daemonheim floors 18-22.\n  - You might need to talk to Skaldrun to check whether the Nadir saga is already unlocked.","Then start saga with Skaldrun south-west of the Daemonheim entrance."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Wait approximately one minute for Zemouregal and Lucien to finish their conversation.","Finish the dialogue and cutscene then continue north to interrogate the merchant.","Hunt for 3 memories (having sound turned on helps a lot here).\n  - Move your mouse around until the orange circle rapidly beats on one spot and click. There are three speeds--you want to click at the fastest, highest-pitched ping (there are three settings). Repeat until all three memories are recovered.\n  - If only half the memory is recovered, you did not do this step correctly and as a result an unabridged tome will not be awarded, you can lobby to restart the saga.\n  - A pinging sound will play if game sounds are turned on: a slow hum (level 1), a moderately fast ping (level 2, indicating you are close to the correct position), and a fast, high-frequency ping that plays ~2 times a second. This is the correct location for full memory retrieval.\n  - The correct location does not always correspond to the centre of a memory you can see. It can also be an empty space.\n  - Note: On mobile, there is a bug, read the full article to find out how to deal with this.","Continue north and climb down the dungeon entrance."],"t":"The Ritual Site"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Continue east through the door.","Attempt to pass the captain.","Probe 3 memories again.","Continue through the east door, then the south door.}}"],"t":"Frozen floors"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head north through the door and about half way into the room to get a message then leave the same way.","Continue south through the door and finish dialogue with the soldier.\n  - Select \"Got something to get off your chest, soldier? Be my guest.\"","Continue south and then west and finish dialogue with the mage.\n  - Select \"Ask me later, Druf. I have no time for you right now.\"","Continue south through the door and finish dialogue with the soldier.\n  - Select \"Tell them to wait there, and no practice until I return.\"","Continue east.\n  - If you enter combat in this room then you have failed the dialogue options above, restart from checkpoint.","Continue east, south, and south.","Probe 3 memories again.","Kill the necrolord and continue south."],"t":"Furnished floors"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head east and east again. Walk into the centre of the room with bodies. Continue west to view a cutscene.","Exit the room and continue south, then finish the dialogue with the necrolord.\n  - Select \"Cut off their hands.\"","Continue south, west and finish dialogue with the necrolord again.\n  - Select \"Kill him, or I will kill you.\"","Continue west and move into the room. You will move toward both portals and drain their power.","Continue south and finish the dialogue with the necrolord.\n  - Select \"His body is on the floor above. Fetch it yourself, I am busy.\"","Continue east.\n  - If you enter combat in this room then you have failed the dialogue options above, restart from checkpoint.","Continue east and drain the portals.","Continue south, then east.","Kill the Hooved Mage and then drain the portal.","Continue east, kill the four soldiers and two rangers, and then continue east.}}"],"t":"Occult floors"},{"n":"Active standard spellbook","r":"","s":["Drain the power from the portal, then head south and kill the two rangers and three soldiers.","Head east, drain the north west portal and unlock the silver shield door.","Continue east and kill the three soldiers, one ranger, and one mage. Drain the portal power and continue south, drain the portal, and then continue south again.","Kill the two hellhounds and two soldiers drain the portal, then unlock the green pentagon door.","Continue west and kill the three soldiers, one ranger, and one mage. Drain the portals and continue west.\n  - Your adrenaline will stay constant and will no longer drain. Your adrenaline may drain during the following cutscene, but full completion is still awarded.","Continue east, continue dialogue and investigate the ritual marker. {Chat: Any}","Talk to Bilrach. {Chat: 5 Why is the Ritual Marker here? > 4 What is this place? What is it for? > 3 How long have you been here? > 2 Tell me of the portals and their power. > 1 How did you know I was talking to Lucien? > 5 What happens now? > Any}","Saga complete!"],"t":"Warped floors"}]},"Nature Spirit":{"sections":[{"n":"Ghostspeak amulet","r":"","s":["Make sure you have prayer points before starting.","Talk to Drezel, who is located underground near Paterdomus. The entrance is north from the temple's door. You should have six empty backpack space; otherwise the food he gives you will appear on the floor.\n  - If you have lost Wolfbane: {Chat: 2 Talk about something else. > 2 Is there anything else interesting to do around here? > Accept > 4 Yes, I'll go and look for him. > 1 Yes, I'm sure.}\n  - If you have Wolfbane in your bank or backpack: {Chat: 2 Is there anything else interesting to do around here? > Accept > 4 Yes, I'll go and look for him. > 1 Yes, I'm sure.}\n  - If you have just completed Priest in Peril, then you might need to exit and reenter the Mausoleum before the quest dialogue will appear. Drezel should be standing in the last chamber before the holy barrier.","Exit into Morytania and travel south to a fence.","Look along the fence for a gate and go through it.","Go south until a round island is found with a grotto tree.","Jump across the broken bridge and onto the island."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Search the bench nearby for a small mirror.","Search the grotto tree for Filliman's journal.","Equip your ghostspeak amulet and talk to Filliman Tarlock. {Chat: 2 How long have you been a ghost? > 2 So, what's your plan? > 4 How can I help?}\n  - He'll give you a druidic spell."],"t":"The ghost of the grotto"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Drezel to be blessed and teleported back to Filliman.\n  - If you have lost the wolfbane: {Chat: 2 Talk about something else. > 1 Yes, please}\n  - If you have the wolfbane in your backpack or bank: {Chat: 1 Yes, please}","Jump the bridge and find a nearby rotting log in the swamp.\n  - There is some directly West of the Grotto tree island.","Cast the druidic spell in your backpack, then pick the fungus from the log.","Take the Mort myre fungus mushroom from the log and talk to Filliman.","Use the Mort myre fungus on the western, yellow stone.","Use a used spell on the eastern, grey stone.","Stand on top of the southern, orange stone in the centre by right-click selecting \"Walk here\".","Tell Filliman the puzzle is solved. {Chat: 3 I think I've solved the puzzle!}","Enter the Grotto tree.","Search the Grotto in the centre.","Continue speaking with Nature Spirit {Chat: 4 Ok, thanks.} and he will ask you for a silver sickle."],"t":"Becoming a nature spirit"},{"n":"Silver sickle, at least 1 prayer point","r":"","s":["Obtain a silver sickle via:\n  - Purchasing it from the Grand Exchange.\n  - Crafting one yourself:\n    - Obtain a sickle mould from a Crafting shop or the Grand Exchange. You may add it to the tool belt.\n    - Smelt at a furnace with a silver bar. Select \"silver bar\" under \"Casting Metals & Glass\" section on the interface, and then select the \"silver sickle\" option in the \"Silver Casting\" section.","Return to the grotto either by speaking to Drezel {Chat: 1 Yes, please}, or by navigating via the Morytania Swamp.","Enter the grotto tree.","Talk to the Nature Spirit with a silver sickle in your backpack. He will bless it for a silver sickle (b).","Exit the grotto, jump the bridge into the swamp and stand next to the nearby rotting log.","Right-click Bloom the silver sickle (b) in your backpack. Blooming requires at least 1 prayer point.","Pick the fungi from the log. You will need at least 3 total fungi (ghasts can rot the contents of the pouch).","Fill the druid pouch in your backpack to add the fungi into it.","Invoke and kill 3 nearby ghasts, consuming 1 fungus per invocation."],"t":"Killing the ghasts"},{"n":"3 backpack spaces","r":"","s":["If you drop anything to receive the rewards, it will be lost.","Return to the Nature Spirit in the grotto.","Quest complete!","(Optional) Pray at the altar to complete one of the easy Morytania achievements, Fortified Spirit."],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Necromancy!":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Interact with the white portal north of the Draynor lodestone. {Chat: Accept}","Speak to Death.","After the cutscene ends, speak to Death again."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Malignius Mortifer.","Clear the mounds of dust around the ritual site.","Place the bones on the pedestal.","Speak to Malignius again.","Place the basic ritual candles on the four pentagon-shaped light source spots around the ritual site.","Speak to Malignius again.","Draw the Commune I glyph on a nearby glyph spot. Repeat this again at another glyph spot.","Speak to Malignius again.","Repair the broken glyph.","Stand on the nearby skull platform."],"t":"Communion ritual"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After the dialogue, manage the Well of Souls.","Select the Conjure Skeleton Warrior talent at the bottom of the interface.","Wield the death guard that Sostratus gives you.","Kill the nearby ghost troll brute and ghost troll lout.","Interact with the Well of Souls again, and unlock the Conjure Skeleton Warrior talent.","Speak to Malignius Mortifer.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The Well of Souls"}]},"New Foundations":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the New Foundations portal outside King Roald's throne room in Varrock Palace. {Chat: 1 Yes}","After the conversation has ended, enter through the door and talk to King Roald. {Chat: Accept}","After the cutscene, talk with King Roald. {Chat: 2 Sign me up!}"],"t":"The beginning"},{"n":"","r":"Combat gear and food","s":["Travel north-east from Varrock, near Jolly Boar Inn and the easternmost boundary of the Wilderness wall.\n  - Fastest way to get there is by teleporting to the Infernal Source Dig Site and run slightly north-east (need level 20 Archaeology).\n  - Alternatively, just use Archaeology journal and then head north.","Click the portal to \"Continue New Foundations\". {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Defeat the armoured zombies.","Talk to Bill towards the north of the well.","When the chat has ended, go southwest to the Fort Forinthry blueprints (table behind the bank chest) to build the Workshop."],"t":"Saving Bill the architect"},{"n":"8 wooden frames and 6 stone wall segments","r":"96 planks or 96 logs, and 24 limestone bricks or 24 limestone to make the required items","s":["Check the plans with the Fort Forinthry blueprints and start building the Workshop (Tier 1) which requires:\n  - 6 stone wall segments (can be made from 24 limestone bricks)\n  - 8 wooden frames (can be made from 96 planks)","Build the Workshop by interacting with one of the six Construction hotspots around the edges of the Workshop area.\n  - The optimal Construction hotspot moves periodically but improves the progress slightly.","Talk to Bill."],"t":"Building the Workshop"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the Blue Moon Inn in Varrock and talk to Aster (outside by the tables).","Head to Gunnarsgrunn (Barbarian Village) and talk to Overseer Siv (centre of the village).","Head to Draynor Village and speak to Father Flint in the Draynor Village marketplace.","Head back to the fort and speak to Bill."],"t":"Recruiting help"},{"n":"20 planks and 82 stone wall segments","r":"20 logs, and 328 limestone bricks or 328 limestone to make the required items","s":["Proceed to build the fortifications around the fort. The order does not matter.","Find the appropriate hotspot located within the area."],"t":"Building the fortifications"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Front gate\n  - 6 stone wall segments (can be made from 24 limestone bricks)\n  - 10 planks","Rear gate\n  - 6 stone wall segments (can be made from 24 limestone bricks)\n  - 10 planks","West wall\n  - 10 stone wall segments (can be made from 40 limestone bricks)","North-west wall\n  - 5 stone wall segments (can be made from 20 limestone bricks)","North wall section 1\n  - 10 stone wall segments (can be made from 40 limestone bricks)","North wall section 2\n  - 10 stone wall segments (can be made from 40 limestone bricks)","North-east wall\n  - 5 stone wall segments (can be made from 20 limestone bricks)","East wall\n  - 10 stone wall segments (can be made from 40 limestone bricks)","South-east wall\n  - 5 stone wall segments (can be made from 20 limestone bricks)","South wall section 1\n  - 5 stone wall segments (can be made from 20 limestone bricks)","South wall section 2\n  - 5 stone wall segments (can be made from 20 limestone bricks)","South-west wall\n  - 5 stone wall segments (can be made from 20 limestone bricks)"],"t":"Fortifications"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Once all structures have been built, talk to Bill and finish the dialogue.\n  - The title you choose may be changed afterwards.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Nomad's Elegy":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Make sure you have combat equipment (but not your familiar yet) from this point. If you die, you will be returned to Death's office and will have to leave and re-enter via Death's Hourglass (i.e. not War's Retreat) to resume progress with the quest.","Speak to Zimberfizz in the Soul Wars area. {Chat: 2 Talk about Nomad's Elegy > Accept}","Investigate Nomad's tent to the east.","Investigate the throne, some crystals to the west, and sticky goo south of that.","Investigate the strange emissions to the southwest. You will be sent to Death's Realm.","Go through the dialogue and travel through Death's door to the north (the mosaic of Death behind his desk)."],"t":"Beginning"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Death again. {Chat: 1 What do we need to do now? > 5 I have to go.}","Embark on the Bloodstained Jetty to the north-east. (You cannot bring a familiar here.) {Chat: 1 Yes}","If you leave the Underworld, you can return by entering Death's Office from Draynor. Do not enter from War's Retreat.","Defeat oncoming waves of Bandosians to protect the cave goblins. There are three waves, and progress is saved after each wave. Aggression potions can help, though some of the Bandosians can slip past."],"t":"Freeing Zanik"},{"n":"2 free inventory spaces","r":"","s":["Embark on the Dusty Jetty to the north-west. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Speak to Astrid/Brand."],"t":"Gathering your allies"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Korasi/Jessika in the house north of Bob's Brilliant Axes.","Travel to the south-west of Lumbridge Castle grounds. Speak to Wizard Grayzag for half of Korasi's/Jessika's memories. {Chat: 1 I'm not Korasi/Jessika. > 3 My name is Korasi/Jessika. > 2 Wizard Grayzag? > 2 You represent danger. > 4 I am not afraid of you! > 1 Then I won't fail.}","Travel to the floor 2 of the Lumbridge Castle wall using the southern gate ladder (not within the main castle keep), and speak to the person you saved in The Void Stares Back to recover the other half of Korasi's/Jessika's memory.","Combine the memory halves.","Return Korasi's/Jessika's completed memory to her north of Bob's Axes."],"t":"Jessika/Korasi"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Hazelmere on the floor 2 of Lumbridge castle.","Find and talk to him again on the floor 2 and above on the floor 4 above where the bank normally is by using the ladder on the north side of the building.","Climb either of the two tower ladders of the castle gate (not within the main castle keep); he will be on the floor 3.","Speak to Hazelmere in what would normally be Bob's Axes.","Speak to Hazelmere west of Lumbridge Castle.","Speak to Hazelmere next to Astrid/Brand. {Chat: 1 I need you to help me fight Nomad.}"],"t":"Hazelmere"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Xenia in the Lumbridge Castle floor 1. {Chat: Any}","Attempt to open the chest in the northern room on the floor 2.\n  - Kill Guilt, pick up the guilt ridden key, then open and search the chest for a Xenia memory half. The key will not drop if you are in a group.","Climb to the floor 3 and attempt to open the chest in the room.\n  - Kill Shame, pick up the shame filled key, then open and search the chest for a other Xenia memory half.","Combine the memory halves and return the completed memory to Xenia.","Talk to Astrid/Brand. {Chat: Any}","Enter the portal to leave. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Xenia"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Plan the war table in the centre area.","Begin interrogating Legio Septimus. The player has the option to kill him outright by repeated torture which will end this section quickly, or to make his willpower low and restore his sanity high, so he answers your questions truthfully which unlocks a shortcut in the battering ram battle later.\n  - To kill him outright, select Threaten him, then 'remove' crystals until Legio dies. {Chat: 1 [Ask him about subject] > 1 Tell me about Nomad. > 1 What is Nomad's plan? > 2 Who was Nomad's master? > 3 Tell me about Nomad's defences. > 4 How do I defeat him? > 5 [Back] > 2 Tell me about the Order. > 1 What is the order up to? > 2 What do they need the souls for? > 3 Why are you working with Nomad? > 4 [Ask something else] > 2 [Threaten him] > 2 [Threaten him] > 2 [Threaten him] > 2 [Threaten him] > 2 [Threaten him] > 3 ['Remove' crystals] > 3 ['Remove' crystals] > 3 ['Remove' crystals] > 3 ['Remove' crystals] > 3 ['Remove' crystals] > 3 ['Remove' crystals] > 3 ['Remove' crystals] > 3 ['Remove' crystals] > 3 ['Remove' crystals] > 3 ['Remove' crystals]}\n  - To fully interrogate him instead, threaten him until it is no longer effective. Then use Zanik's Good Cop option and Xenia's Bad Cop option until his sanity is about 50%. Then use Charm to lower his willpower to about 50% as well. Finally raise his sanity back up to about 80% using Zanik's Bad Cop option and Xenia's Good Cop Option. Ask the questions, and his answers should be sane and cooperative. Once answered, choose whether to kill or release him (choice currently has no effect on future events)"],"t":"Interrogation"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Click the war table and select any two companions.","Collect 25 wood and 25 metal. You can put both companions on the same material; by the time you complete the other, they will be finished.","Leave through the exit once complete.","Build the battering ram to the north (takes a few minutes while dialogue plays).","Return to the war table.","Slowly walk the battering ram across the bridge and through the doors.","Suggestion 1: Put Zanik north-west by battering ram, Death north-east and the remaining four block off the start of the bridge while fighting.","Suggestion 2: Place your companions three on each side of the ram, and stand on the bridge's edge blocking off all the monsters while using an aggression potion which requires level 82 Herblore. Fight or withstand the attacks until the ram is done.","Choose to either head north and assault the fortress head-on, or if you unlocked the information in the earlier interrogation, detour through the east door and enter the secret passage in the north wall of the cave, which will bypass the second half of the assault.","Once inside, you'll have to fight Nomad."],"t":"Battering ram"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Dwindle away Nomad's health, and move away from the centre of the bridge to avoid Gielinor's hand. Also move away from shadows that appear on the ground to avoid rapid powerful magic attacks. Use Surge if you can."],"t":"First combat phase"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Stand in the middle of each of the three sections in the area and constantly use the 3 abilities made available. Move to the next one when one side is finished.\n  - Use Fire Blast when Rorarii are present.\n  - Use Shield Dome when Gladii are present.\n  - Use Shadow Stalk when Scutarii are present.\n  - Every time you attack a Capsarii, it will heal Xenia for a small amount."],"t":"Xenia"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["In addition to the previous phase's attacks, when Nomad teleports you near him and orders you to 'face his wrath', switch to your shield to use Resonance to negate any and all damage from the attack."],"t":"Second combat phase"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go directly north, south, east and west of Gielinor. Each time provoking him and quickly getting out of the way, to then use Scythe on the hand, and finally claim the released spirit."],"t":"Death"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["In addition to the previous phases' attacks, Nomad will create a clone of himself when he reaches half health. Kill them both (you might kill Nomad first, in which case you will move on)."],"t":"Third combat phase"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Quickly and without stopping, run around the area anti-clockwise, releasing the souls as you get in the middle of a group of them. Make sure to get over half of the initial total number of spirits.","The more souls you release, the more powerful the attack reflected onto Gielinor will be.","Once all souls have been released, continue circling until Gielinor stops firing the beam, then shield yourself from Gielinor's attack with the ability, in order to reflect the damage onto Gielinor.","You will have to repeat this process a few times."],"t":"Icthlarin"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["In this phase, Nomad will only be using rapid melee attacks. Kill him by any means. If using Ranged, Magic or Necromancy, then you can run around the room to avoid damage from Nomad, using Surge to gain distance. Watch out for Gielinor's attacks. Protect from Melee or Deflect Melee, especially combined with Devotion, can reduce or negate much of Nomad's damage in this phase, though the speed of his attacks can still be problematic."],"t":"Final combat phase"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Choose who ends Gielinor. {Chat: Any}","Decide Nomad's fate. {Chat: Any > Any > Any}","After the cutscene, speak with Death. {Chat: Any}","Choose Zanik's fate. {Chat: Any > Any > Any}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Aftermath"}]},"Nomad's Requiem":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to Edgeville and run south-east into the Soul Wars portal.","Talk to Zimberfizz the imp in the lobby. {Chat: Accept}","Investigate Nomad's tent and watch the cutscene."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Nomad. {Chat: 2 Zimberfizz sent me here to see where you went.}","Go up the ladder.","Talk to Zimberfizz. {Chat: 1 Talk about Nomad's Requiem.}","Investigate the tent."],"t":"The hidden temple"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the south-western doorway.","Climb up the south-eastern ladder and pull the north lever.","Climb up the north-eastern ladder and move both pillars over the drains.","Climb down the ladder and make sure that water is flowing through the southern channel. If it is not, operate the levers until it is. The symbol at the top of a pillar represents the direction of water flow through the pillar.","Climb down the south-eastern ladder and complete the puzzle. A solution is pictured to the right and another solution is right below. Click on the statues in the following order:\n  - Centre, west statue\n  - North, west statue\n  - North, centre statue\n  - North, east statue\n  - Centre, east statue\n  - South, east statue\n  - South, centre statue\n  - Centre, centre statue\n  - North, centre statue\n  - North, east statue\n  - Centre, east statue\n  - South, east statue\n  - South, centre statue\n  - South, west statue\n  - Centre, west statue\n  - North, west statue\n  - North, centre statue\n  - North, east statue\n  - Centre, east statue\n  - South, east statue"],"t":"Water"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb up the ladder.","Mine the rubble at the tunnel at the end of the eastern channel","Pull the southern lever until water flows to the new tunnel.","Climb down the ladder to the bottom floor.","Enter the northern doorway,","Enter the south-eastern doorway.","There should be a waterfall in this room. If water is only dripping, the levers were not operated properly.","Take some Elemental fuel out of the Fuel hopper located at the north-eastern or south-eastern corner of the room (take 6 if following the solution pictured to the right).","Lure an Elemental creature out of the strange device and into the waterfall by placing the fuel on the floor.","Do the above step a total of three times.","Exit the room through the northern doorway."],"t":"Elementals"},{"n":"Combat gear, weapons, food","r":"","s":["Enter the arcane doorway and then enter the western doorway.","Attempt to destroy a root surrounding the strange device.","Follow the vines on the floor and destroy four lone roots to which the vines lead.","Go back to the strange device.","Kill the Decaying avatar. Destroy the roots when they appear at the corners of the room. Strategies can be found here.","Exit the room through the eastern doorway."],"t":"Vines"},{"n":"Magic weapon, fire runes, air runes, 5 free inventory spaces, Restore potions or standard prayers","r":"","s":["Talk to the knight near the eastern doorway.","Before entering the next room, consider turning on Piety to avoid constant damage and stat reduction or bringing a super restore potion to keep your magic level high enough to cast a fire spell. The Corruption beasts inside restore prayer upon death.","Enter the eastern doorway.","Pick up five stone slabs (Take-slab from the rubble piles all around the room).","Place the stone slabs to complete and cross the bridge across the central body of water.","Ignite the barrels with a magic weapon equipped and a fire spell active (75 Magic required to ignite the barrels).","Cross the bridge and exit the room through the western doorway."],"t":"Smoke"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Make any necessary preparations to fight Nomad. You can teleport out, and bank to prepare for the fight.","To return to the area, teleport to Edgeville, enter into the Soul Wars portal, and investigate the tent again.","Enter the arcane doorway at the northern wall then the arcane doorway on the inner southern wall. {Chat: 1 Yes. > Any}","Kill Nomad. (Deathtouched darts work)","Strategies can be found here. Recommended if you haven't fought him before.\n  - If you are a high combat level (130+) and have tier 80 gear or higher, you will likely kill him easily without worrying about his final stun ability. Bring high-healing food like shark or sea turtle and just keep attacking him and healing while standing directly beside him.\n  - In short; bombs laid on the floor deal 4,000 damage when stepped on.\n    - Avoid them by walking DIRECTLY south, he does not place one there.\n  - \"You cannot hide from my wrath\" deals 7,500 damage. Either eat above that or hide behind a pillar.\n  - If he summons clones, the real one attacks you last, otherwise kill them all.\n    - An alternative is hide from them, after about 90 seconds the three fake ones will despawn. Make sure to re-attack him quickly after this so he does not reset, he does not use \"Face me!\" while clones are present.\n  - \"Face me!\" if he doesn't hit you in time, he restores his life points and teleports you. For example, if you were hiding behind a pillar.\n  - Towards the end of the fight he teleports you to the centre and stuns you. The next attack deals all your maximum life points, minus 1. So eat to full.\n    - If you bring a shield, swap to it and use resonance. This blocks the attack 100% but does not heal you.\n  - \"This. Ends. Now\" starts attacking you rapidly. It's important to finish him off at this point and not hide, otherwise he will restore his life points and you'll have to restart the fight."],"t":"Nomad"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Zimberfizz. {Chat: 1 Talk about Nomad's Requiem. > Any}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Observatory Quest":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Observatory professor in the house near the Observatory which is located north of Castle Wars. {Chat: 1 Talk about the Observatory Quest. > 2 An Observatory? > Accept}","Obtain a bronze bar, 3 planks, and molten glass.","Talk to the professor three times (until he takes all of the above items). {Chat: 1 Talk about the Observatory Quest.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Leave the house and go east to the abandoned buildings.","Climb down the stairs in the western building.","Open and then search specific chests for a goblin kitchen key.\n  - Be sure to finish the dialogue after searching to receive the key.\n  - Every dead end will have a searchable chest. Head south (and slightly east) first and if the key is not found in the two chests directly south from the stairs, it is guaranteed to be in the far south-east chest in the dungeon.","Go back to the staircase at the entrance, but do not exit the dungeon.","Go east, then north, and then head west until a guard is seen guarding a kitchen.","Kill him or lure him away from the kitchen.","Inspect the stove in the kitchen to receive lens mould.","Return to the surface and talk to the professor. {Chat: 1 Talk about the Observatory Quest.}","Use the lens mould on the molten glass.","Talk to the professor. {Chat: 1 Talk about the Observatory Quest.}"],"t":"Obtaining a lens"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go back to the abandoned building and climb down the stairs.","Head to the southern section and climb the stairs to the observatory, as indicated on the map.","Watch the cutscene.","Go upstairs. Look through the telescope and identify which constellation is seen (see table below).}} :{| class=\"wikitable\" !Name !Picture !Name !Picture !Name !Picture |- |Aquarius | |Aries | |Cancer | |- |Capricorn | |Gemini | |Leo | |- |Libra | |Pisces | |Sagittarius | |- |Scorpio | |Taurus | |Virgo | |} {{Checklist|","Talk to the professor and tell him which constellation was seen. {Chat: 1 Talk about the Observatory Quest. > ?}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Ode of the Devourer":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Read note on the cabbage dummy at Fort Forinthry's Workshop. {Chat: Accept}","Talk to Overseer Siv in the Command Centre to the south-east. {Chat: 2 Talk about quests.}"],"t":"Visiting Bill"},{"n":"Combat equipment","r":"","s":["Continue with the Ode of the Devourer portal west of the Al Kharid lodestone. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Kill the feline akhs near the following civilians, then save them by fully finishing their dialogue:\n  - Ali Morrisane, south of Ranael's Super Skirt Store.\n  - Ayesha, north of the tanner's building.\n  - Zeke, between three tents, east of the silk stall.","Crawl under the cart south of the Al Kharid bank.","Kill the feline akh.","Talk to Bill."],"t":"Finding Bill"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the City of Um northern docks.","Take the gondola that's located next to where the Suspicious Stranger was sitting.","Continue with the Ode of the Devourer portal outside the Sanctum of Rebirth. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Icthlarin. {Chat: 4 Continue Quest.}","Enter the floor hatch in Fort Forinthry (outside the eastern wall of the Command Centre). {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Zemouregal. {Chat: 1 Find the idol of Amascut.}"],"t":"Icthlarin and Zemouregal"},{"n":"1 free backpack space","r":"4 free backpack space to save banking for next section","s":["Continue with the Ode of the Devourer portal south-west of the Kalphite Hive (Fairy code BIQ). {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 What's he talking about? > 3 Not much. Tell me the abridged version. > 3 Continue Conversation.}","Continue with the Ode of the Devourer portal outside Al Kharid's north-eastern entrance. If the game is bugging out and there is green fog everywhere then change the skybox. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Father Salman just north of Zeke's Superior Scimitars.","Talk to Ali Morrisane north-east. {Chat: 2 Look for a different option.}","Walk five game squares away.","Talk to Zemouregal.","Talk to any 5 citizens around the city with an option to spread rumours about Ali Morrisane. {Chat: 1 Spread rumours about Ali Morrisane.}","Talk to Ali Morrisane.","Talk to Father Salman."],"t":"Idol of Amascut"},{"n":"3 free backpack space","r":"","s":["If you haven't completed Ritual of the Mahjarrat:\n  - Return to Fort Forinthry.\n  - Talk to Zemouregal. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Ode of the Devourer'. > 1 Travel to the ritual site.}","If you have completed Ritual of the Mahjarrat:\n  - Use fairy ring DKQ to travel to the Glacor Cave, leave via the exit to the north-east, then run north-west.\n  - Continue with the Ode of the Devourer portal near the ritual marker. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Icthlarin. {Chat: 3 Continue Conversation.}","Search the north-western and south-eastern forgotten warriors.","Talk to Zemouregal.","Use the absorption rune on the ritual marker twice.","Use the ceremonial dagger on the ritual marker to receive Shard of the Gate. {Chat: 1 Do it.}","Talk to Zemouregal."],"t":"Shard of the Gate"},{"n":"Idol of Amascut and shard of the Gate","r":"combat equipment for the next part","s":["Carry an almost empty backpack and your best mining equipment, plus 10 pieces of food and a beast of burden.\n  - Optionally follow The Gate of Elidinis strategy article for help on gear setup.","Continue with the Ode of the Devourer portal outside the Sanctum of Rebirth. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Icthlarin.","Receive blessing on the idol of Amascut or the shard of the Gate.","Enter The Gate of Elidinis stream.","Cleanse The Gate of Elidinis.\n  - Begin the encounter. Staying south of the moonstone conduits will make learning The Gate of Elidinis encounter easier.\n  - Gather 25-40 moonstone fragments from nearby moonstone outcrops. Moonstone fragments provide 10% barrier strength per repair action on any of the moonstone conduits. Moonstone fragments also deal 7,500 damage per throw to summoned feline akhs by clicking on the feline akhs.\n  - Repair any of the moonstone conduits located in the middle of the encounter with moonstone fragments until the barrier's strength reaches at least 30%. Staying south of the moonstone conduits will use their barrier strength to reduce the damage taken from each \"Begone!\" mechanic proportional to the barrier's strength. This mechanic also depletes up to 30% of the barriers strength.\n  - Transmute any corrupt shard of Elidinis until it becomes a cleansed shard of Elidinis. Transmuting adds corruption stacks which increases the damage the player takes over time in the encounter.\n  - Mine the cleansed shard of Elidinis to obtain cleansed statue shards.\n  - Activate the action button once 10+ cleansed statue shards have been collected to ask Icthlarin for aid. This will spawn pillars to help the player jump up to The Gate of Elidinis, consuming all the cleansed statue shards on them and applying a damage bonus depending on how quick the player performed all the jumps. Corruption stacks decrease by the amount of cleansed statue shards consumed with the jump.\n  - Stand within Icthlarin's protective shield after performing all the jumps. Icthlarin's shield will mitigate the incoming attack. The attack also depletes all the barrier strength from the moonstone conduits.\n  - Keep collecting cleansed statue shards by transmuting corrupt shards of Elidinis and mining cleansed shards of Elidinis, using the action button as needed, repairing the moonstone conduits as needed, and clicking on summoned feline akhs to throw moonstone fragments at them."],"t":"Cleansing The Gate of Elidinis"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Carry your highest level combat equipment, food and potions.","Proceed through the cutscene. {Chat: 3 Meow.}","Kill the four waves of monsters.\n  - Pray against melee. The easiest way to beat this is to stay close to Icthlarin constantly, and attack the monsters that come near you.\n  - Stay inside the green barrier to avoid instant kills occurring when the timer at the top runs out."],"t":"The Shadowsands"},{"n":"7 free backpack space","r":"","s":["Proceed through the dialogue. {Chat: 3 We all got what we wanted.}","Talk to Zemouregal. {Chat: 2 Send Zemouregal to the Fort Forinthry Prison.}","Enter the floor hatch in Fort Forinthry. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Bill.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Aftermath"}]},"Olaf's Quest":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Olaf Hradson north-east of Rellekka. {Chat: Accept}","Go east up the icy mountain and chop the windswept tree.","Return and talk to Olaf."],"t":"Family honour"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to Rellekka and talk to Ingrid Hradson next to the well in the south-east.","Head north and talk to Volf Olafson who is wandering outside the helmet shop.","Return and talk to Olaf.","Use the damp planks on the embers on the ground next to him.","Talk to Olaf. {Chat: 1 Alright, here, have some food. Now give me the map.}","Read the map."],"t":"The windswept tree"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go back up the icy mountain and dig west of the windswept tree (left-click a pile of snow).","Once inside the caverns, follow the path east and then north, continuing along the northern path until you reach a \"picture wall\" door.","Kill a nearby skeleton and pick up the key that it drops from the ground.","Search the door and solve the puzzle:\n  - Down\n  - Right\n  - Left\n  - Up\n  - Bottom","Search the door again to pass through."],"t":"Brine Rat Cavern"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["In the next area, pick up two rotten barrels and six ropes.","Head towards the north-east walkway made of planks and use rotten barrels on the gaps in the walkway.\n  - Make sure you walk over all obstacles here, running will give you a 100% failure rate.\n  - Toggle by clicking the Energy button.","Open the gate by clicking the keyhole that matches the key (e.g. if the bottom of the key is triangle, then it goes into the triangle key slot).\n  - If you were running, which causes you to slip and fall after this step re obtain the key before trying again.","Attempt to open the chest inside the wrecked ship.","Kill Ulfric.\n  - If he spawns again, re-open the chest before killing him a second time.","Attempt to open the chest again and you'll receive a parchment.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Resilience"}]},"Once Upon a Slime":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Peter, next to the well in Rimmington. {Chat: 1 Yeah, I know all about it > 1 Aye, I mean, yes. > Accept}","After the cutscene, continue talking to Peter."],"t":"Return of the king"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Thessalia in her clothing store in Varrock for a giant top hat. {Chat: 1 Talk about Once Upon a Slime.}","Talk to Peter next to the well in Rimmington.","Return to Thessalia. {Chat: 1 Talk about Once Upon a Slime.}"],"t":"Top hat shenanigans"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Eva inside the building south of Varrock east bank. The building is attached to Aubury's Rune Shop, and features an anvil.","Shrink Something on the Shrinking Machine. {Chat: 1 Silver Button > 3 Hot > 1 Red Button > 2 Increase > 2 No > 1 KSL} It will automatically put in the hat to shrink it.","Go back to Peter and return the top hat."],"t":"Shrinking Machine"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After the cutscene, talk to Peter again.","Poke the Queen Slime for pink goop.","Talk to Peter.","Use the bucket on the cauldron in Hetty's house, east of the well in Rimmington.","Use the bucket of purple goop on King Slime and watch the cutscene.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Gloop gloop gloop"}]},"Once Upon a Time in Gielinor: Finale":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Closure. {Chat: Accept}","Walk into the southern waiting lobby and complete the flashbacks for Kami, Meg, and Philipe."],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Kami. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Relomia. {Chat: 3 Assign a task to Fraji. > 4 Fend off the Tiger's Claw!}","Assign ally to the Big door (large green door). {Chat: 1 Kami.}","Assign ally to any of the Intricate locks (blue circular matrix at the center). {Chat: 2 Honovi.}","Assign ally to the Strange symbols (the large golden gong to the east). {Chat: 3 Sojobo.}","Talk to Relomia {Chat: 4 Play back memory.}","Talk to Kami after the cutscene."],"t":"Kami"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Meg. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Relomia. {Chat: 3 Assign a task to the Raptor. > 4 Delay Sutcliffe's return!}","Assign ally to the front door of the castle. {Chat: 1 Meg.}","Assign ally to the Black Knight patrol (he stands west of the start of the bridge). {Chat: 2 Eva Cashien.}","Assign ally to the Roof access (the step-ladder east of the start of the bridge). {Chat: 3 Captain Higgs.}","Talk to Relomia. {Chat: 4 Play back memory.}","Talk to Meg after the cutscene."],"t":"Meg"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Philipe Carnillean. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Relomia. {Chat: 3 Assign a task to Oreb. > 4 Taunt the Bright Inquisitor!}","Assign ally to the World Gate controls. {Chat: 1 Philipe.}","Assign ally to the Defender position. {Chat: 2 Commander Zilyana.}","Assign ally to the Bright Inquisitor. {Chat: 3 Nymora.}","Talk to Relomia. {Chat: 4 Play back memory.}","Talk to Philipe after the cutscene."],"t":"Philipe"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Closure twice."],"t":"Wrapping up"}]},"Once Upon a Time in Gielinor: Flashback":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Closure who can be found in the Closure's Study in Death's office. {Chat: Accept}","Watch the cutscene.","Talk to the bartender in the Blue Moon Inn for the handwritten message. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Read the handwritten message.","Head to the Jolly Boar Inn located north-east of Varrock, outside the city walls near the Infernal source digsite and the Fort Forinthry lodestone.","Talk to Relomia at the bar for a stack of Closure's biographies.","Return and talk to Closure with his biographies."],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Merlin in the waiting room of Closure's office to enter his memory.","Interact with the Oneiric manipulator in your inventory to play the memory. {Chat: 1 Play the memory}","Interact with it again to reset the memory. {Chat: 2 Reset the memory}","Interact with the NPC next to you (shares your character's name). {Chat: 3 Excalibur}","Interact with the Latsyrc crystal twice so it becomes a Giant crystal.","Interact with the 'Merlin sucks' shield on the western wall once so it becomes a Wallshield.","Interact with the Oneiric manipulator in your inventory again. {Chat: 1 Play the memory}","Once back in Closure's office, talk to Merlin."],"t":"Merlin"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ozan to enter his memory.","Interact with the Oneiric manipulator in your inventory to play the memory. {Chat: 1 Play the memory}","Interact with the Oneiric manipulator to reset the memory. {Chat: 2 Reset the memory}","Interact with Ozan. {Chat: 2 Jump second.}","Interact with the NPC that shares your character name. {Chat: 1 Jump first.}","Enter the portal and interact the empty cart once so it becomes a cart.","Interact with the Oneiric manipulator in your inventory. {Chat: 1 Play the memory}","Once back in Closure's office, talk to Ozan."],"t":"Ozan"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ava to enter her memory.","Interact with the Oneiric manipulator to play the memory. {Chat: 1 Play the memory}","Interact with the Oneiric manipulator. {Chat: 2 Reset the memory}","Interact with NPC that shares your character's name. {Chat: 2 Undead chickens}","Investigate Lever B on the wall twice so it becomes a lever.","Investigate the Spooky clock twice so it becomes a wardrobe.","Interact with the Oneiric manipulator again. {Chat: 1 Play the memory}","Once back in Closure's office, talk to Ava."],"t":"Ava"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Closure."],"t":"Closure"}]},"Once Upon a Time in Gielinor: Foreshadowing":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Relomia at the Blue Moon Inn in Varrock. {Chat: Accept}","Take a drink from the party table. {Chat: ~}","Drink the punch and wear the party hat.","Relomia will then tell stories of your adventures. In order to end the dialogue and progress choose the correct statement about the quests.","Talk to Relomia again. {Chat: 3 It was a wooden stake > 3 It wasn't called Blacklight! > 4 It had one head, not three!}","Continue the dialogue with Death."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Unequip the party hat as this will save time by skipping some dialogue.","Enter the Closure's Study, the door to the east of Death's office.\n  - If you cannot interact with the door, go back to the lobby and log back in.","Talk to Delrith. {Chat: 3 Carlem. > 1 Aber. > 2 Camerinthum. > 5 Purchai. > 4 Gabindo.}","Talk to Count Draynor.","Talk to Elvarg for the Last Will and Testament.","Head to the kitchen in the northwest corner of the floor 1 of Draynor Manor and turn off the range.","Talk to a banker (e.g Varrock west / east bank, Varrock Grand Exchange, Draynor) to receive Elvarg's treasure hoard from the Last Will and Testament.","Return to the Closure's Study in Death's office.","Talk to Elvarg. {Chat: ~}","Talk to Count Draynor.","Talk to Closure to the north.","Re-equip the party hat and speak to Relomia in the Blue Moon Inn. {Chat: 3 Hello, [player name]. > 4 I'm [player name]'s biggest fan! > 3 Can I get your autograph?}\n  - The party hat can be taken from the table again in case you destroyed it.","Return to Closure."],"t":"Closure"}]},"Once Upon a Time in Gielinor: Fortunes":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Closure. {Chat: Accept}","Talk to Ariane.","Talk to Sir Tiffy.","Talk to Zanik.","Talk to Closure. {Chat: 1 Icthlarin > 2 Sliske > 3 Death}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go into the wheat field in Draynor Village south east of the lodestone and pick up three spooky scarecrows.","Place the scarecrows at the markers north-west of the lodestone, just behind the entrance to Death's Office by the trees. Look for the lit candles near wooden markers. Click on the wooden markers to plant the scarecrows.","Go back and talk to Closure again.","Hide the confiscated sword at the marker just west of the scarecrow markers.","Go back and talk to Closure again.","Go to the Dancing Donkey Inn (south east Varrock) and talk to Relomia twice. {Chat: Any}","Empty your Backpack and get rid of all your worn equipment and followers, then talk to Closure. {Chat: 1 Yes!}"],"t":"Setting up the quest"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Relomia.","Follow Relomia and talk to her each time she approaches the Evil Goons, and finally at the sword.","Equip the wand. Attempt to kill Relomia but let her defeat you.","Talk to Relomia.","Talk to Closure."],"t":"Relomia's quest"}]},"One Foot in the Grave (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Check your bank for a Hand (Back to my Roots).\n  - You may obtain one from an RPDT employee in East Ardougne or by killing creatures in the jade vine maze (at least one empty backpack space is required to obtain it as a drop).","With the hand, head to the Wizards' Guild in Yanille and ring the bell outside on the eastern side of the guild.","Speak to Zavistic Rarve. {Chat: 2 I have a rather sandy problem that I'd like to palm off on you > Accept}}}"],"t":"Off to see the wizard"},{"n":"","r":"Combat equipment","s":["Before you begin, search your bank for already-obtained body parts listed below and withdraw them now.","Go to the Jade vine maze on Karamja.","Kill creatures inside the maze until you receive the six body parts. These do not show up on area loot, the pieces drop in order and you must pick up the piece prior to the next drop or duplicates drop. Ensure your backpack is never full as pieces cannot drop if it is.\n  - Foot\n  - Torso (Back to my Roots)\n  - Left arm\n  - Right arm\n  - Left leg\n  - Right leg","Giant ant soldier","Frog","Giant ant worker","Pernicious parrot These creatures have an equal drop rate for body parts.","Tenacious toucan","Giant wasp","Jungle spider"],"t":"Back to your roots"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go back to the Wizards' Guild and ring the bell to speak to Zavistic Rarve. {Chat: 2 I have a rather sandy problem that I'd like to palm off on you. > 1 Yes, I'm ready to go.}","Search Sandy's desk to receive a locked diary.","Click on the locked diary to unlock it.\n  - There is a rare chance that you may trigger a trap so it is advised you do this in a safe area as it can cause over 8,000 damage."],"t":"Sandy's diary"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to the Wizards' Guild and ring the bell to speak to Zavistic Rarve. {Chat: 2 I have a rather sandy problem that I'd like to palm off on you. > 1 Sure, I'd be honoured to attend.}"],"t":"Remembrance of Clarence"}]},"One Piercing Note":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Sister Catherina east of Al Kharid and the Desert strykewyrms. {Chat: 1 Yes! I've come to answer your prayers! > 2 Yes, I'll help you. > Accept}","Talk to Abbess Benita in the abbey, in the centre room north of the fountain. {Chat: 2 What can I do to help? > 1 Of course.}","The cells are in the southeast corner. Enter the westernmost one (Anna's cell).","Inspect the bed and window.","Go back northwest to the room west of Abbess Benita's office and inspect the beds in there for another cloth fragment.","Run directly south and inspect the body (the body is covered up in the bed in the southwesternmost room).","Question 5 people around the abbey.\n  - Valerio - Musician outside the abbey (3 clues). {Chat: 1 What were you singing about? > 1 You were singing about Sister Anna, weren't you? > 2 Where were you between Vespers and Compline yesterday? > 2 I can't tell you, sorry.}\n  - Sister Elena, north of the cabbages, in the kitchen (3 clues). {Chat: 2 Where were you between Vespers and Compline yesterday? > 2 What did you think of Sister Anna? > 4 Goodbye.}\n  - Sister Cecilia, in the east-central room, the chapel (3 clues). {Chat: 1 What are you rehearsing? > 1 No - could you tell me? > 2 Go on. > 3 Back to my other questions... > 2 Where were you between Vespers and Compline yesterday? > 4 Goodbye.}\n  - Sister Catherina, in the chapel (2 clues). {Chat: 1 Where were you between Vespers and Compline yesterday? > 1 I'd like that. > 1 What did you think of Sister Anna? > 1 What other applicant? > 2 I can't tell you, sorry. > 3 Goodbye.}\n  - Feet (known as Sister Debora), on the floor 3 of the clock tower on the northeast side, sticking out under the clock mechanism. Talk to her {Chat: 2 Where were you between Vespers and Compline yesterday?}, then, operate the clock mechanism to show 12 o'clock. Afterwards, talk to her again (2 clues). {Chat: 1 Where were you between Vespers and Compline yesterday? > 2 Tell me about the troubadour outside. > 2 What did you think of Sister Anna? > 3 Goodbye.}","Return to Abbess Benita, select any suspect. {Chat: 1 I've finished investigating for now. > Any}"],"t":"Murder Mystery"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb down the stairs to the cellar in the room northeast of the chapel.","Investigate the bloodstains (1 clue) and body (5 clues).","Search the robe cabinet south of Sister Elena's body. (1 clue)","Return to Abbess Benita for a cell key. {Chat: 2 I need the key to Sister Elena's cell.}","Search the sack (singular, not the sacks) in the kitchen adjacent, east of Abbess Benita.","In the southeast corner of the building, enter the second cell from the east (Elena's cell) and inspect the bed.","Read the letters, talk to Valerio the musician about Sister Elena's death (1 clue). {Chat: 1 Were you having an affair with Sister Elena? > 2 Sister Elena is dead. > Any}","Talk to Sister Cecilia in the chapel for a clue. {Chat: 2 Can you tell me exactly what happened?}","Return to Abbess Benita and blame anyone. {Chat: 1 I've finished investigating for now. > Any}","Talk to Sister Catherina, who is now dancing outside near Valerio. {Chat: 1 Abbess Benita asked me to bring you back to the abbey. > 3 No. You should get back into the abbey.}","Talk to Sister Catherina again. {Chat: 1 Abbess Benita asked me to bring you back to the abbey.} A cutscene begins.","Climb the nearby ladder (immediately south of the closed gate), operate the winch, then climb back down.\n  - You do not need to do this step if you skip the cutscene.","Talk to Valerio near the dead body.","Talk to Abbess Benita. {Chat: 4 (More...) > 4 (More...) > 4 I don't know who did it. > 3 We should lay a trap. > 4 A new victim. > 2 They were all associated with Valerio.}"],"t":"A Development"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pick a cabbage and climb down the stairs to the cellar in the room northeast of the chapel.","Click move on the candelabrum near the eastern wall in the centre of the room north of the Reliquary, then use a cabbage on it (but don't eat it).","Search the robe cabinet, then use the robes on the cabbage-on-candelabrum.","Hide-in the cabinet {Chat: 1 Hide in the robe cabinet and wait.}. You may skip the cutscene.","Knock out the killer, then chase after them around the abbey.","Talk to the killer at the top of the tower. {Chat: Any > Any > 4 Enough talk!}","Climb down the stairs. You will get sent all the way down.","Climb up the stairs twice and operate the clock mechanism so that the minute hand points to 12.","Climb up the stairs and talk to the killer about the bell. {Chat: 4 Listen - is that the bell ringing?}","Talk to Sister Debora, she'll leave. {Chat: 3 What should we do with Sister Anna?}","Talk to Sister Anna (the killer) {Chat: Any}. You may skip the cutscene.","Talk to Abbess Benita. {Chat: Any}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Catching the Killer"}]},"One Small Favour":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Yanni Salika in Shilo Village (north of the bridge). {Chat: 2 Is there anything else interesting to do around here? > 5 Ok, see you in a tick! > Accept}","Talk to one of the jungle foresters south of the village. You will receive their blunt hatchet. {Chat: 4 I need to talk to you about red mahogany. > 1 Ok, I'll take your hatchet to get it sharpened.}"],"t":"Karamja"},{"n":"3 steel bars, clean harralander, clean marrentill, and vial of water","r":"","s":["Speak to Brian in Port Sarim (Axe shop north-east of the lodestone). Make sure he takes the blunt hatchet before you leave. {Chat: 3 Do you sharpen hatchets? > 2 Look, can you sharpen this cursed hatchet or what? > 4 Ok, ok, I'll do it! I'll go and see Aggie.}","Speak to Aggie, the witch in Draynor Village. {Chat: 1 Talk about One Small Favour. > 3 Let me guess, you're going to ask me to do you a favour? > 2 Oh, Ok, I'll see if I can find Jimmy.}","Go to the H.A.M. Hideout (north-west of the Lumbridge Castle, in the Lumbridge forest). Pick the lock on the trapdoor, and climb down. Head to the middle southern cavern and speak to Johanhus Ulsbrecht. {Chat: 4 I'm looking for Jimmy the Chisel. > 3 And I suppose you need me to do you a favour? > 2 Ok, Jimmy has to be worth more than a few scrawny chickens!}\n  - Or if player has completed The Chosen Commander. {Chat: 2 One Small Favour > 4 I'm looking for Jimmy the Chisel. > 3 And I suppose you need me to do you a favour? > 2 Ok, Jimmy has to be worth more than a few scrawny chickens!}","Talk to Fred the Farmer in the house of the sheep's pen in Lumbridge. {Chat: 2 I need to talk to you about Jimmy.}\n  - Or if player has seen \"The Thing\". {Chat: 3 I need to talk to you about Jimmy.}","Talk with Seth Groats in the house of the chickens' pen in Lumbridge. {Chat: 2 Oh, ok! I guess it's not that much further to Varrock!} (Back on the east side of the river across from the sheep's pen)","Take 3 steel bars (cannot be noted) to Horvik in the platebody shop in Varrock (north-east of the central fountain), who is ill and needs a herbal tincture. {Chat: 2 Talk about One Small Favour. > 3 Hi, I need to talk to you about chicken cages! > 2 Ok, I guess one good turn deserves another.}","Speak to the Apothecary twice, located in south-west Varrock, at the potion icon. {Chat: 1 Talk about One Small Favour. > 5 Horvik is ill, I need herbal tincture. > 2 Oh, ok, I guess it's not that far to the Barbarian Village.}\n  - Or if player has destroyed their Doctor's hat.{Chat: 2 Talk about One Small Favour. > 5 Horvik is ill, I need breathing salts and herbal tincture. > 2 Oh, ok, I guess it's not that far to the Barbarian Village.}","Go to Barbarian Village (also called Gunnarsgrunn) and talk to Tassie Slipcast, located within the pottery building in the south-east. {Chat: 1 Ok, I'll deal with Hammerspike!}","Enter the Dwarven Mine and find Hammerspike Stoutbeard on the far west side (\"Hammerspike's hangout\" on the map). Ask him about Tassie Slipcast. {Chat: 4 Have you always been a gangster? > 2 Ok, another favour..I think I can manage that.}","Go to Taverley and talk with Sanfew, located in the house slightly south-west of Pikkupstix's Summoning Shop. {Chat: 2 Are you taking any new initiates? > 2 Do you accept dwarves? > 3 A dwarf I know wants to become an initiate. > 1 Yep, it's a deal.}\n  - The quest Druidic Ritual must be completed to speak with Sanfew about One Small Favour.\n  - If Eadgar's Ruse is completed, or the third option is \"Are you taking any new initiates?\" {Chat: 3 Are you taking any new initiates? > 2 Do you accept dwarves? > 3 A dwarf I know wants to become an initiate. > 1 Yep, it's a deal.}","Make a Guthix rest by first adding the harralander to the vial of water, then adding the marrentill. Make sure you use the harralander on the vial, instead of clicking the vial, as you may accidentally use the marrentill first.","Travel to White Wolf Mountain, and speak to Captain Bleemadge. {Chat: 2 I have a special potion here for you from Sanfew! > 4 Ok, I'll go and get you some T.R.A.S.H.} Right-click to talk to him.\n  - To reach him enter the cave southwest of the Burthorpe lodestone (behind the Burthorpe mine entrance), then south towards the gnome glider."],"t":"Asgarnia and Misthalin"},{"n":"14 free inventory spaces, around 2000 coins (or 2+ cut opals, jades and red topazes in case you crush the ones you get)","r":"","s":["Travel to Catherby and speak to Arhein on the docks. (General store owner, south of the lodestone) {Chat: 3 I need to talk T.R.A.S.H. to you. > 1 Yes, Ok, I'll do it!}\n  - While here, purchase an empty pot from Arhein's Store.","Go to Seers' Village and speak to Phantuwti Fanstuwi Farsight, south-east of the lodestone. {Chat: 4 Hi, can you give me a weather forecast? > 5 What can I do to help? > 1 Yes, Ok, I'll do it.}","Enter the Goblin Cave south-east of the fishing guild (teleport to the Ardougne lodestone and run north).\n  - Sometimes the cave is not marked on the minimap. It is just outside the fence opposite the fishing guild building near the windmill.","Once inside, head north, then east where you find Petra Fiyed trapped in rock. Search the sculpture.","Go to Ardougne and speak to Wizard Cromperty, located north-east from the market. {Chat: 4 I need to talk to you about a girl stuck in some rock! > 2 Oh! Ok, one more 'small favour' isn't going to kill me..I hope!}","Pick up five pigeon cages from the back yard of the first house south of the north-western bank in Ardougne. There are three cages that will respawn immediately.","Go to Port Khazard (teleport to Catherby and use a charter to Port Khazard or teleport to the Yanille lodestone, run east through town then north) and talk to Tindel Marchant on the southern pier. {Chat: 2 Ask about iron oxide. > 1 Ok, I'll do it!}\n  - While you are here you can also speak to him about identifying swords for one of easy Ardougne achievements, They're Long and Pointy {Chat: 1 Chat about Antiques Store > 1 What do you do here?}","Go to the Feldip Hills and talk to Rantz, located to the far east of fairy ring aks. {Chat: 1 I need to talk to you about a mattress. > 4 Ok, I'll see what I can do.}","Go west to the gnome glider and right-click to talk to Gnormadium Avlafrim. {Chat: 4 Rantz said I should come and help you finish this project. > 1 Yes, I'll take a look at them.}","For each of the 8 gnome landing lights immediately east:\n  - Select the \"Search\" option on the gnome landing light to receive an uncut gem.\n  - Cut the gem. If you crush one talk to the gnome to buy a replacement. {Chat: 4 I need new gem to fix the lights. > 1 Ok, here's 500 gold, I'll buy one.}.\n  - Use the cut gem on the light it came from (from west to east is sapphire, opal, red topaz, jade).\n    - Make sure to use them on the gnome landing light.","Talk to the gnome again. {Chat: 4 I've fixed all the lights!}"],"t":"Kandarin"},{"n":"Armour and a weapon for the fight with Slagilith (weak to air spells), bronze bar, iron bar, steel bar, empty pot, and 5 pigeon cages","r":"","s":["Go back to Rantz to receive a comfy mattress. {Chat: 1 Ok, I've helped that Gnome, he shouldn't bother you anymore.}","Take the mattress to Tindel in Port Khazard, who gives you iron oxide. {Chat: 2 I have the mattress.}","Take the iron oxide to Wizard Cromperty in Ardougne, who gives you an animate rock scroll. {Chat: 4 I have that iron oxide you asked for!}","Read Animate rock scroll in the Goblin Cave near the trapped Petra and kill Slagilith when it appears.","Read Animate rock scroll again, then talk to Petra.","Go to Seers' Village and speak to Phantuwti in his house. {Chat: 4 I've released Petra, she should have returned. > 4 I'll run you through if you don't give me that weather report. > 2 Why can't you get a clear picture? > 2 Which special Seers tools do you mean? > 1 What do you mean, 'special combination of items'?}","Access the roof via either the ladder on the north wall of Phantuwti's house, or the ladder in the building to the east (you have to go up two ladders to get to the roof).","Search the weather vane twice to get three broken vane parts.","With a bronze bar, an iron bar, and a steel bar, use each of the the parts of the weather vane on any anvil (there is an anvil just north of the house).","Go back to the roof of the house and put the weathervane pillar, the directionals and the ornament back.","Talk to Phantuwti again and he will give you the weather report. {Chat: 4 I've fixed the weather vane!}","Take the report to Arhein in Catherby. {Chat: 3 I have the weather report for you.}","Talk to Captain Bleemadge on the White Wolf Mountain. {Chat: 2 Hey there, did you get your T.R.A.S.H?}","Talk to Sanfew in Taverley. {Chat: 2 Hi there, the Gnome Pilot has agreed to take you to see the ogres!} ( {Chat: 3 Hi there, the Gnome Pilot has agreed to take you to see the ogres!} If the player has completed \"Eadgar's Ruse.\")","Talk to Hammerspike Stoutbeard in the Dwarven Mine. Kill his minions. Talk to him again.","Talk to Tassie Slipcast in Barbarian Village.","Form the unfired pot lid at the nearby potter's wheel.","Fire the pot lid in the pottery oven.","Use the pot lid on an empty pot to get an airtight pot.","Go to the apothecary in Varrock and give him the pot. {Chat: 1 Talk about One Small Favour. > 5 Hey there! I have an air-tight pot for you!}\n  - Or if player has destroyed their Doctor's hat.{Chat: 2 Talk about One Small Favour. > 5 Hey there! I have an air-tight pot for you!}","Go to Horvik (Varrock Platebody Shop) and give him the herbal tincture and breathing salts. {Chat: 2 Talk about One Small Favour. > 3 I have the tincture and the breathing salts.}","Talk to him again with five pigeon cages to get some chicken cages. {Chat: 2 Talk about One Small Favour. > 3 I have the five pigeon cages you asked for!}","Go to Seth Groats in the house of the chickens' pen in Lumbridge and give him the chicken cages.","Go to the H.A.M. Hideout and talk to Johanhus. {Chat: 4 You're in luck, I've managed to swing that chicken deal for you.}","Go to Draynor Village and talk with Aggie the witch. {Chat: 1 Talk about One Small Favour.}","Go to Port Sarim and talk with Brian in his axe shop (north-east of the lodestone), who gives you a sharpened hatchet. {Chat: 3 I've returned with good news.}","Go back to Shilo Village and speak with any jungle forester (closest fairy ring ckr), who gives you red mahogany logs in exchange for the hatchet. {Chat: 4 Good news, I have your sharpened hatchet!}","Speak with Yanni in Shilo Village. {Chat: 2 Here's the red mahogany you asked for.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Completing the favours"}]},"One of a Kind":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"2 backpack spaces","s":["Talk to Mr. Mordaut in his office in the basement of Varrock Museum that is accessed behind the stairs. {Chat: 1 [One of a Kind] > Any > Accept}","Read the book Hannibus Hunted.","Talk to Mr. Mordaut. {Chat: Any > Any > 2 Bob the Cat? > Any}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"Catspeak amulet (e)","r":"","s":["Locate Bob the Cat with the catspeak amulet. An easy method to locate him is to hop worlds at the west Varrock anvils or searching nearby the Burthorpe lodestone. Most of the time he is inside Carwen Essencebinder Magical Runes Shop","Talk to Bob. {Chat: ? [One of a Kind] > 2 A human to look after? > 2 Maybe I'll check out this house...}"],"t":"Bob the Cat"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to Unferth's house east of Burthorpe lodestone.","Talk to Unferth. {Chat: 1 I want to search your house for a hidden library. > 3 I'm not interested in your novels. > 1 I'm looking for the lost library of Robert the Strong. > 1 Is there any place that Bob the Cat seemed drawn to? > 2 That's all for now.}","Search the bookcase.","Investigate the fireplace.","Inspect the table.","Remove the carpet.","Enter the trapdoor."],"t":"Unferth's house"},{"n":"Emerald","r":"","s":["Search the desk in the centre of the room.","Investigate the weapon rack to the north. {Chat: 1 Take some rust from the weapons.}","Use iron oxide on emerald to get Animate Rock scroll.","Read the Animate Rock scroll by the statue to the south.","Talk to Hannibus. {Chat: 1 Yes > 1 This is the Sixth Age. > Any > 1 What now? > 1 You could go home. > 4 We could look around this library! > 2 Let's take a look!}","Search the bookcase for the Dragonkin Primer to the east and Flight of the Dragonkin to the west.","Click the map in the south of the room to update location names"],"t":"Robert the Strong's library"},{"n":"Animate Rock scroll","r":"Portable fairy ring or Ardougne cloak and a law altar teleport","s":["Head to the mysterious statue east of the Seers' Village bank.","Read the Animate Rock scroll by it. {Chat: 3 None of those - I'm human! > 1 I'll rotate you now. > 2 Goodbye.}","Repeat for the next 3 statues. Rotating all 4 statues gives access to 10,000 bonus experience in any skill. At least one is required to continue.\n  - North-west of the Karamja lodestone. {Chat: 1 Just tell me how to rotate you. > 2 Goodbye.}\n  - North-west of the Ardougne lodestone. {Chat: 1 Just tell me how to rotate you. > 2 Goodbye.}\n  - North of the Tower of Life (fairy ring djp, Ardougne cloak for east of Kandarin Monastery, or Kandarin Monastery Teleport). {Chat: 1 Just tell me how to rotate you. > 2 Goodbye.}","Travel to the north-west corner of Entrana.","Read the animate rock scroll by the submerged statue. {Chat: 3 Who was your other visitor? > 3 Do you know of a way to travel between worlds? > 4 Goodbye.}"],"t":"The mysterious statues"},{"n":"Dragonkin Primer","r":"Wilderness sword 2","s":["Run to the green dragons in the south east corner of the Forinthry Dungeon. Hannibus will talk to you if you brought the Dragonkin Primer book. {Chat: 1 Yes}\n  - This dungeon is located in the Wilderness, so make sure that you are not opted in to PvP combat by talking to Vala.\n  - A quick method is to use the Wilderness sword 2 teleport to the dungeon, or run east to the Wilderness Crater lodestone and run straight west to the dungeon entrance.\n  - If you don't see Hannibus, exit the dungeon and re-enter it, then run towards green dragons, it will give you an option to continue the quest. Make sure you brought the Dragonkin Primer book.","Run close to the east wall of the room, near the lava. {Chat: 2 Let's investigate!}","Study the rock (on the ground east of the green dragon)."],"t":"Forinthry Dungeon"},{"n":"","r":"Combat equipment method to kill three iron dragons (weak to water spells), Antifire potion or other means of dragonfire protection, Dragonkin Primer, 875 coins (unless you use a Dungeoneering cape to enter or have the hard Karamja achievements completed)","s":["Travel to the iron/steel dragons in Brimhaven Dungeon. {Chat: 1 Yes}\n  - A quick method is using the Dungeoneering cape and selecting \"Brimhaven metal dragon dungeon\"\n  - A slower method is walking west from the Karamja lodestone, entering the dungeon, and walking to the iron and steel dragons\n  - If you don't get the question about 'One of a Kind' go back to the entrance of the room and walk slowly into the room again.","Kill 3 iron dragons. {Chat: Any > Any}","Head to the west wall by the mysterious entrance to study the dragonkin writing."],"t":"Brimhaven Dungeon"},{"n":"","r":"Remoras Necklace}}{{Checklis","s":["Travel to the Grotworm Lair north-west of Port Sarim lodestone.\n  - Remora's necklace will take you directly outside of the portal.","Enter the bottom level of the Grotworm Lair. You can use the shortcut to the south-east of the first floor to get there quickly. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Investigate the summoning portal. The portal is right next to the shortcut, a square hole in the wall gleaming green. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Talk with Hannibus. {Chat: 3 Your majesty - I have some questions. > 1 I seek means to travel between worlds. > 1 Tell me about the Dragonkin. > 1 Yes}"],"t":"Grotworm Lair"},{"n":"Ghostspeak amulet or cramulet if Morytania Set Tasks - Hard is not complete or Big Book o' Piracy isn't used.","r":"Ectophial to get to Port Phasmatys or Big Book o' Piracy, or Dungeoneering Master Cape (0, 3) for Dragontooth Teleport. Antifire potion and food to survive fighting celestial dragons for 2 minutes","s":["Travel to Dragontooth Island by talking to the Ghost captain east of Port Phasmatys (South, in the small boat). {Chat: 1 Please take me to Dragontooth Island.}\n  - The fastest method is teleporting to Dragontooth Island directly, using the Dungeoneering cape teleport, or using the elder divination outfit to teleport to the \"Radiant Wisp Colony\"\n  - A quick method is heading to Port Sarim and taking a charter ship to Port Phasmatys (talk to Trader Stan south-east of the lodestone)\n  - There are two ghost captains, you need to talk to the southern one who is standing next to a rowboat, not a ship","Enter the mysterious entrance to the south.","Fight/Tank a celestial dragon until Hannibus's bond reaches 100% (approximately 2 minutes).\n  - Attack multiple to reach 100% faster.","Talk to Hannibus again."],"t":"Dragontooth Island"},{"n":"","r":"Combat gear, food and potions to fight 3 Dragon-Hunters (Ranged/Magic/Melee)","s":["Activate the Artefact north of Edgeville Monastery to meet with Hannibus in the King Black Dragon Lair. {Chat: 1 Yes - Meet with Hannibus. > 1 Continue}\n  - You will not enter a player-versus-player enabled area despite the warning.","Talk with the King Black Dragon. {Chat: 1 Sorry about killing you.}","Enter Mysterious entrance.","Talk with Therragorn. {Chat: 1 Listen to Hannibus. > 1 Can you help Hannibus get home?}","Kill the 3 Dragon-Hunters.","Talk to Hannibus for a cutscene."],"t":"The white dragon"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kerapac will talk to you. {Chat: 3 Aaaaargh! A Dragonkin! > 2 Ask about companions. > 1 How's Hannibus? > 1 What's the favour? > 1 Okay, I'll help.}","Head into the far northern room. Kerapac will talk to you. {Chat: 2 Just tell me what to do.}","Harvest 25 dragonkin memories from the protoplasmic wisps and channel them into the cage.","Talk with Kerapac to fight Echo of Jas. {Chat: 1 I am ready!}","Kill the Echo of Jas and then talk to it after you defeat it."],"t":"Daemonheim with Kerapac"},{"n":"5 free backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Kerapac will talk to you. {Chat: 4 What now? > 1 Yes. > 1 [Decide Hannibus's fate] > Any}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Wrapping up"}]},"Osseous Rex":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the 'Calm' Archaeologist at the rex skeleton in Anachronia base camp to begin the quest. {Chat: Accept > 1 Yes.}","Head to the teleportation device in the spirit grove.","Activate the teleportation device.","Head east and talk to the 'Calm' Archaeologist."],"t":"Learning about Osseous"},{"n":"Free backpack space to excavate an artefact","r":"Excavation equipment such as mattock, archaeology outfit, and porters.","s":["Go north-east towards the Matriarch lair entrance, and then through the archway to the north and follow the path anti-clockwise until you reach an Ancient Artefact (Inactive).","Activate the Ancient Artefact (Inactive) to unlock the first gate.","Go back to the area near the archaeologist and Pass Through the gate.","Go south, then east, then north through the arch, and activate the second Ancient Artefact (Inactive).","A cutscene ensues, unlocking two more gates.","Go south, looping around to the immediate west and Pass Through the gate.","Go east, following the path south and around anti-clockwise up a hill.","Pass Through the gate.","Uncover the soil.","Excavate the crystallised rubble for a teleportation crystal (damaged)."],"t":"Finding a teleportation crystal"},{"n":"Teleportation crystal (damaged), 20 orthenglass in material storage container","r":"","s":["Restore the teleportation crystal (damaged) at an archaeologist's workbench.","Talk to the 'Calm' Archaeologist in the Rex Matriarch lair with the restored teleportation crystal.\n  - He will no longer be found in in the Anachronia base camp, you have to travel to the Rex Matriarch lair to speak with him.","Watch the cutscene.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Our Man in the North":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Grand Vizier Hassan in the Merchant district, south of the bank deposit box. {Chat: 1 Talk about Our Man in the North. > Accept}"],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"","r":"Combat gear and food, Pollnivneach Teleport, 1 free backpack space","s":["Go to the Grand Library of Menaphos in the Imperial district. The entrance is next to the deposit box (bank chest).","Talk to Kohnen the librarian, who is just north of the entrance. {Chat: 1 *whisper* I'm looking for a book.}","Exit the Grand Library.","Head north to talk to Commander Akhomet. {Chat: 1 Talk about Our Man in the North. > 2 Historical text and bloodlines.}","Head to Pollnivneach.","Speak to Aristarchus, who is north-west of the south magic carpet station. {Chat: 1 Talk about Our Man in the North}","You will have to fight four Menaphite Thugs.\n  - They are level 122 and fight using melee.\n  - You can hide behind Aristarchus if you need a safe spot and are using ranged/magic/necromancy.","Speak to Aristarchus again who will agree to meet you in the library. {Chat: 1 Talk about Our Man in the North}","Return to the Grand Library and speak to Aristarchus, who is south of the entrance inside the library.","Go to Uzer Mastaba and enter the pyramid to trigger a cutscene. (fairy code DLQ)","After the cutscene, enter the pyramid once more and speak to Senliten. {Chat: 4 Talk about Our Man in the North. > 4 Ozan is Senliten's descendant? > 2 Where are you going with this?}","Go to Al Kharid and speak to Osman, who is in the throne room, south of the lodestone.","Speak to Emir Ali Mirza in front of the throne. {Chat: 1 Talk about Our Man in the North.}"],"t":"The bloodline"},{"n":"","r":"Have the 'remove roofs' setting set to 'selectively' in your graphics settings","s":["Leave the Palace and head north-east to Dommik's Crafting Store.\n  - Ignore the quest active area marked on the minimap.","Climb the stairs on the inside of the crafting store.","Climb the ladder south of the stairs.","Follow these steps across the rooftops:\n  - Walk across the plank to the south.\n  - Slide down the awning to the south.\n  - Go through the building.\n  - Walk across the washing line (north-west from where you started).\n  - Climb the ladder to the west.\n  - Talk to Jabari.\n  - Cross the planks to the west.\n  - Climb the ladder to the southwest.\n  - Jump from the scaffold to the west.\n  - Climb down the rug to the south.\n  - Swing across the wooden frame immediately west.\n  - Jump from the scaffold (west) to the next building.\n  - Bounce on the awning (south) to the bank.\n  - Climb up the brickwork to the west on the wall.\n  - Talk to Jabari.\n  - Parrot drop on the rug to the south.\n    - Do not shimmy across the rope.\n  - Run north of the bank, west of the furnace, and talk to Jabari.\n  - Run north-east of the Al Kharid lodestone into a tent, and talk to Jabari.\n  - Run north to the house near the north-east exit of Al Kharid, and talk to Jabari.\n    - You can get a free heal from the Surgeon General west of this house.","Go to Het's Oasis."],"t":"Tracking down Jabari"},{"n":"Combat equipment and food","r":"","s":["Prepare to battle Jabari four times. He is level 112 and uses magic. He has a weakness to slash.","Talk to Jabari. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Jabari will teleport you into the centre of the arena, surrounding you with his clones.\n  - Choosing the wrong Jabari will cause an explosion that damages the player and scales with level.\n  - Find the real Jabari by attacking the odd one out. As it is random for each player, it could be any of these:\n    - The only one facing backwards.\n    - The only one in attack position.\n    - The one with the smallest sceptre.\n    - The largest one of them.\n    - The one targeted by the audience.\n    - The one with the correctly spelled name.\n    - The one with a different robe colour.\n    - The one without prayer renewal particles.\n    - The one who is not translucent.","Talk to Het.","Talk to Emir Ali Mirza, in the Al Kharid throne room. {Chat: 1 Talk about Our Man in the North.}","After the cutscene, talk to Emir Ali Mirza again. {Chat: 1 Talk about Our Man in the North.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Fighting Jabari"}]},"Perils of Ice Mountain":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Lakki the delivery dwarf, who can be found to the east of the Invention Guild, north of Falador. {Chat: 1 What's the matter? > 2 I could help you find the crate. > Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Along the path west towards Falador are eight bushes you can search. Search each of them until a crate is found.","Give the crate to Drorkar, who is in the Power Station west of the Dwarven Mines. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 2 Okay.}","Head to the Edgeville Monastery (use the Edgeville lodestone to save time).","Give the letter to Brother Bordiss in the garden. {Chat: 1 I have a letter for you.}","Talk to Brother Althric. {Chat: 2 Can I help? > 1 I'll go and get some compost.}","Use compost on the dying roses, then water them. If your watering can is empty, you may use the fountains in the monastery to fill it."],"t":"Delivery"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Professor Arblenap (the gnome) half way up to the top of Ice Mountain. {Chat: 1 What are you doing? > 2 Can I help?}","Wield the icefiend net and catch the four baby icefiends.","Talk to Professor Arblenap.","Talk to the Oracle, who is just north on the mountain. {Chat: 1 What happened to your tent? > 1 I could fix your tent for you.}","Take the wrecked tent from the base of the mountain, south of the Black Knights' Fortress entrance and east of the Oracle. It does not appear as a red dot on the minimap.","With the tent, two planks, and two nails, use the tent on the remains atop the mountain, next to the Oracle.","Continue dialogue with the Oracle. {Chat: 5 I'm going to go and do something.}"],"t":"Ice Mountain"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Drorkar at the Power Station. {Chat: 1 You've got to shut down this power station. > 4 The Oracle predicted it would cause the end of civilisation! > 4 I'll go and talk to Nurmof, then.}","Pickpocket Drorkar for a Dwarven key.","Go in the Dwarven Mines and talk to Nurmof in the north-western corner of the mines, at the pickaxe shop. {Chat: 4 You've got to shut down the power station! > 1 What was this other power source? > 3 Goodbye.}","Talk to Brother Bordiss at the Edgeville Monastery. {Chat: 1 Nurmof says you made plans for an alternative power station.}","Head back down into the Dwarven Mines, then immediately east into a small alcove.","Open the small, bright chest against the north wall.","Return to the pickaxe shop and talk to Nurmof. {Chat: 4 You've got to shut down the power station. > 1 I have the plans to the alternative power station here.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing Up"}]},"Pharaoh's Folly":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk with Leela outside of the northern gates of Menaphos. {Chat: Accept > 2 We should get it over with. (Continue quest)}","Empty your backpack, worn equipment and dismiss any followers and then head to the throne room inside the Golden Palace. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to anyone inside to begin the conversation. {Chat: Any}}}"],"t":"The folly of man"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Attempt to exit the shifting tomb via the rope.","Search the arrow shafts to receive a mysterious message and a spare arrow shaft.","Read the mysterious message.","Speak to the four cats (indicated by yellow dots on your minimap) to receive a curved bone:\n  - Bestopet\n  - Katarina\n  - Shebit\n  - Takhuit","Mine crystalline corruption to obtain crystal shards.","Search treasure chests to obtain feathers.","Smash urns to obtain a gut string.","Search sarcophagi to obtain mouldy bandages. To do this, click on the panels the energy bounces off in the order of which it started.","Use the gut string on the curved bone to create a fragile bow.","Use the feathers on the spare arrow shaft to create a feathered spare arrow shaft.","Use the crystal shards on the feathered spare arrow shaft to make a scrappy arrow.","Stand next to the arrow shafts where the exit rope was, then fire arrow with the bow in your backpack.","Exit the rope.","Talk to Ozan.","Talk to Commander Akhomet outside the northern gates of Sophanem. {Chat: Any > 2 Just tell me what to do. (Continue quest) > 5 I'll crack on. (Continue quest)}"],"t":"A shifting perspective"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the following people:\n  - Maisa next to the High priest in Sophanem.\n  - Grand Vizier Hassan in the south-west building of the Menaphos merchant district. {Chat: 1 Yes.}\n  - Lydia in Pollnivneach, south-east of Sumona.\n  - Emir Ali Mirza in the Al Kharid palace. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"The keys to Menaphos"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ozan back in the Shifting Tombs lobby. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Exit the tomb west to the Imperial district. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Sneak past the guards and enter the library.\n  - Head north and around the edge of the pool towards the VIP skilling area.\n  - Go west and go behind the two guards near the Golden Palace.\n  - Head south to the library, going behind the stationary guards. Be careful of the roaming guards who can still catch you.","Talk to Ozan for a cutscene, and finish the dialogue to get the signal torch.","Go south and make your way to the staircase on the south side, avoiding the guard.","Stand halfway down the stairs and use the signal torch in your backpack.","Head a bit west and talk to Leela to have her follow you (you will be able to continue the next step if she gets stuck).","Continue to the bottom floor using the eastern stairs and talk to Ozan. {Chat: Any}","Speak to Leela or Ozan on the Sophanem beach. {Chat: Any}"],"t":"Jailbreaking Leela"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the throne room inside the Golden Palace. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to each of the members to turn the bar over their heads red. Exhausting all chat options is not required.\n  - Grand Vizier Ehsan. {Chat: 2 I want to call a witness. > 4 Emissary Qar > 1 Emir Ali.}\n  - 'Admiral' Wadud. {Chat: 2 I want to call a witness. > 1 Lydia > 1 Coenus' death.}\n  - Batal. {Chat: 2 I want to call a witness. > 2 Maisa > 1 Scabaras.}\n  - Commander Akhomet. {Chat: 2 I want to call a witness. > 3 Grand Visier Hassan > 2 Osman's strengths.}","Re-enter the Golden Palace {Chat: 1 Go to throne room.}","Talk to Pharaoh Leela.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The end of the follies"}]},"Pieces of Hate":{"sections":[{"n":"1 free inventory space","r":"","s":["Enter the player-owned house portal. Postie Pete will appear and give you a letter from Bill Teach.","Read the letter. {Chat: Accept}","Deposit all items.","Go to the Rimmington Customs Office without any items, then talk to the Customs Sergeant. {Chat: 1 Talk about Pieces of Hate. > 4 I would like to confess! > Any} You will be sent to the Rock."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Bill Teach about Pieces of Hate.","Talk to Two-Eyed Eric through barred window. {Chat: 1 Two-Eyed Eric > 3 Can you give me a hand? > 4 Goodbye.}","Use the hook on the bed, then combine the cloth with the hook.","Go outside and use the cloth-hook on the fishing spot.","Use the fish on the perch rock to attract a seagull.","Use the fish on the door, then use the hook on the door.","Push the barrels by the door to block out the guards.","Use the hook on Bill Teach's cell door.","Search the desk and locker. Put the customs uniform on.","Investigate the pile of crates to take a small crate.","Use the spoon on the crate to make a trap, then use the sandwich on it to bait it.","Use the trap on the rat hole in Bill Teach's cell. {Chat: 3 [Firmly admonish the rat.] > 4 [Inform the rat of your plight.] > 2 [Introduce yourself properly.] > 4 [Ask for a way to free the others.]}","Use the guard's keys on any remaining prisoner's cell door.","Attempt to open the door in the middle of the prison (leading to the stairs).","Talk to Madame Shih.","Talk to Jimmy the Parrot (one of the pirates).","Open the door in the middle of the prison (leading to the stairs).","Investigate the poster next to the stairs, then climb the stairs wearing the customs outfit.\n  - If the \"investigate\" option doesn't appear on the bed, make sure you have checked the poster downstairs.","Search the lockers (to the north). Use the pineapple on the puddle of slime in the corner, then use it on Wilson (the rat).","Use Pineapple Wilson on the door to the south room.","Enter the room and investigate the east bed to find first floor keys.","Open the north door between the beds.","Right-click \"Use\" the 'rum' on the strange egg. {Chat: 1 Yes - I am the god of hellfire.}\n  - If you drink the 'rum' accidentally, then you can get a new one from the lockers to the east.","Climb up the stairs to the east.","After the cutscene, dive off the pier.","Speak to anyone. {Chat: Any > 1 Yes.} This is the first point where you can leave the quest and save progress.}}"],"t":"Escape the Rock (again)"},{"n":"2 pieces of leather, 1 gold bar, 1 free inventory space; recommended = Varrock teleport","r":"","s":["Sit in the chair in the north-east corner of Harpoon Joe's House of 'Rum'. {Chat: 1 A Long Drop.}","Speak to the Zombie pirate head. {Chat: Any > 2 [Kind interrogation.] > 3 Maybe we can come to an arrangement. > Any > 1 Deal.}","Go to the west of Varrock and speak to Gertrude in her house. {Chat: 4 Ask about a pet for the zombie head.} (or {Chat: 5 Ask about a pet for the zombie head.}if completed Rat Catchers)","Talk to Philop or Kanel inside Gertrude's house.","Go to the abandoned house northwest of the apothecary in south-west Varrock and search the jiggling crate to find Wilson. {Chat: 1 Yes - I fear nothing. > 1 Yes - it's probably fine.}"],"t":"Finding a friend"},{"n":"Blurberry special, Drunk dragon, Chocolate saturday","r":"","s":["Travel to the Karamja lodestone and head about 10 paces south of the deposit chest; the head will tell you to stop. {Chat: 1 Put the zombie head down.}","Talk to the head again. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 Yes. > 1 Yes. > 1 Yes.} A cutscene of the sunset will start. {Chat: Any}"],"t":"Seeing the sunset"},{"n":"Combat gear","r":"Food and prayer potions","s":["Prepare for combat. Return to Harpoon Joe's House of 'Rum' and return to the Interrogation Room by sitting in the north-east chair. {Chat: 1 A Long Drop.}","When ready for the fight, head south-west of Harpoon Joe's House of 'Rum' and row the rowboat. {Chat: 1 Yes!}","Enter the door to the south.","Kill all four tentacles; a cutscene follows.","Kill Zogoth; a cutscene follows.\n  - Stay within melee range to avoid a typeless damage attack from the tentacles.\n  - Move away from the water jet attack to avoid being pushed to the back of the boat.\n  - Move away from shadows when Zogoth shields itself to avoid acid spray attacks (occurs at 50% and 25% health). The acid will follow you around until the attack ends."],"t":"Zogoth"},{"n":"Combat gear","r":"Food and prayer potions","s":["Once on Mos Le'Harmless, during Rabid Jack's Invasion, the player must clear two waves of enemies.","Wave 1 (initial attack):\n  - Kill the barrelchest and zombie captains at the main gate to the north and repair the barricades.\n  - Kill the zombie captains up the ramp (on the western wall), then help up the pirate on the wall.\n  - Kill the zombie captains at the south-east coast of the town, then repair the cannons and sink the zomboats.\n  - Kill the zombie captains at the south-west coast of the town, then repair the cannons and sink the zomboats.","Wave 2 (next attack):\n  - Kill the DKS and the zombie captains at the main gate and repair the barricades.\n  - Kill the zombie captains up the ramp (on the western wall), then help up the pirate on the wall.\n  - Kill the zombie captains at the south-east coast of the town, then repair the cannons and sink the zomboats.\n  - Kill the zombie captains at the south-west coast of the town, then repair the cannons and sink the zomboats.\n  - Kill the zombie captains at river east of the town, then destroy the makeshift bridges.\n  - Kill the DKS and the zombie captains at the wheat field north of the town, then destroy the cannon.\n  - Kill the DKS and the zombie captains at the coast north-west of the town, then destroy the grounded ship. This should be done last.","Finish the conversation with the pirates in the invasion. You will not be able to progress without doing so."],"t":"Rabid Jack's invasion"},{"n":"Four free backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Head to Braindeath Island via Pirate Pete north of Port Phasmatys. {Chat: 1 Travel to Braindeath Island (Pieces of Hate).} You can also use the pirate spell sheet {Chat: 1 Braindeath Island > 1 Travel to Braindeath Island (Pieces of Hate).} or Dungeoneering cape. {Chat: 8 Braindeath Island > 1 Travel to Braindeath Island (Pieces of Hate).}","Head south, and down the wooden stairs. Run west along the building and up the wooden stairs on the west of the bunkroom.","Head through the bunkroom to the east side, then north-east. Listen at the window to the room with Captain Braindeath.","After the dialogue, head back to the bunkroom, and talk to Davey.","Head down the wooden stairs, put on the barrelchest disguise then talk to Captain Donnie south-east. {Chat: 3 Mi-Gor is in need of some witchwood.}","Head up the nearby wooden stairs, and talk to the Barrelchest Mk I.","Return to Captain Donnie again to learn the passphrase {Chat: 2 Mi-Gor wants to see you right now!}","Head back up the wooden stairs, and once again talk with the Barrelchest Mk I. {Chat: 5 'How appropriate. You fight like a zombie sea cow.'}","Remove the disguise, for speed.","Climb the ladder in the south-east corner of the building.","Head west, and take the Barrels of 'rum' from on top of the crate, head north and do the same again.","Block the pressure barrel (just south-east of the second of the barrels of 'rum'), then overload the pressure lever beside it.","Return down the ladder, and then the stairs.","Head north-west and pass through the gate by 66.6...% Luke.\n  - You cannot use the dungeoneering cape teleport here to get to the north of the island.","Head north, up the mountain to the pool (marked with on the minimap) and investigate the perch rock.","Baron von Hattenkrapper will appear. Complete the dialogue, then select Unleash! {Chat: 1 Unleash!}","Guide Baron von Hattenkrapper and hit the mysterious entrance to the south-west 3 times; a cutscene follows.","Talk with Mi-Gor, and set sail. {Chat: 1 [Set sail...for Kraken Tooth Island.]}"],"t":"Braindeath Island"},{"n":"Combat gear","r":"Food and prayer potions","s":["Head south and equip gear from the crate of diving gear, then head north and dive into the cracked hull.","Head south-west, and jump off the edge.","Head south, then west, then north to the shimmering barrier.\n  - EPILEPSY WARNING: If you suffer from epilepsy, talk to the shimmering kitten to prevent aggravating symptoms.\n    - You need to prepare for combat for the next part.","If well-prepared for combat, pass through the shimmering barrier; a cutscene follows.\n  - Note: If you choose to re-gear use the rowboat in the south-west of Mos Le'Harmless to get back to the temple."],"t":"Underwater"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Reduce Jack's health to 0.\n  - Stand at the north, south, west, east walls or doorway to avoid being damaged and stunned by the black hand in the centre of the room.\n  - Use Freedom or Anticipation if stunned by Jack's stun attack. Avoid running from Jack to reduce the frequency of this attack.\n  - Drink 'rum' from barrels in the room to reduce \"insanity\". Insanity is indicated by the black cat debuff icon and will cause Jack hallucinations to spawn and the camera to spin if it becomes too high. Drink as soon as the debuff icon appears.\n  - If you die you can return to fight Rabid Jack by travelling back to Mos Le'Harmless and taking the small rowboat.","Loosen an ancient chain.","Repeat this process for the 3 other chains; a cutscene follows.","Speak with Madame Shih. {Chat: 5 Let's go!}","Sit in the chair in Harpoon Joe's House of 'Rum' {Chat: 1 A Long Drop.}","Talk to Bill Teach with 6 free inventory spaces; a cutscene follows.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Rabid Jack fight"}]},"Pirate's Treasure":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Redbeard Frank just outside Port Sarim's pub. {Chat: 1 I'm in search of treasure. > Accept}","Walk south along the docks, pay 30 coins to Captain Tobias to go to Karamja. {Chat: 1 Yes please.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head inside the pub.","Buy one Karamjan rum from Zembo.","Do not leave the island yet or more rum will have to be obtained.","Pick 10 bananas from the Banana Trees to the north-west.","Go east to the house by the docks.","Talk to Luthas about the officer. {Chat: 2 That customs officer is annoying isn't she?}, then talk to him a second time to ask for a job. {Chat: 1 Could you offer me employment on your plantation?}","On the east side of Luthas' house will be a wooden crate.","Use the Karamjan rum on the crate, then right-click Fill the crate.","Talk to Luthas."],"t":"The smuggling job"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to Wydin's Food Store in Port Sarim.","Equip your white apron and attempt to open the door to the back room. {Chat: 1 Well, can I get a job here?}\n  - A free white apron can be obtained from the back wall in the fishing store.","Search the crate with the banana on it.","With the rum, return to Redbeard Frank for a chest key. {Chat: 1 Ok thanks, I'll go and get it.}"],"t":"Retrieving the rum"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go upstairs in the Blue Moon Inn in south Varrock.","Open the chest in the south-west room for a pirate message. Read it.","Go to Falador Park and stand on the east end of the pond, directly west of the statue of Saradomin, indicated by X on the ground.","Right-click Dig using the pirate message. Kill the gardener. Alternatively, leave the site for a while and the gardener will be gone.","Right-click Dig using the message again.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Treasure hunting"}]},"Plague City":{"sections":[{"n":"Dwellberries, rope","r":"","s":["Talk to Edmond who is located at a house north of the Ardougne Castle and Flying Horse Inn in East Ardougne. {Chat: 1 What's happened to her? > Accept}","Talk to his wife Alrena directly east in the house and give her the dwellberries.","Pick up the picture of Elena from the table in the eastern room of their house."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Edmond.","Equip the gas mask.","In his garden, use all 4 buckets of water on the mud patch in the south part of his garden, between the cabbages and potatoes.","Bring all of the required items with you before you enter the mud patch. Once inside the city, there is no bank nearby. If you leave the city, you will need to re-enter the mud patch and climb through the pipe to return.","Dig the mud patch.","Go south and try to open the grill on the pipe.","Use a rope on the grill and talk to Edmond.","Make sure the gas mask obtained earlier is equipped and climb up the pipe."],"t":"Breaking in"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use the picture on Jethick, who is found walking around the town square, and tell him that you will help return the book. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll return it for you}\n  - Optional: Talk to the nearby Recruiter for one of easy Ardougne achievements, Red Revolution.","Talk to Martha Rehnison or Ted Rehnison in their house, north of the town hall building.","Go up the ladder and talk to Milli Rehnison.","Exit the house and go south of the town square.\n  - Optional: Pray at the altar in the church for one of easy Ardougne achievements, Preaching to the Infected.","Go to the central southern house with spooky stairs and attempt to open one of the doors with a big X. {Chat: 1 But I think a kidnap victim is in here. > 2 I want to check anyway.}"],"t":"The search for Elena"},{"n":"Chocolate dust, bucket of milk, snape grass","r":"","s":["Go north to the large building you first arrived at, in the town square.","Talk to the Clerk on the floor 1, and tell him it's urgent. {Chat: 2 Who is through that door? > 1 This is urgent though!}","Climb the stairs and enter the eastmost room.","Talk to Bravek. {Chat: 1 This is really important though! > 3 Do you know what's in the cure?}","Add the chocolate dust to the bucket of milk and then add snape grass to make a hangover cure.","Talk to Bravek and give him the cure. {Chat: 3 They won't listen to me!}. He will give you a warrant to enter.","Go back and enter the house with the black Xs.","Search the barrel on the western side of the building's floor 1 to obtain a small key.","Go down the stairs, open the gate and talk to Elena."],"t":"Getting to Elena"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to the town square you arrived at, and re-enter the manhole.","Talk to Edmond.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Plague's End":{"sections":[{"n":"Mourner outfit","r":"Combat equipment","s":["Talk to Arianwyn in Lletya. {Chat: 1 Let's go! > Accept > 1 I have the Mourner disguise with me. > 1 I'm ready to teleport.}","Enter western door."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"1 backpack space","r":"","s":["Open northern door. {Chat: 3 We thought we saw a mouse. > 2 It might get into the food stores. > 1 We knew you were busy, so we dealt with it.}","Head to the north-western room.","Talk to a Mourner.","Talk to Iestin Edern. {Chat: 2 The captain wants you to hurry.}"],"t":"Infiltration"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb up the nearby stairs (north wall).","Talk to the Mayor of Prifddinas in the house north of the camp. {Chat: 2 I've got a report from Iestin Edern.}","Talk to the Mourner at the bridge, south of the camp. {Chat: 1 The mayor wants you to distribute the food to the crowd.}","Return to the Mayor. {Chat: 1 The guards are distributing it to the crowd!}","Take Iorwerth master plan from the desk.","Head south-east back downstairs and talk to Iestin Edern. {Chat: 1 I have a document with Lord Iorwerth's plans here. > 3 How can we stop him?}"],"t":"Iorwerth master plan"},{"n":"Iowerth master plan, 3 backpack space","r":"","s":["Talk to Councillor Halgrive outside the East Ardougne church (south west of lodestone), located just west of the main square. {Chat: 1 I need to show you this document.}","Talk to Bravek in the upper floor of Civic Office of West Ardougne. {Chat: 1 I need to show you this document. > 2 If you suspected, why didn't you do anything? > 2 We need to overthrow the Mourners.}","Unequip 1 mourner piece. The people won't speak to you with a full set of mourner outfit equipped.","Talk to the 6 people on the list:\n  - Ted or Martha Rehnison - In a building north of the civic office. {Chat: 1 I need your help to overthrow the Mourners.}\n  - Jethick - On the eastern side of the large paved area outside the civic office. {Chat: 1 We would if we tore down the city's walls. Join my revolution!}\n  - Nurse Sarah - In a building south-west of the church. {Chat: 1 I'd feel better if you joined my revolution.}\n  - Carla - In an open area, north of the graveyard to the west of the church. {Chat: 1 Join my revolution and avenge your son.}\n  - Koftik - Entrance to the Underground Pass. {Chat: 1 I want to help you overthrow the Mourners.}\n  - Elena - Found in the house just west of the log balance in the northern part of East Ardougne (from the lodestone run south-west and then take log balance to cross the river). {Chat: 1 Yes - and it's time to stop them.}"],"t":"Incite an uprising"},{"n":"1 backpack space, Mourner outfit","r":"crystal teleport seeds, Halgrive's proclamation, combat equipment, food, and 10 magic logs in the bank.","s":["Go to the church in West Ardougne.","Talk to any of the 6 NPCs at the church (not the priest). {Chat: 1 Yes - I'll explain everything, and then we'll strike! > 5 Enough talk - it's time to strike!}","Head to the Mourner Headquarters (north-east).","Kick down door and kill the mourners. (If door is not closed, transport away and come back. No mourner gear needed.)","Open trapdoor in north-west corner and kill the mourners.","Defeat then talk to Head Mourner. {Chat: 1 I have some questions. > 2 How were you going to summon the Dark Lord? > 3 Enough questions. > Any}","Talk to Elena with one free inventory space.","Go up to the floor 2 and replace the Mourners standard.","Head to the entrance of Ardougne Castle.","Talk to Sir Edmond at the entrance. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Head upstairs, talk to King Lathas.","Kill Sir Hugo.","Talk to King Lathas. {Chat: 3 You need to pay with your death.}","Talk to Sir Edmond.","Return to Lletya, switch back into full mourner's gear and talk to Arianwyn to go back to the undercity. {Chat: 1 I'm ready to teleport.}","Talk to Iestin Edern. {Chat: 3 Okay - what do I do now? > 2 Go on... > 1 Yes - teleport me to Lletya now.}","Talk to Gwir, just north. {Chat: 1 I need to find the Elders of Prifddinas.}","If you don't have 3 free inventory spaces, use the bank in the building","Search a bookcase for The Lost Elders book. {Chat: 1 The Lost Elders}","Read the book.","Talk to Gwir for 2 items. {Chat: 1 I need to find the Elders of Prifddinas. > 4 Lord Amlodd. > 5 More... > 2 Lady Meilyr. > 5 That's all.}"],"t":"Time to attack"},{"n":"10 magic logs","r":"","s":["The blue symbols you need to inspect are on the walls, near the floor, in Lletya. Ground level:\n  - Ranging shop (south west building), along western wall\n  - Southern building, south wall.\n  - Bank, east wall, south of the table.","Upper level:\n  - Up the central stairs, outside altar room, north wall\n  - Up the clothing store stairs, west wall.","Head to the centre of Lletya and build the statue hotspot.","Climb upstairs.","Speak to Kelyn. {Chat: 4 It's time. I'm gathering the clan leaders.}"],"t":"Finding Lady Ithell"},{"n":"Rune bar, combat equipment, 1 empty summoning pouch, 200 spirit shards, 1 gold charm, 1 green charm, 1 crimson charm, 1 blue charm, and 1 Amlodd charm","r":"Plant cure (you can buy a plant cure at the fruit tree patch elf), Meilyr potion recipe (to avoid banking later)","s":["Make your way to the Well of Voyage:\n  - Exit Lletya, pass tree (north-west).\n  - Step-over tripwire (west).\n  - Enter dense forest (west).\n  - Jump leaves (north).\n  - Head east until you find a cave entrance and enter it.","Head east, mine cracked wall (south of the well).","Enter tunnel.","Kill 3 level 70 automatons (each automaton uses a different side of the combat triangle).","Wake Lady Trahaearn. {Chat: 1 Repair the exoskeleton. > 4 It's time. I'm gathering the clan leaders.}"],"t":"Finding Lady Trahaearn"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go north back into the room where you mined the wall.","Use the Amlodd Charm on the obelisk to the north-west. {Chat: 1 Create the Amlodd pouch.}","Summon Amlodd pouch. {Chat: 1 Are you my summoned creature now? Can I command you? > 3 It's time. I'm gathering the clan leaders.}"],"t":"Finding Lord Amlodd"},{"n":"Plant cure, Meilyr potion recipe","r":"","s":["Home teleport to Tirannwn Lodestone.","Pick a blue mushroom (you must have the Meilyr potion recipe in order to pick the mushrooms).","Enter Dense Forest (west of Tirannwn Lodestone).","Pick a red mushroom (these mushrooms are for later. Might appear very light shade of red).","Step over trip-wire (north-west).","Enter dense forest two times (north - do not pass the third one).","Chop down tree (east).","Inspect tree (west).","Use plant cure on the tree.","Talk to Lord Crwys. {Chat: 4 It's time. I'm gathering the clan leaders.}"],"t":"Finding Lord Crwys"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Make your way to the Poison Waste:\n  - Take Fairy ring code DLR to the small island in the swamp. Head west once arriving onto the island via fairy ring.\n  - Alternatively, go to Lletya:\n    - Exit Lletya, pass tree (north-west).\n    - Head far south to the large swamp area, past the magic trees.","Jump the small rocks to each island, going west, referencing the map captioned right (read map from right to left).","Talk to Elf Hermit. {Chat: 2 I seek the wisdom of Seren. > 2 Seren's faithfulness to the elves. > 1 The symmetry of crystals. > 3 I don't know. > 4 It's time. I'm gathering the clan leaders.}}}"],"t":"Finding Lady Hefin"},{"n":"blue Isafdar mushroom, red Isafdar mushroom, super defence (3)","r":"Ring of kinship","s":["Grind your red and blue Isafdar mushrooms.","Use on super defence (3) potion.","Teleport to Daemonheim by using ring of kinship or taking the ferry by talking to Bryll Thoksdottir in Taverley.","Drink Meilyr potion in the Dungeoneering lobby at Daemonheim.","Enter the portal that appears on the west side.","Talk to Lady Meilyr. {Chat: 4 It's time. I'm gathering the clan leaders.}"],"t":"Finding Lady Meilyr"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Lletya.","Talk to Arianwyn. {Chat: 1 I'm ready to teleport.}","Talk to Iestin Edern. {Chat: 3 That's all for now.}","Travel to Tyras Camp (west of Tirannwn lodestone) or charter ship to Tyras Camp via Port Sarim.","Talk to General Hining. {Chat: 4 The time has come to face the darkness.}","Prepare for combat (fire-based spells preferred).","Return to Lletya.","Talk to Arianwyn. {Chat: 1 I'm ready to teleport.}","Talk to Iestin Edern."],"t":"Distraction"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the Grand Library and walk west to the puzzle. {Chat: 2 Okay, what do I do now?}","Talk to Lord Crwys to begin stage 1."],"t":"Boss fight"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Direct light into the centre (place/rotate mirrors as needed).","Use Protect/Deflect Magic and keep moving when Dark Lord is alive. You can either kill the enemies between puzzles or tank their hits.\n  - Each puzzle completed saves, so you can leave for more food and return between puzzles/fights.","After directing the beam into the Crwys Crystal, there will be some dialogue.","Quest complete!","Recommended: exit the Grand Library and speak to Arianwyn to teleport to the entrance of Prifddinas, or walk there yourself. After a skippable cutscene, the city of Prifddinas will be unlocked."],"t":"Light puzzle"}]},"Player-owned farm tutorial":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Start the tutorial by talking with Granny Potterington in front of her house at the centre of the farm.","Pick up Jack the yak from behind the farmhouse and talk to Granny.","Sell Jack to Prezleek (yak trader), located beside the well in front of the house (gain 500 beans).","Add the beans to the currency pouch.","Buy a small animal pen kit (tutorial) from the Farmers' Market (right-click \"Farmers' Market\" on Granny; costs 100 beans).","Buy two rabbits from the market and check each of them in the inventory (cost 10 beans each).","Build the small pen (click \"build\" on the broken paddock (small)) and place the two rabbits inside (click \"check animals\" or use the common brown rabbit on small paddock).","Check the rabbits by clicking on them in the pen and click \"cure disease\". Then investigate all options and choose \"administer treatment\". Click flu.","Talk to Granny to get fruity mush and return to pen to 'fill trough' and head back to Granny.","Pass the time with her until the rabbits have matured; talk until option to advance time or wait 22 minutes.","Take the two rabbits out of the pen. (Optionally \"gather produce\" for 275 Farming experience (137.5 each))","Talk to Granny to get more fruity mush.","Bring the rabbits to the breeding pen behind the main farmhouse. Click \"check animals\" on the breeding paddock or use the rabbit on it.","Fill trough. Soon a child bunny will appear (or talk to Granny to advance time until this happens).","Talk to Granny to complete the tutorial."],"t":"Walkthrough"}]},"Priest in Peril":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to King Roald in Varrock Palace. {Chat: 2 Greet the king. > Accept} (if New Foundations is started. {Chat: 3 Greet the king. > Accept})","Go to the temple in Silvarea which is east of the earth altar.\n  - Players with an invitation box can teleport twice to arrive outside the temple.","Knock at the large door of the temple. {Chat: 2 Knock at the door. > 1 Roald sent me to check on Drezel. > 1 Yes.}","Go north and enter the mausoleum.","Kill Cerberus.","Teleport to Varrock.","Talk to King Roald. {Chat: 1 Talk about Priest in Peril.}"],"t":"A missing monk"},{"n":"A bucket","r":"","s":["At this time you can bring the 25 unnoted pure essence to save a trip later.","Enter the Temple and kill a level 23 Monk of Zamorak to obtain a golden key.","Go outside and enter the Mausoleum to the north and through the gate.","Study the monuments.","Use the golden key on the one that has the iron key.","Fill a bucket with water from the well in the centre of the monument room."],"t":"Making things right"},{"n":"Iron key, bucket of murky water, and 50 unnoted rune essence or 25 unnoted pure essence","r":"","s":["Go back to the temple and climb to the top floor.","Use the iron key on the cell door and talk to Drezel.","Use the bucket of blessed water on the Morytania coffin.","Return to the mausoleum, enter the monument room, and speak with Drezel.","Talk to him again to give him 50 unnoted rune essence or 25 unnoted pure essence.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Saradomin's blessing"}]},"Princess and the Pauper":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Rodney in the kitchen of Fort Forinthry. {Chat: 1 Start 'Princess and the Pauper'. > Accept}\n  - If Princess does not follow you, talk to Princess one square west of Rodney. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Aster at Fort Forinthry {Chat: 1 Talk about quests... > 1 Talk about 'Princess and the Pauper'.}","Talk to Overseer Siv in the Command Centre {Chat: 2 Talk about quests.}","Exit the Command Centre and stand west of it, just by the wooden barrels.","Talk to Princess to obtain a lost sausage.","Talk to the Cook in the Jolly Boar Inn. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Head north to the Wilderness wall just outside the inn and talk to Princess to obtain a half-eaten meat pie.","Go to the small cabbage patch south of the Blue Moon Inn within Varrock and talk to Princess.","After the cutscene, talk to Princess again. Pick up the raw beef nearby if you don't have one."],"t":"Yet another mystery"},{"n":"Bowl of water, raw salmon, raw meat, and a hammer (tool belt does not work)","r":"","s":["Get the ingredients for the dinner:\n  - Use a hammer on raw meat to obtain tenderised meat.\n  - Pick the redberry bush south of Varrock, near the elder tree. {Chat: 2 The juiciest redberries.} Do this after the conversation with Princess, otherwise you won't get the juiciest redberries.\n  - With a free inventory space, talk to Gertrude in her house about the secret ingredient. {Chat: 4 Ask about the 'secret ingredient leaves'.}\n    - If you have started Rat Catchers, {Chat: 5}\n  - Use the raw salmon on the range in Gertrude's house to make a gently smoked salmon. {Chat: 2 Smoked salmon.}","Use a bowl of water on any of the ingredients to make an uncooked dog's dinner.","Cook the uncooked dog's dinner on the range to obtain an unseasoned dog's dinner.","Use the finest doogle leaves on it to make a perfect dog's dinner.","Talk to Princess to show her the completed perfect dog's dinner.","Go back to the cabbage patch near the south entrance of Varrock and talk to Princess there. She will lead you back in the direction of the Jolly Boar Inn.","Go back to the Jolly Boar Inn. Stand inside, west of the kitchen, and talk to Princess. {Chat: 1 Continue 'Princess and the Pauper'.}","After the cutscene, talk to Princess.","Go directly north, and talk to the stray dog outside the inn (the dog is just south of the wilderness wall).","Talk to Rodney at Fort Forinthry. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Preparing a meal"},{"n":"2 wooden frames, 6 planks, 10 steel nails, 2 bolts of cloth and 2 wool","r":"","s":["Talk to Bill. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Bill again with the materials in the backpack. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Choose a name for the dog to finish the quest. {Chat: ~}"],"t":"Building a doghouse"}]},"Purple Cat (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Wendy, West of Draynor lodestone. {Chat: 4 Have you seen that purple cat wandering around? > 2 If I brought you a cat, could you make it purple? > Accept}","Travel to Betty's Magic Emporium in Port Sarim and enter the trapdoor.","Talk to Lottie."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Blackbird to empty holding pen","Lizard to Blackbird pen","Rat to Rat pen","Snail to Reptile pen","Spider to Spider pen","Bat to Snail pen","Lizard to Bat pen","Spider to Blackbird pen","Snail to Spider pen","Rat to Reptile pen","Spider to Rat pen","Lizard to Blackbird pen","Bat to Bat pen","Snail to Snail pen","Lizard to Spider pen","Spider to Blackbird pen","Rat to Rat pen","Lizard to Reptile pen","Spider to Spider pen","Blackbird to Blackbird pen"],"t":"Solving puzzle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open the chest to the northwest and search it.","Bring the magic unguent back to Wendy. {Chat: 4 I have some magic unguent for you!}"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Quiet Before the Swarm":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Sir Tiffy Cashien in the Falador Park about the void knights. {Chat: 1 Void Knights. > Accept}\n  - Or, if Slug Menace isn't complete {Chat: 2 Void Knights. > Accept}","Go to the Void Knights' Outpost.\n  - To get there, speak to the Squire on the pier at Port Sarim to travel to the island by ship free of charge. {Chat: 3 I'd like to go to your outpost.}","Speak to Commodore Matthias in the north-east building.","Talk to Captain Tyr just south of the building.","Talk to the following people about escaping pests:\n  - Knight Ami {Chat: 4 That's all, thanks.}\n  - Knight Bernard {Chat: 3 Have you heard anything about pests escaping? > 4 That's all, thanks.}\n  - Knight Diana {Chat: 3 Have you heard anything about pests escaping? > 4 That's all, thanks.}\n  - Knight Mikhal {Chat: 3 Have you heard anything about pests escaping? > 4 That's all, thanks.}\n  - Jessika {Chat: 4 Have you heard anything about pests escaping? > 5 That's all, thanks.}\n  - Mariah {Chat: 4 That's all, thanks.}\n  - Mrs Gord {Chat: 3 Have you heard anything about pests escaping? > 4 That's all, thanks.}\n  - Squire Sam {Chat: 1 Ask about escaped pest. > 2 That's all, thanks.}\n  - Terry Gord {Chat: 3 Have you heard anything about pests escaping? > 4 That's all, thanks.}"],"t":"Starting"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Captain Tyr.","Talk to Jessika about the crimes she has committed. {Chat: 5 Confront about a crime. > 3 You let a pest escape to the mainland.}","Talk to Captain Tyr.","Talk to Commodore Matthias.","Agree during the cutscene. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"The accused"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Solve the 3x3 slider puzzle. The border helps you find their correct positions.\n  - The centre piece will appear when you have placed the border pieces.","Watch the cutscene and continue the dialogue with Commodore Mathias.}}"],"t":"Inside Jessika's mind"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Bank all your items, both equipped and in your inventory. Dismiss any pets or familiars.","Return to Sir Tiffy and talk about Void Knights. {Chat: 1 Void Knights.}\n  - Or, if Slug Menace isn't complete {Chat: 2 Void Knights.}"],"t":"Arresting Jessika"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Commander Korasi. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to the toll booth to start the puzzle. {Chat: 2 What do I need to do?}","Complete the puzzle:\n  - Talk to Bernard and cross with him. {Chat: 1 I'll cross with you.}\n  - Talk to the toll booth to send yourself over. {Chat: 1 Send someone over the bridge. > 1 Yourself}\n  - Talk to Ami or Diana and have them cross together. {Chat: 2 You cross with [Diana/Ami].}\n  - Talk to the toll booth to send Bernard over. {Chat: 1 Send someone over the bridge. > 1 Bernard}\n  - Talk to Bernard and cross with him. {Chat: 1 I'll cross with you.}"],"t":"Bridge and the sword"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Completing the puzzle correctly triggers a cutscene."],"t":"Ship positions"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill the torcher.","Go up the ladder.","Kill the shifter and wait for another cutscene.","Once teleported, talk to Sir Tiffy.","Speak with Captain Tyr at the Void Knights' Outpost.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The Pests' attack"}]},"Rag and Bone Man":{"sections":[{"n":"one or more empty pots (can be reused)","r":"","s":["Talk to the Odd Old Man in Silvarea. {Chat: 1 Anything I can do to help? > Accept}","Go to Draynor Village market and talk to Fortunato about the quest (do not steal from the stalls before talking to him, as you won't be able to initiate the conversation for a couple of minutes). {Chat: 2 Talk about Rag and Bone Man.}","Buy 8 jugs of vinegar.","Use the jugs of vinegar on your empty pots.","Gather and use each bone listed below on the pots of vinegar.}}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Obtain the bones. Use the table below as a reference.","East of the River Lum in Lumbridge","Near the Draynor lodestone and the Wizard's Tower","East of Barbarian Village and south-west of the Grand Exchange","Stronghold of Security","Goblin Village","Port Sarim","By the Coal truck mine and Hemenster","Goblin Cave","Around the Varrock Dig Site","God Wars Dungeon","Directly east of the Captured Temple","South of the Mind altar","Legends' Guild south-west mine (Fairy ring code BLR)","South of the fruit tree patch by the Tree Gnome Village","East of Rellekka","Inside of the Lumbridge Swamp Caves in the area in the south-east corner","Dorgesh-Kaan South Dungeon (fairy ring code AJQ)","Fred the Farmer's pen, north of Lumbridge","Near the Wilderness wall, north of the Edgeville Monastery","South-west of Falador","In the Fisher Realm (Fairy ring code BJR)","South of Seers' Village","South of Yanille","Ardougne Zoo (fairy ring code BIS)","East of Rellekka","Varrock south-east mine","South of Wilderness Crater","North of Karamja lodestone","East of Karamja Volcano","Ardougne Zoo (must have level 33 Magic for Telekinetic Grab)","Mos Le'Harmless","Stronghold of Security","Behind the Dancing Donkey Inn in south-east Varrock","Varrock sewers","South-west of Port Sarim","Behind Lumbridge Castle and Lumbridge swamp","In the pen south of Varrock","Edgeville dungeon","Yanille Dungeon","Legends' Guild basement","Heroes' Guild basement","Coal truck mine","Temple of Ikov","Goblin Cave","Taverley Dungeon","Chaos Druid Tower dungeon"],"t":"Obtaining the Bones"},{"n":"8 core logs of any type (eternal magic logs does not work)","r":"","s":["Go back to the Odd Old Man's hut.","Add logs, then a pot of bones to the pot boiler, and light it. Collect the bone when it finishes boiling after 12 seconds (hopping worlds will skip the boiling).","Repeat for the remaining bones.","Talk to the Odd Old Man.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Raksha, the Shadow Colossus (quest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Laniakea, south-east in the ruins on Anachronia. {Chat: 2 The doorway at the top of the ruins. > Accept > 1 Zaros? > 3 Can we open the door somehow?}\n  - She is also at the ruins around the lodestone but she tells you to go to the south-east and talk to her there.\n  - You can use option 2 on the Slayer cape to get to her quickly or teleport to Xolo City [X] via the Orthen teleportation device, then run south-east.","Run west, up to the top of the stairs.","Siphon the shadow anima pools until you reach 100%.\n  - Completing each pool will damage you 200 points. Be aware of that in case you are on low life points.","Unlock the door.","Talk to Zaros.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Walkthrough"}]},"Rat Catchers":{"sections":[{"n":"a cat, hellcat or kitten, 1 backpack space","r":"","s":["Talk to Gertrude in west edge of Varrock. {Chat: 3 Talk about the 'Ratcatchers' quest. > Accept}\n  - If you have a Hellcat out {Chat: 4 Talk about the 'Ratcatchers' quest. > Accept}","Take out your cat or kitten.","Talk to Phingspet or Grimesquit in the Varrock Sewers right next to the eastern entrance of Varrock Palace (down the manhole).","Catch 8 rats with your cat or kitten by choosing the \"interact-with\" option. {Chat: 2 Chase-Vermin.}\n  - The \"Hide familiar options\" setting must be off in the Gameplay settings.","Talk to them again to obtain a rat pole."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"1 free inventory space","r":"","s":["Talk to Jimmy Dazzler in the house in East Ardougne, directly west of the Flying Horse Inn, north-west of the Ardougne Castle. Ensure you finish the dialogue, or you will not be able to follow the next step.","Read the \"directions\" scroll he gives you. {Chat: 1 Follow the directions to the house.}"],"t":"Just the ticket"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Avoid guards whilst traversing throughout. You can use Surge or Dive to navigate quickly.","Hide behind the hedges directly west of the mansion when the southwest guard walks toward the bridge.","Run to the north-west corner when the guard is behind the hedges.","Run to the hedges directly north of the mansion.","Climb up the nearby trellis on the northern of the mansion."],"t":"Going through the garden"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Once inside continue to avoid guards. You can hide by the potted flower on the balcony first.","Wield your rat pole.","Catch 1 rat with your cat in the north-west room. You may pick up your cat to prevent stuck outside. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Find your way into the opposite bedroom across the hall and wait (or wait for one guard to be on the balcony and the second have his back appropriately turned to dash to the next room).","Catch 2 rats with your cat in the south-east room. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 Yes.}","Go down the ladder in the north-east of this room.","Catch 2 rats with your cat in this room, then 1 in the room to the north. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 Yes. > 1 Yes.}\n  - There is a chance that a rat will spawn west of the ladder room instead of to the north.","Leave the area by using Home Teleport to Ardougne lodestone.\n  - You can also return to the trellis and climb down it to return directly to Jimmy.","Talk to Jimmy Dazzler.\n  - You can destroy your directions scroll now."],"t":"Catching the rats"},{"n":"a cat, 4 pieces of cheese, a bucket of milk, clean marrentill, unicorn horn dust, rat poison (alternatively, clean kwuarm, red spiders eggs and an empty vial), 5-10 raw or cooked fish for your cat (even if you're using a fully grown cat)","r":"","s":["Talk to Hooknosed Jack in south-east Varrock, inside the fenced area past the guard.","If you need to make the rat poison and do not have the ingredients (clean kwuarm, red spiders eggs and an empty vial) in the backpack on the first talk, talk to him again. {Chat: 1 Can you make me some rat poison?}","Climb up the ladder in the warehouse directly south of the Dancing Donkey Inn.","Use rat poison on all 4 pieces of cheese.","Use poisoned cheese on all of the rat holes.","Talk to Hooknosed Jack. {Chat: 2 Can I help?}","Talk to the Apothecary in south-western Varrock for cat antipoison. {Chat: 5 I need to talk to you about cats.}\n  - If the first option is not 'Can you make a strength potion?', {Chat: # Talk about something else. > 5 I need to talk to you about cats.}","Talk to Hooknosed Jack. Finish the dialogue or you will not be able to progress.","Climb up the ladder in the warehouse.","Pick up your cat and use it on the hole in wall (not the rat holes). {Chat: 1 Yes > 1 Be careful in there, cat!} Make sure you finish the dialogue to start the fight, life points bars appear.","Keep using fish on the hole in wall (not on the cat) to restore the cat's life points until the king rat dies.\n  - If you lose your cat by going down the ladder, exit to lobby out and join the world should return it to you.\n  - If you are in a group or have lootshare active, then the kill will not register and you will need to go down the ladder to reset the king rat.","You may retrieve your cat by calling your follower or by climbing down the ladder.","Talk to Jack to tell him the king rat is dead."],"t":"Hooknosed Jack"},{"n":"a cat, a catspeak amulet, an empty pot, weeds","r":"","s":["Talk to Smokin' Joe in east Keldagrim, just east of the mining shop. {Chat: 1 I could help you.}",": If this is your first time entering Keldagrim proceed with the following route:\n  - Enter the tunnel north-east of Rellekka and Fremennik Province lodestone.\n  - Go-through the cave entrance between the two dwarven statues.\n  - Talk to the Dwarven Boatman and get him to take you into Keldagrim, this may cause you to automatically start the quest The Giant Dwarf.\n  - Proceed to the east part of Keldagrim and talk with Smokin' Joe.","Use some weeds on an empty pot and light the pot of weeds.","Use the smouldering pot on the rat hole near the crates on the southern wall.","Use the pot on the same hole again with your cat out and your catspeak amulet on, your cat will offer to help.\n  - If your cat doesn't automatically initiate a conversation with you, you may have to attempt this a third time.","Talk to Joe again.\n  - You can drop the smouldering pot now."],"t":"Smokin' Joe"},{"n":"101 coins (51 coins with the ring of charos(a)), and one free inventory space.","r":"Pollnivneach Teleport Scroll and/or ring of charos(a)","s":["Talk to Felkrash, north of Port Sarim lodestone.","Talk to The Face nearby.","Head south of the bar in Pollnivneach.","Throw a coin into the money pot next to Badir the Snake Charmer {Chat: 1 Yes.} and then complete the conversation. {Chat: 2 I want to talk to you about animal charming. > 3 What if I offered you some money? > 2 Forget about it. I don't care. > 2 Walk away slowly > 1 Stop} (unless wearing a ring of charos).\n  - He will give you a music scroll.","If you have a snake charm in bank, retrieve it.","Return to Port Sarim.","Play the snake charm. Only 1 note can be set per page.\n  - Go through the pages and click the correct notes (one note per page). The red dots in the music scroll correspond to the black dots on the flutes.\n  - On page 5, click the <) icon in the top left before you play the note. You can go back and make corrections to the pages if needed.\n  - Click play once all the notes are correctly selected.\n  - There will be short cutscene upon completing correctly.","Talk to Felkrash.\n  - You can destroy your music scroll now.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The Face and the Felkrash"}]},"Rebuilding Edgeville (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Start by talking to Vannaka near the lever teleport from Edgeville, for a To-Do list. {Chat: 3 Did you see what attacked Edgeville? > Accept}.","Head to Aggie's house which is north-west of the Draynor Village bank and take the broom when Aggie is not looking at you to obtain Aggie's broom (uncharged).","Charge the uncharged broom with 100 water runes to obtain Aggie's broom.","Head back to Edgeville and sweep four scorch marks.","Talk to Jeffery, who is east of the bank and near a furnace, for Jeffery's hammer. {Chat: 2 Have you seen the damage done to Edgeville?}","Fix the following buildings by getting close to the locations and selecting the first option of the hammer in your backpack. You will need to remove them from your plank box if using that to carry them.\n  - The house north of the bank, requiring ten mahogany planks.\n  - The market stall north of the bank, requiring ten planks.\n  - The broken window on the north side of the bank, requiring five planks and a unit of molten glass.\n  - Jeffery's Armoury, east of the bank, requiring five planks.\n  - The guard house, north-east of the bank, requiring a marble block.\n  - The house across River Lum, between the river and Grand Exchange, requiring ten oak planks.","Use five bittercap mushrooms on the fairy ring south of Quercus.","Clear the Destroyed Roof and Destroyed Wall just west of the fairy ring.","Consecrate or desecrate the burnt skeleton north of the bank.","Nurture four burnt trees. Any four around Edgeville work.","Go back to Vannaka for your reward. {Chat: 3 Rebuilding Edgeville}"],"t":"Checklist"}]},"Recipe for Disaster":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the doors to the dining room (you must view the cutscene).","The members of the council must now be freed.\n  - Recipe for Disaster: Freeing the Goblin Generals/Quick guide\n  - Recipe for Disaster: Freeing the Mountain Dwarf/Quick guide\n  - Recipe for Disaster: Freeing Evil Dave/Quick guide\n  - Recipe for Disaster: Freeing the Lumbridge Sage/Quick guide\n  - Recipe for Disaster: Freeing Pirate Pete/Quick guide\n  - Recipe for Disaster: Freeing Skrach Uglogwee/Quick guide\n  - Recipe for Disaster: Freeing Sir Amik Varze/Quick guide\n  - Recipe for Disaster: Freeing King Awowogei/Quick guide"],"t":"Freeing council members"}]},"Recipe for Disaster: Another Cook's Quest":{"sections":[{"n":"1 Eye of newt, 1 Greenman's ale, 1 Rotten tomato, 1 Ashes, 1 Fruit blast (premade does not work)","r":"","s":["Talk to the Cook in the kitchen of Lumbridge Castle. {Chat: 1 Do you have any other quests for me? > Any > 1 What seems to be the problem? > Accept}","Use the ashes on the fruit blast.","Give the items to the cook.","Subquest complete!","Go through the dining hall door and complete the dialogue to unlock the rest of subquests.\n  - It is recommended to inspect each character first, complete every subquest outside this instanced area and then finish all of them at once."],"t":"Another small favour"}]},"Recipe for Disaster: Defeating the Culinaromancer":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["It is recommended to bring good food and possibly super potions.","Prayers and Ancient Curses, Summoning familiars, and cannons cannot be used.","Each boss spawns immediately after its predecessor is defeated.","Leaving the boss area and restocking after each boss is allowed.","If killed, your gravestone will appear right outside the Culinaromancer portal.","The Gelatinnoth Mother cannot be damaged with necromancy attack. She can be damaged with poison damage from Putrid Zombie."],"t":"Notes"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill Agrith-Na-Na.","Agrith-Na-Na uses melee when in range and uses Fire Blast when not in melee range.","Ranged attack is effective against him."],"t":"Agrith-Na-Na"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill Flambeed.","Ice gloves must be used if using a weapon. Be sure to have a backpack space for your weapon, which will automatically be unequipped when engaging Flambeed. If you do not have an backpack space when Flambeed spawns, your ice gloves might be sent to your bank to make room for your weapon in the backpack.","Using water spells or ranged attack is effective against him."],"t":"Flambeed"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill Karamel.","It is recommended to bring stat restore potions.","It is also recommended to fight her in melee range with a fire spell as her melee attacks do little damage."],"t":"Karamel"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill Dessourt.","Iban Blast and ranged attack works well on him.","At least one restore potion is recommended as he has a chance of draining stats."],"t":"Dessourt"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill Gelantinnoth Mother.","Damage can be done to her in this order: (necromancy attack does not work)\n  - Wind spells (white)\n  - Water spells (blue)\n  - Melee attack (orange)\n  - Earth spells (brown)\n  - Fire spells (red)\n  - Ranged attack (green)\n  - After green, she repeats the cycle."],"t":"Gelatinnoth Mother"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["The Culinaromancer has little to no defence but can hit over 200.","Kill the Culinaromancer with any combat style.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The Culinaromancer"}]},"Recipe for Disaster: Freeing Evil Dave":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Inspect Evil Dave inside Lumbridge Castle Banquet Hall.","West of Edgeville's bank, talk to Doris. {Chat: 1 Is Dave in? > 1 Yes, I'm evil!}","Head into the house's basement.","Talk to Evil Dave. {Chat: 2 General chat > 3 What did you eat at the secret council meeting? > 4 You've got to tell me because the magic requires it!}","Return to Doris. If you miss this step, the hellrats will only drop ashes.","Head back in the basement, interact with your cat and select \"Chase-Vermin\". {Chat: 2 Chase-Vermin}(Switch off 'Hide Familiar Options' in Gameplay->Combat & Action Bar-> 'Choose Option' Menu)","As your cat catches the rats, pick up the spices that drop.","Do so until at least six doses of each of the four spices are collected.","Make Dave's Evil stew by combining doses of each spice on the stews.","After determining the right combination, have Evil Dave taste it and finish the dialogue. This won't consume the stew.","Head to Lumbridge and give Evil Dave the stew.","Subquest complete!"],"t":"Freeing Evil Dave"}]},"Recipe for Disaster: Freeing King Awowogei":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["The completion of this subquest will require players to have a ninja monkey greegree, zombie monkey greegree, and gorilla greegree as well as a monkeyspeak amulet."],"t":"Forenote"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Inspect King Awowogei in the Lumbridge castle dining room.","Travel to Ape Atoll.","If not already, equip any monkey greegree and the monkeyspeak amulet.","If you do not already have a banana and monkey nuts head to Solihib's Food Stall on the north-east of the market and buy one of each.","If you do not already have a rope, buy one from Ifaba at the south-west of the market.","Head to the south-easternmost building in Marim.","Talk to the Elder Guard.","Talk to Awowogei. Ask about his favourite dish.","Head to the Temple of Marimbo to the north of Awowogei's seat.","Talk to the three wise monkeys in the north-west corner of the temple. {Chat: 3 Do you know anything about the king's favourite dish?}","Talk to the three wise monkeys two more times (first discussing the banana and then the same for the monkey nuts)."],"t":"King Awowogei"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to Crash Island and enter the pit east of Lumdo. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm as hard as nails.} Lower level combat players may find it useful to turn on Protect from Melee before entering the pit and also having an emergency teleport. Anti-poison is also useful.","Kill a snake to get a snake corpse. Optionally, collect multiple in the event you burn the dish."],"t":"The Snake"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Find the Red Banana Tree on the coast west of Marim.","Equip a gorilla greegree.","Use a rope on the Red Banana Tree.","Slice the red banana. Once the previous one is sliced, you can collect another, however it has no other uses."],"t":"The Red Banana"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head south of Marim to the Ape Atoll Agility Course.","Equip the ninja greegree.","Proceed through the course until reaching the hole right after the rope swing. The course starts with the small stone in the water next to the palm tree.\n  - If you have a ninja monkey greegree (small) and fairy ring access, you may also teleport to fairy ring CLR and climb through the hollow log to quickly get there.","Enter the hole and pick tchiki monkey nuts from the bush.","Grind the nut. Once the previous one is ground, you can collect another, however it has no other uses.","Climb up the rope and finish the course."],"t":"Tchiki Nuts"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["If below level 70 Cooking, make sure to have the boost at this part.","Use the snake corpse on either the red banana slices or the tchiki monkey nut paste to prepare a raw stuffed snake.","Enter the trapdoor near the eastern wall of the temple.","Walk down one of the wooden platforms and Enter the crack in the east wall between the wooden platforms, called \"Exit\".","Equip the zombie greegree.","Walk across the coals and Use the raw stuffed snake on the long rock.","Head to Lumbridge Castle and make sure you have equipped your monkeyspeak amulet.","Use the stuffed snake on King Awowogei. Be careful not to eat it.","Subquest complete!"],"t":"Freeing King Awowogei"}]},"Recipe for Disaster: Freeing Pirate Pete":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Inspect Pirate Pete in the banquet hall in Lumbridge Castle.","Talk to the Cook in the Lumbridge Castle. {Chat: 3 Protecting the Pirate > 1 Where do I get Ground Cod? > 2 Where do I get Ground Giant Crab Meat? > 3 Where do I get Breadcrumbs? > 5 Thanks!}"],"t":"Pirate Pete"},{"n":"1 fishbowl, 1 needle, 3 bronze wire, any weapon unequipped in the backpack, at least 8 backpack space","r":"","s":["Bank any Summoning pouches or Pets.","Talk to Murphy on the docks of Port Khazard. {Chat: 1 Talk about Recipe for Disaster.}","With your fishbowl, talk to him again. {Chat: 1 Talk about Recipe for Disaster. > 2 Not just yet.}","Equip the fishbowl helmet and diving apparatus.","Whilst weighing under or exactly 27, having your needle and bronze wire, talk to Murphy again. {Chat: 1 Talk about Recipe for Disaster. > 1 Yes, Let's go diving.}\n  - There is a bank deposit box next to Murphy.","Pick some kelp (your inventory is hidden).\n  - It is advisable to obtain multiple in the event you burn the fishcake.","Swim north and talk to Nung.","Head west to the Mudskipper cave and pick up five rocks.","Enter the cave and equip your weapon.","Kill mudskippers for 5 hides.","Return to Nung with the five hides, your needle, and three bronze wire.","Talk to Nung again.","Enter the crab pen and equip your weapon.","Kill some crabs and take their meat.\n  - It is advised to obtain multiple in the event you burn the fishcake.","While in the pen teleport out to Lumbridge.\n  - Alternatively, leave the crab pen and climb up the anchor chain to the south."],"t":"Diving"},{"n":"kelp, crab meat, raw cod, bread","r":"","s":["Return to the kitchen in Lumbridge Castle.","Prepare the ingredients:\n  - Grind the kelp.\n  - Choose the Grind option on the crab meat.\n  - Choose the Grind option on the raw cod.\n  - Choose the Slice option on the bread.\n  - If at any point while preparing the ingredients, the message \"Nothing interesting happens\" appears, talk to the Cook.","Talk to the Cook. {Chat: 3 Protecting the Pirate}","Use the ingredients on each other.","Cook the Raw fishcake.","Use fishcake on Pirate Pete.\n  - If the fishcake is eaten, you need to re-obtain all of the ingredients.","Subquest complete!"],"t":"Freeing Pirate Pete"}]},"Recipe for Disaster: Freeing Sir Amik Varze":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Inspect Sir Amik Varze.","Talk to the Cook in the Lumbridge Castle kitchen. {Chat: 4 More... > 5 More... > 2 Protecting Sir Amik Varze}"],"t":"Sir Amik"},{"n":"Pot of cream, bucket of milk, and sweetcorn","r":"Empty pot","s":["Use a bucket of milk with a pot of cream.","Locate a windmill (Taverley windmill doesn't work) and pick up an empty pot on the floor 1 .","Put sweetcorn into the hopper on the floor 3.","Operate the hopper controls, then take from the flour bin on the floor 1.","Use the milky mixture with the pot of cornflour."],"t":"The Brulee"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the Kharazi Jungle with a machete and hatchet (tool belt works for both) or use cjs if unlocked.\n  - Have Radimus notes with you, if Legends' Quest isn't completed.","Head southwest of the pool to the beach to find five vanilla plants.","Search a Vanilla plant and add the vanilla pod to the cornflour mixture for brulee."],"t":"Vanilla Pod"},{"n":"","r":"Dragonfire protection}}{{Checklis","s":["Go to Draynor Village and talk to the Wise Old Man. {Chat: 3/4 I'd just like to ask you something. > 2 Strange beasts > 4 The Evil Chicken > 2 Thanks, maybe some other time.}","Head to Zanaris. Use a raw chicken on the Chicken shrine. (Kill a chicken near the shrine for a raw chicken if you need one).","Head north and kill the Evil Chicken.\n  - If the chicken is not in the shrine, talk to the Cook and attempt to fight it again.","Take the evil chicken's egg (right-click the loot pile, as area loot won't show it).","Head south and kill a black dragon.","Take the dragon token it drops (right-click the loot pile, as area loot won't show it).","Use the egg on the brulee."],"t":"Evil Chicken's Egg and Dragon Token"},{"n":"1 dramen branch","r":"","s":["Craft your dramen branches branch, selecting pestle and mortar.\n  - If you do not have Dramen branches, cut one from the dramen tree in the Entrana Dungeon.","Add the cinnamon to the brulee.}}"],"t":"Cinnamon"},{"n":"","r":"Ice gloves or dragonfire protection","s":["Wear the ice gloves or dragonfire protection, otherwise you can take up to 500 damage if you don't have them on for the next few steps.","Rub the dragon token in either Lumbridge or Zanaris.","Ask the Fairy Dragon to flambé the brulee. {Chat: 1 Please flambe this creme brulee for me.}","Head back to Lumbridge Castle then use brulee supreme on Sir Amik.","Subquest complete!"],"t":"Freeing Sir Amik"}]},"Recipe for Disaster: Freeing Skrach Uglogwee":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Inspect Skrach Uglogwee. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm sure I can get some Jubbly Chompy. > 2 Oh Ok then, I guess I'll talk to Rantz.}","Head to Feldip Hills aks and talk to Rantz to the north-east. {Chat: 1 I'm trying to free Skrach. Can you help? > 3 Ok, I'll do it.}","Follow the coast south and talk to Rantz. {Chat: 1 I guess this is the watery place. What now?}","Cut the roots of the old tree, carve it","Talk to Rantz. {Chat: 1 Okay, the boat's ready; now tell me how to get a jubbly.}","With a raw chompy, iron spit, and logs, teleport to the Karamja lodestone.","Head south until a row boat is seen along the western coast. Just south-east of the boat is a small tree with Rantz's arrow stuck in it.","Use the iron spit on the raw chompy and light a fire just west of the small tree.","Cook the chompy on the fire.","Board the nearby ogre boat. {Chat: 1 Yes please, I'll get a lift back with you.}","Talk to Rantz. {Chat: 1 Okay, now tell me how to get jubbly.}","Make a balloon toad by using the following steps (it is advised to make a few in the event you burn the raw jubbly).\n  - Just west, fill your ogre bellows with swamp bubbles from the swamp, then use the bellows on a swamp toad.\n  - Directly west of the swamp pool, mine a feldip swamp rock (near aks).\n  - With the rock, toad, and a ball of wool in your inventory, use the bellows on the bloated toad again to make a balloon toad (the bellows must be filled).","Drop the balloon toad in the area where Rantz is.","When a jubbly bird appears, kill it with an ogre bow and pluck it.\n  - If a jubbly bird does not spawn by the time the balloon toad disappears, you will need to make another one.","Head north to the ogre spit-roast fire and cook the raw jubbly. If you burn it, you must repeat the hunting process.","Return to Lumbridge Castle and Use cooked jubbly on Skrach.","Subquest complete!"],"t":"Skrach"}]},"Recipe for Disaster: Freeing the Goblin Generals":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Inspect either General Bentnoze or General Wartface. They are located in the Lumbridge Castle banquet room.","Head to Goblin Village and climb down the ladder in the eastern building.","Talk to Goblin Cook. {Chat: 2 I need your help... > 1 What do you need? Maybe I can get it for you.}","Give him charcoal. {Chat: 1 I've got the charcoal you were after.}","After the cutscene, talk to him again. {Chat: 3 I need your help...}","Slice an orange into orange slices (not chunks) and use any colour of dye except orange, yellow, red, or pink on the slices to create dyed orange.","Use spice on fishing bait to create spicy maggots.","Right click Use bread on bucket, bowl, or jug of water to create soggy bread.","Talk to Goblin Cook. {Chat: 3 I've got the ingredients we need...}","Head back to the dining room in Lumbridge Castle, use the slop of compromise on either of the Generals.","Subquest complete!"],"t":"Freeing the Generals"}]},"Recipe for Disaster: Freeing the Lumbridge Sage":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Inspect the Lumbridge Sage. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm sure I can make a cake.}","Head to the floor 3 of the Wizards' Tower and talk to Wizard Traiborn who is west of the beam. {Chat: 1 [Ask about the Lumbridge Sage.]}"],"t":"The sage"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Traiborn again for the first quiz. {Chat: 1 [Ask about the Lumbridge Sage.] > 1 Ok. Let's Start!}"],"t":"The egg"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Traiborn again for the second quiz. {Chat: 1 [Ask about the Lumbridge Sage.] > 1 Ok. I'm ready!}"],"t":"The milk"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Traiborn for the final quiz. {Chat: 1 [Ask about the Lumbridge Sage.] > 1 Quiz me!}","After completing his final quiz, you receive an enchanted egg, a bucket of enchanted milk and pot of enchanted flour."],"t":"The flour"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use any of the raw ingredients on a cake tin.","Bake the raw guide cake on a range.","Use the cake of guidance on the Lumbridge Sage back in Lumbridge.","Subquest complete!"],"t":"Freeing the Lumbridge Sage"}]},"Recipe for Disaster: Freeing the Mountain Dwarf":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Inspect the Dwarf.","Head to the Rising Sun Inn pub in Falador.","Ask Emily about dwarves and ale (wear Ring of charos (a) if you have it). {Chat: 2 What can you tell me about dwarves and ale? > 2 I could offer you some in return, how about 200 gold?}\n  - If wearing Ring of charos (a): {Chat: 2 What can you tell me about dwarves and ale? > 3 (Persuade)I'm really quite trustworthy once you get to know me.}","Buy 4 Asgarnian ales from Emily.","Add 1 gold coin to each glass of ale. (you can take coins out of your money pouch by right clicking the price checker in your inventory and selecting withdraw)","Head to the tunnel under White Wolf Mountain (cave north of Taverley lodestone).","Talk to the Old Dwarf, Rohak. You must finish this dialogue to proceed.","Use 4 Asgoldian ales on him and then after the fade, talk to him.",": You may need to repeat this process if you either: exit the cave before the next step, or do not give him the four ales quickly enough.","Talk to Rohak again to give him one-hundred coins, a bucket of milk, an egg, a pot of flour, and a bowl of water.","Quickly pick up the Dwarven rock cake whilst wearing gloves.\n  - If the cake is not picked up fast enough, the ingredients are required to make another one.","Cooling the cake:\n  - If ice gloves were worn whilst picking up the cake, simply return to Lumbridge.\n  - If ice gloves were not worn, either drop the cake and pick it up with ice gloves equipped or kill an icefiend with it in your inventory."],"t":"Freeing the Dwarf"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use the cooled rock cake on the Dwarf.","Subquest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Recruitment Drive":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to Falador.","Go to the White Knights' Castle, and head up to the floor 3 of the western tower.","Talk to Sir Amik Varze. {Chat: 2 I seek a quest! > Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Sir Tiffy Cashien without any items equipped or in the inventory. He can be found in the Falador Park. {Chat: 3 Yes, let's go!}","Optionally, sit on the bench next to Sir Tiffy Cashien to complete the achievement: Tiffy Time."],"t":"The puzzles"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["In this room there will be eleven statues when there should be twelve. The goal is to study the statues then, when the twelfth one is returned, pick the one that was originally missing.\n  - Easy method: look for the colour (bronze, silver, gold) of statue that only has 2 statues instead of 3, then note which weapon of that colour is missing out of the 4 possibilities (sword, halberd, great axe, or mace.)\n  - Alternative method: the moment it shows 12 statues, take a screenshot. Then open the screenshot and compare which was missing and click it.","Find the statue that wasn't there originally and touch it."],"t":"Lady Table"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["As a female character, kill Sir Leye.\n  - If you have not visited the Makeover Mage before starting the quest, you can change your gender via the Customisation interface, under the Appearance tab.\n  - Low level players are encouraged to use Legacy Combat Mode as the life points range won't be as high, thus, quickly ending the fight."],"t":"Sir Kuam Ferentse/Sir Leye"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["In this room, the chicken, grain, and the fox must all be transported to the other side of the bridge in a specific order.","Take the chicken across and put it down. In order to put down an object, open your equipment panel and click on the equipped object.","Take the fox across and put it down. Grab the chicken and return back.","Drop the chicken and take the Grain across.","Drop the grain and return back.","Take the chicken across and drop it."],"t":"Sir Spishyus"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Search the most south-western bookshelf for a knife.","Search all four of the most southern shelves with vials, take all of them.","Search the north-eastern middle-sized crate next to the chest for a tin.","Search the four northern shelves for the remaining vials, take all of them.","Pick up the metal spade on the table.","Use the metal spade on the bunsen burner in the room.","Use the Metal spade (head) on the door.","Use cupric sulphate on the door.","Use a vial of liquid on the door.","Pull on the spade to open the door.","Use the gypsum on the Tin (empty).","Use a vial of liquid on the Tin (gypsum).","Use the tin on the key chained to the south-western wall.","Use the cupric ore powder on the Tin (impression).","Use the tin ore powder on the Tin (copper).","Heat the Tin (tin and copper) on the bunsen burner.","Use a knife, Bronze wire (Recruitment Drive), or chisel on the Tin (key).","Walk-through the open first door.","Unlock the door with the Bronze key (Recruitment Drive)."],"t":"Miss Cheevers"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Sir Ren Itchood.","The first letter of each line he says is the answer to the door's lock.","Possible combinations are: BITE, FISH, LAST, MEAT, RAIN, or TIME."],"t":"Sir Ren Itchood"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ms. Hynn Terprett.","She will give you a riddle."],"t":"Ms. Hynn Terprett"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After you talk to him, do not move, stand there and do nothing until he talks again. Do not take the hourglass."],"t":"Sir Tinley"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After all the puzzles are done, quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Regicide":{"sections":[{"n":"Any bow, arrows, 1-5 ropes, plank","r":"","s":["Talk to King Lathas on the floor 2 of Ardougne Castle.","Travel through the Underground Pass which can be found on the far west side of West Ardougne. You do not need to find another Iban's doll or complete any of the steps from Underground Pass quest. You only need to reach Iban's temple.","Refer to this guide for instructions navigating the Underground Pass.","Enter the well in Iban's Temple.","Exit the cave to the west."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"Limestone","r":"","s":["Run through the forest, talk to Idris. Watch him die then continue.\n  - If Idris does not spawn, log out and back in to trigger the scene.","Go west to jump the leaves trap (a dark green patch on the ground).","Proceed southwest of the musician. Between some trees find a trap of sticks on the ground, click the sticks (choose the \"pass\" option, clicking beyond the sticks has a 100% failure rate).\n  - This may take a few tries (if you spam click the trap, it will let you pass - make sure you're clicking the trap itself, as it has a small hitbox. If you're running low on health, return to the musician to recuperate before trying again.","Continue south towards the lodestone.","Activate the Tirannwn lodestone once you find it.","Run back north-west towards the elf camp.","Jump another leaves trap, run past the bears and cross the log into the elf camp.","Talk to Lord Iorwerth.","Teleport to the Tirannwn lodestone, talk to the elf tracker.","Talk to Lord Iorwerth again which requires at least one free inventory space.","Talk to the elf tracker back at the Tirannwn lodestone.","Follow the tracks just west of the lodestone in front of the dense forest entrance.","Talk to the elf tracker.","Enter the dense forest and kill the guard that appears.","Go north, step-over the tripwire and go through more dense forest.\n  - Stepping over avoids taking damage as opposed to walking through.","Continue north through the dense forest and west, then once again through dense forest to enter Tyras Camp.","Talk to General Hining in the camp.","Take two barrels behind the largest rectangular tent.\n  - The second is required for completing Mourning's End Part I.","Teleport to the Tirannwn loadstone again and head north-west into the elf camp to talk to Lord Iorwerth.","Read the Big Book of Bangs he gives you and pick up the empty pot north of him if you need one.","Teleport to the Tirannwn lodestone again and head south to reach the shoreline of the swamp.","Use the barrels on the tar to fill them into barrels of tar.\n  - There are only two clickable tiles near the corpse and trees. Mouse over along the shoreline until you find the clickable area.","Take some sulphur from the floor, then grind it into ground sulphur.","Go to a furnace and use the limestone on it {Chat: 1 Yes} to obtain some quicklime."],"t":"Tirannwn"},{"n":"The Big Book of Bangs, empty pot, quicklime, strip of cloth, cooked rabbit, barrel of coal-tar, ground sulphur and at least 10 pieces of coal (cannot be in an ore box or noted - more may be required as you fail to operate the still)","r":"","s":["Talk to the Chemist in Rimmington. {Chat: 3 Ask about Regicide. > 1 What is naphtha and how do I make it? > 2 What's quicklime? > 3 What's brimstone?}\n  - The book must be in your inventory, otherwise your Quest Journal will not update.","Use your barrel of tar on the fractionation still outside."],"t":"Sabotage"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Click the tar regulator side twice.","Wait until the arrow gauge is within the green on the pressure valve side, then click the pressure valve once. This should keep the pressure indicator in the green without fluctuating.","Now add coal in 2x increments using the middle \"Add coal\" button to get the tar regulator indicator in the green.","Now that the pressure valve and tar regulator are both in the green, the distillation bar at the bottom of the interface will begin to fill up.","When the distillation bar is full, you may exit out of the interface, You should now have a barrel of naptha in the backpack.\n  - If you plan on completing Mourning's End I a barrel of naphtha is required for that quest, repeat this process for a second barrel."],"t":"Operating the still"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Make the bomb:\n  - Use ground sulphur on the barrel of naphtha for naphtha mix.\n  - Grind the quicklime with an empty pot in your backpack.\n  - Use the pot of quicklime on the naptha mix.\n  - Use a strip of cloth on the barrel bomb.","Teleport back to the Tirannwn lodestone.\n  - Kill and cook a rabbit just north if you didn't bring a cooked rabbit.","Head to the catapult north of Tyras Camp (west through the dense forest and tripwires if you used the lodestone).","Right-click use the cooked rabbit on the Tyras guard standing next to the catapult.","Use the barrel bomb on the catapult.","Talk to Lord Iorwerth at the Elf Camp."],"t":"Preparing barrel bomb"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Attempt to enter Ardougne Castle. Arianwyn will talk to you.","Talk to King Lathas.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The lord's message"}]},"Remains of the Necrolord":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Death in the City of Um. {Chat: Accept}","Talk to the following three listless dead around Daemonheim to free them:\n  - West of the fountain south of the ring of kinship's teleport location.\n  - Beside the entrance to the Kal'gerion resource dungeon (Dungeoneering cape teleport {Chat: 0 More... > 9 Kal'gerion demon dungeon}).\n  - Along the east coast, at the Marmaros & Gorgonite Mine north of the Fremennik ship (Shadow reef)."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport with the ring of kinship again and talk to Lord Yudura (with ghostspeak amulet equipped if you haven't completed the hard Morytania achievements).\n  - Lord Yudura is located immediately at the teleport location, but may be difficult to see, as he blends into the snow. Using High Contrast Mode can be helpful.","Inspect Captain Toma's corpse.","Inspect Taevas's corpse and Vengeance's corpse.","Inspect Lord Yudura's corpse.","Enter the room to the west and take at least the following number from the crates (you can use secondary option to take 5 at a time).\n  - 12 inkwells of basic ghostly ink\n  - 12 inkwells of regular ghostly ink\n  - 6 inkwells of greater ghostly ink\n  - 4 greater ritual candles","Go two rooms east and set up the ritual site.\n  - Place Lord Yudura's corpse on the focus object spot.\n  - Place a greater ritual candle on each of the light source spots.\n  - Draw a glyph on each of the glyph spots.","Return west and talk to Lord Yudura."],"t":"Exploring the floors of Daemonheim"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Lord Yudura.","Go to the southern room.","Talk to Lord Yudura again.","Kill the skeletal archer, sorcerer, and warrior.","Talk to Lord Yudura again.","Talk to Death in the City of Um.","Quest complete!"],"t":"After the ritual"}]},"Requiem for a Dragon":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Aster in the Fort Forinthry Town Hall. {Chat: 1 Talk about quests... > 1 Talk about 'Requiem for a Dragon'. > Accept}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"5 free backpack spaces","r":"Combat equipment","s":["Head east to the rowboat docked next to the Grove cabin.","Interact with the rowboat to travel to Ungael. {Chat: 1 Yes.}\n  - You will spawn next to hostile Zamorakian scouts; praying against Ranged can be helpful. This is a safe encounter, and you will respawn outside of the rowboat upon death.","Run north-west past the scouts and enter the colossal cave.","Head north-west and approach Vorkath. {Chat: 2 Reach out your hand. (friendly) > 2 Keep your hand extended. (friendly) > 2 Encourage Vorkath. (friendly) > 2 Try not to shiver. (friendly) > 1 Study the creature. (neutral) > 2 Lay the dragon's soul to rest. (Necromancy)}","Inspect the crystal shard in the backpack.","Return to the Ungael beach, this time travelling north-east up the hill and interact with the Ruins Entrance to enter.","Head north, just in front of the Imposing Statue, and interact with the doorway to the south.","Follow the path south-west and kill the translator.","Pick up the dropped Zamorakian translator's notes and read them.","Search the bookcase on the northern wall for Zorgoth's Journal.","Search the shelves immediately southeast for a broken focus.","Inspect the dragonkin mural on the western wall.","Pick up the congealed potion in the south-eastern corner.","Listen to the Archivist about all findings. {Chat: 1 The wall mural. > 2 The congealed potion. > 3 The broken focus. > 4 The crystal shard.}"],"t":"Approaching Vorkath"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Fort Forinthry and enter the floor hatch east of the Command Centre (south-east).","Talk to Zemouregal.\n  - If your Necromancy level is 120, you can skip most of the conversation {Chat: 1 Show off your mastery of necromancy. > 3 What did you do to Vorkath? > 4 I've heard enough.}\n  - Otherwise, you must follow further dialogue options {Chat: 3 Mock his skeletal form. > 1 Remind him of the other times you've defeated him. > 1 I have a soul and you don't. > 3 What did you do to Vorkath? > 4 I've heard enough.}"],"t":"Fort Forinthry"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the City of Um and talk to Death. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 3 Just tell me what the lead is.}"],"t":"City of Um"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Tree of Balance, south of the Archaeology Guild. {Chat: 1 Continue Requiem for a Dragon. > 3 Let's get straight to the point.}"],"t":"Tree of Balance"},{"n":"Backpack space to excavate two artefacts","r":"Archaeology equipment","s":["Head to Memorial to Guthix (do not enter the Hall of Memories)\n  - You can teleport directly there using memory strand or Sixth-Age circuit, otherwise teleport to Eagles' Peak lodestone and run north-west","South-east outside the memorial, uncover both fertile soil spots","Excavate both halves of the soul beacon from the uncovered standing stone debris and runic debris. There is a material storage container just north of the spots.\n  - Damaged soul beacon (base)\n  - Damaged soul beacon (core)"],"t":"Memorial to Guthix"},{"n":"Damaged soul beacon (base), damaged soul beacon (core), 30 white marble (material storage works), 30 white oak (material storage works), and 5 greater ensouled bars","r":"","s":["Return to the Tree of Balance with the two damaged parts. {Chat: 1 Continue Requiem for a Dragon.}","Head to any archaeologist's workbench to restore the damaged soul beacon.","Return to the Tree of Balance with the restored soul beacon. Chat options can vary, but the correct order is: Change, Elemental, Commune, Change. {Chat: 1 Continue Requiem for a Dragon. > 1 Deduce the glyph order. > 4 Change > 1 Elemental > 2 Commune > 4 Change}"],"t":"Restoring the beacon"},{"n":"Soul beacon and ingredients to perform a soulfarer ritual","r":"","s":["Return to the City of Um and talk to Death. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Complete a soulfarer ritual at the Um ritual site."],"t":"City of Um"},{"n":"Soul beacon and ingredients to perform a soulfarer ritual","r":"Combat equipment, super restore","s":["Travel to Fort Forinthry and take the boat back to Ungael.{Chat: 1 Yes.}","Return to the colossal cave in Ungael and head north.","Repair the 13 spots of the ruined ritual site, just east of Vorkath.","Set up the soulfarer ritual.","Perform the ritual. A cutscene will begin. {Chat: 1 Yes.}\n  - Note that this is a safe encounter, and you will respawn outside of the rowboat upon death.","Perform the ritual again, pausing to:\n  - Kill Vengeance whenever she appears. Vengeance can drastically drain your stats so super restores can be useful. Deathtouched darts can be used. If you use speed III on spare ritual space, and speed II or higher in necromancy cape, and never miss a shadow rift, you will only have to kill Vengeance once.\n  - Close any Shadow Rifts as soon as they appear. Continuing the ritual while a Shadow Rift is open will reverse the ritual's progress meter.","Watch the cutscene.","Head west and inspect Vorkath."],"t":"Ungael"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Death in City of Um. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Head south-east, south of Selene and directly north of the large cave opening in the southern part of the city and approach Vorkath."],"t":"City of Um"},{"n":"Three empty backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Return to Fort Forinthry and enter the floor hatch east of the Command Centre.","Talk to Zemouregal to complete the quest."],"t":"Confronting Zemouregal"}]},"Ritual of the Mahjarrat":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Sir Tiffy Cashien in Falador Park about the Ritual of the Mahjarrat. {Chat: # Ritual of the Mahjarrat. > Accept}","Accept the teleport. {Chat: 1 I'll get right on it. > 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Sir Tendeth in the southern pub on Mos Le'Harmless. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Sir Tendeth again after the cutscene.","Talk to the injured pirates outside and other pirates outside."],"t":"Mos Le'Harmless"},{"n":"","r":"Food and armour as well as protection against dragonfire","s":["Go north past the walls, to the blue area marked on the mini-map.","Using the western side of the trees as cover and following the burnt areas, head to the east side of the island.\n  - Hide west of tropical trees and jungle grass with the examine Looks good for hiding in.... Once north of Trouble Brewing, you must keep hiding on the west side of the trees or grass. Do not move too quickly. Count at least 1 or 2 seconds before moving to next square.\n  - Surge, the Magic ability may be used.\n  - The music will change when you are not behind cover.\n  - If hit by a fireball, heal by entering the nearby bank.\n  - Remaining in the open for too long will cause a fireball to do damage and reset the player to the town gates.\n  - If you misclick while going through the dialogue during the cutscene, you will exit it. Take one step to the west then step back behind the tree to re-trigger the cutscene.","After the cutscene, report back to Sir Tiffy."],"t":"The mighty jungle"},{"n":"Catspeak amulet (e) or Cramulet","r":"","s":["Talk to Sir Tiffy and explain the situation to him. {Chat: 2 Ritual of the Mahjarrat. > 3 I think they were dragonkin.} If you haven't completed Quiet Before the Swarm then {Chat: 1 Ritual of the Mahjarrat. > 3 I think they were dragonkin.}","Talk to Lady Table or Sir Tiffy.{Chat: 1 I think I understand the reincarnation bit. > 2 He's reincarnated as a cat. > 1 I think I understand the stonetoucher part. > 3 I think it's me.}","Use the Catspeak Amulet to find Bob back on the surface, who will be roaming anywhere in Asgarnia or Misthalin. Or can be easily found in Apprentice Clara's Shop in Burthorpe.","Once found, ask him for his collar.","Study Bob's collar — the back, too!"],"t":"The archives"},{"n":"Bob's collar, a spade (tool belt does not work), eight empty inventory spaces","r":"Food and weight reduction gear for the Agility course","s":["Go through any fairy ring, dial DIR and teleport to the Gorak Plane.","Right-click on the fairy ring and click \"Select Destination\", dial AKS and teleport to Kethsi.","Head north-west and search the rubble west of the mural to get tetrahedron 4. (If you do not receive the tetrahedron 4, check the bank for it.)","Go south-east and climb up the ramp.","Use Bob's collar on the wall design and solve the puzzle by positioning Bob's collar, pictured right.","Press the up arrow once to submit your puzzle solution.","Investigate the wall design to get tetrahedron 1, statue arm, note to you, note to Robert and Robert's necklace. Robert's necklace has no purpose in the quest and may be destroyed or banked.","Go south-west and jump across the ledge.","Use the Statue arm on the statue.","Cross the fallen spire that appears and go down the ladder.","Go east and up the wall jump.","Climb the wall to the west.","Use the swing pole to the north.","Walk across the beam.","Jump east over the gap.","Jump from the floor to the south.","Go down the southern ladder twice.","Squeeze through the pipe to the northeast of the ladder.","Use a pickaxe to mine the rocks or right-click and choose mine if using the pickaxe on your tool belt.","Climb the nearby wall and run across the walls to the west. If you fail either wall run or the handholds, go back to the pipe.","Climb across the handholds then go down the ladder.","Go east (along the northern coast) and search the rubble to find tetrahedron 3 and a strange device.","Go back up the ladder twice and jump from the floor to the south.","Slide down the roof to the south\n  - Grab the nearby spade if you didn't have one with you.","Walk across the plank to the south.","Search the rubble to find tetrahedron 2."],"t":"Traversing Isle of Sann"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Once all four tetrahedrons are collected, go down the stairs north of the area where tetrahedron 2 was located.","Use each tetrahedron on an indentation (on the walls close to the entrance, also a second spade spawns by the stairs)","Check the quest journal for the code that must be found.","Find the coordinates received and dig there with a spade to receive a Kethsian key. The strange device tells you your current location. Below is a map of Kethsi with coordinates.","Go back to the dungeon and through the door to the south.","Search the southern bookcase for Dathana's message.\n  - Optional: Search the south-east bookcase for the tune banite ore scroll."],"t":"The lost library"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Read the message, then take it to Sir Tiffy. {Chat: 2 Ritual of the Mahjarrat.} If you haven't completed Quiet Before the Swarm then {Chat: 1 Ritual of the Mahjarrat.}","Go to the White Knights' Castle and talk to either Idria, Thaerisk Cemphier, or Akrisae. {Chat: 3 So, instead, you'd risk all our lives? > 1 I can't think of another way. > 2 Yes, we'll have to be careful. > 3 I will risk my own life to negotiate.}","Make sure to get Arrav's heart before going to speak to Azzanadra or he will not talk to you about this quest.","Go to the north-eastern Varrock Dig Site winch, climb down and talk to Dr Nabanik. Ask him about the quest. {Chat: 1 Ritual of the Mahjarrat.}}}"],"t":"Planning"},{"n":"Ring of visibility, rope, all items from the previous step, and at least one free inventory space","r":"Super energy potions, food, and weaponry.","s":["From the Rellekka Hunter area (fairy ring code: DKS) take the canoe (north-west from fairy ring code: DKS, north of Larry and past the hunter area) to the Mahjarrat Ritual Site Cavern, then squeeze-past the ice block to the east (do not enter the cavern itself). This allows one to skip the Wilderness.\n  - If there is no heat globe on the pedestal, you may reclaim it from Azzanadra and place on it.","At the Ghorrock Fort, jump over the pillar to the south (it is outside of the walls of the fort, there is no red line to indicate it, the obstacle is to the south along a line of trees and pillars.) then go through the tunnel.\n  - Avoid the undead Broavs or the player will get thrown into Zemouregal's dungeon. To escape, search the bed and lift up the tiles to the east of the cell. Enter the tunnel to escape.","Several items will need to be placed around the ritual site:\n  - Northern Beacon: Run west from the ice entrance at the north of the plateau. Place the beacon on the closest tree.\n  - Southern Beacon: Run directly south, and place the second beacon in the tree south-south-west of the ritual stone. If this is done correctly, you should have a message saying the south beacon is opposite the northern beacon.\n  - Arrav's Heart: Place Arrav's heart in the rocks south of the ritual marker. The site is several paces south of the marker and just a pace or two east. If you cannot place the heart in a pile of rocks, you are at the wrong place.\n  - Western Beacon: Run up the west side of the plateau until you find a tree just north of a central line. Place the beacon here. Using the tree just south of the central line will not work.\n  - Eastern Beacon: Run straight east and place the beacon on the tree directly opposite the western tree. You should have a message saying the east beacon is directly opposite the west beacon.\n  - Go to the north-west corner of the plateau and look for an Overhanging Tree above the Cavern entrance. Use a rope on it to create a rope climb from the beach to the plateau, turning it into a Snow-covered Tree with an attached rope. This will be used for your allies to climb to the ritual. (From now on, you can also use the rope yourself to get between the canoe landing site and the plateau without having to go past the dragons around Ghorrock.)"],"t":"Setting up the site"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to Zemouregal's fort which is south-west of the ritual site.","Kill the Armoured zombie outside of the main entrance and pick up the Code key and Decoder strips.","Read the code key and open the main entrance by obtaining the code from the key and strips. (In this example we take the code \"EIHC\", see the image on the right for the solution)\n  - Drag the red strip number 1 to the first letter of the code key (example: \"E\").\n  - A single number will be revealed by the code strip (example: \"E\" row). Enter that number in the code box using the controls.\n  - Drag the red strip number 2 to the second letter of the code key (example: \"I\").\n  - A single number will be revealed by the code strip (example: \"I\" row). Enter that number in the code box using the controls.\n  - Drag the red strip number 3 to the third letter of the code key (example: \"H\").\n  - A single number will be revealed by the code strip (example: \"H\" row). Enter that number in the code box using the controls.\n  - Drag the red strip number 4 to the fourth letter of the code key (example: \"C\").\n  - A single number will be revealed by the code strip (example: \"C\" row). Enter that number in the code box using the controls.","Go through the front door and search the crate by the north-eastern weapon rack for the storeroom's Code key.","Read it and use it to open the storeroom door to the west in the same manner as the front entrance.","In the northern part of the storeroom, search the crates (2 empty spaces required).","Read the Heart magic notes.","Exit the room, head up the western stairs, and stand next to the southern door to listen to Zemouregal and Sharathteerk (you may have to move to the tile east of the door to allow the dialogue to play).","Head back downstairs, then go up the eastern stairs. Use the previously acquired Code key to enter the reliquary.","Smash the black stone in the southern half of the room."],"t":"Zemouregal's fort"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Exit the fortress and head to the south-eastern part of the ritual site.","Talk to Movario. {Chat: 1 So, you're still working for Lucien? > 1 What are you doing up here?}","With the ring of visibility equipped, run west from Movario along southern wall of the site to find a shadow pedestal (almost directly south-east from the ritual marker).","Go back inside the centre of the Ghorrock Castle courtyard (past the dragons), and climb the western stairs next to the statue of Khazard.","Go east and climb down the stairs.","Scale the Damaged Wall next to the door.","Run past the smashed pedestal, and climb down the smashed rampart on west side of the trapdoor in the courtyard.","Enter the trapdoor. The icefiends encountered here will hit hard and there will be a good number of them. Bring high level food (sharks or swordfish) just in case for comfortable exploration.","Enter the room to the west and then head south.","Take the Heat globe and exit the same way you came.","Return to the shadow pedestal, south east of the ritual marker.","Put the globe on the pedestal.\n  - If you try to put heat globe on the shadow pedestal and it says \"That could be a good idea, but you've got other things to do first.\", it means either that the beacons are not aligned properly, you have not placed Arrav's heart in the rocks to the south of the Ritual marker, you haven't placed the rope to the north-west of the tunnel or you have not talked to Movario after having done so. If you are completely sure you have done all of these things, talk to Movario to the east of the shadow pedestal, and he will place the heat globe in the pedestal. A few players have removed a beacon from a tree and put in back in the tree—this also has worked. Some report that reading the notes/Dathana's message also fixes this."],"t":"Searching for the Stone of Jas"},{"n":"","r":"Food and Prayer Potions (Certain sections of this battle will call for no Prayer, and others will work with prayer just fine. Read ahead to understand the fight and allocate resources as necessary.)","s":["Enter the newly opened entrance, south of the shadowy pedestal.","Follow the open passageway and touch the Stone of Jas."],"t":"The ritual"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After the cutscenes, defeat Khazard.","It helps to pray against magic and when Bouncer is summoned, lure him to Wahisietel so that he dies."],"t":"Khazard"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Defeat the Enhanced ice titans.\n  - Lucien will be casting spells at the player whilst fighting the ice titans. If a smoking black skull is flying towards you, move at least two squares away from your current position. Also, praying melee completely negates damage from the titans' normal attacks. If ice starts encasing the player, they should click rapidly on the ground around them to escape.\n  - You will only be able to damage the two enhanced ice titans that run at you; your teammates must kill the rest.\n  - Avoid attacking Lucien, as doing so causes Lucien to hit you with a high damage attack.}}"],"t":"Ice titans"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Defeat the Ice Demons\n  - Praying against magic helps limit the damage the demons can cause. They will also summon icicles which will fall around the player. When this happens, run out of the icicles to avoid being trapped due to Lucien still casting the skull spell at the player.\n  - You will only be able to damage the two ice demons that run at you; your teammates must kill the rest.\n  - You are able to use Split Soul on the two that your teammates are meant to kill to speed up the process.}}"],"t":"Ice demons"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Attack the armoured zombies until Arrav is summoned.","Attack Arrav until he follows you. You may have to attack the zombies before Arrav will follow you.","Lure him over to where his heart is placed and wait for Arrav to fight Zemouregal before proceeding.\n  - If you have a combat follower out, it is best to dismiss it when Arrav starts following you. Otherwise, it is possible that the combat familiar and Arrav will fight. If this occurs when Arrav gets his heart back, the familiar's attack may distract Arrav from attacking Zemouregal. Instead, Arrav will stand near the rockpile where his heart was hidden and will not move. This is a glitch, and the only way to overcome it is to leave the battle, return, and fight the fourth battle again from its start."],"t":"Arrav"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to where the southern beacon was.","Turn on a prayer against ranged or magic attacks and pick up the beacon pieces.","Click on a piece to assemble all of them and then place the beacon back into the tree."],"t":"The broken beacon"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Watch the cutscenes and pick a number for the new hiding spot for the Stone of Jas.","Go to the stalls area of the town (north-west of where the bank would be in Draynor Village) in the destroyed version of Draynor Village.","Watch the last cutscene.","Talk to Sir Tiffy. {Chat: 1 Ritual of the Mahjarrat.} If Quiet Before the Swarm isn't completed {Chat: 2 Ritual of the Mahjarrat.}.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"River of Blood":{"sections":[{"n":"3 steel med helms, 3 steel platebodies, 3 steel platelegs, 2 blisterwood sickles, blisterwood polearm, food, any combat gear of your choice with a blisterwood weapon for killing the vyrewatches.","r":"","s":["Talk to King Roald in Varrock Palace. {Chat: 1 Talk about River of Blood. > Accept}","Talk to Drezel in the Paterdomus mausoleum west of Canifis (fairy ring CKS, invitation box or Skeletal horror Teleport for quick access). {Chat: 2 Talk about something else. > ~}\n  - Reclaim the wolfbane dagger if you had previously destroyed it.","Talk to Aeonisig south of the temple. You can use the invitation box to get there. Otherwise, exit the building on the west side and head towards the beacon (or exit east side and use agility shortcut). He is at the bottom of the stairs.","Defeat the 3 Vyrewatches using blisterwood weapons.","Talk to Aeonisig. {Chat: Any > 4 Farewell.}","Talk to Captain Rovin (one of the three guards slightly north east) to supply him with armour.","Kill all Zamorak monks in the temple - you can use any combat style/gear here.","Kill the Zamorakian leader and bodyguard on the top floor - you can use any combat style/gear here.","Return and talk to Aeonisig. Go through all the chat options. {Chat: Any}"],"t":"Preparations for Aeonisig"},{"n":"blisterwood logs, super restore (3), Guthix balance, Ectophial, 4 empty inventory spaces","r":"","s":["Talk to Drezel. {Chat: 2 Talk About something else}","Climb-down the nearby trapdoor.\n  - If the trapdoor isn't open, use the temple library key on the keyhole which can be obtained from Drezel.","Pull 7 books off the bookcases in the correct order until you find the Blood of the Covenant:\n  - Lumbridge\n  - Varrock\n  - Edgeville\n  - Falador\n  - Rimmington\n  - Taverley\n  - Draynor\n  - \"Blood of the Covenant\"","Read the book.","Climb-up the ladder.","Talk to Ivan Strom.","Enter the trapdoor behind Canifis pub, search the southern wall in the room and take the first cave entrance on the east side of the tunnel.\n  - If players are taken to Mort'ton they need to go to the Temple Trekking noticeboard next to the temple west of Canifis, click on the medium NPC and on the right hand side, they'll see the NPC with level 99, which is rewarded with the ability to toggle a shortcut from the trapdoor. After toggling it the door will function as normal or the boat can be taken back to the swamp and run to the cellar doors from here to access the tomb without toggling the function.","Use a Guthix balance on the tomb and open it. {Chat: 1}","Open the scroll case and read the Scroll of Balance.","Burn a Blisterwood log and take the ashes. They spawn immediately upon lighting the fire.","Grind the silvthril bar at the ectofuntus grinder. {Chat: 1}","Use the silvthril dust on the Altar of Nature in the Nature Grotto.","Use any of the three ingredients on a super restore (3) to make a super Guthix balance potion. Keep the Ivandis's serum in your inventory for later use."],"t":"Finding the scroll"},{"n":"Super Guthix balance, blisterwood weapon, food, and combat supplies for battle with a Level 117 Wyrd","r":"","s":["Talk to Drezel. {Chat: 2 Talk about something else.}","Pour the Super Guthix balance into the well in the main room to the west.","Talk to Aeonisig south of the church. {Chat: 3 About equipping the Varrock guard... > 2 About claiming the Paterdomus temple... > Any > 1 About strengthening the Salve barrier... > 3 I should investigate this.}","Talk to Vanescula on the bridge. {Chat: Any > Any}\n  - Use the the broken Saradomin statue shortcut to the east if you have 65 Agility or teleport to the fairy ring CKS.","Kill the feral vampyres.","Kill the Wyrd while stepping away from its special attacks.\n  - The Sonic Wave attack deals 7,500 damage when praying melee. Otherwise, it will deal 15,000 damage. This can be avoided by stepping at least two squares back. It is also important to note that if you step off the bridge at any time you will have to redo the fight.","Talk to Ivan Strom on the bridge over the salve river.}}"],"t":"Clash of armies"},{"n":"Sunspear, wolfbane dagger, blisterwood logs, Ivandis's serum, food/armour and 1 free backpack space. optionally vampyre disguise","r":"","s":["Travel to Burgh de Rott via Drakan's medallion. {Chat: 2}","Travel on the boat south of Burgh de Rott to the Icyene graveyard. {Chat: 2 Icyene graveyard.}","Talk to Efaritay.","Inspect the Queen Efaritay statue within the northern crypt, and take the pendant.","Talk to Efaritay.","Craft a Blisterwood shaft from blisterwood logs.","Use the shaft on the sunspear with the wolfbane dagger and blisterwood shaft in your inventory.","Talk to Efaritay.","Teleport to the Meiyerditch Laboratories via Drakan's medallion. {Chat: 5}","Talk to Sarius.","Run through the tunnel to the room with the mutated bloodveld.","Take the book from the research table on the north side and read it.","Talk to Sarius.","Climb the stairs and run north-west into the mine.","With your vampyre disguise on, talk to a guard about the refinery. (if you don't have your disguise on you must manually fill the cart up with 15 ores yourself)","Talk to one of the Juvinate guards. {Chat: 1 Where's the daeyalt refinery?}","Push the cart.","Kill the juvinates.","Open the 5 cell doors."],"t":"Combatting haemalchemy"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Run north and talk to Emilia. {Chat: 5 Let the anger flow through you.}","Talk to Sorin. {Chat: 4 Isn't this technology awesome?}","Talk to Ileana. {Chat: 3 I don't approve of this, and neither should you.}","Talk to Razvan. {Chat: 2 You should be ashamed. Have you no remorse?}","Talk to Florin. {Chat: 1 Cheer up. Don't give up hope.}","Tithe the Shadum blood lock located on the south western part of the wall. {Chat: 6 I accept my fate and put my hand in the machine.}"],"t":"Refinery puzzle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Extract the refined daeyalt from the refined daeyalt mine.","Inspect the rejuvenation tank.","Climb the stairs and talk to Safalaan.","Kill the Skeleton Hellhounds.","Climb the stairs.","On the northern end of the room, go into the eastern door into a long, narrow hallway.","Go into the Library through a door on the southern wall of the hallway.","Take the bottle of holy water from the table (red dot on the map).","Continue east through the narrow hallway.","Throw the bottle of holy water on Harold and climb the stairs.","Cut a log from the blisterwood tree.","Light the firepit in front of the Stone of Jas. It is a small black ring immediately in front of the stone, easy to miss.","Roll the barrel of gunpowder.","Unlock the blood seal in the northern room.","Climb the stairs."],"t":"Curing vampyrism"},{"n":"Ivandis's serum, Refined daeyalt","r":"Combat equipment and food","s":["Kill Safalaan with the Sunspear.","Talk to Efaritay.","Use the daeyalt and Ivandis' serum on Safalaan's blood.","Talk to Efaritay.","Pour the extreme Guthix balance potion into the Paterdomus well.","Talk to Vanescula on the bridge.","Watch the cutscene and then talk to Vanescula once more.","Talk to King Roald. {Chat: 1 Talk about River of Blood.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Wyrd's woe"}]},"Rocking Out":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to Mos Le'Harmless (fairy ring DIP if you have repaired the bridge with 8 planks and 16 nails and partial completion of A Fairy Tale III).","Talk to Bill Teach in The Other Inn. {Chat: 1 Speak about Rocking Out. > Accept}\n  - If you have lost your Little Book o' Piracy, talk to him to get a new one.","Buy three pieces of pirate clothing from Dodgy Mike's Second-hand Clothing.}}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"3 pieces of pirate clothing","r":"","s":["Go to house in south-east Rimmington with the Customs Sergeant while wearing three pieces of pirate clothing.","Read the noticeboard next to the entrance door for information on the answers to the trick questions. The answers to the trick questions are different for everyone.","Talk to the Customs Sergeant {Chat: ? Any option. > ? Varies - match noticeboard.}\n  - Taking note of the ship name/s he references, select the answers that match the story on noticeboard.","Deposit all your items in the Locker on the north side of the room. You need to store all the items you are wearing as well as dismiss any familiars.","Talk to the Customs Sergeant again."],"t":"Getting arrested"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Once in the prison, shout-through the barred window to your east.","Pick up the tin cup in the cell and use it on the cell door 3 times until Heavy-Handed Harry throws stew on you, turning your prison uniform top into a fishy prison uniform top.","Right-click tap the pipes on the eastern wall to receive a pipe.","Shout-through your cell door until you receive a quill, paper, and ink bottle.","Leave your cell through the hole to the north and search the rubble to receive an accordion (broken).","Use the ink bottle on the paper to receive inky paper and ink bottle (empty).","Use the ink bottle (empty) on the sharp rock outside on the east-most wall near the pier to get a smashed bottle.","In order, use the smashed bottle, pipe, and inky paper on the accordion to get a vacuum pump.","Use your fishy prison uniform top on the perch rock just east of the hole in the wall.","Right-click use the vacuum pump on the perch rock once the seagull appears.","Right-click use the vacuum pump and gull on the barred window.","Dive off the pier on the east side of the island. {Chat: 1 Dive}"],"t":"In prison"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to Braindeath Island by speaking to Pirate Pete north of Port Phasmatys. {Chat: 1 Braindeath Island, please!}","Go west and speak to Captain Braindeath. He will give you the fake beard, fake moustache and nose, fake monocle, moustache and nose, curly wig, and straight wig disguises. {Chat: 1 Talk about Rocking Out}","Travel to the bar in north Port Sarim called The Rusty Anchor.","Talk to the Bartender. {Chat: 2 Ask about 'rum'.}","Talk to the Bartender again. {Chat: 3 I'll have a drink... and you have one too!}\n  - Repeat this about five times until he says he's tired.","Go outside, put on a disguise, and then ask about the rum again. Repeat this step with each disguise. {Chat: 2 Ask about 'rum'.}","Talk to the bartender again, this time with no disguise, and he will give you an order slip. {Chat: 2 Ask about 'rum'.}"],"t":"Captain Braindeath"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Redbeard Frank outside of The Rusty Anchor in Port Sarim. {Chat: 3 Speak about Rocking Out.}","Travel to Mos Le'Harmless via the charter boat, fairy ring DIP if you have repaired the bridge, or Bill Teach, and talk to Brother Tranquillity to receive a letter. {Chat: 3 Talk about the letter for Frank.}","Return to Redbeard Frank on the Port Sarim dock and deliver the letter. {Chat: 3 Speak about Rocking Out.}","Put on your pirate clothing and head back to Braindeath Island.","Talk to Captain Braindeath for his mark. {Chat: 1 Talk about Rocking Out.}","Go down the southern stairs, and talk to Captain Donnie to get plans.","Head north-west to 50% Luke by the bridge and use charcoal on him.\n  - There is charcoal in a crate on the other side of the gate near 50% Luke.","Return to Redbeard Frank on the Port Sarim docks and exchange the Charcoal rubbing for Frank's mark. {Chat: 3 Speak about Rocking Out.}","Optional: Talk to the bartender and ask about 'rum' once more to complete the Rusty Reward achievement required for the master quest cape. {Chat: 2 Ask about 'rum'.}"],"t":"Redbeard Frank"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to Mos Le'Harmless.","Talk to Bill Teach in The Other Inn to obtain an introduction letter. {Chat: 1 Speak about Rocking Out.}","Climb-up the bamboo ladder in Harpoon Joe's House of 'Rum' just north and speak with 50 Ships Mufassah. {Chat: 1 Yes! Where do I sign up?}","Talk to Brass Hand Harry for 5 broken hands.","Take-apart the five broken hands.","With the two bronze wires in your inventory, use any piece of the hand on another to trigger a puzzle.","Complete the puzzle to obtain a brass hand (the interface will close automatically when the puzzle has been completed).\n  - Try flipping the brace (bottom) piece if you're having trouble completing the puzzle.\n  - The location of the hand is as important as the components; make sure you're constructing the hand atop the silhouette.","Talk to Brass Hand Harry (nearby) to receive an ink pad. Use the ink pad on the brass hand to get a inky hand. Then use the inky hand on the paper.","Talk to Brass Hand Harry again to show him the completed Brass Hand Harry's mark.\n  - If you haven't done so yet, feel free to destroy the ink pad and hand.","Equip your ghostspeak amulet, diving apparatus, and fishbowl helmet.","Travel to Dragontooth Island by talking to the Ghost captain at the small boat in Port Phasmatys (he is at the south-eastern end of the docks). {Chat: 1 Please take me to Dragontooth Island!}","Travel to the north-east part of Dragontooth Island and dive via the chain.\n  - You will need both hands free to dive.","Swim around until you find a Karamthulhu and catch it. (It is the only fish that appears on the mini map.)","Head over to the ship and climb-up the stairs.","Open and search the chest to get a crowbar.\n  - An aggressive giant lobster may attack you. You can open and search the chest while being attacked.","Return down the stairs and climb down the ladder.","Go west on the bottom floor of the ship and dig the mess a several times to uncover the idol of many heads buried in the pile of planks and sand. Pick it up.\n  - You can wield weapons while down there digging, so you can kill any aggressive giant crabs or lobsters that may be hindering you from digging successfully.","Bring the idol back to Bill Teach to receive Bill Teach's mark. {Chat: 1 Speak about Rocking Out.}"],"t":"Bill Teach and Captain Brass Hand Harry"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to Brimhaven and go to the Brimhaven Agility Arena entrance, located south-east of the docks.","Speak to Cap'n Izzy No-Beard. {Chat: 1 Talk about Rocking Out.}","Return to the Rimmington Customs Office. Deposit all of your items in the locker and get arrested by talking to the Customs Sergeant.","Search the bed for a crude lockpick and use it on your cell door.","Kill one of the customs officers, loot the uniform and equip it to disguise yourself.\n  - You can withdraw your pickaxe from your tool belt to use as a weapon.\n  - Make sure you do not have lootshare enabled, as this can prevent the uniform from being dropped. If you do not get the loot, try relogging.","Climb the stairs twice to the top floor.","Open the door to the room with the cabinets.","Search the northern-most cabinet on the second column from the west for \"Wanda the Fish\". {Chat: 1 Yes. Wanda the Fish}","Talk to the Locker Officer and receive the brooch.","Return to Cap'n Izzy No-Beard in Brimhaven to receive Izzy's mark. {Chat: 1 Talk about Rocking Out.}"],"t":"Cap'n Izzy No-Beard"},{"n":"Izzy's mark, Bill Teach's mark, Frank's mark, Braindeath's mark, and Brass Hand Harry's mark","r":"","s":["Use one of the marks on the file.","Talk to the Customs Sergeant to give him the filled file.","Talk to him again to get sent back to prison.","Search the bed for the crude lockpick and break out of your cell. Kill the Customs Officer(s) for another uniform, equip it, then head to the top floor.\n  - You may get a message saying that the lock is rusty, and the lockpick does not work. Continue trying until it works.","Go to the top floor and talk to the Locker Officer to get back the filled file.","Return to your cell and right-click open the door.\n  - If you do not have the option to open the cell door, hop to a different world.","Shout-through the barred window to Young Ralph. A cutscene will follow.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Back to prison and quest completion"}]},"Roving Elves":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Track down and talk to Islwyn. {Chat: Accept > 1 Tell the truth? > 1 Maybe I could help.}\n  - Islwyn and Eluned move locations regularly: either south-west of Lletya or north-east of the Tyras Camp. Simply hop worlds until you find them.","Talk to Eluned.","Use Glarial's pebble on Glarial's tombstone north-west of the Fishing Guild.\n  - If you're holding any combat equipment or logs, you'll receive the message: It fits perfectly, but nothing happens.\n  - If needed, reclaim Glarial's pebble from Golrie in Gnome Village Dungeon. {Chat: 1 Yes please!}","Kill a moss giant and pick up the consecration seed it drops.\n  - You can remove an item from your tool belt to use as a weapon. Legacy combat mode increases auto attack damage. A ring of recoil may be helpful for lower levelled players.","If needed, reclaim Glarial's amulet from the chest to the west.","Take the seed to Eluned to have her enchant it.","Travel to the Waterfall dungeon.\n  - Via hoardstalker ring or Dungeoneering cape (Baxtorian Falls resource dungeon option, called Waterfall fire giant dungeon in the cape)\n  - Via games necklace, Barbarian Outpost then run south to Baxtorian Falls, then:\n    - Board the log raft north of Baxtorian falls\n    - Use a rope on the rock south across the water\n    - Use a rope on the dead tree\n    - Enter the door","If needed, reclaim a key from the discoloured crates in the eastern room with skeletons.","Go inside the north-west room with the statues.","Plant the enchanted consecration seed anywhere inside.","Return to Islwyn to choose your reward. {Chat: Any}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Islwyn and Eluned"}]},"Royal Trouble":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Advisor Ghrim in Miscellania. {Chat: 2 Has anything been happening in the kingdom recently? > Accept}\n  - Fast access via Ring of Wealth (or higher tier luck enhancer rings, which offer unlimited teleports), fairy ring cip, or the sailor near the larger boat north of the Rellekka market.","Speak to either Prince Brand or Princess Astrid. Wait for the cutscene.","Talk to King Vargas. {Chat: 1 Right away, Your Majesty}","Talk to Gardener Gunnhild at the flax patch. {Chat: 1 Royal Trouble.}","Run east over to Etceteria and talk to Queen Sigrid. {Chat: 1 Of course, it's my duty.}","Talk to Matilda in the Etceteria castle courtyard.","Talk to Queen Sigrid again. {Chat: 2 I suppose so...}","Talk to King Vargas.","Talk to Advisor Ghrim. {Chat: 1 King Vargas asked me to talk to you.}","Talk to the Sailor on the docks in Miscellania (caution to not travel to Rellekka). {Chat: 2 I'm looking for a sailor...}","Talk to King Vargas again with at least 1 inventory space free."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Gear up for the final fight now. Having 8 free inventory spaces is recommended.","Go downstairs and enter the dungeon ladder within the southern portion of the Miscellania courtyard.","Go into the bar to the east, and speak with Donal. {Chat: 1 Of course. Dealing with monsters is what I do best!}","Head north to use the mining prop on the crevice, and go through."],"t":"Miscellania dungeons"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pick up the engine, 3 pulley beams, 3 beams, and 2 rope from the crates.\n  - There is a bug where sometimes you won't be able to pick up the engine. Leave the dungeon and come back, or try to use area loot.","Add 5 coal to the engine (coal can be obtained by mining the rocks in the cavern).","Use a pulley beam on the broken scaffolding.","Use a beam on a pulley beam, and you'll get a long pulley beam.","Attach another beam to get a longer pulley beam, use that on the scaffolding.","Use your last pulley beam on the scaffolding.","Use your rope on the scaffolding.","Use the third beam on the platform (north side).","Use the engine with coal in it on the engine platform (middle).","Once complete you can now use the lift.}}"],"t":"Fixing the lift"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pick up the plank off the ground, and enter the tunnel.","Continue east.","Use the rope in your inventory on the northern end of the rock and swing across the river.","Search the fire remains to obtain a burnt diary.","Use the plank to cross the small rocks.","Search the other fire remains (2 fires before vents) to add pages to the diary.\n  - The steam vents in this area will hurt you slightly. Surge across to avoid any damage.","Make your way to the end of the tunnel, collecting the 2 remaining diary pages.","Read the burnt diary.","Squeeze through the crevice at the end."],"t":"Exploring the tunnel"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After the cutscene, finish the dialogue with the teenagers.","Continue down the tunnel, squeeze through the crevice.","Kill the Giant Sea Snake, and pick up the heavy box.","Go back through the crevice and a guard will drop a rope down to help you up.","Talk to Queen Sigrid with at least 1 free inventory space.\n  - If you forgot to pick up the heavy box, it can be obtained by speaking with the guard by the escape hole.","Talk to King Vargas. You can drop the empty box and diary.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Final fight"}]},"Rum Deal":{"sections":[{"n":"At least four backpack spaces.","r":"","s":["Recharge your prayer if you have fewer than 470 points.","Talk to Pirate Pete, north of Port Phasmatys. {Chat: Accept > 1 Of course, I fear no demon! > 1 Nonsense! Keep the money!}\n  - If you have the ectophial it will place you close to Pirate Pete."],"t":"Braindeath Island"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Note: If at any point you leave the area you can return via Pirate Pete. {Chat: 1 Okay!}","Complete the dialogue with Captain Braindeath. He gives you a blindweed seed.","Run south and Climb-down a Wooden Stair.","Run south to the farming patches.","Rake the south-easternmost Blindweed Patch (the only one which isn't labelled as 'trashed').","Use the seed on the patch.","Pick the blindweed once grown (can take up to 5 minutes).","Return to and Talk to Captain Braindeath.","In the south-east corner of the building, Climb-up the Ladder.","In the north-west corner, Deposit at the Hopper (1 tile east of the Pressure Barrel)."],"t":"Blindweed"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Captain Braindeath, he'll give you an empty bucket if you don't already have one.","Go to the bridges to the west and Open the Gate.\n  - Optional: Wear your ring of charos to distract 50% Luke.\n  - If no ring just click Open and your character will distract him.","Continue north and up the mountain to the Stagnant Lake.","Fill at the Stagnant Lake.","Deposit at the Hopper from earlier (keep the empty bucket for later)."],"t":"Stagnant water"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Captain Braindeath. He will give you a Fishbowl and net\n  - If you accidentally Untangle the fishbowl, just Use the bowl on the net to re-tangle them.","Fish a total of 5 sluglings and/or karamthulhu near the farming patches (a mix of 5 will work).","Use all 5 on the Pressure Barrel next to the Hopper.","Pull the lever."],"t":"Sluglings"},{"n":"Bucket","r":"","s":["Return to Captain Braindeath. He will give you a wrench.","Enter the western room and Talk to Davey to get the holy wrench.","Right-click Use the wrench on the brewing control to the east (the object shaking crazily).","Kill the evil spirit.","Return to Captain Braindeath.","Climb-down the nearby ladder to the south-west.","With slayer gloves equipped, kill a fever spider and take its body.\n  - Slayer gloves are not required with high life points or when safespotting the spider behind a crate (with Magic/Ranged/Necromancy)","Deposit at the hopper.","Return to Captain Braindeath.","With an empty bucket, turn the Output Tap (south of the machinery) to receive unsanitary swill."],"t":"Trouble Brewing"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Captain Donnie north of the farming patches.","Return to Captain Braindeath.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Rune Mechanics":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Apprentice Clerval in the basement of the Mage Training Arena. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"5 steam runes, 5 mind runes, 5 body runes, 5 water rune (if at fire altar) or 5 fire rune (if at water altar), 5 pure essence","r":"","s":["Talk to Wizard Dougal who is also in the basement. {Chat: 1 Complement him and massage his ego.}\n  - You need four free spaces in your inventory for Dougal to give you items. If he doesn't give you the items, he will not accept the steam runes.","Wear the binding necklace that Dougal gave you.","Craft at least one steam rune. The remaining runes (4 steam runes, 5 mind runes, 5 body runes) can be obtained or bought ahead of time.\n  - Steam runes can be crafted by using fire runes on the water altar (consuming a fire talisman).\n  - Alternatively, use water runes on the fire altar (consuming a water talisman).","Talk to Wizard Dougal.","Give the runes to Clerval."],"t":"Wizard Dougal"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Wizard Edvin who is also in the basement. (You will need to dismiss any pets currently active) {Chat: 1 I guess I'll give it a try.}","Solve the portal maze.\n  - From the start, go through the west portal, then go to the northern portal 3 times.","Exit the maze.","Take Edvin's tool to Clerval."],"t":"Wizard Edvin"},{"n":"2 emeralds, 20 pure essence","r":"","s":["Obtain five pizazz points from Mage Training Arena minigame, if you don't already have five. Enchantment Pizazz points are easy to obtain by casting any level jewellery enchantment spell (Lvl-1 Enchant, Lvl-2 Enchant, Lvl-3 Enchant, Lvl-4 Enchant, Lvl-5 Enchant, Lvl-6 Enchant) on a dragonstone lying on the arena floor. (Requires at least level 7 Magic.)","Talk to Wizard Shug on the top floor of the arena. {Chat: 2 Get back on topic! > 2 Get back on topic!}","Enchant the emeralds using the workbench by Clerval."],"t":"Wizard Shug"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Clerval, holding 20 pure essence. {Chat: 2 Comfort and reassure him.}","Fix the animation table nearby.","When finished, click the green check button. {Chat: 1 You are useless, but, yes, I'll do it.}","Use the carving tool on the lump of rune essence.","Talk to Clerval.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Rune Memories":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the ruins beneath the Wizards' Tower.","Pass through the two doors in the ruins and talk to Ariane. {Chat: 2 What do you need help with? > 2 I'd be happy to help. > Accept > 3 How can I get you out? > 3 Okay, what do you want me to do?}","Use the prepared fire rune on a red vortex and the prepared air rune on a grey vortex.","Talk to Ariane. {Chat: 4 OK, I'll do that now.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head through the eastern library door.","Put the glowing fire rune on the red chair and the glowing air rune on the grey chair.","Head west back through the door.","Talk to Ariane. {Chat: 1 I saw them talking about the 'teleportation problem'. > 2 So, what now?}"],"t":"Memories"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use each prepared rune on a vortex corresponding to the colour of the background of the rune.","Talk to Ariane. {Chat: 3 OK, I'll do that now.}","Head west and climb up the staircase to go back to the room with the rune guardian.","Use the following glowing runes on the corresponding statues:\n  - Glowing cosmic rune on the Grey Order statue (north-west)\n  - Glowing nature rune on the Green Order statue (north-east)\n  - Glowing law rune on the Blue Order statue (south-east)\n  - Glowing chaos rune on the Red Order statue (south-west)","Go back down to the main chamber and talk to Ariane. {Chat: 1 The Green master stole the Red apprentice's idea! > 3 Okay, so what do we do now? > 3 OK.}"],"t":"The meeting of the head wizards"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head through the northern studies door then into the north-eastern room.","Use the following glowing runes on the corresponding chairs:\n  - Glowing chaos rune on the large chair\n  - Glowing fire rune on the middle chair","Return to the main chamber and talk to Ariane. {Chat: 1 The Red master summoned a demon! > 3 So what do we do now? > 3 OK.}"],"t":"Memories of the Abyss"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head through the eastern library door.","In the centre, use the glowing runes on the corresponding scenery:\n  - Glowing air rune on the grey chair\n  - Glowing fire rune on the red chair\n  - Glowing earth rune on the green chair\n  - Glowing water rune on the blue chair\n  - Glowing chaos rune on the table","Return to the main chamber and talk to Ariane. {Chat: 1 The wizards were about to start the ritual. > 3 OK, what now? > 2 OK.}","Head through the eastern library door.","Search the shelves for:\n  - Document fragment (1/5)\n  - Document fragment (3/5)","Return to the main chamber.","Head through the northern studies door.","Search the crates and chests in each room for:\n  - Document fragment (2/5)\n  - Document fragment (4/5)\n  - Document fragment (5/5)\n  - Diary","Return to the main chamber and talk to Ariane. {Chat: 2 I found some document fragments. > 2 I found a diary in the ruins. > 3 Enough about the diary. > 2 OK.}"],"t":"The teleportation debate"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Place your glowing runes in their corresponding positions on the floor surrounding the blue beam:\n  - North: Law\n  - North-east: Fire\n  - East: Nature\n  - South-east: Air\n  - South: Chaos\n  - South-west: Water\n  - West: Cosmic\n  - North-west: Earth","A cutscene ensues when the placement is correct.","Head back up to the surface and talk to Wizard Ellaron at the Wizards' Tower entrance. {Chat: 2 Ariane is hurt in the ruins of the old Tower! > 3 I didn't say she was in a coma. > 4 Enough talk! Prepare to fight, Red Wizard!}"],"t":"The beam"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ariane.","Use the following prepared runes on Ariane corresponding to the beam Must be completed in order from top to bottom:\n  - Cosmic rune - Thick (spinning) grey beam\n  - Water rune - Simple blue beam","Ascend the beam\n  - Earth rune - Simple green beam\n  - Fire rune - Simple red beam","Ascend the beam\n  - Law rune - Thick (spinning) blue beam\n  - Nature rune - Thick (spinning) green beam","Ascend the beam\n  - Chaos rune - Thick (spinning) red beam\n  - Air rune - Simple grey beam","Talk to Ariane. {Chat: 1 Are you OK? > 2 So... what now? > 3 So, is there a reward? > 3 We did find out what happened to the old tower.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"The burning tower"}]},"Rune Mysteries":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ariane in the entrance to Wizards' Tower. {Chat: 1 What's happening here? > 2 What can I do to help? > Accept}","Head into the tower, pick up the Tower mindspike and attack the vortex with any spell. You must unequip any ranged, melee, or necromancy armour or you may not be able to lure the vortex.","Lure the vortex into the energy beam."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ariane on the bridge outside. {Chat: 3 What do you want me to do? > 2 I'll get on it.}","Ascend the beam twice, and talk to Wizard Traiborn in the northwestern room. {Chat: 1 Have you seen anything unusual lately? > 2 In the power beam? > 2 Where do these things come from?}","Talk to Archmage Sedridor in the southern room. {Chat: 3 Ariane says the tower is in danger. > 3 What are you going to do? > 4 Goodbye.}\n  - If Love Story has been completed. {Chat: 4 Ariane says the tower is in danger. > 3 What are you going to do? > 4 Goodbye.}","Talk to Wizard Ellaron in the northeastern room. {Chat: 2 Ariane says the tower is in danger. > 2 Thanks.}","Descend the beam twice or right-click and select bottom floor back to the floor 1.","Talk to Ariane. {Chat: 2 I've spoken to some of the wizards... > 3 Wizard Traiborn said something came through the library floor. > 2 Then let's get down there and investigate! > 2 I'll get right on it.}"],"t":"The old tower"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Ascend the beam twice.","Talk to Wizard Ellaron. {Chat: 2 How can I get into the old tower? > 3 You do know, though? > 3 You mean the rumour about Water Surge? > 3 What do you mean, the key lies in understanding Water Surge? > 2 It's such a pity you couldn't help me, Maybe I'll visit the library.}","Go back to the floor 1 and search the easternmost bookcase for The Harmony of the Runes and The Runes of the Spells of Water.","Read the books.","Play the organ at the southern end of the floor 1.","Press the organ keys in the following order: 10x \"B\", 7x \"A#\", 1x \"G#\", and 1x \"G\". (small black keys are # notes)","Take the organ key."],"t":"The hidden key"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the north side of the island and talk to Ariane, {Chat: 2 I've got the key to the ruins. > Any} then head east and enter the door on the seashore.","Talk to Ariane {Chat: 2 We should keep our minds on the job. > 1 Yes, it's inspiring. > 2 Okay, what should we do now?}","Talk to the rune guardian and answer the questions any way. {Chat: 3 I'm ready to be tested. > Any > Any > Any > Any > Any}\n  - The options you pick only dictate the title you're given. See the full guide to learn more.","Enter the door behind the rune guardian.","Walk down the stairs to the gap in front of Ariane.","Climb behind the statue (on the wall above the gap). {Chat: 1 I'm making us a bridge. > 1 Do you have a better idea?}","Cross the statue (gap) and climb down the staircase.","Talk to Ariane. {Chat: 1 I wish I could have seen it.}","Use magic to lure a vortex into Ariane's circle, and keep it there until the circle disappears. You can lure them by attacking them.","Talk to Ariane again. {Chat: 2 Never mind the history, what does that mean for us? > 2 Okay, so what do we do? > 3 Okay, I'll do that now.}}}"],"t":"Descent"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Exit the ruins.","Head back to the organ on the main floor of the tower and play any of the notes from the lowest set of keys to trigger several cutscenes.","Talk to Ariane (east side of the island at the entrance to the lower tower). {Chat: 3 Is there a reward?}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Rune Mythos":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Malignius Mortifer next to the ritual site.{Chat: 1 Yes. > Accept > 4 I'm good. What's next?}","Perform a lesser essence ritual and collect impure essence from the ritual chest. Malignius Mortifer will give you eight basic ghostly ink, four regular ghostly ink, and 200 pure essence for the lesser essence ritual.\n  - You need two Elemental I glyphs, two Change I glyphs, and four light sources.","Withdraw the output of the ritual from the ritual chest on the ritual site.","Head to north-eastern area of the city and enter through the dark portal with some unnoted impure essence.","Attempt to make some spirit runes and interact with Rasial, the First Necromancer. Make sure to actually talk to him after his initial message, otherwise the quest will not progress.","Craft your runes.","Head back to Malignius to complete the quest.{Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Walkthrough"}]},"Salt in the Wound":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Kennith along the east coast of Daemonheim near the Fremennik ship (Shadow reef). {Chat: 1 What are you doing here? > Accept}","Go west, and talk to him again.","Talk to Ezekial {Chat: Any} then Eva (Temple Knight) and tell her you're ready to start. {Chat: Any > 4 I'm ready. Let's go!}","Enter the opening formed in the mountain nearby."],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"1 free inventory space","r":"food and protection prayers for low levels","s":["Kill the three enemies in this room","Find the blue key on the floor","Return to the first room and unlock and enter the puzzle room door"],"t":"Daemonheim Dungeon"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Choose a hero (preferably the one with the most health).","One way to solve the puzzle is:\n  - Jump south across the first gap\n  - Jump west twice\n  - Jump south\n  - Jump north, back to the same spot\n  - Jump east three times\n  - Jump south twice and the puzzle is completed.","Inspect the Seeker of Truth and return across the gap. (Quickest method is to get caught and teleported back).","Kennith will then teleport you to the Fishing Platform. {Chat: 1 Teleport to Fishing Platform.}"],"t":"The Puzzle Room"},{"n":"3 free inventory spaces","r":"","s":["Once on the platform talk to Kennith.","Talk with Bailey. {Chat: 3 *Punch him* > 2 So, you don't feel pain? > 2 No pain? Prove it.}","Head east to the fishing spots.","Lure the fishing spot and go back to Kennith, the slug will follow you.","Talk to Kennith and he will give you a Seeker gland.","Combine the ingredients to make the anti-mind control serum.","Talk to Kennith, a little to the west. {Chat: 1 What should we do now?}","Talk to the Slug thralls. {Chat: 2 Why can't we come in? > 2 I'm not a stranger. > 3 I seek enlightenment in the joining. > 3 I wish to hear...}"],"t":"Fishing Platform"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Leave one character by the Witchaven villager just north of the entrance and move the other 2 to the metal gate to the north-east and kill the Risen knight.","Use the character you left behind to knock out the Witchaven villager and proceed south with your player.","Go into the room with the lever and pull it.","The metal door to the north will now be open. Send a character through.","Pull your player's lever again.","Use the character you left near the entrance to knock out the other villager again, allowing your player to run north to the other characters you left by the gate.","Bring the character you left at the entrance to join your player. Use the character in the room to pull the lever to let you all in. Pull the lever again and run south, east, and then north to the exit while killing any risen knights in your path."],"t":"First Room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Send everyone to the north as far as they can go while avoiding the villager.","Pull the lever and send Kennith and your player into the room to the east. Send Ezekial to the western room and leave Eva in the central chamber.","Leave Kennith in the eastern room and send your player south to pull the lever.","After the lever is pulled send Kennith into the easternmost room to pull the lever.","Have your player pull the southern lever again.","Send Ezekial west (if not already in the western room) then all the way south to pull the lever.","Make Kennith pull the lever again and then send him into the southernmost room on his side to pull the lever.","Send your player back to the central chamber with Eva.","Make Ezekial pull his lever again and then send Kennith back to the central chamber.","Make Ezekial pull the lever once more and send him back to the central chamber.","Now that your party is regrouped, go to the next room."],"t":"Second Room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill all of the Risen Knights.","Send a character to each of the rooms in the four corners.","Pull all four levers in the following order: northeast, southeast, southwest, & then northwest.","Run to the newly opened gates and 'regroup' all of the characters. Proceed to the next room."],"t":"Third Room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use your player to investigate the strange device. Put your arm in. {Chat: 1 Put your arm in.}","Kill the first wave of knights with Kennith, Ezekial, and Eva. Your player will then investigate the second hole.","Kill the second wave of knights. Your player will investigate the third hole.","Kill the third wave of knights.","Enter the tunnel to the north."],"t":"Fourth Room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use Kennith to speak to Brother Maledict to the west.","Once the gate is open, knock down the wall in the west room with Ezekial and move Kennith north. Place him as close as possible to Mother Mallum while standing on the western ledge.","Take control of Ezekial and knock down the wall to the east and proceed north.","Kill the knight and position Ezekial directly opposite Kennith.","Take control of Kennith and attack Mother Mallum.","You now have control of Eva. Talk to Mayor Hobbs and knock him out, then attack Mallum.","Move Eva north of the statue and topple it.","Talk to Lucy. {Chat: Any}","Leave the Citadel using the cave exit.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Fifth Room"}]},"Scorpion Catcher":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Thormac on the top floor of the Sorcerer's Tower, south of Seers' Village, north-east of the Ardougne Lodestone. Be sure to get the scorpion cage from him and don't skip any dialogue. {Chat: 1 > Accept}}}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to the Seers' Village lodestone, run east, and speak to a Seer (south-west of the bank). {Chat: 2 Talk about Scorpion Catcher. > 2 Your friend Thormac sent me to speak to you.} (You have to wait for a while until dialogue appears again)","Bring the scorpion cage and go into Taverley Dungeon and enter the poison spider area. You need to use the dusty key on the blue dragon door and follow the dungeon around past the black demons.\n  - Note if you don't have a dusty key yet, defeat the jailer east of the Black Knights' Base, and pick up his dropped key. There will be a prisoner named Velrak the explorer who thanks you for freeing him and will give you the dusty key to you who is south of the jailer.","Directly south of the level 80 Agility shortcut, search the old wall to enter a small room.\n  - If the wall does not open go back to the Seer and make sure to finish the dialogue.","Use the scorpion cage on the Kharidian scorpion."],"t":"First scorpion"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the Barbarian Outpost (a games necklace is helpful).","Go inside the fenced area near the entrance to the Agility course.","Go inside the building in the north-east corner of the area.","Use the scorpion cage on the Kharidian scorpion."],"t":"Second scorpion"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the Edgeville Monastery (a combat bracelet is helpful, or the Edgeville lodestone).","Climb the eastern ladder and go to the east side of the floor.\n  - If you are stopped, talk to Abbot Langley and join the order. {Chat: 1 Well can I join your order?}","Catch the scorpion."],"t":"Third scorpion"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Thormac.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Sea Slug":{"sections":[{"n":"Swamp paste","r":"","s":["Talk to Caroline in Witchaven east of Ardougne. {Chat: Accept}","Talk to Holgart with swamp paste who is near Caroline.","Talk to him again and take the fixed boat to the fishing platform. {Chat: 1 Will you take me there?}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb up the ladder to the north.","Head west and go inside the building via the door on the eastern wall (do not kick the badly repaired wall).","Talk to Kennith (you can talk to him from the other side of the crates).","Go back down the ladder and head to the south-east corner of the platform.","Talk to Holgart to leave the platform.","Talk to Kent. Kent will talk to you one more time before you talk to Holgart.","Talk to Holgart to return to the platform."],"t":"The Fishing Platform"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head west and talk to Bailey for an unlit torch.","Pick up the broken glass.","Head to the north-east corner of the platform and take some damp sticks.","Use the broken glass on the damp sticks.","Use the sticks' rub-together option to light the torch (may take multiple attempts).","Climb up the ladder and go talk to Kennith.","Go outside and kick the 'badly repaired wall' north of the door and east of Kennith.","Go back inside and talk to Kennith.","Rotate the crane.","Go down the ladder and talk to Holgart.","Talk to Caroline.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Helping Kennith"}]},"Secrets of Amberfell":{"sections":[{"n":"2 ropes, 10 logs (of same kind), 20 nails (of same kind), 1 backpack space","r":"","s":["Talk to the ranger next to the bridge south of Hollow Hill. {Chat: 1 Start 'Secrets of Amberfell'. > Accept}","Take the S.O.S. note to Adam in Wendlewick. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Secrets of Amberfell'.}","Go back and talk to the ranger with 2 ropes, 20 nails and 10 logs to repair the bridge. {Chat: 1 Continue 'Secrets of Amberfell'.}","Go back and talk to Adam to report the findings. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Secrets of Amberfell'.}\n  - Be sure to complete the second set of dialogue when Anya spawns in to continue the quest."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to the bridge and cross to the other side.","Head south to trigger a cutscene with Inanna.","Continue east and speak to Sorrel next to the well.","Talk to Inanna, north of the well, to obtain deduction notes.","Talk to Rowan, next to the pumpkin patch. {Chat: 1 Are these your pumpkins? > 3 Can you tell me where everyone was last night? > 4 Bye.}","Talk to Heather, in the house to the southwest. (She may be outside the house if the door is left open) {Chat: 2 I'm looking for someone who contacted Wendlewick. > 4 Bye.}","Talk to Fern, to the north-east of the well. {Chat: 2 I'm looking for someone who contacted Wendlewick. > 3 Can you tell me where everyone was last night? > 4 Bye.}","Talk to Heywood, who roams around Amberfell (carrying a bow). {Chat: 2 I'm looking for someone who contacted Wendlewick. > 3 Can you tell me where everyone was last night? > 4 Bye.}","Talk to Ash at the barricade to the south-east. {Chat: 3 Can you tell me where everyone was last night? > 4 Bye.}","Talk to Sorrel. {Chat: 1 I'm just here to help. > 3 I'll leave you be, then.}","Open the deduction notes, select the below deductions, and check deductions when populated.","Fern, the gatherer, was in the woods gathering mushrooms.","Ash, the hunter, was by the river sending the message.","Heather, the crafter, was in someone's house arguing with Sorrel.","Rowan, the farmer, was in the vegetable patch tending the pumpkins.","Heywood, the ranger, was on patrol guarding the village."],"t":"Deductions"},{"n":"Combat gear","r":"food, AOE weapon","s":["Talk to Ash.","Go north to the temple and continue Secrets of Amberfell on the quest marker outside.{Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Ash and progress through the dialogue. {Chat: 4 I've heard enough. (Continue quest) > 5 What do you want from me? (Continue quest) > 4 Say nothing. (Continue quest) > Any}","Talk to Inanna and fight waves of level 42 vampyres and sanguine crawlers.\n  - Kill the Sanguine crawlers first. Avoid the special attacks by moving out of the blue box when it appears.\n  - You must use Inanna's special move to finish when you get a wave of only Sanguine crawlers, or the fight will continue indefinitely.","Talk to Inanna after the fight.","Go back and talk to Sorrel in Amberfell. (fairy ring DLP)"],"t":"Fighting the vampyres"},{"n":"5 cooked fish, butterfly net, teasing stick or ferret, vial, antisanguine (3)","r":"","s":["Go to Anya's camp, south-east of the Shrine of Inanna (fairy ring BKS), and talk to Anya. {Chat: 1 Continue 'Secrets of Amberfell'.}","Head north-west and talk to Shrine Tender Joanna to receive a blessed rabbit snare and a spirit jar. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Secrets of Amberfell'.}","South-east of Anya's camp, talk to Mossbrain at the goblin camp. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Secrets of Amberfell'.}","Talk to him again with 5 cooked fish to receive the offering bowl. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Secrets of Amberfell'.}","Go to Highweald Forest, north of Wendlewick, and search a hollow tree (found at the Hunter icons on the minimap) to spawn spirit moths.","With your butterfly net equipped, catch 5 spirit moths.","South-west of the Shrine of Inanna, lay the blessed rabbit snare and, using your teasing stick, flush the jackalope burrows until you catch a Jackalope.\n  - The easiest method is to lay the snare directly in front of a burrow and spam-clicking another burrow.","Go back and talk to Shrine Tender Joanna. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Secrets of Amberfell'.}","Pray at the Altar of Inanna to enter Inanna's Den. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Talk to Inanna. {Chat: 2 Move on. (Continue quest) > 3 Let's do it.}","Talk to Anya to receive a vial of blood.","Go to the top of the Wendlewick lighthouse and talk to Esther. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Secrets of Amberfell'. > Any > 2 I'll get going on that, then. (Continue quest)}","Combine your antisanguine (3) potion with the vial of blood.","Return to Inanna's den and use the empowered antisanguine on Inanna.","Talk to Inanna. {Chat: Any > 1 Yes.}","Go back and talk to Sorrel. {Chat: Any > Any} (fairy ring DLP)\n  - Make sure to have 6 backpack spaces, or you will have to go grab Anya and Inanna again and walk back.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Healing Inanna"}]},"Shades of Mort'ton":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the south-western ruined house in Mort'ton.\n  - Teleport to Canifis and run south-west to the gate of the swamp (must have Nature Spirit quest started), and then head to Mort'ton.\n  - Teleport to fairy ring BKR and then run south by south-east to where the map says the Hollows, to find a rowboat that takes you there.\n  - Alternatively use Drakan's medallion to teleport to the Barrows and run west.","Search the shelf on the wall and read the diary. {Chat: Accept}\n  - If you do not find it, it's probably already in your bank.","(Optional) Chop three swamp trees nearby and burn two logs to get the ashes.\n  - If you have an Underworld Grimoire equipped make sure to disable the auto-storage function, otherwise your ashes will be sent to the bank.","(Optional) Pick up the vials (on the ground near the shelf) and search the smashed table for extra tarromin and one grimy rogue's purse."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Make vials of water by using the empty vials on the sink nearby.","Make Serum 207 by adding clean tarromin and ashes to a vial of water.","Use it on Razmire (afflicted) in the general store. {Chat: 4 What are all these shadowy creatures? > 1 Yes, I'll dispatch those dark and evil creatures.}","Kill five Loar Shades and pick up their remains. Be sure to talk to Razmire first. They can be safespotted using the rocks south west of the waypost in the middle of town.","Give him the remains. He may require more Serum 207.","Use the serum on Ulsquire Shauncy, located in the house east of the general store.","Wait a minute and ask him about the remains and the temple.{Chat: 1 What did you find out about the remains? > 2 What can you tell me about that temple? > 5 Ok, thanks.}","Talk to Razmire. {Chat: 3 I have another question. > 2 What can you tell me about that temple? > 4 Can you open a store for me? > 1 Can I see the general store please?}","Buy at least one olive oil from his general store and optionally a Flamtaer hammer.","Open his builders' store.","Buy 5 timber beams, 5 limestone bricks, 25 swamp paste."],"t":"Serum 207"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Hop to World 88 which is the official world for this minigame.","Head north-east and kill shades or repair the temple to increase your sanctity.","Repair the temple until you reach 100% and at least 20 sanctity.","Light the sacred altar in the centre of the temple.","For solo questers: Shade luring dummies can be used to distract the Loar Shades when repairing the temple. Using the Flamtaer bracelet, the solo player can instantly create the temple walls section by section, until at 100%.","Use your olive oil on the flame to make sacred oil.","(Optional) Use Serum 207 on the flame to make Serum 208, which permanently cures NPCs.","(Optional) Use the Serum 208 on Razmire and Ulsquire in the houses nearby to permanently cure them."],"t":"Repairing the temple"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use the sacred oil on a log to create a pyre log.","Head to south-western Mort'ton to the Funeral Fires (do not cross the river to the west). The Funeral Fires appear as black crosshairs on the minimap on the western part of the Mort'ton.","Use the Pyre Log to light the fire, then use the Loar Remains to sacrifice them on the funeral pyre.","Talk to Ulsquire.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Burning a shade"}]},"Shadow of the Storm":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Father Reen south of Al Kharid bank. {Chat: Accept}\n  - He will give you Silverlight if you've dyed or destroyed it.","Talk to Father Badden at Uzer, east of Shantay Pass. (Optional: take the magic carpet to Uzer) {Chat: 1 Reen sent me. > 3 So what do you want me to do? > 1 How can I do that?}","Pick and grind a black mushroom (the closest is just south-east of the stairs east of Father Badden). Use it to dye Silverlight black. You can find some beside the staircase, downstairs east of the stairwell, or in the north east corner of the room, east of Evil Dave.","Go down the stairs.\n  - If you do not have the strange implement from The Golem quest, you can pick it up from the ground in the northwest room.","Talk to Evil Dave wearing your three black items and your dyed Silverlight. He is standing at the entrance to Agrith Naar's demonic temple in the underground Uzer ruins. {Chat: 2 I want to join your group. > 1 I'm evil!}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Denath. {Chat: 4 What do I have to do?}","Talk to Jennifer to get a demonic sigil mould. {Chat: 2 Do you have the demonic sigil mould?}","Talk to Matthew. {Chat: 3 Do you know what happened to Josef?}","Go to any furnace and smelt a demonic sigil. {Chat: 1 Make Demonic sigil}\n  - Your black outfit can be discarded at this point and replaced with combat gear. Keep Silverlight for the duration of the quest.","Talk to the clay golem outside the ruins about last night. {Chat: 3 Did you see anything happen last night?}","Look in the nearby Broken kilns for a book until you have found the Demonic tome (there's a broken kiln north of the Rug Merchant and one behind the walls east of the staircase that are easy to miss).","Talk to Matthew back in the lair.","Go north to talk to Denath and write down the incantation he tells you. {Chat: 4}","Complete the circle and click the sigil to chant the incantation. Be sure to remember it, as you’ll need it again later in the quest.","Be sure to take the sigil from the floor, or you will have to make a new one at a furnace.","Enter the portal and take Tanya's sigil.","Tell Evil Dave to return to the lair - you should have 4 sigils now. {Chat: 2 You've got to get back to the throne room!}"],"t":"Ritual"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go up the stairs, talk to Father Badden and Father Reen. {Chat: 3 Oh, don't be so simple-minded!}","Talk to the golem. {Chat: 4 [use strange implement]}"],"t":"Rallying the troops"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Matthew to start the incantation. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Chant Demonic Sigil and say the incantation backwards. (If you have forgotten the incantation, it can be found on page 6 of the demonic tome)","Kill the demon with the Silverlight (dyed). After defeating it, you will have the Darklight equipped.\n  - You can damage the demon with any combat style, but you must equip the Silverlight (dyed) as it dies.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The final fight"}]},"Sheep Herder":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Councillor Halgrive south of the Ardougne church and north of the zoo. {Chat: 1 What's wrong? > Accept}","Talk to Doctor Orbon inside the church and buy a pair of clothes for 100 coins. {Chat: 2 Talk about something else. > 2 Ok, I'll take it.}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to the lodestone and go west until you reach the fenced enclosure with a stone building and incinerator (looks like a furnace). It is south of the fishing guild.","Equip the plague jacket and trousers and enter the gate.","Pick up the cattleprod inside the stone enclosure, equip it.","Prod 1 of each colour sheep in and through the incinerator pen's gate. If the sheep are stuck, simply switch worlds."],"t":"Herding the sheep"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the pen and use the sheep feed on each of them.","Take all 4 bones, then use them on the incinerator."],"t":"Euthanising the sheep"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Councillor Halgrive.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Sheep Shearer (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Fred the Farmer north of Lumbridge. {Chat: 3 I'm looking for work. > 1 It takes all sorts, I suppose. > Accept > 1 Of course! > 1 I'm something of an expert, actually.}","Fred takes the 20 balls of wool."],"t":"If you already have the 20 unnoted balls of wool"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Fred the Farmer north of Lumbridge. {Chat: 3 I'm looking for work. > 1 It takes all sorts, I suppose. > Accept > 1 Of course! > 1 I'm something of an expert, actually.}","Climb-over the stile into the sheep pen west of his house.\n  - Alternatively purchase 20 balls of wool from the Grand exchange and continue to the last step.","Shear the six sheep.\n  - You cannot shear black sheep, rams or the odd-looking sheep. If you attack a ram and cannot kill it, run out of the pen until it stops targeting you.","Wait 12 seconds for their wool to grow back, shearing them again.","Repeat this process until you have 20 pieces of wool.","Head to the floor 2 of the Lumbridge Castle.","Use the spinning wheel in the southern room to spin the balls of wool.","Talk to Fred and hand them in. {Chat: 1 I have some balls of wool for you.}"],"t":"If you don't have the balls of wool"}]},"Shield of Arrav":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Reldo in the Varrock Palace library. {Chat: 1 I'm in search of a quest. > Accept}","Search the east side of the centre bookcases (with the navy blue book) for The Shield of Arrav book, then read it."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Reldo and ask about the Phoenix Gang. {Chat: 1 Do you know where I can find the Phoenix Gang?}","Talk to Baraek who is located in the north-east of Varrock square, and give him 10 coins. Ask him every question available. {Chat: 1 Can you tell me where I can find the Phoenix Gang? > 1 Alright. Have 10 gold coins. > 2 Thanks!}","Travel to the Phoenix Gang Hideout which is located south of Aubury's Rune Shop. It will be marked by a dungeon link to the Misthalin Underground on the map.","Climb down the ladder.","Talk to Straven and ask to join. Tell him you know who he is. {Chat: 1 I know who you are! > 1 I'd like to offer you my services.}","Go to the Blue Moon Inn which is just north of Varrock's southern entrance.","Kill Jonny the beard.","Grab the Intel report that he drops.","Talk to Straven.","Search the chest in the south-west corner of the hideout for a broken shield.","After climbing back up the ladder, enter the house east of the Phoenix Gang Hideout and go up the ladder there.","Pick up the two Phoenix crossbows on the floor, you will need these for the next gang."],"t":"The Phoenix Gang"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Charlie the Tramp located just north of Varrock's southern entrance. Ask him what's down the alley. {Chat: 3 Do you know where I can find the Black Arm Gang hideout? > 1 That sounds fair. (Pay 10 gold.)}","Follow the alley to the west and enter the building.","Talk to Katrine. {Chat: 1 I've heard you're the Black Arm Gang. > Any > 1 I want to become a member of your gang. > 1 Well, you can give me a try, can't you? > 1 No problem. I'll get you two phoenix crossbows.}","Talk to Katrine again to give her the crossbows.","Head north through the door and climb up the staircase.","Open and search the cupboard on the south-eastern wall for the other broken shield piece."],"t":"The Black Arm Gang"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use one half of the shield on the other for a restored shield.","Talk to King Roald located in the immediate east room of the Varrock Palace. {Chat: 1 Talk about the Shield of Arrav.}\n  - If you have completed Priest in Peril {Chat: 2 Talk about the Shield of Arrav.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Shilo Village":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to Karamja (shortest teleport is ckr) and run far south/southeast to the southeast corner of Shilo Village.","Speak to Mosol Rei near the Broken cart. {Chat: 1 Why do I need to run? > 1 Rashiliyia? Who is she? > 1 What can we do? > 4 I'll go see the Shaman. > Accept} He will give you a wampum belt.","Teleport to the Karamja lodestone and run southeast to Trufitus, northeast of Tai Bwo Wannai Village, west of the hardwood grove.","Use the belt on Trufitus. Tell him you're going to search for \"Ah Za Rhoon\". {Chat: 2 Mosol Rei said something about a legend? > 1 Why was it called Ah Za Rhoon? > 3 I am going to search for Ah Za Rhoon! > 1 Yes, I will seriously look for Ah Za Rhoon and I'd appreciate your help.}\n  - If you don't yet have a chisel, a rope and torch, you should get those now from Jiminua's Jungle Store. You may also craft bronze wire at the nearby anvil."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"Torch and rope","r":"","s":["Travel east of Trufitus' hut, cross a wooden log and then head south to the mound of earth surrounded by three dead trees, Ah Za Rhoon.","Search the mound of earth and select excavate. {Chat: 1 Try to excavate the mound.}","Use a lit torch on the fissure.\n  - To obtain a lit torch, light the torch in the backpack.","Use a rope on the fissure.","Search the fissure, climb down. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll give it a go!}"],"t":"The mound"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Search the cave in (see map) and wiggle through the rocks to proceed to the second area. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll wriggle through.}","After wiggling through, follow along the west side of the wall and search the loose rocks against the northwestern wall for a tattered scroll. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll carefully move the rocks to see what's behind them.}\n  - You might fail and take damage, retry until you succeed.","Search the old sacks in the far southeast corner for a crumpled scroll.","Search the ancient gallows to the north for the Zadimus corpse. {Chat: 2 Yes, I may find something else on the corpse.}","Read both scrolls. {Chat: 1 Yes please.}"],"t":"Ah Za Rhoon"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use the Karamja lodestone/Tai Bwo Wannai teleport to get back to Trufitus.","Use the two scrolls and the corpse on Trufitus and ask about the sacred ground. {Chat: 1 Is there any sacred ground around here?}","Walk west to the nearby Tribal Statue. Bury the corpse then talk to the Spirit of Zadimus for the bone shard.","Use the bone shard on Trufitus. {Chat: 1 It appeared when I buried Zadimus' corpse. > 1 He said something after he gave it to me. > 1 The spirit said something about keys and kin?}","Talk to Trufitus. {Chat: 2 I need help with Bervirius.} Ensure Trufitus mentions the need to find the Tomb of Bervirius."],"t":"Burial"},{"n":"Chisel, bronze wire (or a bronze bar to make the wire), and three backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Head southwest to Cairn Isle by climbing the rocks and going across the bridge. Be careful, you can sometimes fall - use the Surge ability to bypass this.","Search the well stacked rocks to the north to enter the Tomb of Bervirius. If you fail search again until you are able to enter. {Chat: 1 Yes please, I can think of nothing nicer!}","Inside, run south and search the tomb dolmen to receive three items: sword pommel, locating crystal, and Bervirius notes.\n  - If you do not have enough space the notes will drop on the ground.","Read all 3 options on the Bervirius notes.","Use the chisel on the sword pommel to create bone beads (the chisel on the tool belt will not work).","Use the bone beads on the bronze wire to create beads of the dead.\n  - You can make the bronze wire from a bronze bar at an anvil near Trufitus."],"t":"Cairn Island"},{"n":"Chisel, bone shard, beads of the dead, and 3 regular bones (can be obtained from monsters in cave)","r":"Combat equipment and food, three forms are weak to fire spells.","s":["Travel east of Trufitus' hut, over the agility log and run north, to the general area of The Shaikahan.","Search the foliage, then attempt to open the Ancient Door. (See the map for the location.)","Use a chisel on the bone shard.","Equip the beads of the dead.","Use the bone key on the door to open it.","Open the ancient metal gate.","Climb down the rock.","Run to the south west corner and use 3 bones on the tomb doors. Be careful not to bury them instead.","Open the doors and search the tomb dolmen.","Kill all 3 forms of Nazastarool. The stalagmites to the east of the tomb dolmen can be used as a safe spot.","Search the tomb dolmen again for a Rashiliyia corpse."],"t":"Rashiliyia's Tomb"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel back to the Tomb of Bervirius on Cairn Isle.","Use the Rashiliyia corpse on the tomb dolmen.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Sins of the Father":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Mr Mordaut at the Anachronia base camp. {Chat: 1 Anachronia. > 1 Talk about Kerapac. > Accept}","Talk to either Eliza or Alpheus south of the lodestone. {Chat: 1 Talk about Kerapac. (Sins of the Father)}","Exit Anachronia base camp to the north down the stairs, not via the Agility shortcut.","Continue north up the first set of stairs and investigate the bottom part of the dragonkin statue to your immediate west.\n  - If a message appears telling you to complete this very quest, go back to the open area between the two flights of stairs (by the entrance to Kerapac's laboratory until you trigger a dialogue about something \"out of place\".\n  - You must also trigger another dialogue in front of the statue itself about the statue looking different before you can enter the statue.","Enter the door.","Talk to Vicendithas {Chat: 2 What are you doing here? > 2 Can I help with the machine? > 1 Play tutorial.}.","Talk to Vicendithas again.","Collect an effigy casing from the middle.","Collect 20 resources from one of the nodes.\n  - A chat box will appear. Confirm it or you won't be able to continue dialogue with Vicendithas.","Talk to Vicendithas. You need atleast 2 free inventory spaces.","Go to Kerapac's workbench and construct the effigy.","Talk to Vicendithas.","Turn the valves in the order instructed.","Interact with the incubator hatch to deposit the effigy.","Interact with the incubator hatch again.","Talk to Vicendithas.","Talk to Vicendithas again after ending the tutorial."],"t":"Getting started"}]},"Sliske's Endgame":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"an Armadylean token or skills necklace to the Crafting Guild for quick access to Armadyl's Tower, mind altar teleport for quick access to the Black Knight's Fortress","s":["Talk to Relomia in Draynor Village. {Chat: 1 Sliske's Endgame. > 1 Where are the gods? > Accept}","Talk to each of the gods.\n  - Talk to Seren and Zaros up in the Tower of Voices by using the stairs north-east of the Prifddinas lodestone. {Chat: 1 Speak with Seren about Sliske's Endgame.}\n  - Talk to Saradomin in the throne room on the east side of the floor 3 of White Knights' Castle.\n    - He may not speak to you if you have the Of Zamorak title active. Lobbying may be necessary if he only insults you.\n  - Talk to Armadyl on the roof of his tower north-west of Port Sarim.\n    - Go up the tower by the teleporter.\n    - Climb up the stairs on the west side to the roof.\n  - Talk to Zamorak on the floor 2 of Black Knights' Fortress or at Zamorak's hideout.\n    - You may get there by using the mind altar teleport to mind altar, a communication device, or a Skull of Remembrance.\n  - Talk to Icthlarin in Death's office by entering through portal in the north of Draynor Village. {Chat: 2 Speak to Death about Sliske's Endgame}\n    - You cannot go from War's Retreat directly.","Talk to Relomia in Draynor Village. {Chat: 1 Sliske's Endgame.}"],"t":"Gathering the party"},{"n":"Weapon to defeat Nomad","r":"Armour, food, a teleport to the Heart of Gielinor (such as The Heart teleport or a Desert amulet 2 or above)","s":["Dismiss any familiar or follower you may have following you.","Talk to Relomia in the Heart of Gielinor campsite (west of the entrance, outside of the Heart of Gielinor). {Chat: 1 Yes, I am prepared. > Any > Any}","Defeat Nomad. He uses melee/mage and doesn't use special attacks."],"t":"The final member"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Run through both the mazes to the exit on the north-east. The solutions are given below.","The green lines show the main path to follow, and the blue lines lead to puzzle rooms off the main map that must be completed.\n  - See the puzzles section below with help solving the puzzles.\n  - Return to the green paths after completing the puzzles.","The orange lines lead to optional cutscenes.","These maps and your minimap may not line up exactly until the puzzle rooms have been completed as completing puzzle rooms rotates parts of the labyrinth."],"t":"Maze and puzzles"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Click the Solution panel to view the Clue","Use the table below to find the Solution","Rotate the Shadow casters till they match the solution."],"t":"=Rotation puzzles="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill any wights in the room to obtain missing Masks (they will drop a Mask of Glee, Mask of Sorrow or Mask of Indifference)","Click the Viewing panel to begin the projection mode","If it says one of the projectors are damaged, repair them","Rotate the Shadow casters till it forms the solution image shown on the right (a complete Sliske mask)"],"t":"=Projection puzzles="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Click the solution panel to view the Clue, then view the Solution from the table in the section above","Kill any wights in the room to obtain missing Masks (they will drop a Mask of Glee, Mask of Sorrow or Mask of Indifference)","Take the mask from all the casters that don't match the description, and re-attach the mask on another caster till it matches","When all the casters are matching the solution, the puzzle will be solved"],"t":"=Mask replacement puzzles="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Stand in the spotlight"],"t":"=Spotlight puzzles="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["At the end of the maze, ascend the stairs","Participate in the race and go through the dialogue and cutscenes {Chat: Any}"],"t":"Reaching the stone"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use the purple exit portal to leave, and prepare for a tough fight with the best combat gear you have.\n  - Tier 90 armour like masterwork equipment greatly helps.\n  - Bring a beast of burden with high healing foods.","Return to Relomia using The Heart teleports and resume the battle against Sliske","The fight is divided into 3 phases, at the end of each phase you can bank and return to resume from that checkpoint"],"t":"The final battle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Fight against wights of increasing difficulty, kill enough of them to increase the progress bar on top.\n  - Use Deflect Melee or Deflect Ranged depending on the types of wights you are fighting\n  - Be aware that all remaining unstable wight footsoldiers will explode at the end of the wave, potentially causing death if the player is surrounded but you will continue onto the next wave when you return."],"t":"Phase 1"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill Nomad.\n  - Use Deflect Ranged while fighting him.\n  - Nomad plants mines and Gregorovic rains damage on the arena. Make sure to walk off of marked tiles.","Kill Linza the Disgraced.\n  - Use Deflect Melee while fighting her.\n  - Linza reflects damage which is less deadly after she's the only surviving boss.\n  - She also has a blue charged bar that appears above her head and does a very high damage move. She will also bind before she does this move so have surge or freedom ready. It is recommended to dodge this attack.","Kill Gregorovic.\n  - Use Deflect Ranged while fighting him.\n  - The spirits that spawn towards Gregorovic will heal him if they reach him. Kill them before they touch him."],"t":"Phase 2"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill Sliske. You cannot use deathtouched darts to kill Sliske.\n  - Use Deflect Magic throughout the fight as the majority of the damage will be magic classed. Keep in mind that prayer points are drained faster than normal in this fight.\n  - If you are having trouble, wearing the Armour of Trials and wielding Vanquish can help greatly has it can provide a 25% defensive and offensive bonus during the fight if you die 5 times in a row.\n  - Beware of his special attack where several shadow pits will appear below your feet. Step away to avoid significant damage. He will summon 4 shadow pits in the first round, 5 in the second, and 4 in the subsequent two rounds. On rounds 3 and 4, Sliske's attacks will predict where you are walking towards on the 4th and final shadow pit.\n  - Attack Sliske until he reaches 10,000 health, he will teleport away.\n  - Destroy the Power Source in the centre of the room.\n  - Attack Sliske until he reaches 10,000 health again.\n  - Enter one of the rifts. Sliske will bring you back into the arena.\n  - Attack Sliske until he reaches 10,000 health again.\n  - Jump on the rock formation in front of Sliske.\n  - Attack Sliske until he reaches 10,000 health again.\n  - Defeat Sliske one final time. You have unlimited life points and adrenaline and all ability cooldowns are halved. (If you have Onslaught Ability you can kill him automatically)","Talk to Jas. {Chat: Any > Any} (Except insulting Jas - does not allow you to continue)","Talk to the gods on the surface. {Chat: Any > Any > Any}","Return to Relomia in Draynor. {Chat: 1 Sliske's Endgame. > Any}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Phase 3"}]},"Smoking Kills":{"sections":[{"n":"Catspeak amulet","r":"","s":["Head to Pollnivneach. You can use the magic carpet network from Shantay Pass or Al Kharid lodestone to travel to Al Kharid and head south-east.","Speak to Sumona in Pollnivneach {Chat: Accept} (without a cat pet out).","Equip your catspeak amulet.","Run south to the well in the town centre.","Attempt to climb down the well.","Speak to the cat, finish all prompts.\n  - If you do not wear a catspeak amulet or skip the conversation, you will be unable to open the sealed tomb door later in the quest."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"Bring all items needed for the next section, including cat of any sort, catspeak amulet, ghostspeak amulet, combat gear (ranged, magic, or necromancy, or simply ignore three low damage ranged minions for a few seconds), earmuffs, facemask","r":"rope, waterskins, food for lower-level players","s":["Travel to Sophanem by either one of the following methods.\n  - Use the Magic carpet Network, and then run southeast, then along the seashore to the swamp.\n  - Menaphos lodestone teleport, then run east across the bridge to Sophanem (requires completion of The Jack of Spades and Contact!)","Head southeast towards the sea/swampland","Enter the swamp using the entrance at the south end of the swamp, by the seashore.","Make your way to the north-west part of the swamp, \"climb fallen pillar\", and go up the stairs.\n  - Optional: Go west, \"climb low wall\", use your rope on the \"rock\", jutting out over the edge - this will give you quicker access in the future.","Walk north past the archaeologist's fire, through the opening between the cliffs.","Search the western wall for a sealed door to enter the dungeon."],"t":"Finding the tomb"},{"n":"Cat of any sort, catspeak amulet, ghostspeak amulet, combat gear (ranged or magic recommended), earmuffs, facemask","r":"food for lower-level players","s":["Drop your cat, search the western \"holey wall\". Agree, and your cat will enter, opening the wall.","Go west, kill (or ignore) the 3 skeletons to the south with magic/range/necromancy.","Destroy the broken door until you can walk through it.","Search the west wall (not the odd markings on the east wall) twice to temporarily disable and pass two traps.","Enter the door to the north.","Kill the zombies and skeletons.","After about 10-20 seconds, a level 77 mummy warrior will spawn. Kill it and take the Ranged path key.","Open the door to the east, pull the lever on the northern wall.","Return to the starting room (traps on this side are now permanently disabled)","Repeat steps on the other side.\n  - Go east, kill (or ignore) the 3 skeletons to the south with magic/range/necro.\n  - Destroy the broken door.\n  - Search the east wall (not odd markings on the west wall) twice to disable and pass two traps.\n  - Enter the door to the north.\n  - Kill the zombies and skeletons.\n  - After about 10-20 seconds, a level 77 mummy warrior will spawn. Kill it and take the Magic path key.\n  - Use the key on the door to the west, pull the lever on the northern wall.","Return to the starting room (traps on this side are now permanently disabled).","Walk north, all traps have been disabled and can be ignored.","Equip your Ghostspeak amulet and talk to Catolax.","Use your Earmuffs on your Face mask to create Masked earmuffs."],"t":"Inside the tomb"},{"n":"Masked earmuffs, combat gear, food","r":"","s":["Return to Pollnivneach.","Equip your masked earmuffs and combat gear.","Enter the well in the town centre.","Head north, kill a mighty banshee to get a Banshee voice. The drop must be manually picked up; it will not appear in the area loot interface.","Ensure any follower is dismissed first, then run all the way north to the large blue/purple wavering mystic barrier and pass through it.\n  - Do not click on anything else while the cutscene is in motion, or you will go back outside the barrier and will need to acquire another banshee voice.","After the cutscene, attack the Banshee mistress. She is weak to bolts, so using range is recommended if you're lower-levelled.\n  - Enable the Protect from Ranged prayer after she gets to 50% health.","Finish the fight and watch the cutscene.\n  - If you click on anything else, you will go outside the barrier, but you will not have to fight again; you can easily go back inside the barrier to continue the last cutscene.","Return to Pollnivneach (you can climb out of the well).","Pick up your cat if you have not already done so.","Talk to Sumona again to complete the quest."],"t":"The final fight"}]},"Some Like It Cold":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Chuck the polar bear in Ardougne Zoo.","Speak to him again. {Chat: 1 Some Like It Cold Quest > Accept}","Speak to him a final time to be teleported {Chat: 1 Some Like It Cold Quest > 1 Yes}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After being teleported by Chuck, head west to the seals.","Wake up the seal that can be interacted with. {Chat: 3 I'm looking for a polar bear. > 1 How can I entertain you?}","Use the Dance or Jump For Joy emote.","Talk to the seal. {Chat: 1 What's wrong with penguins? > 2 Where does your band live?}","Use the smaller boat to the north-east. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Ping & Pong. You don't need to be in your tuxedo for this.","After receiving the items from them, do one of the following:\n  - Option one: Use a crafting table 4 in a player-owned house to make their rock costume. To return, use the Fremennik Province lodestone and head north to board the ship to iceberg.\n  - Option two: Head to the north-east corner of the Iceberg and right-click Jim and select 'tuxedo-time'. Head to the north-west and investigate the avalanche of snow. Follow the main hall to the end and talk to the gate guard in the booth. After proceeding through the door, head east and then follow the western wall in the war-room to the western workbench. Craft Ping & Pong's costumes there. To get out of the room click the red button west of the gate. Go to Jim to get out of tuxedo.","Give Ping & Pong their costumes.","Board the nearby boat to return to the seals. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to the seal, bank any items and head to the camp. There is a deposit box option when talking to the seal. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"The seal"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Teddy, the polar bear in a clown costume, in the centre of the camp.","Talk to Larry, north of Teddy","Talk to Teddy again.","Talk to Noodle outside the south-west building.","Try to open the door to the southern building where the Walrus is in.","Take the bat in the box (slightly west of the door where the walrus is) from the front of the building.{Chat: 1 Yes.}","Encourage Teddy, Ping & Pong, and Bouncer to make noise by clicking on them. Click Ping, then Pong, then Bouncer, then Teddy until a cutscene starts. Their bars should all be blue, so it's a good idea to walk in circles.","When the Walrus is outside, enter his building and steal the egg from the table.","Give the egg to Larry in the north.","Talk to Teddy.","Talk to all six of the unnamed penguins. (Four in the courtyard, one between the north and north-west buildings and one on fishing grate in the north-east corner)","Talk to Teddy.","Talk to Plaza outside the easternmost building.","Collect the following items:\n  - Fish the fishing hole in the north-east until you receive a shark tooth and squid.\n  - Take a board from the wood scrap pile north of the easternmost building.\n  - Search the shelves in the easternmost building for olive oil, popsicle tray, and a rock carving hammer.\n  - Right click Teddy and \"Tear off fabric\".\n  - Search the shelves in the south-west building for lye and a cork screw.","Once all of the supplies are obtained:\n  - Use the lye on the olive oil.\n  - Use the unmoulded soap on the popsicle tray.\n  - Use the squid on the popsicle tray.\n  - Use the hammer on the soap.\n  - With a shark tooth in your backpack, use the ripped fabric on the board.","Talk to Plaza.","Talk to Teddy.","Talk to Astoria outside the easternmost building. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Prisoner of Walrus Camp"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Defeat Astoria in a game of Battlefish.\n  - Place your fish anywhere on the board.\n  - You can click on the \"HIT\" and \"MISS\" notifications to speed up this section considerably. But beware spam clicking may exit the game making you start over.\n  - Solution:","In the small building just south-east, take from the circus prop crate on the northern wall.","Talk to Teddy.","To repair the engine:\n  - Use Bowling pin -> lever opening\n  - Use Hula hoop -> broken valve wheel\n  - Use Circus plate -> pressure gauge\n  - Use Foam finger -> pressure gauge\n  - Use Balloon -> metal wire\n  - Use Insulated wire -> wirebox\n  - Use Cloth -> cracked pipe"],"t":"Reparations"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Teddy. {Chat: 2 No, I know what needs to be done.}","Defeat the seals in Battlefish (if you accidentally exit, click on the periscope through the door to the left).\n  - Solution:","Quest complete!"],"t":"Escape"}]},"Song from the Depths":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Lucille who is in a house west of the Rimmington well. {Chat: 1 Is everything okay? > 1 Can I help? > Accept}","Stay within Lucille's house and drink the restless sleep potion.","Follow the souls north-east to a cave entrance located south of the Rimmington mine and north-west of the Port Sarim lodestone and enter it.\n  - If you go past the cave, exit to the lobby, or logout in the cave, you will have to go back to Lucille and obtain the potion once again."],"t":"Dreaming souls"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go north over the bridge.","Continue through the cave to the east.","Talk to the Raptor. {Chat: 1 I'm here to save Waylan.}","Enter the door to follow the Raptor."],"t":"Inside the cave"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the north door.","Enter the west door.","Enter the south door.","Enter the east door.","Follow the souls and enter the final door to the north."],"t":"The maze"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After the cutscene, go to the north-east corner of the room to discover the first symbol. It is two steps south of the wall feature against the north wall and two steps east of the fissure.","Head to the north-west corner where the second symbol will be located a bit south-west of the wavy section of the ground.","Enter the sparkling doorway that just appears. The location will be different for each player.","Go just west of the central fissure to find the first symbol.","Go west of the northern fissure to find the second symbol.","The last symbol is just north-west of the eastern fissure.","Enter the sparkling doorway that just appears. The location will be different for each player.","Follow the souls and enter the door to the north."],"t":"Symbol searching"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take the burning sapling from the centre of the room and plant it in the pot overflowing with water to the southwest.","Enter the doorway with a waterfall to the northeast.","Take the dead sapling from the previous pot and plant it in the pot with living fungi to the northwest.","Enter the doorway surrounded by fungus to the southwest.","Take the budding sapling from the previous pot and plant it in the pot with ivy growing around it to the southeast.","Enter the doorway surrounded by ivy to the west.","Take the healthy sapling from the previous pot and plant it in the pot covered in cobwebs to the northeast.","Enter the doorway covered in cobwebs to the east."],"t":"Tree growing"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Proceed north and enter the doorway.","After the cutscene, jump into the chasm.","Proceed through the three passageways and enter the openings whilst evading the acid, players with high life points or some food can simply run through the acid taking the shortest route to save time. Running straight through the acid deals some (2-150) damage. Use Surge and Dive when available.","After an interactive cutscene, finish the dialogue with the siren, Remora. {Chat: 1 We're not on an island. > 1 What you're talking about isn't real. > 2 Don't you know how you got here? > 2 You have been stealing the souls of villagers. > 1 Alright. > 1 Wait, don't kill her! > 1 We need her to escape.}","Talk to the Raptor. You will receive 3 items. {Chat: 2 What now? > 2 We should talk to Lucille.}","Head south-west to Rimmington and talk to Lucille.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The stomach of the dragon"}]},"Soul Searching":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Trista on the dock north of Soul Supplies in the City of Um.","Choose the \"Eavesdrop\" option on Trista. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Suspicious Stranger"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Death in the City of Um. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Soul Searching'}","Talk to the Suspicious Stranger on the dock where Trista was earlier. {Chat: 1 Convince > 2 Persuade. > 3 Threaten.}","Talk to Death in the City of Um. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Soul Searching'}"],"t":"Death"},{"n":"3 Cadava berries, 10 fishing bait, antipoison (3), charcoal, and papyrus","r":"","s":["Talk to Malignius Mortifer at the Um ritual site with the required items in your backpack. {Chat: 2 Quests. > # Soul Searching. > 1 Yes.}","Return to the dock with the Suspicious Stranger."],"t":"Malignius"},{"n":"potion of zombification","r":"","s":["Drink the potion of zombification at least 8 paces away from the Suspicious Stranger but still closer than the bottom of the stairs to transmogrify into a zombie.","Talk to the Suspicious Stranger.","Board the gondola.","Continue dialogue with Icthlarin. {Chat: 3 What now? (Continue Quest)}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Zombification"}]},"Spirit of Summer":{"sections":[{"n":"Ghostspeak amulet","r":"","s":["Talk to the spirit at the Wilderness wall north of Infernal Source Dig Site. {Chat: Accept}","Keep trying to catch the spirit until you see a cutscene. {Chat: 1 OK}","Talk to the father figure with a ghostspeak amulet equipped.","Use the table below to respond to the man's emotes.\n  - Don't repeat yourself.\n  - Use the Think emote to see the emote again. Talk to him and your character will say the emote he is doing.\n  - The rings around the girl will disappear on successful emotes. When all the rings are gone, the girl is free.","Once the girl is free, talk to her. {Chat: 1 What's going on here? > 1 Okay, I will come with you to the village you're talking about.}"],"t":"The farm"},{"n":"none","r":"Supreme growth potion (leafy)","s":["Once in the village, ask the girl to be taken back. {Chat: 3 Can you take me back, please?}","Search a crate for a limpwurt seed.","Rake the farming patch and plant the seed.\n  - Note: You can use a Supreme growth potion (leafy) on it, but do not harvest the roots yet.\n  - Wait limpwurt plant to grow (roughly 20 minutes), but do not harvest it. You cannot continue the quest until the plant grows.","Pick up 4 steel nails and a hammer in the anvil building (south east).\n  - Note: Sometimes you will find only 3 nails there. More nails can be found in the sacks or the building west of the farming patch, near the bucket. You can also smith nails on the anvil.","Pick up 2 planks in the centre-most building.","Use a plank on the wardrobe in the building south-east of the statue.","With three free inventory slots, Pick from the Hollow log near the statue for button mushrooms.","Grab a bucket from the building directly west of the farm patch.","Use the bucket on the barrel of water south-east of the farming patch which is just outside the anvil building.","After the limpwurt plant is grown, talk to the spirit for a cutscene.","Talk to her again and agree to come along. {Chat: 1 Okay, I'll come along.}"],"t":"Fixing the village"},{"n":"None","r":"","s":["Talk to Summer Bonde once more to be taken back. {Chat: 3 Can you take me back?}","Take a skull and 5 bones east of the farm.","Stand in the portal which is the white circle.","Talk to Summer Bonde. {Chat: 2 What exactly is going on here? > 1 Of course, I will help you.}","Follow her and Climb-down the Trapdoor.","Use the skull and right-click Use the bones on the altar one by one. You do not need to move around the altar to use bones and skull.\n  - Note: Take care not to bury the bones.","If she is not right next to you, Climb-up the ladder and then in both situations, talk to Summer again. {Chat: 1 What should I do now? > 3 I better get to work, then.}"],"t":"Back in the farm"},{"n":"Multiple Spirit wolf pouches, Desert wyrm pouches & Spirit scorpion pouches","r":"food (for lower-levelled players).","s":["Optional: Customise your interface to allow you to dismiss familiars as fast as possible.","Run north to the wolf platform.","Summon a spirit wolf so that it stands on the platform (it doesn't have to be in the centre).","The Spirit Beast will only be lured to a platform with a familiar summoned.","Dismiss the familiar as soon as the beast steps on the platform .\n  - The beast does not need to fully be on the platform.\n  - Your familiar will be dismissed immediately without the \"are you sure\" warning; a lightning effect will show if successful.","Don't let the beast consume your familiar, and don't move your familiar off the platform. It is helpful to try to position yourself between the beast and your familiar.","A cutscene will play if you have succeeded.","If you have to teleport out for more pouches, you must talk to Summer by the quest start location to return to the spirit realm.","Repeat this process with the desert wyrm, using the platform that appears during the cutscene. You can also push the Spirit Beast by walking at beast to position the creature, but it can give you some damage and may push you away sometimes.","And again, for the spirit scorpion - the platform is far west.","Talk to any of the spirits by the Spirit Beast.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Luring the beast"}]},"Spirits of the Elid":{"sections":[{"n":"1 thread, 1 law rune and 1 air rune to cast the Telekinetic Grab spell","r":"","s":["Head to Nardah (south of fairy ring dlq) and talk to Awusah the Mayor in the building east of the fountain. {Chat: 1 I am an adventurer in search of quests. > 2 Any idea how you got this curse? > Accept}","Head to the house north-east of the fountain and talk to Ghaslor the Elder. You should receive a Ballad. {Chat: 1 I am trying to find out the cause of this town's curse. > 1 River spirits, what are they?}","Head to the building that has a statuette plinth just west of Ghaslor's house and north of the fountain.","Telegrab the ancestral key from the table.\n  - You may attach the ancestral key to your steel key ring if you've completed the One Small Favour quest","Go to the other side of the building and open the northernmost cupboard and search it for the robe top and bottom.","Fix the top and bottom robes."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"A weapon and ammo for a combat type other than melee, rope, thread","r":"","s":["Head north, past the Dominion Tower until a waterfall is seen.\n  - You can teleport to there by using a traveller's necklace to south of the Uzer eagles' eyrie.\n  - There is a bronze arrow south-east of Dominion Tower and a shortbow north-east of it.","Climb the waterfall.","Equip the Robes of Elidinis and open the door.\n  - If the door will not open, make sure you repaired and are wearing both robe pieces, and make sure you have the Ancestral key you tele-grabbed earlier.","Head east to the three doors.","Try to open any door, kill the golem that spawns, then enter the room and clear the water channel for each room.\n  - If you click the door before the golem's death animation has finished, it will respawn and you will have to fight it again.}} :{| class=\"wikitable\" !Door!!Golem!!Weakness!!Clear water channel via |- |South||White golem||Stab||Thieving |- |East||Grey golem||Slash||Using a pickaxe (tool belt works) |- |North-east||Black golem||Crush||Shoot target with a bow and arrow, magic, or necromancy |} {{Checklist|","Head through the door to the north and talk to one of the spirits in the large area. {Chat: 4 I come as an emissary from the people of Nardah. > 1 Is there anything they can do to get their fountain working again?}","Head back to Nardah.\n  - It is possible to be bugged when exiting the cave. To get out of the bug, simply use a Home Teleport spell.\n  - Amulet of glory teleport to Al Kharid and then taking the magic carpet to Nardah is a quick option.}}"],"t":"The Golems"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Awusah the Mayor.","Take shoes just south from the entrance door inside the Mayor's house.","Go outside the house, then remove-sole from the shoes to obtain a sole.\n  - Ensure you have a light source or you will not be able to talk to the next NPC without being interrupted.","Head west from the Nardah General Store, past a camp of trainee adventurers and climb-down the crevice.","Talk to the Genie {Chat: 1 I'm after a statue that was thrown down here. > 1 Maybe I can make a deal for it? > 3 Ok I agree to the deal.}, then talk again.\n  - If your backpack was full, pick up the Statuette. - There will be room now as you gave the Genie a sole.","Head back to Nardah and use the statuette on the plinth in the shrine room, north of the fountain.\n  - Optional: Pray at the statue for medium desert task achievement Heathen Idle.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The Genie"}]},"Spiritual Enlightenment (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Charter a ship to Aminishi and talk to Ling. {Chat: Accept}\n  - If you have just completed Impressing the Locals, you may need to relog for the chat option to show up.","Kill creatures on the island until you receive 3 books.\n  - Ordered from best drop rate to worst, kill Anagami, Sakadagami or Sotapanna.\n  - The 3 book names are:\n    - The Path of the Dragon\n    - The Path of the Monk\n    - The Path of the Elemental\n  - Pick up some spirit dragon charms because you will need 1-2 later. (Note: Ensure to have toggled off your spirit imp destroy option)","Return to Ling."],"t":"Creatures of Aminishi"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter The Well of Spirits on the middle tier to travel to the spirit realm.","Head south-west and talk to Yulong on the shore. He is exactly where you would find Ling outside the spirit realm. {Chat: Any}","Return to Ling."],"t":"Spirit realm"}]},"Stellar Born":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the crashed star west of the Piscatoris Fishing Colony. {Chat: Accept}","Mine the crashed star and finish the dialogue."],"t":"Mysterious star found"},{"n":"152 cosmic runes, 52 astral runes and a Wizard Blizzard (or its premade version).","r":"","s":["Go to the south side of the floor 3 of the Wizard's Tower and talk to Wizard Rosalina. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Stellar Born'. > Any > Any}",": Players can quickly teleport to her with stardust.","Return to the crashed star west of Piscatoris.","Talk to Wizard Rosalina to hand her your cosmic and astral runes and the Wizard Blizzard drink. Finish the cutscene.","Head to the desert goebie camp, north-west of Menaphos.",": Players can use Leela's favour to get to the Merchant District (option 2) and exit through the north Menaphos gate.","Talk to Wizard Chambers. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Stellar Born'.}","Return to the Piscatoris crash site and talk to Wizard Chambers or Wizard Rosalina.","Talk to them again.","Shoo away fireflies to keep them away from the crashed star until the portal progress at the top of your screen reaches 50.","Talk to them again."],"t":"Sending Zoob back"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to Zolarea with the portal.","Unequip any items in your main/off-hand slots and jump the rocky edge to the east.","Fly to the large island to the east and jump to the rocky edge to land.",": Players can Surge and Dive during flight.","Head to the giant crystal towards the centre and talk to Wizard Rosalina. {Chat: Any}","Jump the rocky edge on the northernmost side of the main island.","Head to the north-easternmost island and inspect the mysterious decay.","Return to the main island and then inspect the mysterious decay south of the rocky edge and west of the flower patch.","Attempt to enter the cave entrance to the west of the giant crystal. (1/12)","Head to the south side of the main island and inspect the mysterious decay (2/12), then talk to Rox. (3/12)","Head west to the southernmost house and lift the woven rug, then talk to Nuub. (4/12)","Talk to Blip near Wizard Rosalina. (5/12)","Talk to Wizard Rosalina. {Chat: 1 I found some information... > 2 Parts of the planet are dying. > 1 There is a cave in the center of the planet. > 3 The cave is where the elder star sprites go to die. > 1 The cave is where their power source can be found.}",": If the necessary chat options display \"???\", you missed a clue.",": If done correctly, you receive a wrinkly scroll."],"t":"Exploring the homeland of star sprites"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the observatory west of Tree Gnome Village and north of Castle Wars.",": The fastest teleport is 'Chipped' Watchtower teleport made by Dave's spellbook.",": See other ways of getting there.","Climb the rope outside the north side of the observatory, then go up the stairs.","Talk to the Observatory professor on the floor 2. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Stellar Born'.}","After the cutscene, return to Zolarea via the portal at the crash site west of Piscatoris.","Talk to Wizard Rosalina in the centre of the island.","Enter the cave entrance to the west.","Talk to Wizard Rosalina.","Exit the cave.","Gather the dark star wisps that have appeared. Wisps are visible on the minimap as a yellow dot:\n  - A bit north of the cave, west of the mysterious decay. (1/5)\n  - Jump the rocky edge to the north and gather the wisp on the small, north-north-western island. (2/5)\n  - Return to the east side of the main island and gather the wisp near the meteorites. (The mining symbol on your minimap) (3/5)\n  - Go to the south side of the island and gather the wisp near the rocky edge. (4/5)\n  - Jump the rocky edge to the south and gather the wisp on the south-easternmost island. (5/5)","Return to the cave and talk to Wizard Rosalina. {Chat: 1 Could we sacrifice a star sprite? > 2 Could we sacrifice Blip? > 3 Could I sacrifice myself? > 4 Could we sacrifice you?}","Select the star sprites in the following order:\n  - Wave 1: Glorp, Bop, Rox\n  - Wave 2: Zag, Fuz, Nuub, Zorb\n  - Wave 3: Zig, Eetee, Bop, Eetee, Glorp","Exit the cave and talk to Wizard Rosalina in the centre. {Chat: 1 Yes please!}","Talk to Wizard Rosalina back at the crash site.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Playing around dark star"}]},"Stolen Hearts":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ozan in the Draynor Village, just south of the potter, north of the water pump, west of the wheat field. {Chat: Accept}","In the house to the west, open the trapdoor. {Chat: 3 Let me in or I'll poke your eyes out!}","Talk to Khnum. {Chat: Any > Any > Any > Any > 1 Tell me what jobs you have in the works.}","If you have any followers, dismiss them now.","Talk to Ozan. {Chat: 1 How do we find the HQ? > 1 Yes.}"],"t":"The Skulls"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Follow Khnum. Ozan will warn of getting too close or too far.","Open the door Khnum went through.","Talk to Khnum. {Chat: 1 I'll beat the truth out of him! > 1 How about some sort of truth serum? > 2 I'll lock you up and throw away the key.}"],"t":"The headquarters and the jail"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head south of the old jail, towards the shoreline, past the pale wisps.","Talk to a skulls mercenary or Mercenary Joe. Mercenaries will begin to attack you.","Kill the mercenaries and pick up the ransom note.","Talk to Leela and remember the passphrase she gives you as this is needed later.","Agree to travel with Ozan to Al Kharid. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Lady Keli kidnapping Prince Ali"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Home Teleport to Al Kharid lodestone.\n  - If you have the lodestone unlocked, you should Home Teleport so Ozan follows you.","Head south into the Al Kharid palace and talk to the palace guard.","Head northeast of Al Kharid to the Dommik's Crafting Store."],"t":"Getting into Al Kharid palace"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb up the steps inside.","Climb the ladder.\n  - If there is no ladder you should need to talk to the guard in the palace again.","Walk across the plank to the south.","Slide down the awning to the south.","Head inside the room to the north","Walk across the washing line to west.","Climb the ladder to the west.","Cross the planks to the west.","Head west and climb the ladder.","Jump from the scaffold to the west.","Climb down the rug to the south.","Swing across the wooden frame to the west.","Jump from the scaffold to the south.","Bounce on the awning south.","Climb up the brickwork.","\"Leave it to Ozan\" on the flagpole","Shimmy across the rope.","\"Climb up\" the brickwork to activate a cutscene.","After the cutscene, climb up the brickwork.","Head south and \"break in\" through the skylight. Don't log out once inside, or you will respawn outside the palace."],"t":"Parkour"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Inspect the Het scales.","You have exactly two weighings to determine which is the heaviest weight.\n  - The heaviest weight will always be random.\n  - Drag two sets of three weights onto both sides of the scale and click the central green gem to weigh.\n  - If one of the sides is heavier, you know the heaviest weight is part of the 3 weights that went down. Put one of those weights on the left side and one weight on the right side of the scale, the last one in the bottom row and click the green gem again. If either side went down you know the heaviest weight. If they are equal you know it's the one you put back in the bottom row.\n  - If both sides were of equal weight, you know the remaining 3 weights in the bottom row are the heaviest. Put one of those weights on the left side and one weight on the right side of the scale, the last one in the bottom row and click the green gem again. If either side went down you know the heaviest weight. If they are equal you know it's the one you put back in the bottom row.\n  - Once you've determined the heaviest weight drag it onto the backpack icon to grab it.","\"Place weight\" on the Kharid-ib display.","Tell Osman the passphrase that was obtained from Leela. If you don't remember it, try all options as if you get it wrong enough times Ozan will say the passphrase anyway.","During the cutscene, choose either option. {Chat: Any}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Weight on Kharid-ib"}]},"Succession":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Adrasteia in the throne room on the floor of the White Knights' Castle. {Chat: Accept > 1 Yes. > 4 Let's continue our journey.}"],"t":"Investigation time"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the Varrock Dig Site and enter ancient door leading to Senntisten. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Discover the large footprint downstairs. All discoverable entities in this quest should be marked by a red dot on your minimap. (1/5)","Go up the stairs.","Discover one of the bodies of demon cultists. (2/5)","Discover scratch marks. (3/5)","Discover ancient Zarosian architecture. (4/5)","Discover note from a worker in the western room along the southern part of the building where the wall is crumbled. (5/5)","(You must dismiss followers for the following steps. Talk to Adrasteia again to continue.)","Talk to one of the Khazard guards.","Reset the puzzle with one of the long chests. {Chat: 1 Reset to starting position.}","Reset the puzzle with one of the long chests again. {Chat: 1 Reset to starting position.}","Reset the puzzle with one of the long chests once more. {Chat: 2 Skip this puzzle (2 attempts). > 1 Yes, I'm ready to move on. > 4 Let's continue our journey.}"],"t":"Clues in the prison"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to Menaphos and enter the Grand Library. {Chat: 1 Succession. > 1 Yes.}","Talk to Adrasteia in the library. {Chat: 3 Farewell.}","Discover The Corruption on the first level from top, near the south-eastern corner. (1/3)","Discover The Secret Chamber opposite The Corruption, in the south-western corner. (2/3)","Discover The Living Dead on the bottom level, near the north-eastern corner. (3/3) {Chat: 1 Travel to the Magister's chamber (0/3).}"],"t":"=Grand library clues="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Discover the imbued bones on the western side of the chamber. (1/3)","Discover the fragments of an obelisk next to the soul obelisk. (2/3)","Touch the soul obelisk.","Climb the stairs.","Discover the magical residue. (3/3) {Chat: 1 Travel to the Soul Altar. (0/3).}"],"t":"=The Magister's chamber clues="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Discover the scorch marks. (1/3)","Discover the Soul Altar. (2/3)","Talk to Ka. (3/3)"],"t":"=Soul altar clues="},{"n":"No items equipped or in backpack and no follower","r":"","s":["You must dismiss followers and have no items for the following steps. Talk to Adrasteia again to continue or bank items.","Defeat the Magister. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm ready to move on. > 4 Let's continue our journey.}\n  - All prayers are disabled. Use abilities in order to win the fight.\n  - If you die, you will be teleported to Menaphos gate. Enter the gate to return to the quest. {Chat: 1 Yes.}\n  - If you fail to defeat him twice, there will be an option to skip the combat phase. {Chat: 2 Yes, and skip this combat encounter (2 attempts).}"],"t":"Vengeance and the Magister"},{"n":"13 free backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Talk to Adrasteia in the throne room on the floor of the White Knights' Castle. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 4 Never mind. > 1 Yes.}","Mine the argonlike rocks for 28 argonlike ore north-east of Fort Forinthry. {Chat: 4 Let's continue our journey}","Smelt at the furnace in the eastern ruins. {Chat: 4 Let's continue our journey}","Smith at the anvil in the building west of the Mage Arena.","Talk to Adrasteia."],"t":"Preparing disguise in the Wilderness"},{"n":"Argonlike battleaxe, argonlike boots, argonlike full helm, argonlike gauntlets, argonlike kiteshield, argonlike platebody, and argonlike platelegs equipped, no other items equipped or in backpack, and no follower","r":"","s":["Wear or wield all the needed items.","Talk to Adrasteia the Forgotten to the south-east up the stairs leading up to the Mage Arena. {Chat: 1 Yes, enter the Mage Arena.}","(You must have no additional items for the following steps. If you do, you can deposit them through the dialogue.)","Talk to Vengeance. {Chat: 3 I wait for orders. > 1 I chase after them. > 3 I refuse. > 1 I'm ready}","Defeat the 3 waves of enemies.\n  - You can use prayers. It is recommended to use magic protection prayers in waves 1, 2 and melee protection in wave 3.\n  - After each enemy is defeated, restore your health with the health orbs.\n  - If you fail a wave two times, the wave can be skipped to continue. {Chat: 2 Yes, and skip this combat encounter (2 attempts).}","Discover the scuff marks. (1/4)","Eavesdrop the defeated forgotten mage in the north. (2/4)","Discover the scorch mark. (3/4)","Eavesdrop the defeated forgotten mage in the south. (4/4). Then talk to Adrasteia.","Talk to Kolodion.","Exit the Mage Arena. {Chat: 1 Yes, search the caves beneath the Mage Arena.}"],"t":"Mage Arena"},{"n":"Argonlike battleaxe, argonlike boots, argonlike full helm, argonlike gauntlets, argonlike kiteshield, argonlike platebody, and argonlike platelegs equipped, no other items equipped or in backpack, and no follower","r":"","s":["Inspect the modified ritual marker.","Take the rune pouch.","Search the rune pouch in your backpack.","Take the white dust and choose the option empty rune pouch.","Use the one measly fire rune on a sharp rock.","Talk to Adrasteia {Chat: 2 [Show an item in your backpack to Adrasteia.]} and choose the option inert fire rune fragments.","Use the pouch of white dust on the sparkling pool to the south.","Sabotage the modified ritual marker and choose the option volatile fire rune fragments.","Conceal the blatantly sabotaged ritual marker and choose the option soggy pouch of grey paste.","Step into the sparkling pool. {Chat: 1 Exit the cave and return to the deep Wilderness. > 3 [Say nothing]}"],"t":"Ritual marker"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Adrasteia. {Chat: 2 I have the seating plan > 1 The Asgarnian Ambassador > 3 The Kandarian Ambassador > 4 The Menaphite Ambassador > 2 The Misthalinian Ambassador > Any > 1 Yes}"],"t":"Seating plan"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["(Cutscenes appear between the following steps. Clicking out of the dialogue after any of the cutscenes will cause you to rewatch the cutscenes. This will be a roughly 7 minute process.)","Kill 10 forgotten warriors.\n  - Use the abilities via the interface at the top of the screen. Make frequent use of the Blast ability ([3]) to kill multiple enemies around you.","Kill 20 more forgotten warriors."],"t":"The coronation and usurpation"},{"n":"Two free backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Continue dialogue with Adrasteia.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Summer's End":{"sections":[{"n":"Jennica's ring, a ghostspeak amulet, a pickaxe, summoning pouches made from blue charms, and high-healing food (monkfish or better)","r":"","s":["Equip your ghost speak amulet and Talk to Summer at the Wilderness wall, north-east of Varrock. {Chat: Accept}","Stand on the white portal. {Chat: any}","After the dialogue, equip and right-click operate Jennica's ring while standing on the portal to return to the real world.","Run northwest, past the dead trees to the dungeon, right-click and collapse the entrance.","Go back to the ruins and operate Jennica's ring while standing on the white portal to return to the spirit realm.","Run north and lure the beast to the entrance with your blue charm familiar. Enter the cave before it has a chance to consume your familiar. {Chat: 1 Yes, I am.}"],"t":"Luring the beast"},{"n":"Jennica's ring, ghostspeak amulet, food, multiple backpack space (at least 5 recommended), hatchet (best you can use), full prayer points for the final phase","r":"","s":["Avoid the beast's ranged attacks by moving away from the missiles.","Chop roots along the walls to obtain cursed willow logs. You will need 15 in total.\n  - (Optional) Right-click use an extra log on the middle fire pit, and then lure the Beast behind it to avoid attacks while cutting the remaining logs.","Right-click use 5 logs on one of the fire pits and then light it.\n  - Do not light other fire pits during cutscene.","Repeat for a total of three fire pits.\n  - If you die during the encounter your progress will be saved but unlit logs will be cleared.","(Optional) Restock your food and return to Summer to continue."],"t":"Inside the cave"},{"n":"Jennica's ring, ghostspeak amulet, food, energy potions and variants","r":"","s":["Enter the next room by going through the passage in the south-east corner. {Chat: 1 Yes, I know what to do.}","Avoid the missiles like before.","Soon a dark core will appear, dig soft soil and lure the core into the hole.\n  - The core may take several minutes to appear.\n  - Alternatively, rotate in a circle around the room digging.","Repeat this 3 times until you receive a cutscene.\n  - If you die during this encounter, your progress is saved after each trapping."],"t":"The dark core"},{"n":"Jennica's ring, ghostspeak amulet, full prayer points, and food","r":"","s":["Enter the next room by going through the passage to the east. {Chat: 1 Yes, I am ready.}","Take note of which grave the yellow spirit enters.","Wait for the Beast to charge a yellow attack and bless the grave marker.\n  - Blessing a grave consumes prayer points, which may be replenished at the altar in the room.","Repeat for the red and blue spirit."],"t":"The coloured graves"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the spirits {Chat: 1 Alright, I'll come with you.} then once outside, talk again.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Swan Song":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Herman Caranos outside the Piscatoris Fishing Colony (fairy ring code AKQ or memory strand teleport, then run northeast). {Chat: 1 What's the rush? > 1 Do you need any help? > Accept}}}"],"t":"Trollish"},{"n":"5 blood runes, 10 mist runes, 10 lava runes","r":"","s":["Talk to the Wise Old Man in Draynor. {Chat: 1 Would you like to go on a quest?}"],"t":"The Wise Old Man"},{"n":"Combat gear and food","r":"Bring the supplies for the next section to save a trip","s":["Head back to the Piscatoris Colony. Talk to the Wise Old Man. {Chat: 1 I'm ready to fight.}","Kill the sea trolls and open the colony gate.","Talk to Herman in the eastern building."],"t":"Battle at the colony"},{"n":"5 iron bars, 1 log","r":"Cooking gauntlets","s":["Talk to Franklin Caranos near the entrance.","In the building directly north of Franklin, use a log on the firebox, then light the firebox by clicking on it.\n  - Logs and iron ores can be obtained just outside of the colony. The firebox is the metal box on the east side of the metal press.","Use 5 iron bars on the Metal Press to get 5 iron sheets.","Use the iron sheets on the broken colony walls to the west.","Talk to Franklin.","Right-click on Arnold Lydspor in the bank to talk to him.","Catch at least five fresh monkfish to the northwest. You'll be attacked by sea trolls when fishing. This can take up to 10 minutes depending on your Fishing level.","Cook the monkfish in the kitchen southwest. You will need to turn in five fresh monkfish; if any are burned, fish for more. To cook them, just use them on the range and don't proceed on Make-X interface.","Talk to Arnold."],"t":"Repairing the colony"},{"n":"1 pot, 1 pot lid, 7 bones","r":"Bring the supplies for the next section to save a trip","s":["Talk to the Wise Old Man and Herman (furthest building to the east). {Chat: 2 Something else.}","Talk to Wizard Frumscone in the basement of the Wizards' Guild in Yanille. {Chat: 2 I'll see what the necromancer needs me to do.}\n  - Fetch the required supplies now, if you haven't already.","Talk to Malignius Mortifer northwest of Port Sarim near the crossroads. {Chat: 2 I need help with saving a fishing colony.}","Talk to any Almost Master Crafter inside the Crafting Guild until one talks to you about crafting pot lids.","Talk to Malignius Mortifer, he will teleport you to the colony, so gear up before speaking with him. {Chat: 2 I've spoken to the master crafter...}"],"t":"Raising an army"},{"n":"","r":"Combat gear and food","s":["Talk to Herman. {Chat: 1 I'm ready. Let's fight!}","Kill the Sea Troll Queen.\n  - Banks recover health rapidly, and while the bank isn't functional until quest completion, you can run into the building and next to the banker to recover health.","Talk to Herman.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The final battle"}]},"Swept Away":{"sections":[{"n":"1 backpack space","r":"","s":["Talk to Maggie who is located just west of the Draynor lodestone. {Chat: 1 Oo, something smells rather...interesting! > 1 Is there any way I could help? > Accept > 1 Sure, I can do that for you.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Betty in furthest north-western house in Port Sarim. {Chat: 1 Talk to Betty about Swept Away.}","Enter the trapdoor in the south-east corner of the house.","Talk to Lottie. {Chat: 2 I need to retrieve Betty's wand.}","Complete the puzzle.\n  - Put the blackbird in the holding pen.\n  - Put the rat in the blackbird pen.\n  - Put the spider in the spiders pen.\n  - Put the lizard in the reptiles pen.\n  - Put the rat in the rat pen.\n  - Put the blackbird in the blackbird pen.","Open and search the chest near the ladder you came from.","Climb up the ladder and talk to Betty. {Chat: 1 Talk to Betty about Swept Away.}"],"t":"Betty"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to Rimmington (run southwest from Betty's shop in Port Sarim).","Talk to Hetty. {Chat: 2 Talk about Swept Away.}","Enter the trapdoor just south of her house.","Talk to Gus. {Chat: 1 It's a deal.}","Take from the crate that's labelled \"Newts and Toads\".","Place the label of the creature you removed on that box.","If you placed the \"Newts\" label previously, place the \"Toads\" label on the \"Newts\" crate. Otherwise place the \"Newts\" label on the \"Toads\" crate.","Place the remaining label on the last box and talk to Gus.","Take a newt from the newt crate.","Talk to Hetty. {Chat: 2 Talk about Swept Away.}","Use the ointment on the broom."],"t":"Hetty"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Aggie in Draynor Village. {Chat: 2 Talk about Swept Away. > 1 Yes, I'm ready to go now.} You will get teleported to a new area.","Talk to Aggie again.","Complete the puzzle.","Talk to Aggie {Chat: 3 I'd like to go back to Draynor, please.}"],"t":"Aggie"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Maggie. {Chat: 1 I have good news for you. > 1 Of course I could.}","Stir the cauldron with the broomstick.","Talk to Maggie. {Chat: 1 I've stirred the cauldron for you.}","Quest complete!\n  - If drinking the Goulash after the quest, you may want to disable the setting that destroys empty bowls when eating."],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Tai Bwo Wannai Trio":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Timfraku located upstairs in the house northwest of Tai Bwo Wannai. {Chat: Any > 3 Trufitus sent me. > 1 Your gratitude is all I deserve. > Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the lake south of Tai Bwo Wannai and fish 23 raw karambwanji (just north of fairy ring code ckr).","North of the Karamja lodestone, talk to Lubufu. {Chat: 1 I wasn't going anywhere...}","Talk to him again. {Chat: 1 Talk about him... > 3 What do you do? > 3 What do you use for bait? > 1 Talk about him... > 3 What do you do? > 4 I could help collect the bait. > 1 You sound like you could do with the help.}","Talk to Lubufu to give him 20 raw karambwanji.","Talk to Lubufu 3 more times as follows\n  - Talk to him again. {Chat: 2 What do you do with your Karambwan?}\n  - Talk again. {Chat: 3 What do you use to catch Karambwan?}\n  - Talk a third time. {Chat: 4 What does Karambwan taste like? > 1 Yes!}","Drop the karambwan vessel and talk to him to get a second vessel, then pick up the first. {Chat: 3 Actually, I've lost my Karambwan vessel. > Any}\n  - Optional: Use 1 raw karambwanji on a karambwan vessel, then fish at the spot next to Lubufu (requires Fishing) to complete a Medium Karamja achievement.","Use another karambwanji on a vessel and keep it for the next step."],"t":"Lubufu"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the north-east coast of Karamja, across the river and talk to Tiadeche (fairy ring code dkp). {Chat: 3 Is there anything I can do to help?}","Use the loaded vessel on him. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Head south, kill a jogre and take its bones.","Go to Musa Point and buy one Karamjan rum from the pub. You can also buy rum from the Dead Man's Chest in Brimhaven. The rum will break if you teleport with it in your inventory. It will be stolen by a monkey if you ride the cart to Shilo Village with it in your inventory.","Pick a banana or buy one from the traders at the Brimhaven dock, cut it for slices.","Use a banana slice on the Karamjan rum - you can now teleport without having the rum disappear from your inventory."],"t":"Tiadeche"},{"n":"Spear (iron or better), Agility potion (4), raw karambwan","r":"","s":["Take some seaweed near the shore of Cairn Isle (fairy ring code ckr).","Chop nearby dead trees to get 2 logs to light (or go to the fire south of Tai Bwo Wannai).","Use the Karambwan (not the Karambwanji) on the fire; select the option poison karambwan.","Grind the poison karambwan to make Karambwan paste (poison).","Right-click use the paste on your spear to poison it.","Talk to Tamayu southeast of Tai Bwo Wannai, near the mining area.","Talk to him again. {Chat: 3 When will you succeed? > 1 Yes}","After the cutscene, use the poisoned spear and agility potion (4) on him. {Chat: 1 Yes, you can keep it forever.}","Talk to him again. {Chat: 3 Take me on your next hunt for the Shaikahan.}","Kill a nearby monkey, take its corpse, then use it on Tamayu to skin it.}}"],"t":"Tamayu and the Shaikahan"},{"n":"Jogre bones, Karamjan rum with banana slices in it, logs, monkey skin, seaweed, raw karambwanji, karambwan vessel","r":"","s":["Go to Cairn Isle (fairy ring code ckr), climb the rocks and cross the bridge. The surge ability can be used to bypass the agility check for the bridge.","Talk to Tinsay.","Give him the Karamjan rum. {Chat: 1 Yes.}\n  - Use banana slices on the Karamjan rum first if you did not in the previous section.","Use seaweed on the monkey skin, then give it to him. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Right-click light the jogre bones. (Use a furnace if not level 30 in Firemaking.)","Grind your last raw karambwanji (the fish, not the octopus) into paste.\n  - If there is no more raw karambwanji in your inventory, fish for more in the lake northeast of Cairn Isle.","Pick up the burnt jogre bones once the fire dies, then use the green paste on it.","Light a log fire, then right-click use the pasty bones on the fire to cook it.","Give him the marinated jogre bones. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Use a karambwan vessel on Tinsay so that he gives you a crafting manual.\n  - If he will not take the Vessel go back to Tiadeche and use a loaded Vessel, one with a Karambwanji inside of it. After successfully catching a Karambwan, Tiadeche will ask you to take a Vessel to Tinsay to study. Tiadeche will keep the Vessel you give him so you will need to obtain a new one before returning to Tinsay."],"t":"Tinsay"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Tiadeche to give him the crafting manual (fairy ring dkp).","Return to Timfraku at the quest start. {Chat: 4 Eternal gratitude accepted.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing"}]},"Tales of Nomad (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the River of Noumenon by passing through the door behind Death in Death's office. {Chat: 1 River Noumenon.}","Approach the Sinister figure on the west side at the bottom of the stairs, then sift through Nomad's memory.","In each of the following locations, in order, \"Sift through\", \"End\" and then \"Witness\" the memory and receive the text saying where the next memory is.","Once there is text overlaid on your screen, you can click away and move on to the next memory","Return to the start point of the miniquest, and talk to the Sinister figure.","Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Visiting the memories of Nomad"}]},"Tales of Pride":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["During June, talk to the Curator north of the Burthorpe lodestone about \"diverse stories\" for a collection of stories, which can be collected in any order. {Chat: 1 Talk about diverse stories.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go north of Anachronia base camp towards the entrance to the Effigy Incubator.","Pick up Vicendithas's journal from the ground and read it to add it to a collection of stories.","Go to where the Stormbreaker ship is in Varrock Dig Site.","Pick up Vicendithas's journal from the ground and read it to add it to a collection of stories."],"t":"Ace at anthropology"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel to the teleporter of Armadyl's Tower northwest of the Port Sarim lodestone.","Pick up a well-loved letter next to the teleporter and read it to add it to the journal."],"t":"Love letter"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to Edgeville, and climb the ladder to the floor 2 of the house north of the Edgeville bank.","Talk to either of the characters and see what's upsetting Annette. {Chat: 2 [See what's upsetting Annette]}"],"t":"Family matters"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go north-east of the World Gate to find Angof and a list of names.","Pick up the book and read it to add it to the journal.","Go to player-owned house portal in Taverley to find Angof and a list of names.","Pick up the book outside the Pick and Lute and read it to add it to the journal."],"t":"What's in a name?"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to Taverley, upstairs in the Pikkupstix's Summoning Shop.","Talk to Achietties or Runestax."],"t":"A thoughtful gift"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the eastern side of Draynor Manor grounds.","Pick up Greg's journal from near a tombstone and read it to add it to the journal."],"t":"Good dogs"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to Lumbridge Castle and climb down the trapdoor in the castle kitchen.","Pick up Zanik's journal just to the north and read it to add it to the journal."],"t":"Butterflies"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to the Curator north of the Burthorpe lodestone and talk about \"diverse stories\". {Chat: 1 Talk about diverse stories.}"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Tales of the God Wars (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to The Curator at the Heart of Gielinor, north of the Agility Pyramid (fairy code DLQ and run southwest). {Chat: Accept > 2 [Continue...] > 4 [More...] > 3 Goodbye.} Make sure to have at least 4 open inventory spots.","Be sure to bring the chapters with you to fill them.","For chapter #1, collect 20 memory fragments (the green orbs) at the incandescent wisp Divination colony, south of the Poison Waste in Isafdar, west of Castle Wars (fairy code BKP and run west). This will grant 250 Divination XP each, 5,000 Divination XP in total.","For chapter #2, use the empty chapter on the Barrows reward chest. This step will grant you 5,000 Summoning XP.","For chapter #3, kill 40 Zamorak creatures in the God Wars Dungeon to gain access to K'ril Tsutsaroth (killcount is not required if Totem of Intimidation is active on Anachronia, or if you have unlocked War's Blessing 2). Kill K'ril Tsutsaroth once at the God Wars Dungeon (practice or hard mode also count).","For chapter #4, kill 20 each of young grotworms, grotworms, and mature grotworms in any order at the Grotworm Lair, the entrance of which is at the White Knight Camp, west of Port Sarim. This step will grant you 5,000 Slayer XP.","Return to the Heart of Gielinor.","Read the floating tome to deposit the chapters. {Chat: 2 Add the chapters to the tome.}","Read the tome again and select the final memory; watch the cutscene. You do not have to watch the other memories to complete the miniquest, but you have to watch them if you want to unlock the music tracks for the Music Maestro achievement. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 4 [More...] > 2 Final memory.}","Talk to The Curator.","Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Curating the tales"}]},"Tears of Guthix (quest)":{"sections":[{"n":"Oil-filled bullseye lantern, cut sapphire, rope (if this is your first visit to Lumbridge Swamp Caves)","r":"Spiny helmet/slayer helmet or food","s":["Use a cut sapphire on an oil filled bullseye lantern.","Light the sapphire lantern.","Travel to the dark hole under tree slightly north west of the water altar in Lumbridge Swamp.","Climb down the hole to access Lumbridge Swamp Caves.\n  - If this is your first visit, Use the rope on the tree.\n  - Recommended: Equip a spiny helmet/slayer helmet to negate damage from wall beasts, or use a movement ability like Surge or Dive to prevent the wall beasts from attacking.","Run to the south east end of the cavern.","Jump-across the stepping stone to the south (see shortcut icon on the map shown)","Enter the tunnel."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Dismiss all followers and un-equip items held in hand.","On the north side of the cavern near the entrance, Right-click travel across cavern on a light creature.","Mine one of the rocks.","Jump the cliff to the east.","Run north and talk to Juna {Chat: 1 Okay... > Accept}\n  - If you've already completed The Chosen Commander. {Chat: 4 So I'm an enemy of the gods now? > ~ > 1 Okay... > Accept}\n  - If you completed World Wakes {Chat: 2 I'd like to talk about something else. > 1 Okay... > Accept}","Craft the magic stone into a stone bowl.","Talk to Juna again.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Travelling with light creature"}]},"Temple of Ikov":{"sections":[{"n":"A light source and less than 4.5 of weight","r":"","s":["Talk to Lucien in or around the bar north of Ardougne Castle. He will give you a pendant of Lucien.{Chat: 1 I'm a mighty hero! > 2 That sounds like a laugh! > Accept}","Bank all items not needed for the quest until your weight is less than 4.5.","With a light source and the pendant of Lucien, go to the Temple of Ikov, which is located north-east of the Ardougne lodestone.","Go down the ladder.","If you don't have boots of lightness:\n  - Inside the temple, run west and down the stairs.\n  - Cut through the web in the north-east corner and take the boots of lightness.\n  - Go back upstairs","Equip the boots and the pendant of Lucien. Check that your weight is now 0 or less.","Enter the north gate.","Take the bridge across the lava and pick up the lever located in the southern part of the room, in front of the crates.","Near where you first entered the dungeon, use the lever on the lever bracket, which is mounted on the wall just west of the ladder returning to the surface. You must complete the dialogue, or the lever will not be placed.","Pull the lever."],"t":"Inside the temple"},{"n":"bow, 20 limpwurt root, Pendant of Lucien, light source","r":"","s":["Go through the south gate, and loot the chests in the tunnel for ice arrows. After looting the arrows from a chest, the next set of arrows will spawn in another random chest and it is possible they will spawn in the same chest that you just searched. You will only need a couple of arrows. You can just go back and search the chests again, as the respawn/refresh rate is quite quick (no need to hop worlds).","With 20 limpwurt roots and your bow, return to the main chamber with the bridge. Continue north past the trapdoor to the lever on the wall.","Right-click the lever and select Search for traps, then pull it.","Run west and open the wooden door","Open the next door and kill the fire warrior that appears with ice arrows.","Talk to Winelda, and ask to be teleported across the lava. She will ask for 20 limpwurt roots. {Chat: 3 Yes I do!}","(Optional) Take the shiny key in the south-west part with the lesser demons to be able to access this area more easily from McGrubor's Wood. If you have completed One Small Favour this key can be added to your steel key ring.}}"],"t":"Ice arrows"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Heading north, push through the wall to enter the room full of Armadyl guardians.","Remove your pendant and talk to a guardian. {Chat: 1 I seek the Staff of Armadyl. > 1 Lucien will give me a grand reward for it! > 3 You're right, it's time for my yearly bath. > 1 Ok! I'll help!}","West of the Grand Exchange, go inside a small building. (A few tiles south of fairy ring dkr)","Equip the Armadyl pendant and kill Lucien.","Quest complete!"],"t":"If siding with the guardians (recommended)"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the large room to the north through the wall.","Go to the small sub-room in the corner.","Try to take the staff from table, kill any guardians if they stop you until the staff is acquired.","Go inside the shed building west of the Grand Exchange. (A few tiles south of fairy ring dkr)","Hand the staff to Lucien. {Chat: 1 Yes! Here it is.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"If siding with Lucien"}]},"That Old Black Magic":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"That Old Black Magic: Flesh and Bone":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Zommy 'Brains' Walker (red pin on map to the right) at the centre of the City of Um, behind Death, to accept the subquest.","Head north-east to talk to the Former Master Crafter (blue pin on map to the right). {Chat: 1 Ask about piano keys.}","Talk to him to give him 520 bone runes and 360 flesh runes. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 Yes.}","Take the white and black piano keys from the Former Master Crafter and return to Zommy.","Give Zommy the piano keys. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Subquest complete!"],"t":"Delivering the keys"}]},"That Old Black Magic: Hermy and Bass":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Lady Grey about the drummer. {Chat: ? Drummer.}","Kill Hermod, the Spirit of War until you receive animated drumsticks.\n  - Requires 65 Necromancy and completion of The Spirit of War.","Return to Lady Grey. {Chat: ? Drummer.}","Talk to the The Spirit of Rhythm.","Unequip items from both hand slots and talk to Ed. {Chat: 1 Take a boat out onto the lake.}\n  - He's in the boat rental shop east of the northernmost docks.","Manifest the animated drumsticks and a splash will appear at the location of a lost drum. Refer to the location maps below.","Continue to manifest the animated drumsticks until you have found all four drums.","Return to the bandstand and talk to the The Spirit of Rhythm."],"t":"The drummer"}]},"That Old Black Magic: My One and Only Lute":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Lady Grey, behind Death in the City of Um and agree to get her guitar back. {Chat: Accept}","Travel to Lumbridge Catacombs.","At the end of the catacombs, kill Dragith Nurn using necromancy and pick up Lady Grey's guitar.","Return to the City of Um and speak to Lady Grey. Hand her the guitar. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 Trumpeter. > 4 None right now.}","Subquest complete!"],"t":"Help the band"}]},"That Old Black Magic: Skelly By Everlight":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to 'No Gums' Murray in the City of Um's bandstand, behind Death, next to Lady Grey. {Chat: Accept}\n  - If Murray doesn't show up, perform any ritual using a Speed alteration glyph, Speed I, Speed II, or Speed III. Then, return and talk to him.","Talk to 'No Gums' Murray and attempt to give him the restored Everlight trumpet.\n  - If you don't have a restored Everlight trumpet, excavate amphitheatre debris in the Everlight Dig Site to obtain an Everlight trumpet (damaged) (or obtain it from any other source) and restore it.","Perform ensoul trumpet ritual at the Um ritual site.","Take 'No Gums' Murray's trumpet from the ritual chest.","Return to 'No Gums' Murray and talk to him. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Subquest complete!"],"t":"'No Gums' Murray"}]},"The Blood Pact":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Start the quest by talking to Xenia in the Lumbridge graveyard. {Chat: 1 What help do you need? > 1 I'll help you. > Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the catacombs.","After a cutscene, proceed north. {Chat: 4 I can handle this.}\n  - Talk to Xenia if there is no dialogue.","Defeat Kayle then talk to him. {Chat: 2 Yes. Now die!}","Take his chargebow.\n  - (Optional) Equip it if you don't have any Magic, Ranged, or Necromancy weapon.","Head west, open the tomb door, and then go through it.","Defeat Caitlin.","Go south and operate the winch.","Talk to Caitlin. {Chat: 2 Time for you to die!}","Take her staff.","Go down one of the stairs to the west. {Chat: Any}","Defeat Reese and talk to him. {Chat: 2 Time for you to die!}","Untie Ilona. {Chat: 1 Yes, rescue Ilona.}"],"t":"The dungeon"},{"n":"At least 1 backpack space if you picked up all weapons previously","r":"","s":["A cutscene will occur. {Chat: 1 I'm ready for my reward.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"The Branches of Darkmeyer":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Veliaf Hurtz in the Burgh de Rott pub's basement. {Chat: 1 What's wrong? > 1 Is there anything I can do to help? > Accept > 1 Okay, I'll go.}","South of the Burgh de Rott bank, enter the cave entrance.","Take the letter on the floor.","Search the coffin for a mysterious medallion (deals small amount of damage). {Chat: 1}","Climb the rope to leave the cave and return to Veliaf Hurtz. {Chat: 1 I found a medallion. > 1 Yes, please send me!}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Once teleported, head to the northernmost room. The medallion can also teleport you to the Meiyerditch laboratory.","Talk to Safalaan. {Chat: 2 What do you think of this medallion? > 2 What have the vampyres been doing? > 1 I've got a letter for you. > 1 What do you think? > 1 What do you think we should do? > 1 Of course.}"],"t":"An unexpected help"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Exit the base, go through the wall to the north and climb up the stairs.","Jump the floorboards to the west and go down the ladder.","Open the door, then go west a bit, then south to the building with the fireplace.","Enter the building and climb up the ladder, where you will briefly be held up by two vyrewatch.","Now jump over the wall to the building to the west and climb down the ladder.","Open the door, exit and close the door.","Now go north and west around the next building. Enter it and go east, where Vertida will be standing and talk to him.","Climb the wall and speak to Mekritus A'hara.","Stand on the lookout point for a cutscene.","Drop-down the floorboards to the east.","Talk to Nessie who is in the courtyard south of the building. {Chat: 1 How do you know my name? > 1 What are you doing here?}"],"t":"Traversing Meiyerditch"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Attack Vanescula Drakan - she will knock you back (if she does not knock you back, dismiss any active conjured spirits, unequip any armour, and climb up and back down the wall to the east, then try talking to her again).","Talk to her and exhaust all options, eventually learning about the tree and receiving an envelope. {Chat: 1 What are you doing here? > 1 How can you help? > 3 I'm not telling you anything, vampyre scum! > 2 How do you plan on freeing Meiyerditch? > 3 You won't get any information out of me. > 1 Why do you want to kill Drakan? > 3 Why should I trust you? > 1 I'll listen, for now. > 3 Tell me more about this tree. > 1 How do I know you are telling the truth?}","Teleport to Meiyerditch with the medallion {Chat: 2 Meiyerditch} and take the envelope to Safalaan.","In the same room, talk to Vertida Sefalatis. {Chat: 1 What do I need to go to Darkmeyer?}","Head to the most south-western point within the Meiyerditch hideout. Search the crate for 30 smoke bombs.","With your medallion, teleport to the Meiyerditch laboratory. {Chat: 3 Meiyerditch Laboratories}","Go up the stairs, open the door, go through the slashed tapestry, and then out of the building.","Run north and squeeze-through the grate on the north wall.","Talk to Vanescula on the other side of the grate. {Chat: 1 What did you tell Safalaan? > 1 So, where's this tree? > 1 Yes > 2 I'll get on with it, then.} In Darkmeyer, the vyrewatch will attack you when you pass them as opposed to in Meiyerditch.","Use the smoke bombs to avoid being caught by vampyre juvinates. Do not go near vyrewatch.","Search chests inside buildings to find clothing (four pieces in total). You can use another smoke bomb before the previous one dissipates. Enter a building before your smoke shroud vanishes. Once in a building, immediately close the door.","Fix all four pieces and wear them. You no longer need to hide in smoke.","Return to Vanescula. {Chat: 1 So can I go and get those logs now? > 1 No, of course not.}"],"t":"Entering Darkmeyer"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Walk up the ramp to the north-east to enter the floor 1 level of the city.","Talk to Sanguinus Varnis at the top of the ramp, telling him your vampyre name. {Chat: any > any}","Completing vampyric tasks below increases your rating. After completing enough tasks in the middle tier of the city, your rating bar will be half full, allowing progression into the next tier of the city.","Talk to the Vyrewatch guard in the north-eastern jail."],"t":"Gaining Status"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Complete any of the following tasks until you reach a half-full rating bar and access to the upper tier (proceed to next section).\n  - Terrorising Maria Gadderanks {Chat: 1 Quiet, rat. > 1 What a shame. I'm going to be back later for a tithe.}, {Chat: 1 Enough, vermin! > 1 He's dead.}, {Chat: 1 Silence, wretch! > 1 Perhaps we need to 'dispose' of this one.}\n  - Use the Angry or Laugh emotes several times next to Maria Gadderanks\n  - Talk to Maria while wielding the Gadderhammer\n  - Talk to Valentina Kaust {Chat: 1 Ok}, drink the vial of blood she gives you (if you are prepared to be damaged for half of your health) {Chat: 1 Yes}, and then use either chat option.\n  - Vandalise the four posters (after getting the task by speaking with Sanguinus Varnis), shown as purple squares on the image, and then report back to Sanguinus Varnis again.\n  - Recapture six bloodveld younglings (after talking to Grigan Kaninus {Chat: 1 Perhaps I could help you get them back?}). These vanish for long periods of time, so they can appear in places you've already checked. They are displayed as yellow dots on the minimap.\n  - Talking to Sentinel Draemus, Sentinel Gorthaur, or Sentinel Mortshade about citizens in Meiyerditch, the Myreque, and Burgh de Rott (three conversations)."],"t":"Middle tier"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Killing Captured Meiyerditch citizens for the Vyrewatch guards is the fastest way to fill the reputation bar, as each kill gives 2 reputation but there is a limit to how many you can kill in a short period of time. There are about a dozen locked in the jail and they respawn fairly quick. Start the task by talking to a Vyrewatch guard in the south-western jail. {Chat: 1 Yes! > 1 Ok.}","Entertaining Misdrievus Vakan {Chat: 1 What do I need to do?} then approach the nearby blood tither {Chat: 1 Punch the blood tither}. Talk to Misdrievus Vakan again and then enter the building to the west for a cutscene. {Chat: 2 No, I didn't see anything! > 1 I think he deserves to die.}","Speaking to Vanescula Drakan to pledge allegiance to the Drakan family. {Chat: 1 How do I do that? > 1 I pledge fealty to the Drakan family. > 1 I devote my service, land an power to the Drakan before me.}","Talking to Sentinel Bloodmortis, Sentinel Noctantine, or Sentinel Plaguemanst about Vanstrom Klause {Chat: 3 He should be killed.} and Lord Drakan {Chat: 1 I think he should be removed from power.} (two conversations)."],"t":"Upper tier"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After gaining enough status in the upper tier, talk to Vanescula about entering the Arboretum. {Chat: 1 I'll be off to the Arboretum, then.}","Enter the Arboretum (Ranis will stop you). {Chat: 1 Of course not! > 1 I hereby pledge fealty to you, Ranis Drakan.}\n  - Arboretum is a big temple-like building to the east","Proceed to enter the Arboretum.","Solve the four puzzles:\n  - Check the health of the tree for the orb pattern.\n  - Pull the lever (along the eastern edge) to start the first puzzle.\n  - Rotating the orbs by clicking the left-bottom orb of a group of four orbs.\n  - Match the orbs to the puzzle solution.\n  - When the puzzle is complete, pull the lever.","Check the health of the tree again. Repeat the process for all four puzzles.","Chop the tree for three blisterwood logs and a cutscene will play.","In the entrance room to the west, talk to Vanescula to be teleported to out of Darkmeyer. {Chat: 1 But the vampyres will be furious! You've betrayed us!}"],"t":"The Arboretum"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use the medallion to go to Meiyerditch. {Chat: 3 Meiyerditch}","Talk to Vertida Sefalatis. {Chat: 1 I managed to get some logs from the blisterwood tree. > 1 We may be able to trust her, yes. > 1 I'd be happy to dispatch one of the Myreque's most fearsome opponents.}","Talk to Vertida again for a bottle of holy water.","Talk to Kael Forshaw for two silver sickles. {Chat: 1 Do you have any sickles I could use? > 2 That's all, thanks.}","Use the medallion to teleport back to Darkmeyer. {Chat: 4 Darkmeyer}. This will complete the achievement On Wings Of Bling.","Craft each of the logs into a staff, a polearm, and a set of stakes. Remember to set the quantity to 1 in the Build-X interface or you will lose the logs permanently. Fletching the blisterwood polearm leads to the achievement Raising The Stakes.\n  - If you forgot to cut three logs, you can enter Arboretum without any issues and cut some more.","Bank at the Darkmeyer Treasury. The bottle of holy water is required for the fights with Vanstrom Klause and Harold.","Enter the house with Harold in it (just north-east of the captured citizens) and kill him with any weapon. You must throw the bottle of holy water over him to be able to kill him.","Go back to the bank and prepare for the final fight with Vanstrom Klause who is east of Harold."],"t":"Preparing for the fight"},{"n":"Equip full Darkmeyer disguise, Vertida's bottle of holy water, and a blisterwood weapon of choice","r":"Combat armour, prayer potions, stat-boosting potions, and legacy combat mode","s":["Only blisterwood weaponry can deal damage.","If you're attacking at a distance use Deflect/Protect from Magic; otherwise, Deflect/Protect from Melee.","If he shouts \"Stare into the darkness!\" run to the edge of the arena and rotate your camera away from him. Maximum 4000 damage.","If he shouts \"Let the blood consume you!\" run away from the blood splodge on the floor. Maximum 6000 damage.","If he shouts \"Come, fiends, and aid your master!\" kill the two easy minions that he spawns.","If he throws blood bombs towards you, keep running around the room to avoid them. Maximum 4000 damage per bomb.","Once he is very low health he turns into a cloud. Keep using holy water near him until he loses all health. Unequip your ring of life if you're wearing one.\n  - If you are saved by a ring of life after a group of bloodveld guardians spawn, heal up and return without a ring of life. You will be damaged, but in a safe way. You will not have to redo the fight.","Use Deflect/Protect from Magic for this last part as Vanstom can do rapid magic damage to you whilst he is dying."],"t":"The battle with Vanstrom"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take control of Vanescula and kill the Bloodveld guardians. It is recommended to use the Shriek attack repeatedly as soon as it recharges.","When you awaken, speak with Vertida {Chat: 1 What happened? > 1 Vanstrom believed that Safalaan may be the Icyene blood.}, and watch a short cutscene.","Teleport to Burgh de Rott with the medallion {Chat: 2 Burgh de Rott} and talk to Veliaf Hurtz. {Chat: 1 Vanstrom is dead!}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up in Darkmeyer"}]},"The Brink of Extinction":{"sections":[{"n":"4 free backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Speak to TzHaar-Mej-Ak or TzHaar-Mej-Jeh in the main plaza of TzHaar City. {Chat: Accept}","Run east through the arch. A cutscene will begin.","Run north-east to the Birthing Pool and speak to TzHaar-Mej-Het. {Chat: 4 I require TokKul. > 1 That's the TokKul I'm looking for!}","Run around the wall to where the Fight Kiln entrance is, and mine the Statue of TzHaar-Ket-Teg.","Run south-west to the TzHaar City entrance. Mine the nearby Statue of TzHaar-Xil-Kal.","Return to the main plaza. Melt the two stacks of fragments into TokKul with the furnace slightly south-east of the main plaza.","Speak to TzHaar-Mej-Ak or TzHaar-Mej-Jeh again. {Chat: 5 Goodbye.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"Communication orb","r":"","s":["Go to the entrance to the Library, north-west of the main plaza and speak to Ga'al. {Chat: Any}","Run south until you reach the cooking icon on the minimap. Speak to the next Ga'al. {Chat: Any}","Continue south along the eastern wall to the southwest corner of the city (east of the TzHaar City mine), and speak to the final Ga'al. {Chat: Any}","Return to the main plaza and speak to TzHaar-Mej-Ak or TzHaar-Mej-Jeh again.","Enter the Fight Kiln entrance east of Main Plaza. {Chat: 1 'The Brink of Extinction'.}","A cutscene plays. {Chat: 1 We have to take the risk. Reforge the Ga'al in the Kiln.}","Run to the easternmost part of TzHaar City, where a cave entrance is. The entrance is not clickable until after you interact with the orb, cave entrance is indicated on your map.","Activate the communication orb in your backpack. {Chat: 1 TokKul of TzHaar-Mej-Gek.}","Enter the cave."],"t":"The Ga'al"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill the 4 Tz-Kih.","Pick up the mace, sword and knife.","Put the mace on the western and the sword on the eastern scales.","Go through the ancient gate."],"t":"Room 1"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill the 2 Tz-Kek.","Kill the Tz-Kih and Tok-Xil","Move the statues such that TzHaar-Mej faces TzHaar-Ket, who faces TzHaar-Xil, who faces TzHaar-Mej. This involves a triangle formed by Xil and Mej (parallel) to the south and Ket to the north. If it doesn't work, make the triangle smaller.","Go through the ancient gate."],"t":"Room 2"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Turn off Auto-retaliate so your character does not inadvertently step on a glowing square when running to attack a monster (they deal 1000+ damage per second).","Pass the hot vent door to the east.","Avoid standing on glowing floor squares.","Kill the 2 TokHaar-Kets and 2 TokHaar-Hurs.","Kill the 3 TokHaar-Xils.","Kill the TokHaar-Ket Champion and pick up the obsidian maul it drops.","Pass back through the hot vent door.","Place the maul on the scales.","Go through the ancient gate."],"t":"Room 3"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill the 4 Tz-Kils.","Pick up each of the obsidian weapons: throwing ring, sword, mace and staff.","Place each of the obsidian weapons on the scales according to their location:","Go through the Ancient gate."],"t":"Room 4"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill the 3 Tz-Kihs.","Kill the 2 Tz-Kils and Yt-MejKot.","Touch one of the pedestals.","Touch the pedestals in the order that they light up until the puzzle is complete. There are 8 combinations you will need to complete correctly.\n  - Recommended to give each pedestal a number between 1-4. Write the number of the last pedestal that lights up each round in your chatbox, forming a list. When touching pedestals, simply follow the numbers in your chatbox.","Go through the Ancient gate."],"t":"Room 5"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Turn off Auto-retaliate so your character does not inadvertently step on a glowing square when running to attack a monster (they deal 1000+ damage per second).","Pass the hot vent door to the east.","Avoid standing on glowing floor squares.","Kill the 4 TokHaar-Hurs.","Kill the 2 TokHaar-Xils.","Kill the 2 TokHaar-Mejs.","Kill the 2 TokHaar-Ket Champions and pick up the obsidian maul dropped.","Pass back through the Hot vent door.","Place the maul on the scales.","Go through the ancient gate."],"t":"Room 6"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill the 3 Tz-Keks.","Pick up the sword, maul, mace, knife and staff.","Inspect each scale for the TzHaar word. Use the correct obsidian weapon on each scale according to the table below:","Go through the ancient gate."],"t":"Room 7"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill the 3 Tz-Kils.","Kill the Ket-Zek and 2 Tz-Keks.","Rotate the tiles on the ground to form the TzHaar symbol.","Go through the Ancient gate."],"t":"Room 8"},{"n":"","r":"In Legacy Mode, bring a weapon with more than one special attack (dragon dagger recommended).","s":["Pass the hot vent door to the east.","Talk to Ga'al-Xox. {Chat: Any}","Rotate the eastern valve.","Kill TokHaar-Hok.\n  - You cannot teleport out or leave the fight early.\n  - Pray Deflect/Protection from Melee the entire fight.\n  - Avoid standing on glowing floor squares, as always.\n  - You do not need to kill the spawned enemies - higher level players may focus on TokHaar-Hok. When he is defeated, the spawned enemies will die.\n  - Stun TokHaar-Hok once he has lost half his health, this prevents him from healing at the flowing lava.\n    - The stun mechanic may be bugged and you may only be able to use basic Ranged ability, Binding Shot, the basic Magic ability, Impact and the Magic threshold ability, Asphyxiate, and the basic melee ability, Backhand.\n    - In Legacy Mode, you need to stun him with a special attack."],"t":"Room 9"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to TokHaar-Hok.","Talk to Ga'al-Xox. {Chat: Any}","Talk to Ga'al-Xox again. {Chat: 5 Farewell.}","Return to the city through the door. Activate your communication orb.\n  - If you have destroyed your communication orb, talk to either TzHaar-Mej-Ak or TzHaar-Mej-Jeh in the main plaza of TzHaar City.","Go back to the Fight Kiln entrance. {Chat: 1 'The Brink of Extinction'}","A cutscene ensues. {Chat: 1 I can't wait to battle the TokHaar. > Any}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"The Chosen Commander":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Captain Undak, east of the bank (by the eastern water fountain) in Dorgesh-Kaan. (You must dismiss any follower or pet you have or he will not go with you.) {Chat: 2 Can I help with anything? > 1 Yes. > 2 Okay. What's your point? > Accept}","Climb the nearby stairs (north) and talk to Mernik in the nursery. She is the adult in the building.","Talk to Torzek outside. {Chat: 4 Calm down. I'm here to help. > 1 Have the children eaten anything unusual lately? > 1 What did they have?}","Talk to any nearby child against the building wall about what they ate.\n  - Andil: {Chat: ? What food did you eat yesterday?} The chat options may vary from person to person.\n  - Delgon: {Chat: 1 What food did you have yesterday?}\n  - Gerdi: {Chat: 1 What food did you eat yesterday?}","Talk to Captain Undak. {Chat: 3 I've worked out which foods are poisoned.} (If you are unable to talk with Captain Undak, make sure you do not have \"Hide Familiar options\" checked under Settings>Combat & Action Bar>Choose Option Menu and log out and back in)","Go down the stairs and head south to the market.","Talk to Markog, at the south-eastern-most stall of the market. {Chat: 1 Which merchants have you bought ingredients from?}","Talk to Turgok, at the south-western-most stall of the market. {Chat: 1 Which merchants have you bought ingredients from?}","Talk to Merchant Walton, just outside of the market to the south-east. {Chat: 1 This is the one, Captain. > 1 Yes, I'm sure. > 3 [Attack the merchant] > 1 What's that behind you?}","Proceed to kill the merchant (cannot be ranged)."],"t":"Food poisoning"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Zanik. {Chat: Any > Any > 1 Yes! What happened?}","Climb on the goblin south-west of the bowl statue.","Jump on statues to reach the statue holding the bowl of water.\n  - If the jump-on option does not appear, try clicking on the head.","Continue jumping north and take the crossbow from the ledge.","Grapple the spear of the north-eastern statue and take the pendant.","Look into the bowl.","Enter the western portal (the statues will move out of the way) for a cutscene.","Continue conversation with Zanik. {Chat: 1 Let's go.}"],"t":"Zanik"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["With Zanik following, go to the north end of Dorgesh-Kaan and up the northern most set of stairs.","Watch the cutscene. {Chat: Any > 3 Zanik is right. You should kill him. > 1 She means well. > Any}","Continue conversation with Captain Undak. {Chat: 1 Where should I look? > 4 I'll start looking now.}","Run south of the city, up and over staircases until you reach the agility course. Bring a light source.","Descend the ladder top and head all the way south.","Talk to Zanik. {Chat: 4 [Sit down next to Zanik.] > 4 [Say nothing.] > 4 [Say nothing.] > 4 [Say nothing.] > 2 Yes, but you should have respected the council. > Any > 4 What do you wish had happened? > 1 Someday, we'll build that world.}","Watch the cutscene. {Chat: Any > 3 I have nothing else to say.}","After the cutscene talk to Zanik. {Chat: 4 Goodbye, Zanik.}","Talk to Captain Undak for a set of H.A.M. robes. {Chat: 1 What is this task? > 1 I'll do it.}","Prepare for battle, but only wear the H.A.M. robes."],"t":"The council"},{"n":"Full H.A.M. robe outfit","r":"","s":["Enter the H.A.M. Hideout in Lumbridge forest.","Talk to Johanhus Ulsbrecht in the centremost of the three southern rooms. {Chat: 3 What are you planning to do about the cave goblins? > 3 Isn't Sigmund working with you any more? > 3 How can I find Sigmund's base? > 1 I'll go there now.}\n  - Before you do, make sure to wear all of the H.A.M. robes","Talk to Milton in the windmill near the Fishing Guild, north of the Ardougne lodestone. {Chat: 2 I want to get in to Sigmund's base. > 1 Arrav.}","Climb down the ladder inside the windmill.","Run directly east through the door, continuing east through stacks of crates.","Talk to the guard next to the prison. {Chat: 1 I need to see the prisoner. > 1 Letter? > 3 What day is it today? > 3 Never mind.}","Enter the main area (back through the doors to the west) and pickpocket Sam.","Return to the prison guard. {Chat: 1 I have my letter here.}","Enter the prison and take the key, open the gate.","Escape with Grubfoot:\n  - Talk to the prisoner, Grubfoot. {Chat: 4 Wait there. I'll come back for you.}\n  - Run into the kitchen, squeeze through the hole.\n  - Open 1 of the 2 doors.\n  - Go back through and open the other door as well.\n  - Return to Grubfoot. {Chat: 1 Let's go > 3 I'll distract the guard so you can make a break for it.}\n  - Stand north of the guard, talk to him to face you and have his back turned. After selecting the chat option, do not continue the conversation until Grubfoot walks past the guard into the next room. {Chat: Any}\n  - Talk to Grubfoot in the next room. {Chat: 2 Wait at the west door; I'll distract the guard.}\n  - Squeeze into the kitchen. Take the dirty plates from the sink, and wait for the H.A.M. guard to come talk to you. {Chat: 1 Yes. > Any}\n  - Talk to Grubfoot in the bedroom. {Chat: 1 Follow me.}\n  - Exit the east door and run to the big doors north. {Chat: 1 Let's get out of here.}","Watch the cutscene and wait for Sigmund to confront you. {Chat: 3 Time for you to die!}","Kill Sigmund. {Chat: Any}\n  - If Zanik doesn't attack Sigmund, climb up the ladder, then back down.","Kill Zanik repeatedly. {Chat: 1 I won't kill you, Zanik. > 3 Zanik! What's happened to you? > 3 Does our friendship mean nothing to you? > 1 But am I *your* enemy? > 2 Zanik, you're being controlled. Fight it! > 3 Zanik, it's the pendant. Take it off! > 2 You've got to do it, otherwise it will win!}\n  - Turn off revolution in combat settings and avoid using bleeds and channelled abilities as they cancel the dialogue forcing you to repeat the phase.\n  - If revolution was left on and dialogue interrupted, run up and then down the ladder to the west to avoid having to fight again.}}"],"t":"Beef with H.A.M."},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Run west for an earthquake.","Right click Clear the fallen rocks.","Talk to Zanik. {Chat: 4 Try grappling across with your crossbow. > 1 I can see somewhere it could catch. > 2 Right a bit. > 2 Right a bit. > 1 You've overshot. Go left. > 1 It's alright, Zanik. You can do it. > 1 Just a bit further left. > 1 I'm not leaving you, Zanik.}","Go through the cave and talk to Juna.","Run north-west to exit the cave.","Go over the stepping stones and run directly north.","Squeeze through the hole.\n  - If you don't have the shortcut unlocked, you'll have to go all the way around towards Lumbridge Castle's Cellar.\n  - If at any point Zanik stops following you, she can be found back at Juna.","Right click Follow Kazgar. {Chat: 1 Dorgeshuun Mines}"],"t":"Lumbridge caves"},{"n":"2 backpack spaces, light source","r":"","s":["Enter Dorgesh-Kaan and talk to Captain Undak north of the market (between the fountains). {Chat: 4 What can I do? > 4 Goodbye.}","Climb the northern stairs for a cutscene (close the Bandos's Ultimatum screen that pops up). {Chat: Any}","Climb back up the stairs, talk to the Goblin scribe. {Chat: 1 What do you want me to do? > 2 I'll help you. > 1 I'll go now.}","Climb down the stairs and run south-east through a corridor (near the quest start point).","Talk to Tegdak in the north-east room of the floor 1. {Chat: 2 The scribe sent me to get a box of artefacts.}","Return to the Goblin scribe upstairs. {Chat: 1 Here it is. > 1 I'll go now.}","Exit the city through the bone door north-east, downstairs.","Talk to Mistag. {Chat: 1 Could you bury this time capsule?}"],"t":"Time capsule"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to the city and talk to Oldak north of the bank. {Chat: 1 What are you arguing about? > Any > 1 What do you want me to do? > 1 I'll go now.}\n  - {Chat: 2 No - talk about quest or other things.} if invention has been unlocked.","Return to the agility course (south end of Dorgesh-Kaan) - do not climb down the ladder.","Run east to the power station and climb down the stairs.","Talk to Turgall, make sure you have at least 2 free inventory spots . {Chat: 2 Oldak needs a pair of energy projectors and a focusing chamber.}","Talk to Oldak, now south-east of the market. {Chat: 1 I have the parts here.}","Talk to Zanik. {Chat: 1 Oldak has modified your crossbow. > 1 Oldak said it was certain to work. > 3 I'll talk to you later.}","Talk to Mernik in the children's nursery north-east upstairs. {Chat: 1 What can I do? > 1 I'll talk to him.}","Talk to Ambassador Alvijar in the house north-west of the nursery. {Chat: 2 I want to talk about the children. > 1 You coward!}","Return to Mernik. {Chat: 1 I talked to him... He said no. > 1 Nothing. Everything is fine.}"],"t":"Preparing for battle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Prepare to fight enemies weak to magic.","Talk to Zanik, south-east of the market. {Chat: 2 I'm ready now.}","Defeat the Bandos avatar. {Chat: 4 We'll see about that. Zanik - now!}","Pick up all 4 parts of the crossbow while killing statues.","Use the crossbow pieces on each other. {Chat: 5 Enough talk.}","Kill the avatar again. {Chat: 4 [Use Zanik's crossbow's special attack.]}","Take the avatar's pendant.","Talk to Zanik. {Chat: 4 [Sit down next to Zanik.] > 4 [Say nothing.] > 3 About time you woke up! > 2 We won. Oldak's crossbow worked. > 3 The mark on your forehead is gone. > 3 Here it is.}","Follow Zanik through the portal.","Click the screen to exit cutscene.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Final fight"}]},"The Curse of Arrav":{"sections":[{"n":"Trollheim Teleport or Trollheim tablet or God Wars Dungeon Teleport (or climbing boots if you cannot use the teleports), food and equipment for a level 91 monster, several Mining boosts (if required), 7 backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Talk to Ali the Wise in Nardah (north-most building). {Chat: Accept > 3 Where is the tunnel entrance? > 3 Time for me to go to Trollweiss, then.}\n  - To get there: teleport to fairy ring DLQ and run south.\n  - Or teleport to Al Kharid and go south to Shantay Pass, then take a magic carpet to Nardah.","Head to the snowy area northwest of Trollheim, enter the troll tunnels and head north to go through the tunnels, and then head to the east to Ritual plateau tunnels.\n  - Follow the directions on the map below to get to the Ritual plateau tunnels, or use Trollheim Teleport if you have it. If you travel through Death Plateau or Troll Stronghold, you must bring the climbing boots.\n  - Prepare for combat before going through Trollheim as you don't have any access to bank in there."],"t":"Getting to the tunnels"},{"n":"7 backpack spaces and equipment to fight Arrav","r":"","s":["Navigate through the caves by mining the rubble; some rubble must be mined from multiple sides to clear it.\n  - Optional: pick up the stone, granite, slate, and shale tablets.\n  - Optional: Search the small bookcase for notes (a-j) if you want to give all information to Ali the Wise after the quest is completed. There is no reward for doing so.","Enter the room east of the caves.","Climb the stairs.","Talk to Arrav, who will attack you immediately.\n  - After he starts attacking you, if you do not auto-retaliate, right-click and attack him.","Fight until he teleports away. The fight will pause multiple times for dialogue.","Enter the room to the south and search the tapestry on the west wall for base key and base plans.","Travel back to Nardah and speak to Ali the Wise.","After the cutscene, speak with Ali the Wise again."],"t":"The tunnels"},{"n":"3 dwellberries, a ring of life and 1 backpack space","r":"","s":["Enter the nearby Uzer Mastaba pyramid.\n  - To get there, either run north-east of Ali the Wise, use the nearby magic carpet network to get to Uzer and run south, or teleport to fairy ring DLQ and run east.","Enter the pyramid, head north-west through the imposing doors, then south, down the stairs and talk to Senliten for oil in a canopic jar. {Chat: 1 Talk about Curse of Arrav.}\n  - Players who have completed certain quests can also choose to head directly to the Pharaoh Queen from the pyramid doors.","Use (do not eat) your dwellberries and ring of life on the oil in a canopic jar to obtain a full canopic jar.","Return to Ali the Wise and speak to him.\n  - If Leela is in the mummy's tomb, she can return you outside the Uzer Mastaba {Chat: 3 Return to the surface}."],"t":"Preparing the jar"},{"n":"Insulated boots, either a macaw pouch or a ravenous locust pouch, a method of grappling (either any crossbow and a mithril grapple, or an enhanced grappling hook on your toolbelt), a full canopic jar, the base key, 4 backpack space, and enough summoning points to summon your familiar","r":"","s":["Go to the Varrock Palace and speak to Hartwin (northwest tower, floor 3) to travel to Chaos Temple Dungeon. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Climb down the trapdoor.","Follow the path, opening three doors along the way.","Head east to the room with the range.","Equip your insulated boots then enter the pipe on the south wall of the room.","Run through the sewers and attempt to enter the next pipe.","Summon your familiar, interact with it and choose the remote view option.","Run to the room south of you, search all the tables for decoder strips and notes (k-z).","Right-click pick-lock on the chest to obtain the code key.","Go north to the room east of the pipe and operate the keypad and solve the keypad puzzle:\n  - First read the code key and memorise or write down the letters.\n  - Drag-and-drop strip #1 over the line indicated by the first letter of the code key (A, B, C...).\n  - The strip has a hole that reveals a specific number, this is the first digit of the passcode.\n  - Use the up and down arrows to enter that number, and press the right arrow to move to the next digit.\n  - Repeat this for the other three strips.","Enter the room, equip your crossbow and mithril grapple, then grapple the pipe above you.","Take from the pedestal for a heart in a canopic jar, then teleport out.","Return to Ali the Wise and speak to him.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Saving Arrav's heart"}]},"The Curse of Zaros (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Make sure you are wearing your ring of visibility and your ghostspeak amulet.","Speak to the Mysterious ghost near Glarial's tombstone northwest of the Fishing Guild. {Chat: Accept}","This ghost will give you one of three clues which determine your entire route, which we will label Sequence 1, 2, and 3:\n  - Sequence 1 - He mentions pirates and a shipwreck.\n  - Sequence 2 - He mentions the thief being north-east of there.\n  - Sequence 3 - He mentions the thief being south-east of there."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Make your way and speak to Rennard in the location given in the table above to receive Ghostly gloves. {Chat: 1 Tell me your story}","Make your way and speak to Kharrim in the location given in the table above to receive Ghostly boots. {Chat: 1 Tell me your story}","Make your way and speak to Lennissa in the location given in the table above to receive Ghostly robe bottom. {Chat: 1 Tell me your story}","Make your way and speak to Dhalak in the location given in the table above to receive Ghostly hood. {Chat: 1 Tell me your story}","Make your way and speak to Viggora in the location given in the table above to receive Ghostly cloak. {Chat: 1 Tell me your story}","Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Talking to the ghosts"}]},"The Darkness of Hallowvale":{"sections":[{"n":"2 planks (regular, oak, teak, or mahogany), 8 nails (any type except rune nails)","r":"","s":["Go to Burgh de Rott, then enter in the inn where you will climb over the broken down wall and climb down trapdoor in the northwest of inn.","Talk to Veliaf Hurtz in the Burgh de Rott pub basement. {Chat: 4 Is there something I can do to help you? > Accept > 1 What is the Sanguinesti region? > 2 How can I search for the Sanguinesti order of the Myreque? > 3 Can you tell me about the Sanguinesti Myreque? > 4 Tell me again how to get into the Sanguinesti region. > 5 Ok, thanks.}\n  - Search the chest to the north for garlic if you do not have one.","Run south-east of the pub until you find a boathouse.","Search the boat, then use a plank on it to fix it.","South of the boat, use plank on the boat chute to fix it.","Push the boat down the chute, then go down to the docks and board the boat. If a Vyrewatch stops you at any point, just activate Freedom and walk away.\n  - Keybind may not work, recommended to click the ability on your action bar or in the Defence abilities tab.","Exit the boat by jumping onto the nearby rock, and continue north-west a short distance.","Just before the shore, kick down the floor, and climb down it as shown on the image on the right.","Climb the wall rubble to the north and talk to a Meiyerditch citizen. {Chat: 4 (whisper) Do you know about the Myreque? > 4 (whisper) I really need to meet the Myreque. > 4 How can Old Man Ral help me?}","North of the wall rubble, talk to Old Man Ral ( Taskmaster icon on the map). {Chat: 4 Someone said you could help me. > 4 Old Man Ral, the sage of Sanguinesti.}\n  - (Optional) If you want to reduce detection chance by the Vyrewatch, you can buy a set of Vyrewatch clothing from Trader Sven just south of Old Man Ral before continuing."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the house south-west of Old Man Ral with the door facing north (the western of the two houses with northern doors – it has a sickle next to it on the outside wall). Open the door and enter it.","Climb up the ladder there.","Jump to the floorboards in the south.","Jump to the floorboards in the east.","Go to the north-east corner of the room, push the wall and walk across the floor.","Crawl under the wall to the north.","Go north to the second room, look on the west side, push the wall and walk across the floor.","Climb down the ladder.","Search the table next to the wall, open the trapdoor table, and go through the trapdoor tunnel.","Climb up the shelf next to the sickle logo in the north-west corner of the room.","Crawl under the wall to the east side.","Jump to the floorboards in the east.","Climb down the ladder.","Search the pots near the eastern door to get a key and use it to open the door."],"t":"Sector 1 directions"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb up the ladder in the room to the east, by the sickle.","Jump to the floorboards in the south.","Go east, south, west then climb up the shelf to the south.","Climb up the ladder in the west.","Jump to the floorboards in the south.","Walk a little to the south-west and climb down the ladder once.","Go east through the rooms and walk across the washing line.","Climb down the ladder.","Push the wall to the north and walk across the floor.","Climb up the shelf to the north.","Climb down the shelf in the north-eastern corner.","Jump to the floorboards in the north.","Jump to the floorboards in the north again.","Go to the north end of the house and jump to the floorboards in the east.","Climb up the ladder to the east.","Search the wall to the west to get the ladder top.","Climb down the same ladder, repair the broken ladder going down by using the ladder top from inventory to broken ladder and climb down the ladder."],"t":"Sector 2 directions"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open the door to the east and go northwest outside. Go past the house immediately north of the house you just left and into the house with a door on its east side. You should be in a room that has an unlit fireplace, a portrait, and some sort of wall east of it joined to a room that is a perfect diamond.","Go west through the door into the next room, then north out of the house until you see barricades.","Head east at the sickle logo, past the north side of the house with two buckets. Enter the first door to your south; you should be east of the room with two buckets and north of the diamond room from earlier.","Climb up the ladder.","Jump to the floorboards in the east.","Climb down the stairs.","Go south along the eastern side of the stairs. Attempt to push the wall and choose a knife or a sickle to unlock the latch (tool belt knife works), allowing you to push it open.","Push the decorated wall from the southern side.","Open the lumpy rug on the southeast square in the 4-square pattern of the rug. If you take too long, you will have to push the wall again as the mechanism will quickly reset.","Climb down trapdoor to enter the hideout."],"t":"Sector 3 directions"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Run far north and talk to Vertida. {Chat: 3 What should I do now? > 4 Okay, thanks.}","Take the message back to Veliaf Hurtz who is in the basement of the pub in Burgh de Rott. {Chat: 1 I have a message for you from Vertida! > 3 What do you want me to do? > 4 Okay, thanks.}"],"t":"Myreque meetings"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Drezel in the Mausoleum under the Paterdomus temple west of Canifis. Use CKS or the invitation box to teleport nearby. {Chat: 2 Did you hear the sounds as well? > 5 Okay, thanks.}\n  - If you have destroyed your Temple library key {Chat: 1 Talk about items.}","Take the west exit, past the monuments.","Search the small bush slightly south-east of the western church steps.","Return and talk to Drezel in the Mausoleum. He will give you runes to teleport to Varrock.\n  - Depending on other running quests, you might need to talk to him. {Chat: 2 Talk about something else.}","Talk to King Roald in the Varrock Palace. {Chat: 1 Talk about Darkness of Hallowvale. > 4 What should I do now? > 1 Yes thanks, I'll accept the free teleport.}\n  - You will be teleported back to the Paterdomus."],"t":"Ambush at Paterdomus"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Drezel about what to do next. {Chat: 2 What should I do now? > 3 Okay, thanks.}","Talk to Veliaf Hurtz back in the basement of the pub in Burgh de Rott. {Chat: 1 I was attacked near to Paterdomus! > 2 King Roald cannot send troops! > 3 What should we do now? > 4 Okay, thanks.}","Return to Meiyerditch using the boat in the boathouse south-east and try to get caught by a Vyrewatch. {Chat: 2 Do a bit of menial work}","Mine 15 ore from the walls. (Only requires 1 backpack space as the ores stack)","Use them on a minecart {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll place it all in the cart.}, then talk to a guard.","Run south-east to the house marked on the map (right).","Go south through 3 doors and up the ladder.","Jump the floorboards to the east, descend the stairs and enter the hideout.","Talk to Vertida {Chat: 3 What should I do now? > 2 Okay, lead the way.}\n  - You will be teleported back to sector 1.","Climb down the ladder, open the door, run south and climb over the wall rubble near the shore.","Run south and climb the fallen floorboards back towards the boat and onto the top of the wall.","Run north along the top of the wall and climb down the ladder.","Choose the \"search\" option on the rocky surface.","Open the barricade to the north; then go north, and climb up the ladder.","Keep running north along the wall, over more ladders. Talk to Safalaan at the very end to receive papyrus and charcoal. {Chat: 2 I was attacked near Paterdomus on my travels. > 1 Can I help in some way? > 3 Okay, thanks.}","Run clockwise around the wall until you reach the north wall and see a sickle drawn on the ground.\n  - If playing on high graphics settings, the sickle will be hard to see due to the shadows on the ground. The sickle is located just past where the shadows first appear on the north wall.","Use the papyrus on the charcoal and watch the cutscene.","Go anticlockwise around the wall to a sickle on the west wall, and then one on south wall. Use papyrus on charcoal at each of the symbols.\n  - Western wall\n  - Southern wall","Watch cutscene. Let Vanstrom attack you a bit which will knock you out.","Talk to and finish the dialogue with Sarius if she didn't automatically talk to you when Vanstrom knocked you out. You must talk with Sarius until she disappears, otherwise Safalaan will say your sketches are not genuine in the next step.","After being knocked out, go back to the south wall and finish your final sketch.","Go south back to the ladder and climb down.","Return to the hideout and talk to Safalaan {Chat: 1 I have all the sketches for you! > 4 What should I do now? > 5 Okay, Thanks.}\n  - The quickest way to return is to get noticed by the Vyrewatch, get sent to the mine, and then go southeast to the hideout as before. If you are having trouble getting noticed just log out and log back in."],"t":"Meeting Safalaan Hallow"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Leave the hideout, push the wall, climb the stairs, jump the gap, down the ladder.","Go out the north door, walk slightly west and then south, and open the door to a room with a fireplace. Look at the fireplace.","Choose knife from tool belt option to receive a Message.","Read the message.","Search the portrait on the south wall and slash it with the knife.","Search the portrait again to pick up a large ornate key.","Talk to Safalaan in the base and give him the message. {Chat: 2 I have a message for you Safalaan - it may be important.}","Leave the hideout, push the wall, climb the stairs, jump the gap, down the ladder.","Run north through three doors.","Head to north-east in Meiyerditch (follow the eastern wall north). There is a bright red and yellow tapestry (with a door on the east side of the room).","Look-at the tapestry and slash it with a knife.","Walk-through the slashed tapestry.","Use the large ornate key on the vampyre statue.","Go east through the door, then down the staircase, and telekinetic grab Haemalchemy (Vol. 1).\n  - Runes can be found by searching the broken rune case directly west of the stairs."],"t":"Locating the laboratory"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head back to the Meiyerditch Myreque base:\n  - Go up the staircase, out the door, and through the tapestry.\n  - Run south to the previously marked building through three doors.\n  - Go up the ladder, jump to the east floorboards, down the stairs.\n  - Push the wall, push the decorated wall, open the lumpy rug, and climb down the trap door.","Speak to Safalaan. Be sure he hands you a sealed message and shortcut key, which the key can be added to the key ring after the completion of One Small Favour.","Take the sealed message to Veliaf in the Burgh de Rott cellar. {Chat: 1 I have a message for you from Safalaan.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"The Death of Chivalry":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Sir Owen in the garden north of the Edgeville Monastery. {Chat: 1 The who with the what now? > 1 I guess I have one of those faces. > 1 Saradomin must have had a good reason...}","Talk to Saradomin after the cutscene. {Chat: 1 (Kneel before Saradomin.) > 2 How can I help? > Accept}","Alternatively if aligned with another god. {Chat: 1 (Remain standing.) > Any > Any > Accept}","Pick up the suit of armour just south-west of you and equip it.","Talk to Saradomin. {Chat: 1 Yes, teleport us to the Black Knights' Fortress.}"],"t":"Meeting Saradomin"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open the Portcullis.","Fortress guard: (guaranteed suspicion on first chat option){Chat: Any > 1 He is my prisoner. > 1 No, I have something... special planned for him.}\n  - It is required to dismiss pets and familiars before proceeding.","Head north, to Lieutenant York: {Chat: 2 Are you suggesting I cannot handle a mere knight of Saradomin?}","Head north-west, and climb up staircase. The fortress guard will stop you. {Chat: 1 What do you want, maggot? > 2 This prisoner is to be sacrificed.}","Head to the floor 2 to the south, talk to Hierophant Marius. {Chat: 2 Yes. > 3 I shall return after I deal with this Temple Knight.}","Head south-east of the room, and climb up staircase. The fortress guard will stop you. {Chat: 2 I am bringing him to the tallest tower. > 1 We need him to recover the weapon of power, as you know.}","Go upstairs, head north to Lieutenant Graves. {Chat: 3 Stand aside. I will handle this. > 1 The prisoner stays with me.}","Search the Lieutenant's body, and choose whether you want to kill him or not. It doesn't matter."],"t":"Infiltrating the fortress"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head up the stairs in the north-east to the ritual chamber.","Search the wardrobe for a Letter from Lord Daquarius.","Search the box of candles for three red candles.","Search the shelf for chalk.","Pick up the Grimoire and read it. {Chat: 1 Read the book.}","Use a candle on each stand, and fix the symbol on the floor.","Light the candles.","Use chalk on Ritual circle."],"t":"The marker"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Chant over the north-west candle. {Chat: 3 Arom. > 4 Nahrea. > 2 Imperium.}","Chant over the north-east candle. {Chat: 2 Feritas. > 4 Silenti. > 2 Sepulchrum.}","Chant over the south-east candle. {Chat: 4 Igasac. > 2 Perdimit. > 4 Ebulam.}","Enter the portal. {Chat: 1 Yes, enter the portal.}\n  - You must remove the suit of armour that was equipped at the beginning of the quest."],"t":"The candles"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Defeat the three Black Knights.","Search their bodies for Cage door key.","Unlock the hanging cage to the north, freeing the Damsel.","Talk to Dawn and learn all she knows. {Chat: 1 Where are we? > 2 Who's Saint Elspeth? > 3 How did the Kinshra capture you? > 4 Continue. > 1 Let's take her with us.}","Search the supply crate south of the portal.","Enter the doorway to the east.","Inspect the coffins or the heaps of bones."],"t":"The Saradominist crypt"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open the portcullis to the south.","Search the Black Knight's bodies.","Talk to Fern and defeat her. {Chat: 3 I am ready to be judged. > 1 I fight to protect the innocent. > 2 I'm ready.}\n  - If The Restless Ghost has been completed, {Chat: 4 I am ready to be judged. > 1 I fight to protect the innocent. > 2 I'm ready.}\n  - Dodge her charge ability."],"t":"Fern"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head south, to the Wand of Resurrection.","Solve the puzzle by matching the tiles to lower the barrier.\n  - The image of the completed puzzle is taken with the compass facing south.","Try to take the wand. A chat option appears. Select offer to risk your life. {Chat: 2 I shall sacrifice my own blood. > 1 Yes.}"],"t":"The Wand of Resurrection"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head north. Talk to Dawn. {Chat: 3 Give me the wand or you won't live to regret it. > 2 Continue}","Defeat the Black Knights and Sir Owen.","Go north and open the portcullis.","Kill Dawn. Refer to the full guide if you're having trouble."],"t":"Fighting for the wand"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Search Dawn's body.","Head south, enter the Portcullis and speak with Saradomin. {Chat: 4 I've made my decision. > 2 I will give you the wand. > 2 Were we too late? > Any > 2 Why would you help us? > Any}","When Saradomin asks if the player wants to be teleported back to Edgeville, it is recommended to stay in the tombs, to claim the extra post-quest rewards which require level 40 Strength and two other coffins requiring level 60 and 80 Strength.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Saradomin and the wand"}]},"The Dig Site":{"sections":[{"n":"1 backpack space","r":"","s":["Speak to an examiner in the Exam Centre. {Chat: Accept}\n  - Teleport to the Archaeology Campus by using the archaeology journal and run south-east.","Talk to Seth Minas (site manager) in Archaeology Guild. {Chat: 1 The Dig Site quest.} Make sure you have the unstamped letter otherwise the dialogue with Seth does not progress.","Grab a cup of tea from the desk in the south side of the building. It is behind Acting Guildmaster Reiniger or Drew (depends on your progress). Not required if you have one.","Talk to an examiner in the Exam Centre; you will fail the exam. {Chat: Any > Any > Any}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"Cup of tea}}{{Map:The Dig Site; align=right","r":"","s":["Search the green bushes to the west of the Monolith in the middle of the Archaeology Campus (not the ones to the south, near the fences) until you find a teddy bear.","Take the panning tray from the small building south of the screening station.","Pan the water to the east of where you found the panning tray. Someone will try to stop you. Give him the cup of tea to pan the water. {Chat: 2 So how do I become invited then?}\n  - Pan until you find a special cup.\n  - Pan until you find an uncut opal if you have not already.","Pickpocket the Dig Site workman in the north-east corner of the dig site until you get an animal skull.","Talk to Katarina (student) in the central area of the dig site.","Talk to her again.","Run south-east, talk to Dorian (student).","Talk to him again.","Run west, talk to Eduardo (student) who can be found in the dig spot closest to the well.","Talk to him again."],"t":"Lost and found"},{"n":"Opal","r":"","s":["Return to an examiner. {Chat: 1 Yes, I certainly am. > 1 The study of the earth, its contents and history. > 3 All that have passed the appropriate Earth Sciences exam. > 2 Proper tools must be used.}","Talk to all 3 students again.","Return to an examiner. {Chat: 1 I am ready for the next exam. > 3 Samples taken in rough form; kept only in sealed containers. > 1 Finds must be carefully handled. > 2 Always handle with care; strike cleanly on its cleaving point.}","Talk to all 3 students again.\n  - Katarina will demand an opal (talk to her again). You can obtain this by panning.","Return to an examiner. {Chat: 1 I am ready for the last exam... > 1 Samples cleaned, and carried only in specimen jars. > 1 Brush carefully and slowly using short strokes. > 3 Handle bones very carefully and keep them away from other samples.}","Optional: Give Seth Minas (site manager) the level 1, 2 and 3 certificates to receive a Fruit Blast or a chocolate cake. The Fruit Blast can be saved for the quest Recipe for Disaster: Another Cook's Quest."],"t":"Exams"},{"n":"2 ropes (or pickpocket Dig Site workman until you get enough), specimen jar, specimen brush","r":"","s":["Excavate the area on the ground named level 3 grid (near Dorian at the east digsite, see image) until you find an ancient talisman. It may take over 40 attempts to get it.","Talk to Terry Balando back at the Exam Centre.","Go to the north-eastern winch (a square hole in the ground with a rope going down it), at a dig site north from Dorian. You will also find Elissa wandering nearby and a training grid near the winch.","Operate the winch three times to hand in your invitation, attach a rope, and climb down.","Pick up an arcenia root. One is directly to the east of the rope and another is west of the rope, under a torch on the wall. You may use Area Loot to pick them up.","Search the bricks south-east of the rope. {Chat: Any}","Climb back up, then climb down the winch near Katarina to the southwest.","Talk to Doug Deeping to receive a chest key. {Chat: 4 How could I move a large pile of rocks?}"],"t":"Helping the expert"},{"n":"Chest key, vial, trowel","r":"","s":["Optional: Search the sack for an extra charcoal. Do not grind it. You will need it for Desert Treasure, but cannot get it from here after completing the quest.","Go back to the northeastern winch and climb down, use the key to unlock the chest in the north east room and search it for ammonium nitrate.","Use the trowel on the closed barrel directly east of the chest.","Use a vial on the barrel.","Grind the charcoal.\n  - If you didn't bring charcoal, search the sack of charcoal a few steps north.","Mix the nitroglycerine and ammonium nitrate together, add ground charcoal, then finally add the arcenia root.","Search the bricks to the south and select the compound on the brick.","Search the brick again, select your tinderbox.","Enter the large chamber, take the stone tablet."],"t":"Explosives expert"},{"n":"Stone tablet}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["Use the tablet on Terry Balando in the Exam Centre.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"The Elder Kiln":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to TzHaar-Mej-Jeh at the Birthing Pool in TzHaar City. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Keep the gauge within the two arrows using fire spells to heat it and water spells to cool it until the egg hatches.\n  - The two TzHaar will also fire occasionally. Keep an eye on them as both may shoot fire spells at the egg simultaneously which could result in overheating.","Talk to TzHaar-Mej-Jeh. {Chat: 1 What's a Ga'al? > 2 Why do you do this? > 1 Can't you teach them your ways?}"],"t":"Hatching"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go west to the main plaza and talk to TzHaar-Mej-Ak. {Chat: 1 I've come for that Ga'al. > 1 Yes.}","Kill all enemies in the Fight Pits whilst protecting Ga'al-Jeh.","After the cutscene, kill TzHaar-Ket-Yit'tal."],"t":"In the pits"},{"n":"1 backpack space","r":"","s":["Talk to one of the TzHaar-Mejs. {Chat: 1 It's the remains of your dead that you use as currency. > 2 Of course I'll help the TzHaar. > 2 Okay. > 3 I had better be on my way.}","Head east of the plaza to the kiln.","Enter the cave. {Chat: 2 Yes, follow me.}"],"t":"Path to the kiln"},{"n":"Adamant pickaxe or better (tool belt only works when using a melee weapon), as well as melee, ranged, or magic weapon and armour","r":"","s":["Jump the chasm {Chat: 1 Come on, Xox!} and kill all of the monsters.\n  - Do not use protection prayers until the TokTz-Ket-Dill's shell is broken as this will increase the frequency of making the rocks fall on you, dealing over 1,000 damage.\n  - You need a pickaxe to break the shell of TokTz-Ket-Dill, which is weak against water spell after its shell is broken. Necromancy will not work against him.","Investigate the skeleton at the end of the cavern {Chat: 1 Reach in and take the book.} to receive Journal of Perjour.","Proceed to the next room."],"t":"Room one"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take the TokKul on the ground and kill all of the monsters.","Proceed to the next room."],"t":"Room two"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill all of the monsters and examine the note in the Journal of Perjour (the book which should be in your backpack). {Chat: 2 Read the note.}","For the left scale, use the picture to find its resulting sum and put that much tokkul on it. Repeat for the right scale. A Tzhaar number symbol can be higher than 15 that is shown in the picture of this guide on the right.","Proceed to the next room."],"t":"Room three"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go through the room, jumping over chasms and killing the TokTz-Ket-Dill along the way.","Proceed to the next room."],"t":"Room four"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill the monsters in this room.","Proceed to the next room. {Chat: 1 I'm ready.}}}"],"t":"Room five"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Complete all seven waves of the Kiln.","Talk to TokHaar-Hok. {Chat: 2 Let's see what rock you're forged from, then. > 5 I need your help. > 2 I think he should, so the Ga'al can live good lives.}"],"t":"The elder kiln"},{"n":"2 backpack spaces}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["Proceed back through the caves, ignoring monsters along the way.\n  - Teleporting away and attempting to avoid heading back through the caves will result in the player being forced to return where Ga'al Xox was left at the kiln, then head back through the caves as originally intended.","Return to the centre of the Main Plaza and talk to one of TzHaar-Mejs. {Chat: 1 Even after all we've done, you can't trust the Ga'al? > 2 [Let Ga'al-Xox fight] > 3 I'm only interested in the power of that Kiln.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"The Eyes of Glouphrie":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Brimstail in a cave west of the bank in the Gnome Stronghold (View map). Look for dungeon link on minimap {Chat: 1 What's that cute creature wandering around? > 1 Yes, that sounds fascinating... > 1 Oh, yes I love a bit of History. > Accept}"],"t":"Digression"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Inspect the singing bowl in the western portion of the cave.","To the north, attempt to unlock Oaknock's machine and use Oaknock's exchanger.","Talk to Brimstail. {Chat: 1 I've had a look in the other room now. > 1 Of course, I'd love to!}"],"t":"Elven Mystery"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Hazelmere (island east of Yanille, fairy ring cls) for several cutscenes. He provides you with a violet pentagon.","Return and talk to Brimstail. {Chat: 1 I've visited Hazelmere, he told me all sorts of interesting things.}"],"t":"Memories"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Grind mud rune and use on bucket of sap.","Use the magic glue and a set of maple and oak logs on Oaknock's exchanger and repair it.","Talk to Brimstail. {Chat: 1 I think I've fixed the machine now!}","Talk to him again three or more times to receive more discs {Chat: 1 I can't work out what to do with these discs!}. You will need to drop all of your discs and pick them back up after chatting to receive more discs. The more discs, the more streamlined the process in the next step becomes as you require little to no converting."],"t":"Incapacitated"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Unlock machine to view the desired number.","If necessary, use the exchanger to get a disc equal to your number (refer to conversion chart below, insert not more than 35 points at a time). If you have trouble converting, refer to the full guide here.","Unlock the machine with the correct value disc. Click the small green square to submit the disc.","Unlock the machine again to get 3 different numbers (the second unlock will require many more discs). Use the exchanger as necessary. The second number requires using 2 discs and the third requires 3 discs.","Talk to Brimstail. {Chat: 1 Phew! I've got that machine working now. What do I need to do now?}"],"t":"Machinery"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill the evil creature by Brimstail and talk to him again. (1/6).","Kill the 5 remaining evil creatures, which can be done in any order (View map):\n  - (2/6) By the main gate to the stronghold (south-east from Brimstail's cave)\n  - (3/6) South of the spirit tree by the gnome agility course entrance.\n  - (4/6) In the giant tortoise pen north-west of the Grand Tree and north of the swamp.\n  - (5/6) Top floor of the Grand Tree, next to the small prison/by the ladder (wait for the chat response saying you killed it before using the ladder. If it doesn't count it, an evil creature should respawn at one of the locations.)\n  - (6/6) Near King Narnode (may need ranged, magic or necromancy as it can get stuck behind a trapdoor). Check your quest journal if your chat log does not display 6 creatures, if it says you need to talk to the king then you are finished.","Talk to King Narnode Shareen on the floor 1 of the Grand Tree.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Assassination"}]},"The Feud":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ali Morrisane in Al Kharid. {Chat: 1 If you are, then why are you still selling goods from a stall? > 2 I'd like to help you but.... > Accept > 1 No, I'm really too busy.}\n  - If you do not have desert disguise, {Chat: 1 If you are, then why are you still selling goods from a stall? > 2 I'd like to help you but.... > Accept > 2 Okay.} buy Kharidian headpiece and fake beard from the shop and then use these items on each other."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"3 beer (or 6 coins to buy them from Faisal the Barman)","r":"Coins for magic carpet","s":["Travel to south Pollnivneach (talk to the rug merchant just outside Shantay Pass to get there using a magic carpet).","Head to the local bar.\n  - If you do not have three glasses of beer, talk to Faisal the Barman to buy them. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'd like a drink please.}","Right-click to use three glasses of beer on Jalal the Drunk. Finish the dialogue with each beer.","Talk to a Menaphite Thug, who can be found inside the bar or outside the west side of the bar. Make sure to right-click to avoid attacking him.","Talk to a brigand or bandit in the North Pollnivneach. Again, right-click to talk to him."],"t":"In Pollnivneach"},{"n":"500 coins, bucket (or pick 1 up in Sami the Camel Man's shop)","r":"","s":["Head to the kebab seller north-west of the well in the town centre. The map icon is .","Talk to Isma'il the Kebab seller to buy red hot sauce from him. {Chat: 3 Would you sell me that bottle of special kebab sauce? > 2 No thanks, I'm good.}","In the house immediately to the south-west, talk to Sami the Camel Man to ask for two camels. Offer 500 coins. {Chat: 4 Are those camels around the side for sale? > 2 What price do you want for both of them? > 3 Would 500 gold coins for the pair of them do?}","Use the sauce on a trough in the camel shop.","Pick up the dung with a bucket in the backpack if the dung is brown. If it is green, use more sauce on a trough until it is brown.\n  - 2 empty buckets can be found in the camel shop.\n  - Obtain more buckets of dung if you plan to complete Dealing with Scabaras (1 bucket, does not consume) and My Arm's Big Adventure (3 buckets).","Talk to a brigand to the north to give them one of the receipts.","Talk to a Menaphite Thug to the south to give them the other receipt."],"t":"Trading the camels"},{"n":"10 coins","r":"","s":["Go south-west of Pollnivneach to a big purple tent and talk to Rashid the Operator to join his gang. {Chat: 1 Yes, of course, those bandits should be taught a lesson. > 2 No thanks.}","Attempt to pickpocket a villager. You will fail and take 20 damage.","Talk to Rashid the Operator for advice. {Chat: 1 Yeah, I could do with a bit of advice. > 2 No thanks.}","Talk to the street urchin near the well or the fountain. Pay him ten coins and then pickpocket the villager with an arrow over their head. You will fail again and take 20 damage.","Talk to Rashid the Operator. {Chat: 1 Yeah, I could do with a bit of advice.}","Wield the oak-blackjack.","Lure a villager into a secluded area. Knock out the villager with the blackjack and pickpocket them."],"t":"Pickpocketing villagers"},{"n":"Keys, leather gloves, desert disguise (or Kharidian headpiece and fake beard to make it)","r":"","s":["Talk to Rashid the Operator.","Wear the desert disguise and gloves.","Hide-behind the cactus near the mayor's house next to the fountain.\n  - The disguise and the gloves can be safely unequipped after this step.","Use the keys on the door. If lost, talk to Rashid the Operator for another.","Climb the staircase on the northern side.","Search the landscape picture near the bed.","Move the dial to 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 in that order clockwise. Right-click the dials to help with the numbers. Click the centre square button will reset the mechanism.\n  - 1\n  - 1\n  - 2\n  - 3\n  - 5\n  - 8"],"t":"Mayor's wife's jewels"},{"n":"1 coin, ugthanki dung","r":"","s":["Talk to to Rashid the Operator to give the jewels.","Talk to a Menaphite Thug.","Talk to Rashid the Operator. {Chat: 2 No thanks.}","Talk to Faisal the Barman. {Chat: 3 I'm looking for Traitorous Hesham. > 1 No thanks I'm ok.}","Right-click to talk to Badir the Snake Charmer sitting south of the bar. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Right-click to use the snake charm on a desert snake north of the Menaphite tent and wait until it goes into the snake basket to become a full snake basket.\n  - If Badir the Snake Charmer did not give you a snake basket, it may be in your bank or talk to him again. {Chat: 1 Wow, a snake charmer. Can I have a go? Can I have a go? Please?.}","Talk to Maysa the Hag, in the house north-west of the bar, on the hill.","Talk to Maysa the Hag the second time to give her the full snake basket and ugthanki dung respectively.","Use the Hag's poison on the table in the bar. It is the square one with a glass of beer on it, not the one with the empty beer glass.","Talk to Rashid the Operator."],"t":"The traitor"},{"n":"","r":"Combat equipment","s":["Talk to the Menaphite Leader. Located outside the tent.","Kill the Tough Guy.","Talk to a villager. {Chat: 2 Ok I'll get to it.}","Talk to the Bandit Leader east of the northern magic carpet station. The Bandit Leader will not appear if you did not talk to the villager in the previous step.","Kill the Bandit champion.","Talk to a villager.","Talk to Hakeem the Mayor located next to the well in the middle of the town.","Return to Ali Morrisane in Al Kharid.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Dealing with the thugs"}]},"The Firemaker's Curse":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Phoenix south of Eagles' Peak. {Chat: 1 Travelling firemaker? What does that involve? > 1 This seems dangerous. Why put your lives at risk? > 2 What are you waiting for? > Accept > 1 Yes, let's go.}","Enter the tunnel.}}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Flint for a pitch can. {Chat: 3 That's all, thanks.}","Use the pitch can to light fires by right-clicking make-fire-here to complete the arrow on the ground. If you mess up, you can right-click the fire to stomp it out. You can also drag the pitch can onto an action bar, and use a key-bind to light fires with it. However, this will light a fire one tile in front of you."],"t":"Room 1"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Light the fire pit.","Take the Firemaking journal on the rock. {Chat: 2 What plan?}","Light the fire again. {Chat: 2 What do you want from us?}","Enter the tunnel on the east side of the room. {Chat: 1 We must continue through the caves.}"],"t":"Room 2"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Complete the pattern which is in the shape of a falling boulder.","Avoid falling boulders. Pick-up rocks one at a time, placing them on the rock pile to the east. (Repeat this 6 times)","Climb up the rock pile."],"t":"Room 3"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Light the fire pit.","Take the journal. {Chat: 3 Did you say Zaros? > 1 Were you close to Zaros? > 1 What happened to you?}","Tie-up firemaker on the Column, selecting Twig. {Chat: 3 Twig > 1 Yes!}","Light the fire pit again.","Enter the tunnel to the east."],"t":"Room 4"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Using the bowls of red and yellow powder by the entrance, complete the puzzle.","Immediately after the puzzle, dodge 2 fire walls by standing in the open gaps.","Proceed to the next room north."],"t":"Room 5"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["The lights dim after a short time, dealing 50-100 damage every few seconds. Lighting the fires postpones this effect.\n  - If you come close to dying in this room, you will be rescued by the firemakers and restored to full health. If this happens, any activated pillars will remain activated, but all lit fires will be extinguished. You don't have to relight all the fires.","Complete the puzzle:\n  - Go west, light the fire pit. Push nearby column switch.\n  - Go far east, light the fire pit. Push nearby column switch.\n  - Go back west and north to the centre and jump the pillar east of you. Push the nearby column switch.\n  - Jump the ledge just south-east of you, jump the next ledge east. Light the fire pit.\n  - North of you is the flame switch - loop around by going back west then east and push it.\n  - Head west, light the fire pit then push the switch. Move fast here to avoid being hit by the rocks above you.\n  - Jump back to the centre and push the switch immediately south of you.\n  - Head to the north-west corner and light the fire pit, press the switch just south. Watch out for the falling rocks.","Enter the tunnel in the north-east corner."],"t":"Room 6"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Light the fire and pick up the journal. {Chat: 1 Zamorak! > 2 Yes, he's a terrible, hateful god.}","Tie-up firemaker on the Column, selecting Sera. {Chat: 5 More options > 1 Sera > 1 Yes!}","Light the fire again and proceed to the next room east."],"t":"Room 7"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Complete the puzzle.","Immediately after the puzzle, dodge 4 quicker fire walls by standing in the open gaps.\n  - There might be a bug where 2 firewalls spawn at the same time, leaving no open gaps. A solution might be to stand in the far south-east corner of the room or run around the fire walls.","Proceed to the next room north."],"t":"Room 8"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Light one of the oil pools on the wall.","Avoiding being damaged by the fire balls. You have to hold on to all the waves for about 10 minutes.\n  - You can light the oil pool lines as a barricade.\n  - If you stay in the north-west corner and immediately light the oil pools as soon as they're ready you should stay safe. There is no guarantee however.\n  - If the fire balls start congregating on one side, run to opposite corner, placing a barricade behind you.\n  - Another tactic is to use the option on the oil pools and use \"right\" and \"left\" to perform a clockwise rotation of the edges of the pit.","Proceed to the next room north."],"t":"Room 9"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Light the fire and grab the journal.","Tie up Twig again {Chat: 2 Twig > 1 Yes!} and light the fire.","Proceed to the next room east."],"t":"Room 10"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Complete the puzzle.","Light the fire pit.","Take-torch from the fire pit and continue down the path.","When there are dark tendrils, ward them off at the edge of your screen by clicking on them.\n  - Tendrils may hide behind your interface if you have panels on the edges of your screen. To make the tendrils more visible, right click on World Map and click \"Toggle High Contrast Mode\".","Proceed to the next room at the end of the path."],"t":"Room 11"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Light the fire and take the journal.","Tie-up Emmett {Chat: 3 Emmett > 1 Yes!} and light the fire.","Proceed to the next room east."],"t":"Room 12"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["During this fight, you must fight Char with Necromancy, Magic or Ranged.","Teleport out and prepare for the battle.\n  - Carry an inventory full of food (such as sharks or rocktails).\n  - Carry necromancy, range or a mage weapon.\n  - Do not bring any armour as it has no effect during this battle.\n  - Do not bring a familiar as this might cause the dialogue with Char to be glitched.","Teleport back to Eagles' Peak and run south to the entrance of the cave.","Talk to Flint to get another Pitch can.","Climb down the steps to enter Char's lair.","Take the journal. {Chat: 2 That's a good idea. > Any}","Talk to Char to engage the fight.","During the fight, you should keep a distance from Char at all times.","The amount of damage you deal is determined by the amount of flames you have lit (100 damage per active flame).","As you fight her, keep lighting flames.","Add your pitch can to your ability bar to make fires much more easily.","Run around the edges of the arena lighting flames as fast as you can.","When you have 10 active flames, run some distance from Char and attack her a few times, dealing 1,000-5,000 damage in total.","Repeat steps 1-2 until she is defeated.","Remember to avoid the firewalls by maneuvering through the gaps, or you'll be hit for 1,000-4,000 damage.","While Char is glowing she is invincible, so focus on lighting flames during this period."],"t":"Face-off with Char"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After the battle ends, talk to Char. {Chat: 2 How do we get out?}","There may be a glitch where you cannot finish the dialogue, in this case leave the cave through the southern tunnel and come back in."],"t":"After the battle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Exit through the tunnel to the north.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"The Fremennik Isles":{"sections":[{"n":"Raw tuna, one of either 8 tin ores (level 1-10 Mining), 7 coal (11-54 Mining), or 6 mithril ores (55+ Mining)","r":"","s":["Right click and talk to Mord Gunnars on the northern Rellekka dock about Jatizso's history. {Chat: Accept > 1 Tell me more about Jatizso's history. > 3 Can you ferry me to Jatizso?}","In Jatizso, talk to King Gjuki Sorvott IV in the building with tiled floors.","Give the King a raw tuna or use the tuna on the cat.\n  - Can be obtained from the cage/harpoon fishing spots to the south.","Give the King your ores.\n  - There is a mine down the stairs to the north-west if you didn't bring them.","Open the chest (behind the throne) and take the silly jester outfit. {Chat: 1 Take the silly jester hat. > 1 Take the silly jester top. > 1 Take the silly jester tights.}","Return to Rellekka and Travel-Neitiznot Maria Gunnars."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Equip the silly jester outfit, with nothing in your hands, and talk to Slug Hemligssen, north of the bank. {Chat: 4 Free stuff please. > 1 I am ready.}","Talk to Mawnis Burowgar in the building south of the bank. Dismiss any Summoning familiars and pets.","Use the jester controls to follow Mawnis's instructions.","Return to Slug Hemligssen. {Chat: 1 Yes I have. > 3 They will be ready in two days. > 2 Seventeen militia have been trained. > 1 There are two bridges to repair.}"],"t":"Clowning around"},{"n":"8 split logs, 8 ropes","r":"","s":["Remove the silly jester outfit (keep it for later) and talk to Mawnis Burowgar.","If you don't have 8 ropes:\n  - Kill yaks for 8 yak hair and spin them on the spinning wheel in the southeastern-most house.\n    - Optionally, make an additional rope for later in the quest.\n  - Take three yak-hide for later if you don't already have them.","If you don't have 8 split logs:\n  - Cross the bridge to the north.\n  - Chop 8 arctic pine logs if you don't already have them.\n    - Optionally, chop 2 more for later in the quest. Don't split these 2, keep them whole.\n  - Use logs on the woodcutting stump across the bridge to the north (not a regular tree stump).","Talk to Mawnis Burowgar with the items.","Talk to Thakkrad Sigmundson about the bridges. {Chat: 1 How do I repair these bridges again? > 2 Where do I find these bridges?}","Right click bridges, north of Neitiznot, to repair them.","Talk to Mawnis Burowgar."],"t":"Bridge repairs"},{"n":"1 bronze nails, 2 arctic pine logs, 1 rope, 3 yak-hides, 2 thread, silly jester outfit","r":"","s":["Return to King Gjuki Sorvott IV on Jatizso.","Tax the shop keepers of Jatizso:\n  - Hring Hring must pay 8,000; he is in southwesternmost house. {Chat: 1 But rules are rules. Pay up!}\n  - Skuli Myrka must pay 6,000, north of Hring. {Chat: 1 But, rules are rules. Pay up!}\n  - Vanligga Gastfrihet must pay 5,000, north of the king's palace. {Chat: 2 I suppose I could pay the tax for you.}\n  - Keepa Kettilon must pay 5,000, east from Vanligga. {Chat: 1 But rules are rules. Pay up!}","Return to King Gjuki Sorvott IV.","Tax all bearded people for 1k:\n  - Hring Hring. {Chat: 1 But rules are rules. Pay up!}\n  - Raum Urda-Stein in a house with Hring Hring. {Chat: 1 But rules are rules. Pay up!}\n  - Skuli Myrka, north of Raum and Hring. {Chat: 1 But rules are rules. Pay up!}\n  - Keepa Kettilon, he is in the northeasternmost house. {Chat: 1 But rules are rules. Pay up!}\n  - Flosi Dalksson in a house with Keepa Kettilon. {Chat: 1 But rules are rules. Pay up!}","Return to King Gjuki Sorvott IV.","Return to Rellekka, and take the boat to Neitiznot.","Equip the silly jester outfit and talk to Slug Hemligssen.","Empty your hands and entertain Mawnis Burowgar again.","Talk to Slug Hemligssen. {Chat: 1 Yes, I am. > 2 They are in a secluded bay, near Etceteria. > 1 They will be given some potions. > 3 I have been helping Neitiznot.}","Talk to King Gjuki Sorvott IV in Jatizso.\n  - Make sure King Gjuki Sorvott IV gives you the Royal decree first. You may need to speak with him twice.","Remove the silly jester outfit and talk to Mawnis Burowgar in Neitiznot.","To obtain a yak-hide armour set:\n  - Kill three yaks and give the three yak hides to Thakkrad Sigmundson to tan. {Chat: 1 Cure all my hides.}\n  - Craft the top and legs with thread in the backpack.\n    - Thread can be bought from Jofridr Mordstatter in the building with the bank chests north of Mawnis Burowgar.","Talk to Mawnis Burowgar when you have the yak armour.\n  - Make sure Mawnis mentions \"Fremennik round shield\" in order to craft the shield. You may need to speak with him twice.","To obtain a round shield:\n  - Buy 1 bronze nail from Jofridr in the bank, obtain 1 rope, chop two arctic logs\n  - Take everything to a woodcutting stump and interact with the woodcutting stump to craft the Fremennik round shield.","Talk to Mawnis Burowgar with these items."],"t":"Taxes"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Prepare for battle then enter the Ice Troll Caves to the far east of the northern-most island.\n  - Protect from Ranged is advised. Familiars are not allowed. Equipping the Fremennik round shield drastically reduces Range damage taken from Ice Troll Females. Yak-hide armour drastically reduces Melee damage taken from Ice Troll Males, Runts, and Grunts. If you do not have good Ranged Defence, bring high-healing food. Even with Protect From Ranged active, the trolls quickly deplete your health. The Ice Troll King has a very high defence to ranged, so it is not advised to kill the boss with ranged weapons.\n  - Talk to or right click Request-supplies on Bork Sigmundson for seven Tunas, four 4 dose Strength potions, and two 3 dose Prayer potions if you need supplies. {Chat: 1 Give me food, Bork! > 2 I need Strength potions! > 3 I need Prayer potions!}","Kill 10 ice trolls (killing the trolls by farcasting the ones on the east does not count).\n  - There is a chatbox message saying \"You have defeated enough trolls to attack the King.\"","Cross the bridge, kill and then decapitate the Ice Troll King.","Take the head to Mawnis Burowgar.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The final battle"}]},"The Fremennik Trials":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Brundt the Chieftain in the longhall in Rellekka. {Chat: 3 Do you have any quests? > Accept > 1 I want to become a Fremennik!}\n  - If Mountain Daughter has been completed but you never talked to Brundt the Chieftain after its completion: {Chat: 2 Talk about something else > 3 Do you have any quests? > Accept > 1 I want to become a Fremennik!}}} You can complete the trials in any order. Click on either the map circle or the name of the Fremennik below to go to that NPC's section of the guide File:The Fremennik Trials map.png|centre desc none rect 122 19 263 37 The Fremennik Isles rect 6 385 165 402 Brundt the Chieftain rect 7 410 154 426 Manni the Reveller rect 8 435 117 452 Olaf the Bard rect 8 460 114 477 Peer the Seer rect 199 384 351 403 Sigli the Huntsman rect 200 409 378 429 Sigmund The Merchant rect 201 433 377 454 Swensen the Navigator rect 201 460 360 477 Thorvald the Warrior circle 208 214 6 Brundt the Chieftain circle 218 231 6 Manni the Reveller circle 257 228 6 Olaf the Bard circle 110 249 6 Peer the Seer circle 209 302 6 Sigli the Huntsman circle 145 211 6 Sigmund The Merchant circle 165 267 6 Swensen the Navigator circle 243 161 6 Thorvald the Warrior"],"t":"The trials"},{"n":"Beer, 250 coins","r":"","s":["Talk to Manni the Reveller in the longhall next to Brundt. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Pick up a Keg of beer and beer from one of the tables.","Talk to the Poison Salesman at Forester's Arms in Seers' Village. {Chat: 2 Talk about the Fremennik Trials. > 1 Yes.}\n  - Buy a beer from the bartender nearby if you need one.","Use beer on council workman at the bridge south of Rellekka.","Light the strange object and put-inside pipe on the outside eastern wall of the Rellekka longhall.","Enter the longhall. Use low alcohol keg on the keg of beer in the backpack.","Challenge Manni. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Manni the Reveller"},{"n":"Raw potato, onion, cabbage, and a raw shark, manta ray or sea turtle","r":"","s":["Speak to Olaf the Bard, who is located east of the longhall. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Travel south-east to the swaying tree, north-west of the Golden Apple Tree on the world map, surrounded by rabbits and doogle leaves.","Chop off a branch and craft it into an unstrung lyre.","Head south-east and talk to Lalli. {Chat: 1 Other human?}","Talk to Askeladden south of the longhall.","Grab a raw potato, an onion, and cabbage from the farm in south-east Rellekka. It's recommended to pick an extra onion and cabbage in case you accidentally eat them.","\"Use\" the potato, onion, cabbage, and pet rock on Lalli's Stew.","Talk to Lalli to obtain a golden fleece.\n  - Use the drop trick to obtain another if you plan on completing Kili's Knowledge VII.","\"Use\" the golden fleece on a spinning wheel to make golden wool. There's one in south-west Rellekka.","Use the wool on the unstrung lyre.","Use your raw shark, manta ray or sea turtle on the strange altar south-west of Rellekka.","Enter the backstage of the longhall through the north-east door. Play the enchanted lyre in front of the crowd. You will receive Olaf's vote."],"t":"Olaf the Bard"},{"n":"","r":"Combat gear","s":["Talk to Sigli the Huntsman near Rellekka's southern entrance. {Chat: 1 What's a Draugen? > 1 Yes.}","Use the received hunters' talisman to locate and kill The Draugen. The Draugen is not visible until you get close to his location. Look for a tiny grey butterfly. There are only a few of these, one of which is the Draugen. Once in melee distance of the butterfly, use the 'Locate' function on the talisman once again, The Draugen will appear.","Return to Sigli to receive his vote."],"t":"Sigli the Huntsman"},{"n":"5,000 coins","r":"","s":["Talk to Sigmund The Merchant in the marketplace. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to the Sailor on the middle dock. Right-click and select Talk, as Travel is the default option {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Talk to Olaf the Bard, east of the longhall. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Talk to Yrsa in the clothing store, just west of the marketplace. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Talk to Brundt the Chieftain in the longhall. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Talk to Sigli the Huntsman south of the longhall. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Talk to Skulgrimen in the helmet store just north of the longhall. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Talk to the Fisherman on the first dock west of the helmet store. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Talk to Swensen the Navigator in a house south of the market. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Talk to Peer the Seer west of Swensen. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial} or {Chat: 2 The Fremennik Trials > 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial} if you've completed the easy Fremennik achievements","Talk to Thorvald the Warrior in the helmet store. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Talk to Manni the Reveller in the longhall. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Talk to Thora the Barkeep in the longhall. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Talk to Askeladden outside the longhall. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial > 1 Yes}","Give the promissory note to Thora in the longhall. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Give the legendary cocktail to Manni in the longhall. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Give the champions token to Thorvald in the helmet store. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Give the warriors' contract to Peer southwest of the market. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial} or {Chat: 2 The Fremennik Trials > 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial} if you've completed the easy Fremennik achievements","Give the weather forecast to Swensen east of Peer. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Give the sea fishing map to the Fisherman on the first dock west of the helmet store. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Give the unusual fish to Skulgrimen in the helmet store. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Give the custom bowstring to Sigli south of the longhall. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Give the tracking map to Brundt in the longhall. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Give the fiscal statement to Yrsa in the clothing store, just west of the marketplace. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Give the sturdy boots to Olaf east of the longhall. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Give the Fremennik ballad to the Sailor on the middle dock. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Give the exotic flower to Sigmund in the marketplace. You will receive his vote."],"t":"Sigmund The Merchant"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Swensen the Navigator in his house south-west of the longhall. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Merchant's Trial}","Go down the ladder in the small room in his house. In each room, there are four portals. Enter them in the correct order to receive his vote. The first letter of each direction spells out the name SWENSEN. The correct order is as follows:\n  - South\n  - West\n  - East\n  - North\n  - South\n  - East\n  - North","Climb up the ladder, then talk to Swensen to receive his vote."],"t":"Swensen the Navigator"},{"n":"","r":"A lot of food (such as sharks), rings of recoil, super attacks, super strengths, and super defences. Weapon poison also works. Make sure to store all armour and weapons prior to visiting Thorvald. You may speak to Peer the Seer and deposit your items; you cannot use the right click option.","s":["Talk to Thorvald the Warrior in the helmet store north of the longhall. {Chat: 1 Yes.} In order to receive his vote, you must kill a special warrior called Koschei the Deathless. However, the fight has three rules:",": You must defeat him at least three out of four times.",": You must fight to the death.",": You are not allowed to use weapons or armour or beasts of burden. This also means no runes, staves, etc (you can use food, prayer, rings of recoil, already summoned familiars, a pickaxe or hatchet removed from your tool belt, or even a dismantled godsword).","Climb down the ladder and wait for him to appear to begin the fight.","Defeat him three times and either kill him the fourth time or let yourself be defeated. (You will not die).","Talk to Thorvald to receive his vote."],"t":"Thorvald the Warrior"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Peer the Seer, who can be found south-west of the market in Rellekka. {Chat: 1 Yes.} or {Chat: 2 The Fremennik Trials > 1 Yes} if you've completed the easy Fremennik achievements","To enter his house, you must solve a simple riddle. Possible answers include: \"tree\", \"time\", \"life\", \"mage\", \"fire\", \"wind\", \"mind\" and \"disk\".","Enter the building and climb the ladder.\n  - Study the unicorn's head for an old red disk.\n  - Study the bull's head for a wooden disk.\n  - Search the bookcase for a red herring.\n  - Open then search the eastern chest for an empty jug.\n  - Open then search the south-west cupboard for an empty bucket.","Use the red herring on the cooking range to get sticky red goop.","Use the goop on the wooden disk to get a second red disk.","Go down the eastern trapdoor and use the two disks on the abstract mural for a vase lid.","Climb the ladder.\n  - Use the empty jug on the tap, then the full jug on the empty bucket.\n  - Use the empty jug on the tap again and fill the bucket. You'll have a full bucket and a 1/3rds full jug.\n  - Use the full bucket on the drain to get an empty bucket. Or search the cupboard again.\n  - Use the 1/3rds full jug on the empty bucket.\n  - Use the empty jug on the tap, then use the full jug on the 1/5ths full bucket to get a 4/5ths full bucket.\n  - Use the 4/5ths full bucket on the northwestern chest to receive a vase.\n  - Use the vase on the tap.\n  - Use the vase lid on the vase of water to get a sealed vase.","Use the sealed vase on the frozen table to receive a frozen key.","Use the frozen key on the range, then go down the eastern trapdoor again and out the exit. You will receive Peer the Seer's vote."],"t":"Peer the Seer"},{"n":"10 free inventory slots","r":"","s":["Talk to Brundt the Chieftain in the longhall in Rellekka.","Congratulations, quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"The G-Nome Project":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Queen of Snow north of the Grand Exchange. {Chat: Accept}","Talk to Aubury, Doc, and Orla.","Talk to the Queen of Snow.","Talk to Thurgo in his hut south of Port Sarim. (1 Redberry pie) {Chat: 1 Talk about Santa.}","Enter the Grotworm Lair in the White Knight Camp slightly north of the Port Sarim lodestone."],"t":"Track Santa"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["On the platform, investigate the damaged sleigh.","Gather Rudolph's ashes.","Talk to Santa."],"t":"Rescue Santa"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Doc, just north of Santa. (100 Pale energy)","Tinker with the power generator until the damage reaches 0%.","Keep on tinkering with the generator until the control panel starts to smoke, then fix the control panel.\n  - You can configure the generator to gain smithing Smithing or crafting Crafting xp.","Try the machine on yourself, and then try it on the gnome."],"t":"Helping Doc"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Aubury, to the west of Santa. (10 Rune/Pure Essence) {Chat: 1 Anomalies are bad. > 2 I can seal anomalies while channeling the rift. > 1 I will need to seal 15 anomalies.}","Channel the energy rift until it is charged 100%.","Keep channeling the rift, sealing 15 anomalies as they spawn around the rift.\n  - You can configure the rift to gain runecrafting Runecrafting or Summoning Summoning xp."],"t":"Helping Aubury"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Orla, to the east of Santa. (12 Raw lobster)","Talk to the Menaphite Smuggler standing next to the soul obelisk south of the desert strykewyrm area. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Orla.","Siphon the soul obelisk until you absorb the soul 100%.","Use the arrows on screen, or the arrow keys ([←][→]) to keep the gauge balanced.\n  - You can configure the obelisk to gain divination Divination or prayer Prayer xp.","Talk to Orla. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Helping Orla"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Santa.","Talk to Santa again to teleport to the Phoenix Lair. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Santa.","Back at the Grand Exchange, talk to Santa again.","Talk to Santa.","Event complete!"],"t":"Powers combined"}]},"The General's Shadow (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Equip all ghostly robe outfit, the ring of visibility and a ghostspeak amulet or cramulet.","South of the Fremennik Province lodestone and just south-west of the swaying tree, find and then talk to the ghost of General Khazard. {Chat: 1 Uh, well, you don't really have eyes, so how can you tell? > Accept}\n  - Khazard, and all of the ghost scouts you'll locate next, cannot be seen on the minimap and have a fair-sized wander radius.\n  - It is recommended to use the skybox bloodstone if the player has completed The Lord of Vampyrium quest but can be done without, or use High Contrast Mode under Accessibility Options.","Talk to Sin Seer in Seers' Village. She is upstairs in the spinning wheel house. {Chat: 1 Bribe > 1 Here's the money.}","Return to General Khazard.","Talk to the ghost scout south-east of Tai Bwo Wannai (search between the hardwood grove and the drakolith mine).","Talk to the ghost scout south of the Tree Gnome Stronghold entrance (east of the Outpost).","Talk to the ghost scout in the area between Falador and Draynor Manor.","Talk to the ghost scout south of the Shantay Pass.","Return to General Khazard.","Prepare for battle before fighting against a level 91 enemy.","Enter the goblin cave east of the Fishing Guild.","Run to the northeast \"room\" and enter the crack in the southern wall. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Kill the Bouncer. You'll throw the severed leg when its health reaches 0.\n  - If Bouncer's health is stuck at 0, the player should leave the room, dismiss any familiars, and reenter to try killing Bouncer again. Once at 0 health, continue clicking on him until your character automatically throws the severed leg.","Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Ghosting"}]},"The Giant Dwarf":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the tunnel between the two black statues, north-east of Rellekka, close to fairy ring DKS. (teleport to the Fremennik Province and run north-east)","Go through cave entrance east to Keldagrim.","Talk to the Dwarven Boatman inside the cave, not Dwarven Ferryman. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Go west to the Black Guard H.Q.. Enter the building and talk to Commander Veldaban. The chat instance should end with you accepting the quest. {Chat: Accept}","Exit the house, go north-east across the bridge and talk to Blasidar the Sculptor just north-west of the brewery. {Chat: 2 Yes, I will do this.}"],"t":"Under arrest"},{"n":"200 coins, 1 coal, 1 logs","r":"","s":["In the large building just west, talk to Vermundi at the silk icon. {Chat: 2 Yes, I'm looking for some special clothes.}","In the building west of the northern bridge, talk to the Librarian. {Chat: 2 Do you know anything about King Alvis's clothes?}","While weighing less than 30kg, attempt to climb any bookcase.","With the book, return to Vermundi. {Chat: 2 Yes, about those special clothes again...}","Use coal and logs on her spinning machine.","Try to light it until the engine starts. (This may take several attempts)","Talk to Vermundi. {Chat: 2 Yes, about those special clothes again... > 1 I'll pay.}"],"t":"King's clothes"},{"n":"Runes to cast Telekinetic Grab (1 air rune and 1 law rune)","r":"","s":["In the far west of the city, talk to Saro at the anvil icon. {Chat: 2 Yes, I'm looking for a pair of special boots.}","North of the bank, talk to Dromund.","Take the left boot, from the table near the door, while his back is turned.","Leave his house and run around to the north edge, stand next to the western window (adjacent to the right boot).","When his back is turned, cast Telekinetic Grab on the right boot through the window."],"t":"King's boots"},{"n":"3 sapphires, 1 redberry pie (if you have not completed The Knight's Sword), 1 iron bar","r":"","s":["Go to the north-west corner and talk to Santiri. {Chat: 2 Yes, I'm looking for a particular battleaxe. > 2 Blasidar the sculptor needs it for his statue. > 2 Perhaps I can repair the axe?}","Use 3 sapphires on the battleaxe.","If you have not completed The Knight's Sword:\n  - Take a redberry pie with you when you talk to Thurgo.","Talk to Thurgo in his small hut (fairy ring AIQ), south of Port Sarim, and north of Mudskipper Point. {Chat: 2 Something else. (3 if skillcape is owned) > 2 Would you like some redberry pie? > 3 Can you help me with this ancient axe? > 1 Return to Keldagrim immediately.}\n  - If The Knight's Sword is complete {Chat: 2 Something else. (3 if skillcape is owned) > 2 Can you help me with this ancient axe? > 1 Return to Keldagrim immediately.}\n  - Have an iron bar to give to Thurgo (or access your metal bank via the anvil next to Thurgo to obtain one which is stored in it).","With the 4 items, talk to Riki the sculptor's model near Blasidar the sculptor.","Talk to Blasidar for a cutscene."],"t":"King's axe"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Run west to the marketplace building and up the stairs.","Talk to any secretary (yellow is closest to metal bank) - your character's gender may disqualify your eligibility to work for that colour of company, consequently try another colour. {Chat: 3 Is there anything I can help you with? > Any}","Fetch them the required ore (must be un-noted). Repeat with the same secretary for a total of 4 tasks.","Talk to the director. {Chat: 3 Do you have any more tasks for me? > Any}","Fetch them the required bars. You might need to repeat for a second task.","Talk to the director. {Chat: 2 I'd like to officially join your company. > 3 Blasidar the sculptor has sent me. > 1 I would support you. > 1 Yes! Long live the [company]!}","Return to Commander Veldaban in Black Guard headquarters, where you started the quest (west of the palace and west of the bank). {Chat: 1 I'm ready. > 2 I do NOT want to attend, I don't have time to waste. > 2 I just have a lot of smithing to do today, I can't attend.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Climbing the corporate ladder"}]},"The Golem":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head east of the Shantay Pass to Uzer (north-east of the fairy ring DLQ).\n  - If running from the Shantay Pass, pick up the phoenix feather on the way.","Talk to the broken clay golem. {Chat: Accept}","With four soft clay in your backpack, use one on the golem. All four will be used to repair the golem.","Talk to the golem. {Chat: 1 How do I open the portal?}","Pick up and read the letter west of the broken clay golem.","Pick a black mushroom, found on the south-east corner of the stairs leading into the ruins.","Climb down the stairs in the ruins east of the golem.","Head to the north-western room and pick up the strange implement."],"t":"Incomplete Mission"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to the Varrock Dig Site using the Archaeology journal, or teleport to Varrock and run east, or teleport to Fort Forinthry and run south.","Use the letter on Elissa and talk to Elissa who is east of the winch in the north-east corner of the digsite (just north of The Stormbreaker ship). {Chat: 3 I found a letter in the desert with your name on.}","Head to the Exam Centre just south of the Dig Site.","Search the bookshelf on the southern wall and read Varmen's notes.","Talk to Curator Haig Halen in the Varrock Museum about the statuette. {Chat: 3 I'm looking for a statuette recovered from the city of Uzer. > 1 I want to open a portal to the lair of an elder-demon.}","Pickpocket him for the display cabinet key.","Head upstairs and use the display cabinet key on the northwestern most case to get the statuette."],"t":"Statuette"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Shantay Pass and cross into the desert.","Go east to the Desert Phoenix, and grab a phoenix feather.\n  - Make sure you un-equip any item porters, as wearing an activated Porter or grace of the elves will teleport the feather to your bank.\n  - Make sure you un-equip the Thieving Cape or Thieving master cape, as they will cause the feather to be noted.","Go to the ruins of Uzer where you started the quest and go back down the stairs.","In the centre of the room will be four alcoves. Place the statuette in the empty one.","Turn the statuettes so they all point north towards the double doors. You may have to click \"turn\" more than once.","Go north, through the double doors.\n  - Optional: Take the gems from the throne at the north side of the room to unlock the achievement Looting the Demon Throne and obtain two cut rubies, two cut emeralds, and two cut sapphires.","Go back through the south portal."],"t":"The portal"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go back upstairs and talk to the golem.","With an empty vial in your backpack, right click Grind the black mushroom (Don't left click \"Eat\" it).","Use the phoenix feather on the black mushroom ink.","Use the phoenix quill pen on a piece of papyrus to get the golem program.","Use the Strange implement on the golem then quickly use the newly acquired golem program on the golem.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The golem"}]},"The Grand Tree":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to King Narnode Shareen on the floor 1 of the Grand Tree. {Chat: 1 You seem worried, what's up? > Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take the bark sample and book to Hazelmere; he lives east of Yanille (pictured).\n  - If you have A Fairy Tale II - Cure a Queen completed, you can use code CLS, otherwise teleport to the Yanille lodestone.","Up the ladder, talk to Hazelmere.","Take Hazelmere's scroll back to the King.","Talk to the King. {Chat: 1 I think so! > 5 None of the above. > 5 None of the above. > 2 A man came to me with the King's seal. > 1 I gave the man Daconia rocks. > 4 And Daconia rocks will kill the tree!}"],"t":"The crisis"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb up the ladder of the tree house south-east of the Grand Tree, north of the Agility course.","Speak to Glough.","Speak to the King.","Climb to the top floor of the Grand Tree.","Talk to Charlie the prisoner.","Return to Glough's tree house.","Search the cupboard north of the ladder to get Glough's journal.","Speak to Glough.","Speak to Charlie and leave your prison cell.","Talk to the Captain Errdo just north of the cells to get to Karamja. {Chat: 1 Take me to Karamja, please.}\n  - Beware if you are low level, there are multiple level 57 Jogres here so be ready.","Run east and attempt to open the gate.","Tell him you work for Glough, Ka-Lu-Min is the password. {Chat: 2 Glough sent me. > 1 Ka. > 2 Lu. > 2 Min.}","Once inside, run east to the south dock.","Either kill the foreman, or talk to him and answer his questions. {Chat: 3 Sadly his wife is no longer with us! > 2 He loves worm holes. > 1 Anita.}","Take the Lumber order.","Talk to Femi at the Gnome Stronghold gates to enter inside.\n  - You may offer help to get inside for free, or 1,000 coins if you do not.\n  - Alternatively teleport to the spirit tree if Tree Gnome Village quest is complete.","Talk to the King.","Talk to Charlie the prisoner.","Speak to Anita. She can be found in the northwesternmost tree house in the stronghold.","Use the key on the chest in Glough's house and search it to receive the invasion plans.","Talk to the king. Make sure you have 4 free inventory spaces before you do this step, as he will give you 4 twigs."],"t":"Glough"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Prepare to fight a level 98 black demon. Magic works well here, as the demon has a weakness to water spells. There is a safespot along the south wall, behind some rocks where Glough is standing. Using a halberd will allow lower levels to effectively melee the demon using the safespot.","Go to the top level of Glough's house.","Use the twigs on the pillars to spell TUZO.","Open the trapdoor.","Kill the demon. (Can be safespotted by standing within the rocks to the south)"],"t":"The fight"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Run to the middle of the cave and talk to the king. Don't click away yet, wait for the scripted dialogue to finish.","Search the nearby roots for a rock. If you don't find the rock try the other roots in the cave. Be sure to space-through or click through the text boxes, or else the Daconia rock may not appear in your inventory.","Take the rock to the king.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"The Great Brain Robbery":{"sections":[{"n":"4 regular planks, at least 10 nails, a holy symbol, fishbowl helmet, and diving apparatus","r":"","s":["Travel to Mos Le'Harmless (fairy ring DIP if you have repaired the bridge), walk a bit north off the dock and talk to Brother Tranquillity (if you arrived via the fairy ring, run into town and he is north of the docks). {Chat: Accept}","Bank/dismiss any pets or familiars.","Upon arrival on Harmony Island, go through the dialogue, or Brother Tranquillity will teleport you back to Mos Le'Harmless.","Run outside and head slightly north to the statue. Pull the statue, then climb-down statue.","Equip your diving gear and descend the stairs.","Run past the zombie pirates.","Repair the stairs at the end of the tunnel, then climb them.\n  - If you happened to bring your planks in a plank box, be sure to remove them so you can repair the stairs.","Climb the ladder.","Peer-through the peephole on the wall.","Make your way back to Brother Tranquillity on Harmony Island and speak with him.","Travel to the Edgeville Monastery.","Search the southern bookcase on the floor 1 of the western wing to find a prayer book.","Read the book.","Head back to Brother Tranquillity who teleports you to Harmony Island.","Wear your holy symbol and choose the option Recite-prayer on the prayer book."],"t":"Disharmony"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Brother Tranquillity.","Travel to Fenkenstrain's Castle, which is directly north-east of the Canifis lodestone.","Go up on the staircase in the north-western corner.","Go up on the northern ladder behind the jail gate in the centre.","Talk to Dr Fenkenstrain."],"t":"Family doctor"},{"n":"10 wooden cats (10 bear fur and 10 planks if making yourself), 28+ nails, 4 planks, ring of charos, and at least 2 backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Equip your ring of charos and talk to Rufus in the Canifis meat store. {Chat: 1 Talk about the meat shipment}\n  - Speak with Rufus again after the cutscene if you did not receive a wolf whistle and crate parts.","Start crafting on a clockmaker's bench in a player-owned house to make 10 wooden cats with 10 planks and 10 bear fur. You can also buy them off the Grand Exchange.","Travel back to Dr Fenkenstrain with all of the required items.","Build the crate on the hotspot, east of the ladder.","Add-bottom to the crate.","Fill the crate with the wooden cats.","Take off your fishbowl helmet and Blow the wolf whistle to call Rufus.","Use the shipping order on the crate."],"t":"Err... Meow?"},{"n":"fishbowl helmet, diving apparatus, hammer (tool belt does not work), tinderbox (tool belt does not work, can be picked up on the pirate ship), combat gear, at least 6 backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Travel back to Mos Le'Harmless.","Buy a hammer and a tinderbox from the Trader Crewmember (located south-west on the dock).","Speak with Brother Tranquillity to get back on Harmony Island. {Chat: 1 Yes. please.} (Brother Tranquillity now also has a \"transport\" option available to players)","Climb down the ladder and talk to Dr Fenkenstrain.\n  - If he is not there, exit to lobby and join the world again.","Return up the ladder.","Equip your diving suit and head north to the ship that has run aground.\n  - If you walk outside without diving suit, you will be teleported back.\n  - Equip your weapons in preparation for fighting enemies, otherwise you will have to return to the windmill to do so. Attempting to do so outside will give the message: \"You cannot wear that without the gas affecting you.\"","Open and then search the locker on the west end of the floor 1 to get a fuse.","Climb the ladder and take a keg of powder found next to a cannon.\n  - Grab the tinderbox from the front (east side) of the ship if you have not brought your own.","Go to the front door of the monastery (the main building on Harmony Island).","Use the keg on the door.","Use the fuse on the door.","Use your tinderbox on the fuse.","Pass the door to enter the monastery.","Kill some sorebones until you get the following items (the items drop one at a time and the next item won't spawn until the current one is picked up):\n  - 3 bell jars\n  - A pair of brain tongs\n  - A cranial clamp\n  - 30 skull staples","Talk to Dr Fenkenstrain downstairs in the mill. Make sure to give him a hammer or you will be stuck.","After the cutscene, go upstairs and talk to Brother Tranquillity. {Chat: 2 Not right now, thanks.}"],"t":"Scrubs"},{"n":"Combat equipment, fishbowl helmet, diving apparatus","r":"Food and potions","s":["Pass the door of the monastery and confront Mi-Gor.","Kill Barrelchest.","Take the Barrelchest anchor.","Return to Brother Tranquillity.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Barrelchest"}]},"The Hand in the Sand":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Bert in the building near Yanille's house portal. {Chat: 2 Eww a hand, in the sand! Why haven't you told the authorities? > Accept}\n  - If you need a bucket of sand, there is a sand pit directly north of the house portal that you may fill your bucket at for later in the quest.","Give the Guard Captain in the nearby pub a beer.","Go east to the Wizards' Guild and ring the bell on the eastern side of the building. {Chat: 2 I have a rather sandy problem that I'd like to palm off on you.}\n  - If you have at least 66 Magic, you can enter the guild and go upstairs to find Zavistic Rarve, rather than calling him to the front door.","Return to Bert and speak to him to receive Bert's rota.","Go to Brimhaven and find Sandy in a small house between the Dead Man's Chest and The Shrimp and Parrot.","Search his desk to receive Sandy's rota.","Pickpocket Sandy for some sand (may take several attempts, bucket of sand does not count).","Return to Bert and talk to him.","Ring the Wizards' Guild bell and talk to Zavistic Rarve again to receive a magical orb. {Chat: 2 I have a rather sandy problem that I'd like to palm off on you.}\n  - If you have a second empty vial you can teleport to Port Sarim's magic shop by talking to Zavistic Rarve again and give him an empty vial. {Chat: 2 I have a rather sandy problem that I'd like to palm off on you. > 4 Can you help me more?. > 1 Okay}}}"],"t":"A helping hand"},{"n":"an empty vial, redberries, white berries, lantern lens, magical orb, sand","r":"","s":["In Port Sarim's magic shop, talk to Betty. {Chat: 1 Talk to Betty about The Hand in the Sand.}","Use your redberries on the bottled water Betty gave you, then the white berries.","Use the pink dye on your lantern lens.","Talk to Betty again. {Chat: 1 Talk to Betty about The Hand in the Sand.}","Open the door to her shop and stand in the doorway, then use your rose-tinted lens on the counter. Successfully doing so grants you a truth serum potion.","Talk to Betty a third time. {Chat: 1 Talk to Betty about The Hand in the Sand.}","Make your way back to Brimhaven.","Talk to Sandy to distract him. {Chat: Any} Try all three options until Sandy is distracted, this is random for each player. If this still doesn't work, lobby then log in again.","Use the truth serum on the coffee mug on the table.","Activate the magical orb in your backpack.","Talk to Sandy again. {Chat: 1 Why is Bert's rota different from the original? > 1 Why doesn't Bert remember the change in his hours? > 1 What happened to the wizard?}"],"t":"Truth serum"},{"n":"5 earth runes, bucket of sand","r":"","s":["Head back to the Wizards Guild in Yanille and ring the bell once more. {Chat: 2 I have a rather sandy problem that I'd like to palm off on you.}","With your five earth runes and bucket of sand, ring the bell again for a cutscene. {Chat: 2 I have a rather sandy problem that I'd like to palm off on you.}","Go to the sand pit in south-west Entrana.","Talk to Mazion to receive the wizard's head.","Return to Yanille and ring the bell at Wizards Guild a final time. {Chat: 2 I have a rather sandy problem that I'd like to palm off on you.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Retrieving the head"}]},"The Hunt for Surok (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Surok Magis outside the Tunnel of Chaos, at the Saradomin statue south of Jolly Boar Inn, south of Fort Forinthry. If he's not there, click dig on the statue, then enter and leave.","After the cutscene, follow him into the tunnel.","Follow him into the portal in the western room (where Dakh'thoulan Aegis is).","Follow Surok through the Chaos Tunnels portals in the route in the above map.\n  - Be aware that there are aggressive monsters, dragons, and prayer-draining monsters on the way. It is recommended to bring food and combat equipment.\n  - You may be randomly teleported by a portal - if so, locate yourself on the map and make your way back to the route.","You need to see three cutscenes along the route."],"t":"Tunnel chase"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the final portal in the dagannoth room.","Defeat Bork."],"t":"Boss battle"}]},"The Jack of Spades":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Emir Ali Mirza in Al Kharid palace to begin the quest. {Chat: 1 Talk about Jack of Spades. > Accept > 1 Yes.}","Go upstairs. Talk to Osman. {Chat: 5 No more questions.}","From the same floor, climb the central north or northwest staircase to the roof and talk to Grand Vizier Hassan. The steps are built into the wall and may be difficult to notice at a glance. Look south west of the fountain. {Chat: 1 I know all I need - let's go!}","Dismiss any follower and unequip the item in your main and off-hand slots. Talk to Grand Vizier Hassan. {Chat: 1 Yes, let's go!}","Talk to Hassan while on the carpet to teleport to Menaphos. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Follow Hassan into the city."],"t":"New trade deal"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Hassan. {Chat: 1 Talk about Jack of Spades.} Make sure you finish all dialogue. There are (brief) pauses between dialogue after talking to each person below.","Head north east to the shifting tombs entrance in the centre of the market square.","Choose the Travel Ports District option on the tombs to go to the Port district.","Talk to 'Admiral' Wadud (Ports) in The Golden Scarab Inn just north.","Choose the Travel Imperial District option on the tombs to the Imperial district. (This is a good time to activate the Menaphos Lodestone just East of you.)","Speak to Commander Akhomet (Imperial) in front of the entrance to the Great Pyramid just west. Make sure you finish the dialogue, as there is a pause somewhere.","Choose the Travel Worker District option on the tombs to the Worker district.","Talk to Batal (Worker) next to the fire pit. Make sure you finish the dialogue, as there is a pause somewhere."],"t":"The streets of Menaphos"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the shifting tombs to go inside.","Ensure you have 4 backpack spaces.","Talk to the Jack of Spades. {Chat: 3 Why steal from people? > 4 I've heard enough.}","Exit the shifting tombs to any district.","Referencing above locations, return the four stolen items to their respective districts.","Return to Hassan in the Merchant district. {Chat: 1 Talk about Jack of Spades.}","Quest complete!","Before leaving the city, feel free to activate the Menaphos lodestone."],"t":"Shifty"}]},"The Knight's Sword":{"sections":[{"n":"Redberry pie","r":"","s":["Talk to Squire Asrol in the White Knights' Castle courtyard in Falador. {Chat: 1 Chat > 1 And how is life as a squire? > 2 I can make a new sword if you like... > 1 So would these dwarves make another one? > Accept}","Talk to Reldo in Varrock Palace library about the Imcando dwarf tribe. {Chat: 3 What do you know about the Imcando dwarves?}\n  - If The Giant Dwarf quest is complete, skip this step.\n  - If wielding ring of charos remove that, otherwise option does not appear.","Talk to Thurgo south of Port Sarim (pictured right, north of fairy ring aiq) with a Redberry pie in the inventory. {Chat: 2 Something else. > 2 Would you like some redberry pie?}\n  - If Smithing cape is obtained {Chat: 3 Something else. > 2 Would you like some redberry pie?}","Talk to him again. {Chat: 2 Something else.}\n  - If Smithing cape is obtained {Chat: 3 Something else.}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Squire Asrol. {Chat: 1 Chat}","Climb the ladder to the east, then the first staircase to the west.","Enter Sir Vyvin's room directly south.","Look for a cupboard and open it then search it.\n  - If Sir Vyvin keeps noticing, four methods can be used to distract him.\n    - Have a friend talk to Sir Vyvin while you open and search the cupboard.\n    - Open the door to his room and wait for him to walk out. However, this will take a very long time, so keep hopping worlds until you arrive at one where he's already outside, or alternatively just shut the door when he leaves and then search the cupboard.\n    - Wait until he is behind the door, then quickly search the cupboard.\n    - Wait until Sir Vyvin looks at a wall, then quickly search the cupboard."],"t":"The portrait"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Give Thurgo the portrait. {Chat: 2 Something else.}\n  - If Skillcape in Smithing is obtained {Chat: 3 Something else.}","Climb down the trapdoor on the hill east of Thurgo's house to enter the Asgarnian Ice Dungeon.","Follow the dungeon until blurite rocks are seen (see the map).","Mine a blurite ore.\n  - If you wish to complete Defender of Varrock later, mine an extra blurite ore.\n  - If you wish to complete the medium Falador achievements later, mine another one."],"t":"The sword"},{"n":"Blurite ore, 2 iron bars","r":"","s":["Talk to Thurgo with the materials. {Chat: 2 Something else.}\n  - If Skillcape in Smithing is obtained {Chat: 3 Something else.}\n  - Bars can be withdrawn at the anvil in Thurgo's hut.","Report back to the Squire Asrol. {Chat: 1 Chat}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"The Light Within":{"sections":[{"n":"Enchanted key","r":"","s":["Talk to Eluned in the Ithell Clan district, next to the Singing Bowl. {Chat: 1 Of course! > Accept}","Climb the stairs in the Tower of Voices. {Chat: 1 The Light Within. > 2 I've come to offer my help. > 3 How do we decide? > 1 Yes. > 3 What now?}"],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"Enchanted key, 1 backpack space","r":"","s":["Go to Guthixian ruins in the caves west of the Legends' Guild, northwest of Fairy ring BLR.","Walk up to Guthix as close as possible and rub the enchanted key.","Talk to Guthix. {Chat: 1 I am the world guardian. > 4 I need to restore Seren.}","Go west and talk to Haluned. {Chat: 1 Yes, we have. > 1 What are you doing here? > 2 Are you related to Eluned? > 3 [Continue...]}","Talk to Guthix. {Chat: 2 [Continue...] > Any}","Return to the conclave in the Tower of Voices. {Chat: 1 The Light Within.}","Talk to everyone, talking to Eluned is optional.","Read Baxtorian's journal, given to you by Arianwyn."],"t":"Time-travelling"},{"n":"Trahaearn exoskeleton set, 1 backpack space","r":"crystal teleport seed","s":["Equip the Trahaearn exoskeleton set.","Investigate the well in Lletya. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Attempt to pass the Trahaearn automaton mk V. {Chat: 4 Rune > 3 Cynog > 2 Five > 3 The future is doomed}","Take the Seren shard (prudence)."],"t":"Artisan shard"},{"n":"grand defence potion, 3 backpack spaces","r":"crystal teleport seed, Tirannwn quiver 3 or 4, nature's sentinel outfit to teleport to the currently active crystal tree","s":["Talk to Coeden, the living tree surrounded by ivy in the Crwys Clan district. {Chat: 1 The Light Within.}","Click on the elven clan symbols which appear throughout the dialogue.\n  - You will receive a wintercup mushroom.","Pick a bloodcap mushroom just west of the Tirannwn mushroom farming patch. It can be reached by teleporting to the Tirannwn lodestone and going west through the dense forest. Players with a Tirannwn quiver 3 or 4 can use it to teleport directly to the mushroom patch.","Combine the mushrooms with a grand defence potion to create an Elixir of Revealment.","Travel to the currently active crystal tree (excluding the one in Prifddinas) and use the elixir on any of the tree's shards. Players with the Nature's sentinel outfit can teleport there directly.","Enter the cave entrance that appears and take the Seren shard (harmony)."],"t":"Naturalist shard"},{"n":"2 backpack spaces, Baxtorian's journal, Glarial's amulet and a rope","r":"A games necklace to teleport to Baxtorian Falls, or a hoardstalker ring, or Dungeoneering cape to teleport to Baxtorian Falls resource dungeon","s":["Go to the Waterfall Dungeon by boarding the log raft at the top of Baxtorian Falls, using a rope on the rock and then the dead tree, and entering the door.\n  - Alternatively, it can be reached by teleporting to the Baxtorian Falls resource dungeon.","Enter the eastern room.","Search the odd coloured crate to find a key.","Ensure you have read Baxtorian's journal, then proceed to western room and enter through the two doors to the north.","Investigate Statue of King Baxtorian. {Chat: 2 [Polite]My name is Player. > 4 We need to restore Seren.}","Take the Seren shard (integrity)."],"t":"Military shard"},{"n":"three light cores","r":"crystal teleport seed","s":["Go to the Corrupted Seren Stone in the Hefin Cathedral, located in the northern-most part of Prifddinas, a chatbox will appear at the top of the steps. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 2 I'm ready to start!}","Lady Hefin will lead you through the 3 sets of poses and incantations, starting with 3 poses and 3 words, then 4, then 5 poses and words. After she speaks each incantation, you must speak the words in the same order she did.\n  - Consider writing down the first letter of every word of the incantations."],"t":"Wisdom shard"},{"n":"Seren shard (harmony), Seren shard (prudence), Seren shard (integrity), and Seren shard (wisdom)","r":"Sixth-Age circuit, combat equipment, and food, your best tools if you skill for the shards instead of kill","s":["Return to the Tower of Voices and climb up the stairs. {Chat: 1 The Light Within}\n  - There will be a short cutscene.\n  - Go up the stairs again to return to the conclave. {Chat: 1 The Light Within}","Give the Seren shards to the respective Elders:\n  - Lady Meilyr or Lord Crwys - Harmony\n  - Lady Hefin or Lord Amlodd - Wisdom\n  - Lord Iorwerth or Arianwyn - Integrity\n  - Lady Ithell or Lady Trahaearn - Prudence","Talk to Morvran in the Iorwerth Clan district. {Chat: 1 Ask for access to the Grand Library.}","Enter the western door in the Grand Library.","Take Seren shard (dark) in the south-western corner on the edge of the platform. {Chat: Any}","Return to the conclave in the Tower of Voices. {Chat: 1 The Light Within}","Go to the World Gate.","Rotate the controls until you reach .\n  - There is currently a bug where the symbol is not synchronised with its actual rotation direction. The first sentence of the description on the \"Travel to Tarddiad\" prompt when you attempt to enter the World Gate is \"Through the gate you see a world covered almost entirely by trees.\"","Enter the World Gate.","Obtain 50 Tarddian crystals by killing crystal Shapeshifters, or by mining solid crystals, chopping branching crystals, or fishing floating crystals to collect 150 crystal fragments and exchanging them with Angof to the north at a ratio of 3 fragments to 1 crystal.\n  - Angof has a toggle option to increase the amount of shapeshifters in the area, and make them aggressive towards you.","Talk to Angof to get the last piece of the Song of Restoration. {Chat: 1 Hello, pleased to meet you. > 5 [Leave]}","Return to the Tower of Voices by talking to Eluned. {Chat: 1 Let's return.}\n  - If Eluned is beside Angof, you can return with her.","Climb up the stairs. {Chat: 1 The Light Within}}}"],"t":"Tarddiad"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Watch the cutscene and go through the dialogue. Skipping won't work. At the end of the cutscene you will arrive on Freneskae with Seren in your arms. (If the options don't pop up leave and return to the room) {Chat: Any > Any > Any > 1 I'll go now. > 1 I'm ready.}","Avoid Muspah attacks by walking around.","Talk to Zaros."],"t":"Freneskae"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Seren. {Chat: Any > 1 Yes}","Return to the conclave in the Tower of Voices.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Seren's return"}]},"The Lord of Vampyrium":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Vanescula Drakan at the docks south-east of Burgh de Rott. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Board the nearby boat to Icyene graveyard. {Chat: 2 Icyene graveyard.}","Talk to Safalaan.","Solve the ring puzzle by rotating the rings until they turn blue and their markings join together.","Inspect the statue of Queen Efaritay to receive Efaritay's pendant.","Talk to Safalaan.","Travel to the Myreque Hideout with Drakan's medallion {Chat: 3} , use the Meiyerditch teleport option, and walk into the central room.","After the cutscene, talk to Safalaan in the northern room."],"t":"Gathering of the Myreque"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Equip your Darkmeyer disguise.","Use your Drakan's medallion to teleport to Darkmeyer {Chat: 4}","Talk to Veliaf Hurtz inside the Arboretum. He will not appear until you walk into the central chamber.\n  - At this point you are able to craft more types of blisterwood weapons.","Head south-west inside Vanstrom's former mansion.","Open then search the vyrewatch crate to obtain vyrewatch uniforms."],"t":"Vyrewatch uniforms"},{"n":"Four backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Return to Veliaf. {Chat: 1 Yes.} He will give you a set of the House Drakan outfit.","No items other than the Darkmeyer outfit, House Drakan outfit, Drakan medallion, runes, Ivandis flail, and blisterwood weapons and ammo can be taken to Castle Drakan.","Equip the House Drakan outfit, unequip any weapons, and talk to Vanescula near Overwatch Mornid.","Complete the following to gain status:\n  - North-west, talk to Lady Nadezhda Shadum. {Chat: 4 Humiliate it.}\n  - West, talk to Lord Alexei Jovkai. {Chat: 1 Try the old man - he looks defiant.}\n  - East, talk to Lord Mischa Myrmel. {Chat: 4 Show mercy; make her feel better.}\n  - Shoo the bats flying around.","Talk to Vanescula. {Chat: Any > Any > Any > Any}"],"t":"Castle Drakan"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Exit your cell and unlock the five other cells. You will take damage equal to 10% of your life points. You will have a chance to eat in the next section. Make sure you talk to the Myreque while doing this or the portcullis will not open.","Go to the next chamber and solve the ring puzzle. This is similar to the earlier puzzle with the addition that rotating a ring causes the smaller, adjacent ring to rotate as well. Rotating the centre ring causes the outer ring to rotate.\n  - Start from the outside and work your way in.","Go to the next chamber and talk to Safalaan.","Go up the stairs and leave the dungeon.","Go to the eastern room and take all the mysterious jerky you are able to from the butchery table.\n  - Eat to full health, you can take more after eating.","Talk to Vanescula and Mornid in the western room.","Go to the southern room, and read the A Taste of Hope book obtained earlier. Investigate each blood lock. The correct matches are:\n  - Ghrazi - Veliaf {Chat: 5 [More choices.] > 3 Veliaf.}\n  - Alzeph - Radigad {Chat: 5 [More choices.] > 1 Radigad.}\n  - Pyrah - Kael {Chat: 2 Kael.}\n  - Myrmel - Mekritus {Chat: 3 Mekritus.}\n  - Vitur - Polmafi {Chat: 4 Polmafi.}\n  - Shadum - Vertida {Chat: 5 [More choices.] > 4 Vertida.}\n  - Jovkai - Safalaan {Chat: 5 [More choices.] > 2 Safalaan.}\n  - Drakan - Ivan {Chat: 1 Ivan.}","Unlock the tithing door south and escape through the cellar exit.","Enter the tunnel and Lowerniel Drakan will appear."],"t":"Escaping the cells"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Vandalise the statue of Lord Drakan to obtain a statue spear (if the option to vandalise doesn't appear then enter the east door for a cutscene).","Brace the entrance door.","Defeat the venator and climb the stairs."],"t":"Ground floor"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Smash 2 tables and 3 chairs and collect 9 furniture debris.","Barricade the three windows. Do not click away before you get the message confirming the window is barricaded.","Defeat the venator if time runs out and one appears.","You can collect 3 extra debris from smashing the remaining chairs in this room to make subsequent rooms easier.","Unlock the blood lock and enter the second room. Another timer will start."],"t":"=First room="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Smash the table. You should have 6 furniture debris.","Barricade the two windows. Do not click away before the \"the window is barricaded\" message appears.","Defeat the venator if time runs out and one appears.","Unlock the blood lock and enter the third room."],"t":"=Second room="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Lift the table.","Defeat the venator.","Lift the table.","Unlock the blood lock and enter the fourth room."],"t":"=Third room="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Smash the chairs and table to the right of the door and the weapon racks which are against the north and south sides of the staircase.","Barricade the two windows. Defeat the venator if time runs out and one appears.","Solve the puzzle by making the following moves (if you mess up, you can reset the puzzle by talking to Polmafi):\n  - Rotate ring 'E' clockwise once.\n  - Rotate ring 'D' clockwise three times.\n  - Rotate ring 'C' clockwise twice.\n  - Rotate ring 'B' clockwise twice.\n  - Rotate ring 'A' clockwise once.","Climb upstairs."],"t":"=Fourth room="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Veliaf.","Climb the stairs on both sides and open the blood valves in each room.\n  - After defeating the venator in the western room, check on Ivan.","Back on the floor 3, enter the northern door and open the blood valve.","Climb down the stairs and solve the final ring puzzle by making these moves:\n  - Rotate ring A anticlockwise once.\n  - Rotate ring B clockwise three times.\n  - Rotate ring C clockwise once.\n  - Rotate ring D anticlockwise three times.\n  - Rotate ring E anticlockwise three times."],"t":"Second and third floors"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Before entering the fight you can use stat-boosting potions and prayer restoration potions to make the fight easier, but these items cannot be brought to the fight.","Climb the stairs in the ring puzzle room and prepare to fight Lowerniel Drakan.","Kill the three venators. (You can stand behind Vertida, Veliaf and Safalaan when attacking each of the venators and they won't attack you, saving you from needing to eat.)","Fight Lowerniel Drakan.\n  - Run away from bombs which appear after he says \"Ha ha ha!\".\n  - When he says things like \"Still trying to run?\" or \"You think you can escape?\" use Anticipation to avoid being stunned and dealt high damage.","Fight Lowerniel Drakan again.\n  - When he says \"Fear me!\" and transforms into a cloud of dust, run away from the cloud.\n  - When he says \"Embrace darkness\", stand within the sphere of lightning surrounding Safalaan.\n  - When he says \"Graaah!\", use Anticipation or Freedom if you get stunned.","Jump into the portal and fight Lowerniel Drakan again - he will use the same attacks as in the previous fights.","Talk to Lowerniel Drakan and then fight him for the final time.\n  - Avoid bombs as before.\n  - Move away from him when he is doing a special attack (rapid melee attacks) to avoid taking damage."],"t":"Confronting Drakan"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Select the \"finish\" option on Lowerniel Drakan.","Talk to Ivan. A cutscene will follow.","Talk to Ivan again. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Go to Varrock Palace and talk to King Roald. {Chat: 1 Talk about Lord of Vampyrium.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"The Lost Toys (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Lex on the west side of the Hair of the Dog tavern, south of the Canifis lodestone. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Off to Lex"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Squeeze all 13 plushies.","Teleport back to Canifis and talk to Lex. {Chat: 1 Yes.}}} Miniquest complete!"],"t":"Locations"}]},"The Lost Tribe":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Sigmund on the floor 2 of Lumbridge castle. {Chat: 1 Do you have any quests for me? > Accept}","Talk to the following NPCs about Lumbridge cellar around the castle until one of them mentions a goblin:\n  - Duke Horacio, in the same room. {Chat: 3 What happened in the cellar?}.\n    - {Chat: 4 What happened in the cellar?} if Dragon Slayer has been started/completed.\n  - Cook, just downstairs. {Chat: 4 Do you know what happened in the castle cellar?}\n    - {Chat: 2 Ask about what happened in the castle cellar} if Recipe for Disaster has been started but not finished; or\n    - {Chat: 5 Do you know what happened in the castle cellar?} if Cook's Assistant has not started.\n  - Hans, in the courtyard. {Chat: 4 Do you know what happened in the cellar?}\n    - {Chat: 2 Talk about something else. > 4 Do you know what happened in the cellar?} during 2026, for the 25th Anniversary celebrations.\n  - Father Aereck, in the church. If you have not previously spoken to him about gravestones, you must complete that dialogue, then speak to him again. {Chat: 1 Do you know what happened in the castle cellar?}\n  - Bob the smith, in his axe shop. {Chat: 4 Do you know what happened in the castle cellar?}","Talk to Duke Horacio. {Chat: 3 \"X\" says he saw something in the cellar.}\n  - {Chat: 4 \"X\" says he saw something in the cellar.} if Dragon Slayer has been started/completed."],"t":"The goblin"},{"n":"A light source","r":"","s":["Descend the trapdoor in the kitchen.","Mine the wall rubble to the east.","Squeeze through the hole and take the brooch.\n  - Optional: Mine the wall rubble to the south for a shortcut to the Lumbridge Swamp Caves.","Show the brooch to the Duke. {Chat: 3 I dug through the rubble...}\n  - {Chat: 4 I dug through the rubble...} if Dragon Slayer has been started/completed.","Talk to Reldo in Varrock Palace about the brooch. {Chat: 3 Ask about the brooch.}\n  - {Chat: 2 [Talk to Reldo.] > 3 Ask about the brooch.} if you completed Desperate Times.","Search the northern most bookcase on the western wall for a goblin symbol book.","Read the book to the end.\n  - Reldo will force-greet you and mention the Goblin Village.","Talk to Generals Bentnoze and Wartface in the Goblin Village. Make sure you have the brooch with you. {Chat: 2 Have you ever heard of the Dorgeshuun? > 3 It doesn't really matter > 2 Well either way they refused to fight > 3 Well I found a brooch underground... > 3 Well why not show me both greetings? > 1 Thanks}"],"t":"Dorgeshuun"},{"n":"A light source","r":"","s":["Grab your light source and return to Lumbridge Castle.","Climb down the trapdoor in the kitchen.","Squeeze through the hole in the wall you mined earlier.","Run through the Goblin Mine (pictured right).","Use the Goblin Bow emote near Mistag.","Right-click follow on Mistag."],"t":"Finding the lost tribe"},{"n":"7 backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Talk to the Duke. {Chat: 3 I've made contact with the cave goblins...}\n  - {Chat: 4 I've made contact with the cave goblins...} if Dragon Slayer has been started/completed.","Pickpocket Sigmund for a key.","Open the chest in the other room for a H.A.M. hood, shirt, and robe. Make sure to have 3 backpack spaces, otherwise the outfit might disappear with no means of receiving it again.","Enter the H.A.M. Hideout in the Lumbridge forest northwest of the Lumbridge Castle by opening and then climbing down the trapdoor.","Search the crate near the ladder for the missing silverware."],"t":"Sigmund's treachery"},{"n":"Silverware","r":"","s":["Return to the Duke. {Chat: 3 I found the missing silverware in the HAM cave!}\n  - {Chat: 4 I found the missing silverware in the HAM cave!} if Dragon Slayer has been started/completed.","Go back down the trapdoor in the castle kitchen.","Squeeze through the hole in the wall and follow Kazgar, who'll be waiting just on the other side.","Talk to Mistag.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Making peace"}]},"The Mighty Fall":{"sections":[{"n":"Light source","r":"","s":["Speak to councillor Ur-tag in the north-easternmost house on the floor 2 of Dorgesh-Kaan. {Chat: 2 How can I help? > Accept > Any}"],"t":"Graardor's march"},{"n":"Light source","r":"","s":["Climb-down the dark hole under tree in the Lumbridge Swamp. It is northwest of the water ruins.","Head to the north-east in the caves and speak to the group of leaders. {Chat: Any > 5 Enough questions. > Any > Any > Any > 2 I'm done here.}","Return to Dorgesh-Kaan and speak to Zanik, who is standing near Ur-tag back at the quest start. {Chat: 2 They don't stand a chance!}","Travel to the Bandosian camp on the east side of the Goblin Village and talk to Zanik once more (a Goblin Village sphere can be used). {Chat: 1 What do you mean, dying? > 2 Go on. > 1 Don't say that. We can still save them.}","Prepare for combat before proceeding to the next step."],"t":"Bandosian congregation"},{"n":"Weapon(s)","r":"Armour, and melee weapons (otherwise damage will be greatly reduced)","s":["Enter the portal to travel to Yu'biusk.","Go around the mountain, up one ladder and follow the path south until you reach Zarador. Talk to him. {Chat: 4 I have no more rules questions. > 3 I have no more questions.}","Head to your camp (travel west, down 2 ladders into a small room with a cooking pot). Talk to Burntmeat or My Arm. {Chat: 4 Enough questions. > 1 Great, thanks! > 1 That sure is a mystery.}","Kill the human infiltrator when he appears.\n  - If Burntmeat doesn't suggest searching his body, check the normal guide for possible solutions to progress the quest.","Return east to Zarador. {Chat: 1 I'll get right on it.}","Talk to the following goblins and kill them."],"t":"Return to Yu'biusk"},{"n":"Weapon(s)","r":"Armour, food, potions","s":["Return to Zarador once all infiltrators have been dealt with. {Chat: Any}","Use the bank chest beside Zarador to bank any forbidden items. He will also explain the rules of the tournament.","Talk to him once more to begin the tournament. {Chat: 1 Just bring it!}"],"t":"The Kyzaj tournament"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After defeating Yelps, you can choose to kill or spare him. {Chat: Any}","After you have made your choice speak to Zanik outside of the portal. {Chat: Any > 3 I need to get back to the tournament.}"],"t":"Yelps"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Zarador after talking to Zanik. He will inform you that your next opponent is Lol, the troll champion. {Chat: 1 Just bring it!}\n  - Suggested items: Stat-boosting potions such as overloads, extreme potions, or super potions, prayer potions, Enhanced Excalibur (or another good weapon), and lots of good food.\n  - Forbidden items: You cannot wear armour, including auras, pocket items, and jewellery.","After Lol has been defeated, you must once again choose to kill or spare him. {Chat: Any}"],"t":"Lol"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Zarador again and, after some dialogue, he will give you a weapon known as the Kyzaj, the namesake of the tournament. He will tell you that you must use it against your final opponent, General Graardor, the champion of the ourgs. {Chat: 3 Enough questions, give me the Kyzaj so I can practice with it.}","Talk to Zanik outside of the portal and she will teach you how to wield and use the Kyzaj. {Chat: 3 I need you to tell me about the Kyzaj.}","When you are ready to begin the final battle, return to Zarador and talk to him. {Chat: 1 Just bring it!}\n  - Rules for this round: You may not bring in your own weapons (you must use the Kyzaj, a tier 70 weapon), and prayer is disabled. You may equip armour and jewellery, although runes and non-combat items (excluding food) are forbidden.\n  - The Kyzaj will automatically equip itself once the fight starts; you will not be able to equip it beforehand.\n  - Fighting General Graardor he has three main mechanics.\n    - The first one is a ground smash that affects the centre of the arena. Being in the centre makes you get hit for up to 5k damage.\n    - The second attack is a cleave animation with no warning. Sidestep a few tiles and go back to attacking.\n    - The third mechanic he will destroy a section of the outer ring. This will hit for 5k damage if you do not move to another outer ring."],"t":"General Graardor"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Zarador throws Zanik into the arena, giving you two choices: you may either slay Zanik or spare her. {Chat: 4 Enough questions. I need to speak to Zanik > 3 I'm ready. > Any > Any > 2 Goodbye.}\n  - Your Kyzaj appearance will initially depend upon your decision to kill or spare Zanik (you receive the Bloodied kyzaj if you kill her or the Honourable kyzaj if you spare her), but these can be freely exchanged after the quest.","If you chose to kill Zanik, you must speak to General Graardor to find out his plans (Graardor can be found by going south from Zarador, up the ladder, and taking the first pathway to the west to the bank spot). {Chat: Any}","If you chose to spare Zanik, you must speak to her and find out her plans (Zanik is standing next to Zarador). {Chat: Any}","Return to Ur-tag in Dorgesh-Kaan.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The new Big High War God"}]},"The Needle Skips":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Start off using the fairy ring code AKQ or a Phoenix Lair Teleport scroll. You can also use the teleport from the memory strand in the currency pouch. Alternatively, teleport to Eagles' Peak lodestone and run north then west.","Run west of the Piscatoris Fishing Colony until you find a house.","Cross the water eastward over the rocks and go east to search the Needle. {Chat: Accept}","Search the Needle to obtain the shard of the needle.","After the cutscene investigate the body on the ground."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Commune with the shard.","Enter the word fire.","Go into the house to the north-west and interact/explore the fireplace.\n  - For full completion, find all of the other words listed on The Needle Skips#Chapter 1.","Go back to where the Needle is on the hill to the south-east and enter the temporal portal. {Chat: 1 Yes. Continue to Chapter 2}"],"t":"Chapter 1"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Commune with the shard again and enter the word birthday.\n  - For full completion, find all of the other words listed on The Needle Skips#Chapter 2.","Descend the stairs to the east and go back to the Needle.","Enter the temporal portal. {Chat: 1 Yes. Continue to Chapter 3}"],"t":"Chapter 2"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Commune with the shard again and enter the word wenla.\n  - For full completion, find all of the other words listed on The Needle Skips#Chapter 3.","Go back to the Needle and search it. {Chat: 1 Continue to the finale}"],"t":"Chapter 3"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Run back towards the house and harvest the buckthorn bush near the river.","Grind and crush both the leaf and berry.","Go upstairs in the house and give Primrose the smelling salts {Chat: 1 Yes.}.","Go back downstairs, search the bookcase to the north-east.","Talk to Megan and name the demon 'Metum'. {Chat: 1 Name the demon > # Metum}","Use the bottle of crushed berries on the stove on the west side of the house.","Return back to the Needle and use the buckthorn salve on Gail. Finish the dialogue and you will be teleported back to the house.","Finish the dialogue with Megan and go back to the Needle and pick up the note from gail.","Read the note then return to Megan inside the house.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The finale"}]},"The Path of Glouphrie":{"sections":[{"n":"Crystal saw or small crystal seed, drop or bring all crystalline discs if you have some of them","r":"around 10-14 backpack spaces to make room for crystalline discs","s":["Speak to King Bolren in the Tree Gnome Village. {Chat: Accept}","Squeeze through the loose railing to the west.","Climb down ladder to the east.\n  - If you no longer have a key from the Waterfall Quest, go to the east side of the cave and search the off-colour crate to get one.\n  - Note that the identically named a key also received from the Waterfall Quest will not work.","Go to the west side of the cave and talk to Golrie. {Chat: 2 Anti-illusion devices}","Use the key on the northern gate.","Search the chest to obtain crystalline discs.\n  - You may use drop trick to obtain more discs. You should drop all the discs to obtain a new batch of discs.","Talk to Golrie again. {Chat: 2 Anti-illusion devices}","Go to the eastern part of the cave and crawl through the tunnel (followers must be dismissed)."],"t":"Evil dumplings"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Push the monolith north.","Search chest to obtain more crystalline discs.\n  - You may use drop trick to obtain more discs. You should drop all the discs to obtain a new batch of discs.","Go to the next set of monoliths and push the south-western one north.","Push the north-west monolith east.","Search the western chests to the north.\n  - Be sure you receive a key to a chest and Yewnock's notes.","Push the small monolith south.","Right-click sing-glass on the singing bowl to transform the seed into a crystal chime.\n  - If you have a crystal saw instead of the small crystal seed, right-click revert-crystal on the singing bowl.","Push the north-west monolith west.","Open the mahogany chest, then search it to obtain the strongroom key.","Push the south-east monolith west and open the western gate.\n  - If you are stuck, exit using either of the tunnels.\n  - Enter the tunnel again from the other side.\n  - Push south-western monolith north.\n  - Open the western gate.","Read the lectern (Chapter 1). Doing so unlocks a music track."],"t":"Monolith puzzle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Referencing the table below, insert discs on the left side of the machine to equal the values on the right side. Use Yewnock's exchanger to obtain shapes of lesser values (if you are having trouble, see the full guide here).","Drop all discs and 'A key to a chest' as you no longer need them. They are not the same shapes that will be used in The Prisoner of Glouphrie.","Exit through the way you came or teleport, returning to Tree Gnome Village.","Kill the evil creature near King Bolren. (If it respawns, hop worlds and try again.)","Talk to the king.","Use the Spirit Tree to travel to the Tree Gnome Stronghold."],"t":"Oaknock's legacy"},{"n":"Crossbow, mithril grapple, crystal chime, armour and food to fight 3 level 82 bosses.","r":"Prayer potions, super energy potions, ring of duelling and earmuffs/masked earmuffs/slayer helmet.","s":["Climb to the floor 2 of the Grand Tree.","Talk to Gianne Jnr in the north-west corner. {Chat: 2 Longramble the explorer}","Head south-west of Castle Wars until you reach a bridge crossing a river. Ring of dueling, or fairy ring BKP and head north-west, or Yanille lodestone for quick access.","Just north-east of the bridge, grapple the tree to cross the river.","Talk to Longramble.","Head north and talk to the dying spirit tree.","After the cutscene, use the crystal chime on the spirit tree, or ring the crystal chime when next to the spirit tree.","Go west into the large sewer entrance."],"t":"Anima Mundi"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Travel through the dungeon until you reach a room with 4 doors, 2 warped tortoises, and a pit in the centre. (You may want to kill a warped tortoise/terrorbird for the achievement at this point as it is convenient to do so.)\n  - Running through the tar will turn your run off - simply turn it back on.\n  - You can Surge or Dive across the tar to avoid being slowed down.","Enter the east room and kill the 3 warped terrorbirds.","Peek through the hatch door on the east side of the room.\n  - People with sensitivity to light, seizures, or other ailments concerning flashing lights should be cautious during the escape scene (about 3–4 minutes). Recommended to hold spacebar and look away. You must watch the cutscene. In the event you cancel it, simply re-enter the room.","Speak to Hazelmere.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Warped"}]},"The Prisoner of Glouphrie":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["After asking what is next, you will be transported to the surface for a conversation with Golrana.","Talk with Golrana inside the Gnome Village.","Teleport to Castle Wars (or follow Elkoy out of the maze) and head to the highlighted area north of the Observatory and south of the Ourania altar (just north-east of the crystal tree). Make sure to pass the Observatory on its eastern side, alternatively use a 'Chipped' Watchtower teleport to teleport directly there.","Make sure to dismiss your pet/follower. Talk to Golrana. {Chat: 1 Yes, let's go.}","Walk up the path north-west until you reach a large dead tree. Search it, then climb-through it.","Investigate the ledge on the south end of the chasm (the wall near the rocks at the south of the room), continue the conversation with Golrana, she then will cross the chasm and throw a rope for you to cross.\n  - If you encounter a bug in which Golrana disappears, simply re-log and continue from two steps prior.","Move south and continue through the cave by jumping across gaps.","Travel north-west until reaching a water stream with stepping stones, but do not cross yet.","Before crossing the set of stepping stones, investigate the small crevice in the south wall to your immediate east.","Golrana will enter the crevice and emerge on the other side, she then will move a stone for you to complete the jumping part.","Cross the stepping stones, head southwest until you reach a crevice, then climb-through and out of the cave.","Go west to the ledge overlooking Lletya and investigate the sturdy tree, then climb-down it."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After a cutscene, take the handwritten book on the crate next to you and read it.","Search all crates, lamps, shelves and the picture in the room. You will be notified when you have gathered everything in the room.","Build the crate at the desk north of the ladder, then calibrate it.","Note down the number and colour value for all three.","Use the calculator below to get a working pair of shapes for each of the three value pairs. Note down the pair of shapes for each.","Clear any Skyboxes and filters to see the plain colours for this next part.","To change the colour, rotate the prism near the singing bowl until it reaches the desired colour.","To change the shape, right-click fill or empty the singing bowl. Every time you fill or empty the bowl, the crystal will respectively gain or lose a side.","To finalise the crystal into the shape, sing-glass on the singing bowl.","To obtain more minute crystal seeds, search the crate just next to the bowl.","Once you sing all 6 desired shapes, calibrate the device then insert the correct shapes into their corresponding slots.","Click the green tick mark at the bottom to complete the puzzle."],"t":"Bolrie's Lab"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb up the ladder and talk to Golrana underneath the steps just to the east of Lletya centre. {Chat: 1 Yes, let's go.} (If you teleport to Lletya instead of leaving via the ladder, she will not appear. You can return to the lab from a trapdoor in the sheep pen in the northwest Lletya.)","Once back up on the ledge, walk past the large boulder to the east, and Golrana should spot an air vent.","Open the air vent on the rock wall just south of the boulder, then climb-down it.","After the cutscene Climb-up the stairs just next to you.","Head east to the prison and rotate the watcher once.","Enter the prison through the metal doors. Talk to the guard. {Chat: any > any}","Pick-lock on the northwest cell door. Talk to Bolrie. {Chat: 1 I fell down the shaft and we got separated. > 2 Ilfeen. > 3 Gena. > 3 42. > 1 The Grand Tree.}","Lead Bolrie out of the jail and west to the corridor behind the stairs you just came up.","Continue through the door in the end and watch the cutscene.","After the cutscene, stand north of the big boulder and push it southward to block the air vent.","Talk to the gnomes for a cutscene.","Talk to them again to watch a second cutscene.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Arposandra"}]},"The Restless Ghost":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Father Aereck in Lumbridge Church. {Chat: 3 I'm looking for a quest! > Accept}","Go through the graveyard's southern exit and follow the shore to a mining site. Head west to a hut in the swamp."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Father Urhney inside the hut. {Chat: 2 Father Aereck sent me to talk to you. > 1 A ghost is haunting his graveyard.}","Go back to the graveyard and open a coffin located south of the catacombs.","Equip the Ghostspeak amulet and talk to the ghost. {Chat: 1 Yep. Now, tell me what the problem is.}"],"t":"Ghostspeak amulet"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head back through the southern gate of the graveyard, keep walking until you reach the mining site once again.","Look south-east of the mining site, there are some rocks. Search the rocks, you will receive a muddy skull.","Kill the skeleton or run away.","Go back to the graveyard, reopen the coffin and use the skull on the open coffin.","Quest completed!"],"t":"The skull"}]},"The Slug Menace":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Sir Tiffy Cashien in Falador park. {Chat: 1 The Slug Menace. > Accept > 3 Goodbye.}","Talk to Col. O'Niall on the pier in Witchaven (fairy ring BLR or Cape of Legends and run south). {Chat: 3 Who are the important people in Witchaven? > 4 That's enough for now.}","Talk to Mayor Hobb in the western building just south of Caroline. {Chat: Any > 2 What improvements are you making to the shrine? > 4 Nothing at the moment thanks.}","When you try to exit the building, Savant will contact you and request that you scan nearby the Mayor using the Commorb v2","Go back into the mayor's building, stand beside him and begin scanning.","Talk to Brother Maledict in the church. {Chat: 4 That's enough for now.}","Talk to Holgart to the north.","Report back to Col. O'Niall. {Chat: 4 That's enough for now.}"],"t":"Witchaven weirdness"},{"n":"Commorb v2, 2 backpack space","r":"Traveller's necklace, cape of legends","s":["Climb-down the old ruin entrance west of Witchaven.","Push the wall to your immediate east.","Enter the Wall Opening","Run through the cave until you reach a set of imposing doors.\n  - Take the Agility shortcut (requires level 30).","Savant will contact you.","Scan with the commorb to obtain a door transcription.","Pick up the dead sea slug on the ground nearby. You only need one.","Talk to Jorral in the small Outpost, north-west of West Ardougne. {Chat: 2 Translations}\n  - Traveller's necklace to the Outpost.","Savant will contact you while talking to Jorral and after.","Talk to Col. O'Niall in Witchaven (fairy ring BLR or cape of legends and run south).","Go near the church (a cutscene will begin).","Talk to Brother Maledict in the church. {Chat: 2 Talk about something else}"],"t":"Imposing door"},{"n":"Commorb v2, 1 swamp paste, 5 backpack spaces, 1 Dead sea slug","r":"","s":["Search the Mayor's study desk. You may fail, so repeat until you receive Page 1.","Talk to Ezekial Lovecraft in the fishing shop. {Chat: 4 You are a bit too strange for me. Bye.}","Talk to Col. O'Niall. This step requires 3 backpack spaces.","Try to use the swamp paste on the fragments.\n  - Savant will contact you.","Talk to Jeb to reach the fishing platform.","Talk to Bailey to the west.","Use the Sea slug glue on the fragments.","Use the image to solve the puzzle, there are 2 sides to the pieces so you might need to flip some."],"t":"Page pieces"},{"n":"At least 5 rune or pure essence, access to runecrafting altars","r":"","s":["With essence in your inventory, right click the papers to create 5 shapes.\n  - Page 1 to shape a blank earth rune.\n  - Page 1 to shape a blank air rune.\n  - Page 2 to shape a blank fire rune.\n  - Page 2 to shape a blank water rune.\n  - Page 3 to shape a blank mind rune.","Use the blank runes on their respective runecrafting altars.","Using spellbook teleports will use the runes you have created.","It is possible to fail at chiselling the essence and/or at converting the blank shapes at the altar. More rune essence will be required if unsuccessful.","Take caution as to not click on the altar, as your essence may be crafted into runes."],"t":"Shaped runes"},{"n":"The runes you created, Commorb v2, Melee equipment to kill a level 51 monster","r":"","s":["Climb down the old ruins in Witchaven, then enter the wall opening to your immediate east.","Follow the path to the imposing door again.","Use the runes on the door. Immediately after the placement of the last elemental block, a cutscene will happen prompting you into combat.","Kill the Slug Prince.","Talk to Sir Tiffy. {Chat: 1 The Slug Menace.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Final fight"}]},"The Spirit of War":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Interact with Kharen on the docks in the north-western City of Um, close to the transportation icon. {Chat: Accept}","Either:\n  - Speak to Ed in a building to the north-east to rent a boat. {Chat: 1 Take a boat out onto the lake.}\n  - Or choose the option Rent boat on Ed.","Rescue four Wayward Souls. They are ghastly sphere shapes floating above the Lake Mnemosyne in each of the four corners of the map. Some may be a good distance away from the coastline.\n  - High contrast mode is beneficial for spotting them.\n  - Dive and Surge can be used to speed up movement. The Mobile perk (must be on an armour piece, as both hands must be free) and using a powerburst of acceleration will also help.\n  - (Optional) Talk to Deano and Sammy when you see them for a reward of 25 souls each.","Return back to the docks and disembark in the dock south of Kharen. (Or teleport out of the rowboat.)"],"t":"Rescuing Wayward Souls"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Prepare for combat and don't forget to re-equip your weapons.","Interact with Kharen. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 Yes.}","Go through the dialogue to travel to Rasial's Citadel.","Speak to Rasial, the First Necromancer.","Fight Hermod, the Spirit of War in story mode.\n  - Kill minions when they appear, otherwise Hermod will be immune to damage","Speak to Rasial, the First Necromancer once more."],"t":"Fighting Hermod, the Spirit of War"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return and interact with Kharen with two free inventory spots.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"The Tale of the Muspah":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Erjolf on the mountain north-east of Rellekka. (Fairy ring dks) {Chat: Accept > 1 Okay, your secret is safe with me.}","Jump the flat rock to cross the river.","Enter the Cave opening to the north-west.","Talk to Erjolf about his progress and offer to help. {Chat: 2 Tell me more about your Trials. > 2 Perhaps I can help with your Trials. > 2 I'm ready to learn how to melt the ice.}\n  - Continue through the following dialogue and cutscene."],"t":"How to Become a Fremennik"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take at least 14 driftwood from the driftwood pile (can also be done in smaller batches if backpack space is a concern).","Make-fireraft with the driftwood you picked up. {Chat: 4 X}\n  - You should have 14 fire raft in the backpack."],"t":"Rafts of fire"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Block-stream using the ice mound to the west to block the west stream.","Jump the flat rock nearby on your side of the stream (you're now in the NW quadrant).","Jump the flat rock to the northeast (you're now in the NE quadrant).","Block-stream using the ice mound southeast of you to block the east stream.","Jump the flat rock to the northwest (you're now in the NW quadrant).","Walk to the tile as same as the picture shown below.","Launch 5 fire rafts quickly from the northern shore of the pool. Launch them from the same spot such that when they float south, they end up across the east side of the frozen armour and are blocked from leaving the cave by a rock.",": You do not need to face correctly to launch fire rafts, the player character will launch the raft into the water next to the tile they are standing on."],"t":"Melting east side"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Walk to the tile as same as the picture shown below.","Launch 3 fire rafts from the northern shore of the pool. Launch them on 3 adjacent spots that, when they float south, they end up on the north side of the frozen armour."],"t":"Melting north side"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Unblock-stream using blocked icy stream to the west (unblocks the west stream).","Jump the flat rock nearby (you're now in the SW quadrant).","Jump the flat rock to the southeast on your side (you're now in the SE quadrant).","Block-stream on the southern stream using the ice mound in the southeast.","Walk to the tile as same as the picture shown below.","Launch 4 fire rafts quickly from the eastern shore of the pool. Light them on the same spot that, when they float west, they end up across the south side of the frozen armour."],"t":"Melting south side"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Unblock-stream using blocked icy stream to the east.","Jump the flat rock to the southwest (you're now in the SW quadrant).","Block-stream using the ice mound to the west to block the west stream.","Walk to the tile as same as the picture shown below.","Launch 1 fire raft from the western shore of the pool. Light them on the spot that, when they float east, they end up on the west side of the frozen armour. You'll need to light the rafts in the western stream, not against the pool shore.","Jump the flat rock to the west (you're now in the NW quadrant).","Walk to the second tile in the picture shown below.","Launch 1 fire raft from the western shore of the pool."],"t":"Melting west side"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Erjolf. {Chat: 2 What should we do now? > 1 Yes, look at the creature.}","Exit the cave, climb down the mountain and go north across the narrow strip of land. Head north-east and past the sabre-toothed kyatts in the Rellekka Hunter area.","Talk to the natural historian. {Chat: 1 Don't you know what a yeti looks like? > 1 Are you any good at identifying creatures? > 1 Okay, I can start describing it now.}","Describe the creature to him. {Chat: 3 It's yellow. > 2 It has four arms. > 1 It has no legs, like a snail. > 2 It has spikes, which run down its spine. > 2 It has a spiky tail, with vicious spines. > 1 It has pincers, like a crab.}","Continue dialogue with the historian. {Chat: 1 What is the creature I described? > 2 Where can I find out more about this creature?}"],"t":"The monster in ice"},{"n":"","r":"Pollnivneach Teleport scroll or a ring of slaying","s":["Head north of Pollnivneach along the River Elid to a sand pile.","Dig the sand pile.","After Ali the Wise speaks, talk again and ask about the Muspah. {Chat: 3 I've found a creature just like this statue. > 3 Why do you think the creature I've found is a myth? > 3 If the Muspah is a myth, how could I have found it? > 3 How can I clear the ice from around the Muspah? > 4 Can you help me get back to the Muspah cave?}"],"t":"Terror of the mind"},{"n":"4 cut sapphires, 4 water runes , and 4 cosmic runes","r":"","s":["Head back to the Muspah cave.\n  - The ice cave where you started, by Fremennik Province lodestone, or fairy ring dks.","If you haven't obtained sapphires yet, mine the sapphire rocks nearby.","Cross the floating bridge.","Bore-sapphires in the ice block, then enchant-sapphires on it.","Pick up the four sapphires from the ground, or more will have to be obtained.","Talk to the Muspah and offer to help. {Chat: 1 I only wanted to help! > 1 That's okay. > 3 What were you doing in the ice? > 1 Tell me about the rejuvenation ritual. > 1 So what do you need now? > 5 Never mind.}"],"t":"The muspah's true form"},{"n":"4 water runes and 4 cosmic runes, 4 cut sapphires","r":"","s":["Talk to Erjolf just outside the chamber.","Exit the caves and head north to the icy Rellekka Hunter area.","On the western shore, make-canoe with the fallen log, then travel with the canoe.","Enter the cavern.","Dismiss any followers you have (if Jhallan still says to dismiss your pet, turn off any overrides you may have for other pets).","Slightly south, talk to Jhallan. {Chat: 1 Yes, follow me. We'll find somewhere you can rest.}","Lead him to the far south-west corner of the cave, away from the monsters.","At the end of the path, talk to Jhallan. {Chat: 1 Is this spot peaceful enough for you?}","After speaking, bore-sapphires on Jhallan, then enchant-sapphires on him."],"t":"Hibernating"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to the icy hunter area via the canoe or the Fremennik Province lodestone.","Talk to Erjolf to give him the Muspah tail.\n  - Talk to the natural historian for an experience lamp.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Back to the future"}]},"The Temple at Senntisten":{"sections":[{"n":"3 backpack spaces","r":"1 additional backpack space if you can receive Ali's pendant","s":["Talk to Ali the Wise in the northernmost building in Nardah. {Chat: 1 How goes the research? > 1 Well, I certainly don't like those of the Zamorakian faction. > 1 Zaros seems to be an honourable god. > Accept > 2 Can you help me get to the Digsite Exam Centre?}","Go to the Exam Centre.\n  - If you asked Ali for help getting there, he gave you a Dig Site pendant (or Ali's pendant if you have not unlocked the ability to create Dig Site pendants) to teleport directly there.\n  - Alternatively, teleporting to Varrock Dig Site with either pendant for the first time will grant you the Return to Senntisten achievement.","Talk to Dr. Nabanik outside of the Exam Centre south of the Digsite. {Chat: 1 (Whisper) Why are we speaking so quietly? > 1 Azzanadra? You are quite the master of disguise. > 1 Why are you here, away from the pyramid? > 2 What's Ali's part in this? > 3 Why all the secrecy? > 4 Just tell me what you want.}","Talk to Terry Balando inside the exam centre for a restoration certificate. {Chat: 1 I'm here about a close friend of mine: Dr Nabanik. > 1 He was in the pyramid for a very long time. > 1 I've seen those beetles and they're huge. > 1 He studies pyramids, particularly their interiors. > 1 He has an aged benefactor.}","Talk to Dr. Nabanik. He will give you a rope.","Use the rope on the winch in the north-east dig site, north of The Stormbreaker ship.","Operate the winch to enter the Digsite dungeon.","Talk to Azzanadra in the southern part of the dungeon. {Chat: 1 I'd like to talk about the temple. > 1 Is there anything I can do to help? > 1 Okay, what do I need to do? > 2 Tell me about the mission in the north. > Any}","Open the ruined backpack for a battered letter and heat globe.","Read the letter and then talk to Azzanadra. {Chat: 1 I'd like to talk about the temple. > 1 Tell me about the mission in Morytania. > 1 I have some questions about the mission in Morytania. > 2 Do you have any advice for me? > 3 Let's talk about something else. > 4 Tell me about the artefacts you need. > 1 Tell me about the fortress artefact. > 2 Tell me about the Barrows artefact. > 4 Never mind.}"],"t":"The mysterious archaeologist"},{"n":"","r":"Combat equipment and food","s":["Travel to the Barrows.","Kill the six Barrows Brothers found in their tombs below the ground.\n  - Barrows amulets can be used to skip killing up to three brothers.\n  - Amulets can only be used on the tombs before the brother is summoned.\n  - The final brother must be killed without using an amulet.","Once all six brothers are dead, search the chest at the centre of the tunnels beneath the crypts to get the Barrows icon."],"t":"Barrows icon"},{"n":"Telekinetic grab runes, heat globe from the ruined backpack","r":"Food and armour, as you will encounter some aggressive high-level (100+) icefiends and waterfiends, even for players with a high-level combat","s":["Go to the Ghorrock fortress:\n  - First use the canoe near Erjolf from Tale of the Muspah for a quick access. It is located on the west coast of the Rellekka Hunter area, north of fairy ring code dks.\n  - Go east and place the heat globe on the pedestal near the ice block entrance.\n  - Squeeze past the ice block.","Enter the fortress through the south entrance and climb-up the stairs to the west.","Run to the south-east corner of the castle and climb-down the stairs east.","Scale up the damaged wall north of the door.","Climb down the smashed rampart in the north-west corner.","Enter the trapdoor in front of you."],"t":"Frostenhorn"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Run east and take the heat globe.","Return to the entrance room of the basement, and place the heat globe on the pedestal on the west side.\n  - A waterfiend will be released. It is immune to fire damage, but does not need to be killed.","Go inside the west room, then right-click the radiant pedestal to cast Telekinetic Grab on it.","Use the globe on this room's pedestal. Go down the trapdoor.\n  - A waterfiend will be released. It is immune to fire damage, but does not need to be killed."],"t":"Upper level"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pick up the globe in the southern room.","Use it on the pedestal back in the northern room with the ladder. 2 waterfiends will spawn.","Loot the crates in the south room for 40 law runes and 300 air runes.","Go to the east room and take the globe from the pedestal for an imperfect heat globe.","Exit the dungeon the way you entered."],"t":"Lower level"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Scale the damaged wall to the west, then head to the north-east corner to the destroyed pedestal.","Insert-globe in the smashed globe-holder on the ground.","Choose the push option on the smashed globe-holder on the ground.","After a cutscene, climb down the smashed rampart in the north-west corner.","Return to the dungeon by re-entering the trapdoor. {Chat: 1 Yes, carry on from where I was.}"],"t":"Surface"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go down the trapdoor in the western room.","Run through the dungeon and take the heat globe from the pedestal in the southwestern corner.","Head back east through the hallway you ran through until you reach the southeast corner, where the path turns north.","At that corner, look for a pipe on the south wall.","Choose the \"Place-globe\" option on the pipe.","Choose the \"Whack\" option on the pipe.","Continue into the southeastern room and climb the ladder to go up."],"t":"Lower level"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head west and kill the ice demon (it cannot be damaged by water spells).","Take the Frostenhorn that it drops."],"t":"Upper level"},{"n":"Barrows icon and Frostenhorn","r":"","s":["Return to Azzanadra with the items back at the Senntisten Temple underneath the Dig Site. {Chat: 1 I'd like to talk about the temple. > 1 I have something here for you. > 1 What does the Frosthorn do? > 1 Okay, what do I need to obtain next?}\n  - The Dig Site pendant can be used to teleport outside the temple (option 2).","Back outside near the winch, talk to the Assassin for a relic. {Chat: 1 Mask or no mask, I remember you. > Any > Any > Any}","Return to Azzanadra. {Chat: 1 I'd like to talk about the temple. > 5 Anyway, what now? > 2 I'm not interested, I just want a reward > 3 Boring! Get on with it!}","After the cutscene, speak to Azzanadra again. {Chat: 1 I'm glad I could help. > Any}","Quest complete!"],"t":"The big bang"}]},"The Tourist Trap":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["If you don't have desert clothes, buy them from Shantay.","Begin the quest by talking to Irena (south of Shantay Pass). {Chat: 1 What's the matter? > 1 When did she go into the desert? > 3 I'll look for your daughter. > 1 Okay Irena, calm down. I'll get your daughter back for you. > Accept}","Run south and slightly west to the gate of the Desert Mining Camp.","Making sure not to attack him, talk to Mercenary Captain (the one with the all-grey shield). {Chat: 1 Wow! A real captain! > 2 I'd love to work for a tough guy like you! > 2 Can't I do something for a strong Captain like you? > 2 Sorry Sir, I don't think I can do that. > 1 It's a funny captain who can't fight his own battles!}","Kill the Mercenary Captain to obtain a metal key.\n  - The metal key can be added to the steel key ring after One Small Favour.","Unequip all armour (includes amulets, rings, etc.) and weapons, and keep them unequipped whenever inside the mining camp or mine."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Open the gate to enter the camp.","Go east to the mine door entrance and talk to the male slave on the east of the camp (it's the one who never mines). {Chat: 1 I've just arrived. > 2 Oh yes, that sounds interesting. > 1 What's that then? > 1 I can try to undo them for you. > 1 It's funny you should say that... > 1 Yeah, okay, let's give it a go. > 1 Yes, I'll trade.}\n  - If a guard catches you unlocking the slave's chains and you end up in the cell, bend the bars on the window and escape. Talk to the slave to try again.","While wearing the slave outfit, open the mine door entrance. The outfit must be equipped any time you enter the mine.","Upon entering, head north and follow the cave around until you come to a guarded cave entrance.","Making sure not to attack him, talk to one of the guards. {Chat: 2 I'd like to mine in a different area. > 2 Yes sir, you're quite right sir. > 2 Yes sir, we understand each other perfectly.}","Head back to the mine doors and exit.","Unequip your slave clothing and leave the Desert Mining Camp through the gate.","Run west to the Bedabin Camp.","Talk to Al Shabim in the southernmost tent to receive the Bedabin key. {Chat: 1 I am looking for a pineapple. > 1 Yes, I'm interested.}"],"t":"Entering the mine"},{"n":"Bronze bar, 10 feathers","r":"","s":["Run east back to the Desert Mining Camp and climb up the ladder in the white building.","On the western wall search the southernmost bookcase for a book on sailing.","Talk to Captain Siad in the same room and ask him if you can chat with him, then mention the sailing book. {Chat: 1 I wanted to have a chat? > 5 You seem to have a lot of books! > 3 So, you're interested in sailing? > 1 I could tell by the cut of your jib.}","Open the chest beside the table to get the plans.","Go back to the Bedabin Camp and show Al Shabim the plans. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm very interested. > 1 Yes, I'm kind of curious.}","Enter the tent to the north.","Use the experimental anvil with a bronze bar in your inventory and answer the prompt {Chat: 1 Yes. I'd like to try.} to create a prototype dart tip.","Use a feather on the dart tip to make a prototype dart.","Take this back to Al Shabim. He will take the prototype dart, technical plans, and Bedabin key in exchange for a bronze dart and Tenti pineapple."],"t":"The plans"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Wear the slave outfit, head back down into the mine and give the pineapple to one of the guards.","Walk through the mine cave and run east to the mine cart.","Choose \"Search\" option on one of the empty barrels nearby and answer the prompt {Chat: 1 Yeah, cool!} to take it.","Choose \"Search\" option on the mine cart to ride it to the other side, answering the prompt to confirm. {Chat: 1 Yes, of course.}\n  - Failing to enter the cart will cause minor damage. If you fail, attempt to enter the cart again.","Go down the northwestern passageway containing a large number of slaves at the end and you will find Ana.","Use the barrel in your inventory on Ana to squeeze her inside it, and head back to the mine cart."],"t":"Finding Ana"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use Ana on the mine cart first, then ride it yourself when it comes back. {Chat: 1 Yes, of course.}","Search the barrels around the cart and retrieve the one that has Ana in it.","Use the winch bucket north-west of the cart to put the barrel on it.","Accept the guard's offer for help and give him a compliment. {Chat: 1 Yes please. > 1 I said you were very gregarious!}","Head back to the surface and go to the winch bucket in the south-western corner of the camp.\n  - Do not remove your slave clothes at any point.","Operate it and then search the barrel west of it.","Use Ana on the wooden cart at the centre of the camp.","Talk to the Mine cart driver. (Warning: If you use the wrong responses you'll have to rescue Ana again!){Chat: 2 Nice cart. > 2 One wagon wheel says to the other, 'I'll see you around'. > 1 'One good turn deserves another' > 3 Fired... no, shot perhaps! > 3 In for a penny in for a pound. > 3 Well, you see, it's like this... > 1 Prison riot in ten minutes, get your cart out of here! > 2 You can't leave me here, I'll get killed!}\n  - If you fail, you need to head back into the deepest part of the mine with a barrel and get Ana out again.","Search the cart and answer the prompt {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll get on.} to get on.","Run northeast towards Shantay Pass and talk to Irena.","Congratulations, quest complete!"],"t":"Rescuing Ana"}]},"The Vault of Shadows":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Dr Nabanik near the bank chest at Kharid-et Dig Site. He will \"loan\" you any of the spell scrolls that you are unable to obtain. {Chat: Accept}","You will need to activate four buttons within the dig site. After activating each button you will be able to enter the corresponding door and complete a puzzle. While the buttons may be activated in any order, the puzzles are always received in the same order.","You will need to activate all shadow anchors or wait until the Pylon is active to do the 4th puzzle. If you don't have a ring of visibility or have the ability to permanently see the Shadow Realm, this is also required for a step after gathering 500 divination memories.\n  - You will need 80 batteries to charge all eight anchors. You can get these batteries by excavating in Kharid-et Dig Site or by doing Zarosian I collection for Soran, Emissary of Zaros in Varrock. He will give you 20 batteries each time you repeat the collection (after the first time)."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"Pontifex signet ring, 'Incite Fear' spell scroll (or 'Incite Fear' spell scroll (loaned))}}{{Checklist; * Head into the prison block section of the dig sit","r":"","s":["Enter the eastern door which leads to the solitary confinement area.\n  - If you haven't completed Time Served but you have the repaired artefact in your inventory, then just inspect the ancient mechanism to the North. Insert the artefact and then the eastern door will open.","Go down to the southern end of the corridor, there will be an inactive dial on the west wall, just before the last empty room.","Cast an 'Incite Fear' spell scroll whilst standing next to the dial.","Press the ice button and enter the vault {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Pick up the praetor's log page 1 and right click Transcribe."],"t":"Ice button"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Set your compass to face north (so the central vault is on the east of the screen).","Using the image, press each button in order. Backwards turns are denoted by '. For example, SW' means turn south-west back.","You may cancel pressing the wrong direction (e.g. SW instead of SW') by pressing the same button in the other direction (e.g. SW'). You can then proceed with the right move (e.g.SW').","If you make a mistake, you can leave and return via the button on the western wall to reset the puzzle.","NE, E, NE', SW', S, S","SE, SE, C, N'","S', W, NW","The final combination of the dials on the wall is, from top to bottom: shadow, blood, smoke, ice.","The door will open, and you will automatically receive praetor's log page 2, transcribe the page.","To leave, you can use the Vault exit to the south-west."],"t":"First puzzle"},{"n":"Pontifex signet ring, 'Exsanguinate' spell scroll (or 'Exsanguinate' spell scroll (loaned))}}{{Checklist; * Head to the Main Fortress of the Kharid-et Dig Site (first room) and go to the south-east corner (the chapel","r":"","s":["Pass the Pontifex barrier and find the inactive dial on the northern wall, directly north of the Orcus altar.","Cast a 'Exsanguinate' spell scroll whilst standing next to the dial.","Press the Blood button and enter the vault {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Blood button"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Set your compass to face north (so the central vault is on the north of the screen).","Using the image, press each button in order.","Backwards turns are denoted by '. For example, SW' means turn south-west back.","C', C', NE, SE, C'","NE', NE', C', C', NE'","C', SW', SE, C, SE","C, SE, SW, C, SW'","C, C","The final combination of the dials on the wall is, from top to bottom: shadow, blood, smoke, ice.","The door will open and you will automatically receive praetor's log page 3, transcribe the page.","To leave, you can use the Vault exit to the south-east."],"t":"Second puzzle"},{"n":"Pontifex signet ring, 'Smoke Cloud' spell scroll (or 'Smoke Cloud' spell scroll (loaned))}}{{Checklist; * Return to the main fortress of the Kharid-et Dig Site and go directly north of the Pontifex barrier, by the ove","r":"","s":["Find the inactive dial on the wall immediately west of the oven.","Cast a 'Smoke Cloud' spell scroll whilst standing next to the dial.","Press the smoke button and enter the vault {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Smoke button"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Walk to the large door and stand in the centre of the control dials.","This time, set your compass facing west (unlike the other puzzles), making you face the big door.","Using the image, press each button in order.","Backward turns are denoted by '. For example, 5' means turn 5 back.","2, 7', 2'","1, 1, 8', 1', 1'","3, 3, 8, 3, 3 - Second row complete (all red)","7', 4, 8, 4' - Puzzle complete","The final combination of the dials on the wall is, from top to bottom: shadow, blood, smoke, ice.","The door will open and you will automatically receive praetor's log page 4, transcribe the page.","To leave, you can use the Vault exit to the east."],"t":"Third puzzle"},{"n":"All eight Shadow anchors active, or Pylon active, 'Animate Dead' spell scroll (or 'Animate Dead' spell scroll (loaned))","r":"","s":["For the shadow button, you will either need to have activated all the shadow anchors or wait until the Kharid-et pylons are active.","You will need 80 batteries in total to charge all 8 shadow anchors.","To quickly obtain batteries, you can repeatedly complete the Zarosian I collection for Soran, Emissary of Zaros in Varrock. He will give you 20 batteries each time you repeat the collection (after the first time).","Normally, it's best to charge the shadow anchors first (since you will have to charge it sooner or later anyway, you might as well do it now).","However, if the power tower is about to activate (90% or higher), you can consider waiting. Even so, you should use all the batteries (10 of each) to charge the shadow anchor instead of the pylon (because 10 batteries only increase the activation progress by 0.01%), just in case you cannot complete the charging within 30 minutes.","Return to the Main Fortress of the Kharid-et Dig Site and enter the war room by clicking the praetorium war table (middle of the Main Fortress)","Find the inactive dial on the western wall in the small western room.","Cast an 'Animate Dead' spell scroll whilst standing next to the dial.","Press the Shadow button and enter the vault {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Shadow button"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Set your compass so that it is facing south (so the central vault is at the top of the screen).","Using the image, press each button in order.","Backward turns are denoted by '. For example, 5' means turn 5 back.","3, 3, 1', 3, 3","1', 5', 2, 2, 4","1', 3', 1, 5', 3","3, 5, 2', 3', 2'","3, 3, 4, 4, 3, 3","The final combination of the dials on the wall is, from top to bottom: shadow, blood, smoke, ice.","The door and now the vault will open."],"t":"Fourth puzzle"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pick up the shadow engrammeter (depleted) from the centre of the vault.","Collect 500 divination memories (vibrant tier or higher). Recharge the Shadow engrammeter when you have an inventory full of memories to charge it. Enriched memories count as double.","Return to the centre of the vault via any of the dials and Operate the engrammeter.","Take Trindine's memory to Dr Nabanik. {Chat: 3 I want to talk about mysteries. > # The Vault of Shadows.}\n  - You will receive the memory as a book, and be granted 25,000 Divination experience.","Return to the vault using any of the dials.","Speak to Praetor Trindine in the centre. This will complete The Vault of Shadows mystery.\n  - If the shadow anchors weren't activated, or Pylon isn't active, you will need to wear a ring of visibility or have the ability to permanently see the Shadow Realm.","Return to and speak to Dr Nabanik.","Speak to him again after the cutscene.}} Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"The Void Stares Back":{"sections":[{"n":"3 free inventory spaces","r":"","s":["Talk to Korasi in Falador Park. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"5 backpack spaces, limestone brick, hard leather, black full helm (bugged), black platebody (bugged), and black platelegs (bugged); recommended = Food, armour, and a melee weapon","r":"","s":["Go to the entrance of the Black Knights' Fortress north-west of the Edgeville Monastery.","Equip the black full helm (bugged), black platebody (bugged), and black platelegs (bugged). Open the portcullis. Commander Colby will yell at you and teleport you.\n  - Once you finally get to the storage room, your helmet will be taken.","If you leave the room at any point (including disconnect), or once your helmet is taken, you will no longer be able to use the Black Knights' Fortress to return to the storage area.\n  - Instead, enter via the Black Knights' Base inside the Taverley Dungeon.\n  - Inside the Black Knights' Base, enter the door south from the conquest map table, which is found in the middle of the floor."],"t":"Infiltration"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Captain Gilroy.","Attempt to take an item from any crate.","Speak to Gilroy. {Chat: 3 I think I've got it, sir.}","Talk to Gilroy again. {Chat: 3 actually weigh 4 > 1 are of weight 2 > 5 should be labelled 6 > 2 really weigh 3 > 4 need to be marked 5}.","Balance the scale on the wall to the south, arrange the weights to make 15 on each side. (Top: 3-5-3-4 and Bottom: 2-2-5-6)","Proceed to the next room."],"t":"Room 1"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill the enemies in the room and pick up the security blocks that are dropped.","Talk to Gilroy. {Chat: 2 What do we do now?}","Exit the room and head to the jail, northeast of the storage room, and search the crate for a piece of hard leather.","Search a crate in the kitchen for some logs, just north of the jail.","Head to the tiny forge on the west side of the base (icon on minimap).","Search the crate in the south-west corner of the forge room for a limestone brick.","Return to the forge and repair it.","Use the logs on the forge to fuel it.","Light the forge.","Use the broken security block on the forge to repair it.","Go back into the room with Gilroy and place all the blocks within the western wall.","Proceed to the next room."],"t":"Room 2"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Click on the panel on the western wall. {Chat: 2 Search the panels for magical traps.}","Open the panel.","Drag the tiles into the panels so that a horizontal line is going across all three panels, while filling the empty spaces. Press confirm once completed.","Proceed to the next room."],"t":"Room 3"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Reveal yourself and explain the danger to Lord Daquarius. Accept the allegiance. {Chat: 1 Yes, sir. > 3 Explain the danger in calm, logical terms. > 1 Okay, I'll do it.}","Talk to Korasi.","Talk to Commodore Tyr. {Chat: 1 I'm ready.}\n  - At this point you can equip your own armour again instead of the Black Knight (bugged) armour.","Enter the portal and watch the cutscene. {Chat: 1 You bet!}",": Make sure you go through each dialogue box, otherwise it will kick you out of the portal and you will have to start the cutscene from the start.","A game of modified conquest must be played and won.\n  - Spinners are very powerful but do not heal like in Pest Control.\n  - Ravagers have the movement range of Scouts and the damage rate of a Knight.\n  - Shifters are less of a threat than other units and can be tanked if need be.\n  - Torchers are similar to Mages.\n  - Defilers are similar to Archers.\n  - Splatters will explode and deal 100 life points of damage to any adjacent unit that is within 1 square.","Win the game and proceed to the next room."],"t":"A little game"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Sacrifice either Korasi or Jessika.","Speak to Valluta before stocking for the fight or Sir Tiffy won't teleport you back.","Make all necessary preparations to fight the Pest Queen. Korasi's sword will be the primary weapon during the fight and its Special attacks will be used a lot.\n  - It may be helpful to use manual attack abilities rather than Revolution.\n  - You can use necromancy to trivialise the encounter. Summon conjures prior to equipping Korasi's sword, and keep your necromancy offhand equipped. Ghost will provide full sustain without food, and skeleton will do the majority of the damage.","Kill the Pest Queen.\n  - The Weapon Special attack is located under Constitution abilities.\n  - If you die, talk to Sir Tiffy in Falador park and he will teleport you back to the portal. You will lose the weapon if you die. Reclaim this from Jessika/Korasi before you attack the Pest Queen again. {Chat: 3}\n  - Build your adrenaline up more than 60% then use the special attack \"Disrupt\" to stun the Pest Queen when she raises her head and starts shaking for several seconds.\n  - Hurt but don't kill the spawning Elite defilers to defend Void Knight archers. They need to be focussed on you so more don't respawn and so they don't hurt your archers.\n  - More in-depth strategies can be found here."],"t":"The Pest Queen"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Korasi or Jessika. Decide who to let deal with Wizard Grayzag. {Chat: Any}","Talk to Commodore Tyr.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"The World Wakes":{"sections":[{"n":"Gear and food for fights.","r":"","s":["Talk to Orlando Smith, West of the Legends' Guild (fairy code BLR, or use the Ardougne lodestone). {Chat: 1 Can I help at all? > 1 So you just need me to open the doors? > Accept}","Open the door.","Investigate the following 6 artefacts:\n  - Inactive obelisk (north-west)\n  - Stone carvings (north)\n  - The other stone carvings (north-east)\n  - Clouded vials (north-east)\n  - Dusty parchment (south-east)\n  - Shattered blade (south)","Investigate the Guthixian statue to the east.","Enter the next room to the east and kill the 3 automatons.\n  - You must finish the entire dialogue with the Automatons before clicking to attack them (there's a small break in the dialogue) or you will have to redo the cutscene again.\n  - Warning: Automatons can deal high damage to players standing within their special attack range. Lower-level players should use ranged, magic, or necromancy to attack them.","Talk to Sliske. {Chat: 3 I, [Player], stand before you! Do your worst! > 1 What does this mean? > 1 What do you mean, trouble? > 1 Okay then.}","Continue talking to Sliske after the cutscene. {Chat: 1 What do you gain from telling me this? > 2 So how do I come into this? > 1 I already know my decision. > Any}","If Kree'arra and Commander Zilyana don't spawn, talk to Sliske again."],"t":"Helping Orlando"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After the cutscenes, talk to Kree'arra. {Chat: 3 Why are you following Zilyana, then? > 3 If you want to get rid of me, you'll have to do it the hard way.}","Defeat Kree'arra. Avoid standing on the tornadoes.","Pass through the door (east)."],"t":"Defeating Kree'arra"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Run to the other side of the room and activate the control panel. {Chat: 1 Guthix is in trouble. I'm here to protect him.}","While using the control panel you can release a boulder by clicking on the dispenser in the corner of the screen. The goal is to get the boulder from the dispenser to the receptacle tile (circular cavity with a green dot).","To solve the puzzle:\n  - Rotate the tracks to create a path from the dispenser to the green hole, matching the solutions below (NOTE: puzzle can crash based on camera settings try classic)\n  - Click the appropriate dispenser to release the boulder\n  - When the boulder halts at a gate, wait for the next tile to auto-rotate such that the path continues, and click the gates to release the boulder at the right time"],"t":"Lock mechanism"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After the cutscenes (skippable), view the strange map to the east.","Answer four randomised questions to balance the pillars (Chaos, Order, Good, and Evil must all be exactly 50%). Refer to the below table and pick the appropriate answers:","Give the group a motivational speech {Chat: 1 Enthuse the group. > 1 Reinforce the importance of protecting the edicts. > 1 Highlight the strengths of the group.}","Drag the guardian icons to the correct threat based on the hover text in the top row:","Talk to Juna. {Chat: 1 I've finished setting up. > 1 I'm happy with the formation for now.}","Finish the dialogue after the cutscene (including a pause in dialogue) or you will be forced to watch it again.","Drink from the elixirs if you need to restore your health or prayer.","Note: you can bank if you talk to Druidess. Look for the bank icon on the minimap."],"t":"Leading the guardians"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the north-west storage wing guarded by Chaeldar and Thaerisk Cemphier. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm sure. Let's go.}","Defeat General Graardor. Protect from Melee is preferred.","Be aware of his special attacks:\n  - He reflects your damage when he shouts \"Graardor protect!\".\n  - Move away from his charging path when he shouts \"Graardor mad!\".\n  - Avoid the falling debris by looking at the shadows when he shouts \"Graardor smash!\".","Enter the exit."],"t":"Defeating Graardor"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the north storage wing guarded by Cres. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm sure. Let's go.}","Defeat Zemouregal. Bringing Antipoison is recommended.","Protect from magic works best here.","Start by killing the two dark portals.","Stay away from Decaying portals or kill them quickly.","Attack Zemouregal to about 70%.","Kill 4 more dark portals.","Kill the decaying portals to lower his defence, if necessary.","Finish Zemouregal.","Enter the exit."],"t":"Defeating Zemouregal"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the south-west storage wing guarded by Death. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm sure. Let's go.}","Defeat K'ril Tsutsaroth. Be aware of his special attacks.","When he shouts \"You cannot stand against Zamorakian might!\" avoid the spikes that appear under you.","When he shouts \"Run, coward!\" he will charge forwards, simply move out the way.","When he shouts \"Guthix will die in the name of Zamorak!\" you will need to constantly run from K'ril otherwise he will hit you very rapidly.","Enter the exit."],"t":"Defeating K'ril Tsutsaroth"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the south storage wing guarded by Fiara and Valluta.","Defeat Enakhra.","Protect from Magic is preferred.","She will sometimes start to steal from your health. Hide behind any obstacle to stop her. It may help to disable auto-retaliate since her ranged attacks can unintentionally draw you out of hiding.","The lower your health, the less she heals. Low-healing food like cakes, pizzas, or a bunyip can keep you alive for a long time.","She will occasionally stun you. Activating Freedom will free you.","Enter the exit."],"t":"Defeating Enakhra"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Cres in the center.","Talk to Juna in the east.","Defend Juna from the spiritual enemies for 2 minutes.","Jump over a barrier to safety near Juna and simply repair barriers as they slowly become half-broken.","Alternatively, kill the enemies, which are fairly weak. Attacks that hit multiple enemies simultaneously are effective, such as Ancient Magicks.","Talk to Azzanadra after the skippable cutscene. {Chat: Any > Any}"],"t":"Protecting Juna"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Note: The next area does not require combat, but contains environmental hazards that can easily lead to unsafe death, and does not allow teleporting out. You may wish to bank now.\n  - Teleport out to bank all gear and items; bring high-healing food. Fireballs do 20% of your max life points rapidly while running under them. Do not bring life points boosting gear as it will be harder to out-eat them.\n  - Return via the Ardougne lodestone and run east to the entrance of the chamber.","Enter the shattered wall.","Run down the path, avoiding the boulders and flames. If you get trapped between ice spikes, click them to break free.","After the skippable cutscene, walk east down to the pedestal in front of Guthix. He will teleport you.","Walk between the islands, talking to Guthix along the way. {Chat: Any}","On your return, talk to one of the guardians. {Chat: Any > Any}","After a skippable cutscene, Saradomin will appear in front of you. Talk to him. {Chat: Any > Any}","Talk to Juna (10 free inventory slots are required).","Quest complete!"],"t":"Guthix"}]},"Thok It To 'Em (saga)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Find the scribbled note while raiding the 30-35 Abandoned 2 floors of Daemonheim, and recover memory of it.","Talk to Skaldrun and ask him to tell you a story. {Chat: 1 Forgot what he says here > 1 Tell me a story}\n  - You need to bank everything, including the ring of kinship.\n  - If the option to start this saga is not available, that means you haven't found the scribbled note on the floor inside Daemonheim."],"t":"Beginning of the story"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill Stomp like you would in a normal dungeon."],"t":"Starting room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["As Thok, continue down the ladder and kill The Thing with eyes."],"t":"Thok"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Continue east and exorcise dark spirit to the east.","Kill the 2 enemies in the next room and continue south.","Kill the 3 enemies in the next room and continue east.","Pick up the silver curvy thing to the southeast and return back to the starting room to unlock the silver wibbly thing.","Activate the big rock and kill all the squishy ghosts until the monolith is fully charged then continue north."],"t":"Big rock room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head west and kill the coward with a bow.","Once he has been killed, run back to the room where the Silver curvy thing was found (marked by the summoning icon on the minimap).","Next, continue through the rooms to the east, north and east again.","Take the Red block from the floor.\n  - If additional food is required, Crunchy rune rocks can be acquired from the supply table."],"t":"Coward with a bow"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Run back through the rooms: west, south, and 2 more rooms west.","Enter the southern door, then go west by unlocking the red wibbly thing.","Attempt to imbue the tiles 3 times. On the third try, Thok will manage to imbue all the tiles correctly.","Take the blue pointed thing in the northwestern corner of the room.","Go into the next room with the bulky warrior. Kill him and move out of the direction he is facing if he prepares to charge.","Once the bulky warrior has been defeated, return to the room with the summoning icon indicated on the minimap."],"t":"Bulky warrior"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Unlock the Blue wibbly thing.","Upon entering the room, take a pickaxe from the rock and equip it.","Attack the Armoured cow thing until its armour is destroyed.","Continue the fight with Thok's sword.","After the fight, go back to the room with the supply table (North-East side)."],"t":"Armoured cow thing"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["In the room to the north, kill the Ramokee skinweaver first, then move on to killing the other ramokees.","Moving to the next room, talk to Thok-blocker until it allows you to enter the room.","Pick up the Orange stick thing in the southeast corner of the room, and return to the room to the east.","Unlock the Orange wibbly thing to face Gobby demon.","Thok should be able to kill the demon before any of its attacks are used. However, if portals appear on the ground, move away from them and continue attacking.","Go back through the door and take the door to the west."],"t":"Gobby demon"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill Warped Gulega. Avoid the 1 lifepoint attack by moving 1 square away when tentacles appear on the ground.","Talk to Pretty Lass. {Chat: 1 [Tell her about Marmaros] > 2 [Take her to Marmaros]}","Kill the Walking ice cube.\n  - Every 33% damage dealt it will encase itself in ice and running around the dungeon will avoid the player from being hit."],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Thok Your Block Off (saga)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Find the rock and twine bundle while raiding the 36-40 occult floors of Daemonheim, and recover memory of it.","Talk to Skaldrun and ask him to tell you a story. {Chat: 1 Forgot what he says here > 1 Tell me a story}\n  - You need to bank everything, including the ring of kinship."],"t":"Beginning of the story"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill all the enemies in the first room and finish dialogue with Marmaros.","Enter the boss door to the west.","Watch the cutscene and climb down the ladder to the west. }}"],"t":"Starting room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head north and clear more enemies than Marmaros by clearing out the rooms as fast as possible, you are required to have at least 4 more kills than Marmaros at the end of the dungeon for unabridged tome. Continue this throughout the entire dungeon (legacy mode greatly increases hits). Auto-retaliate helps too.","Head west, then west (reinforcement room) and pick up the Orange thing, west and enter the Orange shield door.","Pick Frilly plants to the north of the room and mine Crumbly stuff just west of that. Make stuff on the Spinny stuff-maker south-east of the room to make the Best Thing Ever.","Head east, north, east (reinforcement room) and pick up the Blue brick, unlock and proceed through the Blue rectangle room.","Enter the Blue rectangle room again to give Pretty Lass the Best thing ever.","Continue north then west and fish the bubbling water to find Mini-marm and Mrs mini-marm. This equips them as weapons which increases damage dealt.","Continue north, then east (reinforcement room), then east again, and then south. {Chat: 1 Let's go!}\n  - DO NOT pick up the Red pointy stone.","Attack and kill the Gluttonous behemoth\n  - Allow the gluttonous behemoth to access the other bosses as it will heal it and kill them. Once all other bosses are dead, the 1hp behemonth can be killed.","Head west and watch the cutscene.}} Saga complete!"],"t":"Venturing through the dungeon"}]},"Three's Company (saga)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to Daemonheim and bank everything, including your ring of kinship.","Right-click choose start saga on Skaldrun, choose the first option then Play Saga.","Control Ariane, pick up the dusk eels from the tables."],"t":"Starting room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["As Ariane, enter the south door, kill all the enemies and pick up the dusk eels.","Pick up the gold charm and heim crabs but do not eat them.","Control Sir Owen and check the rocky debris for a novite ore.","Enter the south door."],"t":"Guardian room #1"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Control Ozan and unlock the door by stepping on each of the 4 pressure plates.\n  - The puzzle is different for everyone and every time.\n  - You can slide diagonally.","Open the east door.","Quickly switch to Ariane once in the next room."],"t":"Ice puzzle room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["As Ariane, kill all the enemies.","As Ariane, make a cub skinweaver by using the gold charm on the summoning obelisk.","As Ariane, talk to the cub skinweaver.","Enter the east door."],"t":"Bridge room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["As Ariane, flip all tiles until all yellow or green.\n  - You can right click \"force\" to flip individual tiles."],"t":"Tile flip room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["As Ariane, enter the north door, quickly pick up the green rectangle key, and exit the room.","Switch to Ozan and return to the starting room without teleporting (west, west, north, north).\n  - There is currently a bug where if you use Home Teleport, it will turn the character you are currently controlling into your player character and you'll no longer be able to switch to other characters or continue on. You'll be forced to restart the Saga from last checkpoint."],"t":"Mysterious shade room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Switch to Ariane.","Unlock the green rectangle door and enter.","\"Wait\" on each of the pressure pads for Owen and Ozan.","Enter the south door."],"t":"Magic imbue room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take the crimson triangle key.","Right-click \"Get-premonition\" on any strange crystal.","Touch the following crystals in order:","Enter the north door.","Right-click call Owen and Ozan to walk them off the pressure plates.","Enter the west door.","As Ariane, unlock the crimson triangle door and enter it."],"t":"Strange crystal room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["As Ariane, kill all the enemies and pick up the dusk eels.","Control Ozan, and enter the east door."],"t":"Guardian room #2"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["As Ozan, talk to the guard. {Chat: 1 [Charm] What are you guarding? > 2 Isn't guarding a door in these dungeons a little...redundant? > 1 Who put you up to guarding the door? > 2 Why are you bothering to guard it?}","Enter the east door."],"t":"Door guard room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Control Owen and push the statues into place.\n  - The four southern statues should match the position of the statues in the north."],"t":"Statue puzzle room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the east door and pick up the fractite pickaxe.","Return west to the guard room and mine the zephyrium rock hidden behind the northwest pillar.","Return east to the statue room."],"t":"Pickaxe room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Control Ozan and enter the northern door.","Proceed through the traps and investigate the broken longsword.","Control Ariane and return to the previous room."],"t":"Agility room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the southern door, kill the enemies and pick up the dusk eel.","Enter the east door and pick up the gold crescent key.","Talk to Pikkupstix (in the northwest corner of the room). {Chat: 4 [Leave]}","Return to the room north of the starting room without teleporting (west, north, west, west).","Unlock the gold crescent door north of the starting room."],"t":"Guardian room #3"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the room and continue through the dialogue. {Chat: 1 Sir Owen > 2 Ozan > 3 Ariane}","Kill the two arctic bears and then kill Carn.","Once he is killed, choose any chat option."],"t":"Confronting Carn"}]},"Throne of Miscellania":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to King Vargas, floor 2 in the castle on the western island of Miscellania. You'll first need to open the throne room door and click through the dialogue with the guard. {Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"1 iron bar, 1 logs","r":"","s":["Run to the eastern island. On the floor 2 of the castle, talk to Queen Sigrid.","Go back and talk to King Vargas.","Go back and talk to Queen Sigrid.","Talk to Prince Brand in the bedroom south of King Vargas's room. He will give you an awful anthem.","Talk to Advisor Ghrim in King Vargas's room. He adjusts the anthem, and the awful anthem will convert into a good anthem. {Chat: 2 How do I make peace with Etceteria?}","Take the good anthem to Queen Sigrid.","Talk to King Vargas.","Talk to Derrik at the anvil on the north of the island, and give him an iron bar. {Chat: 2 I have a slightly strange request...}","Use the giant nib on your logs.","Talk to King Vargas.","Talk to Advisor Ghrim about marriage. {Chat: 2 How am I supposed to get the Prince or Princess to marry me?}"],"t":"Being the messenger"},{"n":"1 flowers (can be bought from the Flower Girl for 15 coins), any bow (it will be lost during the quest), and any tradeable non-enchanted metal ring","r":"","s":["Go to the room to the north and talk to Princess Astrid. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Princess Astrid again, read carefully what she says. You must agree with her.","Repeat this about 3 times until the chat options stop appearing.\n  - Hahahaha!\n  - He's been very helpful.\n  - Archery is a noble art!","Use the flowers on her. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Perform the Dance emote in her room.","Talk to Princess Astrid to tell her your name.","Talk to Princess Astrid again and agree with her again 3 times.\n  - What happened next?\n  - That sounds like a good idea.\n  - I'm quite fond of it myself.","Give her a bow by using it on her. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Talk to Princess Astrid.","Talk to Princess Astrid again and agree with her again 3 times.\n  - I suppose you don't have much opportunity to.\n  - It's a lovely little country.\n  - And what a great bard he makes!","Blow a kiss at Princess Astrid.","Use the ring on her. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Talk to King Vargas."],"t":"To marry the princess"},{"n":"1 flowers (can be bought from the Flower Girl for 15 coins), cake, any tradeable, non-enchanted metal ring","r":"","s":["Go to the room to the south and talk to Prince Brand. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Prince Brand about 3 more times, trying to impress and/or agree with him.","Use the clap or cheer emote.","Use the flowers on him. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Talk to Prince Brand and agree with him again 3 times.","Listen to his saga.","Use the cake on him. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Talk to Prince Brand and agree with him again 3 times.","When he calls you 'Dear', blow a kiss at him.","Use the ring on Prince Brand. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Talk to King Vargas."],"t":"To marry the prince"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Advisor Ghrim about support. {Chat: 2 How do I gain the support of the population?}","You need to make the population like you. You can check your approval percentage by talking to the people you're helping. To do this, perform any of the following tasks on the island:\n  - Raking weeds\n  - Chopping trees (logs will not be obtained)\n  - Mining coal (ore will not be obtained but it is the most AFK method here)\n  - Fishing at the docks to the south (fish will not be obtained)\n  - Purchase Flowers (mixed) from the Flower Girl (50% chance of +1% per flower)"],"t":"Helping the population"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Once you have 75% approval, talk to King Vargas.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"TokTz-Ket-Dill":{"sections":[{"n":"2 empty inventory slots}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["After entering the TzHaar City, go east as far as possible along the southern wall, then directly north (just west of Fight Cauldron teleport). Speak to one of the three guards. {Chat: 1 What has happened here? > Accept}","Talk to TzHaar-Ket-Grol south-west, at the crack in the wall (with at least one empty inventory slot). {Chat: 1 I was told to talk to you}","Enter the tunnel to the library north-west of the Main Plaza.","Speak to TzHaar-Mej-Lor. {Chat: 1 I need help with the TzHaar language.}","Talk to Reldo in the Varrock library about TzHaar language. {Chat: 3 I have a question about the TzHaar language.}","Along the west wall, in the cluster of 3 bookcases, search the middle one for the TzHaar Tourist Guide.","Read the TzHaar Tourist Guide along with the note inside.","Return to TzHaar-Ket-Grol. {Chat: 1 I know what to bring now. > 5 A pickaxe. > 5 Oak planks. > 4 Blocks of stone.}","Go east and pass the cave entrance."],"t":"The TzHaar tourist guide"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the mine directly east and speak with TzHaar-Hur-Brekt on the east side {Chat: 2 Can you teach me magma mining? > 1 But it's very important!}, then talk again. {Chat: 2 We should change the plot. > 3 The humans started it.}","Speak to TzHaar-Hur-Klag on the west wall. {Chat: 3 How can I make the story better? > 2 TzHaar who gets assaulted in its home is TzHaar-Hur. > 4 That was it.}","Speak to TzHaar-Mej-Kol, just north. {Chat: 3 How can I make the story better? > 2 One is a TzHaar-Mej who is aware of the situation. > 4 That was it.}","Speak to TzHaar-Xil-Mor, south-east in the mine. {Chat: 3 How can I make the story better? > 1 The criminal could be a TzHaar-Xil.}","Speak to TzHaar-Hur-Brekt. {Chat: 1 We should decide an ending. > 1 The criminal's plans are foiled.}","Speak to TzHaar-Xil-Mor. {Chat: 3 How can I make the story better? > 2 The plans aren't always foiled.}","Speak to TzHaar-Hur-Brekt. {Chat: 3 They are all happy with the plot.}"],"t":"The TzHaar theatre"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak with TzHaar-Ket-Jok, south-west in the mine. {Chat: 1 You will play the role... > 3 ...JalYt-Jenny > 2 What do you think of your current role? > 3 We should modify your current role. > 2 No, we can't have that. > 4 That was it.}","Speak with TzHaar-Xil-Mor. {Chat: 1 You will play the role... > 1 ...TokTz-Ket-Ek-Mack. > 2 What do you think of your current role? > 4 That was it.}","Speak with TzHaar-Hur-Klag. {Chat: 1 You will play the role... > 4 ...TzHaar-Hur. > 2 What do you think of your current role? > 3 We should modify your current role. > 1 Eh, I guess so. > 4 That was it.}","Speak with TzHaar-Mej-Kol. {Chat: 1 You will play the role... > 2 ...KetKul-Schmul. > 3 We should modify your current role. > 4 That was it.}","Finally speak to TzHaar-Hur-Brekt. {Chat: 2 Yes, all roles have been given out.}"],"t":"The TzHaar plot"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Mine the Stone slab vein and craft 4 pillars for the first cave section (you can easily return for more)."],"t":"Obsidian pillars"},{"n":"14 oak planks (bank at Fight Cauldron or the Main Plaza if needed, or store them in a plank box)","r":"","s":["Go to the quest start location and have your planks treated by the small TzHaar-Hur-Frok. {Chat: 1 Can you treat these oak planks for me? > 1 Here you go.}."],"t":"Treating the planks"},{"n":"Magic weapon with runes for water spells, ranged weapon with more distance than just darts, enough pillars and planks for a cave section (there are checkpoints.)","r":"","s":["Enter the crack in the south wall by TzHaar-Ket-Grol.}} Some sections of the walls have caved-in (shown as red corridor sections on the minimap) and some sections of the ceiling have caved-in (shown as piles of rubble, as well as pale brown shapes on the minimap).","If the examine info for a cave-in says \"The damage in this location is bad / isn't too badly damaged\", use a plank on it.","If the examine info for a cave-in says \"The damage in this location is very bad/badly damaged/very badly damaged\", use a pillar on it. You cannot walk through these, and must place them from 1 tile away. Don't accidentally block yourself off with them, or you will need to push them over and get more pillars. If you run out of pillars, you can simply lobby and you'll end up outside of the cave, near the mine. You can then return to where you left off.","Using the wrong item on a cave-in can cause a few hundred damage.","The first cave requires 6 treated planks and 4 pillars. After fixing the cave-ins, mine the blocked tunnel and proceed to the next checkpoint.","The second cave requires 6 treated planks and 6 pillars. The fire monster can only be harmed by magic with water spells or necromancy.","The third cave requires 2 treated planks and 7 pillars. The first two lava monsters can only be harmed by ranged weapons with an attack range of 5 spaces or higher or by using necromancy. You will need to use magic with water spells or necromancy on the final fire monster. You cannot cross the stones before killing all three lava monsters.}}"],"t":"Repairing the tunnels"},{"n":"Adamant pickaxe or better in your inventory or tool belt, full melee or hybrid armour","r":"","s":["Once you are ready to fight the TokTz-Ket-Dill, enter the tunnel to the north. {Chat: 1 Yes.}\n  - If you die, your gravestone will appear in the chamber with the trapped TzHaar-Hurs, outside the tunnel to the TokTz-Ket-Dill.","Kill the TokTz-Ket-Dill by breaking it's armour with a pickaxe equipped, then using any style to finish it off. Do not use prayers until the shell is broken.","After killing the TokTz-Ket-Dill, exit to the north, head south out of the caves, and then talk to any of the three starting TzHaar to finish the quest."],"t":"Battling the TokTz-Ket-Dill"}]},"Tomes of the Warlock":{"sections":[{"n":"Restored necromantic focus","r":"","s":["Talk to Death in the City of Um. {Chat: Accept}","Teleport to Kharid-et Dig Site and talk to Dr Nabanik. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Head to the Exam Centre and talk to the Head of Research next to the research notes, giving him a restored necromantic focus artefact. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 Yes.}","Go through the first three (smoke and blood are the same) book dialogues, which requires talking to him multiple times.\n  - {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 Ice.}\n  - {Chat: 1 Yes. > 2 Smoke.}\n  - {Chat: 1 Yes. > 3 Shadow.}"],"t":"Learning about Orcus"},{"n":"","r":"Varrock Teleport spell","s":["Talk to Reldo, the librarian in Varrock Palace to retrieve the damaged Book of Ice. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"The Book of Ice"},{"n":"","r":"Varrock Teleport spell & wicked hood or infinity ethereal outfit for Wizards' Tower teleport}}{{Checklis","s":["Talk to Aubury at Aubury's Rune Shop, south of Varrock east bank.","Head to the floor 1 of Wizards' Tower, by fairy ring DIS, wicked hood, or teleporting with stardust.","Talk to Wizard Borann located on the west side of the floor 1 to retrieve the damaged Book of Smoke.","Continue the dialogue to ask him about the Book of Blood."],"t":"The Book of Smoke"},{"n":"","r":"Watchtower Teleport spell if hard Ardougne achievements are completed and destination altered, or activated Yanille lodestone","s":["Head to Wizards' Guild.","Talk to Wizard Frumscone in the basement of the guild to receive the damaged Book of Blood."],"t":"The Book of Blood"},{"n":"","r":"Imperial district teleport tablet","s":["Head to Menaphos Imperial district.","Talk to Kohnen the librarian in the Grand Library of Menaphos.","Inspect the sundial in the middle of the bottom floor to retrieve the damaged Book of Shadow."],"t":"The Book of Shadow"},{"n":"120 ancient vis, 104 blood of Orcus and 80 imperial steel in material storage container","r":"","s":["Repair the books at any archaeologist's workbench.","Hand in to Head of Research. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Handing in the books"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Death in City of Um.","Talk to Ted beside the Well of Souls at the ritual site.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Parsing necromancy glyphs"}]},"Tortle Combat (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Postie Pete-za by the entrance to Varrock Sewers with at least 1 free inventory space. {Chat: Accept}","Open the manhole and enter the Varrock Sewers.","Go east and squeeze through the pipe.","Talk to Wolfgang on the bridge. {Chat: 4 What will you do now? > 1 Yes}","Talk to the Varrock estate agent. He is located in a building just north of the sewer entrance. {Chat: 1 Tortle Combat.}","Return to Wolfgang. {Chat: 1 You should probably stop sending rats to the estate agent.}","Build the equipment around the area with the 16 planks, 2 buckets of sand, 1 empty sack, 3 ropes, and 60 iron nails.","Talk to Wolfgang. {Chat: 1 I have constructed all your equipment!}","Talk to Gustav to the north of Wolfgang.","Talk to Granny Potterington at Manor Farm with a kebab and Dense honeycomb in your inventory. {Chat: 1 [Ask about Tortle Combat.]}","Use the extremely dense honeycomb on your adult or elder common brown rabbit.","Bring Gustav the soft clay, 2 law runes and the plump rabbit.","Talk to Edvard to the south.","Talk to Wolfgang.","Talk to Johann to the southwest.","Talk to Hofuthand at the west side of Grand Exchange. {Chat: 1 [Tortle Combat.]}","Return to Johann.","You will then need to give each tortle its correct weapon.\n  - Gustav. {Chat: 1 Give Gustav a weapon > 5 Dwarven army axe}\n  - Johann. {Chat: 1 Give Johann a weapon > 4 Old rake handle}\n  - \"Weird\" Alfred. (northeast) {Chat: 1 Give \"Weird\" Alfred a weapon > 8 Rabid chinchompa}\n  - Wolfgang. {Chat: 1 Give Wolfgang a weapon > 1 Mismatched set of cutlery}","Talk to Wolfgang, wait for the cutscene, and then talk with him again"],"t":"Getting started"}]},"Tower of Life":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Effigy at the Tower of Life near fairy ring code DJP. {Chat: 1 Sure, why not. > Accept}","Talk to Bonafido, the builder lying down north of the door to the tower."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to 'Black-eye'. {Chat: 3 Three > 1 Torn curtains > 2 10 clay pieces}"],"t":"Hard hat"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to 'The Guns' and give him the beer."],"t":"Shirt"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to 'No fingers'.","Pickpocket the boots from him. It may take multiple attempts."],"t":"Boots"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Search the plants south-east of the tower for the trousers."],"t":"Trousers"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Equip the costume and talk to Bonafido. {Chat: 2 Tea > 3 Whistle for attention > 1 Your legs are getting a bit cold > 2 Carry on, it'll fix itself}"],"t":"Gaining entry"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["All of the items you need for the quest will be found on the ground floor of the tower in crates. Refer to image for item crate locations."],"t":"Tower repair"},{"n":"4 coloured balls, 3 metal sheets, and 4 valve wheels","r":"","s":["Go to the floor 2.","Fix the pressure machine.","Turn wheel 1 left until blocked.","Turn wheel 1 right until fixed.","Pull left lever.","Turn wheel 2 left until blocked.","Turn wheel 2 right until fixed.","Turn wheel 3 right until it reaches the hole.","Turn wheel 3 left until blocked.","Turn wheel 3 right until fixed.","Pull right lever.","Turn wheel 4 right until it reaches the hole.","Turn wheel 4 left until blocked.","Turn wheel 4 right until fixed."],"t":"Pressure machine"},{"n":"6 rivets, 4 pipes, and 5 pipe rings","r":"","s":["Go to the floor 3.","Fix the pipe machine and move the pieces as shown in image."],"t":"Pipe machine"},{"n":"5 metal bars and 4 bottles of Binding fluid","r":"","s":["Go to the floor 4.","Fix the cage using the instructions below.","Front side\n  - Vertical 2\n  - Horizontal 3\n  - Horizontal 2\n  - Turn right","Right side\n  - Vertical 4\n  - Vertical 2\n  - Horizontal 2\n  - Turn right","Rear side\n  - Horizontal 4\n  - Vertical 2\n  - Vertical 3\n  - Turn right","Left side\n  - Horizontal 2\n  - Horizontal 2\n  - Vertical 2"],"t":"The cage"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to ground floor, speak to Effigy.","Go to the top of the tower to start a cutscene.","After the cutscene, talk to Effigy outside of the tower.","Return to the top of the tower and talk to Homunculus. {Chat: 1 Get some logs and a tinderbox. > 3 By ignition of gas in their belly as they exhale. > 3 Fletching, Crafting, Smithing. > 1 Bury them. > 2 Run, run as fast as you can. > 2 People mix together ingredients in vials. The nutrients will help you. > 3 Take a rune stone to an altar and use a talisman.}"],"t":"Homunculus"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Effigy for a final cutscene.","Go down the trapdoor inside the tower.","Talk to Homunculus.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Tree Gnome Village":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head through the Gnome Maze and squeeze through the loose railing.","Talk to King Bolren. {Chat: 2 Can I help at all? > Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"6 normal Logs","r":"","s":["Talk to Commander Montai north of the maze. He is wearing red and will be wandering near the catapult to the east of where you are exited out of the maze. {Chat: 1 Ok, I'll gather some wood.}\n  - Talk to him again to give him six logs.","Talk to Commander Montai again. {Chat: 2 I'll try my best}","Talk to the 3 tracker gnomes (map locations below).","West of Commander Montai, fire the ballista and choose coordinate until successful."],"t":"The ballista"},{"n":"recommended = Combat gear and / or food to fight Khazard warlord (level 53)","r":"","s":["The building next to Tracker gnome 1, climb over the crumbled wall which is to the right of the locked door.","Climb up the ladder and search the chest for an orb of protection.","Climb back down the ladder and head out the door or climb back over the crumbled wall.","Run back towards the north-west entrance of the maze, click Elkoy to Follow him.","Talk to King Bolren. {Chat: 1 I will find the warlord and bring back the orbs.}","Head north-west of the battlefield and follow the Ardougne wall all the way west.","Kill the Khazard warlord.","Return back to the maze and follow Elkoy.","Talk to King Bolren.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Orbs"}]},"Tribal Totem":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Kangai Mau in the large building north of Brimhaven's pub. {Chat: 2 I'm in search of adventure! > Accept}","Travel to Ardougne (you can take a ship from Brimhaven to complete Avast Ardougne!, an easy Karamja achievement), and head to the RPDT depot just south of the eastern bank.","Investigate the crate directly north-east of the sacks for the address label.","Use the address label on the stack of two crates directly north of the crate you just investigated.","Talk to an RPDT employee and ask when the crate will be delivered. {Chat: 1 So, when are you going to deliver this crate?}","Talk to Wizard Cromperty in the house north-east of the Ardougne market (the one with the blue checkered floor). {Chat: 2 So what have you invented? > 2 Can I be teleported please? > 1 Yes, that sounds good. Teleport me!}","Once inside the mansion, open the western door, using the code \"KURT\" to get in.","Right-click Investigate the stairs, then Climb-up them.","Once upstairs, enter the next room, Open the chest, then Search it for a totem.","Talk to Kangai Mau in Brimhaven with the totem.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Walkthrough"}]},"Troll Romance":{"sections":[{"n":"Climbing boots (or Trollheim Teleport or Trollheim tablet)","r":"","s":["Go to the middle level of the Troll Stronghold.\n  - Enter the cave entrance from Trollheim and go down one level.\n  - Otherwise, enter the secret entrance from the entrance to Fremennik Slayer Dungeon (fairy ring code AJR) or Death Plateau and go up one level.","Talk to Ug on the middle level of the Troll Stronghold. Offer him your help. {Chat: 1 Awww, you poor troll. What seems to be the problem? > 3 Don't worry now. I'll see what I can do. > Accept}","Talk to Aga in the room to the north. {Chat: 2 So... how's your... um... love life? > 1 Errr... I've got to go.}","Talk to Arrg in the same room. {Chat: 2 Your girlfriend said you know where to find Trollweiss?}","Talk to Ug again."],"t":"Hitch"},{"n":"1 rope, 1 maple logs or yew logs, 1 iron bar, 1 swamp tar, 1 cake tin and 1 bucket of wax","r":"","s":["Teleport to Burthorpe and talk to Freda in the plateaus west of Burthorpe. {Chat: 1 Do you know where I can find Trollweiss? > ? That's all, thanks.}","Talk to Dunstan east of the Burthorpe lodestone about a sled. {Chat: 2 I need a sled!! > 1 Yes.}","Talk to him again to give him a rope, maple or yew logs, and an iron bar.","Use swamp tar on a wax bucket (with a cake tin in your inventory).","Use your wax on the sled."],"t":"Survival techniques"},{"n":"Climbing boots (or Trollheim Teleport or Trollheim tablet), 1 waxed sled, combat gear, and eventual food for next quest step","r":"","s":["Enter the cave entrance opposite the ice gate, which located north-west of the main entrance to Troll Stronghold.\n  - Preferably use Trollheim Teleport here if you have it.\n  - Otherwise, you need to go through the Troll Stronghold and past Trollheim.","Head north-west and exit the cave through the crevasse.","Head south, equip your sled and slide through the slope.","After the end of the first part of the ride, pick the Trollweiss flowers west of your location. Do not sled any further south at this point or you will have to climb the mountain again.","Go back and talk to Ug."],"t":"Sledding"},{"n":"Climbing boots, 1 Trollweiss, combat gear and food, 7 backpack spaces for reward, reward will be dropped on floor if there is not enough space","r":"","s":["Talk to Arrg and tell him you're here to kill him. The fight will start immediately after that. Arrg also attacks immediately after the teleport, so be prepared. {Chat: 1 I am here to kill you!}","Kill Arrg.","Return to Ug and talk to him.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The things we do for love..."}]},"Troll Stronghold":{"sections":[{"n":"1 backpack space, climbing boots","r":"Fremennik round shield","s":["Talk to Commander Denulth in Burthorpe, east of the castle. {Chat: 1 How goes your fight with the trolls? > 2 Is there anything I can do to help? > Accept}\n  - If Denulth tells you that the ambush is still being planned, try asking him about the White Knights first. {Chat: 3 I thought the White Knights controlled Asgarnia.}","If you don't own climbing boots, buy them from Freda {Chat: 3 Can I buy some Climbing boots? > 1 Buy standard boots for 12gp.}","Enter Sabbot's cave from Death Plateau and cross all the obstacles to reach the exit of the tunnel (recommended for low Defence and Constitution levels).\n  - Alternatively, take the shortcut by running through the Death Plateau on the surface, clockwise around it, and climbing the rocks to the northwest, then climb the cliffside while wearing climbing boots. Beware of level 67 thrower trolls - Protect from Ranged, Dive, and Fremennik round shield are advised when taking this route.","Exit the cavern, climb the rocks to the immediate west of the exit and follow the path east over the rocks until you reach the arena entrance."],"t":"Mountain climbing"},{"n":"Combat equipment","r":"","s":["Open the arena entrance and attempt to leave through the northern entrance.","Defeat Dad after he attempts to attack you. You may choose to kill him or spare him after defeating him.\n  - An easy way to kill Dad safely is to bring him over to the northern entrance or down by the southern rocks and safespot him.\n  - Very low level players may need food."],"t":"Dad"},{"n":"","r":"Food, Fremennik round shield","s":["Exit through the north arena entrance.","Follow the path north-west, go through the cave to the north and go outside.","Once outside, continue the path to the stronghold to the north and west; thrower trolls can be dealt with by:\n  - Taking agility shortcuts around them with level 47 Agility. The cliffside shortcut may be used to avoid the thrower trolls completely.\n  - Running counter-clockwise around the mountain, past the thrower trolls (not behind them: they are supposed to throw rocks at you automatically) to the west.\n    - Protect from Ranged against them.\n    - Use Dive to quickly run past them.\n    - Equip Fremennik round shield to reduce their damage greatly.","Look for a dungeon on your minimap northeast of the Troll Stronghold, and enter the cave entrance."],"t":"Advancing towards the stronghold"},{"n":"Combat equipment, 3 backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Run south, go through the open wooden door, then continue north.","Kill a troll general and take the prison key. You can safespot with magic, ranged, or necromancy behind the counter.","Head back towards the entrance, past the door and go down the stone staircase to the north.","Open the exit to the south and enter the secret entrance.","Unlock the Prison Door to the immediate east and head down the stone staircase.","Pickpocket (or kill) Twig and Berry. Safespot them inside one of the open cells if needed.","Take the cell keys and unlock the two jail cells to free the prisoners.","Talk to Dunstan, the blacksmith in north-eastern Burthorpe.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Prison break"}]},"Tuai Leit's Own (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Navigator Jemi (if you have just completed the Harbinger miniquest you may need to relog for the chat option to show up). {Chat: 1 Tuai Leit's Own miniquest. > Accept}","Travel to Tuai Leit.","Talk to Sensei Hakase in the middle of the island.","If you don't have them already, pick 30 rumberries at the south-west farming spot.","Talk twice to Cheri the gnome on the south coast.","Take the rumberry elixir to Lookout Ekahi. {Chat: 1 Tuai Leit's Own miniquest.}\n  - Do not exit the dialogue or you will have to get another elixir.","Return to Sensei Hakase.","Chop down the inferior bamboo to the west of the island to reach Tuai Leit moai.","Talk to Tuai Leit moai. {Chat: 3 I seek a cure for a spiritual affliction.}"],"t":"Rumberry elixir"},{"n":"At least 1 spirit dragon charms}}{{Checklis","r":"","s":["If you don't have them already, harvest 30 positive energy from Cyclosis island.","Travel to Aminishi with some spirit dragon charms.","Enter the spirit realm via The Well of Spirits in the easternmost part of the island near the Sakadagami.","Talk twice to Yulong in the spirit realm, on the south beach.","Hand him the positive energy to trigger a cutscene with a white flash.\n  - Finish dialogue or you have to give positive energy again.","Leave the spirit realm. You can quickly leave by exiting to lobby or by logging out then back in.","Talk to Lookout Ekahi. {Chat: 1 Tuai Leit's Own miniquest.}","Talk to Sensei Hakase in Tuai Leit.","Talk to Sensei Seaworth nearby.","Talk to Sojobo in the Waiko marketplace.","Talk to Navigator Jemi. {Chat: 1 Tuai Leit's Own miniquest.}"],"t":"Positive energy"}]},"Twilight of the Gods":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Sir Cadian outside of the surface entrance to Senntisten. {Chat: Accept} Afterwards, talk to Sir Cadian again and finish the conversation.\n  - To get there, you may use the Archaeology journal teleport and run north.","Enter the nearby ancient door. {Chat: 1 Yes.}\n  - Do not use the pontifex ring's Senntisten teleport as it will exit the instance.","Talk to Naressa or Gregorovic in the house near the southwest corner of Senntisten and agree to meet them in the asylum. {Chat: Any > 1 I'll come with you now.}","Talk to Naressa or Gregorovic once inside.","Talk to them a second time and pull the crane lever under the desk, not the lever on the wall.","Head up the stairs.","Search the drawer (not the chest of drawers) near the filing cabinet for a chain of keys.\n  - If you cannot find the keys, head downstairs and flip the lever again (see image). If you still cannot find the keys, search the crate, then the bookcase upstairs and the drawer near the filing cabinet should be interactable.","Search the notes on the ground to the east for key instructions then read it.","Head downstairs and open the gate {Chat: 6 Short purple key}, then walk through it.","Operate the asylum elevator.","Talk to Naressa and Gregorovic.","Head east into the next room and talk to Yk'Lagor, Cyrillus or Dahaka. {Chat: Any}"],"t":"Investigating the asylum"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Find Rowena (little girl ghost) starting at the south-east.","Follow her through the dungeon and collect the following items from the area.\n  - Syringe from the crate of syringes in the incinerator room (south).\n  - Infernal ashes from the spiky chair several rooms later (west). It is in small rectangular room with a single abyssal savage.\n  - Vial from the crate of vials in the nothernmost room.","Talk to Senecianus (appearing as Rowena) in the north-westernmost room to obtain a Break Curse scroll (Twilight of the Gods).","Create the cure:\n  - Use the syringe on Senecianus to obtain a Syringe of Chthonian blood.\n  - Fill the vial using the sink in the southwestern operating room to obtain a Vial of vile water. {Chat: 1 Yes.}\n  - Right-click to use the infernal ashes on the vial to obtain Experimental potion 6.\n  - Use the blood syringe on the incomplete potion to obtain a SIPD cure.","Return to the large northeasternmost room and talk to Yk'Lagor. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Yk'Lagor again. {Chat: Any}"],"t":"Curing the demons"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Saradomin on his throne in the White Knights' Castle in Falador. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Saradomin again.","Talk to him a third time.\n  - After finishing the last dialogue, your quest journal should mention \"The White Knights in the Jolly Boar Inn\" as the current step."],"t":"Saradomin's counsel"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the four white knights at the Jolly Boar Inn.\n  - Sir Cull\n  - Sir Berus\n  - Sir Dated\n  - Sir Plus","Just west of the inn, descend the lift to enter the Infernal Source Dig Site. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Blythe. {Chat: 1 Growth through chaos. > 3 Philippa Wharton. > 2 Dagon.}","Wear the cultist attire and climb down the secret passage to the north.","Pickpocket cultists until you obtain a cast iron key (pickpocketing the same one works).","Collect information about the cult:\n  - Head north and talk to Wilona. {Chat: 1 Yes. > 2 Domine fortis chaos > 2 In sanguine et in morte > 3 Honoramus tibi hoc sacrificium}\n  - Talk to Audrey (near the east pillar).\n  - Talk to Ridley (in the east hallway).\n  - Talk to Edda (in the southeast room).\n  - Search the crate against the southern wall for spare cultist robes.\n  - Talk to Tyne in the jail cell west."],"t":"Infiltrating the Infernal Source"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return and talk to Saradomin. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Talk to Saradomin again.","Talk to him a third time. {Chat: Any > 1 Can you assault Zamorak directly? > 2 Can the summoning portal at the Infernal Source be disrupted? > 3 Why don't we just kill the attacking demons?}\n  - After finishing the last dialogue, your quest journal should mention \"re-establishing the Edicts of Guthix\" as the current step.","Go downstairs and talk to Adrasteia in the room to the west.\n  - If she is not there, you may lobby and log back in.","Talk to the Tree of Balance south-west of the Archaeology Campus. {Chat: 1 Continue Twilight of the Gods.}","Talk to any of the guardians of Guthix for a cutscene.","Return and talk to Saradomin to obtain an Energy scanner."],"t":"Guardians of Guthix"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Stand in front of the pool and talk to the Archivist if he is visible near the pool.","Scan with the energy scanner, then go to the gleaming wisp divination site south-east of the Karamja lodestone and interact with the green mystical wisp.\n  - You can use the elder divination outfit for a direct teleport to the gleaming wisp colony, or Karamja gloves 3 or higher to teleport nearby to the Shilo Village mine.","Talk to the confused automaton and complete all the dialogue.","Exit the cache and scan with the energy scanner, then talk to Merethiel at the Lost Grove {Chat: 1 Yes > 1 Yes - please send me in.}.\n  - You can use the Boss portal to Solak, fairy ring BJS if repaired (Take 5 Bittercap mushroom to repair it if you have not) and then interact with the magical mushrooms, the elder divination outfit to the incandescent wisp colony, or BKP and then run west to the standstone to get to the Lost Grove.","Talk to the Guardians of Guthix once inside.","Talk to Isaura at the Black Knights' Base (northeastern corner of the base, next to the kitchen) in the Taverley Dungeon {Chat: 1 Yes} for a crate of birds.\n  - You can quickly get to her using the Archaeology teleport or the master archaeologist's outfit teleport to Collectors, then Isaura. ([0]→[4])"],"t":"Preparing for the spell"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to The Lost Grove, then talk to Merethiel. {Chat: 1 Yes > 1 Yes - please send me in.}","Speak to Juna once inside.","Place effigy on the stone circle in the middle of the arena.","Harvest from the energy spring until you have 52 Guthixian energy.","Make all of the letters at the offering cradle (the large orb in the middle of the area).","Collect four stone circle building kits from the material cart slightly north-east of Juna and construct four empty stone circles starting from the west.","The spelling of 3 words is required for each of the 3 rituals (9 total).\n  - For each ritual phase, the order of words is random per player.\n  - To spell words, add a rune (letter) on each of the stone circles you've just constructed.\n  - Words are spelled in clockwise orientation on the stone circles along the perimeter of the arena.\n  - To attempt the word you spelled, place effigy on stone circle, followed by \"start ritual\".\n  - Each successful ritual phase will yield the chat message: {Chat: Ritual #: #/3 words completed.}"],"t":"Casting the spell"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["In the first ritual, the words are; in no certain order:\n  - H A L T\n  - W A R D\n  - G O D S","Talk to Juna.","Collect from the material cart again and build the 5th stone circle.","In the second ritual, the words are; in no certain order:\n  - L E A V E\n  - A N I M A\n  - A E G I S","Talk to Juna.","Collect from the material cart again and build the 6th stone circle.","In the third ritual, the words are; in no certain order:\n  - B A N I S H\n  - S H I E L D\n  - D I V I N E","Talk to Juna.","Return to Saradomin's throne at the White Knights' Castle at Falador {Chat: 1 Yes.} and speak to Adrasteia.","Talk to Adrasteia again."],"t":"Completing the rituals"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the Empyrean Citadel (Adrasteia offers to teleport you). {Chat: 1 Yes please.}\n  - Alternatively use the invitation box. {Chat: 1 Yes > 1 Yes}","Talk to the gods.","Interact with the fake quest completion certificate and talk to the voices in your head.","Quest Complete!"],"t":"Finishing"}]},"Underground Pass":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to floor 2 of Ardougne Castle in East Ardougne.","Talk to King Lathas.{Chat: Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"a shortbow, some arrows, 1–2 ropes","r":"Combat gear and a few food to fight 8 enemies, and a plank","s":["Talk to Koftik in the western most part of West Ardougne. {Chat: 1 I'll take my chances.}","Enter the cave entrance and go on either the north or south passages with rockslides to bypass the middle swamp.","Talk to Koftik for a damp cloth. Use it on an arrow and then light the arrow.","Make sure you are standing around the bend to the north. Equip your bow and the lit arrow. Fire at the guide rope attached to the bridge.","You may pick up the plank for passing through some traps further in the cave. It is located just after the bridge to the north. Only one is needed.","Continue through the cave to the south-east until you reach a gap north of the rope swing.","Use a rope on the old spike near the northern edge of the gap on your side.\n  - You may need to hover at the tip of the spike as its hitbox is so small. Be sure to select your rope first, then use it on the space adjacent to the northern edge. You will lose your rope in the process.\n  - If you fail the obstacle, you can climb out of the pit via the pile of rocks on the north western wall past some rockslides.","Continue through the cave over the two rockslides until you reach a large grid (5x5) next to Koftik."],"t":"Getting in and across the bridge"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Find your path across the grid. Keep a record of the path over the grid for Regicide quest. You will fall through some of the tiles.\n  - You can use the table below to save your path: click a cell to highlight it, and click again to de-highlight it (your browser will remember the path saved in the table as long as you don't clean browser cache for the wiki).","Pull the lever to the south at the end to continue."],"t":"Grid puzzle"},{"n":"4 free backpack space","r":"","s":["Run past the zombie camp, there will be odd markings along the walls of the corridor. These are traps. Search these walls to disarm them.\n  - You can skip disarming by standing right next to the trapped tile and then running to the other side of the tile. This can also be done on the next step.\n  - You can also simply run past the traps, take damage, and then eat to replenish the lost life points.","You will reach a chaos altar, take the north path using a plank on the flat rocks. Take the orb of light. Return back to the altar.","Take the north-west path towards the ogres. Take the orb. Return back to the altar.","Take the middle west path, traversing the flat rocks as before using the plank. Take the orb.","Take the final path and do not pick up the orb right away. Search the flat rock underneath the orb to disarm the trap first and then take the orb. If successful your character will automatically pick up the orb. If not, continue trying to search the rock.","Return to the zombie camp (don't forget about disarming the traps).","Use the 4 orbs on the furnace.","Return to the altar (again, don't forget about the traps).","Climb down the well. You can search the two stacked crates for 2 salmon and 2 meat pies.","Follow the path until you reach the cages.","Pick the lock and dig the mud in the south-easternmost cell.","Walk west and cross the ledge.","Reaching the eastern side of the wooden bridge maze.\n  - If you have level 50 Thieving, take the shortcut through the cages and avoid the bubbles. If you step on a bubble, you will have to start from the beginning, without a rope.\n  - If you lack level 50 Thieving, cross the wooden bridge maze to get to the other side, you may fall and try again.","Head south and enter the obstacle pipe."],"t":"Lights in the night"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Search the unicorn cage to find a piece of railing.","Use the railing on the boulder south of the unicorn.","Search the smashed cage to get a unicorn horn.\n  - The piece of railing can be dropped.","Pass through the tunnel north of the cage, until you reach 3 paladins.\n  - If you are low on health, talk to Sir Jerro for some free food and potions. You will need 7 backpack space.","Kill them and take their badges. Requires 3 backpack space.","Continue forward, using your plank on the flat rocks, until you see a well.","Use the badges and unicorn horn on the well.","Open the door."],"t":"Cold blooded killing"},{"n":"6 free backpack space","r":"","s":["Reach the dwarf camp in the cavern below by following one of the below methods.\n  - Head south along the wall to the south-east corner then head west along the south wall to find the cave stairs there. Take the stairs down.\n  - There are also stairs in the north-west corner that may be easier to find but will require players to make their way through the herd of hostile soulless in the centre of the cavern below on the way to the dwarf camp.\n  - Fail a bridge jump.","Koftik will appear with some brief dialogue.","After the dialogue is finished, go to the dwarf camp in the cavern's south-western corner.","Talk to Niloof the dwarf.","Go back up the stairs to the east."],"t":"Meeting the dwarves"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the central part of the map by crossing the wooden bridges to pick up the witch's cat, the cat should be wandering out on the bridges and platforms north-west of her house (marked by a yellow dot on the minimap). The witch's house is the most south-eastern platform.","Use the cat on the door to the witch's house.","Open the door to the house.","Search the chest in her house for a few items and the History of Iban book.\n  - Click the chest once to trigger a dialogue. Prematurely ending the dialogue will require you to wait for the chest to close, or logout.\n  - The History of Iban can be dropped."],"t":"Black cat in the dark"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Kill Doomion, Othainian, and Holthion west of the witch and take their amulets.","Open and search the chest north of the middle demon.","Pour Iban's shadow on the doll of Iban.","Return downstairs and talk to Klank the dwarf, taking his gauntlets.","Take the bucket in the large house. Use it on the barrel in the smaller house to receive a dwarf brew.","Run east to a tomb in the south-east corner of the cave","Use the dwarf brew on the tomb.\n  - You will not need a bucket for the rest of the quest.","Light the tomb to obtain Iban's ashes.","Use Iban's ashes on the doll of Iban.","Run to the furthest north-east corner, kill Kalrag the spider.\n  - *IMPORTANT* Upon killing Kalrag, the blessed spiders will begin attacking with range, so quickly enable Deflect/Protect from Ranged and run away from the spiders.}}"],"t":"Ashes to ashes"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the north-western corner and ascend the stairs to the half-soulless area.","Walk south to the third walkway and cross the bridge.","Walk north to the first cage, then walk east to the next cage.","Walk a little north then west from here to the cage containing Iban's dove (lowest platform in the centre of several others).","Equip Klank's gauntlets to prevent taking damage.","Search the cage to find Iban's dove.","Use the Iban's dove on the doll of Iban."],"t":"Caging his dove"},{"n":"enough backpack space to unequip the gear and 3 extra spaces","r":"","s":["Head back towards the most recent bridge you crossed BUT...","Instead, follow the bridge to east, then south-east towards the Disciple of Iban.","Kill a Disciple of Iban, grab both the Zamorak robe top and Zamorak robe bottom.","Un-equip everything and equip the robes. You don't need planks or rope anymore.\n  - If you don't have 3 free backpack spaces you will miss out on 15 death runes and 30 fire runes because you will instantly be teleported away after Iban is destroyed.","Jump the bridge to the south and continue south-west to the large door","Open the door to enter Iban's temple and use the doll on the well.\n  - Low level players should try to time the magical spikes to prevent being hit.","Talk to Koftik at the west end of the cave.","Return to King Lathas in Ardougne.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Ultimate demise"}]},"Unwelcome Guests":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"Combat gear, food","s":["Talk to Overseer Siv in the Command Centre at Fort Forinthry. {Chat: 2 Talk about 'Unwelcome Guests'. > Accept}","Talk to the Raptor, to the west.","Go to the northern gates and open them. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Head west and slay ten fetid zombies.","Talk to the Raptor once back inside the fort."],"t":"Starting off"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Bill. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Unwelcome Guests'.}","Leave via the northern gates into the Wilderness. {Chat: 1 Yes, I understand the restrictions.}","Fully construct defences at the building supplies along the walls. Turning off auto-retaliate is recommended, otherwise construction will be interrupted when you are attacked.\n  - Three just outside the western walls of the fort.\n  - Two just outside the northern walls of the fort.\n  - One just outside the eastern walls of the fort."],"t":"Strengthening the fortifications"},{"n":"14 maple frames, 6 stone wall segments","r":"","s":["Talk to Overseer Siv in the Command Centre. {Chat: 2 Talk about 'Unwelcome Guests'.}","Talk to Bill. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Unwelcome Guests'.}","Start building the Guardhouse at the Fort Forinthry blueprints table.","Head to the Guardhouse near the Raptor.","Build at the Construction hotspots within the Guardhouse until it is complete.\n  - Players can speed up this process by building at the optimal Construction hotspots.","Talk to the Raptor or Overseer Siv to trigger a dialogue and watch the cutscene."],"t":"Building the Guardhouse"},{"n":"","r":"Combat gear, food","s":["Go to the northern gates and open them. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Head west and slay another ten fetid zombies.","Watch the cutscene.","Go back to the Raptor.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Investigating the crypt"}]},"Vampyre Slayer":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Morgan in Draynor Village. {Chat: 2 What terrible threat? > Accept}","Go upstairs and search in the northern drawers to get a garlic.","Go to the Blue Moon Inn located in Varrock.","Talk to Dr Harlow. {Chat: 2 Are you Dr Harlow, the famous vampyre slayer?}","Buy a beer from the bartender.","Talk to Dr. Harlow again to get a stake and stake hammer."],"t":"A vampyric threat"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to Draynor Manor which is just north of Draynor Village.","Enter the manor and go to the east side.","Walk down the stairs.","Open the coffin in the back of the room.","Fight Count Draynor until he is almost dead, your character will then automatically use the stake hammer on him to kill him."],"t":"Slaying a vampyre"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Morgan.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Vengeance (saga)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Find a collection of swords while raiding the 12-17 abandoned floors of Daemonheim, and recover memory of them.","Talk to Skaldrun and ask him to tell you a story. {Chat: 1 Forgot what he says here > 1 Tell me a story}\n  - You need to bank everything, including the ring of kinship."],"t":"Beginning of the story"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head south through the door and kill all 4 Forgotten warriors."],"t":"Starting room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["As Vengeance (a forgotten warrior) head back to the starting room and talk to Orin. {Chat: 2 Give Orin the fish, he needs it more than you do.}","Continue south, unlock and open the silver crescent door with the newly acquired key.","Head inside and kill Lotheria Seldorina.","Pick up the food and Lotheria's ring of kinship.","Solve the puzzle by flipping all the tiles to one colour. Right click the tiles to force change them.","Open the east door.\n  - Optional: Kill both dungeon spiders for extra food.","Continue east through the door.","Kill Ican Haz and do not pull the lever.","Pick up the food, Icans ring of kinship and the blue triangle key.","Head back west, unlock the Blue triangle door and enter through it.","Kill the hellhounds for antipoison elixir and drink it, this will only temporarily stop the poison.","Continue north, kill the dungeon spider and talk to Argax. {Chat: 1 Let her die. She's earned her rest.}","Continue east and then south to reach a lever room.","Pull all five levers within the time limit and continue east then north.\n  - Optional: Kill the hellhound for more antipoison elixir or the dungeon spider for food.","Talk to Korel. {Chat: 2 Let Korel go, he's learned his lesson.}","Continue north and kill Lola Wut, pick up the crimson rectangle key, food and Lola's ring of kinship.","Continue through the west door.","Investigate Shianna's body then continue north and east.","Talk to Peleas. {Chat: 1 Lie to him. Give him comfort at the end.}","Head west, unlock and continue through the Crimson rectangle door and then continue once more west.","Attack and then show Kay Thanxby the corpses. {Chat: 1 Confront Kay's lies, show her the corpses.}"],"t":"Vengeance"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head south through the door and kill all 4 Forgotten warriors."],"t":"Starting room"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["As Vengeance (a forgotten warrior) head back to the starting room and talk to Orin. {Chat: 1 Keep the fish, you need your strength.}","Continue south, unlock and open the silver crescent door with the newly acquired key.","Head inside and kill Lotheria Seldorina sneaking behind pillars.","Pick up the food and Lotheria's ring of kinship.","Solve the puzzle by flipping all the tiles to one colour.","Open the east door.\n  - Optional: Kill both dungeon spiders for extra food.","Continue east through the door.","Pull the lever, this summons a horde of skeletons to kill Ican Haz.","Pick up the food, Icans ring of kinship and the Blue triangle key.","Head back west, unlock the Blue triangle door and enter through it.","Kill the hellhounds for antipoison exlir and drink it, this is only temporarily stop the poison.","Continue north, kill the dungeon spider and talk to Argax. {Chat: 2 Keep her awake. She has to fight for life.}","Continue east and then south to reach a lever room.","Pull all five levers within the time limit and continue east then north.\n  - Optional: Kill the hellhound for more antipoison exlir or the dungeon spider for food.","Talk to Korel. {Chat: 1 Kill Korel, prevent him from harming again.}","Continue north and search the table in the south east corner.","Head west and use the poison on the fishing spot, then continue north and east to gain visibility of all four rooms. Return to the starting room and wait for Lola to do a full rotation and eat the poisoned fish. This will damage her for 1999 lifepoints and head back to the room to kill Lola Wut for 1 lifepoint. Pick up the crimson rectangle key, food and Lola's ring of kinship.","Investigate Shianna's body in the south-western part of the room then continue north and east.","Talk to Peleas. {Chat: 2 Tell him the truth. He must understand their brutality.}","Head west, unlock and continue through the Crimson rectangle door and then continue once more west.","Kill Kay Thanxby. {Chat: 4 Make her suffer.}"],"t":"Vengeance"}]},"Vessel of the Harbinger":{"sections":[{"n":"Ghostspeak amulet or cramulet unless the hard Morytania achievements have been completed","r":"Ectophial}}{{Checklis","s":["Speak to Death in the City of Um.","Teleport to the Ectofuntus using the Ectophial.","Speak to Necrovarus."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"Ghostspeak amulet or cramulet unless the hard Morytania achievements have been completed, a bucket of slime and Necromancy weapons","r":"Ectophial","s":["Kill 5 Tortured souls with Necromancy to the north to fill the soul urn.","Worship the Ectofuntus with the filled urn and a bucket of slime in backpack.\n  - Gather a bucket of slime from the Pool of Slime, no bucket is required to gather the slime.","Speak to Necrovarus."],"t":"Cleansing the souls"},{"n":"Ghostspeak amulet or cramulet unless the hard Morytania achievements have been completed, an ectoplasm, and Necromancy weapons including a conduit","r":"A ring of slaying or Dungeoneering cape, an Ectophial, and five spirit runes to cast City of Um Teleport","s":["Head to Netty's house, on the eastern side of the Slayer Tower.\n  - Teleport to the Slayer Tower by using ring of slaying or Dungeoneering cape ([0],[0],[2]) or mask of the Abyss.\n  - Otherwise, teleport to Canifis lodestone and run west past graveyard, where ghouls wander, and then directly north.","Inspect the pile of letters just inside Netty's front door. If you do not have the option to inspect, you have missed a previous step.","Teleport back to the Ectofuntus and enter Port Phasmatys to speak to Velorina who is located at the northernmost house.","Head to the Last Call pub in the City of Um, east of the City of Um lodestone.","Speak to Netty in the northeast corner of the pub to receive Netty's death certificate and will. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Vessel of the Harbinger'.}","Head to the bank in Port Phasmatys and speak to a ghost banker to claim Netty's key.","Head back to Netty's house.","Open the chest.","Use your Conjure Skeleton Warrior with a conduit equipped and attack Netty's skeleton. She will flee.","Open the chest again to receive the book of Haricanto."],"t":"Retrieving the book of Haricanto"},{"n":"Ghostspeak amulet or cramulet unless the hard Morytania achievements have been completed, a bucket, 11 basic ghostly ink, 2 regular ghostly ink, 4 basic ritual candles (or better).","r":"An Ectophial, and five spirit runes to cast City of Um Teleport","s":["Head back to Ectofuntus and talk to Necrovarus.","Use a bucket on the Ectofuntus.","Go to the ritual site in City of Um.","Prepare an empower vessel ritual by using the pedestal.\n  - It requires 2 Elemental I, 1 Change I, 1 Commune I, 4 ritual light sources and 1 bucket of powerful slime as the focus.\n  - Total 11 basic ghostly ink, 2 regular ghostly ink, 4 basic ritual candles or better to prepare the ritual from scratch.","Complete the ritual.","Watch the cutscene.\n  - If the cutscene does not play, talk to Necrovarus."],"t":"Empower vessel ritual"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Speak to Death.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Violet is Blue":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Violet found on the southern tip of White Wolf Mountain. {Chat: Accept}","Enter the Land of Snow portal."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Dodge snowballs and run up the hill. You can run straight up the far east side (or far west side) of the hill and avoid getting hit by any snowballs. If you cannot make it and get hit enough, eventually, it will ask if you want to make it easier.","Talk to Violet.","Knock on the door. {Chat: 3 Break the door down. > 1 To go on an adventure.}","Talk to Trevor or Betty. {Chat: 1 YOU'VE CAPTURED A HUMAN GIRL! > 1 Yes!}","Talk to Violet in the room to the north.","Violet requests an object based on the starting letter five times. Search various objects around the room and bring her items that begin with the letter she requested."],"t":"Land of Snow"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Trevor or Betty.","Exit the building. {Chat: 1 Go on an adventure!}","Investigate the frozen bucket for an empty bucket.","Investigate a maple tree two times to receive maple logs.\n  - Investigate the logs to make a spile. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Use the spile on the maple tree.","Use the empty bucket on the same maple tree to receive a bucket of syrup.","Walk north, and check four leaning trees along the path.","Talk to Trevor to receive the firefly jar. {Chat: 1 Do you have anything useful?}","Shake multiple bushes and catch 10 fireflies. They may be difficult to see if playing on low graphics. To make this easier, right click the globe near your mini-map to toggle high contrast mode. This will make the fireflies stand out easier.","Talk to Violet."],"t":"Going on an adventure"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Violet.","Take icy snow from behind Violet. {Chat: Any > Any > Any > Any > Any}","Click on the headless golems (spam clicking works) and put all 15 heads on.","Talk to Violet."],"t":"Making snow heads"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Collect 75 snowballs at the pile of snow to the south.","Continually search the abandoned crate for 3 carrots, 3 top hats, 21 coal.","Prune a tree to the west three times for 6 branches.","Build all melted snowmen (24 Construction XP), then talk to Violet after each snowman.","Walk north."],"t":"Making snowmen"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Reach into the icy water on the south-east shore to obtain a barrel.","Talk to Violet.","Navigate the ice maze while pushing Violet as shown in the diagram. You may move diagonally.\n  - The controls require precision, best to rotate your camera to give a birds eye view (top down) when trying to move diagonal. It may be helpful to think of a 3x3 square when moving diagonally, with the player character in the centre."],"t":"Crossing the ice"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Violet.","Investigate:\n  - The ice in the small pond to the north-east\n  - The fire to the north\n  - The rotten barrel to the east of the sled (south-east of Violet)\n  - The crate just to the west of the sled","Chop down the Yeti village sign, a few steps south of the crate.","Investigate the open space, just east, multiple times while adding the items each time.","Talk to Violet. You can choose any name for the sled.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Constructing the sled"}]},"Violet is Blue Too":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Postie Pete at the Land of Snow portal. {Chat: Accept}","Enter the portal.","Talk to Posty and watch the cutscene. {Chat: ~}","Go north up the hill to Violet's house.","Knock on the door.","Progress through the dialogue.","Talk to Violet in her room, north-west of Betty and Trevor.","Search the chest in the eastern side of the room with Betty and Trevor.","Search the rug in Violet's room.","Search the fireplace in the western side of the room with Betty and Trevor.","Search the barrel of fish under the stairs.","Progress through the dialogue with Violet. {Chat: 2 What should we do?}","Exit the house and talk to Violet. {Chat: ~}","Talk to one of the snow imps.","Go south to the abandoned farm.","Open the chest by the door.","Proceed through dialogue with the snow imp follower (whose name is randomly selected). {Chat: 3 At least you got out before Christmas.}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Assistant Brad (north-east of the burning Christmas tree). {Chat: 1 How can we help out?}","Go north over the bridge, then west to the Christmas tree farm.","Talk to Taylor north west of the town.","Inspect the wonky tree on the western side of the farm.","Return to the town centre.","Talk to Assistant Brad."],"t":"Assistant Brad"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Assistant Susi south-east of wonky tree.","Knock on 4 doors around town for 4 piles of Christmas decorations:\n  - Southern side of the house east of the town centre.\n  - North-east of the town centre.\n  - North-west of the town centre.\n  - \"The Mug-Inn\" south-west of the town centre.","Talk to Assistant Susi.","Decorate 5 lampposts:\n  - 4 around the centre.\n  - 1 further south, on the path to the hill.","Decorate 4 houses by using the same door that you knocked on before:\n  - Southern side of the house east of the town centre.\n  - North-east of the town centre.\n  - North-west of the town centre.\n  - \"The Mug-Inn\" south-west of the town centre.","Talk to Assistant Susi."],"t":"Assistant Susi"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Assistant Timothy north-west of the wonky tree.","Talk to Posty, who appears north of the wonky tree.","Talk to the children around the town in the following order:\n  - Elizabeth west of the wonky tree.\n  - Peter east of the tree.\n  - Mozzie in the south-eastern part of the town.\n  - Neal in the house on the hill in the southern part of the town.","Take Santa's 'naughty or nice' list outside the eastern window of the house.","Talk to Posty north of the wonky tree."],"t":"Assistant Timothy"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the named snow imp (last name Claus) north of the wonky tree.","Talk to Hal the snow impling just south-west of the wonky tree.","Go up the southern hill without going inside the house and launch the snow impling from your backpack three times.","Admire the wonky tree.","Talk to the named snow imp or Violet.","Talk to Violet.","Knock on the door.","Talk to Betty or Trevor to complete the quest."],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Visions of Havenhythe":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Bartender at the Rusty Anchor tavern in Port Sarim. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Visions of Havenhythe' > Accept}","Drink the dragonfire mead.","After the cutscene, go downstairs via the door on the east side of the room.","Talk to the Bartender. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Visions of Havenhythe'}","Talk to 'Shady' Sullivan by the entrance of the tavern.","Talk to Captain Lorris on the Port Sarim docks just east of the lodestone. {Chat: 1 I'm ready.}"],"t":"Setting sail"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Old Man Jocko on the dock. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Visions of Havenhythe'}","Head east towards the city of Wendlewick, then speak to Adam in the building north of the well in the centre of the village. {Chat: 2 What do we do now? (Continue Quest)}","Head south and then south-east towards the Shrine of Inanna and talk to Shrine Tender Joanna.","Pray at the Altar of Inanna west of the summoning obelisk.","Talk to Shrine Tender Joanna.","Return and talk to Adam."],"t":"Call of the Great Wolf"},{"n":"10 backpack spaces","r":"","s":["Talk to Zeke in the building east of the well.","Head west to the beach and kill 10 juvenile boulder crab. Pick up the limestone they drop.\n  - You must kill the crabs, but you can bring your own limestone bricks to Zeke.","Return to Zeke.\n  - If you do not have level 12 Crafting, now it is time to give the limestone to Adam so that he can turn those limestone into bricks.\n  - If you want to convert them yourself and have the skill to do it, you may do so now.","Run south across the first bridge, through the lighthouse and out the back door. From the outside go up the stairs.","Talk to Esther.","Go back downstairs, walk north, and build at the Lodestone hotspot.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Building along the coast"}]},"Wandering Ga'al (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Use a ring of visibility on a ring of stone anywhere outside of the TzHaar City.","Talk to TzHaar-Ga'al-Kot. {Chat: 3 Can you read the ancient TzHaar Language? > 1 Go. I'll meet you at the Fight Cauldron.}"],"t":"Getting started"}]},"Wanted!":{"sections":[{"n":"Either 10,000 coins or an enchanted gem, law rune and molten glass","r":"","s":["Talk to Sir Tiffy in Falador park. {Chat: 1 Do you have any jobs for me yet? > Accept}","Talk to him again. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Wanted! quest}","Talk to Sir Amik Varze, floor 3 of White Knights' Castle in the west wing. Decline his offer. {Chat: 2 Speak about the Wanted! quest. > 3 No, not right now...}","Return to Sir Tiffy. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Wanted! quest}","Talk to Amik Varze again. {Chat: 2 Speak about the Wanted! quest. > 3 Sure, I'll help you!}","Return to Sir Tiffy for a commorb. {Chat: 1 Ask about the Wanted! quest}\n  - If you are buying a commorb {Chat: 1 Buy one > 1 YES > 1 YES}\n  - If you are making one {Chat: 2 Have One Made > 1 YES}"],"t":"Communicate with White Knights"},{"n":"20 unnoted rune essence or pure essence, Commorb, combat equipment","r":"","s":["Right-click contact with the commorb to view your assignment details. {Chat: 1 Current Assignment}","Head to the Taverley Dungeon and go to the south-westernmost area of the Black Knight's Base.","Talk to Lord Daquarius in the southwest room with the throne, south of the furnace icon.","Kill a Black Knight.","Talk to Lord Daquarius again.","Take twenty unnoted essence to the Mage of Zamorak in the south-east corner of Varrock. {Chat: 2 Solus Dellagar} Make sure not to wear god armour.\n  - If you don't already have the essence, have Aubury (in the rune shop north of the Mage of Zamorak) teleport you to the essence mine and mine the 20 essence.\n  - If you are wearing any Saradomin or Guthix gear, you must remove it before speaking to the Mage.","Talk again to give him the essence. {Chat: 2 Solus Dellagar}","Go to Canifis and you will be contacted, complete the conversation. If you accidentally exit out, right-click 'Contact' on the commorb to restart the dialogue.","Scan using the commorb just outside the Canifis bank to find Solus.","An item will appear in your backpack. The table below shows where to scan next. Repeat this 5 times.\n  - If you are wearing one, take off your ring of life; it will not help you and will be destroyed.","Once you have received the pure essence, teleport to the Rune Essence mine by talking to Carwen Essencebinder in Burthorpe (fastest way from Burthorpe lodestone) or Aubury in Varrock or Archmage Sedridor in the Wizards' Tower. {Chat: 1 yes}","Kill Solus Dellagar.","Give Sir Amik Varze the hat. {Chat: 2 Speak about the Wanted! quest.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finding Solus Dellagar"}]},"Watchtower":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Make your way to the watchtower north-east of the Yanille lodestone.","Climb up the trellis outside on this building's northern wall, then take the ladder to the top floor of the Watchtower.","Talk to the Watchtower Wizard on the top floor of the Watchtower. {Chat: 1 What’s the matter? > 1 So how come the spell doesn’t work? > Accept}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Climb down the ladders to return to the bottom floor.","Search the northwesternmost bush just outside the watchtower to find fingernails.","Return to the Watchtower Wizard. {Chat: 1 What do you suggest I do? > 1 So what do I do?}"],"t":"The pawns"},{"n":"2 ropes, death rune, dragon bones, combat gear to defeat Gorad (level 53)","r":"","s":["Talk to Og, an ogre north-west of the Yanille lodestone. {Chat: 1 I seek entrance to the city of ogres.}","Walk south toward the lake's west side, use rope on the branch of a long-branched tree to swing over.","Talk to Grew. {Chat: 1 Don't eat me; I can help you.}","Pick up some jangerberries dropped on Grew's island.","Head to and enter the cave entrance marked on the world map () southwest of Gu'Tanoth and southeast of Jiggig, and you will arrive at the island east of Gu'Tanoth.\n  - If you didn't bring a death rune, one spawns directly south of the tunnel entrance.\n  - To get there you can:\n    - Leave the island and head to south-east to the passage between Gu'Tanoth and the island south of Yanille, then head to south-west to the cave entrance.\n    - You can use fairy ring AKS and head north-west to reach there.\n    - If A Fairy Tale III - Battle at Ork's Rift is completed, you can use fairy ring ALP, head north to exit the tunnel, and head south-east for quicker access.\n    - If The Grand Tree quest is completed and partially completed the quest One Small Favour, you can use gnome glider to fly to the Feldip Hills {Chat: 6 Lemantolly Undri} and head north-west for quicker access.","Talk to Toban twice, he will take the dragon bones and give you relic part 3. {Chat: 1 I seek entrance to the city of ogres. > 1 I could do something for you…}\n  - If you didn't bring a second rope, take one now from the island.","Talk to Gorad and tell him that you have come to knock out his teeth\n  - Kill Gorad and take the ogre tooth.","Open the Chest and take the gold.","Go back and talk to Grew, giving him the tooth and consuming the second rope.","If you didn't get the yellow crystal, talk to Grew again and ask for it.","Talk to Og, north of Grew's island to receive the relic part 1."],"t":"The kings"},{"n":"light source, 20 coins, ogre relic, death rune","r":"","s":["Talk to the Watchtower Wizard until you receive an Ogre relic (there is a break in the conversation).\n  - If you didn't bring a light source, take the lit candle from the floor 1 of Watchtower.","Enter Gu'Tanoth from the north-eastern corner and go west along the northern path.","Use the Ogre relic on one of the guards at the west gate. Do not talk to them or you will be hit for some damage and sent back near Copernicus.","Head south-east to the Ogre trader marked with on the map but don't talk to him.","Steal a rock cake from the counter.","Return to the path and continue south.","Talk to the guards {Chat: 1 But I am a friend to ogres...}, then give (but do not eat) a rock cake to be able to climb over the battlement.","Continue up the path and jump over the gap, paying 20 coins to the guards {Chat: 1 Okay, I'll pay it.}.","Talk to one of the City guard. Make sure to use the \"Talk-to\" option on the guard. {Chat: 2 I seek passage into the skavid caves.}, then talk to them again and give them a death rune."],"t":"Gu'Tanoth"},{"n":"Skavid map, gold bar, light source, armoured gloves","r":"","s":["Enter the green-pinned east cave, marked 4, on the map. (See map next to(above on mobile) this text, click on the east green marker to reveal the cave number).","Talk to the Scared skavid. {Chat: 2 Okay, okay, I’m not going to hurt you.}","Enter the green-pinned north cave, marked 1.","Talk to the skavid (respond with \"Ig\").","While in this cave, pick up two cave nightshades.\n  - Attempting to pick up a cave nightshade without gloves results in a dialogue \"You have been poisoned by the plant!\", causing minor damage.\n  - Attempting to pick up a cave nightshade with regular, non-armoured gloves results in the same dialogue as above and another suggesting to wear armoured gloves, \"Maybe you should wear armoured gloves instead\".","Enter the grey-pinned north cave, marked 2.\n  - Talk to the skavid (respond with \"Ar\").","Enter the red-pinned north cave, marked 3.\n  - Talk to the skavid (respond with \"Cur\").","Enter the grey-pinned east cave, marked 5.\n  - Talk to the skavid (respond with \"Nod\").","Return to the green-pinned east cave, marked 4.\n  - Talk to the Scared skavid.","Go to a gate south of the 4 cave entrance.","Talk to one of the ogre guards and he will take the gold bar and let you in.","Enter the red-pinned south cave, marked 6.","Talk to the Mad skavid to obtain the pink crystal.\n  - If he says \"Ar cur,\" the correct response is \"Gor.\"\n  - If he says \"Bidith ig,\" the correct response is \"Cur.\"\n  - If he says \"Gor nod,\" the correct response is \"Tanath.\"\n  - If he says \"Cur tanath,\" the correct response is \"Bidith.\""],"t":"The skavids"},{"n":"2 cave nightshades, guam potion (unfinished), jangerberries, bat bones","r":"","s":["Head back to Ogre trader marked with on the map (Ogre marketplace).","Use a cave nightshade on one of the enclave guards.","Enter the enclave while the guard is distracted.","After the cutscene, Home teleport to Yanille lodestone, head back to the Watchtower and talk to the Watchtower Wizard.","Add jangerberries to guam potion (unfinished)","Grind bat bones, then add them to the potion.","Talk to the Watchtower Wizard (there is a break in the conversation).","Return to the Ogre marketplace.","Use the second cave nightshade on an enclave guard to distract them and enter the enclave again.","Use the potion on the six ogre shamans in the enclave to kill them.\n  - If you attack a shaman, it will hit you with a very powerful Magic blow, dealing half your life points in damage.","Mine the Rock of Dalgroth on the peninsula in the centre of the enclave."],"t":"Invincible"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to the Watchtower and talk to the Watchtower Wizard.","Use the pink crystal on the north-eastern pillar.","Use the green crystal on the south-eastern pillar.","Use the yellow crystal on the south-western pillar.","Use the blue crystal on the north-western pillar.","Pull the lever on the west side of the room.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Back in action"}]},"Waterfall Quest":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Almera inside her house, south of the Barbarian Outpost. {Chat: Accept}","Board the raft to the west.","Talk to Hudon north of where you land.\n  - If you do not talk to Hudon you will not be able to find the Book on Baxtorian in the later step.","Click swim on the river to the south to end up back on shore."],"t":"The Treasure"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Once back on shore, head north-west to the house south of Almera's house, and climb either the inside staircase, or the outside staircase on the south side of the larger building.","Search the south-eastern bookcases on the east wall to find the Book on Baxtorian.","Read the book.","Head to the Tree Gnome Village, located north-west of Yanille.","Once there, follow the path through the maze, heading towards the dungeon marked on the map\n  - If the quest Tree Gnome Village is at least partially completed, follow Elkoy, who is at the beginning and end of the maze.\n    - If the quest is not partially completed, it is recommended to squeeze through the loose railing and speak to King Bolren while nearby.\n  - Go east and enter the dungeon.","Inside the dungeon, go to the eastern room.","Search the south-east stack of crates which is a different colour than the others, to find a key (must read book in order to find key).","Head to the westernmost room and use the key on the gate to unlock it.","Enter and speak to Golrie to find Glarial's pebble."],"t":"Glarial's Pebble"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Bank everything except Glarial's pebble and your rope (you may bring food and allowed items).\n  - To enter the tomb, you cannot bring combat-related items such as weapons, armour, or runes.\n  - You may drop 6 air runes, 6 water runes and 6 earth runes outside the tomb and retrieve them upon exiting, in order to skip banking for the final part.","Teleport to Ardougne lodestone and go north-west of the Fishing Guild to find Glarial's tombstone.","Use Glarial's pebble on the tombstone.\n  - If it says It fits perfectly, but nothing happens., it's because you are wearing disallowed items or carrying runes","Go west and search the chest to obtain Glarial's amulet.\n  - Optional: Drop the amulet and search the chest for a second one, preventing having to obtain a second one after the quest for dungeon access.","Go south and search Glarial's Tomb to obtain Glarial's urn.","Head north-east back up the ladder you came down."],"t":"Tomb Raiding"},{"n":"6 air runes, 6 water runes, 6 earth runes, a rope, Glarial's urn, and Glarial's amulet.","r":"","s":["Go north-west to the quest start point (Almera's house) and board the raft once more.","Use your rope on the rock situated on the bank to the south (do not click 'swim to rock').","Use your rope on the dead tree next to you (do not click 'climb tree').","With Glarial's amulet in your inventory, enter the cave door north.","Go north-east, open the door, and search the light-colored crates on the northern wall for another key.","Return to the centre room and go down the western passage, past the fire giants, through the doors north.","Use the key on the last door.","Make sure you follow these three steps carefully or you will be washed up down stream.\n  - Use an air rune, a water rune, and an earth rune on each of the six pillars.\n  - Use Glarial's amulet on the statue of Glarial, the western statue.\n  - Use Glarial's urn on the Chalice of Eternity, in the centre of the room.\n    - If you attempt to take the Chalice you will be washed up down stream and will have to get the amulet back from the chest under Glarial's tombstone before being able to return to the cave.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Baxtorian Treasures"}]},"What Lies Below":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Rat Burgiss, south-east of the Varrock lodestone by the crossroads to Lumbridge. {Chat: 2 Hello there! > 3 Shall I get them back for you? > Accept}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Immediately west of the Grand Exchange is a camp. Kill 5 outlaws there.","Take all 5 Rat's papers that they drop.","Use the 5 papers on an empty folder.","Talk to Rat Burgiss. {Chat: 2 Hello there!}"],"t":"Helping Rat"},{"n":"Bowl, 15 chaos runes or pure essence to craft them, at least 1 empty inventory slot (2 recommended)","r":"","s":["Go to the Varrock palace library, and talk to Surok Magis. {Chat: 1 Go on, then!}\n  - Optional: search the bookcase south of the telescope in the north-east section of the room for the Dagon'hai History; it can be turned in to Historian Minas after the quest for 5 kudos.","Use any method to enter the chaos altar.","With 15 chaos runes, use the wand on the altar.\n  - If you brought essence instead, craft the runes now.","Give Surok Magis a bowl and the infused wand. {Chat: 1 I have the things you wanted!}","Talk to Rat Burgiss. {Chat: 2 Hello there! > 1 Yes! I have a letter for you.}","Talk to Zaff, in his shop north-west of Varrock Square. {Chat: 4 Rat Burgiss sent me.}","Talk to Surok Magis. {Chat: 1 Bring it on!}","Attack King Roald, and right-click summon with the beacon ring when he has 1 life point remaining."],"t":"Surok Magis"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["After the cutscene, return to Rat Burgiss. {Chat: 2 Hello there!}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"What's Mine is Yours":{"sections":[{"n":"2 backpack space","r":"","s":["Talk to Doric in his hut, north of the Falador lodestone, until you get an ore bag and mining sites map. (You'll need 2 backpack space) {Chat: 1 Don't worry, I'll help you. > Accept}","Mine any rock in each of the following locations until a living rock brawler appears, kill it, and take the ore it drops:\n  - Dwarven mines, to the east up the hill\n  - Rimmington mine, west of Port Sarim\n    - Watch the cutscene.\n  - Varrock south-west mine\n  - Varrock south-east mine","Talk to Doric."],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Withdraw the ores from the Ore bag and make two High-quality bronze bars using the furnace. {Chat: 1 Yes}","Using Doric's Anvil, smith a High-quality bronze sword and a High-quality bronze dagger.","Talk to Doric. {Chat: 3 I'll leave right away.}","Go to the Artisans' Workshop in the south-east of Falador.","Talk to Aksel. {Chat: 1 Doric sent me here with these weapons.}"],"t":"The weapons"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the White Knights' Castle and talk to Squire Cerlyn in the west tower on the floor 1.","After the cutscene, help Doric and Boric reconcile. Use the following responses:\n  - Boric, tell Doric about your graduation.\n  - Boric, tell Doric what you thought when Doric sent you away.\n  - Boric, tell Doric what you thought of your education.\n  - Boric, tell Doric why you wanted to stay here.\n  - Boric, tell Doric what you thought of Keldagrim\n  - Doric, tell Boric what you thought when Boric was born.\n  - Doric, tell Boric why you sent him to Keldagrim.\n  - Doric, tell Boric how you felt bringing Boric up alone.\n  - Doric, tell Boric what you want Boric's future to be.\n  - Doric, tell Boric what you hoped sending him away would teach him.","Talk to Doric and agree to take the bars.{Chat: 1 I'd love to. > 1 Yes}","Smith the items that were asked for on Doric's anvil.\n  - Ornamental platebody\n  - Ornamental chainbody\n  - Shop sign","Head down the stairs into Doric's cave (if the \"climb down\" option on the northern doorway does not appear, try switching textures off temporarily, this is a known bug).","Mine the rocks blocking the way.","Head back upstairs and talk to Doric to give him the items and trigger a cutscene. {Chat: 1 Yes, I have them here.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Doric and Boric"}]},"While Guthix Sleeps":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"Varrock teleport, any boosts you wish to use to start the quest, and equipment to kill two Assassins","s":["Talk to Radimus Erkle in the Legends' Guild (fairy ring BLR). {Chat: 4 Yes, I'm interested, where do I report? > Accept}","In Taverley, talk to Ivy Sophista in the house west of the summoning obelisk. {Chat: 1 Ask about 'While Guthix Sleeps'. > 4 Our friend in common places great faith in totems.}","Go upstairs and talk to Thaerisk Cemphier. Kill both assassins that appear.","Talk to Thaerisk again. {Chat: 1 What efforts are you making against Lucien? > 2 What are our options? > 2 I know about the 'Fist of Guthix'. > 3 What do you need me to do? > 4 Okay, thanks.}","Talk to Reldo in Varrock Palace library and \"Talk about Lucien and Movario\" {Chat: ? Talk about Lucien and Movario. > 1 What can you tell me about Movario? > 2 What does Movario do? > 3 Where does Movario live? > 4 Okay, thanks.}\n  - If Desperate Times is completed, you need to choose one more chat option before proceed the aforementioned quest dialogue. {Chat: 2 [Talk to Reldo.]}"],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to the Hunting expert in Feldip Hunter area and ask about tracking down a person. {Chat: ? A creature to help track down a person. > 2 How can I catch a wild broav? > 3 What do I do once I've caught a broav? > 4 Okay, thanks.} She is north of Oo'glog lodestone, or south-west of fairy ring AKS. After the conversation she will give you a mort myre fungus.","Go west and trap pit (which builds a pitfall trap) at the square trap pit (uses one set of logs), then use your mort myre fungus on the built trap.","Dismantle the collapsed trap to obtain an unconscious broav.","Talk to the Hunting expert again about tracking a person. {Chat: ? A creature to help track down a person.}"],"t":"Feldip Hunter area"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to the west of Fight Arena and into the laundry room two houses north of the pub. (Kandarin monastery Teleport then run south, or Watchtower Teleport and run north are quick ways to get there.)","With your ring of charos (a) equipped, talk to the Khazard launderer to obtain dirty laundry. {Chat: 2 Do you know someone called Movario? > 2 (Charm) Tell me all you know about Movario.}\n  - If you brought coins instead, take them out of your coin pouch and use them on the launderer. {Chat: 2 No, I need information. Do you know someone called Movario? > 1 Offer five thousand coins for information on Movario.}","Go to the Khazard Battleground north-west (north of Tree Gnome Village and across the bridges).","Climb-over the crumbled wall inside the north-westernmost building.","Drop your Broav in the room with the broken table then use the dirty laundry on him.","Search the broken table to reveal a trapdoor, then go down."],"t":"Khazard"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Pick-up your Broav.","Go through the door, and follow the path to the north, then climb-down the stairs.","Search the old battered door and find the correct rune to use on it. After you enter the correct rune, you'll hear a click.","Search the door again (boost your Thieving level if needed), and you will find a trap to disarm. {Chat: 1 Yes, I'm an awesome thief, I'll disable it easily!}","Go through the old battered door."],"t":"Old battered door"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Search the painting on the east wall {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll flip the catch and see what happens.}.","Choose the Search option on the bookcases until you receive the chat response CLICK!.","Follow the wire that faintly glows to the next bookshelf. (for those with colourblindness, zoom the camera in to see the wire slightly pulsate)\n  - Search that bookshelf.\n  - Repeat, searching each bookshelf until the electricity on the gate disappears.","Open the gate and search the spiral staircase to disarm the trap, then climb-up.","Search the desk to obtain Movario's notes (volume 1)\n  - Read the notes.","Pick-up the waste-paper basket.\n  - With Movario's notes in your backpack, search the basket.","Search the bookcase to the west of the waste-paper basket.\n  - Use the ruby key on the bookcase.\n  - Climb-up the stairs just north of you.","Search the bed.\n  - Use the ruby key on the bed chest.\n  - Search the bed chest to disarm the traps {Chat: 1 Yes, I'll attempt it.} You may need to attempt again until you disarm the trap.\n  - Open and search it. Use the ruby key on the chest. Open and search the chest to obtain a strange key loop, strange key teeth, and Movario's notes (volume 2). Read these notes too.","Climb back down twice to the wire room and cross-over the broken wall, then search the drawers.","Look-at the thermometer. Note down the number it says. Check your current character's weight in your equipment interface. You must equalise both numbers. If you weigh more than the number: subtract the number from the thermometer from your character's weight to get the result number. For example: if the thermometer says 20 and you weigh 30, you would need 10. If you weigh less than the number: subtract your character's weight from the number from to get the result number.\n  - Pick up your Broav if you haven't already, otherwise it will mess with the numbers.","On the floor of this room is a Pile of weights. Take weights equalling the result number you got. If you have been following the guide, you will need to take two 2kg weights, as Movario's notes and the key parts weigh 4kg collectively. CAUTION: You will not be able to recover any items dropped in this room.","Climb back up the spiral staircase. If you weigh more than the number: use all the weights on the statue just north of you, then open the door just east. If you weigh less than the number: keep the weights in your inventory and open the door east of the statue.","Head east through the door and up the ladder to leave the hideout."],"t":"Inside Movario's base"},{"n":"Strange key loop, Strange key teeth, Movario's notes (volume 1) and Movario's notes (volume 2), equipment to kill two mercenary axemen and a mercenary mage","r":"","s":["Return to Thaerisk Cemphier in Taverley with the items obtained in Movario's base. {Chat: 2 What should I do now? > 5 Sorry, I have to go.}","Head to the building in McGrubor's Wood (Seers' Village lodestone or fairy ring ALS), and a cutscene will start. Kill all the mercenaries.","Search the dead mercenaries and talk to the wounded Guardian of Armadyl.","Go upstairs in the Seers' Village pub and talk to Idria. {Chat: 1 Do you know where Lucien is? > 3 How can I get to Lucien?}","Talk to Sir Tiffy Cashien in the Falador Park. {Chat: 1 While Guthix Sleeps.} or {Chat: 2} if the Slug Menace hasn't been completed.","Go to the White Knights' Castle.","In the eastern room on the floor 1, talk to Akrisae. {Chat: 3 How can I get to Draynor? > 1 Yes, please!}","At Draynor Village, use the teleorb on the shady stranger wearing white robes and near the shore. This may take several attempts.","Talk to Akrisae in the White Knight's Castle. Cutscene plays.","If you don't have a snapdragon seed for the next step, buy one from Thaerisk. {Chat: 2 Could you help me get a snapdragon seed? > 1 Yes.}","Talk to Thaerisk to teleport to Port Sarim. {Chat: 3 Can you teleport me to Port Sarim, please?}"],"t":"Catching Lucien's spy"},{"n":"Lantern lens, snapdragon seed, 20 coins, 6 air runes, 3 cosmic runes, 3 astral runes , lunar spellbook","r":"","s":["Talk to Betty in the Port Sarim magic shop for truth serum and pink dye. {Chat: 1 Talk to Betty about While Guthix Sleeps. > 1 Yes, please can I have a standard truth serum? > 1 Yes, please!} (If The Hand In The Sand quest is completed {Chat: 2 Talk to Betty about While Guthix Sleeps. > 1 Yes, please can I have a standard truth serum? > 1 Yes, please!})","If the snapdragon seed isn't already on the counter, talk to her again until she places the seed on the counter.","Use the pink dye on your lantern lens.","Stand just inside the doorway, use the lens with the counter and take the enriched snapdragon seed by searching the counter.","If not already, switch to the Lunar spellbook.","Using the most western staircase in White Knight Castle, head to the top of the castle and plant the seed in the herb patch.","Go back downstairs and talk to Thaerisk on the ground floor of the eastern part of the castle. {Chat: 1 I've planted the enriched snapdragon seed.}","Cast NPC Contact to talk to the following people:\n  - Turael {Chat: 1 I need to talk to you about Lucien.}\n  - Duradel {Chat: 1 I need to talk to you about Lucien.}\n  - Mazchna {Chat: 1 I need to talk to you about Lucien.}","Talk to Hazelmere upstairs in the hut east of Yanille near fairy ring CLS."],"t":"Super truth serum and recruiting the Heroes"},{"n":"Truth serum, 1 astral rune, 1 cosmic rune, and 2 air runes","r":"","s":["Pick the enriched snapdragon (top of west tower at White Knights' Castle) and mix it into your truth serum for a super truth serum.","Head back to the room with Thaerisk and the others.","Open and search the drawers to find charcoal and papyrus.","Go into the cell and use the serum on the shady stranger. {Chat: ~} The correct chat option varies from player to player. Exhaust chat options until you reach the correct one so that the stranger drinks the serum.","Talk to the shady stranger again.","Talk to Idria.","Cast NPC Contact to talk to Cyrisus. {Chat: 1 I need to talk to you about Lucien.}","Head to the Warriors' Guild and talk to the following:\n  - Ghommal just outside\n  - Harrallak Menarous in the main lobby {Chat: 1 I need to talk to you about Lucien!}\n  - Sloane upstairs {Chat: 1 Recruit Sloane for the hero party.}","Return to the White Knights' Castle and speak to Idria, then Akrisae."],"t":"Questioning the spy"},{"n":"Unpowered orb, runes for any charge Orb spell (3 cosmics and 30 runes of any element or any elemental staff), items to enter Black Knights' Fortress (Skull of Remembrance, bronze med helm/iron chainbody, black armour set or Black Knight captain's armour), equipment for two combat styles or Necromancy (Necromancy recommended).","r":"Falador teleport, Food for fighting multiple enemies, Elite Black Knight armour from the Grand Exchange to save some time. Once you have a set of Elite Black Knight armour, you will need 9 free inventory slots to proceed. If you have purchased Elite Black Knight armour, you do not need combat gear, but some food is still advised. Bringing a summoning familiar with a different combat style will make the fights much easier.","s":["Switch back to the standard spellbook.","You will need 11 free inventory slots to proceed.","Equip your disguise and head inside Black Knights' Fortress with all the items above or use the skull of remembrance to teleport to the ritual chamber, and make your way down to the floor 1.","Climb down the ladder in the south-west corner.","Along the east wall, right-click search the floor tile. Cast your charge orb spell on the floor tile.","Climb-down the trapdoor.","Kill Elite Black Knights to obtain a helmet, platebody and platelegs if you don't have a set already. The three pieces of armour are guaranteed to drop until 3 pieces are received. Do not use multi-target abilities as killing two Elite Black Knights at once will cause them both to drop the same piece, with both counting toward the first 3 pieces received. Equip the full set to remove their aggression.","Head north by jumping across the broken bridge, go east, and climb up the wall.","Jump over the barricade and walk north-west until you reach a fork in the path, then head east.","Talk to Silif in the northmost cell. {Chat: 1 Silif, it's me, [Name]. Are you okay? > 2 I want to get you out of here. Any suggestions? > 3 I'll be back to try to get you out.}","Go back west and enter the northern centre Solid black door.","Search all desks and wardrobes in the room for:\n  - Another set of elite black armour\n  - Full set of Dagon'hai robes\n  - Restore potion (4) (Do not drink the restore potion)\n  - Strange teleorb\n  - Lobster (Do not eat the lobster)\n    - If you accidentally eat the lobster, any kind of cooked food will work as well.","Right-click search the key rack on the northern wall (a few tiles east of the wardrobe) for a Cell key.","Enter Silif's cell. Use the piece of food on Silif, then the potion. {Chat: 2 Do you have a plan?}","Give Silif a set of elite black armour (dismiss your familiar if you have one).","Return to the northern room. Walk to the map board on the southern wall then talk to Silif.","Plant the teleorb on Dark Squall, who is located in the east of the room, then escape back to Falador."],"t":"Into the Black Knights' Fortress"},{"n":"Strange teleorb, Dagon'hai robe armour, one law rune, one death rune","r":"In this section, there is a brief encounter in the Wilderness, where it is possible to encounter danger from creatures and/or events. Therefore, carrying food and defensive armour is recommended. Teleport (preferably to Falador)","s":["Talk to Akrisae. {Chat: 1 What would this orb look like? > 2 How will I be able to get to Lucien's base? > 3 Okay, thanks.}","Wear your Dagon'hai robes and enter the nearby jail cell.","Climb up the ladder in the north-eastern corner, stand in the stone circle in the middle of the room, and right-click activate the strange teleorb. (Note: Activation will fail if the required runes are in a pouch.)","Follow the north-eastern path towards the chapel and climb-up the ice wall. There is a stick in the ice wall to indicate where to climb.","Jump-to the ledge on the chapel into the Wilderness.","Walk east to activate a cutscene.","Return to Falador after the cutscene.","Talk to Idria.\n  - If she won't talk about Movario and instead keeps saying to investigate Lucien's camp, then unfortunately the game glitched and you must go back and rewatch the cutscene. Remember to bring the strange teleorb, a law rune, and a death rune. A good indicator that the cutscene registered is to check for the \"You have unlocked a new music track: The Evil Within\" game message."],"t":"Lucien's Army"},{"n":"Sapphire lantern, Dagon'hai robe armour, equipment for two combat styles (or Necromancy) and some food (You can go back to get these at a later step), prayer points to use the Bloom ability (a sickle and pouch are provided) OR two druid pouch charges (neither needed if you have an ouroboros pouch). You also need enough free inventory space to unequip anything in your main hand and off hand, plus 6 additional free inventory slots","r":"Games necklace, emergency teleport, energy potions, super restore potions for fighting the balance elemental.","s":["Go to the Tears of Guthix cavern.","Equip your Dagon'hai robes and talk to Movario North. {Chat: 3 I am Surok, Lucien has sent me to check on your progress. > 1 I could go down to the bottom first, to make sure it's safe! > 3 I shall return.}","With a sapphire lantern lit, right-click travel into cavern with a light creature.","Search the northernmost skeleton for a silver sickle (b) and 6 druid pouch charges.\n  - If you have an Ouroboros pouch or brought two druid pouch charges of your own, you can drop the silver sickle to save inventory space.","Search the rocks {Chat: 1 Yes} in the north-eastern corner. Then search on the brazier that appears, choosing the chisel option to receive a fire orb.","Repeat on the north-west rock for the earth orb.","Repeat for the standing lit braziers for air and water orbs in the south-western and south-eastern corners.","Head further south to reach three skull cavities on the southern wall. Examine each recessed block and use the respective orb on the block.","Climb up the wall twice and use the water orb on the recessed block.","Jump down the same way you came up. For each of the three lower skulls, enter its nose cavity.\n  - Dismiss any followers and empty both your main and off-hand slots before entering the cavities.","Crawl along the tunnel in each cavity to its end. Examine the door there and insert the respective element key into the door lock. Crawl back through the tunnel and exit the skull.","Climb up the walls to the upper skull. Use the fire key on the skull's recessed block, then search the stone cube in front of the skull.","Climb-through the cave opening to enter the Guthixian temple."],"t":"Into the chasm"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["You will now need at least two free backpack spaces, though more can make it quicker to proceed. Ensure that you have also deactivated any sign of the porter effects.","There are eight statues in this temple. Each, when examined, will reveal what type of potion must be \"made\" at that statue.","Use your druid pouches on the druid spirits. Each will drop required ingredients for the statues once - if these are lost (e.g. by dropping and letting them timeout), you will have to get replacements yourself. Grace of the elves will send items to the bank so unequip it or disable its porter functionality.","Do not let your druid pouch empty completely or it disappears! You need 3 open inventory slots to add 3 flowers into the druid pouch.\n  - Use the Bloom spell on your silver sickle (b) while standing on or close to the dead vine to grow some vine flower to recharge your druid pouch.","Use the herbs and the secondary ingredients on the various statues referencing the table below. Not all keywords will be on statues.\n  - If you have an ouroboros pouch, you do not need to worry about the druid pouch losing charges. However, you must carry a druid pouch in the backpack to \"use\" it on the spirits, though it will never deplete.\n  - If you need to refill your druid pouch, right-click bloom with your silver sickle near dead vines to get flowers. These can be used to refill the druid pouch. If you received a mort myre fungus from the druids, use it with the correct statue or drop it for a moment before filling the druid pouch else you will lose it!","Use the dolmens you receive from the statues on the Stone Table in the middle of the temple. It will open the huge door in front of it."],"t":"=Intended method="},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Make whatever arrangements necessary to battle the level 117 Balance Elemental that can use all three combat styles, and lowers your combat stats (except for Necromancy). You can leave the area to get supplies, but always bring your lit sapphire lantern. Don't forget to bring at least two combat styles for the tormented demon fight, unless using Necromancy. The Balance Elemental drains combat stats during the fight, so be sure to bring at least one full super restore.","Proceed down the corridor and enter a large chamber.","Once ready, search the mysterious stone {Chat: 1 Yes, I need to investigate this, even if it kills me!} and kill the Balance Elemental that appears. See the strategy guide here.","Search the mysterious stone again for a cutscene. Doing so boosts all your combat stats to level 255 except Prayer.","Continue dialogue with Movario {Chat: 1 What are you going to do with the Stone of Jas? > 2 What is the Stone of Jas? > 3 You can't let Lucien get the Stone of Jas! > 4 What if someone should stand in your way?}, then with Lucien. {Chat: 1 What are you going to do with the Stone of Jas? > 2 Why is the Stone of Jas so important to you? > 3 Do you really hope to follow in the footsteps of Zamorak?}","Kill the two Tormented demons, switching between your two combat styles.","Talk to Idria to have her teleport you to Falador. {Chat: 1 Yes, a teleport out of here would be good.}","Continue dialogue with Idria in Falador.","Quest complete!","Optional: after using of all four of Idria's 100,000 exp boosts, talk to her again to view the \"Elsewhere...\" epilogue."],"t":"The Stone of Jas"}]},"Witch's House":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Harvey standing by the long garden just west of Falador, just west of the crumbling wall which requires level 5 Agility to cross. {Chat: 1 What's the matter? > Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the front door of the house.","Look under the northern potted plant for the house key and enter.","Climb down the stairs into the basement.","If you didn't bring leather gloves, search the nearby crates for a pair. You may have to search several times.","While wearing leather gloves, enter the gate.","Open and search the cupboard, straight ahead on the western wall for a magnet.","Go back up the stairs and grab the cheese off of the table.","Go to the room located on the south end of the house.","Right-Click Use cheese on the mouse hole on the eastern wall. (If you accidentally eat it, it will respawn on the table.)","Use the magnet on the mouse."],"t":"Entering the house"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Exit the door and make your way to the fountain, being careful not to be seen by the witch.\n  - Strategically walk behind the shrubs to hide, being sure to stand in the middle space of each shrub. Surge can be used; timing is key.","Check fountain for a shed key.","Return east down the shrubs to the shed, being careful not to be caught by the witch, and open the door.","Try to take the ball, the experiment will appear and attack you.\n  - Don't forget to actually take the ball after the experiment has been killed.","Kill the Witch's experiment four times.\n  - (All forms of the experiment/shapeshifter are weak to Water Spells)."],"t":"Retrieving the ball"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take the ball.","Return and talk to Harvey (getting caught teleports you outside, you'll keep the ball)","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"Witch's Potion (miniquest)":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Hetty in her house in Rimmington, west of the Port Sarim lodestone and south of Falador. {Chat: 3 I'm looking for work. > Accept}","Kill a rat for a rat's tail.\n  - Some rats can be found in Brian's Archery Supplies.","Give her the ingredients.","Drink from the cauldron."],"t":"Getting started"}]},"Within the Light":{"sections":[{"n":"Two sets of mourner outfit, new key, tarnished key, one backpack space; recommend=Crystal trinket, Death talisman are needed immediately afterwards, grab before teleporting with Arianwyn","r":"","s":["Talk to Arianwyn in Lletya in the large building to the east. {Chat: Accept}\n  - To get to Lletya easily, use a crystal teleport seed, a Tirannwn quiver 1, or pass through the forest from Tirannwn lodestone.","With your mourner gear equipped, enter the Mourner Headquarters in the north-east of West Ardougne and climb down the trapdoor.","If you need the keys, search the Head Mourner's desk in the basement's south-east room for the tarnished key and new key.","Enter the tunnels with the new key and run to the west to approach the Temple of Light.","Remove your gas mask and chant-to the blank teleport crystal in your backpack, whilst standing east of the first slave on the square directly between the north and south crates (picture for reference).","After the cutscene, return to the room next to the Head Mourner's office.","Talk to the gnome. {Chat: 1 Talk about Within the Light. > 2 Stay undercover.}\n  - Talk to Head Mourner if you want to honour your deal.","Optionally for the second set of mourner outfit, you can kill a mourner nearby.","Return to Lletya.","Bank for food to fend against shadows.","Use a piece of mourner's outfit on Arianwyn.","Use the enchanted crystal on Arianwyn.","Talk to Arianwyn and accept the teleport. Dismiss your pet or familiar if you have any. {Chat: 1 About those tasks I need to do... > 1 I'm ready, let's go.}\n  - Make sure to have a second set of mourner gear to hand in, if not done earlier, talk to him again once he is dressed."],"t":"Trouble in the temple"},{"n":"Crystal trinket, Death talisman","r":"","s":["Proceed to Thorgel in the temple. Do not teleport out of the room to the death altar until rotating the red beam back the way it started, or else the light door will be locked on return.\n  - Go up the stairs to the west, up the ladder to the south, down the stairs in the centre, down again, and through the light door. Rotate the red beam west and go through another light door.\n  - Do not use death altar teleport at this point unless you are absolutely certain the light beam is situated to let you out of the altar room.","Talk to Thorgel near the death ruins. {Chat: 1 Within the Light.}","Talk to Arianwyn.","Investigate the energised pillar (east multi-coloured 4-beam pillar).","Talk to Arianwyn.","(Epilepsy warning about 2s duration) Use the crystal trinket on the energised pillar.","Talk to Arianwyn. {Chat: 3 I'm not even going to argue.}\n  - Speak to Arianwyn again if you need a death talisman.","Enter the death ruins.","Remember the following steps and do them quickly, or you'll have to try again:\n  - Talk to Thorgel to become energised. {Chat: 1 Within the Light. > 2 Okay, let's do this.}\n    - He is south of the altar, and does not appear as a yellow dot on the minimap.\n  - Exit the altar.\n  - Pass the door of light.\n  - Rotate the first pillar of light mirror by the stairs.\n  - Go up the first stairs and immediately take the stairs to your left (north).\n  - Run all the way east then south to the large crystal and investigate it. (If it speaks, you were not fast enough and have to go back to Thorgel.)\n  - Run back down the stairs and touch the energised pillar. (If you don't get transported, you were not fast enough.)"],"t":"The death altar"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Once inside, search the dead slave on the ground.","Chop, then fix the eastern crystal tree with the blue light beam.","Solve the puzzles by reflecting the light beams to the opposite coloured receivers. You only have one receiver available at a time.",": For example: if the receiver in the end is yellow and since the opposite of yellow is blue (refer to the colour wheel), you need to direct the blue light beam to the yellow receiver. Due to how mirrors reflect, you often have to reroute, just keep trying different paths for the quickest solution.",": Refer to the in-depth guide if you cannot figure it out.\n  - Redirect the blue light to the yellow receiver. This enables the red light.\n  - Redirect a combination of red and blue light to the green receiver. This enables the green light.\n  - Redirect a combination of blue and green light to the red receiver.\n  - Redirect all three colours to the colourless receiver. When done all receivers on the western wall will be white. See below for example solutions.","Exit using the ladder in the south-east (not the portal)."],"t":"Within the light itself"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Reach the platform with the ballista by jumping between the platform and trying to avoid the spikes in the floor.","Shoot it at the right time to hit the target."],"t":"Sharpshooter"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go back the way you came and jump to the ladder.","Go-through the large stone door on the west wall.","Search the Elf messenger.","Read the report.","Important: Before you leave the temple, rotate the mirror of the red beam back to the east, so that when you return to the Temple again, you will be able to access the Death Altar room.","Now is your last chance to inquire about saving the Gnome, if you intend to (it's completely optional).","Return to Arianwyn in Lletya and give him the report.","Quest complete!"],"t":"The passage to Prifddinas"}]},"Wiz Kid":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Ben at Marigold Farm in Havenhythe. {Chat: Accept > ~}","Talk to him again to give him the runes. {Chat: 1 Yes, I brought enough runes for me too.}","Talk to him again to continue the quest. {Chat: 1 Yes.}"],"t":"Training Ben"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Cast the Wendlewick Teleport spell, and talk to him again.","Enter the windmill to the north, climb up the ladder to the top floor, and talk to him.","Go back to the bottom floor and talk to him outside."],"t":"Teleportation"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the farmhouse to the south and take the flowers off the counter in the eastern room.","Place the flowers on the stool east of Ben, then cast Telekinetic Grab on them.","Place the flowers back on the stool and talk to Ben."],"t":"Telekinetic Grab"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["If you don't already have bones, head to the western side of the farmhouse and dig in the dirt mound for 2 sets of crow bones.","Place a bone on the stool near Ben, then cast the Bones to Bananas spell.","Talk to Ben."],"t":"Bones to Bananas"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go to the Wizards' Tower floor 3 and talk to Archmage Sedridor to the southwest. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Wiz Kid'.}\n  - If unlocked, the teleport option on stardust in the currency pouch places you near Archmage Sedridor.","Go down one floor and talk to Wizard Isidor to the west. {Chat: 1 Talk about 'Wiz Kid'.}","Return to Ben and talk to him or Wizard Isidor. {Chat: 1 Yes.}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finding a Mentor"}]},"Wolf Whistle":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to Pikkupstix in his house just north of Taverley's east entrance. {Chat: 2 Do you have a quest for me? > Accept}"],"t":"Getting started"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Head to south of the Taverley lodestone, enter the well, and watch the short cutscene. {Chat: 1 Look, I'll just go and take a look myself...}","Talk to Pikkupstix back at the east side of Taverley. {Chat: 2 Bowloftrix has been kidnapped by trolls! > 5 I think I had better go.}"],"t":"Assistants"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Go upstairs at Pikkupstix's house and search the cluttered drawers in the north-west corner.","Go to the pet shop south of Pikkupstix and ask the owner about white hare meat. {Chat: 1 Ask about the white hare meat.}","Go back towards the well and go west onto White Wolf Mountain.","Take the eastern path and search Stikklebrix's body.","Talk to Pikkupstix after the items are obtained. {Chat: 2 I need to ask you something about the quest...}"],"t":"Pouch materials"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Talk to him again. {Chat: 2 I need to ask you something about the quest... > 1 I made the giant wolpertinger pouch!}","Go west back to the well and talk to Scalectrix (make sure you dismiss your pet if you have one out).","Watch the cutscene.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Finishing up"}]},"You Are It":{"sections":[{"n":"","r":"","s":["Teleport to Seers' Village and run north-west to McGrubor's Wood (fairy ring ALS).","Enter the woods through the Loose railing.","Attempt to chop the tree 14 paces west and 6 paces south of the crate. (Slightly different colour, and near the quest marker on the minimap)","Read the mysterious clue scroll. {Chat: Accept}","Talk to Reldo in the library of Varrock Palace.","Read the mysterious clue scroll again."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Stand in the room with Duke Horacio on the floor 2 of Lumbridge Castle.","Remove all worn items, then perform the Cry and Panic emotes (in that order). You should see a cutscene if it works.","Go to Lumbridge cemetery. Using the mysterious clue's dig option, dig one square to the north of the largest tombstone along the southern fence. You will get a locked casket. You must complete the cutscene in order to continue.","Teleport to Port Sarim and run west to Rimmington. Enter the POH portal in Rimmington to trigger a cutscene.\n  - Read the scroll again.","Teleport to Draynor, run into the Draynor Manor, and head into the first door to the west after entering the building.","Search the bookcase in the north-western part of the room to find the casket key.","Open the locked casket to obtain an old necklace."],"t":"Treasure trail"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Take a rope, and go back into McGrubor's Wood. Enter the railing shortcut and stand two squares south of the crate (which is south of the building).","Dig via the old necklace.","Inspect and then descend into the Mysterious Hole.","Follow the path to the end and investigate the coffin for a cutscene.","Talk to the double agent.{Chat: 3 What happens next? > 4 I'm going to look around.}","Investigate the mantle to the east for a cutscene. {Chat: 6 The Stone > 1 Yes.}","Talk to Uri.","Quest complete!"],"t":"Mysterious hole"}]},"Zogre Flesh Eaters":{"sections":[{"n":"Around 10 free inventory spaces, combat equipment","r":"","s":["Talk to Grish in Jiggig, located a short run south of the Castle Wars. {Chat: 3 What are Zogres? > 4 Can I help in any way? > Accept}","Talk to the ogre guard (without the combat level, east).","Climb over the crushed barricade.","Run east and down the stairs.","Run as far north-west as you can, and search the skeleton, kill the zombie, and take his ruined backpack.\n  - If you're in combat when trying to search the skeleton, the zombie will not spawn.","Open the ruined backpack. You will get a dragon inn tankard, a knife, and rotten food. Drop all except the dragon inn tankard.","Search the broken lectern behind the skeleton.","Read the torn page.","Search the nearby ogre coffin until you find a black prism."],"t":"Starting out"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Enter the Dragon Inn pub in Yanille.","Use the dragon inn tankard on the bartender.","Talk to Zavistic Rarve on the floor 2 of the Wizards' Guild. Ring the bell outside if you lack the requirements. {Chat: 1 What did you say I should do?}","Enter the house just north of the guild, floor 2, talk to Sithik in bed. {Chat: 3 Do you mind if I look around?}","Search the drawers, the cupboard, and the wardrobe.","Read the 3 books, use the papyrus on Sithik to make a portrait, then use the portrait on Sithik.","Make sure that Sithik says that he appreciates \"honesty\" of the portrait or you will have to make another. If he says 'truth' you will have to try again. There is more papyrus in the drawers.","Use the portrait on the bartender. He will return it as a Signed portrait.\n  - If he just says that he recognises Sithik without signing the portrait, it means that you forgot to show him the dragon inn tankard.","Talk to to Zavistic Rarve. He will give you a strange potion. {Chat: 1 I'm here about the sicks...err Zogres. > 3 I have some items that I'd like you to look at.}","Use the strange potion on the cup of tea beside Sithik.","Climb down the ladder, climb up the ladder, ask Sithik all the possible questions. {Chat: 1 How do I remove the effects of the spell from the area? > 2 How do I get rid of the undead ogres? > 3 How do I get rid of the disease? > 4 Sorry, I have to go.}"],"t":"Yanille"},{"n":"","r":"","s":["Return to Grish at the quest start, he will give you a key. {Chat: 1 I found who's responsible for the Zogres being here.}","Talk to him again to be able to create a comp ogre bow and brutal arrows, which can be used to fight the upcoming boss. {Chat: 2 There must be an easier way to kill these zogres!}\n  - (Optional) Use a clean rogue's purse on a vial of water, and then add a clean snakeweed to create a relicym's balm. Use this on Uglug Nar next to Grish, and you unlock his shop Uglug's Stuffsies which sells the comp ogre bow. This will also complete the Brutal Stuffsies achievement.\n  - (Optional) Either buy brutal arrows from the Grand Exchange, or fletch them at this point; there are achey trees to the west of Grish, chop them down and fletch their logs into shafts, then attach feathers, and tip them with nails of your choosing.","Cross the barricade to the east and go down the stairs again.","Once inside, run directly west, through the double doors and down more stairs.","Go north-east and search the stand in front of the pile of skulls. Prepare for battle.","Kill Slash Bash, pick up the Ogre artefact he drops.","Return to Grish at quest start. {Chat: 1 Yeah, I have them here!}","Quest complete!"],"t":"Final Battle"}]}};
